{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1443592-the-official-v5-vs-v20-thread","id":1443592,"title":"The official V5 vs. V20 thread","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","World of Darkness","Vampire: The Masquerade"],"posts":[{"date":"2021-04-12T07:14:08-07:00","id":1443592,"title":"The official V5 vs. V20 thread","content":"The edition wars are over and got very personal. However, it's been a much better and more polite place these past few months. As such, I think it'll be okay to make a thread for officially debating the merits of V5 vs. V20.<br /> <br /> 1. <b>Be polite</b>: Everyone here is a fan of Vampire: The Masquerade after all.<br /> <br /> 2. <b>Respect there's no obvious answer</b>: Some people like different things.<br /> <br /> 3. <b>Have Fun</b>: This is a debate that's meant to be about your love of the game, not frustrated with other poster's opinion or specific details.<br /> <br /> 4. <b>Remember this is an OPP forum</b>: This is kind of an off-beat mentioning but it should be noted that Onyx Path Publishing created V20 and yet also has done extensive numbers of supplements for V5. They have dogs on both sides of this fight and this is their forum, so, hey.<br /> <br /> 5. <b>You're welcome to like and dislike elements of both</b>: There's things I love about V5 and things I hate. Same for V20.<br /> <br /> 6. <b>Try not to threadcrap:</b> If you flat out don't like one. Focus on the positives of the one you do. Focus criticism specifically versus saying, &quot;V20/V5 sucks.&quot;<br /> <br /> So with these rules in place, feel free to say what you think both sides did better and why you like or dislike things.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Author of <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Cthulhu-Armageddon-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01KUOM7SI/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982844&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Cthulhu+Armageddon\" target=\"_blank\">Cthulhu Armageddon</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Teenage-Weredeer-Bright-Falls-Mysteries-ebook/dp/B075TTN2FN/ref=sr_1_2?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982717&amp;sr=1-2&amp;keywords=Weredeer#customerReviews\" target=\"_blank\">I was a Teenage Weredeer</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Straight-Outta-Fangton-Comedic-Vampire-ebook/dp/B01KNHICCC/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982774&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Straight+Outta+Fangton\" target=\"_blank\">Straight Outta Fangton</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Lucifers-Star-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01MDM9MCT/ref=mt_kindle?_encoding=UTF8&amp;me=&amp;qid=\" target=\"_blank\">Lucifer's Star</a>, </i>and the <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Rules-Supervillainy-Saga-Book-ebook/dp/B07MB89S33/\" target=\"_blank\">Supervillainy Saga</a>.</i><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":12002,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","user":"CTPhipps","date":". 04-12-2021, 01:03 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","name":"CTPhipps","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12002_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13933"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-04-12T08:05:34-07:00","id":1443596,"title":"","content":"Who are you and what god did you pray to in order to get permission to create this thread? <br /> <br /> <br /> Out of Curiosity, Like this post if you think V20 is better.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":48}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25794-mywifeisscary","name":"MyWifeIsScary","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25794_2.png","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3711"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-04-12T08:06:07-07:00","id":1443597,"title":"","content":"Out of curiosity, like this post if you think V5 is better.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":9}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25794-mywifeisscary","name":"MyWifeIsScary","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25794_2.png","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3711"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-04-12T08:07:53-07:00","id":1443598,"title":"","content":"The hunger system and feeding restrictions are far too sever and random. I feel like they are murphy's law waiting to destroy hours of hard work for a couple bad rolls.<br /> <br /> Touchstones being people only=bad, but I actually like touchstones in concept. Maybe they should have called it obsessions. Beckets need to find more knowledge, that Lasombra that needed to quest for the grail, The Salubri Warrior who needs revenge, Helena who has to control every aspect of her city. It gives them a reason to get out of bed and motivation to endanger themselves to play the game and go after what they want. A person could be a touchstone but not every player is Peter Parker worrying about Aunt May.<br /> <br /> Disciplines in volume five are also limiting choices even if I liked the idea of the physical disciplines having specific powers (I don't) the fact that getting one thing closes you off from other things is wrong. Disiplines are also not powerful enough for elders. Helena can trash groups of enemy vampires or Lupines in volume 20, not so much in vol 5. How do these elders survive thousands of years playing the game? How does <span style=\"color:#3A3A3A\"><span style=\"font-family:Verdana\"><span style=\"font-size:14px\">Ur-Shulgi come out of Torpor to rule his clan and slaughter the unworthy while wiping away a curse set down by a blood god as if it was no big thing.</span></span></span><br /> <br /> Playstyle wise I think V20 is the game of Yes, V5 is the game of No.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":14}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24221-vamps-like-us","name":"Vamps Like Us","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"390"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-04-12T08:19:50-07:00","id":1443599,"title":"","content":"<b>V20 vs. V5</b><br /> <br /> I think that the biggest advantage of V5 over V20 is the fact that I'm a huge metaplot fan while V20 was designed to be metaplot agnostic. All of the characters were effectively frozen at the end of Revised and I had all of the Revised books so it didn't bring me much necessity to get V20. There's some good supplements that I enjoyed picking up toward the end like the revised Black Hand, Anarchs Unbound, and the Red List but I feel like it was limited by the fact that it was &quot;frozen&quot; without any way to move forward.<br /> <br /> V5 may not have always made popular changes but it made changes and moved the setting into the 21st century.<br /> <br /> <b>V5 vs. OPP V5</b><br /> <br /> One of the things that needs to be acknowledged is the fact that I think there's multiple versions of V5 and this is a reboot that has also undergone &quot;course correction.&quot; I feel like the main book of V5 had a lot of very provocative changes to the setting that caused people to react badly. The Elders being Beckoned, the Sabbat going off to fight the Gehenna War, the lack of detail on certain clans, and so on. However, I think that <i>Chicago by Night</i> went a long way to correcting a lot of these flaws. Both it and <i>Cults of the Blood Gods</i> went a long way to providing flavor to the setting that was missing as well as dialing back the more overt changes. This made a much more playable and interesting V:TM and follows up on a lot of the metaplot elements of <i>Beckett's Jyhad Diary</i>.<br /> <br /> <u>Chicago by Night Fixes</u><br /> <br /> * Nope, not all the Elders went to the Middle East.<br /> * Nope, not every Elder feels the Beckoning.<br /> * This is how the Anarchs work as a separate sect in the same city as the Camarilla.<br /> * The Elders lie about banning cell phones. It's just no social media and that's so stupid that only Anarchs would do it.<br /> * The Sabbat are still around enough to have the Lasombra defection matter. They're not all in the Middle East.<br /> * Here's the Lasombra so you can USE the Sabbat if you want.<br /> * The Second Inquisition is dangerous and has killed some vampires but is more interested than monitoring vampires than total extermination. It's also very divided.<br /> <br /> <u>V5 Reviews</u><br /> <br /> THE V5 EDITION: <a href=\"https://booknest.eu/reviews/charles/1313-vampirethemasquerade5thedition\" target=\"_blank\">https://booknest.eu/reviews/charles/...rade5thedition</a><br /> <br /> THE ANARCH: <a href=\"https://booknest.eu/reviews/charles/1379-anarchvampirethemasquerade\" target=\"_blank\">https://booknest.eu/reviews/charles/...ethemasquerade</a><br /> <br /> THE CAMARILLA: <a href=\"https://booknest.eu/reviews/charles/1380-thecamarillavampirethemasquerade\" target=\"_blank\">https://booknest.eu/reviews/charles/...ethemasquerade</a><br /> <br /> CHICAGO BY NIGHT 5E: <a href=\"https://booknest.eu/reviews/charles/1609-chicagobynight\" target=\"_blank\">https://booknest.eu/reviews/charles/1609-chicagobynight</a><br /> <br /> CULTS OF THE BLOOD GODS: <a href=\"https://booknest.eu/reviews/charles/2199-cultsofthebloodgods\" target=\"_blank\">https://booknest.eu/reviews/charles/...ofthebloodgods</a><br /> <br /> V5 COMPANION: <a href=\"https://booknest.eu/reviews/charles/2184-vampirethemasqueradecompanion\" target=\"_blank\">https://booknest.eu/reviews/charles/...eradecompanion</a><br /> <br /> THE CHICAGO FOLIOS: <a href=\"https://booknest.eu/reviews/charles/1786-thechicagofolios\" target=\"_blank\">https://booknest.eu/reviews/charles/...echicagofolios</a><br /> <br /> LET THE STREETS RUN RED: <a href=\"https://booknest.eu/reviews/charles/2080-letthestreetsrunred\" target=\"_blank\">https://booknest.eu/reviews/charles/...estreetsrunred</a><br /> <br /> CHILDREN OF THE BLOOD: <a href=\"https://booknest.eu/reviews/charles/2222-childrenoftheblood\" target=\"_blank\">https://booknest.eu/reviews/charles/...drenoftheblood</a>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Author of <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Cthulhu-Armageddon-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01KUOM7SI/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982844&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Cthulhu+Armageddon\" target=\"_blank\">Cthulhu Armageddon</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Teenage-Weredeer-Bright-Falls-Mysteries-ebook/dp/B075TTN2FN/ref=sr_1_2?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982717&amp;sr=1-2&amp;keywords=Weredeer#customerReviews\" target=\"_blank\">I was a Teenage Weredeer</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Straight-Outta-Fangton-Comedic-Vampire-ebook/dp/B01KNHICCC/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982774&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Straight+Outta+Fangton\" target=\"_blank\">Straight Outta Fangton</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Lucifers-Star-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01MDM9MCT/ref=mt_kindle?_encoding=UTF8&amp;me=&amp;qid=\" target=\"_blank\">Lucifer's Star</a>, </i>and the <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Rules-Supervillainy-Saga-Book-ebook/dp/B07MB89S33/\" target=\"_blank\">Supervillainy Saga</a>.</i><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":12002,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","user":"CTPhipps","date":". 04-12-2021, 11:27 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","name":"CTPhipps","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12002_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13933"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-04-12T08:55:35-07:00","id":1443601,"title":"","content":"I like both,and i believe each of them.have different strenghts","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4621-nicolas-milioni","name":"Nicolas Milioni","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4621_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3605"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-04-12T09:22:36-07:00","id":1443603,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Vamps Like Us</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">It gives them a reason to get out of bed and motivation to endanger themselves to play the game and go after what they want.</div> </div> </div> </div>Might aswell have the Obsession idea for a replacement for Touchstones just be a Mental Flaw instead at that point. And just have Touchstones by itself just be removed.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Jade Kingdom Warrior","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25523-shakanaka","name":"Shakanaka","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25523_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"951"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-04-12T09:46:39-07:00","id":1443607,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Shakanaka</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1443592-the-official-v5-vs-v20-thread?p=1443603#post1443603\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Might aswell have the Obsession idea for a replacement for Touchstones just be a Mental Flaw instead at that point. And just have Touchstones by itself just be removed.</div> </div> </div> </div>Touchstones for me are a thing that I believe could be improved but are also severely misunderstood. Basically, because I believe it is ANY mortal that the Vampire actually cares enough about to think about something other than BloodTM as their primary resource. If you care about your daughter, father, brother, lover, or slave then they are a Touchstone.<br /> <br /> It seems like a lot of gamers think it must be someone they're nightmarishly obsessed with or in love with.<br /> <br /> Any characters transferred with emotional mortal ties in V20 or before should have these added as Touchstones.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Author of <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Cthulhu-Armageddon-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01KUOM7SI/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982844&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Cthulhu+Armageddon\" target=\"_blank\">Cthulhu Armageddon</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Teenage-Weredeer-Bright-Falls-Mysteries-ebook/dp/B075TTN2FN/ref=sr_1_2?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982717&amp;sr=1-2&amp;keywords=Weredeer#customerReviews\" target=\"_blank\">I was a Teenage Weredeer</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Straight-Outta-Fangton-Comedic-Vampire-ebook/dp/B01KNHICCC/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982774&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Straight+Outta+Fangton\" target=\"_blank\">Straight Outta Fangton</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Lucifers-Star-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01MDM9MCT/ref=mt_kindle?_encoding=UTF8&amp;me=&amp;qid=\" target=\"_blank\">Lucifer's Star</a>, </i>and the <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Rules-Supervillainy-Saga-Book-ebook/dp/B07MB89S33/\" target=\"_blank\">Supervillainy Saga</a>.</i><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","name":"CTPhipps","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12002_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13933"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-04-12T09:54:42-07:00","id":1443608,"title":"","content":"i think V5 vs V20 is an ultimately pointless argument because they're clearly trying to be 2 different things, and the answer will ultimately be decided by preference. that being said, V5 is just not a good system, it just has to many problems.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":9}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25992-archderd","name":"archderd","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25992_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2020"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"205"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-04-12T13:09:56-07:00","id":1443636,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CTPhipps</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1443592-the-official-v5-vs-v20-thread?p=1443607#post1443607\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Basically, because I believe it is ANY mortal that the Vampire actually cares enough about to think about something other than BloodTM as their primary resource. If you care about your daughter, father, brother, lover, or slave then they are a Touchstone.</div> </div> </div> </div>While in theory they could be Touchstones (that's how VtR 2e does things), mechanically they aren't inherently Touchstones that matter to the Stains/Humanity system. For a Touchstone to matter mechanically, they have to represent a Conviction in the eyes of the vampire. Deep emotional connections to humans, by itself, doesn't do anything in V5.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> It seems like a lot of gamers think it must be someone they're nightmarishly obsessed with or in love with. </div> </div> </div>It's certainly hyperbole that's gotten worse in critical-of-V5 circles, but V5 didn't do itself any favors here. If you don't want your Touchstones slapping you with more Stains than the Conviction linked to them actually saves you from, you do have to really carefully manage your Touchstones; which translated to in-game actions is very hard to avoid looking like an obsessive and abusive thing.<br /> <br /> You risk gaining two Stains any time a V5 Touchstone does something that is significantly out of line with your idealized version of them in your head. So your choices are: not have Touchstones (getting rid of them is a pain, but once they're gone they're gone) but recovering from Aggravated WP damage is harder, rack up Stains as people get on with their lives without living just to be a symbol for you, or use your influence (mundane or supernatural) to force them into the role you need them to function as.<br /> <br /> So you can toss yourself to the Beast, or you can be an obsessive creep that controls people's lives to lock them into a static image of what you think they should be.<br /> <br /> It's not that this is an inherently bad conflict for a game to explore, but a lot of V20 and V5 fans alike really don't like how it's forced into the system the way it is. It feels, to me, that Touchstones are one of the aspects of V5 that's very quickly approaching &quot;so house ruled/Rule Zeroed/Golden Ruled/etc. that most players don't even realize they're playing a modified version of the rules,&quot; status. It's sort of like the assumption that if you're playing a d20 game, 1s are botches and 20s are crits. A lot of people assume this about d20 games and never bother checking to see if the rules are actually written that way because it's just gotten ingrained in people's minds that's how it works.<br /> <br /> ------------------------<br /> <br /> That all said, I'm largely in agreement with archderd. There really isn't a &quot;V20 vs. V5 debate.&quot; What people have really been arguing is &quot;change to V5 or stick with earlier books&quot; and V20 is just the most recent of the earlier books making it the most played of the pre-V5 editions at the moment.<br /> <br /> I don't know anyone that considers V20 to be some massive step up from Revised. It's great for compiling a lot of late 2e/Revied material into a much smaller package than all those supplements, and has a few nice changes here and there (and some inexplicable ones), but it's the nostalgia omnibus edition it was always meant to be. If polled a many &quot;sticking with V20 over V5&quot; folks as possible with the question of, &quot;would you like a new edition of VtM that advances the metaplot into the 21st century, and involves a major rules overhaul to improve on all the issues of classic VtM?&quot; I'm confident you'd easily get 90% or more responding enthusiastically with &quot;Yes!&quot;<br /> <br /> When Onyx Path announced what they were calling VtM 4th Edition (not seeing 20th as a proper edition), the vast majority of the response was excitement over the potential for what a real change up was going to look like. All the acrimony on the &quot;sticking with V20 side,&quot; is that V5 didn't live up to what we wanted to see out of that. Hence we didn't change over to V5.<br /> <br /> --------------------<br /> <br /> I don't want to beat a dead horse, but I also think one of the biggest issues is how rushed V5 was by nWW because they got it stuck in their heads that they had to get V5 out for GenCon that year. It's painfully obvious V5 needed more development; and perhaps a lead that wasn't as stubborn as Martin (it felt like a lot of the designers lower on the ladder were more open to some of the feedback during the public playtests, but a lot of that feedback was ignored by the time V5 was put out, and it's hard not to see Martin as the guy that made that decision) who clearly had a few ideas he wanted in the game no matter what.<br /> <br /> CT's point about V5 vs. OPP V5 illustrates this a lot to me because V5 has a lot of potential in my eyes, but constantly shoots itself in the foot. Almost everything listed in what makes V5 Chicago and Cult of the Blood Gods such improvements to V5 are things nWW got direct feedback about during the playtest in exactly those directions. It wasn't stuff &quot;fixed&quot; in hindsight, it was stuff that needed to get fixed because the wrong people were in-charge of V5 (not that it had to be Onyx Path, since plenty of us fans spotted the same things).<br /> <br /> V5 is as frustrating and divisive as it is, partially because to a lot of us it was so close to being what we wanted when Eddy and Rich announced their idea for a new edition, and so many of the spots that are deal breakers are things that we've been highlighting since the first public alpha.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":16}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-04-12T13:15:28-07:00","id":1443638,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Heavy Arms</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1443592-the-official-v5-vs-v20-thread?p=1443636#post1443636\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> While in theory they could be Touchstones (that's how VtR 2e does things), mechanically they aren't inherently Touchstones that matter to the Stains/Humanity system. For a Touchstone to matter mechanically, they have to represent a Conviction in the eyes of the vampire. Deep emotional connections to humans, by itself, doesn't do anything in V5.</div> </div> </div> </div>True but I think Convictions aren't really meant to be as complicated either.<br /> <br /> To use a simple example:<br /> <br /> &quot;I care about Loretta the Bartender a lot.&quot;<br /> <br /> Touchstone: Loretta the Bartender<br /> <br /> Conviction: &quot;Do not let anyone harm my friends.&quot;<br /> <br /> Loretta doesn't have to represent your hidden communist sympathies. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /> Sort of like Chronicle Tenets doesn't have to be more complex than, &quot;Don't kill innocent people.&quot;<br /> <br /> This also means that the Touchstone &quot;damage&quot; would primarily come from her stopping being your friend. I admit, this is badly explained. There's some definite attempts to make PCs into the Phantom of the Opera and not everyone will want to be even remotely like that.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Author of <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Cthulhu-Armageddon-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01KUOM7SI/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982844&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Cthulhu+Armageddon\" target=\"_blank\">Cthulhu Armageddon</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Teenage-Weredeer-Bright-Falls-Mysteries-ebook/dp/B075TTN2FN/ref=sr_1_2?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982717&amp;sr=1-2&amp;keywords=Weredeer#customerReviews\" target=\"_blank\">I was a Teenage Weredeer</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Straight-Outta-Fangton-Comedic-Vampire-ebook/dp/B01KNHICCC/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982774&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Straight+Outta+Fangton\" target=\"_blank\">Straight Outta Fangton</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Lucifers-Star-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01MDM9MCT/ref=mt_kindle?_encoding=UTF8&amp;me=&amp;qid=\" target=\"_blank\">Lucifer's Star</a>, </i>and the <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Rules-Supervillainy-Saga-Book-ebook/dp/B07MB89S33/\" target=\"_blank\">Supervillainy Saga</a>.</i><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":12002,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","user":"CTPhipps","date":". 04-12-2021, 04:19 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","name":"CTPhipps","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12002_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13933"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-04-12T14:06:43-07:00","id":1443647,"title":"","content":"I'm not sure what &quot;as complicated&quot; means there.<br /> <br /> The big thing missing from your example is why Loretta represents &quot;Do not let anyone harm my friends&quot; to the vampire, so the ST can judge actions Loretta takes as possibly ones that damage her as a Touchstone.<br /> <br /> The big problem coming from V5, is that it directly says STs should insert things like, &quot;it turns out Loretta, your friend, is secretly self-harming to deal with stress, she now counts as a Damaged Touchstone until she gets treatment, also have +2 Stains,&quot; or, &quot;Loretta's dating one of your mortal friends, and you found out she's cheating on them, what's that you failed your frenzy check as your friend confides that news in you? OK you kill him in your Frenzy, take +3 Stains, and she's a Damaged Touchstone so take +2 more Stains, how do you plan to make sure she doesn't hurt one of your friends again so heal her status as a Touchstone?&quot;<br /> <br /> The book telling us that STs are supposed to use Touchstones like that is a primary driving in people turning their vampires into controlling creeps as a way to shield against it.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":9}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-04-12T14:31:58-07:00","id":1443649,"title":"","content":"<a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar617_2.jpeg');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"617\" data-vbnamecard=\"617\">Heavy Arms</a> <br /> \u200b<br /> That's a lot to quote, but as someone who seems to like to discuss mechanics, do you think there is a way for V5 to fix the problems without putting out a new core edition, thus being V6? Can you see a way forward where a hefty rules supplement say fee to download with future printing saying 5.5 could fix all the problems that were rushed out or is it too much to make changes so fundamental without voiding the core book people spent money on?<br /> <br /> Do you think it's possible to get a more classic feel that some of us wanted? Or would fixing the rushed out problems be too much of a move away from what V5 is for those that like it? I ask as someone who flipped through it, watched a youtube play session, and read about it but never played or read it cover to cover.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24221-vamps-like-us","name":"Vamps Like Us","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"390"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-04-12T14:55:41-07:00","id":1443652,"title":"","content":"What I really like on V5 is, that it brought new wind to the setting. I think the new Metaplot is really something that has potential. It is really something that I think is long overdue.<br /> MY problem with it is it whas to abrupt. Like they really tried with V5 to make a generation change to let all this veterans behind and target mainly new people and for them hastly create a timeline about what happened in the shadows when they grow up. I mean the biggest flaw seen is blaming ISIS for Vienna that whas big during time it whas wrote but more like a small unknown gang to time it should have attacked vienna. But how they would have made it better is I think already discussed on the other threads.<br /> What I really like on the german side is, that FINALLY a long misstranslation whas corrected because Ulisses felt with the target consumer base has been big enough changed they can finally translate Kindred more to its meaning and not as Kainskind (in english Caines Children).<br /> I think the blood potency and hunger mechanic are interessting and could have either been for an alternative ruleset or a flaw.<br /> <br /> Now what I do not like<br /> I REALLY do not like the new humanity and touchpointsystem. The touchpointsystem is more like a Bane instead of a Boon and only enforces people to be more loner then they are already.<br /> From my opinion Humanitysystem would have had been enough if they sad, killing and hurting in self defense is not hurting humanity. Mayby with the optional rule that if you kill in self defense you need to make a remorse roll that if you fail you have for like W6 nights a reduced willpower or something.<br /> What I do not like either is the new disciple system.<br /> For the rest of the generall gameplay I can not really say anything because I whas so fed up with V5 rules already, that I did not read because I felt like it is easier to continue using V20 than making V5 to likeability.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>As I am from Austria I need to clarify two things.<br /> First my native language is german and so please point out if the english I write is broken so I can improve.<br /> Second I do not own VTMV beyond first three books nor any line after M20 Corebook because it is not out there and I wait for the translation.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":8}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26160-koronus","name":"Koronus","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2020"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"366"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-04-12T15:02:44-07:00","id":1443654,"title":"","content":"For me the best part of V20 is the lore, that I feel goes from 1991 to 2000ish. Yes I have a tendency to think Theo Bell either does not kill Hardestadt or is himself dead too, but that's just my feel for how it would go down, and I ignore the mass slaughter in general that only occured because the line was ending, while feeling based on upper power level much of the history could never occur in the V5 universe, so it has much less meta plot and history than V20. Novels have characters that could never do what was done in the books just by the elder changes.<br /> <br /> I think Second Edition to Revised is an example of it being easier to add power than take it away if you had players attached to certain things on their sheet or certain character concepts.<br /> <br /> I think V20 does a much better job for higher end city games like London or Chicago. Even lesser cities with more reasonable elders than 4th gen gods are more controlled and interesting in v20.<br /> <br /> With all the changes in power levels and lore and game mechanics I wish they would have fixed the Sabbat and Independent clans into the Camarilla like they are in the Sabbat and just said they were always there. I'd have made Ravnos and Tzimisce and the rest not shocking at all to be in a Camarilla city. They changed so much even adding Ministry, Banu Haqim, and Lasombra why stop short.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":6}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24221-vamps-like-us","name":"Vamps Like Us","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"390"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-04-12T15:10:02-07:00","id":1443657,"title":"","content":"I have an absolutely massive investment in VtM products. Getting me to switch over would take something truly extraordinary. Mind, I did say that about V20 too, though. Since I am a massive Noddist fan, things like the<i> Lores </i>and <i>Becketts Jyhad Diary</i> pulled me in. Although the Brujah sections disappointed. But I am not seeing anything like Beckett's diary here.<br /> <br /> The Bad:<ul><li>I don't like the art and presentation. Very subjective opinion there. It reminds me of the change from the old Vampire cards to the new &quot;webpage&quot; looking ones.</li> <li>Several metaplot developments are deal-breakers to me. Brujah leaving the Camarilla, and the whole Hecatea mess in particular. Fall of Vienna. Stuff like the last two ruins my sense of internal plausibility and suspension of disbelief.</li> <li>Lack of elders and elder powers.</li> </ul><br /> <br /> The good<ul><li>I like the idea of some clan curses like the Lasombra getting worse over time.</li> <li>Touchstones are a concept I'll back-port for some types of games. The mechanics would be totally changed, but I feel the concept is strong.</li> <li>The fiction is very high quality. I've borrowed books from friends just to enjoy it.</li> </ul><br /> <br /> The neutral<ul><li>The Second Inquisition seems a natural outgrowth of increased kine handheld media capacity. I don't really buy the learning curve they've had though.</li> </ul><br /> <br /> The short version is, V5 wants you to play a very specific sort of game and is not an asset if you want any other sort of game. In fact it would be detrimental compared to previous versions of the game that can do more things. And it has a laser-like focus on the whole anarch, anarch versus Camarilla sort of games we were totally played out on by the mid-90s. It feels like it could have been a softback alternate setting for the people who want those games.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":2471,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2471-trollroot","user":"Trollroot","date":". 04-12-2021, 06:15 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2471-trollroot","name":"Trollroot","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"311"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-04-12T15:23:04-07:00","id":1443661,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Trollroot</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1443592-the-official-v5-vs-v20-thread?p=1443657#post1443657\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">And it has a laser-like focus on the whole anarch, anarch versus Camarilla sort of games we were totally played out on by the mid-90s.</div> </div> </div> </div>Weird, because I felt the whole Sabbat vs. Camarilla thing totally spoiled the Anarch vs. Camarilla thing. They removed the central conflict of the setting. Old vs. Young vampires and replaced it with Good Vampires vs. Bad Ones.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Author of <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Cthulhu-Armageddon-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01KUOM7SI/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982844&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Cthulhu+Armageddon\" target=\"_blank\">Cthulhu Armageddon</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Teenage-Weredeer-Bright-Falls-Mysteries-ebook/dp/B075TTN2FN/ref=sr_1_2?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982717&amp;sr=1-2&amp;keywords=Weredeer#customerReviews\" target=\"_blank\">I was a Teenage Weredeer</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Straight-Outta-Fangton-Comedic-Vampire-ebook/dp/B01KNHICCC/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982774&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Straight+Outta+Fangton\" target=\"_blank\">Straight Outta Fangton</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Lucifers-Star-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01MDM9MCT/ref=mt_kindle?_encoding=UTF8&amp;me=&amp;qid=\" target=\"_blank\">Lucifer's Star</a>, </i>and the <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Rules-Supervillainy-Saga-Book-ebook/dp/B07MB89S33/\" target=\"_blank\">Supervillainy Saga</a>.</i><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","name":"CTPhipps","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12002_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13933"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-04-12T15:23:58-07:00","id":1443662,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Vamps Like Us</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1443592-the-official-v5-vs-v20-thread?p=1443649#post1443649\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">That's a lot to quote, but as someone who seems to like to discuss mechanics, do you think there is a way for V5 to fix the problems without putting out a new core edition, thus being V6?</div> </div> </div> </div>Oh, I can go on, and on, and on about the lore side of things too. My focus on the mechanics is that there's more objective facts about them to discuss in a neutral fashion. I have written massive posts about why the attack on the Vienna Chantry as written is wildly suspension of disbelief breaking for me, point out dozens of factors, write paragraphs about how to account for the WoD vs. our world, and so on. But in the end, lots of people like the fall of the Pyramid and are willing to overlook any iffy bits in the execution just as I've come to terms with plenty of meh parts of the metaplot in previous editions.<br /> <br /> To the question? Whether you want to call it 5.5 or 6, I don't think so. While some of the changes I would make are simple, and others would have to be extensive, I would estimate a need to revise ~80% of the rules on some level. If your errata starts getting to be 5% the length of the book or more... it's time to consider a new core book. The only reason I think you could get away with V5.5 is that there aren't that many V5 books, and most of the supplements aren't that mechanics heavy so they could remain useful with minimal to no errata (though there's some non-rules stuff I'd want to redo if I were in charge.... looking at you Cam V5).<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Do you think it's possible to get a more classic feel that some of us wanted? </div> </div> </div>I think it depends on what you mean by &quot;classic feel.&quot; I think there's a lot of potential in changes that aren't at all &quot;classic&quot; VtM. The idea of having both a Clan Bane and a Clan Compulsion for example is a novel inclusion in V5. In general, I think the Banes are a step up esp. the Severity concept. The Compulsions are great as an idea, but the execution leaves a lot to be desired, and are very responsible for some bad classic feels (ex: the Ravnos Compulsion completely destroys the attempt to salvage them from their racist beginnings).<br /> <br /> A new edition with a new feel is a good thing!<br /> <br /> I think the balance act V5 failed at, was bridging the editions. While V5 doesn't have to be mechanically backwards compatible with pre-V5, it should have been more conceptually so. As I've said elsewhere, there are concepts that make perfect sense in the previous editions that are hampered (if not outright denied if the concept is heavily focused on supernatural stuff) by the system. What I feel is important here is that if V5 says, &quot;you can't play X out of the box any more,&quot; I need a compelling reason. Axing some of the racism hardboiled into some of the old stuff? Valid. Because you want the list of Disciplines to be shorter (even if they're getting bloated as new books at new powers too them anyway), or you want the new spiffy Hunger mechanics to make my character's undeath unbearable because they do something that involves a lot of rolling? Yeah, no thanks.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Or would fixing the rushed out problems be too much of a move away from what V5 is for those that like it? I ask as someone who flipped through it, watched a youtube play session, and read about it but never played or read it cover to cover. </div> </div> </div>I can't really speak for the V5 fans. I know there are rules changes I would make which I've suggested in various places that some V5 fans have loved and say they've adopted as house rules, others that V5 fans generally say that they're ambivalent towards and they wouldn't care either way, and some that are extremely divided in reactions.<br /> <br /> I think that balancing act is possible, but I'm biased in a fashion that means I'm not qualified to do it.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":6}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-04-12T15:24:34-07:00","id":1443663,"title":"","content":"I haven\u2019t tried V5 yet so I\u2019m much more familiar with V20 but it sounds like a cool game and I\u2019m willing to switch over if that\u2019s what my group decides to do. I did buy Fall of London and thought both the adventure and the metaplot stuff were pretty cool. I also read Anarchs and I thought it did a pretty good job of conveying the mood of a 2020s Anarchs game.<br /> <br /> As long as I\u2019m here, how much info is there on the Ashirra in V5? One of my friends is thinking about playing an Ashirra if we ever run V5 and she was wondering what the Camarilla book said about them.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"","name":"Guest","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/default/default_avatar_large.png","title":"","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-04-12T15:33:59-07:00","id":1443665,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CTPhipps</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1443592-the-official-v5-vs-v20-thread?p=1443661#post1443661\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Weird, because I felt the whole Sabbat vs. Camarilla thing totally spoiled the Anarch vs. Camarilla thing. They removed the central conflict of the setting. Old vs. Young vampires and replaced it with Good Vampires vs. Bad Ones.</div> </div> </div> </div>We did young vs. old for a few years. Maybe it was coincidence that we did it when we were young. Then we did other games. In the end, we ended up more into immersing ourselves in the alien culture of the predatory Kindred. But I've known people who have played Sumerian city-states setting, ancient Rome, elders through the centuries of the medieval nights up through the age of steam, revenants in 18th century Innsmouth, kindred pirates in the Caribbean, etc, etc. I see the older editions toolkits as far more useful for things like that than V5.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":7}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2471-trollroot","name":"Trollroot","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"311"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-04-12T17:10:57-07:00","id":1443675,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CTPhipps</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1443592-the-official-v5-vs-v20-thread?p=1443661#post1443661\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Weird, because I felt the whole Sabbat vs. Camarilla thing totally spoiled the Anarch vs. Camarilla thing. They removed the central conflict of the setting. Old vs. Young vampires and replaced it with Good Vampires vs. Bad Ones.</div> </div> </div> </div>I think this phrasing is difficult for the conversation because it's far too black and white for what either conflict is about.<br /> <br /> Let's remember that Smiling Jack, the strongest of the Anarchs in Bloodlines 1, is ~200 years older than LaCroix, Camarilla Prince. And lots of people cite Bloodlines 1 as returning to the Anarchs vs. Camarilla state of VtM despite being made far later in the original VtM run. People side with the Anarchs a lot because Nines, Jack, and Damsel are clearly &quot;good&quot; vampires, while LaCroix and the Sheriff are obviously &quot;bad,&quot; and a few others are &quot;bad&quot; if you poke beyond their better PR.<br /> <br /> The Sabbat and Camarilla have, as a major part of their conflict, the threat of ancient vampire blood-gods as an issue: the Sabbat considers them active existential threats, while the Camarilla don't think they matter if they're even out there any more. It's all about Young vs. Old, just on a scale of millennia instead of centuries.<br /> <br /> The Sabbat (at least in Revised) can make a great case that they're &quot;bad&quot; by human standards, but as they're not humans any more, they're &quot;good&quot; by vampire standards. The Camarilla struggles to really make a great argument on either side of that.<br /> <br /> I think it's more important to acknowledge what I've said, and what Trollroot is saying: being overly focused on one narrative isn't great for VtM. &quot;Young&quot; punk Anarchs vs. the stodgy old Camarilla was a great and evocative start for the game, but the game grew to be more, and it's better for before more.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Penelope</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1443592-the-official-v5-vs-v20-thread?p=1443663#post1443663\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">As long as I\u2019m here, how much info is there on the Ashirra in V5? One of my friends is thinking about playing an Ashirra if we ever run V5 and she was wondering what the Camarilla book said about them.</div> </div> </div> </div>Not really enough to know how to play it. But I don't think it really conflicts with any of the previous sources on them, so if you're willing to grab those source books, you shouldn't really have a problem making a member of the Ashirra that's accurate to the setting.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":7}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-04-12T17:20:44-07:00","id":1443676,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Trollroot</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1443592-the-official-v5-vs-v20-thread?p=1443665#post1443665\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> We did young vs. old for a few years. Maybe it was coincidence that we did it when we were young. Then we did other games. In the end, we ended up more into immersing ourselves in the alien culture of the predatory Kindred. But I've known people who have played Sumerian city-states setting, ancient Rome, elders through the centuries of the medieval nights up through the age of steam, revenants in 18th century Innsmouth, kindred pirates in the Caribbean, etc, etc. I see the older editions toolkits as far more useful for things like that than V5.</div> </div> </div> </div>EH, I agree it's good for the game to expand outwards but the plotline of the Sabbat was designed to SUPPLANT the previous ones.<br /> <br /> It's why the Anarch Free States were destroyed by the Kuei-Jin.<br /> <br /> They thought the Anarchs whole &quot;freedom, chaos!&quot; thing was filled by the Sabbat so they tried to write them out.<br /> <br /> I felt that was a bad storytelling move, especially since making the Kuei-Jin the new big bad to slay was...in poor taste. I don't know if they're coming back for V5 but I wouldn't be too unhappy if they didn't.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Author of <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Cthulhu-Armageddon-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01KUOM7SI/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982844&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Cthulhu+Armageddon\" target=\"_blank\">Cthulhu Armageddon</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Teenage-Weredeer-Bright-Falls-Mysteries-ebook/dp/B075TTN2FN/ref=sr_1_2?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982717&amp;sr=1-2&amp;keywords=Weredeer#customerReviews\" target=\"_blank\">I was a Teenage Weredeer</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Straight-Outta-Fangton-Comedic-Vampire-ebook/dp/B01KNHICCC/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982774&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Straight+Outta+Fangton\" target=\"_blank\">Straight Outta Fangton</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Lucifers-Star-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01MDM9MCT/ref=mt_kindle?_encoding=UTF8&amp;me=&amp;qid=\" target=\"_blank\">Lucifer's Star</a>, </i>and the <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Rules-Supervillainy-Saga-Book-ebook/dp/B07MB89S33/\" target=\"_blank\">Supervillainy Saga</a>.</i><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","name":"CTPhipps","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12002_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13933"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-04-12T17:38:07-07:00","id":1443678,"title":"","content":"It's kinda strange to say that the Anarch Free States were destroyed so the Sabbat could supplant the Anarchs... while also acknowledging that the Free States were destroyed so the KotE could have a permanent foothold in the US as a new faction to combat. All of which happened well after the Sabbat were being shifted towards the major antagonists of the Camarilla (though they were always supposed to be significant enemies even way back in 1e).<br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":6}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-04-12T17:44:58-07:00","id":1443679,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Heavy Arms</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1443592-the-official-v5-vs-v20-thread?p=1443678#post1443678\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">It's kinda strange to say that the Anarch Free States were destroyed so the Sabbat could supplant the Anarchs... while also acknowledging that the Free States were destroyed so the KotE could have a permanent foothold in the US as a new faction to combat. All of which happened well after the Sabbat were being shifted towards the major antagonists of the Camarilla (though they were always supposed to be significant enemies even way back in 1e).<br /></div> </div> </div> </div>I'm combining the Anarchs being slowly written out as one long series of events.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Author of <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Cthulhu-Armageddon-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01KUOM7SI/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982844&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Cthulhu+Armageddon\" target=\"_blank\">Cthulhu Armageddon</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Teenage-Weredeer-Bright-Falls-Mysteries-ebook/dp/B075TTN2FN/ref=sr_1_2?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982717&amp;sr=1-2&amp;keywords=Weredeer#customerReviews\" target=\"_blank\">I was a Teenage Weredeer</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Straight-Outta-Fangton-Comedic-Vampire-ebook/dp/B01KNHICCC/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982774&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Straight+Outta+Fangton\" target=\"_blank\">Straight Outta Fangton</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Lucifers-Star-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01MDM9MCT/ref=mt_kindle?_encoding=UTF8&amp;me=&amp;qid=\" target=\"_blank\">Lucifer's Star</a>, </i>and the <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Rules-Supervillainy-Saga-Book-ebook/dp/B07MB89S33/\" target=\"_blank\">Supervillainy Saga</a>.</i><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","name":"CTPhipps","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12002_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13933"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-04-13T05:59:20-07:00","id":1443732,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Vamps Like Us</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1443592-the-official-v5-vs-v20-thread?p=1443654#post1443654\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">For me the best part of V20 is the lore, that I feel goes from 1991 to 2000ish. Yes I have a tendency to think Theo Bell either does not kill Hardestadt or is himself dead too, but that's just my feel for how it would go down, and I ignore the mass slaughter in general that only occured because the line was ending, while feeling based on upper power level much of the history could never occur in the V5 universe, so it has much less meta plot and history than V20. Novels have characters that could never do what was done in the books just by the elder changes.<br /> <br /> I think Second Edition to Revised is an example of it being easier to add power than take it away if you had players attached to certain things on their sheet or certain character concepts.<br /> <br /> I think V20 does a much better job for higher end city games like London or Chicago. Even lesser cities with more reasonable elders than 4th gen gods are more controlled and interesting in v20.<br /> <br /> With all the changes in power levels and lore and game mechanics I wish they would have fixed the Sabbat and Independent clans into the Camarilla like they are in the Sabbat and just said they were always there. I'd have made Ravnos and Tzimisce and the rest not shocking at all to be in a Camarilla city. They changed so much even adding Ministry, Banu Haqim, and Lasombra why stop short.</div> </div> </div> </div>Actually in the later V20 Books lore goes to 2015.<br /> One of the reason I critize the Metaplot being rashed and forced. I think it would have been better if they mayby just said the Camerilla did put the Sabbat on the NSA list but nearly two decades later it is shown how foolish the idea whas because all the secret agencies have during ISIS decided it whas time to put all this well planed and carefully prepared effort into action and so took during all this islam terror care of the vampires and until 2015 the metaplot is more calm like some local things happened but nothing really world moving but more of a warning signs before the desaster came into happen.<br /> Would be way better then let us long term fans feel like we just woke up from a two decade long torpor.<br /> I think they think all the V20 lovers are used to play without (an official) metaplot so they could use the time to get wild for new fans that have no idea from what happened before and so would not care that nearly two decades of real time just get a metaplot like this or find it even better to have such rich instead of a small story where nothing really happens.<br /> Mayby it would have been really better if all those new fans get instead of a fifth edition a honest reboot but mayby that would have sold not so well.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>As I am from Austria I need to clarify two things.<br /> First my native language is german and so please point out if the english I write is broken so I can improve.<br /> Second I do not own VTMV beyond first three books nor any line after M20 Corebook because it is not out there and I wait for the translation.","edited":{"userid":26160,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26160-koronus","user":"Koronus","date":". 04-13-2021, 09:04 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26160-koronus","name":"Koronus","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2020"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"366"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-04-13T09:07:33-07:00","id":1443751,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Koronus</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1443592-the-official-v5-vs-v20-thread?p=1443732#post1443732\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Actually in the later V20 Books lore goes to 2015.</div> </div> </div> </div>Ehhh.<br /> <br /> Yes and no. Beckett's Jyhad Diary leads it up to 2015 but it was also written with a lead-in to 5th Edition--which was very professional of OPP.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Koronus</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1443592-the-official-v5-vs-v20-thread?p=1443732#post1443732\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Mayby it would have been really better if all those new fans get instead of a fifth edition a honest reboot but mayby that would have sold not so well.</div> </div> </div> </div>V5 is like V20 in that it was a &quot;deboot&quot; of Requiem.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Author of <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Cthulhu-Armageddon-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01KUOM7SI/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982844&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Cthulhu+Armageddon\" target=\"_blank\">Cthulhu Armageddon</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Teenage-Weredeer-Bright-Falls-Mysteries-ebook/dp/B075TTN2FN/ref=sr_1_2?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982717&amp;sr=1-2&amp;keywords=Weredeer#customerReviews\" target=\"_blank\">I was a Teenage Weredeer</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Straight-Outta-Fangton-Comedic-Vampire-ebook/dp/B01KNHICCC/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982774&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Straight+Outta+Fangton\" target=\"_blank\">Straight Outta Fangton</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Lucifers-Star-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01MDM9MCT/ref=mt_kindle?_encoding=UTF8&amp;me=&amp;qid=\" target=\"_blank\">Lucifer's Star</a>, </i>and the <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Rules-Supervillainy-Saga-Book-ebook/dp/B07MB89S33/\" target=\"_blank\">Supervillainy Saga</a>.</i><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":12002,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","user":"CTPhipps","date":". 04-13-2021, 12:10 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","name":"CTPhipps","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12002_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13933"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-04-13T09:54:25-07:00","id":1443753,"title":"","content":"I greatly prefer the V20 mechanics... V5 goes far too abstract for my tastes and veers in places towards trying to be a narrative in real time (which can drag you out of character as you have to resolve aspects not from your character\u2019s viewpoint, but from what is best for the narrative) vs. being played as events experienced by your PCs that can later be recounted in story form.<br /> <br /> I\u2019m also not a fan of the rearranging of disciplines; particularly turning the straight-forward physical disciplines and turning them into grab bags of powers that often leave gaping holes; ex. Potence 1 in V20 gives you all the benefits of an extra dot of Strength; lift more, jump further, punch harder, etc. and a boost when you spend blood on it. In V5 you either deal more damage to mortals (but not objects or vampires) or jump a very specific distance (which is quite odd given how utterly non-specific the resolutions of other physical tasks are... it also takes no account of basic strength and so unless you have multiple ranks of Potence it ends up being significantly less than just a non-boosted Str+Athletics check could achieve in V20 (5 successes on a a difficulty 3 check will achieve results equal to that V5 Potence 1 power).<br /> <br /> The less I say about V5 Touchstones and Humanity the better; suffice it to say I much prefer the internalized Virtues to requiring your beliefs be dependent on mortal morality pets the GM is encouraged to screw with and because they must be unchanging you are punished for not being a creepy control freak stalker.<br /> <br /> Similarly, there\u2019s no backstop on Humanity loss in V5. It takes real work at depravity to sink below a 4 in V20 (or any of the previous versions... which I think is ultimately what people mean by V20, at least that\u2019s what I mean by it).<br /> <br /> I\u2019m also not a fan of Rouse Checks/Hunger dice over the V20 blood pool; particularly the change where the ONLY way to ever be fully satiated in V5 requires you to murder your victim. Drink a pint of blood off a hundred people and you\u2019re still hungry (instead of bloated like a tick)... kill one person by drinking five to eight pints and you\u2019re full.<br /> <br /> To be blunt, in V5 you don\u2019t actually feed on blood, you feed on murder with blood as an inferior substitute. The only way to ever be fully in control is to be a cold blooded murderer with morality pets to give you the conviction that you\u2019re not actually so bad after all as you micromanage their lives so they remain stuck instead of being able to grow and change like healthy human beings do.<br /> <br /> My general feeling is that Humanity in V5 should be renamed \u201cDelusion\u201d as high Humanity doesn\u2019t actually make you more moral since murdering and manipulating are required to maintain that state... it\u2019s just how good you are at lying to yourself.<br /> <br /> Contrast the humane vampire of previous editions who can be fully satiated by animal blood, blood bags or small sips from volunteers (and because you can keep yourself \u201ctopped off\u201d there is little to no danger of ripping their throat out) and who can allow the humans they care about to grow, change and experience full lives because their morality isn\u2019t dependent on others telling them they\u2019re a good person every time they experience a setback (i.e. take aggravated willpower damage or suffer a stain).<br /> <br /> High Humanity in V20 and before actually meant being humane; not hurting people or stealing from them and feeling remorse and a desire to repent when you did screw up.<br /> <br /> About the only mechanical bits I can appreciate are the better attribute spread (just as I find the CoD spread of power, precision and resistance superior), making Willpower entirely into points instead of also being a dice pool to resist certain actions, and decoupling Generation from the point buy of character creation.<br /> <br /> The latter I\u2019ve even made a house-rule version of for V20 where Gen 8-16 are all trade-offs of raw power vs. fewer weaknesses that are roughly equivalent. Gen 7 or less still break that curve so there remains an incentive to diablerize your way up, but in terms of PC creation your Generation is now an independent choice instead of something to take up background dots.<br /> <br /> I also liked a few individual discipline powers and ported those over to V20.<br /> <br /> Now, one thing I DO like about V5 are the metaplot elements; though with the caveat that they work FAR better as events players are experiencing now instead of ones that happened 5-15 years earlier. <br /> <br /> For example; I just dropped the destruction of the Vienna Chantry into my chronicle. All the factions are in turmoil over who might really be behind it (and what this means in terms of favors owed by and to the Tremere). The Tremere Primogen (and head of the local Chantry) hasn\u2019t been seen since a week before news of the attack hit and the Whip and next in line for head of the local chantry aren\u2019t actually the same vampire.<br /> <br /> Just before the dust settles on that I\u2019ll be dropping news of the Scouring of London onto the weekly gathering in Elysium. Vienna is happenstance, London is coincidence... now the NPCs will be bracing for confirmation of enemy action.<br /> <br /> The PCs haven\u2019t encountered it yet, but when they actually follow through on their plans to take out the Sabbat Pack in the satellite tourist trap town to claim the territory as their own (thus side-stepping the local Prince) they\u2019ll learn the Pack has been essentially abandoned by the Sabbat hierarchy who\u2019ve gone off to the Middle East to fight and shortly after that some (not all) of the Elders will start to feel the Beckoning to the Middle East as well to build the creepiness of the event.<br /> <br /> I\u2019ve got basically the entire V5 metaplot on an accelerated timeline for my chronicle and how each of the local vampires NPCs are likely to react to each one as they come. Playing out the effects of all V5\u2019s backstory events is just far more compelling than reading of them in the past tense.<br /> <br /> V5 has some interesting ideas, and the older system did need SOME cleanup (particularly the combat engine), but V5 feels a LOT like the same sort of over-correction that D&amp;D 4E was, including the shift towards more narrative-based rules, extreme streamlining of certain mechanics, and \u201cvideo-gamey\u201d changes to the powers and abilities.<br /> <br /> I do think there\u2019s a middle ground to be found where probably 90% of both the V20/R/2e/1e and V5 players would be satisfied. But it will almost certainly take a D&amp;D 5e-like compromise edition to actually get there as V5 has far too many assumptions built into its mechanics to serve as the compromise foundation.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":8}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1328-chris24601","name":"Chris24601","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"520"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-04-13T10:12:32-07:00","id":1443754,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Chris24601</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1443592-the-official-v5-vs-v20-thread?p=1443753#post1443753\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The less I say about V5 Touchstones and Humanity the better; suffice it to say I much prefer the internalized Virtues to requiring your beliefs be dependent on mortal morality pets the GM is encouraged to screw with and because they must be unchanging you are punished for not being a creepy control freak stalker.</div> </div> </div> </div>That seems like it's reading too much into it. A Touchstone gets damaged if they change too much but what if your Conviction from them is, &quot;They are a good person.&quot; Also, &quot;person I love&quot; will only be hit if they stop loving you back. It would only be damaged if they become bad. Touchstones CAN be very creepy and disturbing but they don't necessarily have to be. I think the writers of V5 wanted to make sure that any of the Humanity system COULD be run for horror but doesn't have to be.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Similarly, there\u2019s no backstop on Humanity loss in V5. It takes real work at depravity to sink below a 4 in V20 (or any of the previous versions... which I think is ultimately what people mean by V20, at least that\u2019s what I mean by it). </div> </div> </div>The previous versions had you lose Humanity at 1 if you killed anyone, even in self-defense. The system was terribly broken and V20 was a major change that I approved of. V5 allows you a lot more freedom than even V20.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> I\u2019m also not a fan of Rouse Checks/Hunger dice over the V20 blood pool; particularly the change where the ONLY way to ever be fully satiated in V5 requires you to murder your victim. Drink a pint of blood off a hundred people and you\u2019re still hungry (instead of bloated like a tick)... kill one person by drinking five to eight pints and you\u2019re full. </div> </div> </div>Yes, I feel like that is much more effective for establishing horror. Still, rules wise, Hunger 1 is nothing.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> To be blunt, in V5 you don\u2019t actually feed on blood, you feed on murder with blood as an inferior substitute. The only way to ever be fully in control is to be a cold blooded murderer with morality pets to give you the conviction that you\u2019re not actually so bad after all as you micromanage their lives so they remain stuck instead of being able to grow and change like healthy human beings do. </div> </div> </div>Yep. It's great if you want vampire to be a monster rather than being just a superpower that you can manage with ethical consumption (hehe) of blood. That's just me, though.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> My general feeling is that Humanity in V5 should be renamed \u201cDelusion\u201d as high Humanity doesn\u2019t actually make you more moral since murdering and manipulating are required to maintain that state... it\u2019s just how good you are at lying to yourself. </div> </div> </div>It's definitely a stronger and more thematically interesting take on the subject. Humanity is now a Masquerade as a human to keep you from being overwhelmed by a genuinely terrifying curse.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Contrast the humane vampire of previous editions who can be fully satiated by animal blood, blood bags or small sips from volunteers (and because you can keep yourself \u201ctopped off\u201d there is little to no danger of ripping their throat out) and who can allow the humans they care about to grow, change and experience full lives because their morality isn\u2019t dependent on others telling them they\u2019re a good person every time they experience a setback (i.e. take aggravated willpower damage or suffer a stain). </div> </div> </div>Yep, easily a powerful and awesome twist that gives you a reason for wanting to play High Generation vampires. Feeding is actually interesting now because you have to really work to manage it in a way that is less dangerous to humans. Previously, everyone would want to get lower and lower in generation. Now, there's an actual reason to want to play Thin Bloods if you want to be a &quot;moral&quot; vampire or even 13th and 12th generation just so you can get subsistence on Blood Bags or Animal blood.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> High Humanity in V20 and before actually meant being humane; not hurting people or stealing from them and feeling remorse and a desire to repent when you did screw up. </div> </div> </div>Humanity has been combined with Paths so really it represents how your ethics or moral values (whatever they may be) can be defined by the players as well as chronicies. You can do action focused ones, alien morality ones, or values dissonance.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Now, one thing I DO like about V5 are the metaplot elements; though with the caveat that they work FAR better as events players are experiencing now instead of ones that happened 5-15 years earlier.<br /> <br /> For example; I just dropped the destruction of the Vienna Chantry into my chronicle. All the factions are in turmoil over who might really be behind it (and what this means in terms of favors owed by and to the Tremere). The Tremere Primogen (and head of the local Chantry) hasn\u2019t been seen since a week before news of the attack hit and the Whip and next in line for head of the local chantry aren\u2019t actually the same vampire.<br /> <br /> Just before the dust settles on that I\u2019ll be dropping news of the Scouring of London onto the weekly gathering in Elysium. Vienna is happenstance, London is coincidence... now the NPCs will be bracing for confirmation of enemy action. </div> </div> </div>I agree. I actually ran the FALL OF LONDON and hope they do THE FALL OF VIENNA as a Chronicle too.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Author of <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Cthulhu-Armageddon-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01KUOM7SI/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982844&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Cthulhu+Armageddon\" target=\"_blank\">Cthulhu Armageddon</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Teenage-Weredeer-Bright-Falls-Mysteries-ebook/dp/B075TTN2FN/ref=sr_1_2?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982717&amp;sr=1-2&amp;keywords=Weredeer#customerReviews\" target=\"_blank\">I was a Teenage Weredeer</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Straight-Outta-Fangton-Comedic-Vampire-ebook/dp/B01KNHICCC/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982774&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Straight+Outta+Fangton\" target=\"_blank\">Straight Outta Fangton</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Lucifers-Star-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01MDM9MCT/ref=mt_kindle?_encoding=UTF8&amp;me=&amp;qid=\" target=\"_blank\">Lucifer's Star</a>, </i>and the <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Rules-Supervillainy-Saga-Book-ebook/dp/B07MB89S33/\" target=\"_blank\">Supervillainy Saga</a>.</i><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":12002,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","user":"CTPhipps","date":". 04-13-2021, 01:15 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","name":"CTPhipps","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12002_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13933"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-04-13T10:24:35-07:00","id":1443757,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Chris24601</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1443592-the-official-v5-vs-v20-thread?p=1443753#post1443753\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> My general feeling is that Humanity in V5 should be renamed \u201cDelusion\u201d as high Humanity doesn\u2019t actually make you more moral since murdering and manipulating are required to maintain that state... it\u2019s just how good you are at lying to yourself.<br /> <br /> .</div> </div> </div> </div>Sounds like the perfect Idea for Revenant:The Ravishing.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":6}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25794-mywifeisscary","name":"MyWifeIsScary","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25794_2.png","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3711"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-04-13T10:40:22-07:00","id":1443760,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MyWifeIsScary</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1443592-the-official-v5-vs-v20-thread?p=1443757#post1443757\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Sounds like the perfect Idea for Revenant:The Ravishing.</div> </div> </div> </div>Like all true fans of REAL roleplaying, Zombie: The Putrescence is the actual TRUE Black Dog experience.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Author of <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Cthulhu-Armageddon-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01KUOM7SI/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982844&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Cthulhu+Armageddon\" target=\"_blank\">Cthulhu Armageddon</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Teenage-Weredeer-Bright-Falls-Mysteries-ebook/dp/B075TTN2FN/ref=sr_1_2?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982717&amp;sr=1-2&amp;keywords=Weredeer#customerReviews\" target=\"_blank\">I was a Teenage Weredeer</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Straight-Outta-Fangton-Comedic-Vampire-ebook/dp/B01KNHICCC/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982774&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Straight+Outta+Fangton\" target=\"_blank\">Straight Outta Fangton</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Lucifers-Star-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01MDM9MCT/ref=mt_kindle?_encoding=UTF8&amp;me=&amp;qid=\" target=\"_blank\">Lucifer's Star</a>, </i>and the <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Rules-Supervillainy-Saga-Book-ebook/dp/B07MB89S33/\" target=\"_blank\">Supervillainy Saga</a>.</i><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","name":"CTPhipps","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12002_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13933"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-04-13T10:58:44-07:00","id":1443763,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CTPhipps</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1443592-the-official-v5-vs-v20-thread?p=1443754#post1443754\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> The previous versions had you lose Humanity at 1 if you killed anyone, even in self-defense. The system was terribly broken and V20 was a major change that I approved of. V5 allows you a lot more freedom than even V20.<br /> <br /></div> </div> </div> </div>Yeah well in V20 killing in heat of passion is humanity 4 perversion which be interpreted like you got angry and killed some or that you do it in self defense. It is though clear that it draws a line to 3 where you really need to plan to kill or in humanity 2 where you kill because people where in your way.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>As I am from Austria I need to clarify two things.<br /> First my native language is german and so please point out if the english I write is broken so I can improve.<br /> Second I do not own VTMV beyond first three books nor any line after M20 Corebook because it is not out there and I wait for the translation.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26160-koronus","name":"Koronus","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2020"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"366"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-04-13T14:04:54-07:00","id":1443802,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CTPhipps</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1443592-the-official-v5-vs-v20-thread?p=1443751#post1443751\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Yes and no. Beckett's Jyhad Diary leads it up to 2015 but it was also written with a lead-in to 5th Edition--which was very professional of OPP.</div> </div> </div> </div>Where exactly is the no in there? V20, thanks to BJD, updates the metaplot into the mid 2010s. BJD works just fine even if you never use V5's stuff (in fact, I've seen plenty of V5 fans complain that V5 didn't follow BJD's lead more).<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> V5 is like V20 in that it was a &quot;deboot&quot; of Requiem. </div> </div> </div>What the heck does that even mean?<br /> <br /> Requiem is still a game with active support and development. V20 didn't end that nor was it ever intended to, V5 didn't either. They both exist because there's still a market for VtM.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CTPhipps</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1443592-the-official-v5-vs-v20-thread?p=1443754#post1443754\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">...but what if your Conviction from them is, &quot;They are a good person.&quot;</div> </div> </div> </div>Then we're getting into some serious forum-wankery and not taking about the games any more. &quot;They are a good person,&quot; is not a Conviction as they're clearly intended to be.<br /> <br /> V5 core, page 172: &quot;They might reflect a religious code, a personal ethical core, a vampiric path, or just things the character does or balks at doing without ever really considering their philosophi-cal weight.&quot;<br /> <br /> They are a good person does not fit with that concept of what Convictions are, or mesh at all with the sample list. Just believing that some mortal is a good person doesn't address the function of a Conviction to mitigate Stains your character gets for violating Tenets. <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> I think the writers of V5 wanted to make sure that any of the Humanity system COULD be run for horror but doesn't have to be. </div> </div> </div>And it ended up a muddled mess for it rather than something that a few more rounds of development might have be able to pull off effectively. The foundations of what you like about V5's approach are certainly there, but you can acknowledge how rough the execution is; to the point where it can easily fail a lot of people.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> The previous versions had you lose Humanity at 1 if you killed anyone, even in self-defense. </div> </div> </div>This is false. No edition prior to V5 allowed for this. Here, trimmed for space:<br /> <br /> V1, page 130:<br /> <br /> &quot;6 -Unintentional killing<br /> ...<br /> 2 -Murder<br /> 1 -The most heinous and demented acts&quot;<br /> <br /> V2, page 125:<br /> <br /> &quot;6 Negligent killing<br /> ...<br /> 4 Murder in the heat of passion<br /> ...<br /> 2 Premeditated murder<br /> 1 The most heinous and demented acts&quot;<br /> <br /> VRev, page, 221:<br /> <br /> &quot;6 Accidental violation (drinking a vessel dry out of starvation)<br /> ...<br /> 4 Impassioned violation (manslaughter, killing a vessel in frenzy)<br /> 3 Planned violation (outright murder, savored exsanguinations)<br /> 2 Casual violation (thoughtless killing, feeding past satiation)<br /> 1 Utter perversion or heinous acts&quot;<br /> <br /> As we can see, over time the game got more nuanced about taking life, but killing in self-defense as never be a Humanity 1 sin, and thus has never dropped you to Humanity 0. However you want to argue about where self-defense falls given the limited levels, even outright coldblooded murder is never worse than a Humanity 2 sin in any edition. The odd thing about all this? V5 is the first game where killing in self-defense might drop you to 0, if it violates your Tenet Chronicles.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Still, rules wise, Hunger 1 is nothing. </div> </div> </div>Do we really need to have this debate, again?<br /> <br /> How much Hunger 1 &quot;is&quot; is highly dependent on a number of factors; namely how good your character is at something (the better the worse Hunger 1 gets. because the more likely you are to roll Messy Crits) and how often you roll (the more your roll the worse, because while the odds on one roll aren't that high, rolling multiple times per session jumps the odds up a lot).<br /> <br /> For people that are happy to make heavy use of the automatic success rules and roll for far less things, Hunger doesn't feel as punishing. For people that feel you roll if it's dramatically important, and most things happening on screen are dramatically important, Hunger, even at 1, quickly grows into a huge headache.<br /> <br /> As even Matthew Dawkins has acknowledged, having Hunger apply to every roll was too heavy handed.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Yep. It's great if you want vampire to be a monster rather than being just a superpower that you can manage with ethical consumption (hehe) of blood. That's just me, though. </div> </div> </div>It's also great if you want VtM to be a nuanced game where you can effectively explore all those cool conflicts Justin Achilli just posted about, rather than some falling very flat because the rules push way to hard on, &quot;vampires are evil monsters and everything has to constantly remind you of that and how pointless it is to fight it.&quot; I can say that's not just me though, because multiple developers and writers for the game have actually worked essays about that into the books.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Humanity is now a Masquerade as a human to keep you from being overwhelmed by a genuinely terrifying curse. </div> </div> </div>Humanity has always done this. It's aways impacted your ability in pretend to be human, hide your curse, and keep you from falling irrevocably to the Beast.<br /> <br /> Doing it differently doesn't make it do it &quot;for real&quot; for the first time. One of the downsides of the flexibility of DIY Tenets and Convictions, is that it isn't actually stronger or more thematic, it's less defined, and therefore more subjective. You personally might feel it's stronger and more thematic, but that's heavily colored by picking things that resonate more strongly with you than the set-in-stone version of the previous editions, not because the mechanics without that are inherently better at enforcing themes.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Yep, easily a powerful and awesome twist that gives you a reason for wanting to play High Generation vampires. </div> </div> </div>Technically, it's just a pressure to play low Blood Potency games, since that's what really matters to feeding restrictions. You can be Gen 8 and, if you manage your BP, never feed off a live human. You can be Gen 5 and still only feed from volunteers.<br /> <br /> Fortunately most games don't cover enough spans of time to worry about the automatic increase in BP/torpor to reduce it cycle.<br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":9}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-04-13T14:18:42-07:00","id":1443804,"title":"","content":"<a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar617_2.jpeg');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"617\" data-vbnamecard=\"617\">Heavy Arms</a> thanks for the advice about the Ashirra.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"","name":"Guest","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/default/default_avatar_large.png","title":"","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-04-13T18:19:39-07:00","id":1443815,"title":"","content":"To be totally honest I'm not too sure this thread exist for more reason than to be a hot topic, but I guess thats what forums are fore.<br /> <br /> Thing is, I love V5. I played V20 and for me it's just and update, a fix on 3e system, with some little mechanic changes, and that's what it was, it wasn't called V4 even, it was a love project, and I really like the people for having done it. But for me it's of no use anymore, everything I didn't like is gone, and everything I liked was kept or made better in V5. I'm not really offended by changes I didn't entirely like either, but nothing was set in stone (as nothing really is in an rpg) that made look with disgust. And everything that would make me think &quot;uhm, wish it was different&quot; is small or off to the side enough to make changes easier. And Lore-wise that's easy-peasy too. Although I'm a bit of customizer when it comes to rpg and headcanons, so something not adequate to my tastes is right away changed when I'm the Storyteller, and I don't mind other interpretations from other Storytellers or GMs, that's part of the fun.<br /> <br /> Anyway, I don't see nothing in V5 that makes the game less, most things seen as bad are easily removed, or adapted, and the game is getting better by the book. But I also understood since I started playing that the player-base is deeply rooted and old, sticking to what it knows and likes, and that is nothing wrong, people play D&amp;D 3,5 till this day, and will defend it with tooth and nail.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>Strange... When coincidence seems too convenient, I prefer to call it fate.</i><br /> <br /> <b><sup>-Blood Omen: Legacy of Kain</sup> </b>d=","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25534-banu_saulot","name":"Banu_Saulot","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25534_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"335"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-04-13T18:21:46-07:00","id":1443816,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Banu_Saulot</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1443592-the-official-v5-vs-v20-thread?p=1443815#post1443815\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">To be totally honest I'm not too sure this thread exist for more reason than to be a hot topic, but I guess thats what forums are fore.</div> </div> </div> </div>My idea is that enough time has passed that people can speak a little more calmly about the subject and accept reasons for liking one or the other. It's something people want to talk about it so we might as well keep all the conversation here rather than spread it out.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Heavy Arms</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\"> Then we're getting into some serious forum-wankery and not taking about the games any more. &quot;They are a good person,&quot; is not a Conviction as they're clearly intended to be.<br /> <br /> V5 core, page 172: &quot;They might reflect a religious code, a personal ethical core, a vampiric path, or just things the character does or balks at doing without ever really considering their philosophi-cal weight.&quot;<br /> <br /> They are a good person does not fit with that concept of what Convictions are, or mesh at all with the sample list. Just believing that some mortal is a good person doesn't address the function of a Conviction to mitigate Stains your character gets for violating Tenets.</div> </div> </div> </div>If it's okay, I'd like to move this back over to the Touchstone section. Not much comparison to V20.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"b-bbcode b-bbcode__url b-bbcode__url--preview\"> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1443448-tips-for-running-touchstones\" class=\"urlimg_container\"> <img class=\"js-img-fallback\" src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/filedata/fetch?filedataid=1074\"> </a> <div class=\"urlinfo\"> <div class=\"title ellipsis\"> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1443448-tips-for-running-touchstones\"> Tips for Running Touchstones - Onyx Path Forums </a> </div> <div class=\"url ellipsis\"> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1443448-tips-for-running-touchstones\"> http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1443448-tips-for-running-touchstones </a> </div> <div class=\"meta\"> There's been a couple threads on Touchstones lately. I&rsquo;ve used Touchstones in my games since a while before V5 came out. Some have been awesome. Some have been </div> </div> </div>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Author of <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Cthulhu-Armageddon-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01KUOM7SI/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982844&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Cthulhu+Armageddon\" target=\"_blank\">Cthulhu Armageddon</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Teenage-Weredeer-Bright-Falls-Mysteries-ebook/dp/B075TTN2FN/ref=sr_1_2?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982717&amp;sr=1-2&amp;keywords=Weredeer#customerReviews\" target=\"_blank\">I was a Teenage Weredeer</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Straight-Outta-Fangton-Comedic-Vampire-ebook/dp/B01KNHICCC/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982774&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Straight+Outta+Fangton\" target=\"_blank\">Straight Outta Fangton</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Lucifers-Star-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01MDM9MCT/ref=mt_kindle?_encoding=UTF8&amp;me=&amp;qid=\" target=\"_blank\">Lucifer's Star</a>, </i>and the <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Rules-Supervillainy-Saga-Book-ebook/dp/B07MB89S33/\" target=\"_blank\">Supervillainy Saga</a>.</i><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":12002,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","user":"CTPhipps","date":". 04-14-2021, 02:08 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","name":"CTPhipps","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12002_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13933"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-04-14T00:04:03-07:00","id":1443854,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Vamps Like Us</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1443592-the-official-v5-vs-v20-thread?p=1443649#post1443649\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar617_2.jpeg');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"617\" data-vbnamecard=\"617\">Heavy Arms</a><br /> \u200b<br /> That's a lot to quote, but as someone who seems to like to discuss mechanics, do you think there is a way for V5 to fix the problems without putting out a new core edition, thus being V6? Can you see a way forward where a hefty rules supplement say fee to download with future printing saying 5.5 could fix all the problems that were rushed out or is it too much to make changes so fundamental without voiding the core book people spent money on?<br /> <br /> Do you think it's possible to get a more classic feel that some of us wanted? Or would fixing the rushed out problems be too much of a move away from what V5 is for those that like it? I ask as someone who flipped through it, watched a youtube play session, and read about it but never played or read it cover to cover.</div> </div> </div> </div>I think this is like Classic and Retail WoW. Every flaw people see in Classic/Retail WoW would already go into the direction that exist with Retail/Classic. From V20 to V5 there whas such a big difference to like SR3 to SR4 or from D&amp;D 3.5 to D&amp;D 4.<br /> The only possibility I would see is now have additional to VtR another VtM Spinn-off.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>As I am from Austria I need to clarify two things.<br /> First my native language is german and so please point out if the english I write is broken so I can improve.<br /> Second I do not own VTMV beyond first three books nor any line after M20 Corebook because it is not out there and I wait for the translation.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26160-koronus","name":"Koronus","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2020"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"366"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-04-14T06:56:44-07:00","id":1443872,"title":"","content":"One thing I'll say about V5 is that it's given me a deeper appreciation for Vampire: The Requiem, ironically. V5 uses a lot of concepts from there, but VTR generally does them better. I'd always been put off VTR because of the setting, but now I'm open to just stealing mechanics I like because V5 has kind of thrown the rulebook out the window (as it were).<br /> <br /> I have said this before, I think, but the Hunger mechanic works better in a one-off cinematic game like Alien. Alien has Stress Dice that work pretty much the same, except they add to your dice pools rather than replacing dice. For a while, a bit of Stress is okay, but it soon spirals out of control. For games where everyone freaks out and then gets killed, it works, but even there, we got exhausted with it after a few sessions (so longer adventures of even three sessions don't hold up as well as one-shots).<br /> <br /> In VTM, there's no benefit to Hunger Dice, and every Messy Crit or Bestial Failure brings problems, whereas rolling 1s on Stress Dice in Alien only presents a risk of something going wrong (you roll on another table to see what happens and anything under a certain threshold is fine).<br /> <br /> But there's something I want to like about Hunger Dice. I think Shadow Dice and Nightmare Dice present better examples of how the system could work. They present a better feeling of risk, and you get a tangible benefit from engaging with that part of the system. In V5, they're all stick and no carrot. I want some carrot. The CoD has some good models for this (Satiety in Beast, for example, and the Lost Boys in Hurt Locker, who gain power as they run low on juice before hitting a point of no return).<br /> <br /> I also think the simplicity of blood points can't be overlooked. I never once thought, 'Gee, I wish we didn't have to track these mana points.' I find the various tables of rouse checks and rerolls more complex than just saying 'this costs x BP, and you can only use y BP per turn'.<br /> <br /> I love the Paths in V20 (and V20DA). Those hit the sweet spot for me. I think, as others have said, we started out with Anarchs v elders, playing Camarilla games, for a few years. Then we felt that was done and wanted to explore more things.<br /> <br /> The benefit of something like the Sabbat is how alien those vampires can be. And that, for me, was always the biggest pull after those early games. I came to the table because of vampires, angst and Gothic Punk. I hung around for decades because of the kitchen sink setting, the ability to explore wildly different mindsets or belief systems, all the lore we could engage with without ever running out, and for the chance to actually be the bad guys.<br /> <br /> When so many settings are still--even now--about killing evil monsters, even in games with lots of shades of grey, it's still incredibly refreshing to play Vampire. Sometimes you just want to be evil, and enjoy that.<br /> <br /> That's why, after playing a Sister of Sigmar in Warhammer 4th Edition for months, for example, I'll feel such relief when we switch to Vampire for a while. Of all the popular games we regularly play, VTM is the one that really lets us scratch that itch. Of course there are other games that do that, but there seem to be some that are more popular than others and which we therefore get to play a lot more.<br /> <br /> Going back to what Heavy Arms said, VTM is best when it lets you do lots of things. It has always been a kitchen sink setting, despite what the marketing said. In this case, I don't think four iterations of the game were wrong--I think the marketing was. Yes, it can be 'A Beast I Am Lest a Beast I Become', but it can also be so much more than that. That was a strength, not a weakness.<br /> <br /> Now, onto something more positive, I do like the Bane/Compulsion system. The Compulsions add something nice. I just don't think they need to be as common as they are in play. I'm also thinking that, as suggested in some of the Requiem books, it would be nice for each Clan to also get a 'boon' like in CTD. So Lasombra get bonus dice for being in pitch black, for example. That balances all the negatives out a bit, IMO.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Writer, publisher, performer<br /> Mostly he/his, sometimes she/her IRL <a href=\"https://adam-lowe.com\" target=\"_blank\">https://adam-lowe.com</a>","edited":{"userid":5291,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5291-adambeyoncelowe","user":"adambeyoncelowe","date":". 04-15-2021, 03:20 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":8}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5291-adambeyoncelowe","name":"adambeyoncelowe","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5291_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2802"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-04-14T09:42:56-07:00","id":1443887,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CTPhipps</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1443592-the-official-v5-vs-v20-thread?p=1443661#post1443661\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Weird, because I felt the whole Sabbat vs. Camarilla thing totally spoiled the Anarch vs. Camarilla thing. They removed the central conflict of the setting. Old vs. Young vampires and replaced it with Good Vampires vs. Bad Ones.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> I agree that the Sabbat in Revised really sucked up the oxygen in the setting. I actually lost a couple players that just wanted Sabbat games, and I personally prefer Camarilla. I only had 1 friend who really liked the Anarchs though so I think it was just a case of the Sabbat being the more compelling story for most players, they made the stuff that sold. As much as I can enjoy a Clan novel or source book with the Sabbat I feel like if I was a shovel head and found out camarilla cities existed, I would just wander over and pretend I was a Brujah who got abandoned or something. I might even prefer the life of a Caitiff to that of a Sabbat cannon fodder depending on the city.<br /> <br /> Anarchs by definition are chaos. Sabbat for all the chaos has a lot of order for players to lean into. The structure is I'm sure why they seem more appealing.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24221-vamps-like-us","name":"Vamps Like Us","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"390"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-04-14T09:53:35-07:00","id":1443889,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CTPhipps</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1443592-the-official-v5-vs-v20-thread?p=1443754#post1443754\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">That seems like it's reading too much into it. A Touchstone gets damaged if they change too much but what if your Conviction from them is, &amp;quot;They are a good person.&amp;quot; Also, &quot;person I love&quot; will only be hit if they stop loving you back. It would only be damaged if they become bad.</div> </div> </div> </div>This is a discussion about V5 as written vs. V20 as written, not your house rules to make V5 actually work.<br /> <br /> A Conviction must be a value the PC upholds, not what they think about other people\u2019s values.<br /> <br /> And even if \u201cthis is a good person\u201d were a valid conviction, you\u2019d better be sure they\u2019re a freaking saint, because Touchstones must embody those convictions or you take a stain every time they fail to do so. So every selfish act by your Touchstone \u201cgood person\u201d is going to hit you with a stain... and the core book outright states the GM should mess with the Touchstones to break them... so forcing the \u201cgood person\u201d repeatedly into situations where they\u2019ll have to be selfish or where they question whether not just looking out for number one is even worth it should be regular occurrences if the GM is running as the book says they should.<br /> <br /> But none of the actual examples support that type of conviction. A Rousseau-ish \u201cHumans are Good\u201d would be valid, but then it\u2019s not just your Touchstone being good, it\u2019s ensuring those around them are good too... because \u201cGood people are taken advantage of by others\u201d isn\u2019t your Conviction.<br /> <br /> Ultimately, your examples fall far enough from the standards presented that you\u2019re essentially arguing \u201cV5 is great if you houserule it enough,\u201d but I can make RIFTS into a great game if I houserule it enough too. \u201cEase of houseruling\u201d is a quality worth discussing... but the need to do so just to make the game function isn\u2019t really a point in its favor.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CTPhipps</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1443592-the-official-v5-vs-v20-thread?p=1443754#post1443754\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The previous versions had you lose Humanity at 1 if you killed anyone, even in self-defense. The system was terribly broken and V20 was a major change that I approved of. V5 allows you a lot more freedom than even V20.</div> </div> </div> </div>Give me the page reference from 1e, 2e or Revised where it said this then. Because a poster above already provided the references showing the opposite.<br /> <br /> I dunno if you\u2019re remembering an old house rule from a crap GM or what, but blatantly misrepresenting past editions doesn\u2019t help your argument, it just makes your other arguments into things people will go and fact check instead of just taking you at your word.<br /> <br /> For review; in V1/2/R/20 you only need to check for Humanity loss if you commit a sin as bad or worse than your current level. Even if you did perform such an act, a successful Conscience check (max of your present Humanity so it did get easier to fail at the low end, but the conditions to even need a check also got rarer) vs. difficulty 8 meant your present level wasn\u2019t lost.<br /> <br /> At Humanity 7 you don\u2019t have to check for inflicting injury to others (so normal folks fighting back if attacked doesn\u2019t risk any loss). At 6 you can rob people blind every day without ever risking losing a point of humanity. <br /> <br /> At 5 you can accidentally kill people without risking further humanity loss (which is where killing in self-defense typically falls, you don\u2019t intend to kill them, it\u2019s just what happened in trying to get them to stop). At 3 you can commit manslaughter at will without a check. At 2 you can be a serial killer and not risk further Humanity loss. At Humanity 1 you basically have to do things like use your victim\u2019s corpses as lawn ornaments before that final check will need to be made.<br /> <br /> And even then it\u2019s just to need the check to see if it was actually lost<br /> <br /> There\u2019s a reason most Elders hover around Humanity 4 in the previous editions; it takes real work in terms of depravity to drop much below that. If you accidentally drink a vessel dry or kill someone in a frenzy regularly you might drop as low as 3, but that\u2019s what is meant by saying the old system has backstops in place... even vamps who treat humans like livestock or \u201cHappy Meals on Legs\u201d won\u2019t actually hit Wassail and Wight status.<br /> <br /> And maybe it\u2019s just the people in my gaming circles, but the number of players I\u2019ve met interested in playing characters that monstrous is essentially zero. Even the ones who express interest in Paths aren\u2019t picking ones that regard active malice against humans as a good thing (outside of Humanity, the most common Path in my experience is Honorable Accord which is comprehensible enough that I could even see actual humans following it).<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CTPhipps</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1443592-the-official-v5-vs-v20-thread?p=1443754#post1443754\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Yes, I feel like that is much more effective for establishing horror. Still, rules wise, Hunger 1 is nothing.</div> </div> </div> </div>Then, with respect, you\u2019re unfamiliar with how probability works.<br /> <br /> Hunger dice are basically the equivalent of the d20 System\u2019s climb and swim checks. Something that looks innocuous... you need a 5 or better each round to keep afloat in calm water; easy peasy... until you have to roll it every round and with only an 80% success rate per check, you\u2019ve got only about a 10% chance of not starting to drown inside of a minute (10 rounds).<br /> <br /> The same goes for Hunger dice. 10% chance of triggering (since 10\u2019s only matter for success and 1\u2019s only on failures) means you\u2019ve got a 50/50 shot at the Hunger die triggering a bestial success/failure by your 5th roll of the night and if you have 15 tests in a session it\u2019ll trigger at least once in 80% of your sessions.<br /> <br /> That\u2019s with Hunger 1.<br /> <br /> At Hunger 2 (akin to a 13th Gen who\u2019s burned four blood points) you will have the dice trigger at least once in the first five tests 2/3rds of the time and have a 90% chance of triggering it within the first ten tests.<br /> <br /> So even in a campaign with minimal dice rolling (5 tests per session) a vampire who doesn\u2019t murder people will have a hunger-related screwup about every other session IF they can keep themselves at Hunger 1.<br /> <br /> And that\u2019s PER CHARACTER. A coiterie of four who keep the no killing rule with minimal rolling (5 tests per player per night) and all keeping at Hunger 1 will experience a Hunger-related screwup from at least one of the PCs in 95% of sessions.<br /> <br /> That\u2019s a NOT rare occurrence and if it was intended to be rare, then whoever designed that rule was flat off their game in the math department.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CTPhipps</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1443592-the-official-v5-vs-v20-thread?p=1443754#post1443754\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Yep. It's great if you want vampire to be a monster rather than being just a superpower that you can manage with ethical consumption (hehe) of blood. That's just me, though.</div> </div> </div> </div>I don\u2019t see why you\u2019d think ethical blood consumption is some sort of funny impossibility. You can get a gallon (8 pints) of fresh pork blood for about $15-20 from any butcher and can even order it online (it\u2019s commonly used in dishes like blood pudding and blood sausage).<br /> <br /> In V20 a pig\u2019s blood is about 40% as filling as a human and even if you halve that for being cold you\u2019re still looking at at 1 BP per bucket or basically feeding yourself for $15-20 a day ($7300 a year even at $20/gallon... a vampire on welfare could afford that).<br /> <br /> It\u2019s as easy as typing \u201cpig blood\u201d into your search bar and as ethical as buying pork chops. Seriously, they sell it by the bucket in the real world. The only thing to keep a vampire from just working a night shift and dropping by the local butcher before sun up to buy a fresh bucket is the social stigma within vampire society.<br /> <br /> So, yeah it\u2019s something easily possible in past editions if you wanted to go that route.<br /> <br /> And again... my experience is that the number of players who want to run vampires as absolute monsters is basically nil. Edgy and emo? Yes. Monster? No.<br /> <br /> Honestly, I think there\u2019s just a massive disconnect between how you prefer to play and how a lot of players on this board like to play. The unofficial opening poll by MyWifeIsScary is currently running 17-2 in favor of V20 over V5 for which version is preferred.<br /> <br /> V5 scratches your particular itch and that\u2019s great for you, but understand your perspectives are a distinct minority that are not aligned with the majority of other registered posters here.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":7}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1328-chris24601","name":"Chris24601","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"520"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-04-14T09:55:24-07:00","id":1443890,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Chris24601</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1443592-the-official-v5-vs-v20-thread?p=1443889#post1443889\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">This is a discussion about V5 as written vs. V20 as written, not your house rules to make V5 actually work.</div> </div> </div> </div>It's also not true.<br /> <br /> Heavy Arms cited the point that a Touchstone is often an embodiment of what a person thinks about their ideals. I.e. a Good Person.<br /> <br /> A Touchstone is linked to a Conviction.<br /> <br /> The Touchstone is the Good Person, a Conviction might be &quot;Protect my Friend&quot; or &quot;Protect Good People.&quot;<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Give me the page reference from 1e, 2e or Revised where it said this then. Because a poster above already provided the references showing the opposite. </div> </div> </div>I think frankly the cited material shows that &quot;in the heat of anger&quot; isn't nearly as reflective as people think. Hyperbole or not, I feel like it is a far too punishing system.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> I don\u2019t see why you\u2019d think ethical blood consumption is some sort of funny impossibility. You can get a gallon (8 pints) of fresh pork blood for about $15-20 from any butcher and can even order it online (it\u2019s commonly used in dishes like blood pudding and blood sausage). </div> </div> </div>Then why is vampirism a curse?<br /> <br /> Why lament it?<br /> <br /> It needs to have a downside or everyone would do it.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Author of <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Cthulhu-Armageddon-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01KUOM7SI/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982844&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Cthulhu+Armageddon\" target=\"_blank\">Cthulhu Armageddon</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Teenage-Weredeer-Bright-Falls-Mysteries-ebook/dp/B075TTN2FN/ref=sr_1_2?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982717&amp;sr=1-2&amp;keywords=Weredeer#customerReviews\" target=\"_blank\">I was a Teenage Weredeer</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Straight-Outta-Fangton-Comedic-Vampire-ebook/dp/B01KNHICCC/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982774&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Straight+Outta+Fangton\" target=\"_blank\">Straight Outta Fangton</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Lucifers-Star-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01MDM9MCT/ref=mt_kindle?_encoding=UTF8&amp;me=&amp;qid=\" target=\"_blank\">Lucifer's Star</a>, </i>and the <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Rules-Supervillainy-Saga-Book-ebook/dp/B07MB89S33/\" target=\"_blank\">Supervillainy Saga</a>.</i><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":12002,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","user":"CTPhipps","date":". 04-14-2021, 01:01 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","name":"CTPhipps","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12002_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13933"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-04-14T09:57:33-07:00","id":1443892,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>adambeyoncelowe</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1443592-the-official-v5-vs-v20-thread?p=1443872#post1443872\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Now, onto something more positive, I do like the Bane/Compulsion system. The Compulsions add something nice. I just don't think they need to be as common as they are in play. I'm also thinking that, as suggested in some of the Requiem books, it would be nice for each Clan to also get a 'boon' like in CTD. So Lasombra get bonus dice for being in pitch black, for example. That balances all the negatives out a bit, IMO.</div> </div> </div> </div>Agreed, I also stole those as part of my rewrite of Generation to be a trade-off system instead of a background point cost in V20. Though I do like the idea of a clan boon (beyond clan discipline cost breaks) as well. I might look into that.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1328-chris24601","name":"Chris24601","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"520"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-04-14T11:34:08-07:00","id":1443903,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CTPhipps</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1443592-the-official-v5-vs-v20-thread?p=1443890#post1443890\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Then why is vampirism a curse?<br /> <br /> Why lament it?<br /> <br /> It needs to have a downside or everyone would do it.</div> </div> </div> </div>Because never again being able to see the sun (even twilight burns and this greatly diminishes your travel options), an inability to have children and outliving everyone you\u2019ve ever loved are pretty sucktacular curses all on their own.<br /> <br /> Throw in a falling into a coma during the hours normal people are out and about, a heightened temper (full belly or not), a phobia of fire (no cookouts or bonfires for you) and being unable to ever again enjoy the taste of ordinary food (or even be able to hold it down) and your eternal so-called life is one almost entirely divorced from anything like an ordinary human life.<br /> <br /> Really, the need to drink blood is the smallest part of what makes vampism a curse. At most it\u2019s the cherry atop a shit sundae of suck to anyone who isn\u2019t some Zoomer who thinks life ends at 30 (when really it\u2019s only just starting).","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":7}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1328-chris24601","name":"Chris24601","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"520"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-04-14T11:37:30-07:00","id":1443904,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Chris24601</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1443592-the-official-v5-vs-v20-thread?p=1443903#post1443903\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Because never again being able to see the sun (even twilight burns and this greatly diminishes your travel options), an inability to have children and outliving everyone you\u2019ve ever loved are pretty sucktacular curses all on their own.<br /> <br /> Throw in a falling into a coma during the hours normal people are out and about, a heightened temper (full belly or not), a phobia of fire (no cookouts or bonfires for you) and being unable to ever again enjoy the taste of ordinary food (or even be able to hold it down) and your eternal so-called life is one almost entirely divorced from anything like an ordinary human life.<br /> <br /> <b>Really, the need to drink blood is the smallest part of what makes vampism a curse. </b>At most it\u2019s the cherry atop a shit sundae of suck to anyone who isn\u2019t some Zoomer who thinks life ends at 30 (when really it\u2019s only just starting).</div> </div> </div> </div>100% the opposite for me. The blood is the big deal. I think that's more than the lamentations of immortality ala Highlander. For me, the central element of being a vampire is being forced to prey on your fellow human beings. You can try to limit the amount of damage you do but the Hunger for blood is the worst part of it.<br /> <br /> But that's entirely up to you at your game. The thing about this thread is it's not meant to criticize other people's preferences. There's no wrong way to play the game if you're having fun.<br /> <br /> Obviously, how we feel about how important feeding should be to a vampire impacts our feelings on V5 where it's strongly emphasized.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Author of <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Cthulhu-Armageddon-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01KUOM7SI/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982844&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Cthulhu+Armageddon\" target=\"_blank\">Cthulhu Armageddon</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Teenage-Weredeer-Bright-Falls-Mysteries-ebook/dp/B075TTN2FN/ref=sr_1_2?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982717&amp;sr=1-2&amp;keywords=Weredeer#customerReviews\" target=\"_blank\">I was a Teenage Weredeer</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Straight-Outta-Fangton-Comedic-Vampire-ebook/dp/B01KNHICCC/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982774&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Straight+Outta+Fangton\" target=\"_blank\">Straight Outta Fangton</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Lucifers-Star-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01MDM9MCT/ref=mt_kindle?_encoding=UTF8&amp;me=&amp;qid=\" target=\"_blank\">Lucifer's Star</a>, </i>and the <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Rules-Supervillainy-Saga-Book-ebook/dp/B07MB89S33/\" target=\"_blank\">Supervillainy Saga</a>.</i><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","name":"CTPhipps","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12002_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13933"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-04-14T12:55:09-07:00","id":1443920,"title":"","content":"The thing that sucks about being a vampire is that you're up for 8 hours a day, sunlight burns you, and your piers are pricks. The blood is supposedly better than heroin, and I watched that film where Obi-Wan greatly enjoys heroin so I understand it might be worth the bother of stealing it from people, but only in that movie Obi-Wan wasn't powerful in the force whilst in Vampire we've got a few powers to make it easier for us. Once you're good at stealing blood, the blood itself ceases to be more of a problem than the joy you get out of taking it, and the greatest problem remains that your piers are pricks and when everyone else has gone to bed they're the only people around to talk to. Though I suppose nowadays we have internet.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":6}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25794-mywifeisscary","name":"MyWifeIsScary","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25794_2.png","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3711"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-04-14T13:46:38-07:00","id":1443929,"title":"","content":"I think the problem with the focus on blood, is that V5 doesn't even manage to do that in a satisfying way. The major mechanic is called Hunger for a reason. You could change what the vampires are hungry for to almost anything and Hunger itself would barely change. Change it to a hunger for material wealth. The Beast wants things, things to sate it empty heart but they never truly fill it. It wants a lavish lair appointed with the finest goods to show its superiority over others. Young vampires can copy the kine and play the games of capitalism to gather wealth, but their powers let them jump past all that tedium and take. And nothing soothes the Beast like taking with force. The draw to steal, to murder others for their things grows and gnaws in a vampire's mind.<br /> <br /> Hunger? Didn't change a bit. Rousing is just you getting bored with the stuff you have as you get hungry for more stuff. &quot;Lesser&quot; feedings work for the weak and young, but older and stronger vampires require more, and take with more damaging results to the mortals around them.<br /> <br /> Even Blood Resonance, the part really focused on blood itself, can easily be twisted to any Hunger. It is just the emotional state of the victims that matter in the end. Instead of who you drain of blood for a specific Resonance, now it's who you rob instead.<br /> <br /> If the very specific substance of blood was really what was the most important part? VtM would be an entirely different game. VtM uses blood because it's vampire pop culture (actual mythology contains more than the a hunger for blood in various types of vampires), not because blood is inherently necessary to make vampires work as a fictional element.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":6}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-04-14T23:29:34-07:00","id":1443991,"title":"","content":"That little poll i threw in at the start of the thread is currently 19:3. Honestly very surprised, I wouldn't think it would be such a landslide so far, especially given which side gets banned more. Or maybe it's the result of only hardcore fans/people with an axe to grind being on the forums and all the people happy with the new edition are busy enjoying the new edition. Maybe a very dedicated fan had 19 accounts and just really wanted the developers/publishers to know his anguish. In any case it's nice to have numbers, and in this case some very strong numbers.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":25794,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25794-mywifeisscary","user":"MyWifeIsScary","date":". 04-15-2021, 07:58 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25794-mywifeisscary","name":"MyWifeIsScary","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25794_2.png","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3711"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-04-14T23:34:59-07:00","id":1443992,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MyWifeIsScary</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1443592-the-official-v5-vs-v20-thread?p=1443991#post1443991\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">That little pole i threw in at the start of the thread is currently 19:3. Honestly very surprised, I wouldn't think it would be such a landslide so far, especially given which side gets banned more. Or maybe it's the result of only hardcore fans/people with an axe to grind being on the forums and all the people happy with the new edition are busy enjoying the new edition. Maybe a very dedicated fan had 19 accounts and just really wanted the developers/publishers to know his anguish. In any case it's nice to have numbers, and in this case some very strong numbers.</div> </div> </div> </div>Eh, V20 was very nice. Some people prefer it and it did save V:TM so it could be reintroduced to a larger audience.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Author of <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Cthulhu-Armageddon-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01KUOM7SI/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982844&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Cthulhu+Armageddon\" target=\"_blank\">Cthulhu Armageddon</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Teenage-Weredeer-Bright-Falls-Mysteries-ebook/dp/B075TTN2FN/ref=sr_1_2?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982717&amp;sr=1-2&amp;keywords=Weredeer#customerReviews\" target=\"_blank\">I was a Teenage Weredeer</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Straight-Outta-Fangton-Comedic-Vampire-ebook/dp/B01KNHICCC/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982774&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Straight+Outta+Fangton\" target=\"_blank\">Straight Outta Fangton</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Lucifers-Star-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01MDM9MCT/ref=mt_kindle?_encoding=UTF8&amp;me=&amp;qid=\" target=\"_blank\">Lucifer's Star</a>, </i>and the <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Rules-Supervillainy-Saga-Book-ebook/dp/B07MB89S33/\" target=\"_blank\">Supervillainy Saga</a>.</i><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","name":"CTPhipps","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12002_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13933"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-04-14T23:43:00-07:00","id":1443996,"title":"","content":"During 2020, V5 was number 57 on drivethrough rpg's top 100 . V20 is at 27. (cult of the blood gods is at 13)<br /> Granted, V5 probably gets some of that number taken away by physical sales (which V20 never got for some reason?) but... ehh..<br /> <br /> <br /> Just give me V30 already.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25794-mywifeisscary","name":"MyWifeIsScary","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25794_2.png","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3711"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-04-14T23:58:41-07:00","id":1443998,"title":"","content":"V20 was made for The Grand Masquerade 2011, where it had physical sales, and CCP-WW sold physical copies through a private online storefront for a limited time. V20 is (last I checked) still available for PoD from DTRPG.<br /> <br /> The big source of a dent in V5's position on DTRPG can most easily be put on the fact that initially it was distributed through Modiphius's store front. Selling the book through multiple retailers limits the usefulness of DTRPG's sales metric.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-04-15T00:11:35-07:00","id":1444000,"title":"","content":"At the end of the day V5 is really just D&amp;D4th edition Electric Boogaloo.<br /> <br /> In both cases, we got a new edition with some pretty major mechanical overhauls and huge changes to the setting due to questionable in-world events because the designers felt that the existing metaplot had gotten so massive that new players found it intimidating. So the designers decided to clean house by sweeping a lot of that stuff away and making it a &quot;new player friendly edition.&quot; <br /> <br /> Of course, this has the effect of annoying the old school players who had been following that metaplot for years and years, and the mechanic changes were also not met all that well by various older members of the playerbase. <br /> <br /> I'm hopeful that maybe someday we'll get a &quot;D&amp;D5th edition&quot; version of Vampire than rolls back a lot of the setting changes introduced by V5 and rolls back some of the mechanical changes in favor of a smoother game that holds closer to the older editions.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":13}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/741-anubisxy","name":"AnubisXy","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar741_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5693"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-04-15T06:29:45-07:00","id":1444029,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MyWifeIsScary</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1443592-the-official-v5-vs-v20-thread?p=1443996#post1443996\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">During 2020, V5 was number 57 on drivethrough rpg's top 100 . V20 is at 27. (cult of the blood gods is at 13)<br /> Granted, V5 probably gets some of that number taken away by physical sales (which V20 never got for some reason?) but... ehh..<br /> <br /> Just give me V30 already.</div> </div> </div> </div>It also won Origins awards and is going through its third physical reprinting. Worrying about its popularity is not important, especially since it has also sold excellent spin offs like Winter's Teeth and visual novels. It's also reaching an audience of millions with LA by Night's various platforms. Vampire: The Masquerade products are now available in stores like Amazon and we do have multiple World of Darkness video games out now (even if Bloodlines 2 is taking forever because they're not satisfied with the progress). It's a Renaissance of the product and a very exciting time to be a fan.<br /> <br /> I hope my fellow fans will take time to watch the many news feeds, discussions of fan theories, and engage with the reviewers as well as discussions going on.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>AnubisXy</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1443592-the-official-v5-vs-v20-thread?p=1444000#post1444000\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">At the end of the day V5 is really just D&amp;D4th edition Electric Boogaloo.<br /> <br /> In both cases, we got a new edition with some pretty major mechanical overhauls and huge changes to the setting due to questionable in-world events because the designers felt that the existing metaplot had gotten so massive that new players found it intimidating. So the designers decided to clean house by sweeping a lot of that stuff away and making it a &quot;new player friendly edition.&quot;<br /> <br /> Of course, this has the effect of annoying the old school players who had been following that metaplot for years and years, and the mechanic changes were also not met all that well by various older members of the playerbase.<br /> <br /> I'm hopeful that maybe someday we'll get a &quot;D&amp;D5th edition&quot; version of Vampire than rolls back a lot of the setting changes introduced by V5 and rolls back some of the mechanical changes in favor of a smoother game that holds closer to the older editions.</div> </div> </div> </div>Needless to say, I feel differently.<br /> <br /> I feel 5th Edition, especially the OPP supplements for it, are among the best Vampire products ever created. I feel its reached a far larger audience and has the potential to really push the IP beyond where it used to be. I feel like the initial release was very rough but we've already had all the lore corrections and the rules ones are continuing to come out as is. There's no need for a Sixth Edition because its an issue of clarification for me rather than one of changing.<br /> <br /> But hey, feel what you feel.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Author of <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Cthulhu-Armageddon-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01KUOM7SI/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982844&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Cthulhu+Armageddon\" target=\"_blank\">Cthulhu Armageddon</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Teenage-Weredeer-Bright-Falls-Mysteries-ebook/dp/B075TTN2FN/ref=sr_1_2?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982717&amp;sr=1-2&amp;keywords=Weredeer#customerReviews\" target=\"_blank\">I was a Teenage Weredeer</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Straight-Outta-Fangton-Comedic-Vampire-ebook/dp/B01KNHICCC/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982774&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Straight+Outta+Fangton\" target=\"_blank\">Straight Outta Fangton</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Lucifers-Star-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01MDM9MCT/ref=mt_kindle?_encoding=UTF8&amp;me=&amp;qid=\" target=\"_blank\">Lucifer's Star</a>, </i>and the <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Rules-Supervillainy-Saga-Book-ebook/dp/B07MB89S33/\" target=\"_blank\">Supervillainy Saga</a>.</i><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":12002,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","user":"CTPhipps","date":". 04-15-2021, 09:49 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","name":"CTPhipps","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12002_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13933"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-04-15T09:13:50-07:00","id":1444038,"title":"","content":"The Star Wars sequel Trillogy made bank because it was called &quot;Star Wars&quot; despite considerable contention to the possession of worthwhile qualities. Similarly, V5 can largely attribute it's success to the title &quot;Vampire: The masquerade&quot; despite having ugly art, terrible mechanics, a very questionable metaplot, not capturing the spirit of prior products, having an almost entirely fresh group of developers, and creating controversies concerning real life issues. Just by brand recognition alone, V5 has clawed its way to success. Were it called &quot;Vampire, the inquisition&quot; or something more appropriate it wouldn't have done half as well (Though &quot;Vampire: The inquisition&quot; sounds like a baller title so it might get points for that, and I wouldn't be half as mad at it because it wouldn't be dragging down a good IP)<br /> <br /> Older titles had more mass appeal. They allowed for more different kinds of games to be played. They put storytelling before mechanics (and had better mechanics) If V5 released as something more like V28 it would've had scores of investors, a TV show, Bloodlines 2 would've been released by now, and it'd be competing with 5th edition DnD.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":9}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25794-mywifeisscary","name":"MyWifeIsScary","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25794_2.png","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3711"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-04-15T09:57:56-07:00","id":1444042,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MyWifeIsScary</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1443592-the-official-v5-vs-v20-thread?p=1444038#post1444038\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The Star Wars sequel Trillogy made bank because it was called &quot;Star Wars&quot; despite considerable contention to the possession of worthwhile qualities. Similarly, V5 can largely attribute it's success to the title &quot;Vampire: The masquerade&quot; despite having ugly art, terrible mechanics, a very questionable metaplot, not capturing the spirit of prior products, having an almost entirely fresh group of developers, and creating controversies concerning real life issues. Just by brand recognition alone, V5 has clawed its way to success. Were it called &quot;Vampire, the inquisition&quot; or something more appropriate it wouldn't have done half as well (Though &quot;Vampire: The inquisition&quot; sounds like a baller title so it might get points for that, and I wouldn't be half as mad at it because it wouldn't be dragging down a good IP)<br /> <br /> Older titles had more mass appeal. They allowed for more different kinds of games to be played. They put storytelling before mechanics (and had better mechanics) If V5 released as something more like V28 it would've had scores of investors, a TV show, Bloodlines 2 would've been released by now, and it'd be competing with 5th edition DnD.</div> </div> </div> </div>I strongly disagree, My Wife is Scary and think 5th Edition has a large appeal in large part because of its inherent merit. But yes, tastes may vary. Its important to respect that both ways.Over in the Inconnu thread, a guy actually wrote in the comments on MD's video that he used to love watching his videos but dropped him the moment he started doing videos on &quot;V5 trash.&quot;<br /> <br /> <div class=\"b-bbcode b-bbcode__url b-bbcode__url--preview\"> <a href=\"https://youtu.be/CsnXIX05Tfk\" target=\"_blank\" class=\"urlimg_container\"> <img class=\"js-img-fallback\" src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/default/google-material/image_placeholder.svg\"> </a> <div class=\"urlinfo\"> <div class=\"title ellipsis\"> <a href=\"https://youtu.be/CsnXIX05Tfk\" target=\"_blank\"> </a> </div> <div class=\"url ellipsis\"> <a href=\"https://youtu.be/CsnXIX05Tfk\" target=\"_blank\"> https://youtu.be/CsnXIX05Tfk </a> </div> <div class=\"meta\"> </div> </div> </div><br /> <br /> That attitude helps no one. I feel the same for someone who dismisses that the only reason we HAVE V5 is do to the tireless efforts of V20 to remind people of what an awesome game classic V:TM was.<br /> <br /> I'm also probably not the best person to talk about Star Wars since I devoted 10 years of my life to collecting the Star Wars EU which was one of the most important things of my life for a long time despite it all being non-canon now.<br /> <br /> I also disagree with Gail Simone's tweet: <a href=\"https://twitter.com/Willowhugger/status/1382379360745840640\" target=\"_blank\">https://twitter.com/Willowhugger/sta...79360745840640</a>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Author of <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Cthulhu-Armageddon-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01KUOM7SI/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982844&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Cthulhu+Armageddon\" target=\"_blank\">Cthulhu Armageddon</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Teenage-Weredeer-Bright-Falls-Mysteries-ebook/dp/B075TTN2FN/ref=sr_1_2?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982717&amp;sr=1-2&amp;keywords=Weredeer#customerReviews\" target=\"_blank\">I was a Teenage Weredeer</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Straight-Outta-Fangton-Comedic-Vampire-ebook/dp/B01KNHICCC/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982774&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Straight+Outta+Fangton\" target=\"_blank\">Straight Outta Fangton</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Lucifers-Star-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01MDM9MCT/ref=mt_kindle?_encoding=UTF8&amp;me=&amp;qid=\" target=\"_blank\">Lucifer's Star</a>, </i>and the <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Rules-Supervillainy-Saga-Book-ebook/dp/B07MB89S33/\" target=\"_blank\">Supervillainy Saga</a>.</i><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":12002,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","user":"CTPhipps","date":". 04-15-2021, 01:30 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","name":"CTPhipps","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12002_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13933"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-04-15T11:01:19-07:00","id":1444045,"title":"","content":"First Issue is that with so many people rejecting V5, it becomes difficult as to determine what exactly we're talking about when we mention &quot;Vampire The Masquerade&quot;; Are we doing the first four editions, the fifth edition, the mechanics of one and the story of the other or vice versa or perhaps some very finicky thing that's mostly one but takes cues from another. Hell; Absolutely nobody seems to be playing V5 without prepping houserules, so even when people say they like V5 they're usually forgetting about all the duct-tape they're using to put it together. <br /> <br /> Second issue is that a lot of V5isms seem to maliciously target things people liked in prior editions. Oh you liked the Sabbat? They've fucked off! The Tremere? We blew them up and robbed them of their spells. Those sexy Lasombra? The half that haven't fucked off are now bitch-boys in the caricature of the Camarilla that became the truth, and also their new weakness is emasculating and their signature discipline is garbage. Samedi for unlife? Well guess who got sucked up into the Hecata.... There's just too much here. It comes across as mean spirited. That's not even getting into nonsense like Thin blood alchemy and how mechanics impact the story in a massively negative way. <br /> <br /> Third issue is that mechanical changes range between -arguably a mild improvement- and -how could you possibly fuck this up so bad?-. The game is absolutely centered around a one-true-way of play once more, and some mechanics are so.... I can't say it. Look at the rules for diablerie and ask yourself if the person who wrote that has ever played a long running game with those mechanics without realising what a horrendous idea they are, nevermind how utterly antithetical they are to how diablerie has been for the past four editions, they're an absolutely fantastic way to utterly destroy the dynamics of a party. You'd think as a 2018 release they'd have the hindisight of four editions of vampire, two editions of requiem, and however many other titles they bothered to look at during development; It should be downright easy to come up with something objectively better, and yet they've excelled at making something near-objectively worse. Touchstones for example; Just so much better done in requiem. <br /> <br /> Ultimately, what a lot of people wanted was -Vampire: the Masquerade, but with some improvements. V5 could never be described as such. If I hold back I can describe it as a reckless, disrespectful attempt to capitalize on an IP. And people are so against it in the vain hope that paradox will realise they did wrong, make it Ravana's fever dream, and put v6 on track.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":9}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25794-mywifeisscary","name":"MyWifeIsScary","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25794_2.png","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3711"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-04-15T11:05:21-07:00","id":1444046,"title":"","content":"My view is that all of them are Vampire: The Masquerade. You shouldn't gatekeep. A fan of 1st Edition, 5th Edition, V20, or the video games is a fan. Period. Same for LARP and tabletop.<br /> <br /> Why make the fandom smaller?<br /> <br /> I also disagree with a lot of your statements since the Lasombra in the Camarilla seems to be because the number of Lasombra Antitribu n the Camarilla in LARPS has always been huge, regardless of their supposed rarity. We're also getting the Sabbat book finally. I fully agree it should have been the fourth book released, though. Even the adding of things like the Samedi to the Hecata are about making them more available as a mainstay of the setting. Before, they were a rare bloodline barely involved but now they're a major mover and player.<br /> <br /> This fits into the fact, though, that interpretation is a major part of these issues. One man's trash is another man's treasure and a lot is up to the way STs choose to play it.<br /> <br /> I also love the new system.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Ultimately, what a lot of people wanted was -Vampire: the Masquerade, but with some improvements. V5 could never be described as such. </div> </div> </div>Allow me. &quot;V5 is Vampire: The Masquerade but with some improvements.&quot;<br /> <br /> <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Author of <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Cthulhu-Armageddon-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01KUOM7SI/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982844&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Cthulhu+Armageddon\" target=\"_blank\">Cthulhu Armageddon</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Teenage-Weredeer-Bright-Falls-Mysteries-ebook/dp/B075TTN2FN/ref=sr_1_2?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982717&amp;sr=1-2&amp;keywords=Weredeer#customerReviews\" target=\"_blank\">I was a Teenage Weredeer</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Straight-Outta-Fangton-Comedic-Vampire-ebook/dp/B01KNHICCC/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982774&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Straight+Outta+Fangton\" target=\"_blank\">Straight Outta Fangton</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Lucifers-Star-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01MDM9MCT/ref=mt_kindle?_encoding=UTF8&amp;me=&amp;qid=\" target=\"_blank\">Lucifer's Star</a>, </i>and the <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Rules-Supervillainy-Saga-Book-ebook/dp/B07MB89S33/\" target=\"_blank\">Supervillainy Saga</a>.</i><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":12002,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","user":"CTPhipps","date":". 09-21-2021, 09:13 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","name":"CTPhipps","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12002_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13933"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-04-15T11:19:13-07:00","id":1444047,"title":"","content":"Imagine for 6th edition someone deleted the malkavians, the anarchs, and... what else do you like?<br /> Imagine when you get frustrated and actually talk about how an edition destroyed your favourite clan and your favourite sect, deprived you of your favourite power, and then did the same for all the runner-ups; in the face of your complaints someone accuses you of &quot;gatekeeping&quot;.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":25794,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25794-mywifeisscary","user":"MyWifeIsScary","date":". 04-15-2021, 02:24 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":9}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25794-mywifeisscary","name":"MyWifeIsScary","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25794_2.png","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3711"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-04-15T11:27:08-07:00","id":1444048,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MyWifeIsScary</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1443592-the-official-v5-vs-v20-thread?p=1444047#post1444047\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Imagine for 6th edition someone deleted the malkavians, the anarchs, and... what else do you like?<br /> Imagine when you get frustrated and actually talk about how an edition destroyed your favourite clan and your favourite sect, deprived you of your favourite power, and then did the same for all the runner-ups; in the face of your complaints someone accuses you of &quot;gatekeeping&quot;.</div> </div> </div> </div>I would definitely dislike it. I also would encourage the creators to reintroduce the elements I did like. I'm very much of the mind that Chicago by Night and Blood Gods went a long way to repairing V5's weaknesses. I hope the Sabbat sourcebook will do the same. Mind you, I think you can love something about a book series and appreciate what it does well while wanting changes elsewhere. Other things I'd like to see for V5 is a return of Elder Disciplines.<br /> <br /> I feel like some posters here don't believe when I say the Sabbat is my second favorite sect. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> And everyone should also be proud for their efforts in supporting things like CBN, COTBG, and other supplements that are improving V5. The Sabbat book wouldn't exist without everyone clamoring for it.<br /> <br /> V5 belongs to you.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Author of <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Cthulhu-Armageddon-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01KUOM7SI/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982844&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Cthulhu+Armageddon\" target=\"_blank\">Cthulhu Armageddon</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Teenage-Weredeer-Bright-Falls-Mysteries-ebook/dp/B075TTN2FN/ref=sr_1_2?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982717&amp;sr=1-2&amp;keywords=Weredeer#customerReviews\" target=\"_blank\">I was a Teenage Weredeer</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Straight-Outta-Fangton-Comedic-Vampire-ebook/dp/B01KNHICCC/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982774&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Straight+Outta+Fangton\" target=\"_blank\">Straight Outta Fangton</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Lucifers-Star-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01MDM9MCT/ref=mt_kindle?_encoding=UTF8&amp;me=&amp;qid=\" target=\"_blank\">Lucifer's Star</a>, </i>and the <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Rules-Supervillainy-Saga-Book-ebook/dp/B07MB89S33/\" target=\"_blank\">Supervillainy Saga</a>.</i><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":12002,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","user":"CTPhipps","date":". 04-15-2021, 02:33 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","name":"CTPhipps","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12002_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13933"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-04-15T12:25:59-07:00","id":1444051,"title":"","content":"Right, say they haven't been deleted but everything you loved about them, or loved-to-hate about them, has been ceremoniously derailed into something awful; The Anarchs are Nazi infernalists, The Sabbat are lobbying to have vampires accepted among the mortal populace, the malkavians are all of the fishy variety. <br /> <br /> How can we reasonably undo the damage V5 has done to the anarchs,assamites, camarilla ,Lasombra Sabbat, Samedi, settites,Thinbloods, Tremere, and so on and so forth without hard retcons? (as if most of those werent wildly out of character to fit the V5 story). you could perhaps jump through the right hoops to make course corrections organic for a few pf those factions but for the most part you can't and given the quality of some V5 changes it would be unreasonable to assume many of these factions could be saved with good writing.<br /> <br /> as for the alleged quality of suplements; why would anyone disatisfied with V5 fork out for those? It wouldnt matter if the last book was cancer-curing gold; Why buy in for a product that has so far gone out of its way to ruin things many of us like?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":25794,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25794-mywifeisscary","user":"MyWifeIsScary","date":". 04-15-2021, 03:29 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":7}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25794-mywifeisscary","name":"MyWifeIsScary","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25794_2.png","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3711"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-04-15T12:42:28-07:00","id":1444053,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MyWifeIsScary</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1443592-the-official-v5-vs-v20-thread?p=1443991#post1443991\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">That little poll i threw in at the start of the thread is currently 19:3. Honestly very surprised, I wouldn't think it would be such a landslide so far, especially given which side gets banned more. Or maybe it's the result of only hardcore fans/people with an axe to grind being on the forums and all the people happy with the new edition are busy enjoying the new edition. Maybe a very dedicated fan had 19 accounts and just really wanted the developers/publishers to know his anguish. In any case it's nice to have numbers, and in this case some very strong numbers.</div> </div> </div> </div>I suspect those of us who enjoyed the game or the lore or the world enough to make an account and discuss it here are unusually invested in the game. Very skewered sample.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>AnubisXy</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1443592-the-official-v5-vs-v20-thread?p=1444000#post1444000\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">At the end of the day V5 is really just D&amp;D4th edition Electric Boogaloo.<br /> <br /> In both cases, we got a new edition with some pretty major mechanical overhauls and huge changes to the setting due to questionable in-world events because the designers felt that the existing metaplot had gotten so massive that new players found it intimidating. So the designers decided to clean house by sweeping a lot of that stuff away and making it a &quot;new player friendly edition.&quot;<br /> <br /> Of course, this has the effect of annoying the old school players who had been following that metaplot for years and years, and the mechanic changes were also not met all that well by various older members of the playerbase.</div> </div> </div> </div>I wouldn't go that far. To me, D&amp;D 4th edition felt soulless. Like it was made by consensus by a marketing focus group and a computer game tie.in designer. V5 does not feel anywhere that... empty to me. Whatever else you can say, there is love there. At least for a small slice of the game and the world<br /> <br /> I did think about comparing it to 4rth ed D&amp;D in one way though. The level of mechanical changes is so large, I think it is off-putting to a section of the fan base.<br /> <br /> It is one more reason for me not to shell out money on it (and my treshold for spending money on stuff is much lower than when 1st ed was published). Even concepts I like need a lot of mechanical overhaul. Subjectivly I don't like the visual presentation, there is no mechanics I can use, no elders or elder powers, the metaplot changes are immersion breaking. There is no reason for me to spend money on it.<br /> <br /> I think the level of mechanical change loses more of the fan base than what was necessary.<br /> <br /> You know, its like they have cut out the old game and grafted a new and more limited game into the space in the WoD it occupied. Its not VtM, it is a new game dressed in VtMs worldbuilding, setting and fiction.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":2471,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2471-trollroot","user":"Trollroot","date":". 04-15-2021, 03:47 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2471-trollroot","name":"Trollroot","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"311"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-04-15T12:59:45-07:00","id":1444055,"title":"","content":"For the whole D&amp;D 4e comparison, something worth noting:<br /> <br /> D&amp;D 4e <b>sold</b> really well. Not 5e well, but it outsold 3.X. Why? Because it's D&amp;D. D&amp;D is in an utterly unique market position in the RPG world: they get new players on brand name alone. Since D&amp;D is &quot;the&quot; RPG to most of the world, WotC losing a bunch of older players because the new edition utterly turns them off is actually a drop in the bucket for them. Their brand brings the biggest crowds to organized play (both at local events and bigger ones), their brand is in every major outlet because Hasbro gives them access to a massive distribution machine, etc. For the vast majority of new RPG players every year, their first RPG is going to be the current edition of D&amp;D.<br /> <br /> What V5 has conclusively shown, is that VtM (and the WoD) is not lost as a brand. If you can get the budget to push it so it's in front of people there's still a large chunk of customers out there to buy it that weren't while oWW, CCP, OPP, and so on were keeping it going more like a big indie game than a small medium business game.<br /> <br /> We have no idea how to even start to measure how much of that is the ongoing strength of the VtM brand despite spending the better part of two decades off the casual buyer's radar, or anything specific about V5's take on the game. We're not going to even be able to make educated guesses for until we see things like W5 and how it lands, what it does, etc. Even then, VtM was always the bigger brand and guesses will be tempered by that.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MyWifeIsScary</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1443592-the-official-v5-vs-v20-thread?p=1444051#post1444051\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">why would anyone disatisfied with V5 fork out for those?</div> </div> </div> </div>While the rest is a bit too strongly worded for me, I'd like to point out how vital of a point this is.<br /> <br /> Onyx Path can continually put out top tier books for V5, but you can't sell a core book on the supplements. Who buys something on the pitch of, &quot;Hey, the base product isn't great, but if you double the price for these add-on products it's good!&quot;<br /> <br /> As well, are these supplements even making it to the wider V5 audience in a fashion where any fixing in them is considered &quot;official?&quot; The Kickstarters for the OPP books didn't explode with V5 fans backing in droves. They were solid, but by OPP standards average, KS campaigns. Or are they too obscure with the whole decentralized development thing?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-04-15T13:01:10-07:00","id":1444056,"title":"","content":"I feel a lot of V5's decision making came from a point of 'I don't like this so i will change it' rather than something more constructive and understanding. Most metaplot changes are big and sweeping and hinge on something unlikely. I get the impression that a dev just wanted to canonize their wild homebrew.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":10}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25794-mywifeisscary","name":"MyWifeIsScary","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25794_2.png","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3711"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-04-15T13:34:08-07:00","id":1444061,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Heavy Arms</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1443592-the-official-v5-vs-v20-thread?p=1444055#post1444055\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">For the whole D&amp;D 4e comparison, something worth noting:<br /> <br /> D&amp;D 4e <b>sold</b> really well. Not 5e well, but it outsold 3.X. Why? Because it's D&amp;D. D&amp;D is in an utterly unique market position in the RPG world: they get new players on brand name alone. Since D&amp;D is &quot;the&quot; RPG to most of the world, WotC losing a bunch of older players because the new edition utterly turns them off is actually a drop in the bucket for them. Their brand brings the biggest crowds to organized play (both at local events and bigger ones), their brand is in every major outlet because Hasbro gives them access to a massive distribution machine, etc. For the vast majority of new RPG players every year, their first RPG is going to be the current edition of D&amp;D.</div> </div> </div> </div>Uh... I don't think thats accurate. I mean, everything you say about the advantages of being the brand leader, the household name, the distribution machine is correct. And each of those advantages are huge. But... 4th ed D&amp;D was published in 2007. A 3.5 OGL take by a third party, Pathfinder, was published in 2009. By Q2 in 2011 it was outselling 4rth edition, and 4rth never came back. The third part small publisher 3.5 game utterly destroyed 4th despite all its huge advantages.<br /> <br /> That is why 4th edition is considered such a byword for failiure among RPGs. And a lot of that was the mistakes they made in alienating their fan base. All the new players turned out not to care that they were the new edition of D&amp;D. 4rth ed only outsold 3.5 for about 2 years when they were both published at the same time, and then never again.<br /> <br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2471-trollroot","name":"Trollroot","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"311"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-04-15T13:43:26-07:00","id":1444065,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MyWifeIsScary</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1443592-the-official-v5-vs-v20-thread?p=1444051#post1444051\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Right, say they haven't been deleted but everything you loved about them, or loved-to-hate about them, has been ceremoniously derailed into something awful; The Anarchs are Nazi infernalists, The Sabbat are lobbying to have vampires accepted among the mortal populace, the malkavians are all of the fishy variety.<br /> <br /> How can we reasonably undo the damage V5 has done to the anarchs,assamites, camarilla ,Lasombra Sabbat, Samedi, settites,Thinbloods, Tremere, and so on and so forth without hard retcons? (as if most of those werent wildly out of character to fit the V5 story). you could perhaps jump through the right hoops to make course corrections organic for a few pf those factions but for the most part you can't and given the quality of some V5 changes it would be unreasonable to assume many of these factions could be saved with good writing.<br /> <br /> as for the alleged quality of suplements; why would anyone disatisfied with V5 fork out for those? It wouldnt matter if the last book was cancer-curing gold; Why buy in for a product that has so far gone out of its way to ruin things many of us like?</div> </div> </div> </div>I think then probably its not going to happen because I don't see the changes you hate so much getting reverted. It's a shame but I actually do understand because the Spellplague resulted in me dropping my 20 year love of the Forgotten Realms and even 5th Edition apparently dealt with them but I have no interest in reviving my interest. All future Forgotten Realms games, of which I haven't played any yet, will be set Pre-Spellplague.<br /> <br /> There's just nothing that can repair it.<br /> <br /> So I sympathize. But we fundamentally disagree on what's a good change or not and I would probably drop Vampire forever if it went back to Classic V20 continuity the same way. Which is a sad place to be as a fan.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Heavy Arms</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1443592-the-official-v5-vs-v20-thread?p=1444055#post1444055\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">What V5 has conclusively shown, is that VtM (and the WoD) is not lost as a brand. If you can get the budget to push it so it's in front of people there's still a large chunk of customers out there to buy it that weren't while oWW, CCP, OPP, and so on were keeping it going more like a big indie game than a small medium business game.<br /> <br /> We have no idea how to even start to measure how much of that is the ongoing strength of the VtM brand despite spending the better part of two decades off the casual buyer's radar, or anything specific about V5's take on the game. We're not going to even be able to make educated guesses for until we see things like W5 and how it lands, what it does, etc. Even then, VtM was always the bigger brand and guesses will be tempered by that.</div> </div> </div> </div>Honestly, Paradox Interactive's best contribution to White Wolf's revival is the fact that they seem to understand that the problem is getting awareness of the IP out there. The use of cross-media platforms, Twitch, Youtube, and multimedia is the best way to tell people that Vampire: The Masquerade still exists since a huge chunk of the fanbase thought it ended in 2004.<br /> <br /> One of the most recent videos by Outstar stated that LA BY NIGHT, which was originally a very successful Twitch series had its fanbase doubled by its release on Youtube. A couple of million views. Then it got doubled AGAIN by its release on TikTok. People willing to sit down to watch 3 hours (!) of other people gaming in one sitting.<br /> <br /> WINTER'S TEETH is being written by Tim Seeley, Tini Howard, and Blake Howard of Hack/Slash fame. I'm doing some interviews with them for Grimdark Magazine and Booknest.EU fanzines and they talk about how the comic book is a much bigger success than any of them expected. Most of their fans had no idea 4th Edition/V20 existed and think of it as a revival from the dead or are being introduced to it for the first time by their horror comic fandom.<br /> <br /> The video games are so far small projects but the Visual Novels have hit the top of Steam. They are all mediums for which to experience to the World of Darkness and V5 is serving as the shared medium for handling it.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> While the rest is a bit too strongly worded for me, I'd like to point out how vital of a point this is.<br /> <br /> Onyx Path can continually put out top tier books for V5, but you can't sell a core book on the supplements. Who buys something on the pitch of, &quot;Hey, the base product isn't great, but if you double the price for these add-on products it's good!&quot;<br /> <br /> As well, are these supplements even making it to the wider V5 audience in a fashion where any fixing in them is considered &quot;official?&quot; The Kickstarters for the OPP books didn't explode with V5 fans backing in droves. They were solid, but by OPP standards average, KS campaigns. Or are they too obscure with the whole decentralized development thing? </div> </div> </div>Which seems to be that people who didn't know about the Kickstarter before aren't going to know about it now but previous fans of OPP aren't leaving it behind either. Here's the thing, I bought V20 products and now I buy V5 products. My enthusiasm for either is essentially irrelevant as from a financial standpoint, they read as identical.<br /> <br /> But even then, a larger question is going to be, &quot;Is the tabletop actually the most important product anymore?&quot;<br /> <br /> It's very much a question of how comic book sales matter to Disney's IP with Marvel comics now. It's important but not the main branch of the sales now anymore.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Author of <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Cthulhu-Armageddon-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01KUOM7SI/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982844&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Cthulhu+Armageddon\" target=\"_blank\">Cthulhu Armageddon</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Teenage-Weredeer-Bright-Falls-Mysteries-ebook/dp/B075TTN2FN/ref=sr_1_2?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982717&amp;sr=1-2&amp;keywords=Weredeer#customerReviews\" target=\"_blank\">I was a Teenage Weredeer</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Straight-Outta-Fangton-Comedic-Vampire-ebook/dp/B01KNHICCC/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982774&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Straight+Outta+Fangton\" target=\"_blank\">Straight Outta Fangton</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Lucifers-Star-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01MDM9MCT/ref=mt_kindle?_encoding=UTF8&amp;me=&amp;qid=\" target=\"_blank\">Lucifer's Star</a>, </i>and the <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Rules-Supervillainy-Saga-Book-ebook/dp/B07MB89S33/\" target=\"_blank\">Supervillainy Saga</a>.</i><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":12002,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","user":"CTPhipps","date":". 04-15-2021, 05:01 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","name":"CTPhipps","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12002_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13933"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-04-15T14:06:18-07:00","id":1444066,"title":"","content":"To put an interesting frame-work into it:<br /> <br /> * Not everyone bought Chicago by Night 5th Edition (their loss).<br /> <br /> * Chicago by Night 5th Edition published the rules for the Lasombra and made them part of the Camarilla.<br /> <br /> * The Lasombra being part of the Camarilla is a major part of Season 3 and Season 4 of LA by Night as well as Penny Arcade's V:TM game.<br /> <br /> * The Lasombra being part of the Camarilla is the basis for SHADOWS OF NEW YORK's visual novel.<br /> <br /> * It probably will be incorporated into other upcoming V:TM products like Bloodlines 2 and Swansong.<br /> <br /> * Chicago by Night 5th Edition thus has a much bigger impact on the lore than necessarily its sales suggests.<br /> <br /> * V5 is now the shared language for reaching a far larger audience that may not tabletop game anymore. Just like Bloodlines became that for many video gamers but not tabletop gamers.<br /> <br /> I admit part of my opinion is also driven by the fact that OPP may not be the primary purveyor of World of Darkness RPG publications (which is a shame because they are top quality writers) but they are certainly people whose members are heavily involved in the molding of the intellectual property to Paradox Entertainment.<br /> <br /> Matthew Dawkins wrote for The Camarilla and the ancestor cutls that eventually got approved to make Cults of the Blood Gods. He also is writing for Swansong (good for him) so he's moved to working on video game writing as well. He also is the guy who wrote for the Ministry's current status as well as the Lasombra defecting to the Camarilla in the first place.<br /> <br /> Other writers of the gameline from past Editions like Jason Carl, Mark Rein Hagen, and Justin Achilli are also adding their stuff to the work. So it's not like the DNA has fundamentally changed to the game.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Author of <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Cthulhu-Armageddon-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01KUOM7SI/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982844&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Cthulhu+Armageddon\" target=\"_blank\">Cthulhu Armageddon</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Teenage-Weredeer-Bright-Falls-Mysteries-ebook/dp/B075TTN2FN/ref=sr_1_2?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982717&amp;sr=1-2&amp;keywords=Weredeer#customerReviews\" target=\"_blank\">I was a Teenage Weredeer</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Straight-Outta-Fangton-Comedic-Vampire-ebook/dp/B01KNHICCC/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982774&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Straight+Outta+Fangton\" target=\"_blank\">Straight Outta Fangton</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Lucifers-Star-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01MDM9MCT/ref=mt_kindle?_encoding=UTF8&amp;me=&amp;qid=\" target=\"_blank\">Lucifer's Star</a>, </i>and the <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Rules-Supervillainy-Saga-Book-ebook/dp/B07MB89S33/\" target=\"_blank\">Supervillainy Saga</a>.</i><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":12002,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","user":"CTPhipps","date":". 04-15-2021, 05:16 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","name":"CTPhipps","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12002_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13933"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-04-15T15:12:46-07:00","id":1444071,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Heavy Arms</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1443592-the-official-v5-vs-v20-thread?p=1444055#post1444055\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">For the whole D&amp;D 4e comparison, something worth noting:<br /> <br /> D&amp;D 4e <b>sold</b> really well. Not 5e well, but it outsold 3.X. Why? Because it's D&amp;D. D&amp;D is in an utterly unique market position in the RPG world: they get new players on brand name alone. Since D&amp;D is &quot;the&quot; RPG to most of the world, WotC losing a bunch of older players because the new edition utterly turns them off is actually a drop in the bucket for them. Their brand brings the biggest crowds to organized play (both at local events and bigger ones), their brand is in every major outlet because Hasbro gives them access to a massive distribution machine, etc. For the vast majority of new RPG players every year, their first RPG is going to be the current edition of D&amp;D.<br /> <br /> What V5 has conclusively shown, is that VtM (and the WoD) is not lost as a brand. If you can get the budget to push it so it's in front of people there's still a large chunk of customers out there to buy it that weren't while oWW, CCP, OPP, and so on were keeping it going more like a big indie game than a small medium business game.<br /> <br /> We have no idea how to even start to measure how much of that is the ongoing strength of the VtM brand despite spending the better part of two decades off the casual buyer's radar, or anything specific about V5's take on the game. We're not going to even be able to make educated guesses for until we see things like W5 and how it lands, what it does, etc. Even then, VtM was always the bigger brand and guesses will be tempered by that.<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> While the rest is a bit too strongly worded for me, I'd like to point out how vital of a point this is.<br /> <br /> Onyx Path can continually put out top tier books for V5, but you can't sell a core book on the supplements. Who buys something on the pitch of, &quot;Hey, the base product isn't great, but if you double the price for these add-on products it's good!&quot;<br /> <br /> As well, are these supplements even making it to the wider V5 audience in a fashion where any fixing in them is considered &quot;official?&quot; The Kickstarters for the OPP books didn't explode with V5 fans backing in droves. They were solid, but by OPP standards average, KS campaigns. Or are they too obscure with the whole decentralized development thing?</div> </div> </div> </div>About this there has something to be said. D&amp;D 4 except core rules and most of WoD and CofD where not even translated into other languages. Now both x20 Series and V5 is same as D&amp;D5 is a big translated market.<br /> So V20, V5 and D&amp;D 5 will just getting massivly bought by many people just because they heard of the name of it and it is finally translated again.<br /> A study shows that at least 40% of the customers will not buy a product if it is not in their language which I think is even higher in P&amp;P because you need to read and understand what is written their to really use it and have fun with it. The german market means you get another 16% aka 1/6 of your english consumer base.<br /> V20 and D&amp;D 5 are released 15 and 17 in German and are both already at the fifth reprint. V5 released last June in German is still at first print with even the collectors version still available.<br /> The crowdfundings for german V20 and DA20 where each 114.000\u20ac and for the translation of Beckett's Jyhad Diary and the lates W20 books we have 234 people paying a total of 45.194\u20ac.<br /> Comparing the english and german Kickstarter show the 1/6 is true so the german V20 brought at least 400 additional well paying fans. If we go by the numbers of reprints where one series has between 300 and 500 books that means we have between 1000 and 2000 ordinary fans though even that may be higher if only one book is bought per group.<br /> <br /> Anyway I think we can see from the reprint rates that My Wife is Scary's poll from the first page is representative showing that despite thise whole more money and reaching the masses that the fifth edition is only reaching a fifth of the VtM fans.<br /> <br /> Sources:<br /> <div class=\"b-bbcode b-bbcode__url b-bbcode__url--preview\"> <a href=\"https://csa-research.com/More/Media/Press-Releases/ArticleID/31/Survey-of-3-000-Online-Shoppers-Across-10-Countries-Finds-that-60-Rarely-or-Never-Buy-from-English-only-Websites\" target=\"_blank\" class=\"urlimg_container\"> <img class=\"js-img-fallback\" src=\"https://csa-research.com/Portals/0/Images/Banners/cover.jpg\"> </a> <div class=\"urlinfo\"> <div class=\"title ellipsis\"> <a href=\"https://csa-research.com/More/Media/Press-Releases/ArticleID/31/Survey-of-3-000-Online-Shoppers-Across-10-Countries-Finds-that-60-Rarely-or-Never-Buy-from-English-only-Websites\" target=\"_blank\"> CSA Research </a> </div> <div class=\"url ellipsis\"> <a href=\"https://csa-research.com/More/Media/Press-Releases/ArticleID/31/Survey-of-3-000-Online-Shoppers-Across-10-Countries-Finds-that-60-Rarely-or-Never-Buy-from-English-only-Websites\" target=\"_blank\"> https://csa-research.com/More/Media/Press-Releases/ArticleID/31/Survey-of-3-000-Online-Shoppers-Across-10-Countries-Finds-that-60-Rarely-or-Never-Buy-from-English-only-Websites </a> </div> <div class=\"meta\"> Succeed in a global business environment. CSA Research is the first place to look for data and market research on globalization, localization, internationalization, content marketing, and language technology. </div> </div> </div><br /> <div class=\"b-bbcode b-bbcode__url b-bbcode__url--preview\"> <a href=\"https://hbr.org/2012/08/speak-to-global-customers-in-t\" target=\"_blank\" class=\"urlimg_container\"> <img class=\"js-img-fallback\" src=\"https://hbr.org/assets-mfe-articles/_next/static/media/Twitter.2ht2cms5y_jst.svg\"> </a> <div class=\"urlinfo\"> <div class=\"title ellipsis\"> <a href=\"https://hbr.org/2012/08/speak-to-global-customers-in-t\" target=\"_blank\"> Speak to Global Customers in Their Own Language </a> </div> <div class=\"url ellipsis\"> <a href=\"https://hbr.org/2012/08/speak-to-global-customers-in-t\" target=\"_blank\"> https://hbr.org/2012/08/speak-to-global-customers-in-t </a> </div> <div class=\"meta\"> Do you struggle to reach customers beyond your own country&rsquo;s borders? If targeting clients in other countries seems daunting, there is one simple step you can start with: Translate something. You have to speak the language of your customers. And that isn&rsquo;t just an overused metaphor. It refers to actual languages &mdash; like Spanish, French, [&hellip;] </div> </div> </div><br /> <div class=\"b-bbcode b-bbcode__url b-bbcode__url--preview\"> <a href=\"https://blog.supertext.ch/en/2020/08/translation-and-localization-is-it-worth-it/\" target=\"_blank\" class=\"urlimg_container\"> <img class=\"js-img-fallback\" src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/default/google-material/image_placeholder.svg\"> </a> <div class=\"urlinfo\"> <div class=\"title ellipsis\"> <a href=\"https://blog.supertext.ch/en/2020/08/translation-and-localization-is-it-worth-it/\" target=\"_blank\"> </a> </div> <div class=\"url ellipsis\"> <a href=\"https://blog.supertext.ch/en/2020/08/translation-and-localization-is-it-worth-it/\" target=\"_blank\"> https://blog.supertext.ch/en/2020/08/translation-and-localization-is-it-worth-it/ </a> </div> <div class=\"meta\"> </div> </div> </div><br /> <a href=\"https://www.kickstarter.com/projects/200664283/deluxe-v20-becketts-jyhad-diary/description\" target=\"_blank\">https://www.kickstarter.com/projects...ry/description</a><br /> <div class=\"b-bbcode b-bbcode__url b-bbcode__url--preview\"> <a href=\"https://www.gameontabletop.com/cf175/vampire-werwolf-die-jubilaumsausgaben.html\" target=\"_blank\" class=\"urlimg_container\"> <img class=\"js-img-fallback\" src=\"https://www.gameontabletop.com/contenu/image/fb_share/175_rc-Ey_0w8nT-4ig9x-x2ey5gCzvw.jpg\"> </a> <div class=\"urlinfo\"> <div class=\"title ellipsis\"> <a href=\"https://www.gameontabletop.com/cf175/vampire-werwolf-die-jubilaumsausgaben.html\" target=\"_blank\"> Vampire &amp; Werwolf: Die Jubil&auml;umsausgaben (Ulisses Spiele) </a> </div> <div class=\"url ellipsis\"> <a href=\"https://www.gameontabletop.com/cf175/vampire-werwolf-die-jubilaumsausgaben.html\" target=\"_blank\"> https://www.gameontabletop.com/cf175/vampire-werwolf-die-jubilaumsausgaben.html </a> </div> <div class=\"meta\"> Crowdfunding: Vampire &amp; Werwolf: Die Jubil&auml;umsausgaben (Ulisses Spiele) </div> </div> </div><br /> <div class=\"b-bbcode b-bbcode__url b-bbcode__url--preview\"> <a href=\"https://www.teilzeithelden.de/2017/03/23/magus-die-erleuchtung-im-ulisses-crowdfunding/\" target=\"_blank\" class=\"urlimg_container\"> <img class=\"js-img-fallback\" src=\"https://i1.wp.com/www.teilzeithelden.de/wp-content/uploads/2017/03/magus.jpg?fit=708%2C404&amp;ssl=1\"> </a> <div class=\"urlinfo\"> <div class=\"title ellipsis\"> <a href=\"https://www.teilzeithelden.de/2017/03/23/magus-die-erleuchtung-im-ulisses-crowdfunding/\" target=\"_blank\"> Magus: Die Erleuchtung im Ulisses Crowdfunding - </a> </div> <div class=\"url ellipsis\"> <a href=\"https://www.teilzeithelden.de/2017/03/23/magus-die-erleuchtung-im-ulisses-crowdfunding/\" target=\"_blank\"> https://www.teilzeithelden.de/2017/03/23/magus-die-erleuchtung-im-ulisses-crowdfunding/ </a> </div> <div class=\"meta\"> Bereits 2015 legte Ulisses das beliebte Regelwerk zu Vampire: Die Maskerade&nbsp;anl&auml;sslich des 20-j&auml;hrigen Jubil&auml;ums in einem Crowdfunding neu auf. &Uuml;ber 113.000 EUR konnte der Verlag in rund einem Monat sammeln. [&hellip;] </div> </div> </div><br /> <div class=\"b-bbcode b-bbcode__url b-bbcode__url--preview\"> <a href=\"https://www.f-shop.de/die-welt-der-dunkelheit/vampire-die-maskerade-v20/regel-und-quellenbaende/573/vampire-die-maskerade-jubilaeumsausgabe-v20\" target=\"_blank\" class=\"urlimg_container\"> <img class=\"js-img-fallback\" src=\"https://www.f-shop.de/media/image/54/4a/61/US80000_0.jpg\"> </a> <div class=\"urlinfo\"> <div class=\"title ellipsis\"> <a href=\"https://www.f-shop.de/die-welt-der-dunkelheit/vampire-die-maskerade-v20/regel-und-quellenbaende/573/vampire-die-maskerade-jubilaeumsausgabe-v20\" target=\"_blank\"> Vampire: Die Maskerade Jubil&auml;umsausgabe (V20) </a> </div> <div class=\"url ellipsis\"> <a href=\"https://www.f-shop.de/die-welt-der-dunkelheit/vampire-die-maskerade-v20/regel-und-quellenbaende/573/vampire-die-maskerade-jubilaeumsausgabe-v20\" target=\"_blank\"> https://www.f-shop.de/die-welt-der-dunkelheit/vampire-die-maskerade-v20/regel-und-quellenbaende/573/vampire-die-maskerade-jubilaeumsausgabe-v20 </a> </div> <div class=\"meta\"> Vampire: Die Maskerade hat Anfang der 1990er Jahre die Rollenspiel-Welt ver&auml;ndert. Der Spielleiter wurde zum Erz&auml;hler und gemeinsam gestaltete die Gruppe&hellip; </div> </div> </div><br /> <div class=\"b-bbcode b-bbcode__url b-bbcode__url--preview\"> <a href=\"https://www.f-shop.de/vampire-v5/1698/v5-vampire-die-maskerade-regelwerk\" target=\"_blank\" class=\"urlimg_container\"> <img class=\"js-img-fallback\" src=\"https://www.f-shop.de/media/image/6e/f8/c0/Vorderseitewe8LmUY9VNUgK.jpg\"> </a> <div class=\"urlinfo\"> <div class=\"title ellipsis\"> <a href=\"https://www.f-shop.de/vampire-v5/1698/v5-vampire-die-maskerade-regelwerk\" target=\"_blank\"> V5 Vampire - Die Maskerade: Regelwerk </a> </div> <div class=\"url ellipsis\"> <a href=\"https://www.f-shop.de/vampire-v5/1698/v5-vampire-die-maskerade-regelwerk\" target=\"_blank\"> https://www.f-shop.de/vampire-v5/1698/v5-vampire-die-maskerade-regelwerk </a> </div> <div class=\"meta\"> Niemand hat Gewalt &uuml;ber mich. Kein Mensch. Kein Gott. Kein Prinz. Was bedeutet der Anspruch des Alters f&uuml;r diejenigen, die unsterblich sind? Was bedeutet&hellip; </div> </div> </div>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>As I am from Austria I need to clarify two things.<br /> First my native language is german and so please point out if the english I write is broken so I can improve.<br /> Second I do not own VTMV beyond first three books nor any line after M20 Corebook because it is not out there and I wait for the translation.","edited":{"userid":26160,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26160-koronus","user":"Koronus","date":". 04-15-2021, 06:15 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26160-koronus","name":"Koronus","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2020"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"366"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-04-15T15:20:50-07:00","id":1444072,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CTPhipps</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1443592-the-official-v5-vs-v20-thread?p=1444066#post1444066\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">So it's not like the DNA has fundamentally changed to the game.</div> </div> </div> </div>For me, the issue is exactly that the DNA has fundamentally changed. Other people have articulated their frustrations with the changes much better than I have, so I won't get into comparing and contrasting specific system, lore and flavor changes, but I will say there is nothing I actively, strongly dislike about 2nd Ed, Rev, V20, V:tDA, DA:V or V:tDA20.<br /> <br /> With V5, I have a list. And I did give it a couple years, so it's not just a knee-jerk reaction of a 40-something who fears change.<br /> <br /> Sidenote, Achilli did work on past editions, sure, but he also wrote the Companion which effectively deleted Clan Tzimisce as we've known it for 30 years by fundamentally changing their DNA...the irony of which I can actually appreciate.<br /> <br /> Anyway, it does seem that there are plenty of people who enjoy and even prefer V5, and I think that's pretty cool. I wouldn't want to do anything to take away from that. V5 won't miss my dollars, and I can always keep hope alive for future V:tM supplements.<br /> <br /> V40 perhaps...","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":10}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24351-garygeneric","name":"Garygeneric","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24351_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"108"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-04-15T15:32:55-07:00","id":1444075,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Koronus</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1443592-the-official-v5-vs-v20-thread?p=1444071#post1444071\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> About this there has something to be said. D&amp;D 4 except core rules and most of WoD and CofD where not even translated into other languages. Now both x20 Series and V5 is same as D&amp;D5 is a big translated market.<br /> So V20, V5 and D&amp;D 5 will just getting massivly bought by many people just because they heard of the name of it and it is finally translated again.<br /> A study shows that at least 40% of the customers will not buy a product if it is not in their language which I think is even higher in P&amp;P because you need to read and understand what is written their to really use it and have fun with it. The german market means you get another 16% aka 1/6 of your english consumer base.<br /> V20 and D&amp;D 5 are released 15 and 17 in German and are both already at the fifth reprint. V5 released last June in German is still at first print with even the collectors version still available.<br /> The crowdfundings for german V20 and DA20 where each 114.000\u20ac and for the translation of Beckett's Jyhad Diary and the lates W20 books we have 234 people paying a total of 45.194\u20ac.<br /> Comparing the english and german Kickstarter show the 1/6 is true so the german V20 brought at least 400 additional well paying fans. If we go by the numbers of reprints where one series has between 300 and 500 books that means we have between 1000 and 2000 ordinary fans though even that may be higher if only one book is bought per group.<br /> <br /> Anyway I think we can see from the reprint rates that My Wife is Scary's poll from the first page is representative showing that despite thise whole more money and reaching the masses that the fifth edition is only reaching a fifth of the VtM fans.<br /> <br /> Sources:<br /> <a href=\"https://csa-research.com/More/Media/Press-Releases/ArticleID/31/Survey-of-3-000-Online-Shoppers-Across-10-Countries-Finds-that-60-Rarely-or-Never-Buy-from-English-only-Websites\" target=\"_blank\">https://csa-research.com/More/Media/...-only-Websites</a><br /> <div class=\"b-bbcode b-bbcode__url b-bbcode__url--preview\"> <a href=\"https://hbr.org/2012/08/speak-to-global-customers-in-t\" target=\"_blank\" class=\"urlimg_container\"> <img class=\"js-img-fallback\" src=\"https://hbr.org/assets-mfe-articles/_next/static/media/Twitter.2ht2cms5y_jst.svg\"> </a> <div class=\"urlinfo\"> <div class=\"title ellipsis\"> <a href=\"https://hbr.org/2012/08/speak-to-global-customers-in-t\" target=\"_blank\"> Speak to Global Customers in Their Own Language </a> </div> <div class=\"url ellipsis\"> <a href=\"https://hbr.org/2012/08/speak-to-global-customers-in-t\" target=\"_blank\"> https://hbr.org/2012/08/speak-to-global-customers-in-t </a> </div> <div class=\"meta\"> Do you struggle to reach customers beyond your own country&rsquo;s borders? If targeting clients in other countries seems daunting, there is one simple step you can start with: Translate something. You have to speak the language of your customers. And that isn&rsquo;t just an overused metaphor. It refers to actual languages &mdash; like Spanish, French, [&hellip;] </div> </div> </div><br /> <a href=\"https://blog.supertext.ch/en/2020/08/translation-and-localization-is-it-worth-it/\" target=\"_blank\">https://blog.supertext.ch/en/2020/08...s-it-worth-it/</a><br /> <a href=\"https://www.kickstarter.com/projects/200664283/deluxe-v20-becketts-jyhad-diary/description\" target=\"_blank\">https://www.kickstarter.com/projects...ry/description</a><br /> <a href=\"https://www.gameontabletop.com/cf175/vampire-werwolf-die-jubilaumsausgaben.html\" target=\"_blank\">https://www.gameontabletop.com/cf175...sausgaben.html</a><br /> <a href=\"https://www.teilzeithelden.de/2017/03/23/magus-die-erleuchtung-im-ulisses-crowdfunding/\" target=\"_blank\">https://www.teilzeithelden.de/2017/0...-crowdfunding/</a><br /> <a href=\"https://www.f-shop.de/die-welt-der-dunkelheit/vampire-die-maskerade-v20/regel-und-quellenbaende/573/vampire-die-maskerade-jubilaeumsausgabe-v20\" target=\"_blank\">https://www.f-shop.de/die-welt-der-d...umsausgabe-v20</a><br /> <a href=\"https://www.f-shop.de/vampire-v5/1698/v5-vampire-die-maskerade-regelwerk\" target=\"_blank\">https://www.f-shop.de/vampire-v5/169...rade-regelwerk</a></div> </div> </div> </div>I feel kind of bad pointing out that the translation of V5 to different languages and the embracing of the international fandom is a major point of Paradox's marketing strategy.<br /> <br /> I mean, we wouldn't have had the controversy for Chechnya if it wasn't translated and put in....Russian by the localizers.<br /> <br /> <a href=\"https://www.modiphius.com/modiphius-press-releases/vampire-the-masquerade-5th-edition-launching-in-seven-languages\" target=\"_blank\">https://www.modiphius.com/modiphius-...even-languages</a><br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <b><span style=\"color:#000000\">Vampire: The Masquerade 5th Edition Launching in Seven Languages </span></b><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\">Modiphius Entertainment is proud to announce a host of partnerships that will bring Vampire: The Masquerade Fifth Edition into the hands of fans around the world who\u2019ve been waiting on this new edition to release in their language.</span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\">Arkhane Asylum, Need Games!, and Nosolorol have already brought us V5 in </span><span style=\"color:#000000\">French</span><span style=\"color:#000000\">, </span><span style=\"color:#000000\">Italian, </span><span style=\"color:#000000\">and </span><span style=\"color:#000000\">Spanish</span><span style=\"color:#000000\"> respectively this summer. Now, the list of languages Vampire is going to be translated into includes </span><span style=\"color:#000000\">German</span><span style=\"color:#000000\">, thanks to Ulisses Spiele, </span><span style=\"color:#000000\">Portuguese</span><span style=\"color:#000000\">, thanks to Gal\u00e1pagos Jogos, and </span><span style=\"color:#000000\">Russian</span><span style=\"color:#000000\">, thanks to Studio 101!</span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\">Sign up on the partner's websites for more information about product releases and availability. Further partners will be advanced in the near future. </span><ul><li><span style=\"color:#000000\">France - Arkhane Asylum -</span><a href=\"https://www.arkhane-asylum.fr/\" target=\"_blank\">https://www.arkhane-asylum.fr/</a></li> <li><span style=\"color:#000000\">Germany - Ulisses Spiele -</span><a href=\"https://ulisses-spiele.de/\" target=\"_blank\">https://ulisses-spiele.de/</a></li> <li><span style=\"color:#000000\">Spain - Nosolorol -</span><a href=\"https://www.nosolorol.com/\" target=\"_blank\">https://www.nosolorol.com/</a></li> <li><span style=\"color:#000000\">Italy - Need Games! -</span><a href=\"https://www.needgames.it/\" target=\"_blank\">https://www.needgames.it/</a></li> <li><span style=\"color:#000000\">Brazil - Gal\u00e1pagos Jogos -</span><a href=\"https://www.galapagosjogos.com.br/\" target=\"_blank\">https://www.galapagosjogos.com.br/</a></li> <li><span style=\"color:#000000\">Russia - Studio 101 -</span><a href=\"https://studio101.ru/\" target=\"_blank\">https://studio101.ru/</a></li> </ul> </div> </div> </div>So it's in French, German, Spanish, Italian, Portugese, and Russian. Oh and English.<br /> <br /> I am curious, though.<br /> <br /> Do people not actually think V5 is succeeding fantastically? I mean, it's irrelevant to the quality of the product but I thought it was accepted that V5 is an unqualified sales success.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Author of <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Cthulhu-Armageddon-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01KUOM7SI/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982844&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Cthulhu+Armageddon\" target=\"_blank\">Cthulhu Armageddon</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Teenage-Weredeer-Bright-Falls-Mysteries-ebook/dp/B075TTN2FN/ref=sr_1_2?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982717&amp;sr=1-2&amp;keywords=Weredeer#customerReviews\" target=\"_blank\">I was a Teenage Weredeer</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Straight-Outta-Fangton-Comedic-Vampire-ebook/dp/B01KNHICCC/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982774&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Straight+Outta+Fangton\" target=\"_blank\">Straight Outta Fangton</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Lucifers-Star-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01MDM9MCT/ref=mt_kindle?_encoding=UTF8&amp;me=&amp;qid=\" target=\"_blank\">Lucifer's Star</a>, </i>and the <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Rules-Supervillainy-Saga-Book-ebook/dp/B07MB89S33/\" target=\"_blank\">Supervillainy Saga</a>.</i><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":12002,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","user":"CTPhipps","date":". 04-15-2021, 06:35 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","name":"CTPhipps","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12002_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13933"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-04-15T15:41:24-07:00","id":1444076,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Garygeneric</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1443592-the-official-v5-vs-v20-thread?p=1444072#post1444072\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> For me, the issue is exactly that the DNA has fundamentally changed. Other people have articulated their frustrations with the changes much better than I have, so I won't get into comparing and contrasting specific system, lore and flavor changes, but I will say there is nothing I actively, strongly dislike about 2nd Ed, Rev, V20, V:tDA, DA:V or V:tDA20.<br /> <br /> With V5, I have a list. And I did give it a couple years, so it's not just a knee-jerk reaction of a 40-something who fears change.<br /> <br /> Sidenote, Achilli did work on past editions, sure, but he also wrote the Companion which effectively deleted Clan Tzimisce as we've known it for 30 years by fundamentally changing their DNA...the irony of which I can actually appreciate.<br /> <br /> Anyway, it does seem that there are plenty of people who enjoy and even prefer V5, and I think that's pretty cool. I wouldn't want to do anything to take away from that. V5 won't miss my dollars, and I can always keep hope alive for future V:tM supplements.<br /> <br /> V40 perhaps...</div> </div> </div> </div>Understandable.<br /> <br /> I admit, though as a Tzimisce fan but of the Dark Ages version, what did you feel was lost by the Tzimisve 5E?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Author of <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Cthulhu-Armageddon-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01KUOM7SI/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982844&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Cthulhu+Armageddon\" target=\"_blank\">Cthulhu Armageddon</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Teenage-Weredeer-Bright-Falls-Mysteries-ebook/dp/B075TTN2FN/ref=sr_1_2?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982717&amp;sr=1-2&amp;keywords=Weredeer#customerReviews\" target=\"_blank\">I was a Teenage Weredeer</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Straight-Outta-Fangton-Comedic-Vampire-ebook/dp/B01KNHICCC/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982774&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Straight+Outta+Fangton\" target=\"_blank\">Straight Outta Fangton</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Lucifers-Star-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01MDM9MCT/ref=mt_kindle?_encoding=UTF8&amp;me=&amp;qid=\" target=\"_blank\">Lucifer's Star</a>, </i>and the <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Rules-Supervillainy-Saga-Book-ebook/dp/B07MB89S33/\" target=\"_blank\">Supervillainy Saga</a>.</i><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","name":"CTPhipps","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12002_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13933"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-04-15T15:48:01-07:00","id":1444077,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Garygeneric</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1443592-the-official-v5-vs-v20-thread?p=1444072#post1444072\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> For me, the issue is exactly that the DNA has fundamentally changed. Other people have articulated their frustrations with the changes much better than I have, so I won't get into comparing and contrasting specific system, lore and flavor changes, but I will say there is nothing I actively, strongly dislike about 2nd Ed, Rev, V20, V:tDA, DA:V or V:tDA20.<br /> <br /> With V5, I have a list. And I did give it a couple years, so it's not just a knee-jerk reaction of a 40-something who fears change.<br /> <br /> Sidenote, Achilli did work on past editions, sure, but he also wrote the Companion which effectively deleted Clan Tzimisce as we've known it for 30 years by fundamentally changing their DNA...the irony of which I can actually appreciate.<br /> <br /> Anyway, it does seem that there are plenty of people who enjoy and even prefer V5, and I think that's pretty cool. I wouldn't want to do anything to take away from that. V5 won't miss my dollars, and I can always keep hope alive for future V:tM supplements.<br /> <br /> V40 perhaps...</div> </div> </div> </div>Just so. I've been here before, with Requiem. Give it a few years, or decades if we must,<br /> <br /> 4th ed looked really successful until it got a competitor. I suspect there is some underestimation of how much roleplaying is a socially transferred hobby, how many pick it up through their friends and what percentage do it trough buying a book and reading it.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":2471,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2471-trollroot","user":"Trollroot","date":". 04-15-2021, 06:51 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":6}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2471-trollroot","name":"Trollroot","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"311"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-04-15T15:52:40-07:00","id":1444079,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CTPhipps</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1443592-the-official-v5-vs-v20-thread?p=1444075#post1444075\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I feel kind of bad pointing out that the translation of V5 to different languages and the embracing of the international fandom is a major point of Paradox's marketing strategy.<br /> <br /> I mean, we wouldn't have had the controversy for Chechnya if it wasn't translated and put in....Russian by the localizers.<br /> <br /> <a href=\"https://www.modiphius.com/modiphius-press-releases/vampire-the-masquerade-5th-edition-launching-in-seven-languages\" target=\"_blank\">https://www.modiphius.com/modiphius-...even-languages</a><br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> So it's in French, German, Spanish, Italian, Portugese, and Russian. Oh and English.<br /> <br /> I am curious, though.<br /> <br /> Do people not actually think V5 is succeeding fantastically? I mean, it's irrelevant to the quality of the product but I thought it was accepted that V5 is an unqualified sales success.</div> </div> </div> </div>Well in DACHL people are more annoyed that Paradox is not giving out licences for giving the right to translate everything after the M20 core rulebook.<br /> So we got complete V20 and W20 in german but M20 is staying alone. Fans regulary ask Ulisses Spiele about news when finally the crowdfundings for the rest of the x20 series is starting and they start saying that there is no plan for now because they still got now licence to translate the rest.<br /> Actually we cheered about every news where it is said, that V5 is having another setback.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>As I am from Austria I need to clarify two things.<br /> First my native language is german and so please point out if the english I write is broken so I can improve.<br /> Second I do not own VTMV beyond first three books nor any line after M20 Corebook because it is not out there and I wait for the translation.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":6}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26160-koronus","name":"Koronus","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2020"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"366"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-04-15T15:53:48-07:00","id":1444080,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Trollroot</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1443592-the-official-v5-vs-v20-thread?p=1444077#post1444077\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Just so. I've been here before, with Requiem. Give it a few years, or decades if we must,<br /> <br /> 4th ed looked really successful until it got a competitor. I suspect there is some underestimation of how much roleplaying is a socially transferred hobby, how many pick it up through their friends and what percentage do it trough buying a book and reading it.</div> </div> </div> </div>Yes, I also think people should be prepared that this will become the introduction for large numbers of new players and their reality.<br /> <br /> And the basis of the next edition may be even more different.<br /> <br /> But I don't begrudge you cynicism versus optimism. I do hope you'll find something you like in the future works of the game, though.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Author of <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Cthulhu-Armageddon-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01KUOM7SI/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982844&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Cthulhu+Armageddon\" target=\"_blank\">Cthulhu Armageddon</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Teenage-Weredeer-Bright-Falls-Mysteries-ebook/dp/B075TTN2FN/ref=sr_1_2?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982717&amp;sr=1-2&amp;keywords=Weredeer#customerReviews\" target=\"_blank\">I was a Teenage Weredeer</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Straight-Outta-Fangton-Comedic-Vampire-ebook/dp/B01KNHICCC/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982774&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Straight+Outta+Fangton\" target=\"_blank\">Straight Outta Fangton</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Lucifers-Star-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01MDM9MCT/ref=mt_kindle?_encoding=UTF8&amp;me=&amp;qid=\" target=\"_blank\">Lucifer's Star</a>, </i>and the <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Rules-Supervillainy-Saga-Book-ebook/dp/B07MB89S33/\" target=\"_blank\">Supervillainy Saga</a>.</i><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","name":"CTPhipps","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12002_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13933"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-04-15T16:07:29-07:00","id":1444084,"title":"","content":"To be fair V5 has had millions more advertising dollars spent on promoting it than any previous edition...and yet is still consistently decimated in every single online poll on every platform by previous editions.<br /> <br /> By the amount of investment it's had it should be steamrolling everything in its path...the only game receiving more marketing dollars currently is D&amp;D 5e.<br /> <br /> Some may say that the majority of V5 players don't use forums...or Facebook...or YouTube...or Discord...but Paradox certainly doesn't feel that way considering their marketing campaign.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":479,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/479-damian-may","user":"Damian May","date":". 04-15-2021, 07:12 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":6}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/479-damian-may","name":"Damian May","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar479_1.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1199"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-04-15T16:12:04-07:00","id":1444085,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Koronus</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1443592-the-official-v5-vs-v20-thread?p=1444079#post1444079\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Well in DACHL people are more annoyed that Paradox is not giving out licences for giving the right to translate everything after the M20 core rulebook.<br /> So we got complete V20 and W20 in german but M20 is staying alone. Fans regulary ask Ulisses Spiele about news when finally the crowdfundings for the rest of the x20 series is starting and they start saying that there is no plan for now because they still got now licence to translate the rest.<br /> Actually we cheered about every news where it is said, that V5 is having another setback.</div> </div> </div> </div>Paradox killing translation and development for lines that they weren't going to develop themselves for years to come was an arsehole move to be sure. They've since loosened up slightly on W20 and M20 giving new books the go ahead so maybe translations might happen.<br /> <br /> They certainly don't seem overly bothered about isolating vast swathes of the OWoD fandom.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/479-damian-may","name":"Damian May","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar479_1.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1199"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-04-15T16:36:52-07:00","id":1444088,"title":"","content":"This is a very eye opening thread. Apparently people see things very differently than me. I appreciate everyone taking the time to share their thoughts.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Author of <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Cthulhu-Armageddon-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01KUOM7SI/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982844&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Cthulhu+Armageddon\" target=\"_blank\">Cthulhu Armageddon</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Teenage-Weredeer-Bright-Falls-Mysteries-ebook/dp/B075TTN2FN/ref=sr_1_2?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982717&amp;sr=1-2&amp;keywords=Weredeer#customerReviews\" target=\"_blank\">I was a Teenage Weredeer</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Straight-Outta-Fangton-Comedic-Vampire-ebook/dp/B01KNHICCC/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982774&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Straight+Outta+Fangton\" target=\"_blank\">Straight Outta Fangton</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Lucifers-Star-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01MDM9MCT/ref=mt_kindle?_encoding=UTF8&amp;me=&amp;qid=\" target=\"_blank\">Lucifer's Star</a>, </i>and the <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Rules-Supervillainy-Saga-Book-ebook/dp/B07MB89S33/\" target=\"_blank\">Supervillainy Saga</a>.</i><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","name":"CTPhipps","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12002_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13933"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-04-15T16:39:53-07:00","id":1444089,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CTPhipps</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1443592-the-official-v5-vs-v20-thread?p=1444080#post1444080\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Yes, I also think people should be prepared that this will become the introduction for large numbers of new players and their reality.</div> </div> </div> </div>I think you may have misunderstood. While I do believe that V5 is a better game than D&amp;D 4th edition, I think there was an important lesson in 4th eds failiure.<br /> It had a big launch, huge initial success. Corebooks on the bestseller lists. Marketing engine, market leader, conventions, it had the works.<br /> <br /> It folded as soon as a competitor arrived.<br /> <br /> Partially that was because it was just not a very good game. But it was also because 4th failed to win over the fans of 3.5, and instead repulsed them. It turned out that the initial book sales were not sustained, and they did not translate into new players who bought more books much. Because most people who get into roleplaying do so by learning it from someone who already plays. Few people do so by picking up a fairly daunting rulebook. I think there is a sales and marketing term for products like that. Been decades since my classes.<br /> <br /> New players come organically from old players. 4th ed did not manage to get into the replication chain to a sufficient degree and got outreplicated and squeezed out by a competitor. I think there is an underestimation of how serious it is to fail to get into the core reproduction process. Now, as far as I know, VtM is not OGL, so that might help.<br /> <br /> But I notice Requiem is not the main line any more.<br /> <br /> <br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2471-trollroot","name":"Trollroot","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"311"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-04-15T16:59:38-07:00","id":1444093,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Trollroot</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1443592-the-official-v5-vs-v20-thread?p=1444089#post1444089\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I think you may have misunderstood. While I do believe that V5 is a better game than D&amp;D 4th edition, I think there was an important lesson in 4th eds failiure.<br /> It had a big launch, huge initial success. Corebooks on the bestseller lists. Marketing engine, market leader, conventions, it had the works.<br /> <br /> It folded as soon as a competitor arrived.<br /> <br /> Partially that was because it was just not a very good game. But it was also because 4th failed to win over the fans of 3.5, and instead repulsed them. It turned out that the initial book sales were not sustained, and they did not translate into new players who bought more books much. Because most people who get into roleplaying do so by learning it from someone who already plays. Few people do so by picking up a fairly daunting rulebook. I think there is a sales and marketing term for products like that. Been decades since my classes.<br /> <br /> New players come organically from old players. 4th ed did not manage to get into the replication chain to a sufficient degree and got outreplicated and squeezed out by a competitor. I think there is an underestimation of how serious it is to fail to get into the core reproduction process. Now, as far as I know, VtM is not OGL, so that might help.<br /> <br /> But I notice Requiem is not the main line any more.</div> </div> </div> </div>Sorry, I got that. I think my biggest difference in opinion is my view of V5 as a massive unqualified success that has drawn back in huge numbers of old players and brought in entirely new ones.<br /> <br /> Which is completely the opposite of other poster's perceptions.<br /> <br /> Hence my thanking everyone for helping me understand why they have such a different opinion.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Author of <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Cthulhu-Armageddon-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01KUOM7SI/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982844&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Cthulhu+Armageddon\" target=\"_blank\">Cthulhu Armageddon</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Teenage-Weredeer-Bright-Falls-Mysteries-ebook/dp/B075TTN2FN/ref=sr_1_2?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982717&amp;sr=1-2&amp;keywords=Weredeer#customerReviews\" target=\"_blank\">I was a Teenage Weredeer</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Straight-Outta-Fangton-Comedic-Vampire-ebook/dp/B01KNHICCC/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982774&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Straight+Outta+Fangton\" target=\"_blank\">Straight Outta Fangton</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Lucifers-Star-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01MDM9MCT/ref=mt_kindle?_encoding=UTF8&amp;me=&amp;qid=\" target=\"_blank\">Lucifer's Star</a>, </i>and the <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Rules-Supervillainy-Saga-Book-ebook/dp/B07MB89S33/\" target=\"_blank\">Supervillainy Saga</a>.</i><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","name":"CTPhipps","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12002_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13933"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-04-15T17:09:41-07:00","id":1444095,"title":"","content":"As far as I know in the french online community, V5 has yet to well... exist.<br /> <br /> I spoke with a few GM who were enthusiastic to play the new game, but it has yet to translate to anything online. I am sure if I looked hard enough I can maybe find one game, but I would have to first discover some obscure and hidden place (dark web?).<br /> <br /> Even in tabletop, those rare GM struggle to find players. The issue in France is that VTM is an ageing game that has been declining for years. Most GM still plays V1 or V2 and only the youngsters have adopted V20 (and some GM's who lost their old books). So most GM are not interested in playing V5 at all and neither are most players.<br /> <br /> Then again Requiem never took of either, and it's quite challenging to find a cWod game as well (although they at least exist), so that's maybe why. Also as far as I know only the core book and the Camarilla-Sabbat book were released in French so there's that. (I don't follow V5 news, just what I gathered when talking with other people)<br /> <br /> This just my personal observations. But the release of DA20 in french (happened after the translation of V5) was met with much more enthusiasm. Especially since it came with both a France by night supplement and a Cathare heresy campaign (forgot the name). And I have seen since a few DA20 campaign be launched.<br /> <br /> As for my view in which I think is better. Well I think already made it clear. V20 all the way.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":24936,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24936-morbus","user":"Morbus","date":". 04-15-2021, 08:14 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":7}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24936-morbus","name":"Morbus","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"119"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-04-15T17:18:27-07:00","id":1444099,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CTPhipps</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1443592-the-official-v5-vs-v20-thread?p=1444076#post1444076\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Understandable.<br /> <br /> I admit, though as a Tzimisce fan but of the Dark Ages version, what did you feel was lost by the Tzimisve 5E?</div> </div> </div> </div>I have harped on this at length before, so I don't want to bore people with my rant again, but in my opinion, losing Auspex removes such facets as scholarly, erudite, seer, mystic, oracle, sorcerer, &quot;thirst for knowledge,&quot; etc., mentioned in almost every description of the Clan, and in many cases the first aspect described. <br /> <br /> Giving them a ham-fisted social Discipline such as Dominate undermines a history of ruling through fear, superstition, Revenant proxies, torture, etc. <br /> <br /> What is left? <br /> <br /> Also a flavor-change: their compulsion feels more like a Ravnos vice. Feels too thievish. Uncouth for a Fiend.<br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":7}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24351-garygeneric","name":"Garygeneric","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24351_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"108"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-04-15T17:26:28-07:00","id":1444102,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Garygeneric</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1443592-the-official-v5-vs-v20-thread?p=1444099#post1444099\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I have harped on this at length before, so I don't want to bore people with my rant again, but in my opinion, losing Auspex removes such facets as scholarly, erudite, seer, mystic, oracle, sorcerer, &quot;thirst for knowledge,&quot; etc., mentioned in almost every description of the Clan, and in many cases the first aspect described.<br /> <br /> Giving them a ham-fisted social Discipline such as Dominate undermines a history of ruling through fear, superstition, Revenant proxies, torture, etc.<br /> <br /> What is left?<br /> <br /> Also a flavor-change: their compulsion feels more like a Ravnos vice. Feels too thievish. Uncouth for a Fiend.<br /></div> </div> </div> </div>Thanks for sharing! That explains a lot.<br /> <br /> I admit, I always associated the Auspex Discipline with Anne Rice Psychic Powers. The fact that I always made sure my Tzimisce possessed Dominate as part of my desire to as closely represent the literary Drakul as possible also impacted me. For me, I strongly hewed to the Tzimisce that were the absolute lords of their domains<br /> .<br /> Animalism, Dominate, and mastery over the very flesh of their subjects with Koldunic sorcery something that I wish had been made a main part of their Discipline spread. I feel like giving the Assamites Blood Sorcery and not the Tzimisce was a serious error even if Protean/Vicissitude gives a more Vlad Tepes-ish sort of feel. The lack of Dominate was also something that I felt was a serious error. A lot of people have stated that they assumed the Tzimisce lack of Dominate was a feature not a bug but I've never agreed. PRESENCE is the Discipline for winning people over to your side naturally. Dominate is when you command and are obeyed by SLAVES. It is a Discipline to make people into property not friends or allies--which is how I tended to view the Tzimisce's relationship with their subject.<br /> <br /> A Tzimisce rules all of their domains and absolutely so a Flaw related to that felt good. However, I also note that I never felt the current flaw of being tied to the land of their birth was ever a bad one. It didn't particularly need updating, IMHO. The current Dragon-like Greed and desire for domination seems more like a Compulsion than a Claw Flaw.<br /> <br /> I admit my version of the Tzimsice would be Animalism, Dominate, and Blood Sorcery [Vicissitude as a set of Rituals] with the difference being Animalism than the Tremere's spread.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Author of <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Cthulhu-Armageddon-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01KUOM7SI/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982844&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Cthulhu+Armageddon\" target=\"_blank\">Cthulhu Armageddon</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Teenage-Weredeer-Bright-Falls-Mysteries-ebook/dp/B075TTN2FN/ref=sr_1_2?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982717&amp;sr=1-2&amp;keywords=Weredeer#customerReviews\" target=\"_blank\">I was a Teenage Weredeer</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Straight-Outta-Fangton-Comedic-Vampire-ebook/dp/B01KNHICCC/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982774&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Straight+Outta+Fangton\" target=\"_blank\">Straight Outta Fangton</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Lucifers-Star-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01MDM9MCT/ref=mt_kindle?_encoding=UTF8&amp;me=&amp;qid=\" target=\"_blank\">Lucifer's Star</a>, </i>and the <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Rules-Supervillainy-Saga-Book-ebook/dp/B07MB89S33/\" target=\"_blank\">Supervillainy Saga</a>.</i><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","name":"CTPhipps","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12002_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13933"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-04-15T17:43:20-07:00","id":1444108,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CTPhipps</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1443592-the-official-v5-vs-v20-thread?p=1444093#post1444093\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Sorry, I got that. I think my biggest difference in opinion is my view of V5 as a massive unqualified success that has drawn back in huge numbers of old players and brought in entirely new ones.<br /> <br /> Which is completely the opposite of other poster's perceptions.<br /> <br /> Hence my thanking everyone for helping me understand why they have such a different opinion.</div> </div> </div> </div>That this is not really happen with V5 but has happened with V20 I think I made it already clear. There V5 actually hit a really unlucky time in DACHL too. We got only Core rules and Anarch and Camerilla book last june and just now fall of London released. The veterans stay a clear line with V20 and the new players that want new V5 books and new sources have to wait even longer for new content because Covid slowed everything down. Then the one book we await most because it is practically right near us with the fall of Vienna exist not even. So yeah while V5 maybe is a success in the US in DACHL there is a preference for V20 because it is already complete there and is not let us hanging with a confusing metaplot or what is preferred from many people too is letting us make our own sandbox.<br /> Anecdote in DACHL there are very clear lines about Metaplot.<br /> Either you LOVE it but want then really much where at best every month is comming another sourcebook for a local city or you despise it because it is only keeping you from doing your own thing.<br /> This is because the Germans grow up with The Dark Eye aka DSA which is the local equivalent of D&amp;D and it is famous for it's metaplot and that practical even every small village has its own description.<br /> There is V20 practical perfect because you can either play it without other sources or because of all the old material you can go big into the lore.<br /> V5 is on the other side here worst of both.<br /> You have a forced plot and the description of how exactly the situation is is for all the lore lovers way to less because of its big changes the existing stuff is effective useless so here the main selling point of V5 is, it has actual rules, it is 20\u20ac cheaper then the last edition and you do not &quot;need&quot; many books for really understanding it. Though the last point is debatable because V20s free lore aspect.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>As I am from Austria I need to clarify two things.<br /> First my native language is german and so please point out if the english I write is broken so I can improve.<br /> Second I do not own VTMV beyond first three books nor any line after M20 Corebook because it is not out there and I wait for the translation.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":6}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26160-koronus","name":"Koronus","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2020"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"366"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-04-15T17:47:31-07:00","id":1444110,"title":"","content":"One thing I'm very grateful of is the monthly tidbits of RPG content in WINTER'S TEETH. Saint Paul and Minneapolis are really getting fleshed out underneath his pen.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Author of <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Cthulhu-Armageddon-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01KUOM7SI/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982844&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Cthulhu+Armageddon\" target=\"_blank\">Cthulhu Armageddon</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Teenage-Weredeer-Bright-Falls-Mysteries-ebook/dp/B075TTN2FN/ref=sr_1_2?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982717&amp;sr=1-2&amp;keywords=Weredeer#customerReviews\" target=\"_blank\">I was a Teenage Weredeer</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Straight-Outta-Fangton-Comedic-Vampire-ebook/dp/B01KNHICCC/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982774&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Straight+Outta+Fangton\" target=\"_blank\">Straight Outta Fangton</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Lucifers-Star-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01MDM9MCT/ref=mt_kindle?_encoding=UTF8&amp;me=&amp;qid=\" target=\"_blank\">Lucifer's Star</a>, </i>and the <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Rules-Supervillainy-Saga-Book-ebook/dp/B07MB89S33/\" target=\"_blank\">Supervillainy Saga</a>.</i><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","name":"CTPhipps","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12002_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13933"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-04-15T18:18:00-07:00","id":1444116,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CTPhipps</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1443592-the-official-v5-vs-v20-thread?p=1444088#post1444088\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">This is a very eye opening thread. Apparently people see things very differently than me. I appreciate everyone taking the time to share their thoughts.</div> </div> </div> </div>They do... as has been fairly obvious by the post Likes by various posters for pretty much as long as I\u2019ve been coming here.<br /> <br /> Purely anecdotal mind you, but the proportions of likes various sentiments generally get align rather well with the local WoD playerbase as well. There\u2019s maybe one person who actually prefers V5 over V20 and, if there is a particular playstyle preference it\u2019s much closer to \u201cVampions\u201d than \u201cA Monster I am lest a monster I become\u201d or any sort of \u201cPersonal Horror\u201d style of play.<br /> <br /> Basically, most players are interested in playing Blade/Underworld the RPG and trying to get them to consider morality or something like Touchstones would get lip service at best. My current set of players for the most part latched right onto acquiring power and privilege by sucking up to the Camarilla.<br /> <br /> Attempts to suck them into the nightly hunt led to them finding work arounds including previously mentioned pig\u2019s blood and taking their Resources and opening a blood donation clinic near the university campus with a PR campaign to encourage donations with all but a couple of pints a day (labeled defective in inventory and \u201cdisposed of\u201d) going to a local children\u2019s hospital.<br /> <br /> Basically, they have no interest in RPing that part beyond the bit now played for laughs of the gal playing a hot vampire chick in the game who uses Tinder as an online delivery menu for feeding on casual hookups... \u201cI\u2019m feeling like Italian tonight; swipe right.\u201d<br /> <br /> V5 spent too much effort trying to cater to one particular playstyle with a very vocal social media presence that it basically shot down the universal urban fantasy toolkit that previous editions were. That\u2019s pretty much the exact same mistake D&amp;D 4E made... it listened to some very loud, but few in actual number voices on their available social media c. 2006-7 who were griping about edge cases and took it as permission to completely gut and rewrite the core of the game when 95% would have preferred just cleaning up those edges.<br /> <br /> Which actually brings me to...<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Trollroot</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1443592-the-official-v5-vs-v20-thread?p=1444089#post1444089\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">It [4E] folded as soon as a competitor arrived.</div> </div> </div> </div>Worth noting is that it wasn\u2019t just ANY competitor, it was a competitor offering a continuation of D&amp;D 3.5e with a few tweaks to things everyone agreed were broken... essentially a 3.75e or \u201cwhat most fans were hoping 4E was going to be.\u201d<br /> <br /> That\u2019s what let them steal a bit more than HALF of D&amp;D 4E\u2019s potential market by telling customers \u201cwe respect your preferences and wish to cater to them.\u201d<br /> <br /> Also worth noting on the flip side is that D&amp;D 5e was heavily marketed as a return to form complete with a year long open \u201cplaytest\u201d with regular polls asking \u201cdoes this feel like D&amp;D?\u201d Now, I\u2019m not foolish enough to believe that playtest was anything other than a giant marketing campaign that maybe changed a few things in the margins, but in terms of public perception it at least made people feel they were listening to the fans and the final 5e rules were a LOT closer to a streamlined 3.5e... (and rebranding a bunch of mechanics from 4E that they did keep with new names and saying they were new to 5e) which is why they pretty well pulled back the majority of what they\u2019d lost to their competitor.<br /> <br /> So, it\u2019s probably NOT an accident that V20 is outperforming V5 on drivethuRPG... if the ability to keep buying 3.5e had been available c. 2008 when 4E launched I suspect a similar trend would have emerged for it as well.<br /> <br /> Basically, the biggest competitor to V5 is that you can still buy new copies of V20... and because of existing player preferences, V20 is far more likely to be a player\u2019s entry point than V5.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":9}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1328-chris24601","name":"Chris24601","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"520"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-04-15T18:21:20-07:00","id":1444117,"title":"","content":"I THINK Social Media has changed the inroads vector for the hobby. Being able to watch &quot;How its done&quot; On various platforms has changed things. Hell I'm pretty sure there are people unfamiliar with Warhammer 40k who got into it from watching Warhams. I know I basically know everything about that system from watching voxcast","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2715-lian","name":"Lian","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5218"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-04-15T19:08:34-07:00","id":1444120,"title":"","content":"I am curious, and I don't think we'll really know any time soon, if there's a risk for V5 in terms of a disconnect between streaming and playing the game.<br /> <br /> While I'm not a huge fan of watching gaming streams, in my limited experience a lot of pre-V5 streams (and OPP game streams beyond) tend to play the games a bit closer to the rules. It certainly can't hurt that V20's broader and more traditional ruleset is less prone to asking the ST to wing it (which also applies to things like CofD streams as CofD has a broad toolkit design). V5's biggest stream is LA by Night, which is a game that is noted for taking some significant liberties with the rules at time.<br /> <br /> There's nothing wrong for a game to not be super into the RAW, but it feels like it could be risky for the most recommended/popular V5 stream to do that, since it creates a significant possibility for people watching it to not know how to replicate things from the videos in their home game.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":6}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-04-15T20:32:35-07:00","id":1444124,"title":"","content":"I think you bring up a valid point. Another one worth considering is \u201cto what degree do V5 Book purchases translate into active campaigns and how many are being read for the prose and the hope that someday a campaign will be run, but it\u2019s otherwise gathering dust because the local GM is only into V20 (or Revised or 2e or Mage or Werewolf for which 5e\u2019s haven\u2019t even come out)?<br /> <br /> How many of the purchases are people expecting an edition basically like every prior one only with updated lore and ended up just trying to find some parts worth salvaging into your V20 so you don\u2019t feel you completely wasted your money (this is basically the boat I\u2019m in with V5... scavenging a few good ideas and using the past events as real time adventure seeds).<br /> <br /> We don\u2019t know those answers because there\u2019s no guage for it. We know that several years after release the V5 core book has fallen behind the V20 core book in DriveThruRPG sales, with only the newest V5 releases surpassing V20 core... suggesting a market for new V5 content, from existing users, but not the sustained demand of the V20 rules (which, since its basically digital means their respective sales ranking are most likely indicators of new players at existing tables buying the rules rather than existing players needing extra copies... because, again, digital).<br /> <br /> I do have a random thought though following on MyWifeIsScary\u2019s polls though, if you\u2019ll indulge multi-posting...","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":6}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1328-chris24601","name":"Chris24601","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"520"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-04-15T20:35:11-07:00","id":1444126,"title":"","content":"Irrespective of which edition you prefer; LIKE this post if you are currently PLAYING or RUNNING a V20 or earlier edition campaign...","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":15}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1328-chris24601","name":"Chris24601","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"520"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-04-15T20:35:45-07:00","id":1444127,"title":"","content":"Irrespective of which edition you prefer; LIKE this post if you are currently PLAYING or RUNNING a V5 campaign...","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1328-chris24601","name":"Chris24601","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"520"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-04-16T00:21:55-07:00","id":1444137,"title":"","content":"Just for comparison, lets say I want to complain about v20<br /> <br /> Big things;<br /> too many rolls in combat.<br /> lore of the bloodlines is garbage. <br /> Character creation leads to an imbalance given scaling xp costs. <br /> <br /> minor things<br /> V1/2 soak rules are better, as are Diablerie rules. <br /> Some disciplines are somewhat imbalanced. Celerity and Obtenebration are too strong, Fortitude and Quietus too weak. <br /> I think its impractical for Assamite sorcerers to completely withold sorcery from the other castes. It would be more reasonable to trust the others with a limited selection. <br /> Some merits are terrible ideas. <br /> The Lasombra's boob still haunts me. <br /> I disagree with Daimonion being an irreconcilably evil discipline. <br /> Dark thaum is too strong. <br /> I'd appreciate better armour rules/ rules for big guns. <br /> Disciplines above level 6 are usually poorly designed. <br /> A few discipline powers should clearly be rituals. <br /> <br /> <br /> mixed<br /> DAV20 is an exciting mix of both exquisite and completely garbage ideas. <br /> <br /> ... and thats all i can think of from the top of the head. If i were to do this on V5, I'd write essays (and i have)","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25794-mywifeisscary","name":"MyWifeIsScary","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25794_2.png","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3711"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-04-16T01:18:02-07:00","id":1444139,"title":"","content":"it's kinda funny how this &quot;V20 vs V5&quot;-thread turned into a &quot;let's all talk shit about V5&quot;-thread","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25992-archderd","name":"archderd","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25992_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2020"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"205"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-04-16T02:50:11-07:00","id":1444146,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>archderd</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1443592-the-official-v5-vs-v20-thread?p=1444139#post1444139\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">it's kinda funny how this &amp;quot;V20 vs V5&amp;quot;-thread turned into a &amp;quot;let's all talk shit about V5&amp;quot;-thread</div> </div> </div> </div>The versus implies a conflict, doesn't it? I don't think it's that surprising, really.<br /> <br /> As always, the complaints on one side seem to be 'I don't have the options I used to have,' and the opposite complaint seems to be '1e marketing always promised this other game, and that's what V5 offers us, so IMO you're wrong.'<br /> <br /> You're never going to get agreement between those two viewpoints. One took the game's initial pitch, its first few books, and its early marketing as the ideal of what the game is supposed to be, and the other took the way the game was popularly played and the way it was developed as the way it was supposed to be.<br /> <br /> In a way, both groups are right. VTM was supposed to be a particular type of game, but it didn't always pull that off well, and quickly outgrew those initial ideas. So in that sense, it *was* (and is again) supposed to be played that way.<br /> <br /> But the game is also the sum of all its parts, and it's also true that the initial intent wasn't well executed or that important to a lot of people. And a game is more than design as intended--it's how it's actually played and how it is laid out in official materials. If everywhere but a few books and some marketing materials it is a kitchen sink setting rather than a narrow experience, then it's fair to infer that that's actually what it is, regardless of what was initially intended.<br /> <br /> What usually makes things go up in flames is when the 'this is the original intent' side implies 'you're guilty of badwrongfun' or when the other side gets too heated about 'you took away my toys'. <br /> <br /> It's not inevitable that it turns to flames, by any means, but managing expectations and setting the right tone in threads that discuss the differences between the editions is very important.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Writer, publisher, performer<br /> Mostly he/his, sometimes she/her IRL <a href=\"https://adam-lowe.com\" target=\"_blank\">https://adam-lowe.com</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":11}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5291-adambeyoncelowe","name":"adambeyoncelowe","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5291_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2802"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-04-16T03:51:27-07:00","id":1444150,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>archderd</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1443592-the-official-v5-vs-v20-thread?p=1444139#post1444139\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">it's kinda funny how this &quot;V20 vs V5&quot;-thread turned into a &quot;let's all talk shit about V5&quot;-thread</div> </div> </div> </div>If people don't like it, they don't like it.<br /> <br /> It's just weird there's the objectively wrong view it's not successful or popular. But knowing that perception helps the forum's harmony.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MyWifeIsScary</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1443592-the-official-v5-vs-v20-thread?p=1444137#post1444137\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">lore of the bloodlines is garbage.</div> </div> </div> </div>Of course I think it's the best of V20 after Beckett's Jyhad Diary.<br /> <br /> <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> What did you dislike about Lore of the Bloodlines?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Author of <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Cthulhu-Armageddon-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01KUOM7SI/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982844&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Cthulhu+Armageddon\" target=\"_blank\">Cthulhu Armageddon</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Teenage-Weredeer-Bright-Falls-Mysteries-ebook/dp/B075TTN2FN/ref=sr_1_2?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982717&amp;sr=1-2&amp;keywords=Weredeer#customerReviews\" target=\"_blank\">I was a Teenage Weredeer</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Straight-Outta-Fangton-Comedic-Vampire-ebook/dp/B01KNHICCC/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982774&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Straight+Outta+Fangton\" target=\"_blank\">Straight Outta Fangton</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Lucifers-Star-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01MDM9MCT/ref=mt_kindle?_encoding=UTF8&amp;me=&amp;qid=\" target=\"_blank\">Lucifer's Star</a>, </i>and the <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Rules-Supervillainy-Saga-Book-ebook/dp/B07MB89S33/\" target=\"_blank\">Supervillainy Saga</a>.</i><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","name":"CTPhipps","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12002_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13933"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-04-16T04:01:12-07:00","id":1444151,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CTPhipps</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1443592-the-official-v5-vs-v20-thread?p=1444075#post1444075\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Do people not actually think V5 is succeeding fantastically? I mean, it's irrelevant to the quality of the product but I thought it was accepted that V5 is an unqualified sales success.</div> </div> </div> </div>One measure of success, and probably the best one available to us without sensitive market data which is unlikely to be generally available, are the icv2.com retailer surveys. A full version of these, going back to 2004, can be found <a href=\"https://www.enworld.org/wiki/top_rpgs/\" target=\"_blank\">here</a>. What is quite noticeable is that the World of Darkness was a perpetually strong performer between 2004 and 2009, even though this was arguably a period in which interest in the product lines of White Wolf were declining. V5, meanwhile, appears in the autumn of 2018, remains in the chart in the spring and summer of 2019, and then disappears. This is, of course, a game with a massive marketing budget, a strong community of players and former players which could be tapped into, and strong potential relevance to a modern audience. By the end of 2020 V5 was being outperformed by games which should, in my opinion, be generating far less community interest, such as <i>Fate </i>and <i>Alien</i>. This is not the story of a sales success.<br /> <br /> This is notable given how V5 <i>ought </i>to be performing. <i>Vampire: the Masquerade</i> is the only roleplaying game other than <i>Dungeons &amp; Dragons</i> to break out of being a niche interest and into mainstream consciousness. People tend to forget this now (and I expect that there are quite a few people on this forum who may be too young to have first-hand experience of this) but back in the 1990s <i>Vampire: the Masquerade</i> was a game that was played by people who didn't see themselves as gamers. In reality, it <i>ought </i>to be a very approachable game. You basically play a human being in the modern world, with a few added supernatural touches. Character creation in the early games was very simple and comprehensible to people who had no gaming experience. There was a sense of style and a relationship which current affairs which just wasn't seen in gaming. People mock the eco-warrior notions of <i>Werewolf: the Apocalypse</i> nowadays, but having a game in which environmentalism was a prominent feature was a mind-blowing idea in the 1990s. There were good reasons why <i>Vampire: the Masquerade</i> outsold <i>Dungeons &amp; Dragons</i> by a significant margin back then. <br /> <br /> So, competently managed, V5 should be at the top of the icv2 charts. That it isn't shouldn't be seen as a disaster, but is an indication that it's massively underperforming its potential. This is a game that is modern and political, something different (in theory) to most other roleplaying games. It can effectively deploy sexy, mature themes, attract fans of horror and modern drama, and escape the nerd associations that generally surround other games. It can capitalise on popular franchises such as Twilight, and can support a wider range of game styles. That it isn't topping the charts shows that there is something going very, very badly wrong. <br /> <br /> And it is, I think, clear to understand the underlying problem if you look at the core rulebook from the viewpoint of a disinterested outsider, rather than as a fan. The first thing to notice is that, in terms of a product trying to communicate information, V5 is a mess. The writing and editing leave very much to be desired in terms of being a functional text. Visually, meanwhile, the point that a rulebook is supposed to be a reference book is completely missed. It is not an approachable volume for a person who is not already a player of the game. Ironically, for people who are not already players of the game it is not that approachable either. <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":14}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/317-james_willoughby","name":"James_Willoughby","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar317_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"297"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-04-16T04:10:37-07:00","id":1444152,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Chris24601</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1443592-the-official-v5-vs-v20-thread?p=1444124#post1444124\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I think you bring up a valid point. Another one worth considering is \u201cto what degree do V5 Book purchases translate into active campaigns and how many are being read for the prose and the hope that someday a campaign will be run, but it\u2019s otherwise gathering dust because the local GM is only into V20 (or Revised or 2e or Mage or Werewolf for which 5e\u2019s haven\u2019t even come out)?<br /> <br /> How many of the purchases are people expecting an edition basically like every prior one only with updated lore and ended up just trying to find some parts worth salvaging into your V20 so you don\u2019t feel you completely wasted your money (this is basically the boat I\u2019m in with V5... scavenging a few good ideas and using the past events as real time adventure seeds).<br /> <br /> We don\u2019t know those answers because there\u2019s no guage for it. We know that several years after release the V5 core book has fallen behind the V20 core book in DriveThruRPG sales, with only the newest V5 releases surpassing V20 core... suggesting a market for new V5 content, from existing users, but not the sustained demand of the V20 rules (which, since its basically digital means their respective sales ranking are most likely indicators of new players at existing tables buying the rules rather than existing players needing extra copies... because, again, digital).<br /> <br /> I do have a random thought though following on MyWifeIsScary\u2019s polls though, if you\u2019ll indulge multi-posting...</div> </div> </div> </div>I liked neither because while in my friend circle there is interesst there is no time for it so here I am buying all the books except D&amp;D 5 and if I have dublicates because of Reprints I just gift them some friends.<br /> <br /> Oh and there is another thing that I just remind which could bring complete newbies to V5 in DACHL over V20. You have more estimateable costs because you get access to all the german books first hand. Because while we had many books from earlier editions for VtM translated and on Drive Trough some time arround V5 came the licence to it ran out and no more renewal.<br /> Newbies will likely do not know this and so get scared alone from the thought of having to look hard through EBay or Amazon for it with high prices or having to relay on English versions because they are only ones with Digital Sales and even PoD.<br /> But again with so many changes and so little explenations that are all over the places and not even a book about the mayby biggest change in the Neighbourhood with Vienna I doubt how many people will stay at it. But this is my personal view. I can not say how a real newbie that only heard regulary about WoD or VtM like people talk about WoW will feel about VtM.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>As I am from Austria I need to clarify two things.<br /> First my native language is german and so please point out if the english I write is broken so I can improve.<br /> Second I do not own VTMV beyond first three books nor any line after M20 Corebook because it is not out there and I wait for the translation.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26160-koronus","name":"Koronus","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2020"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"366"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-04-16T04:30:52-07:00","id":1444154,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>James_Willoughby</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1443592-the-official-v5-vs-v20-thread?p=1444151#post1444151\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> One measure of success, and probably the best one available to us without sensitive market data which is unlikely to be generally available, are the icv2.com retailer surveys. A full version of these, going back to 2004, can be found <a href=\"https://www.enworld.org/wiki/top_rpgs/\" target=\"_blank\">here</a>. What is quite noticeable is that the World of Darkness was a perpetually strong performer between 2004 and 2009, even though this was arguably a period in which interest in the product lines of White Wolf were declining. V5, meanwhile, appears in the autumn of 2018, remains in the chart in the spring and summer of 2019, and then disappears. This is, of course, a game with a massive marketing budget, a strong community of players and former players which could be tapped into, and strong potential relevance to a modern audience. By the end of 2020 V5 was being outperformed by games which should, in my opinion, be generating far less community interest, such as <i>Fate </i>and <i>Alien</i>. This is not the story of a sales success.</div> </div> </div> </div>I think I see where the issue is and why I can have such a dramatically different view than the posters here in the thread.<br /> <br /> Yes, I pretty much don't agree with this measure of Vampire: The Masquerade's success or the continued interest in V5. I also think it's basing its measure of success on the wrong criteria, especially as the development of the intellectual property by Paradox Interactive hasn't been focused on the core game alone. I made a comparison earlier to the comic sales and MCU but the focus of Paradox Interactive has been in multimedia performance rather than just trying to sell the V5 corebook as a whole. I think this may actually account for the dramatically different perceptions of the line by subjects, though.<br /> <br /> People who are measuring V5's success by sales of the corebook and subsequent lines versus the measuring of all Vampire: The Masquerade 5th Edition products and success of media tie-ins.<br /> <br /> Delays related to Bloodlines 2, aside, there are multiple games on PS4's network, Steam, and Xbox now with more coming this fall. Things that have sold more than their production costs in their first week and also been financial successes enough to justify sequels. Successful comic book series and other merchandising opportunities. From my perspective, every sale of COTERIES OF NEW YORK, SHADOWS OF NEW YORK, NIGHT ROAD, and WINTER'S TEETH is effectively another sold sale of a V5 book. Chapters, the new Vampire Card Game, and other spin offs are also measures of V5's popularity as the audience isn't going to be limited to traditional tabletop buyers as they're trying to broaden it as far as possible.<br /> <br /> I feel the online games being watched are also equivalent to Convention attendence and Fanclub participation equivalent to the 90s Camarilla, just virtually.<br /> <br /> Regardless of whether its a visual novel or not, someone saw enough money to be made to make a Switch and PS4 physical game release: <a href=\"https://badlandpublishing.com/vampire-the-masquerade-coteries-of-new-york-shadows-of-new-york-will-have-a-deluxe-collectors-edition-for-ps4-nintendo-switch-and-pc-next-spring-2021/\" target=\"_blank\">https://badlandpublishing.com/vampir...t-spring-2021/</a><br /> <br /> Edit:<br /> <br /> And you know what, you could argue I'm moving the goal posts and that's fair. I get what you're saying. Origin Awards do not compensate for the fact it could be viewed as underperforming tabletop game sales wise and fan enthusiasm wise.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Author of <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Cthulhu-Armageddon-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01KUOM7SI/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982844&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Cthulhu+Armageddon\" target=\"_blank\">Cthulhu Armageddon</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Teenage-Weredeer-Bright-Falls-Mysteries-ebook/dp/B075TTN2FN/ref=sr_1_2?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982717&amp;sr=1-2&amp;keywords=Weredeer#customerReviews\" target=\"_blank\">I was a Teenage Weredeer</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Straight-Outta-Fangton-Comedic-Vampire-ebook/dp/B01KNHICCC/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982774&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Straight+Outta+Fangton\" target=\"_blank\">Straight Outta Fangton</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Lucifers-Star-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01MDM9MCT/ref=mt_kindle?_encoding=UTF8&amp;me=&amp;qid=\" target=\"_blank\">Lucifer's Star</a>, </i>and the <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Rules-Supervillainy-Saga-Book-ebook/dp/B07MB89S33/\" target=\"_blank\">Supervillainy Saga</a>.</i><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":12002,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","user":"CTPhipps","date":". 04-16-2021, 07:40 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","name":"CTPhipps","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12002_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13933"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-04-16T04:40:25-0