s link</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","name":"CTPhipps","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12002_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13933"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-04-16T04:58:10-07:00","id":1444166,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CTPhipps</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1443592-the-official-v5-vs-v20-thread?p=1444154#post1444154\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I think I see where the issue is and why I can have such a dramatically different view than the posters here in the thread.<br /> <br /> Yes, I pretty much don't agree with this measure of Vampire: The Masquerade's success or the continued interest in V5. I also think it's basing its measure of success on the wrong criteria, especially as the development of the intellectual property by Paradox Interactive hasn't been focused on the core game alone. I made a comparison earlier to the comic sales and MCU but the focus of Paradox Interactive has been in multimedia performance rather than just trying to sell the V5 corebook as a whole. I think this may actually account for the dramatically different perceptions of the line by subjects, though.<br /> <br /> People who are measuring V5's success by sales of the corebook and subsequent lines versus the measuring of all Vampire: The Masquerade 5th Edition products and success of media tie-ins.<br /> <br /> Delays related to Bloodlines 2, aside, there are multiple games on PS4's network, Steam, and Xbox now with more coming this fall. Things that have sold more than their production costs in their first week and also been financial successes enough to justify sequels. Successful comic book series and other merchandising opportunities. From my perspective, every sale of COTERIES OF NEW YORK, SHADOWS OF NEW YORK, NIGHT ROAD, and WINTER'S TEETH is effectively another sold sale of a V5 book. Chapters, the new Vampire Card Game, and other spin offs are also measures of V5's popularity as the audience isn't going to be limited to traditional tabletop buyers as they're trying to broaden it as far as possible.<br /> <br /> I feel the online games being watched are also equivalent to Convention attendence and Fanclub participation equivalent to the 90s Camarilla, just virtually.<br /> <br /> Regardless of whether its a visual novel or not, someone saw enough money to be made to make a Switch and PS4 physical game release: <a href=\"https://badlandpublishing.com/vampire-the-masquerade-coteries-of-new-york-shadows-of-new-york-will-have-a-deluxe-collectors-edition-for-ps4-nintendo-switch-and-pc-next-spring-2021/\" target=\"_blank\">https://badlandpublishing.com/vampir...t-spring-2021/</a><br /> <br /> Edit:<br /> <br /> And you know what, you could argue I'm moving the goal posts and that's fair. I get what you're saying. Origin Awards do not compensate for the fact it could be viewed as underperforming tabletop game sales wise and fan enthusiasm wise.</div> </div> </div> </div>I have to disagree. Because you like the VTM genre itself does not mean you do like V5 too. I would say the whole games and media would work well without V5. Because in it we are rarely confronted with a 1:1 copy of the Book rules.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>As I am from Austria I need to clarify two things.<br /> First my native language is german and so please point out if the english I write is broken so I can improve.<br /> Second I do not own VTMV beyond first three books nor any line after M20 Corebook because it is not out there and I wait for the translation.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":8}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26160-koronus","name":"Koronus","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2020"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"366"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-04-16T05:00:32-07:00","id":1444167,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Koronus</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1443592-the-official-v5-vs-v20-thread?p=1444166#post1444166\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I have to disagree. Because you like the VTM genre itself does not mean you do like V5 too. I would say the whole games and media would work well without V5. Because in it we are rarely confronted with a 1:1 copy of the Book rules.</div> </div> </div> </div>I think that summarizes part of the issue. If you like V:TM 1-V20 then you like 90% of V5 already. I don't see that many differences while other people see a lot I suppose.<br /> <br /> The primary differences?<br /> <br /> More Lasombra in the Camarilla, more Hunters.<br /> <br /> Mind you, I'd argue it's perfectly reasonable to hate 90% of the changes of V5 while also buying the books for lore updates or character material.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Author of <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Cthulhu-Armageddon-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01KUOM7SI/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982844&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Cthulhu+Armageddon\" target=\"_blank\">Cthulhu Armageddon</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Teenage-Weredeer-Bright-Falls-Mysteries-ebook/dp/B075TTN2FN/ref=sr_1_2?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982717&amp;sr=1-2&amp;keywords=Weredeer#customerReviews\" target=\"_blank\">I was a Teenage Weredeer</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Straight-Outta-Fangton-Comedic-Vampire-ebook/dp/B01KNHICCC/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982774&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Straight+Outta+Fangton\" target=\"_blank\">Straight Outta Fangton</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Lucifers-Star-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01MDM9MCT/ref=mt_kindle?_encoding=UTF8&amp;me=&amp;qid=\" target=\"_blank\">Lucifer's Star</a>, </i>and the <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Rules-Supervillainy-Saga-Book-ebook/dp/B07MB89S33/\" target=\"_blank\">Supervillainy Saga</a>.</i><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":12002,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","user":"CTPhipps","date":". 04-16-2021, 08:03 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","name":"CTPhipps","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12002_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13933"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-04-16T05:00:50-07:00","id":1444168,"title":"","content":"Ey don't make him get out the red text, this thread is great and it'd be sad to see it go <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/biggrin.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Big Grin\" smilieid=\"3\" class=\"inlineimg\" /> <br /> Also it's undoubtedly not the most asinine thing on this forum. If it was I'll need to step up my game.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":8}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25794-mywifeisscary","name":"MyWifeIsScary","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25794_2.png","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3711"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-04-16T05:03:31-07:00","id":1444169,"title":"","content":"The only thing V5 needed as an &quot;update&quot; for oWoD VTM was a better combat system (without the need of removing the classic Attributes for &quot;Presence, Composure, or Resolve&quot;), a much more spruced up Hierarchy of Sins chart for Humanity, more new Backgrounds, and a new mass combat system (for when say for instance, you're a Prince and another player or SNPC is a Sabbat Warleader, and you have to have rolls for the fighting that is going on in the city; I already have my own homebrewed system for Mass Combat, but it would've been nice if the mainstream was graced with such).","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Jade Kingdom Warrior","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":7}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25523-shakanaka","name":"Shakanaka","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25523_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"951"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-04-16T05:07:29-07:00","id":1444171,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CTPhipps</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1443592-the-official-v5-vs-v20-thread?p=1444154#post1444154\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Yes, I pretty much don't agree with this measure of Vampire: The Masquerade's success or the continued interest in V5. I also think it's basing its measure of success on the wrong criteria, especially as the development of the intellectual property by Paradox Interactive hasn't been focused on the core game alone. I made a comparison earlier to the comic sales and MCU but the focus of Paradox Interactive has been in multimedia performance rather than just trying to sell the V5 corebook as a whole. I think this may actually account for the dramatically different perceptions of the line by subjects, though.<br /> <br /> ...<br /> <br /> And you know what, you could argue I'm moving the goal posts and that's fair. I get what you're saying. Origin Awards do not compensate for the fact it could be viewed as underperforming tabletop game sales wise and fan enthusiasm wise.</div> </div> </div> </div>You are moving the goal posts. But even in terms of the wider intellectual property, V5 isn't doing all that well. <i>Vampire: the Masqurade - Winter's Teeth</i>, for instance, just made the top 100 comics for its first issue, and has seen its sales slide ever since. Most recent sales figures put it comfortably under 10,000 copies per month, and no-one is going to get rich on that. It isn't just an underperforming game, it's an underperforming game with underperforming tie-in products.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/317-james_willoughby","name":"James_Willoughby","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar317_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"297"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-04-16T05:12:00-07:00","id":1444172,"title":"","content":"e<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CTPhipps</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1443592-the-official-v5-vs-v20-thread?p=1444167#post1444167\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I think that summarizes part of the issue. If you like V:TM 1-V20 then you like 90% of V5 already. I don't see that many differences while other people see a lot I suppose.<br /> <br /> The primary differences?<br /> <br /> More Lasombra in the Camarilla, more Hunters.</div> </div> </div> </div>Ok, this is indeed extremely... <br /> <br /> The Camarilla in V5 are completely different, going from a monopolistic, secular organization to a small religious bunch of elitists. They're a completely different group. <br /> The Anarchs went from marginalized underdogs to being at least half the vampire population. They're a completely different group.<br /> The Sabbat are gone. <br /> The Followers of Set don't exist anymore, being replaced by two branches of heretics. <br /> The Assamites don't have a caste system anymore.<br /> The Ravnos are just a different clan. <br /> The bloodlines of death are now one with the Giovanni... I suppose that's not the greatest loss since they were always peripheral, and the families are still there... <br /> <br /> Sect Wise... the least changed is the Giovanni. They just abducted a few cooler bloodlines. The Cam is basically unrecognizable to me, and the anarchs not being the underdogs negates their appeal whilst it also undermines the appeal of more intriguing sects. <br /> <br /> Thaumaturgy as it was known is gone.<br /> Diablerie is about getting XP rather than becoming closer to caine. <br /> Generation is bad and you should avoid it. Blood potency above 5 is unplayable. <br /> &quot;The Beast made me do it&quot; works in V5 where it didn't in V20. <br /> <br /> <br /> either it's not similar at all, or it's just similar enough to be absolutely aggravating in how much better things used to be.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":9}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25794-mywifeisscary","name":"MyWifeIsScary","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25794_2.png","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3711"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-04-16T05:22:09-07:00","id":1444174,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CTPhipps</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1443592-the-official-v5-vs-v20-thread?p=1444165#post1444165\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Specifically, it's not the actual sentiment because that's how, but the lack of context. Saying you completely disagree or strongly disagree is fine. Even privately thinking another poster is full of shit, like, say, me, is also cool.<br /> <br /> However, please state your reasoning and keep things civil. I'm really hoping we can continue this helpful discussion without devolving into the Edition Wars that previously got the topic banned.</span><br /> <br /> <img src=\"https://encrypted-tbn0.gstatic.com/images?q=tbn:ANd9GcSiYMWEj_87BoScEd11Obutr7X71_bTVM09Wmo_3h0bMLj7l9sM7vTSaM96KwO2Wck54hA&amp;usqp=CAU\" class=\"bbcode-attachment bbcode-attachment--lightbox js-lightbox\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" itemprop=\"image\" loading=\"lazy\"/><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#FF0000\">I feel its important we establish what is and is not permissible here. Thanks to everyone for listening.</span></div> </div> </div> </div>i'm trying to remain nice here, but god damn my dude, i'm getting a headache trying to follow your train of thought.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25992-archderd","name":"archderd","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25992_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2020"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"205"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-04-16T05:24:43-07:00","id":1444175,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>archderd</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1443592-the-official-v5-vs-v20-thread?p=1444174#post1444174\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> i'm trying to remain nice here, but god damn my dude, i'm getting a headache trying to follow your train of thought.</div> </div> </div> </div>I'm happy to explain anything you don't understand. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>James_Willoughby</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1443592-the-official-v5-vs-v20-thread?p=1444171#post1444171\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> You are moving the goal posts.</div> </div> </div> </div>I think that's literally in the post.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>James_Willoughby</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">But even in terms of the wider intellectual property, V5 isn't doing all that well. <i>Vampire: the Masqurade - Winter's Teeth</i>, for instance, just made the top 100 comics for its first issue, and has seen its sales slide ever since. Most recent sales figures put it comfortably under 10,000 copies per month, and no-one is going to get rich on that. It isn't just an underperforming game, it's an underperforming game with underperforming tie-in products.</div> </div> </div> </div>10K sales on individual issues for an indie production house is fantastic and that's not incorporating the TPB sales. It also regularly tops out Drive Thru RPGs comic sales that don't get added to normal sales.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Author of <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Cthulhu-Armageddon-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01KUOM7SI/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982844&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Cthulhu+Armageddon\" target=\"_blank\">Cthulhu Armageddon</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Teenage-Weredeer-Bright-Falls-Mysteries-ebook/dp/B075TTN2FN/ref=sr_1_2?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982717&amp;sr=1-2&amp;keywords=Weredeer#customerReviews\" target=\"_blank\">I was a Teenage Weredeer</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Straight-Outta-Fangton-Comedic-Vampire-ebook/dp/B01KNHICCC/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982774&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Straight+Outta+Fangton\" target=\"_blank\">Straight Outta Fangton</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Lucifers-Star-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01MDM9MCT/ref=mt_kindle?_encoding=UTF8&amp;me=&amp;qid=\" target=\"_blank\">Lucifer's Star</a>, </i>and the <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Rules-Supervillainy-Saga-Book-ebook/dp/B07MB89S33/\" target=\"_blank\">Supervillainy Saga</a>.</i><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":12002,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","user":"CTPhipps","date":". 04-16-2021, 08:33 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","name":"CTPhipps","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12002_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13933"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-04-16T05:46:27-07:00","id":1444183,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CTPhipps</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1443592-the-official-v5-vs-v20-thread?p=1444167#post1444167\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I think that summarizes part of the issue. If you like V:TM 1-V20 then you like 90% of V5 already. I don't see that many differences while other people see a lot I suppose.<br /> <br /> The primary differences?<br /> <br /> More Lasombra in the Camarilla, more Hunters.</div> </div> </div> </div>... and mechanics that are damned near unplayable as written.<br /> <br /> I think the disconnect in viewpoints between you and most everyone posting here is that you\u2019re a \u201cfluff first\u201d sorta guy for whom the game mechanics are more suggestions than rules, while in my experience, most gamers are \u201ccrunch first\u201d where the mechanics are basically the physics of the setting and expect the fluff to flow logically from what the physics/rules causes to happen.<br /> <br /> Basically, the stuff you say we 90% agree with... is just a fancy wrapper for the part we care about. The part we care about, the mechanics that let us take our OWN ideas and turn them into games with are friends are the part that\u2019s been gutted to an even greater degree than 4E did to D&amp;D (which at least still had the same attributes, task resolution system and hit points).<br /> <br /> Honestly? My experience is that few players and even fewer GMs give two wet farts about the metaplot you so adore. Who the frack really cares about Hardestadt and Theo Bell? Their PCs and what happens to them are what matter to the players and the NPCs the GM has created for THEIR city and what they\u2019re up to are important to them.<br /> <br /> So when V5 says, \u201cjust about all the Brujah left the Camarilla after Theo Bell killed Hardestadt\u201d the average player in my neck of the woods would say, \u201cFuck that! My PC isn\u2019t going to abandon their position in the Cam because some writer\u2019s snowflake GMPC I\u2019ve never heard of did something.<br /> <br /> They also say \u201cwhy can I only jump a short distance or do more damage to mortals with my Potence now without having to make a, what the frak is a \u2018rouse check\u2019, when I used to be able to rip steel doors open and throw motorcycles without even making a check?\u201d<br /> <br /> The disconnect is that you think the part you label as 90% of the content is what\u2019s important to most players, but most players only care about the 10% you casually discard as irrelevant.<br /> <br /> Also, these are the Onyx Path forums, not Paradox\u2019s, so it stands to reason that the people here care more about the actual table top rpg than the broader performance of a brand. It\u2019s like telling a fan of actual comic books that \u201cthe Marvel brand is doing fantastic\u201d when the latest actual books aren\u2019t selling 10k copies and getting cancelled and relaunched in less than a dozen issues.<br /> <br /> Great for the brand is not the same thing as great for the table top rpg player... where the evidence in terms of Likes here is that V20/previous campaigns outnumber V5 ones by 10:1 as of typing this. THAT is the metric people here complaining about the table top game specifically care about.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":15}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1328-chris24601","name":"Chris24601","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"520"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-04-16T05:46:48-07:00","id":1444184,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CTPhipps</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1443592-the-official-v5-vs-v20-thread?p=1444175#post1444175\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I'm happy to explain anything you don't understand. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /></div> </div> </div> </div>it's not that i don't understand your arguments.<br /> what gives me a headache is not what you argue, it's how you argue.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25992-archderd","name":"archderd","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25992_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2020"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"205"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-04-16T06:11:08-07:00","id":1444187,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Chris24601</strong> <a 