my Potence now without having to make a, what the frak is a \u2018rouse check\u2019, when I used to be able to rip steel doors open and throw motorcycles without even making a check?\u201d<br /> <br /> The disconnect is that you think the part you label as 90% of the content is what\u2019s important to most players, but most players only care about the 10% you casually discard as irrelevant.<br /> <br /> Also, these are the Onyx Path forums, not Paradox\u2019s, so it stands to reason that the people here care more about the actual table top rpg than the broader performance of a brand. It\u2019s like telling a fan of actual comic books that \u201cthe Marvel brand is doing fantastic\u201d when the latest actual books aren\u2019t selling 10k copies and getting cancelled and relaunched in less than a dozen issues.<br /> <br /> Great for the brand is not the same thing as great for the table top rpg player... where the evidence in terms of Likes here is that V20/previous campaigns outnumber V5 ones by 10:1 as of typing this. THAT is the metric people here complaining about the table top game specifically care about.</div> </div> </div> </div>Chris this could actually be said about Shadowrun too.<br /> From what I understood most players just accept that there is now the SI and there is more Brujah in the Anarchs but rest is just played like before.<br /> Though you could say at SR the german fans care even more about the Metaplot just take the german errated Edition 5 rules while here as I said most people will just play in their Sandbox V20 with Metaplot like from the Compendium.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>As I am from Austria I need to clarify two things.<br /> First my native language is german and so please point out if the english I write is broken so I can improve.<br /> Second I do not own VTMV beyond first three books nor any line after M20 Corebook because it is not out there and I wait for the translation.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26160-koronus","name":"Koronus","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2020"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"366"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-04-16T06:24:49-07:00","id":1444189,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CTPhipps</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1443592-the-official-v5-vs-v20-thread?p=1444175#post1444175\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">10K sales on individual issues for an indie production house is fantastic and that's not incorporating the TPB sales. It also regularly tops out Drive Thru RPGs comic sales that don't get added to normal sales.</div> </div> </div> </div>I think the problem is that Paradox is not an indie company, and VtM isn't an indie property. VtM has been treated like an indie property since the CCP buyout because CCP didn't care about investing in the TT side of the IP, and later because Rich Thomas was literally building Onyx Path into existence meaning it was at least for a time an indie company (though it strains that definition now).<br /> <br /> VtM doing well by indie standards isn't good when it should be in a higher league than that; something Paradox has the resources to make happen and is willing to invest in a broad brand that CCP wasn't interested in and Onyx Path couldn't handle.<br /> <br /> You have a point that in the wider scheme of things that the TT books aren't the core of what will make the WoD brand a major brand again. But that undercuts any argument that changes that pissed off a significant portion of the existing TT fans was worth it. If the TT books aren't really that important (and as Chris very well pointed out it doesn't seem like you quite get how much the mechanics are part of that), all the more reason to make it something that appeals to the TT fans, and let the multimedia stuff reach out to spread the brand.<br /> <br /> <br /> --------------<br /> <br /> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25992-archderd\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar25992_2.jpeg');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"25992\" data-vbnamecard=\"25992\">archderd</a> <br /> <br /> Probably best to let it go man. As someone that very, very easily can be assumed to have the most asinine post on the forums (in a rare move, I'll pull out my post count on this one, I've had serious time to rack up some dumbass posts) without being banned, and someone that sucks at stopping when I should have by a few pages, including a few times with CT himself, I hope I can carry a bit of weight on this.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":7}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-04-16T06:35:06-07:00","id":1444193,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Heavy Arms</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1443592-the-official-v5-vs-v20-thread?p=1444189#post1444189\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Probably best to let it go man. As someone that very, very easily can be assumed to have the most asinine post on the forums (in a rare move, I'll pull out my post count on this one, I've had serious time to rack up some dumbass posts) without being banned, and someone that sucks at stopping when I should have by a few pages, including a few times with CT himself, I hope I can carry a bit of weight on this.</div> </div> </div> </div>i know i need to let it go, it's just hard","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25992-archderd","name":"archderd","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25992_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2020"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"205"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-04-16T06:50:45-07:00","id":1444197,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>archderd</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1443592-the-official-v5-vs-v20-thread?p=1444193#post1444193\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> i know i need to let it go, it's just hard</div> </div> </div> </div>DOS EQUIS:<br /> <br /> &quot;CT Phipps is...the most annoying man in the world.&quot;<br /> <br /> <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Author of <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Cthulhu-Armageddon-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01KUOM7SI/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982844&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Cthulhu+Armageddon\" target=\"_blank\">Cthulhu Armageddon</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Teenage-Weredeer-Bright-Falls-Mysteries-ebook/dp/B075TTN2FN/ref=sr_1_2?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982717&amp;sr=1-2&amp;keywords=Weredeer#customerReviews\" target=\"_blank\">I was a Teenage Weredeer</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Straight-Outta-Fangton-Comedic-Vampire-ebook/dp/B01KNHICCC/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982774&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Straight+Outta+Fangton\" target=\"_blank\">Straight Outta Fangton</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Lucifers-Star-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01MDM9MCT/ref=mt_kindle?_encoding=UTF8&amp;me=&amp;qid=\" target=\"_blank\">Lucifer's Star</a>, </i>and the <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Rules-Supervillainy-Saga-Book-ebook/dp/B07MB89S33/\" target=\"_blank\">Supervillainy Saga</a>.</i><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":12002,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","user":"CTPhipps","date":". 04-16-2021, 02:12 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","name":"CTPhipps","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12002_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13933"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-04-16T07:57:40-07:00","id":1444205,"title":"","content":"Someone mentioned \u201cfluff\u201d before and it brings to mind a conversation my people have had concerning writing in V5. Older editions\u2019 books have an immense re-readability factor for us whereas newer books lack that appeal, and we sorta narrowed it down to the amount of in-character fluff. <br /> <br /> For instance, the Cam and Anarch books are mostly collections of essays supposedly from a bunch of different characters but all sounding pretty much the same snark edginess, so it comes across as a bit pretentious in that the authors are forcing this particular voice to be the entire outlook of the game. Very difficult to get into. Some fluff is okay, but \u201cmostly fluff\u201d ruins immersion. Give us the bones, the facts and figures, and definitely some interspersed fluff as flavorful asides, but let players find their own voices. <br /> <br /> Again, completely subjective opinions. The writing quality is good, but being 90% in-character feel intrusive. Maybe it\u2019s just us.<br /> <br /> \u201cOur ways...are not your ways.\u201d -D","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":9}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24351-garygeneric","name":"Garygeneric","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24351_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"108"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-04-16T11:12:06-07:00","id":1444233,"title":"","content":"I think Onyx Path Publishing has really been pulling the cart for White Wolf/Paradox to a certain extent in making sure the Tabletop Game has remained relevant to the gaming industry. The number of tabletop game releases for V5 have been limited to the initial three (one of which had a huge international controversy) and <i>The Fall of London</i>. I'm not sure how to classify <i>The Vampire: The Masquerade Companion</i> either and whether it qualifies as a full-release on its own despite its importance.<br /> <br /> This is compared to the fact that <i>Chicago by Night</i> had two additional supplements and <i>Cults of the Blood Gods</i> have three planned. We also know that its writers have been involved in the larger planning for the World of Darkness as a whole. I don't know what went down with Modiphius but I think we can all agree that OPP filled an empty space that very much needed filling (and makes me wonder why they don't have a bigger role to begin with--they deserve to get the nod for their efforts).<br /> <br /> I do think its' important to note that 5th Edition isn't exactly evenly distributed over the World of Darkness as a whole and it's not like OPP hasn't been pulling the cart in other lines as well. W5 is something they have planned but its still regularly producing content for every other line. <i>Heart of the Forest</i> and <i>Earthblood</i> are present-day Werewolf releases but are still technically part of the previous group. We've just started releasing <i>Wraith: Afterlife</i> material too and OPP are still taking the lead on that as well. All of its material is still canon and contributing to the stuff that will be included in the next edition.<br /> <br /> Indeed, that is one element that I do like about Paradox's handling of the World of Darkness that it is not afraid to let people canonize material for the setting regardless of the media format.<br /> CHAPTERS will be updating Montreal, LA by Night is canonizal and updating LA, Coteries/Shadows updated New York, and Swansong is going to be an update for The Giovanni Chronicles/Dark Colony version of Boston.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"videocontainer with-aspect-ratio videocontainer-horizontal\" style=\"aspect-ratio: 16/9;\"> <a class=\"video-frame\" href=\"https://youtu.be/fJwNrKkXdhA\" data-code=\"fJwNrKkXdhA\" data-provider=\"youtube_share\" data-height=\"0\" data-width=\"0\" itemprop=\"video\"> <div class=\"videothumbnail\" style=\"\"> <img src=\"https://img.youtube.com/vi/fJwNrKkXdhA/maxresdefault.jpg\" alt=\"\" /> <div class=\"videothumbnailoverlay\"></div> </div> </a> </div><br /> <br /> The tabletop information is still there and being updated but through various new mediums. NIGHTROAD and COTERIES are still V:TM RPGS in the World of Darkness they're just through a different medium. I felt this way about my old Star Wars Legends days where the cartoons, comics, and literature all blended--the tabletop game too when it was done under West End Games and not Wizards.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Author of <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Cthulhu-Armageddon-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01KUOM7SI/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982844&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Cthulhu+Armageddon\" target=\"_blank\">Cthulhu Armageddon</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Teenage-Weredeer-Bright-Falls-Mysteries-ebook/dp/B075TTN2FN/ref=sr_1_2?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982717&amp;sr=1-2&amp;keywords=Weredeer#customerReviews\" target=\"_blank\">I was a Teenage Weredeer</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Straight-Outta-Fangton-Comedic-Vampire-ebook/dp/B01KNHICCC/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982774&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Straight+Outta+Fangton\" target=\"_blank\">Straight Outta Fangton</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Lucifers-Star-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01MDM9MCT/ref=mt_kindle?_encoding=UTF8&amp;me=&amp;qid=\" target=\"_blank\">Lucifer's Star</a>, </i>and the <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Rules-Supervillainy-Saga-Book-ebook/dp/B07MB89S33/\" target=\"_blank\">Supervillainy Saga</a>.</i><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","name":"CTPhipps","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12002_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13933"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-04-16T11:22:41-07:00","id":1444235,"title":"","content":"Something I like to use for that sort of thing: &quot;fluff&quot; vs. &quot;lore.&quot;<br /> <br /> &quot;Fluff&quot; is extraneous. It might be interesting, it might be well written, it might be fun, but it doesn't add anything to either help you play the game, or expand your idea of what the game can do. Fluff is frequently associated with purple prose, but fluff can be tightly worded too... you just tend to notice it less when it's like that.<br /> <br /> &quot;Lore&quot; is in the range of useful to essential information about the setting that is vital for communicating what playing the game is about, and what the characters can do.<br /> <br /> There is a level of subjectivity to the assignments here, because there's a very big grey area around different people finding different things useful for getting them into the setting and playloop of the game.<br /> <br /> That said, it isn't too hard, usually, to check your biases on this. I don't particularly like city books. I have run two games in 25 years of GMing (not just WoD) where I used cities/etc. fleshed out in a book, adventure module, etc. Even for very well established settings, like Star Wars, where players might visit one of the places featured and highlighted in SW media, I tend to put the focus on new places (both to give the players something fresh to deal with, and to satisfy my preferences). I can still acknowledge that a lot of stuff in city books is still solidly in the &quot;lore&quot; category because lots of people enjoy using premade locations either straight from the box or as inspiration for how to create their own<br /> <br /> Fluff and lore are also usually mixed together, making it hard to tease out sometimes. The Ashirra in V5 books so far is a mix. There's lore there, but also there's a lot of writing that doesn't help you really understand how to play an Ashirra character, or how to include them as a ST outside of them being an exotic darker skin toned mostly the same but not exactly Camarilla..","signature":"","edited":{"userid":617,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","user":"Heavy Arms","date":". 04-16-2021, 02:45 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":6}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-04-16T12:04:36-07:00","id":1444245,"title":"","content":"One thing I feel about V5 is that while the mechanics might be simpler and more streamlined for players the same is not necessarily true for the ST.<br /> I often see people say that hunger dice are not derailing because you are only supposed to roll at dramatic moments or take half but unless you have experience,how are you supposed to make that decision?<br /> If your player rolls a messy critical what should happen?What if your player disagrees?<br /> What if one player insists on going off hunting because they want to stay at hunger one and the others want to continue with the plot,just roll for hunting?If they fail should I have them play out a scene while the others wait?<br /> <br /> How to integrate twelve touchstones without bogging down the story and leaving other players with nothing to do?<br /> To me,the core book seems to assume that the ST is pretty experienced and good at making these kind of decisions which would mean that getting the old fan base on board would be important.<br /> <br /> I think V5 could have been clearer in presenting both the system and how to practically use it possibly by hiring an editor.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25477-perisa","name":"Perisa","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-04-16T14:28:39-07:00","id":1444262,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Perisa</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1443592-the-official-v5-vs-v20-thread?p=1444245#post1444245\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">How to integrate<b> twelve touchstones </b>without bogging down the story and leaving other players with nothing to do?</div> </div> </div> </div>I've been writing my own game system for a few years now (why so long? Dayjob and an insistence on playtesting to get things right) and Touchstones is like one of many concepts I started out with that sounded great on paper, but ran headfirst into reality like it was a brick wall once it was actually handed over to my play-testers.<br /> <br /> Its one thing if every PC had ONE touchstone and/or you could also pick things that aren't NPCs to be your touchstone (ex. your childhood home, an organization you belonged to in life) because then you could keep the numbers manageable. But three touchstone NPCs per PC, in addition to other merit/background NPCs a PC might take just creates a mass of NPCs over and above the ones the GM needs for the basic city power struggles (a prince, a sheriff, probably some primogen, a few higher up-and-comers looking to replace one of the above, etc.) just turns into a massive amount of juggling...<br /> <br /> ...and that's before you consider how absolutely lethal V5's combat engine is and that every time you introduce a replacement PC because a previous one was ganked the GM has to completely redo the relationship chart with three MORE touchstone NPCs and associated background/merit NPCs.<br /> <br /> Frankly, V5 doesn't feel like it was designed to be played with more than two (three at most) PCs with combat as something exceedingly rare so as to avoid regular PC deaths. The relationship charts just get too complex even at four PCs.<br /> <br /> I can't even conceive of trying to manage all the NPCs necessary for the largest table I ever ran... 15 players. It was enough that plots mostly became self-generating so I mostly just had to be witness when checks of serious consequence were required and run various NPCs here and there... but I can't imagine having to track 45 Touchstone NPCs on top of everything else.<br /> <br /> And that's the problem with a LOT of V5's mechanics. A lot of them sound great on paper... then you try to use them in a real campaign and you find yourself having to slap on duct tape and bailing wire by the roll just to keep it from falling apart in practice. Some of them may even be good mechanics, but they're just so poorly expressed that people end up house-ruling them to what they THINK the rule is trying to say and so you get a patchwork where you can barely even discuss the system with people because no can even agree on the basic rules (ex. I've read the rules on combat several times over for V5 and I'm still not certain if my interpretation of how they say to handle multiple attackers and making multiple attacks yourself actually interface with each other... and what the hell merging the dice of both attackers into a single conflict pool is supposed to even mean, you and your opponent's dice all get added together?).","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1328-chris24601","name":"Chris24601","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"520"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-04-16T14:32:39-07:00","id":1444263,"title":"","content":"I think part of the issue is there's an unconscious backlash to Requiem which shouldn't exist and it's unfortunately impacted the number of RPG books that <i>should</i> exist for Vampire: The Masquerade Fith Edition.<br /> <br /> One of the benefits of Requiem was that it was very experienced player/ST friendly and strongly focused the DIY mechanics so that you could do almost anything you wanted to it with a very wide-opened sandbox of possibilities. The problem was that part of the appeal of V:TM was always that it was very much, &quot;This is an easy set of things to use. 13 kinds of vampire. Easy rules. Go nuts.&quot;<br /> <br /> Requiem put out books like NOMADS, COTERIES, and lots of stuff about how to roleplay the Hunger as well as feeding. These are things that made the gameline work for me and why I always liked the more obscure books of V:TM ala Elysium or the faith books. The absence of similar material for V5 is one of its larger weakness.<br /> <br /> I've mentioned that I wasn't a fan of either THE ANARCH or THE CAMARILLA because both books really are just collections of in-universe fiction. The Anarch even more so than the latter that at least contains some interesting new ideas. But I feel like they lacked out of character information and roleplaying hints that would have made them great. But it goes beyond this with THE SABBAT and SECOND INQUISITION books being <i>necessary</i> supplements that never got made.<br /> <br /> You know what is also a necessary supplement?<br /> <br /> <b>TOUCHSTONES and PREDATOR TYPES</b><br /> <br /> I was really hoping this would be something that would be covered by the Player's Guide but the lack of its publication means that we'll never know. Still, I think we needed expanded rules for Touchstones and Predator types that explains how they can be made more organic additions to campaigns.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> How to integrate twelve touchstones without bogging down the story and leaving other players with nothing to do? </div> </div> </div>I feel like LA by Night did a good job of integrating Annabele, Victor, Nelli, and Jasper's touchstones. Mark being both Victor and Annabelle's shared Touchstone was also hilarious as they both liked him for different reasons.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Author of <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Cthulhu-Armageddon-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01KUOM7SI/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982844&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Cthulhu+Armageddon\" target=\"_blank\">Cthulhu Armageddon</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Teenage-Weredeer-Bright-Falls-Mysteries-ebook/dp/B075TTN2FN/ref=sr_1_2?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982717&amp;sr=1-2&amp;keywords=Weredeer#customerReviews\" target=\"_blank\">I was a Teenage Weredeer</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Straight-Outta-Fangton-Comedic-Vampire-ebook/dp/B01KNHICCC/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982774&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Straight+Outta+Fangton\" target=\"_blank\">Straight Outta Fangton</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Lucifers-Star-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01MDM9MCT/ref=mt_kindle?_encoding=UTF8&amp;me=&amp;qid=\" target=\"_blank\">Lucifer's Star</a>, </i>and the <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Rules-Supervillainy-Saga-Book-ebook/dp/B07MB89S33/\" target=\"_blank\">Supervillainy Saga</a>.</i><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":12002,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","user":"CTPhipps","date":". 04-16-2021, 05:34 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","name":"CTPhipps","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12002_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13933"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-04-16T16:35:49-07:00","id":1444272,"title":"","content":"Phips your last post is something where I think we have mostly same thinking points.<br /> While I disagree with Touchpoints and Predator Type Part you really put my feeling about the V5 Source books into words.<br /> It is my third try to read those because I felt offput all the time though I could not put my finger on it. Because in theory it should be great when Ingame authers share their thoughts but it seems this books are more like a fiction and not really answering questions about the fluff that I have.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>As I am from Austria I need to clarify two things.<br /> First my native language is german and so please point out if the english I write is broken so I can improve.<br /> Second I do not own VTMV beyond first three books nor any line after M20 Corebook because it is not out there and I wait for the translation.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26160-koronus","name":"Koronus","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2020"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"366"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-04-16T19:06:03-07:00","id":1444280,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CTPhipps</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1443592-the-official-v5-vs-v20-thread?p=1444154#post1444154\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I think I see where the issue is and why I can have such a dramatically different view than the posters here in the thread.<br /> <br /> Yes, I pretty much don't agree with this measure of Vampire: The Masquerade's success or the continued interest in V5. I also think it's basing its measure of success on the wrong criteria, especially as the development of the intellectual property by Paradox Interactive hasn't been focused on the core game alone. I made a comparison earlier to the comic sales and MCU but the focus of Paradox Interactive has been in multimedia performance rather than just trying to sell the V5 corebook as a whole. I think this may actually account for the dramatically different perceptions of the line by subjects, though.<br /> <br /> People who are measuring V5's success by sales of the corebook and subsequent lines versus the measuring of all Vampire: The Masquerade 5th Edition products and success of media tie-ins.<br /> <br /> Delays related to Bloodlines 2, aside, there are multiple games on PS4's network, Steam, and Xbox now with more coming this fall. Things that have sold more than their production costs in their first week and also been financial successes enough to justify sequels. Successful comic book series and other merchandising opportunities. From my perspective, every sale of COTERIES OF NEW YORK, SHADOWS OF NEW YORK, NIGHT ROAD, and WINTER'S TEETH is effectively another sold sale of a V5 book. Chapters, the new Vampire Card Game, and other spin offs are also measures of V5's popularity as the audience isn't going to be limited to traditional tabletop buyers as they're trying to broaden it as far as possible.<br /> <br /> I feel the online games being watched are also equivalent to Convention attendence and Fanclub participation equivalent to the 90s Camarilla, just virtually.<br /> <br /> Regardless of whether its a visual novel or not, someone saw enough money to be made to make a Switch and PS4 physical game release: <a href=\"https://badlandpublishing.com/vampire-the-masquerade-coteries-of-new-york-shadows-of-new-york-will-have-a-deluxe-collectors-edition-for-ps4-nintendo-switch-and-pc-next-spring-2021/\" target=\"_blank\">https://badlandpublishing.com/vampir...t-spring-2021/</a><br /> <br /> Edit:<br /> <br /> And you know what, you could argue I'm moving the goal posts and that's fair. I get what you're saying. Origin Awards do not compensate for the fact it could be viewed as underperforming tabletop game sales wise and fan enthusiasm wise.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> That's an interesting way to look at things. But keep in mind that previous editions had two AA video game titles, a TV show, and I don't know how many novels to show for them vs a handful of visual novels, and some comic book for V5.<br /> <br /> Anyone who is even just a casual fan of those mediums would tell you that the comparison is not exactly in favor of V5 either. Even if true neither VTM:B or Kindred: The Embraced managed to be successful in their times. And Paradox far less ambitious strategy is probably wiser... well except for VTM:B 2.<br /> <br /> Frankly I don't know any rpg fan who would not be triggered if someone tried to compare Bloodline with some visual novels. Fan of vampire or not. So yeah dramatically different way to see things is putting it middly.<br /> <br /> And of course when we directly compare previous editions to V5, there's no contest. And I don't include V20 here, because as its critics rightly point out: it's not a real edition.<br /> Albeit, to be fair. This is not V5 fault. The market has changed since the 2000's. Vampire used to be second only to DnD. Now it's a niche game by any serious standard. Be it V20 or V5.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":24936,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24936-morbus","user":"Morbus","date":". 04-16-2021, 10:10 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24936-morbus","name":"Morbus","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"119"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-04-16T19:10:33-07:00","id":1444281,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Morbus</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1443592-the-official-v5-vs-v20-thread?p=1444280#post1444280\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Frankly I don't know any rpg fan who would not be triggered if someone tried to compare Bloodline with some visual novels. Fan of vampire or not. So yeah dramatically different way to see things is putting it middly.</div> </div> </div> </div>I should note that I really enjoyed both games and recommend you play them. Have you?<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> And of course when we directly compare previous editions to V5, there's no contest. And I don't include V20 here, because as it's critics rightly point out: it's not a real edition.<br /> Albeit, to be fair. This is not V5 fault. The market has changed since the 2000's. Vampire used to be second only to DnD. Now it's a niche game by any serious standart. Be it V20 or V5/ </div> </div> </div>Similarly, I think its bizarre to compare V 1-3 to V5 because V5 builds off the foundations of 1-3.<br /> <br /> I do agree that the problem is rebuilding the brand and its loyalty more than anything else. The market has changed, the fans pursue new medium, and a lot of people aren't even aware that V:TR and V20 existed.<br /> <br /> Its an intellectual property that needs to make itself aware as something that is still going strong. That will require shows, socia; media, and merchandising.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Author of <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Cthulhu-Armageddon-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01KUOM7SI/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982844&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Cthulhu+Armageddon\" target=\"_blank\">Cthulhu Armageddon</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Teenage-Weredeer-Bright-Falls-Mysteries-ebook/dp/B075TTN2FN/ref=sr_1_2?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982717&amp;sr=1-2&amp;keywords=Weredeer#customerReviews\" target=\"_blank\">I was a Teenage Weredeer</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Straight-Outta-Fangton-Comedic-Vampire-ebook/dp/B01KNHICCC/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982774&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Straight+Outta+Fangton\" target=\"_blank\">Straight Outta Fangton</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Lucifers-Star-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01MDM9MCT/ref=mt_kindle?_encoding=UTF8&amp;me=&amp;qid=\" target=\"_blank\">Lucifer's Star</a>, </i>and the <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Rules-Supervillainy-Saga-Book-ebook/dp/B07MB89S33/\" target=\"_blank\">Supervillainy Saga</a>.</i><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","name":"CTPhipps","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12002_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13933"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-04-16T19:24:06-07:00","id":1444282,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CTPhipps</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1443592-the-official-v5-vs-v20-thread?p=1444281#post1444281\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I should note that I really enjoyed both games and recommend you play them. Have you?</div> </div> </div> </div>I played the first New york game. Coteries, I think? Didn't like it. Very bland and linear. There are much better visual novels out there. Even Choice of game's vampire is better and it's also... FREE.<br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Similarly, I think its bizarre to compare V 1-3 to V5 because V5 builds off the foundations of 1-3. </div> </div> </div>Well it's certainly bizarre coming from the guy who opened a V5 vs V20 thread. You realize that V20 is literally a compilation of V1 to V3?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":24936,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24936-morbus","user":"Morbus","date":". 04-16-2021, 10:26 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24936-morbus","name":"Morbus","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"119"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-04-16T19:49:38-07:00","id":1444283,"title":"","content":"I think NIGHT ROAD and SHADOWS OF NEW YORK are much better than Coteries. The latter significantly improved by not going with a personality-less blank slate.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Morbus</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1443592-the-official-v5-vs-v20-thread?p=1444282#post1444282\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Well it's certainly bizarre coming from the guy who opened a V5 vs V20 thread. You realize that V20 is literally a compilation of V1 to V3?</div> </div> </div> </div>Yes, I have long disagreed with there being any need to dislike one or the other. I love both.<br /> <br /> However, I felt it was good to let people share their opinion as I don't think mine is the dominant one.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Author of <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Cthulhu-Armageddon-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01KUOM7SI/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982844&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Cthulhu+Armageddon\" target=\"_blank\">Cthulhu Armageddon</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Teenage-Weredeer-Bright-Falls-Mysteries-ebook/dp/B075TTN2FN/ref=sr_1_2?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982717&amp;sr=1-2&amp;keywords=Weredeer#customerReviews\" target=\"_blank\">I was a Teenage Weredeer</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Straight-Outta-Fangton-Comedic-Vampire-ebook/dp/B01KNHICCC/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982774&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Straight+Outta+Fangton\" target=\"_blank\">Straight Outta Fangton</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Lucifers-Star-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01MDM9MCT/ref=mt_kindle?_encoding=UTF8&amp;me=&amp;qid=\" target=\"_blank\">Lucifer's Star</a>, </i>and the <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Rules-Supervillainy-Saga-Book-ebook/dp/B07MB89S33/\" target=\"_blank\">Supervillainy Saga</a>.</i><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","name":"CTPhipps","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12002_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13933"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-04-16T20:01:55-07:00","id":1444285,"title":"","content":"I am curious to see how Bloodlines II will affect V5 sales. If it's good it'll give them a pretty big bump, but if the game ends up being mediocre or worse (and honestly my expectations have been going down the more I've heard about it and the more it's been delayed) then it might actually end up actually hurting V5 sales.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/741-anubisxy","name":"AnubisXy","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar741_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5693"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-04-16T20:23:17-07:00","id":1444288,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>AnubisXy</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1443592-the-official-v5-vs-v20-thread?p=1444285#post1444285\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I am curious to see how Bloodlines II will affect V5 sales. If it's good it'll give them a pretty big bump, but if the game ends up being mediocre or worse (and honestly my expectations have been going down the more I've heard about it and the more it's been delayed) then it might actually end up actually hurting V5 sales.</div> </div> </div> </div>I am curious what the real motivation of Bloodlines 2's separation was. Was it because the game was not yet complete and nowhere near completion or was it because the game was janky and Paradox is wanting a triple A game rather than a double A game?<br /> <br /> I played Earthblood but that game was very much a game that felt like it was from the PS2 era.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Author of <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Cthulhu-Armageddon-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01KUOM7SI/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982844&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Cthulhu+Armageddon\" target=\"_blank\">Cthulhu Armageddon</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Teenage-Weredeer-Bright-Falls-Mysteries-ebook/dp/B075TTN2FN/ref=sr_1_2?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982717&amp;sr=1-2&amp;keywords=Weredeer#customerReviews\" target=\"_blank\">I was a Teenage Weredeer</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Straight-Outta-Fangton-Comedic-Vampire-ebook/dp/B01KNHICCC/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982774&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Straight+Outta+Fangton\" target=\"_blank\">Straight Outta Fangton</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Lucifers-Star-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01MDM9MCT/ref=mt_kindle?_encoding=UTF8&amp;me=&amp;qid=\" target=\"_blank\">Lucifer's Star</a>, </i>and the <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Rules-Supervillainy-Saga-Book-ebook/dp/B07MB89S33/\" target=\"_blank\">Supervillainy Saga</a>.</i><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","name":"CTPhipps","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12002_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13933"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-04-16T21:14:53-07:00","id":1444292,"title":"","content":"Off hand I'd guess some mixture of the two. I think Paradox was surprised at how much hype Bloodlines II generated (numerous polls showed it as the second most anticipated game of the year, just behind Cyberpunk) so there was this real pressure to turn this AA game into an AAA game because of the huge expectations from gamers. And then I have to imagine what they had on their hands was still far from complete and barely meeting the standards of an AA game (if that game trailer was anything to go by).","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/741-anubisxy","name":"AnubisXy","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar741_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5693"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-04-16T21:26:15-07:00","id":1444295,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>AnubisXy</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1443592-the-official-v5-vs-v20-thread?p=1444292#post1444292\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Off hand I'd guess some mixture of the two. I think Paradox was surprised at how much hype Bloodlines II generated (numerous polls showed it as the second most anticipated game of the year, just behind Cyberpunk) so there was this real pressure to turn this AA game into an AAA game because of the huge expectations from gamers. And then I have to imagine what they had on their hands was still far from complete and barely meeting the standards of an AA game (if that game trailer was anything to go by).</div> </div> </div> </div>One thing the game benefited from at least was stylized cartoonish Borderlands-esque art ages MUCH MUCH better than photorealism attempts.<br /> <br /> Oh, btw, Matthew Dawkins is a writer on SWANSONG:<br /> <br /> Trailer: <a href=\"https://youtu.be/E7L7M0R8fzA\" target=\"_blank\">https://youtu.be/E7L7M0R8fzA</a><br /> <br /> Matthew Dawkins: <a href=\"https://youtu.be/0qcfgZ2IYUs\" target=\"_blank\">https://youtu.be/0qcfgZ2IYUs</a>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Author of <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Cthulhu-Armageddon-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01KUOM7SI/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982844&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Cthulhu+Armageddon\" target=\"_blank\">Cthulhu Armageddon</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Teenage-Weredeer-Bright-Falls-Mysteries-ebook/dp/B075TTN2FN/ref=sr_1_2?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982717&amp;sr=1-2&amp;keywords=Weredeer#customerReviews\" target=\"_blank\">I was a Teenage Weredeer</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Straight-Outta-Fangton-Comedic-Vampire-ebook/dp/B01KNHICCC/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982774&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Straight+Outta+Fangton\" target=\"_blank\">Straight Outta Fangton</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Lucifers-Star-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01MDM9MCT/ref=mt_kindle?_encoding=UTF8&amp;me=&amp;qid=\" target=\"_blank\">Lucifer's Star</a>, </i>and the <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Rules-Supervillainy-Saga-Book-ebook/dp/B07MB89S33/\" target=\"_blank\">Supervillainy Saga</a>.</i><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","name":"CTPhipps","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12002_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13933"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-04-16T23:56:01-07:00","id":1444307,"title":"","content":"I can't be alone in always skipping the fiction parts in VTM books? I usually go back to those later, but since they're frequently by unreliable narrators or in purple prose, I always go for the lore and crunch first.<br /> <br /> When reading Anarchs and Camarilla, I found myself flicking through the books without really reading anything because there was nothing much of substances outside of the very partial and contradictory IC fiction. That, to me, is a big flaw with the ParaWolf supplements.<br /> <br /> OPP's books are obviously head and shoulders above those ones. I honestly think Paradox/WW should just have given OPP the resources to make everything, but I would say that, as a fan of 90% of what OPP does.<br /> <br /> To use a cliche, I've often wanted more to sink my teeth into. That said, I have still bought every V5 release so far. I just haven't had much use for them.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Writer, publisher, performer<br /> Mostly he/his, sometimes she/her IRL <a href=\"https://adam-lowe.com\" target=\"_blank\">https://adam-lowe.com</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5291-adambeyoncelowe","name":"adambeyoncelowe","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5291_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2802"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-04-17T03:34:31-07:00","id":1444317,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>archderd</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1443592-the-official-v5-vs-v20-thread?p=1444184#post1444184\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">it's not that i don't understand your arguments.<br /> what gives me a headache is not what you argue, it's how you argue.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> You just need to take 50% of what CT posts as semi-&quot; Devils Advocate &quot; type statements. I literally thought I ws going insane a year or so ago when me and him had regular interactions as the discussion would go on for pages and then suddenly he'd agree with a post of mine and state that that was what he was saying all along. I reacted badly and honestly thought I was being trolled and did some....regrettable....things. <br /> <br /> I've worked out its just an idiosynchratic post style since then and reduced my interaction because it just hurts my brain a little too much but I know now that its all 100% legitimate posts on his behalf and I think we're all good now. ( except over KotE.....but that is a battle that will one day likely claim my very soul. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/biggrin.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Big Grin\" smilieid=\"3\" class=\"inlineimg\" /> )","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/479-damian-may","name":"Damian May","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar479_1.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1199"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-04-17T03:39:25-07:00","id":1444318,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>adambeyoncelowe</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1443592-the-official-v5-vs-v20-thread?p=1444307#post1444307\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I can't be alone in always skipping the fiction parts in VTM books? I usually go back to those later, but since they're frequently by unreliable narrators or in purple prose, I always go for the lore and crunch first.<br /> <br /> When reading Anarchs and Camarilla, I found myself flicking through the books without really reading anything because there was nothing much of substances outside of the very partial and contradictory IC fiction. That, to me, is a big flaw with the ParaWolf supplements.<br /> <br /> OPP's books are obviously head and shoulders above those ones. I honestly think Paradox/WW should just have given OPP the resources to make everything, but I would say that, as a fan of 90% of what OPP does.<br /> <br /> To use a cliche, I've often wanted more to sink my teeth into. That said, I have still bought every V5 release so far. I just haven't had much use for them.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> As most of my Campaigns are set in Oceania or South East Asia the Metaplot and Signature Characters have been essentially irrelevant for the past 30ish years even if I followed Canon. I had no idea people thought Bloodlines was anything more than a relatively unpopular badly flawed rpg/beat-em-up that was only playable due to extensive modding until a few years ago when a bunch of people said it was the key to them getting into VtM.<br /> <br /> *shrug*<br /> <br /> We all have different experiences.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/479-damian-may","name":"Damian May","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar479_1.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1199"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-04-17T04:33:13-07:00","id":1444322,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CTPhipps</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1443592-the-official-v5-vs-v20-thread?p=1444288#post1444288\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I am curious what the real motivation of Bloodlines 2's separation was. Was it because the game was not yet complete and nowhere near completion or was it because the game was janky and Paradox is wanting a triple A game rather than a double A game?<br /> <br /> I played Earthblood but that game was very much a game that felt like it was from the PS2 era.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> They probably put Bloodlines 2 on the temporary back burner because of Hardsuit Labs. That company was responsible for really borking up a formerly semi-popular game called &quot;Blacklight: Retribution&quot; with absolutely horrendous patches/updates that changed the game for the worse. I actually wonder how badly they made Bloodline 2 before being scrapped by Paradox. lol","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Jade Kingdom Warrior","edited":{"userid":25523,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25523-shakanaka","user":"Shakanaka","date":". 04-17-2021, 11:43 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25523-shakanaka","name":"Shakanaka","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25523_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"951"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-04-17T07:35:35-07:00","id":1444330,"title":"","content":"So, we\u2019ve had few days for some poll results to come in and I think it has some interesting results.<br /> <br /> The first poll about which edition you prefer is currently sitting at 29 for V20 and 6 for V5... so 83% prefer V20 and 17% perfer V5 (I added 1 to the V20 count because MWIS couldn\u2019t like his own post).<br /> <br /> The second about which edition you\u2019re actually playing is sitting at 15 for V20 and 1 for V5 (the like count is 14:1 but I couldn\u2019t vote on my own post).<br /> <br /> Now we can\u2019t account for thread attrition, but by raw numbers that would mean 54% aren\u2019t playing VtM at all, 43% are playing V20 or earlier, and just 3% are playing V5. The raw numbers would also indicate that just 17% of people who prefer V5 are actually playing V5.<br /> <br /> Taking the numbers for the second poll on their own, 94% of respondents are playing V20 or earlier and just 6% are playing V5.<br /> <br /> Regardless of how well the IP as whole might be doing, I think those numbers tell a story of the tabletop portion of the IP is not delivering content most of the IP\u2019s fans in that medium would find useful.<br /> <br /> Serious suggestion for the people at OPP; I know it\u2019d be a longshot getting Paradox to approve, but I think there\u2019d be a market for a book that took V5\u2019s concepts (ex. Thinblood Alchemy, banes as alternate clan weaknesses, new V5 powers as V20 style alternate/combo powers, etc.) expressed .them in V20 mechanical terms and which used a more objective presentation of the metaplot updates.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":7}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1328-chris24601","name":"Chris24601","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"520"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-04-17T08:10:56-07:00","id":1444333,"title":"","content":"Don't act like all our problems are with the mechanics. Lots of problems are fluff related. One that's often undiscussed is how uneccessary a lot of the mean changes were. Like, even though I don't agree with it, I can see why the Tremere pyramid got blown up and I can even imagine a scenario where that's actually a wonderful plan and not just a crazy stunt/bullshit move to justify whatever house Carna is supposed to be. But, say, why were the Followers of Set deleted? I'd be estatic to have the FoS deal with the two new heretical factions, the Church and Ministry, but instead the followers are completely and utterly gone and replacing them you've either got Church or Ministry; who does that serve? certainly not the Settites. The Brujah are leaving the Cam? Why? so players don't get confused by the rebel clan in the Cam? But what about in universe reasons? What about my Brujah already in the Cam who are rather attached to the whole thing? The Hecata, that can work as a sect, but why are they a clan, doesn't that just serve to deny players all the interesting discipline and weakness combinations that necromancers had? Why would my necromancers join a block of necromancers when they've done so well so far as necromancers while avoiding the giovanni? These choices, or really the cutting down of choices, are just so pointlessly bad for players and characters.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":8}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25794-mywifeisscary","name":"MyWifeIsScary","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25794_2.png","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3711"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-04-17T08:13:49-07:00","id":1444334,"title":"","content":"<a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1328-chris24601\" style=\"background-image:url('data:image/svg+xml;base64,');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"1328\" data-vbnamecard=\"1328\">Chris24601</a> <br /> <br /> I think you are right it would never be green lit. They wont encourage people to buy products away from the V5 game line. I think some ideas for 5 are good in V20, and it's amazing how much I approve of my implementation of those things <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> With WowWikiVTM and message boards you really don't need to spend any money to take stuff from V5. I think that's a good thing. I think as long as the game is in it's current state I will be hoping for well reviewed novels more than any other product they could put out. I also think that between DAV20 and V20 to choose between for rules and Disciplines write ups (DAV20 for Auspex and Celerity, V20 for Obeah and Temporis, etc...) I struggle to find a reason to even want a V6. Unlike many on these boards I don't find combat overly taxing. How often are you really battling a dangerous foe for your unlife? If it's a few times or even once a night it's gonna be a short game anyway.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24221-vamps-like-us","name":"Vamps Like Us","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"390"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-04-17T08:31:37-07:00","id":1444335,"title":"","content":"Also I don't want to give a single flying fuck about Hardestart or Theo bell. Every game I've been in, people have ran their own cities. V5 leans heavily into nerding about these guys, but so few actually care when they're picking a city and filling it with their own colourful characters. Unless it's an antedeluvian or an absolutely legendary methuselah like Ur-Shulgi, Montano or Mithras, it's very unlikely that I'm ever going to factor them into my game (and even these legends aren't likely to be of relevance to my city). The part where the Brujah leave because of these guys... <br /> <br /> like, if you've got a cunning, masterful plan, that's all well and good, if there's some deeper reason to the Brujah leaving the cam then that's great, but it'd be wise to tell us so we don't just think you've gone stupid drooling over some guy that might've been cool nearly 30 years ago. Acting mysterious is a good way to act like an idiot.... shit am I insulting writers again or do you think this is general enough that it's ok? I think it should be alright.... Anyhow the Brujah leaving the Cam is a joke and Tyler is presented like a clown (and Dragonsbreath rounds aren't likely to be powerful enough to kill Hardestardt the younger)","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25794-mywifeisscary","name":"MyWifeIsScary","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25794_2.png","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3711"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-04-17T08:46:09-07:00","id":1444337,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MyWifeIsScary</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1443592-the-official-v5-vs-v20-thread?p=1444333#post1444333\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Don't act like all our problems are with the mechanics. Lots of problems are fluff related. One that's often undiscussed is how uneccessary a lot of the mean changes were. Like, even though I don't agree with it, I can see why the Tremere pyramid got blown up and I can even imagine a scenario where that's actually a wonderful plan and not just a crazy stunt/bullshit move to justify whatever house Carna is supposed to be. But, say, why were the Followers of Set deleted? I'd be estatic to have the FoS deal with the two new heretical factions, the Church and Ministry, but instead the followers are completely and utterly gone and replacing them you've either got Church or Ministry; who does that serve? certainly not the Settites. The Brujah are leaving the Cam? Why? so players don't get confused by the rebel clan in the Cam? But what about in universe reasons? What about my Brujah already in the Cam who are rather attached to the whole thing? The Hecata, that can work as a sect, but why are they a clan, doesn't that just serve to deny players all the interesting discipline and weakness combinations that necromancers had? Why would my necromancers join a block of necromancers when they've done so well so far as necromancers while avoiding the giovanni? These choices, or really the cutting down of choices, are just so pointlessly bad for players and characters.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> I, like another poster, enjoy reading about the meta plot, but mostly don't use it. Your right the Brujah wouldn't all leave any more than the Gangrel all would have, All the clans were not included in the Camarilla because they weren't invented yet, and a Follower of Set would stay a Follower of Set, just like a path of harmony follower would still follow the path of harmony. I wonder how many people use all the NPC's and premade cities? I'm sure most everyone whos played for a long time has used CbN, but I've never put Lucita or Bell or Becket in a game. I've never even used Harderstat, The Camarilla never lost all the Gangrel nor Brujah, My Giovanni are streamlined and more pure now than before V5 plot due to the civil war/Cap revenge play I &quot;borrowed&quot; and reworked.<br /> <br /> I don't disagree with you, I'm just wondering if someone should have made a 2 post poll thread of do you use the meta plot and published NPC's often? or do most people just make up their own and borrow the broad strokes you find inspiring?<br /> <br /> As much as I mentioned liking the Red Death trilogy there's no point to using 4th gen gods or Horus king of all mummies. Even CbN doesn't really hold up because any real opposition aligned with Menele would be gone after a few years and Helena's regained strength and takeover of a few clans. The correct response to meeting Helena was illustrated by Becket. &quot;well, that was fun, gotta go now, bye&quot;<br /> <br /> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25794-mywifeisscary\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar25794_2.png');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"25794\" data-vbnamecard=\"25794\">MyWifeIsScary</a> <br /> <br /> Ha you posted again before my slow typed reply.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":24221,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24221-vamps-like-us","user":"Vamps Like Us","date":". 04-17-2021, 11:49 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24221-vamps-like-us","name":"Vamps Like Us","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"390"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-04-17T08:57:36-07:00","id":1444338,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MyWifeIsScary</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">But, say, why were the Followers of Set deleted?</div> </div> </div> </div>They probably killed off the Followers of Set, which despite being iffy, had atleast some ancient Egyptian facets and interest into it; for the &quot;Ministry&quot; because now they have to be a Televangelist trope faction for the Anarchs. And since now they're supposed to be a &quot;main-line Clan&quot; and not a mere so-called &quot;Sn0wf1ake Bloodline&quot;, now we have to wipe out all the Egyptian stuff and motifs completely for the aforementioned &quot;Televangelist&quot; seeming. That's why they have this rebranding of being a &quot;Ministry&quot; or &quot;Church&quot;. <br /> <br /> I wonder how they're even going to address the fact that the main head dwellings and means of operation for the Followers of Set turned &quot;Ministry/Church&quot; are in North Africa/Egypt (duh) and why haven't any of the Setite leaders reacted to this mass heresy or if they're even aware these Heretics have made them joined the Anarchs.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Jade Kingdom Warrior","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25523-shakanaka","name":"Shakanaka","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25523_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"951"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-04-17T09:00:49-07:00","id":1444339,"title":"","content":"We used Vienna in our only round well because we live in Vienna, there is german sourcebook about it and yeah. From my point of view I will repeat myself and say, I find downfall of the Chantry there a good thing because it is often misunderstood about the pyramid. But I honestly find it stupid being A already 2008 and B giving ISIS the fault. Mayby I whas to young back then but I never felt like 9/11 hit Europe that hard like it hit the US. From my opinion this whole terrortalk started during the Syrian War back then and so ISIS doing it 2015+ would have been more believable then Al-Quaida doing it 2008. And about Brujah leaving the came out of there own volatil is something I could understand neither. From my point I could see the Gangrel doing it mainly but I could hardly believ all the Brujah doing it. I always imagined under the Brujah there is a brothertwist like in Code Geass where one side says we need to be rebells and be in the Anarch to change things while the other side says you can only change the Camerilla from within. I would have found it more believable that Theo Bells action would have been seen more as a kind of warning so the Cam is excluding all the Brujah out of their Elitist club because everyone fears the Brujah next to him is doing the same no matter how civilized he looks.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>As I am from Austria I need to clarify two things.<br /> First my native language is german and so please point out if the english I write is broken so I can improve.<br /> Second I do not own VTMV beyond first three books nor any line after M20 Corebook because it is not out there and I wait for the translation.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26160-koronus","name":"Koronus","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2020"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"366"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-04-17T09:08:02-07:00","id":1444340,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Shakanaka</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1443592-the-official-v5-vs-v20-thread?p=1444338#post1444338\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> They probably killed off the Followers of Set, which despite being iffy, had atleast some ancient Egyptian facets and interest into it; for the &quot;Ministry&quot; because now they have to be a Televangelist trope faction for the Anarchs. And since now they're supposed to be a &quot;main-line Clan&quot; and not a mere so-called &quot;Sn0wf1ake Bloodline&quot;, now we have to wipe out all the Egyptian stuff and motifs completely for the aforementioned &quot;Televangelist&quot; seeming. That's why they have this rebranding of being a &quot;Ministry&quot; or &quot;Church&quot;.<br /> <br /> I wonder how they're even going to address the fact that the main head dwellings and means of operation for the Followers of Set turned &quot;Ministry/Church&quot; are in North Africa/Egypt (duh) and why haven't any of the Setite leaders reacted to this mass heresy or if they're even aware these Heretics have made them joined the Anarchs.</div> </div> </div> </div>I think what you're describing is actually V20 not V5.<br /> <br /> I have a theory about the developments with the Followers of Set that they actually just were renamed for V5 and the entirety of the split between the V5 Church of Set and Ministry is the product of Onyx Path pitching their plotline for their update of the Clan before it getting accepted. Remember that OPP had their own plans for V5 (that I will call OPP5 for the sake of argument) that they've been incorporating elements of into canon from the beginning.<br /> <br /> <i>Beckett's Jyhad Diarty</i> talks extensively about how there's a brewing battle between the various non-Set themed cults that have existed since the early days of the Clan (as early as the Serpents of Light in fact) versus the orthodox Heirophants in the Fire Court that believe in Set alone. If you read BJD you'd note that the Church of Set is the one who caused the break rather than the Ministry as like Ur-Shulgi, it was their crackdown that caused a rift rather than a desire to secede.<br /> <br /> Early Ministry was just said to be a &quot;rebranding&quot; but Cults of the Blood Gods made it a Civil War that followed up on the original OPP plotline introduced in V20.<br /> <br /> OPP5 was always going to happen and not everything was going to stay the same. Mind you, I'm biased because BJD is my all time favorite supplement for V:TM so I payed religious attention to it and even did a WIR of it.<br /> <br /> Edit:<br /> <br /> Here's the relevant chapter from BJD:<br /> <br /> <div class=\"b-bbcode b-bbcode__url b-bbcode__url--preview\"> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1323475-wir-beckett-s-jyhad-diary-the-big-book-of-metaplot?p=1327865#post1327865\" class=\"urlimg_container\"> <img class=\"js-img-fallback\" src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/filedata/fetch?filedataid=1074\"> </a> <div class=\"urlinfo\"> <div class=\"title ellipsis\"> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1323475-wir-beckett-s-jyhad-diary-the-big-book-of-metaplot?p=1327865#post1327865\"> [WIR] Beckett's Jyhad Diary - The Big book of Metaplot - Onyx Path Forums </a> </div> <div class=\"url ellipsis\"> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1323475-wir-beckett-s-jyhad-diary-the-big-book-of-metaplot?p=1327865#post1327865\"> http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1323475-wir-beckett-s-jyhad-diary-the-big-book-of-metaplot?p=1327865#post1327865 </a> </div> <div class=\"meta\"> https://vignette.wikia.nocookie.net/whitewolf/images/5/50/225322.jpg/revision/latest?cb=20180110170618 So, who loved Beckett's Jyhad Diary? It wasn't just my </div> </div> </div><br /> <br /> <div class=\"b-bbcode b-bbcode__url b-bbcode__url--preview\"> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1323475-wir-beckett-s-jyhad-diary-the-big-book-of-metaplot?p=1327869#post1327869\" class=\"urlimg_container\"> <img class=\"js-img-fallback\" src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/filedata/fetch?filedataid=1074\"> </a> <div class=\"urlinfo\"> <div class=\"title ellipsis\"> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1323475-wir-beckett-s-jyhad-diary-the-big-book-of-metaplot?p=1327869#post1327869\"> [WIR] Beckett's Jyhad Diary - The Big book of Metaplot - Onyx Path Forums </a> </div> <div class=\"url ellipsis\"> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1323475-wir-beckett-s-jyhad-diary-the-big-book-of-metaplot?p=1327869#post1327869\"> http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1323475-wir-beckett-s-jyhad-diary-the-big-book-of-metaplot?p=1327869#post1327869 </a> </div> <div class=\"meta\"> https://vignette.wikia.nocookie.net/whitewolf/images/5/50/225322.jpg/revision/latest?cb=20180110170618 So, who loved Beckett's Jyhad Diary? It wasn't just my </div> </div> </div>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Author of <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Cthulhu-Armageddon-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01KUOM7SI/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982844&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Cthulhu+Armageddon\" target=\"_blank\">Cthulhu Armageddon</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Teenage-Weredeer-Bright-Falls-Mysteries-ebook/dp/B075TTN2FN/ref=sr_1_2?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982717&amp;sr=1-2&amp;keywords=Weredeer#customerReviews\" target=\"_blank\">I was a Teenage Weredeer</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Straight-Outta-Fangton-Comedic-Vampire-ebook/dp/B01KNHICCC/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982774&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Straight+Outta+Fangton\" target=\"_blank\">Straight Outta Fangton</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Lucifers-Star-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01MDM9MCT/ref=mt_kindle?_encoding=UTF8&amp;me=&amp;qid=\" target=\"_blank\">Lucifer's Star</a>, </i>and the <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Rules-Supervillainy-Saga-Book-ebook/dp/B07MB89S33/\" target=\"_blank\">Supervillainy Saga</a>.</i><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":12002,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","user":"CTPhipps","date":". 04-17-2021, 12:12 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","name":"CTPhipps","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12002_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13933"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-04-17T09:23:47-07:00","id":1444342,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Damian May</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1443592-the-official-v5-vs-v20-thread?p=1444317#post1444317\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">You just need to take 50% of what CT posts as semi-&quot; Devils Advocate &quot; type statements. I literally thought I ws going insane a year or so ago when me and him had regular interactions as the discussion would go on for pages and then suddenly he'd agree with a post of mine and state that that was what he was saying all along. I reacted badly and honestly thought I was being trolled and did some....regrettable....things.<br /> <br /> I've worked out its just an idiosynchratic post style since then and reduced my interaction because it just hurts my brain a little too much but I know now that its all 100% legitimate posts on his behalf and I think we're all good now. ( except over KotE.....but that is a battle that will one day likely claim my very soul. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/biggrin.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Big Grin\" smilieid=\"3\" class=\"inlineimg\" /> )</div> </div> </div> </div>I worked in academia before becoming an author so I try and examine all of the angles of an argument to come to the most holistic possible answer. I also try and take the view that when dealing with matters of artistic criticism (I was a literature teacher) that most complaints are going to subjective or have value. The same with praise as well as enjoyment. I have also been known to have my opinion on things completely changed by posters, which sometimes throws them for a loop.<br /> <br /> I am very Pro-V5 as a general rule but I also was not blown away by some of the decisions in the original V5 releases and think of the first three books (ANARCH, CAMARILLA, main) as &quot;ehhhh&quot; in places. My unqualified enthusiasm for V5 is pretty much entirely the Chicago Chronicles books and the Cults of the Blood Gods. Plus I really have loved the visual novels and comic.<br /> <br /> I should mention that I was also a latecomer to V20. I played Vampire like a fanatic to Revised then started playing Masquerade with Requiem rules before dropping it. I came to V20 relatively late with Beckett's Jyhad Diary (i.e the last book) and Anarchs Unbound.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Damian May</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1443592-the-official-v5-vs-v20-thread?p=1444318#post1444318\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">As most of my Campaigns are set in Oceania or South East Asia the Metaplot and Signature Characters have been essentially irrelevant for the past 30ish years even if I followed Canon. I had no idea people thought Bloodlines was anything more than a relatively unpopular badly flawed rpg/beat-em-up that was only playable due to extensive modding until a few years ago when a bunch of people said it was the key to them getting into VtM.<br /> <br /> *shrug*<br /> <br /> We all have different experiences.</div> </div> </div> </div>I think, like the Rocky Horror Picture Show, Bloodlines is the very definition of a cult classic. It developed a fandom that helped keep it alive and the Official Patch showing the game's actual potential meant that it actually was a fantastic game underneath. Steam really was a second release for this and a much more successful one.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Chris24601</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1443592-the-official-v5-vs-v20-thread?p=1444330#post1444330\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Regardless of how well the IP as whole might be doing, I think those numbers tell a story of the tabletop portion of the IP is not delivering content most of the IP\u2019s fans in that medium would find useful.</div> </div> </div> </div>I have the different theory that the posters in the OPP forum are a sample size of people who are mostly V20 players. One's opinion might be different if one went to the World of Darkness 5th Edition or Vampire: The Masquerade 5th Edition Facebook groups.<br /> <br /> Similarly, there's the massive Bloodlines fandom groups that would probably outnumber all of them put together several times over and go, &quot;Oh yeah, the tabletop game. That's kinda nerdy.&quot;","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Author of <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Cthulhu-Armageddon-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01KUOM7SI/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982844&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Cthulhu+Armageddon\" target=\"_blank\">Cthulhu Armageddon</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Teenage-Weredeer-Bright-Falls-Mysteries-ebook/dp/B075TTN2FN/ref=sr_1_2?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982717&amp;sr=1-2&amp;keywords=Weredeer#customerReviews\" target=\"_blank\">I was a Teenage Weredeer</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Straight-Outta-Fangton-Comedic-Vampire-ebook/dp/B01KNHICCC/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982774&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Straight+Outta+Fangton\" target=\"_blank\">Straight Outta Fangton</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Lucifers-Star-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01MDM9MCT/ref=mt_kindle?_encoding=UTF8&amp;me=&amp;qid=\" target=\"_blank\">Lucifer's Star</a>, </i>and the <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Rules-Supervillainy-Saga-Book-ebook/dp/B07MB89S33/\" target=\"_blank\">Supervillainy Saga</a>.</i><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":12002,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","user":"CTPhipps","date":". 04-17-2021, 12:32 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","name":"CTPhipps","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12002_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13933"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-04-17T09:39:15-07:00","id":1444343,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Koronus</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1443592-the-official-v5-vs-v20-thread?p=1444339#post1444339\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">We used Vienna in our only round well because we live in Vienna, there is german sourcebook about it and yeah. From my point of view I will repeat myself and say, I find downfall of the Chantry there a good thing because it is often misunderstood about the pyramid. But I honestly find it stupid being A already 2008 and B giving ISIS the fault. Mayby I whas to young back then but I never felt like 9/11 hit Europe that hard like it hit the US.</div> </div> </div> </div>There were some horrifying incidents like the 2005 London attacks that killed 56 people and the 2004 attack on Madrid where 193 people were killed.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> From my opinion this whole terrortalk started during the Syrian War back then and so ISIS doing it 2015+ would have been more believable then Al-Quaida doing it 2008. </div> </div> </div>Yes, this is just a research failure and the proper &quot;cover story&quot; would be Al-Qaeda blows up an old castle historical site on page 3. That should be corrected in errata and future prints of the book.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> And about Brujah leaving the came out of there own volatil is something I could understand neither. From my point I could see the Gangrel doing it mainly but I could hardly believ all the Brujah doing it. I always imagined under the Brujah there is a brothertwist like in Code Geass where one side says we need to be rebells and be in the Anarch to change things while the other side says you can only change the Camerilla from within. I would have found it more believable that Theo Bells action would have been seen more as a kind of warning so the Cam is excluding all the Brujah out of their Elitist club because everyone fears the Brujah next to him is doing the same no matter how civilized he looks. </div> </div> </div>Well as we saw with the Gangrel, the Brujah leaving doesn't mean that they HAVE to leave. It primarily means they lost their Inner Council member and Justicar, which almost no Brujah loyalist is going to care about unless they planned to be so themselves. This was established in THE CAMARILLA too with Critias and Damien talking about how they were still members.<br /> <br /> Mind you, I've stated I want the following books:<br /> <br /> * Touchstones and Predator Types<br /> * The Fall of Vienna (similar to the Fall of London)<br /> * The Council of Prague<br /> <br /> I feel like 90% of the events described in the books would be better Chronicles than they would be metaplot developments. I offer to write them, OPP, if you want to pitch them!","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Author of <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Cthulhu-Armageddon-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01KUOM7SI/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982844&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Cthulhu+Armageddon\" target=\"_blank\">Cthulhu Armageddon</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Teenage-Weredeer-Bright-Falls-Mysteries-ebook/dp/B075TTN2FN/ref=sr_1_2?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982717&amp;sr=1-2&amp;keywords=Weredeer#customerReviews\" target=\"_blank\">I was a Teenage Weredeer</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Straight-Outta-Fangton-Comedic-Vampire-ebook/dp/B01KNHICCC/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982774&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Straight+Outta+Fangton\" target=\"_blank\">Straight Outta Fangton</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Lucifers-Star-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01MDM9MCT/ref=mt_kindle?_encoding=UTF8&amp;me=&amp;qid=\" target=\"_blank\">Lucifer's Star</a>, </i>and the <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Rules-Supervillainy-Saga-Book-ebook/dp/B07MB89S33/\" target=\"_blank\">Supervillainy Saga</a>.</i><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":12002,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","user":"CTPhipps","date":". 04-17-2021, 12:41 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","name":"CTPhipps","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12002_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13933"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-04-17T12:09:11-07:00","id":1444368,"title":"","content":"Predator types are too crude. The idea is fine, the execution is a joke. It reminds me of the background system from 5e, only the background system from 5e is leaps and bounds better because the mechanics of it are clear and it's easy to make adjustments to fit your character: Pick two skills, two tool/language profeciences, one feature, and... well, I guess the starting crap you get from those backgrounds is rather uneven. V5 predator types are just... there's no clear system to derive an adjustment, and every single one has debilitating weaknesses because they assume this is the only way you feed which is quite laughable. Let's say you cleave: How do you cleave? Consent? Stealth? Abuse? Is your family big enough to be healthy while you cleave or are they merely a supplement? Let's say you're a farm-feeder; Your prey is actually going to die when you feed from them, unlike with human feedings; why do you think you deserve an extra point of humanity you deranged fucking lunatic? <br /> <br /> The other thing is that V5 has a very regimented character creation system, and Predator types are the one thing that destabilizes everything.<br /> <br /> Speaking of predator types; the idea of resonances is very much at odds with the idea that you get disciplines through hunting a certain way/practicing the disciplines/ that they're a natural extention of you and that clans who are very charismatic and tend to seduce are more likely to have presence whilst those that are more forceful are going to have potence. I don't think the first four games explicitly said how vampires cultivate disciplines, but the implications are pretty strong. Resonances could certainly be a secondary thing for learning powers, but they aren't going to be the main thing.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25794-mywifeisscary","name":"MyWifeIsScary","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25794_2.png","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3711"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-04-17T12:50:41-07:00","id":1444374,"title":"","content":"Predator Types are pretty explicitly your character's preferred method, not their only method, or even most common method given their recent circumstances.<br /> <br /> But that doesn't really help the lack of balance in the spreads presented.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-04-17T12:52:57-07:00","id":1444375,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Heavy Arms</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1443592-the-official-v5-vs-v20-thread?p=1444374#post1444374\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Predator Types are pretty explicitly your character's preferred method, not their only method, or even most common method given their recent circumstances.<br /> <br /> But that doesn't really help the lack of balance in the spreads presented.</div> </div> </div> </div>I admit my interpretation of Predator Types is basically just a bonus to give to players at the start as an incentive to encourage thinking about how you get blood.<br /> <br /> &quot;If you choose something hard like feeding on vampires then you get an addition dot of Blood Potency!&quot;","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Author of <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Cthulhu-Armageddon-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01KUOM7SI/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982844&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Cthulhu+Armageddon\" target=\"_blank\">Cthulhu Armageddon</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Teenage-Weredeer-Bright-Falls-Mysteries-ebook/dp/B075TTN2FN/ref=sr_1_2?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982717&amp;sr=1-2&amp;keywords=Weredeer#customerReviews\" target=\"_blank\">I was a Teenage Weredeer</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Straight-Outta-Fangton-Comedic-Vampire-ebook/dp/B01KNHICCC/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982774&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Straight+Outta+Fangton\" target=\"_blank\">Straight Outta Fangton</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Lucifers-Star-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01MDM9MCT/ref=mt_kindle?_encoding=UTF8&amp;me=&amp;qid=\" target=\"_blank\">Lucifer's Star</a>, </i>and the <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Rules-Supervillainy-Saga-Book-ebook/dp/B07MB89S33/\" target=\"_blank\">Supervillainy Saga</a>.</i><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","name":"CTPhipps","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12002_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13933"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-04-17T13:29:10-07:00","id":1444381,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CTPhipps</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1443592-the-official-v5-vs-v20-thread?p=1444342#post1444342\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I have the different theory that the posters in the OPP forum are a sample size of people who are mostly V20 players. One's opinion might be different if one went to the World of Darkness 5th Edition or Vampire: The Masquerade 5th Edition Facebook groups.</div> </div> </div> </div>Using those Facebook groups though won't get you a valid sample either as they're self-selecting to exclude those who dislike V5 and prefer V20. It'd be akin to going to a DC Comics Facebook group and saying &quot;based on the numbers 95% of the population prefers DC to Marvel.&quot;<br /> <br /> The OPP forums at least have subjects that cater to both V20 and V5 fans and, if you go back and look at the older forum posts, there was no particular initial animus towards V5 here before its release. The sentiment against entirely arose from people who could have gone either way reading and disliking it. Thus, it feels like a place where you're more likely to get a relatively normalized sample of both V20 and V5 players.<br /> <br /> Another thing we know is that V20 is an Adamantine Best Seller on DriveThruRPG while V5 is only Mithral (the minimum threshold for which is half that of Adamantine).<br /> <br /> Lastly, since Bloodlines was released in 2004 I feel that trying to claim its popularity as part of the overall V5 brand popularity is a bit disingenuous, By Edition era its initial release falls solidly on the tail end of Revised and became a cult classic during the interegnum that was NWoD and V20 era.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1328-chris24601","name":"Chris24601","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"520"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-04-17T13:36:18-07:00","id":1444383,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Chris24601</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1443592-the-official-v5-vs-v20-thread?p=1444381#post1444381\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Using those Facebook groups though won't get you a valid sample either as they're self-selecting to exclude those who dislike V5 and prefer V20. It'd be akin to going to a DC Comics Facebook group and saying &quot;based on the numbers 95% of the population prefers DC to Marvel.&quot;<br /> <br /> The OPP forums at least have subjects that cater to both V20 and V5 fans and, if you go back and look at the older forum posts, there was no particular initial animus towards V5 here before its release. The sentiment against entirely arose from people who could have gone either way reading and disliking it. Thus, it feels like a place where you're more likely to get a relatively normalized sample of both V20 and V5 players.<br /> <br /> Another thing we know is that V20 is an Adamantine Best Seller on DriveThruRPG while V5 is only Mithral (the minimum threshold for which is half that of Adamantine).</div> </div> </div> </div>Eh, even then V20 was something where long term posters were introduced to the game world and V20 was a OPP project while the V5 books are licensed products. They're also fairly recent additions to the catalogs with only 4 books having come out from OPP for the V5 world. Which is a small number compared to the entire V20 catalog. People who purchased V5 are also likely to have purchased V20 here.<br /> <br /> I also think DriveThru RPG is something we need to ditch as an indicator of success because it's misleading with V5 the same way that comic book sales are the same.<br /> <br /> <img src=\"https://i.pinimg.com/originals/76/54/d5/7654d5a78c14e8362f4d839c3ece2b5b.jpg\" class=\"bbcode-attachment bbcode-attachment--lightbox js-lightbox\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" itemprop=\"image\" loading=\"lazy\"/><br /> <br /> Entirely different markets than the &quot;specialty&quot; market have opened up as we see by the review numbers here. The store sales are also a major contribution there. This isn't to say that DriveThru RPG isn't an important vendor, far from it, and it is a major source of publicity and revenue for awesome people like OPP but there was a reason that the Kickstarters were also designed with the idea of having sales specially available for bookstores.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"b-bbcode b-bbcode__url b-bbcode__url--preview\"> <a href=\"https://www.drivethrucomics.com/\" target=\"_blank\" class=\"urlimg_container\"> <img class=\"js-img-fallback\" src=\"https://www.drivethrucomics.com/themes/dtcomics/site-logo-redesignd.png\"> </a> <div class=\"urlinfo\"> <div class=\"title ellipsis\"> <a href=\"https://www.drivethrucomics.com/\" target=\"_blank\"> DriveThruComics.com - The First Download Comic Shop </a> </div> <div class=\"url ellipsis\"> <a href=\"https://www.drivethrucomics.com/\" target=\"_blank\"> https://www.drivethrucomics.com/ </a> </div> <div class=\"meta\"> Your one-stop, on-line shop for new and vintage Comic Books from independent publishers, delivered fresh to your desktop in electronic format. </div> </div> </div><br /> <br /> DriveThru Comics lists V:TM as a best seller alongside Buck Godot and Girl Genius consistently as its top seller but that doesn't mean it is a breakthrough hit (and it doesn't mean it's not).<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Chris24601</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1443592-the-official-v5-vs-v20-thread?p=1444381#post1444381\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Lastly, since Bloodlines was released in 2004 I feel that trying to claim its popularity as part of the overall V5 brand popularity is a bit disingenuous, By Edition era its initial release falls solidly on the tail end of Revised and became a cult classic during the interegnum that was NWoD and V20 era.</div> </div> </div> </div>I'm not sure where you assumed I did believe that. Bloodlines is a perfect example of cross platform advertising, though, as it introduced an entirely non-tabletop group of gamers to the setting and its concepts. Thus growing the band and intellectual property as a whole. There's a reason V5 heavily promotes charcters from that game, though.<br /> <br /> Its why I think that Bloodlines 2's popularity will be the biggest introduction for V5 to people. I am disappointed it's been delayed a year but I suppose better than the fiasco of Cyberpunk 2077.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Author of <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Cthulhu-Armageddon-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01KUOM7SI/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982844&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Cthulhu+Armageddon\" target=\"_blank\">Cthulhu Armageddon</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Teenage-Weredeer-Bright-Falls-Mysteries-ebook/dp/B075TTN2FN/ref=sr_1_2?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982717&amp;sr=1-2&amp;keywords=Weredeer#customerReviews\" target=\"_blank\">I was a Teenage Weredeer</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Straight-Outta-Fangton-Comedic-Vampire-ebook/dp/B01KNHICCC/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982774&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Straight+Outta+Fangton\" target=\"_blank\">Straight Outta Fangton</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Lucifers-Star-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01MDM9MCT/ref=mt_kindle?_encoding=UTF8&amp;me=&amp;qid=\" target=\"_blank\">Lucifer's Star</a>, </i>and the <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Rules-Supervillainy-Saga-Book-ebook/dp/B07MB89S33/\" target=\"_blank\">Supervillainy Saga</a>.</i><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":12002,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","user":"CTPhipps","date":". 04-17-2021, 04:50 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","name":"CTPhipps","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12002_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13933"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-04-17T16:43:20-07:00","id":1444403,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CTPhipps</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1443592-the-official-v5-vs-v20-thread?p=1444383#post1444383\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I also think DriveThru RPG is something we need to ditch as an indicator of success because it's misleading with V5 the same way that comic book sales are the same.</div> </div> </div> </div>It's not misleading, in that it is a relative measure, which is a reasonable enough perspective. Moreover, none of the relative measures are actually terribly impressive; given that you posted an image from Amazon, I checked the local sales rank. V5 is at 24,670 in the toys and games category. The <i>Dungeons &amp; Dragons</i> starter set, meanwhile, sits at 76. <br /> <br /> (Sales rank may vary by country and category, of course.)<br /> <br /> Again, this goes back to my point earlier in the thread; <i>Vampire: the Masquerade </i>used to outsell <i>Dungeons &amp; Dragons</i> back in the 1990s, and should be absolutely killing it right now. But, it underperforms in every category where public data is available. V5 should have killed the market for every single previous edition of <i>Vampire: the Masquerade</i>, but V20 remains a very strong seller. The points of comparison are limited, in so far as sales outlets for V20 are extremely limited, but I would predict that, should V20 be more readily available on Amazon, it would outsell V5 there as well.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/317-james_willoughby","name":"James_Willoughby","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar317_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"297"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-04-17T16:44:31-07:00","id":1444404,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>James_Willoughby</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1443592-the-official-v5-vs-v20-thread?p=1444403#post1444403\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> It's not misleading, in that it is a relative measure, which is a reasonable enough perspective. Moreover, none of the relative measures are actually terribly impressive; given that you posted an image from Amazon, I checked the local sales rank. V5 is at 24,670 in the toys and games category. The <i>Dungeons &amp; Dragons</i> starter set, meanwhile, sits at 76.</div> </div> </div> </div>It's not really a good argument since it's 570 Ratings versus V20's.....5. Because V20 isn't available on Amazon.<br /> <br /> Which means every sale there is an additional market.<br /> <br /> Ditto Modiphius (which no longer publishes the books anyway).<br /> <br /> Which I take to mean that it's blowing it away sales wise. But I've stated my opinion is very different in terms of V5's success. The quality of the book is entirely debatable but I believe it's a big success and building back up V:TM to becoming a cultural touchstone. No pun intended.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> The points of comparison are limited, in so far as sales outlets for V20 are extremely limited, but I would predict that, should V20 be more readily available on Amazon, it would outsell V5 there as well. </div> </div> </div>Like I said, I feel like the issue is people are trying to set them up as enemies when they're separate editions. I like V5 slightly more but I bought both. Why wouldn't I?<br /> <br /> The hope for V5 should be that it reaches more countries than V20, more languages, and brings in new gamers.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Author of <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Cthulhu-Armageddon-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01KUOM7SI/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982844&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Cthulhu+Armageddon\" target=\"_blank\">Cthulhu Armageddon</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Teenage-Weredeer-Bright-Falls-Mysteries-ebook/dp/B075TTN2FN/ref=sr_1_2?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982717&amp;sr=1-2&amp;keywords=Weredeer#customerReviews\" target=\"_blank\">I was a Teenage Weredeer</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Straight-Outta-Fangton-Comedic-Vampire-ebook/dp/B01KNHICCC/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982774&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Straight+Outta+Fangton\" target=\"_blank\">Straight Outta Fangton</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Lucifers-Star-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01MDM9MCT/ref=mt_kindle?_encoding=UTF8&amp;me=&amp;qid=\" target=\"_blank\">Lucifer's Star</a>, </i>and the <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Rules-Supervillainy-Saga-Book-ebook/dp/B07MB89S33/\" target=\"_blank\">Supervillainy Saga</a>.</i><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":12002,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","user":"CTPhipps","date":". 04-17-2021, 07:54 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","name":"CTPhipps","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12002_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13933"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-04-17T17:13:15-07:00","id":1444411,"title":"","content":"It's not people trying to set them up as enemies in this case, it's about trying to make the case that V5's success is basically not about V5, but about the strength of the VtM brand. V5's quality isn't why it's successful, but that the market is hungry for VtM is the conclusion people are drawing from the data available. Thus if V20 were as widely distributed with the same financial investment by Paradox in marketing, it would be doing as good as V5 at least. If not better because V20 has shown a much more enduring sales status, while V5 seems to have sold a lot on release but shown to be weaker over time. Again, all of this is educated guesses based on a very incomplete sample based on how little of this data is public, but it's the most data we're getting.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":617,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","user":"Heavy Arms","date":". 04-17-2021, 08:15 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-04-17T19:08:30-07:00","id":1444425,"title":"","content":"\u200b<a href=\"https://www.freecomicbookday.com/Catalog/APR210047\" target=\"_blank\">https://www.freecomicbookday.com/Catalog/APR210047</a><br /> <br /> Cool, Winter's Teeth #1 will be one of the comics given away on Free Comic Book Day! Hopefully this will help promote the series to being a Top 100 comic regularly.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Author of <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Cthulhu-Armageddon-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01KUOM7SI/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982844&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Cthulhu+Armageddon\" target=\"_blank\">Cthulhu Armageddon</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Teenage-Weredeer-Bright-Falls-Mysteries-ebook/dp/B075TTN2FN/ref=sr_1_2?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982717&amp;sr=1-2&amp;keywords=Weredeer#customerReviews\" target=\"_blank\">I was a Teenage Weredeer</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Straight-Outta-Fangton-Comedic-Vampire-ebook/dp/B01KNHICCC/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982774&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Straight+Outta+Fangton\" target=\"_blank\">Straight Outta Fangton</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Lucifers-Star-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01MDM9MCT/ref=mt_kindle?_encoding=UTF8&amp;me=&amp;qid=\" target=\"_blank\">Lucifer's Star</a>, </i>and the <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Rules-Supervillainy-Saga-Book-ebook/dp/B07MB89S33/\" target=\"_blank\">Supervillainy Saga</a>.</i><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":12002,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","user":"CTPhipps","date":". 04-17-2021, 10:15 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","name":"CTPhipps","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12002_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13933"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-04-18T01:44:39-07:00","id":1444461,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Heavy Arms</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1443592-the-official-v5-vs-v20-thread?p=1444374#post1444374\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Predator Types are pretty explicitly your character's preferred method, not their only method, or even most common method given their recent circumstances.</div> </div> </div> </div> Yet farmer, consensualist and blood leech all give you pretty severe prey exclusion flaws; that's not a preference, that's your one-and-only-way.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25794-mywifeisscary","name":"MyWifeIsScary","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25794_2.png","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3711"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-04-18T02:16:50-07:00","id":1444465,"title":"","content":"Yep. The mechanics aren't correct for the concept... but that's pretty much my feeling on most of the book.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-04-18T05:25:57-07:00","id":1444489,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MyWifeIsScary</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1443592-the-official-v5-vs-v20-thread?p=1444461#post1444461\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Yet farmer, consensualist and blood leech all give you pretty severe prey exclusion flaws; that's not a preference, that's your one-and-only-way.</div> </div> </div> </div>Yes, because they're about playing the &quot;nice&quot; vampire. You don't break the Masquerade if you don't care about grabbing some random dude.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Author of <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Cthulhu-Armageddon-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01KUOM7SI/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982844&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Cthulhu+Armageddon\" target=\"_blank\">Cthulhu Armageddon</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Teenage-Weredeer-Bright-Falls-Mysteries-ebook/dp/B075TTN2FN/ref=sr_1_2?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982717&amp;sr=1-2&amp;keywords=Weredeer#customerReviews\" target=\"_blank\">I was a Teenage Weredeer</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Straight-Outta-Fangton-Comedic-Vampire-ebook/dp/B01KNHICCC/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982774&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Straight+Outta+Fangton\" target=\"_blank\">Straight Outta Fangton</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Lucifers-Star-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01MDM9MCT/ref=mt_kindle?_encoding=UTF8&amp;me=&amp;qid=\" target=\"_blank\">Lucifer's Star</a>, </i>and the <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Rules-Supervillainy-Saga-Book-ebook/dp/B07MB89S33/\" target=\"_blank\">Supervillainy Saga</a>.</i><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","name":"CTPhipps","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12002_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13933"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-04-18T05:41:07-07:00","id":1444492,"title":"","content":"Thats just bad design right there, because it doesnt actually encapsulate what I or most players want to do. What if i just inherited a slaughterhouse and decided to take advantage of it? What if I prefer consent but only for 'the right people' and i am happy to hunt others ordinarily or when times are tough? Which Diablerist excludes mortals after the first vitae indulgence?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25794-mywifeisscary","name":"MyWifeIsScary","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25794_2.png","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3711"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-04-18T05:49:49-07:00","id":1444494,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MyWifeIsScary</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1443592-the-official-v5-vs-v20-thread?p=1444492#post1444492\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Thats just bad design right there, because it doesnt actually encapsulate what I or most players want to do. What if i just inherited a slaughterhouse and decided to take advantage of it? What if I prefer consent but only for 'the right people' and i am happy to hunt others ordinarily or when times are tough? Which Diablerist excludes mortals after the first vitae indulgence?</div> </div> </div> </div>Oh I agree with that as giving bonuses for it is a great idea but the books show that vampires DO go outside their Predator Types all the time. The Thin Blood or 13th generation who can drink Animal Blood and does but also hunts on occassion for humans is valid.<br /> <br /> It's why we need more information on when and where to use these things.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Author of <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Cthulhu-Armageddon-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01KUOM7SI/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982844&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Cthulhu+Armageddon\" target=\"_blank\">Cthulhu Armageddon</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Teenage-Weredeer-Bright-Falls-Mysteries-ebook/dp/B075TTN2FN/ref=sr_1_2?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982717&amp;sr=1-2&amp;keywords=Weredeer#customerReviews\" target=\"_blank\">I was a Teenage Weredeer</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Straight-Outta-Fangton-Comedic-Vampire-ebook/dp/B01KNHICCC/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982774&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Straight+Outta+Fangton\" target=\"_blank\">Straight Outta Fangton</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Lucifers-Star-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01MDM9MCT/ref=mt_kindle?_encoding=UTF8&amp;me=&amp;qid=\" target=\"_blank\">Lucifer's Star</a>, </i>and the <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Rules-Supervillainy-Saga-Book-ebook/dp/B07MB89S33/\" target=\"_blank\">Supervillainy Saga</a>.</i><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","name":"CTPhipps","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12002_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13933"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-04-18T12:37:14-07:00","id":1444531,"title":"","content":"But it's not a matter of information about when and where to use the mechanics. It's a question of if the mechanics do what they say they do for the play experience of the game.<br /> <br /> Predator Types can't be a set of bonuses to reward having a preferred feeding style for your character, but not force you into feeding that way exclusively, if they're coupled with forced Flaws that impact how you can feed.<br /> <br /> If Predator Types were more &quot;build your own,&quot; where you can pick Flaws that don't impact feeding the same way if you want a character loosely impacted, or Flaws that are very controlling if you want, it wouldn't be the same kind of issue (and would probably make it easier to solve some of the imbalance in them when you look at how much XP they're worth).","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-04-18T14:17:38-07:00","id":1444546,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MyWifeIsScary</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1443592-the-official-v5-vs-v20-thread?p=1444461#post1444461\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Yet farmer, consensualist and blood leech all give you pretty severe prey exclusion flaws; that's not a preference, that's your one-and-only-way.</div> </div> </div> </div>Yeah, Farmer doesn't really seem to have a mechanic for transitioning to a different feeding method once your Humanity drops, which seems rather silly. What if you are playing someone who starts as a Farmer, then transitions to Alleycat once his Humanity drops to 6?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3598-cajunkhan","name":"CajunKhan","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3598_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1700"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-04-18T14:28:42-07:00","id":1444548,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CajunKhan</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1443592-the-official-v5-vs-v20-thread?p=1444546#post1444546\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Yeah, Farmer doesn't really seem to have a mechanic for transitioning to a different feeding method once your Humanity drops, which seems rather silly. What if you are playing someone who starts as a Farmer, then transitions to Alleycat once his Humanity drops to 6?</div> </div> </div> </div>I like these rules but there's a lot of confusion.<br /> <br /> * How do you get new Convictions.<br /> * How do you get new Touchstones<br /> * How do you switch Predator types<br /> <br /> And so on.<br /> <br /> A lot is left to the Storyteller with only the implication that they are allowed to do so.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Author of <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Cthulhu-Armageddon-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01KUOM7SI/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982844&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Cthulhu+Armageddon\" target=\"_blank\">Cthulhu Armageddon</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Teenage-Weredeer-Bright-Falls-Mysteries-ebook/dp/B075TTN2FN/ref=sr_1_2?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982717&amp;sr=1-2&amp;keywords=Weredeer#customerReviews\" target=\"_blank\">I was a Teenage Weredeer</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Straight-Outta-Fangton-Comedic-Vampire-ebook/dp/B01KNHICCC/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982774&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Straight+Outta+Fangton\" target=\"_blank\">Straight Outta Fangton</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Lucifers-Star-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01MDM9MCT/ref=mt_kindle?_encoding=UTF8&amp;me=&amp;qid=\" target=\"_blank\">Lucifer's Star</a>, </i>and the <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Rules-Supervillainy-Saga-Book-ebook/dp/B07MB89S33/\" target=\"_blank\">Supervillainy Saga</a>.</i><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","name":"CTPhipps","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12002_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13933"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-04-18T16:21:38-07:00","id":1444565,"title":"","content":"I'm not really sure it's confusion, but that's a fairly redundant debate<br /> <br /> There is a significant difference between Touchstone/Convictions and Predator Types though. It's really not complicated to come up with a way to add Touchstones and Convictions, because they're fairly isolated elements.<br /> <br /> Switching a Predator Type is a problem because there's a pile of traits you get with one. Either you get what you get at creation, and changing types is just a descriptive matter, or you have to deal with a bunch of mechanical decisions on how changing one impacts the character.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":7}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-04-19T00:24:56-07:00","id":1444605,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CTPhipps</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1443592-the-official-v5-vs-v20-thread?p=1444548#post1444548\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I like these rules but there's a lot of confusion.<br /> <br /> * How do you get new Convictions.<br /> * How do you get new Touchstones<br /> * How do you switch Predator types<br /> <br /> And so on.<br /> <br /> A lot is left to the Storyteller with only the implication that they are allowed to do so.</div> </div> </div> </div>I'm not even sure there's an implication in the last example. Feeding Types are often restrictive enough that you can't switch them without mechanical guidance.<br /> <br /> Personally, I would've gone with a more VTR 'carrot' system where pursuing your favoured feeding method gave you little bonuses, rather than the current approach (where certain types of feeding are heavily penalised or outright banned).","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Writer, publisher, performer<br /> Mostly he/his, sometimes she/her IRL <a href=\"https://adam-lowe.com\" target=\"_blank\">https://adam-lowe.com</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5291-adambeyoncelowe","name":"adambeyoncelowe","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5291_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2802"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-04-19T00:31:01-07:00","id":1444606,"title":"","content":"I think a non-canon rule would be that if you are getting a heavy benefit from a largely restrictive Prey type that you can buy it off. Eventually, the Consensualist learns to willingly grab people off the street with EXP.<br /> <br /> Also, that if you DO have a heavy penalty Predator Type that you can overcome it with spent willpower for a scene.<br /> <br /> You know, these are the kind of rules we need.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Author of <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Cthulhu-Armageddon-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01KUOM7SI/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982844&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Cthulhu+Armageddon\" target=\"_blank\">Cthulhu Armageddon</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Teenage-Weredeer-Bright-Falls-Mysteries-ebook/dp/B075TTN2FN/ref=sr_1_2?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982717&amp;sr=1-2&amp;keywords=Weredeer#customerReviews\" target=\"_blank\">I was a Teenage Weredeer</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Straight-Outta-Fangton-Comedic-Vampire-ebook/dp/B01KNHICCC/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982774&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Straight+Outta+Fangton\" target=\"_blank\">Straight Outta Fangton</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Lucifers-Star-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01MDM9MCT/ref=mt_kindle?_encoding=UTF8&amp;me=&amp;qid=\" target=\"_blank\">Lucifer's Star</a>, </i>and the <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Rules-Supervillainy-Saga-Book-ebook/dp/B07MB89S33/\" target=\"_blank\">Supervillainy Saga</a>.</i><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","name":"CTPhipps","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12002_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13933"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-04-19T02:43:05-07:00","id":1444617,"title":"","content":"Another thing is, say, I think cleavers are stupid and should be rare, But I'm very likely to pick cleaver because its the only option for more Animalism that offers me room to grow; Farmer is wiser in fluff but mechanically cancerous. If I wanted Celerity, I'd have a choice between stupid (alleycat) and suicidal (Blood leech) which is a bit of a weird look for the so-humane Toreador. Extortionist seems very strong for the 3 resources it can grant you, while sandman and siren, two should-be-popular choices, are very middle of the pack. <br /> <br /> I just find myself as a player looking at these for the mechanics and finding myself disconnecting from the fluff as a result. In V20, my predator type is the result of how i make my character, not something I tack on at the end.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":6}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25794-mywifeisscary","name":"MyWifeIsScary","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25794_2.png","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3711"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-04-19T06:37:13-07:00","id":1444641,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MyWifeIsScary</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">my predator type is the result of how i make my character, not something I tack on at the end.</div> </div> </div> </div>Exactly! This is the exactly why I hated this &quot;Predator Type&quot; &quot;Mechanic&quot; as soon as I heard of it. Its forced and nonsensical, because it doesn't take into the account the inherently variable and non-linear situations in how a PC will gain blood. Even if your PC DOES have a &quot;constant&quot; way of getting blood, that can get disrupted entirely as the chronicle/story shifts. It feels too &quot;hard&quot;-mechanic, which V5 seems to love leaning into for whatever reason.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Jade Kingdom Warrior","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25523-shakanaka","name":"Shakanaka","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25523_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"951"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-04-19T07:12:42-07:00","id":1444653,"title":"","content":"Another point in V20\u2019s favor for me is that it has proper rules for Dhampirs and Revenants. The former are my preference when I actually get to play and both feature significantly among the PCs circle in my present campaign.<br /> <br /> V5 doesn\u2019t have those; their ghouls are anemic (good as NPCs, lousy as PCs) and don\u2019t really cover the degree of extra oomph that a Revenant has over a ghoul (most notably, having a replenishing blood pool means they can afford to use it to heal or pump stats when needed) and the step up from that that is a Dhampir (bigger blood pool that is entirely spiritual, plus basically the Timex of supernaturals).<br /> <br /> Similarly, compare the two very specific options for V5 Potence 1 (deal agg to mortals or jump based on rank when you\u2019re limited to 1 rank) to the broad applicability of V20 Potence 1. It\u2019s not earth-shattering power, but the Dhampir PC in our group can throw a motorcycle, rip steel doors open, reliably make a running jump two stories high and clear a two-lane city street.<br /> <br /> Nor are V5 thinbloods; who still need to feed and can\u2019t actually have disciplines; a good substitute for them (honestly, I\u2019ve considered adapting the V5 \u201cDuskborn\u201d to V20 as a whole separate category from the usual thinbloods... some sort of new mutation that lets them pick up temporary discipline dots from feeding and mix their blood with other crap to gain even weirder powers... so there are Thinbloods that are your usual 14-16th Gen with disciplines and possible Insight and Inceptor abilities and Duskborn with feeding-based temporary disciplines and adaptive blood mixing that are something else entirely).<br /> <br /> Just the sheer number of weird demi-vampires in V20 (ex. Hellhounds - revenant canines are a thing in V20) makes it a far more interesting setting to play in even if sticking straight VtM. Throw in access to other fully developed supernaturals (wraiths, werewolves, mages, changelings, hunters with numina, imbued hunters, demons, mummies, risen, hungry dead, spirits, bygones, etc.) for spice when needed and there\u2019s just no comparison in terms of not just playing the same basic vampire vs. vampire struggle in chronicle after chronicle.<br /> <br /> We\u2019re already several years in on V5 and W5 is still somewhere on the horizon with M5 so far out that Paradox has let OPP begin work on new M20 books. Likewise, their answer for some of the other edge case weirdness (ex. the Nagaraja) was to merge it into another group and make it less weird.<br /> <br /> So in terms of enjoying a larger and weirder supernatural world, V20 beats V5 hands down and likely will for years to come yet.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1328-chris24601","name":"Chris24601","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"520"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-04-19T09:59:32-07:00","id":1444673,"title":"","content":"Oh, here's where Renegade Studios is republishing Books 1-3 for retail purchase in stores. It doesn't appear they will be doing another run of FALL OF LONDON, which makes sense since Modiphius made that book.<br /> <br /> <a href=\"https://icv2.com/articles/news/view/47866/renegade-game-studios-printings-vampire-the-masquerade-5e-books-headed-retail?fbclid=IwAR2wMPXI4e95Q3fNlBmh8coN0QGL674iqg4ZInm9bcWT8OTI2apbd6b24rM\" target=\"_blank\">https://icv2.com/articles/news/view/...OTI2apbd6b24rM</a><br /> <br /> The books will be updated with the errata and new interior content (no Chechnya or feeding babies blood).","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Author of <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Cthulhu-Armageddon-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01KUOM7SI/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982844&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Cthulhu+Armageddon\" target=\"_blank\">Cthulhu Armageddon</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Teenage-Weredeer-Bright-Falls-Mysteries-ebook/dp/B075TTN2FN/ref=sr_1_2?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982717&amp;sr=1-2&amp;keywords=Weredeer#customerReviews\" target=\"_blank\">I was a Teenage Weredeer</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Straight-Outta-Fangton-Comedic-Vampire-ebook/dp/B01KNHICCC/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982774&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Straight+Outta+Fangton\" target=\"_blank\">Straight Outta Fangton</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Lucifers-Star-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01MDM9MCT/ref=mt_kindle?_encoding=UTF8&amp;me=&amp;qid=\" target=\"_blank\">Lucifer's Star</a>, </i>and the <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Rules-Supervillainy-Saga-Book-ebook/dp/B07MB89S33/\" target=\"_blank\">Supervillainy Saga</a>.</i><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","name":"CTPhipps","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12002_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13933"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-04-19T12:38:17-07:00","id":1444699,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Chris24601</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1443592-the-official-v5-vs-v20-thread?p=1444653#post1444653\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Another point in V20\u2019s favor for me is that it has proper rules for Dhampirs and Revenants. The former are my preference when I actually get to play and both feature significantly among the PCs circle in my present campaign..</div> </div> </div> </div>V20 doesn't too my knowledge have rules for Dhampirs,can you point them out? i believe it just references them and for some reason I think of them as backwards revenants. I actually don't mind playing ghouls in a vampire game. Being an underdog is... thrilling.<br /> <br /> V5 thinbloods are just an episode of absolute quackery.<br /> <br /> First off, &quot;Alchemy&quot;. Magic in the World of Darkness has always strayed far from DnD's idea &quot;looking through a spell list&quot;. Rather, it looks at real world esoteric practices; the Tremere are a <i>Hermetic </i>order, the Settites have a <i>Gnostic</i> belief system, the Assamites draw power from the stars and spirits just as real world mystics did. Alchemy thus isn't just a bog-standard western fantasy way of giving you +3 strength or 8 minutes of fire protection, it's a part-science part mystic approach to transform you (lead) into something greater (gold). It's an exercise of understanding the universe and self betterment. TBA is not only a lazy bog-standard potion brewing exercise, but it's an affront to the larger WoD practice of treating everything like it belongs in a cohesive, esoteric understanding of the world; the embrace is alchemy, with Caine being divine, purer gold and weaker bloods more earthly like lead; the thinbloods shouldn't be different because they're half and half, they should just be weaker. Even if you don't bother with all this esotericism, it's just unfitting that, say, mortals have disciplines up to 0, ghouls have disciplines of... let's say 1 for simplicity, 13th gen vampires have disciplines up to 5 and instead of being right in the middle and having disciplines up to 3 thinbloods instead... have something entirely different<br /> <br /> This esoteric outlook also goes into a lot of other things, for example having <b>abilities beyond the fifth dot </b>is tied to this idea that we can throw off our chains and unlock our potential through enlightenment and self betterment and alchemy; reality is a prison, that kind of thing. V5 is missing that, and not only is it disempowering, it invalidates the beliefs of mortal philosophies and the vampires who follow them: The Tremere, Settites, Ravnos and even V5's own Church of Caine all suffer heavily as a result.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25794-mywifeisscary","name":"MyWifeIsScary","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25794_2.png","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3711"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-04-19T14:21:58-07:00","id":1444714,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MyWifeIsScary</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1443592-the-official-v5-vs-v20-thread?p=1444699#post1444699\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">V20 doesn't too my knowledge have rules for Dhampirs,can you point them out?</div> </div> </div> </div>You can find the V20 versions in <i>Beckett's Jyhad Diary &quot;The Blood Matures&quot;, p. 144</i><br /> <br /> The main things of note with the update are that, unlike Revenants, they still get a blood pool of 10, they regenerate limbs with a Willpower test (diff 8) and blood (vs. a Stamina test, a point of willpower AND blood) and they not only soak lethal, they also treat all aggravated damage they take as lethal (which is why I refer to them as Timex's... they can take a licking and keep on ticking) meaning they can heal from fire, werewolf claws, etc. for a single blood point per health level at a rate of one per turn (until they're out of blood).<br /> <br /> On the downside it also clarifies that while they can be blood bound by drinking vitae, they never become ghouls (from BJD... <i>&quot;The Dhampir\u2019s vampiric heritage makes it impossible for her to become a changeling, demon, mage, mummy, werewolf, or their related kin. She can be blood bound to a vampire, though she does not become a ghoul.&quot;</i>)<br /> <br /> Thus, they have a hard discipline cap of 1 (i.e. no hooking up with a low gen vampire to get those higher dots like ghouls and revenants can), which is why I don't find their &quot;soak like a 7th Gen Ventrue&quot; and &quot;heal more efficiently than damned near anything&quot; to be particularly unbalanced (if anything it makes them feel a bit Slayer-ish in that they can get the crap kicked out of them and still bounce back... and get even more Slayer-ish if you give them the Fist of God merit) and also explains why they get fewer Freebies than Ghouls or Revenants.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MyWifeIsScary</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1443592-the-official-v5-vs-v20-thread?p=1444699#post1444699\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">V5 thinbloods are just an episode of absolute quackery.</div> </div> </div> </div>You'll get no argument from me.<br /> <br /> It's why for my V20 game I think I'd like to introduce the Duskborn (vs. Thinblood) as something completely different from the Thinblooded. Right now I'm leaning towards a Tremere experiment in trying to reverse engineer the process of creating Revenants that went awry and created a quasi-vampire that feeds on the resonance (in the Mage the Ascension sense) in blood rather than blood itself.<br /> <br /> A couple of them escaped when Vienna blew up and started multiplying like vampires are wont to (so they first turn up in numbers in European cities). One of them who was starving drank blood contaminated with something else and, in addition to picking up a resonance-linked discipline, also picked up a trait based on the resonance of the contamination... then they started experimenting and they call it Alchemy because most of these experiments are millennial's whose only experience with alchemy is actually from pop-culture fantasy.<br /> <br /> So basically, they're mutant quasi-vampires that escaped from a lab and have been messing things up for regular vampires ever since.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1328-chris24601","name":"Chris24601","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"520"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-04-19T15:33:00-07:00","id":1444722,"title":"","content":"I might consider something other than a Tremere experiment simply because that overlaps a lot with Gargoyles; just with different ways they're not normal vampires.<br /> <br /> For example (though I can understand some people might not be comfortable doing the research on doing this right), making them something the Ashirra made (they don't have any of the Revenant happy Clans, and might not want to be so reliant on the Banu Hakim or Setties as having local monopolies on blood magics (which also explains how the experiments got out of hand) given any number of events in the history/metaplot.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-04-19T15:44:05-07:00","id":1444724,"title":"","content":"CULTS OF THE BLOOD GODS pretty much establishes that Thin Blooded Alchemy is a Tremere creation and more specifically the Ashfinders. Specifically, Doctor Mortius. He may not have created ALL OF IT but he started the ball rolling.<br /> <br /> My biggest issue with V5, even with all my support, is the fact that they seem so very uninterested in explaining how all of this happens so I'm excited when they take the time to do so. If you're going to limit lower generation vampires to 5's in every Discipline and Attribute then I would appreciate if you gave an in-story reason like the Withering. If you're going to introduce something like Thin Blooded Alchemy then I think you should do the same for explaining who discovered it and why.<br /> <br /> I'm not really a big fan of &quot;this is how it's always been.&quot; That's something that drives me up the wall and it's all over V5.<br /> <br /> So I appreciate it when they DO give an explanation like this.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Author of <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Cthulhu-Armageddon-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01KUOM7SI/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982844&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Cthulhu+Armageddon\" target=\"_blank\">Cthulhu Armageddon</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Teenage-Weredeer-Bright-Falls-Mysteries-ebook/dp/B075TTN2FN/ref=sr_1_2?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982717&amp;sr=1-2&amp;keywords=Weredeer#customerReviews\" target=\"_blank\">I was a Teenage Weredeer</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Straight-Outta-Fangton-Comedic-Vampire-ebook/dp/B01KNHICCC/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982774&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Straight+Outta+Fangton\" target=\"_blank\">Straight Outta Fangton</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Lucifers-Star-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01MDM9MCT/ref=mt_kindle?_encoding=UTF8&amp;me=&amp;qid=\" target=\"_blank\">Lucifer's Star</a>, </i>and the <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Rules-Supervillainy-Saga-Book-ebook/dp/B07MB89S33/\" target=\"_blank\">Supervillainy Saga</a>.</i><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":12002,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","user":"CTPhipps","date":". 04-19-2021, 06:47 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","name":"CTPhipps","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12002_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13933"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-04-20T01:31:35-07:00","id":1444800,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CTPhipps</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1443592-the-official-v5-vs-v20-thread?p=1444673#post1444673\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Oh, here's where Renegade Studios is republishing Books 1-3 for retail purchase in stores. It doesn't appear they will be doing another run of FALL OF LONDON, which makes sense since Modiphius made that book.<br /> <br /> <a href=\"https://icv2.com/articles/news/view/47866/renegade-game-studios-printings-vampire-the-masquerade-5e-books-headed-retail?fbclid=IwAR2wMPXI4e95Q3fNlBmh8coN0QGL674iqg4ZInm9bcWT8OTI2apbd6b24rM\" target=\"_blank\">https://icv2.com/articles/news/view/...OTI2apbd6b24rM</a><br /> <br /> The books will be updated with the errata and new interior content (no Chechnya or feeding babies blood).</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Honestly they're better off folding the clan material in those two books into the core book and dumping all the IC waffle that is basically wasted paper. There's very little actual useful game material on the Camarilla or the Anarchs in them.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":6}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26564-badfurryfanfic","name":"BadFurryFanFic","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2020"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"93"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-04-20T01:35:36-07:00","id":1444801,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>BadFurryFanFic</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1443592-the-official-v5-vs-v20-thread?p=1444800#post1444800\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> Honestly they're better off folding the clan material in those two books into the core book and dumping all the IC waffle that is basically wasted paper. There's very little actual useful game material on the Camarilla or the Anarchs in them.</div> </div> </div> </div>That would be just redoing the book and it also wouldn't be a very good business decision. After all, you want people to buy more than the Core Book.<br /> <br /> That's just my greedy evil way of thinking, though.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Author of <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Cthulhu-Armageddon-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01KUOM7SI/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982844&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Cthulhu+Armageddon\" target=\"_blank\">Cthulhu Armageddon</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Teenage-Weredeer-Bright-Falls-Mysteries-ebook/dp/B075TTN2FN/ref=sr_1_2?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982717&amp;sr=1-2&amp;keywords=Weredeer#customerReviews\" target=\"_blank\">I was a Teenage Weredeer</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Straight-Outta-Fangton-Comedic-Vampire-ebook/dp/B01KNHICCC/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982774&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Straight+Outta+Fangton\" target=\"_blank\">Straight Outta Fangton</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Lucifers-Star-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01MDM9MCT/ref=mt_kindle?_encoding=UTF8&amp;me=&amp;qid=\" target=\"_blank\">Lucifer's Star</a>, </i>and the <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Rules-Supervillainy-Saga-Book-ebook/dp/B07MB89S33/\" target=\"_blank\">Supervillainy Saga</a>.</i><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","name":"CTPhipps","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12002_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13933"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-04-20T03:48:05-07:00","id":1444809,"title":"","content":"The fact that there are going to be three different versions of the print book out there isn't really a good business decision either. Regular updates for PDFs to include errata is one thing, but having there's a reason a lot of RPG don't do reprints to update physical books like this. It just creates confusion unless you actually make it really clear like &quot;V5.2, V5.3,&quot; etc. so people instantly know what version they're looking at.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":10}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-04-20T04:40:55-07:00","id":1444813,"title":"","content":"The Origin Awards win keeps getting brought up like it means something so its probably worth looking at the company V5 is keeping with its win:<br /> <br /> 2020- Teens in Space.....has anyone ever heard of this game?<br /> 2019- V5.<br /> 2018- Adventures in Middle Earth. 5e adaption of the The One Ring rpg. A solid book in my experience.<br /> 2017- No Thank You, Evil.....nope, never heard of this either.<br /> 2016- Star Wars: Force and Destiny. Solid performer from Fantasy Flight.<br /> 2015- D&amp;D 5th Ed- Pretty sure we all know this one.<br /> 2014- Numenera- seems to get mentioned fairly often as having good ideas but the execution is lacking. A mid-range performer.<br /> <br /> So thats 1 800lb gorilla, 2 solid games, 1 middling and 2 that are essentially unknowns........so Origin Awards can be given to pretty much anything and for a game to win it doesn't have to be either popular, particularly high quality or selling very well.<br /> <br /> So winning the award doesn't really tell us anything more than that some people on the jury ( 90% weighting) liked the game.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":6}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26564-badfurryfanfic","name":"BadFurryFanFic","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2020"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"93"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-04-20T11:46:29-07:00","id":1444880,"title":"","content":"As a note about what I like most about the V5 rules updates if anyone cares:<br /> <br /> <u>What I really like</u><br /> <br /> * The generation tied to what sort of blood you can drink.<br /> * Blood Potency tied to age.<br /> * Moving Humanity away from one single inflexible code of ethics to a more flexible series of personal convictions.<br /> * Thin Bloods having permanent Blush of Life.<br /> * Blush of Life just requiring one single rouse check versus a bunch of blood spent.<br /> * The changes to the Malkavian, Gangrel, and Ventrue weaknesses.<br /> * The updated Tzimisce rules.<br /> * Merging Serpentis, Vicisstitude, and Protean.<br /> * Combining the Abyss of Wraith and Lasombra.<br /> * Getting rid of Thaumaturgy Paths to be replaced with Rituals. Thaumathurgy Paths felt like they didn't want to make new Disciplines.<br /> * Loresheets allowing player characters to get much more hardcore into the Lore.<br /> * Being able to choose your own Generation as related to prey style and power level<br /> * Stains as a replacement for just automatic Humanity Loss.<br /> * Having a human ties or loved one to guard against Humanity loss. I had similar &quot;True Love&quot; rules that helped vampires guard against the Beast.<br /> * The revised rules so you can't blood bond someone without them knowing by spiking their drinks.<br /> * Ditto ghouldom.<br /> * The fact that Dominating mortals doesn't cost Blood and is automatic for the most part.<br /> * I like that Hunger never goes away unless you kill someone.<br /> * I like that Hunger is more erratic and unpredictable versus resource management.<br /> * Chronicle Tenet morality allows more flexibility whether you want to run a pacifist angst-ridden weepy game versus an action game with hundreds of bodies.<br /> <br /> <u>What I'm okay with</u><br /> <br /> * More flexibility about Nosferatu appearance is a good thing.<br /> * Loresheets as a means of tying Bloodlines to existing Clans indicates we may be getting a lot more variety on these without removing them from Clans entirely. After all, a lot of Bloodlines feel like they should be part of Clans but just &quot;off center.&quot;<br /> * Predator Types incentivize roleplaying out your feeding style.<br /> <br /> <u>What I don't like</u><br /> <br /> * I hate the Lasombra technology weakness.<br /> * I am not a big fan of giving vampires literal mental compulsions related to their Clan's stereotype.<br /> * The limit of 5 dots in Attributes and Disciplines is lore breaking and makes no goddamned sense.<br /> * The Amalgam purchase limitations are needlessly limiting and make no sense as well.<br /> * Healing ghouls should be allowed to be done by giving them blood.<br /> * Thin Bloods should be able to have at least one dot in Disciplines and not just as a Merit.<br /> * Thin Blooded Alchemy should not be their only thing.<br /> * I think Touchstones don't need to be linked with Convictions whatsoever.<br /> * I don't get the appeal of Resonances and think its a weird thing to introduce this late in the game.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Author of <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Cthulhu-Armageddon-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01KUOM7SI/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982844&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Cthulhu+Armageddon\" target=\"_blank\">Cthulhu Armageddon</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Teenage-Weredeer-Bright-Falls-Mysteries-ebook/dp/B075TTN2FN/ref=sr_1_2?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982717&amp;sr=1-2&amp;keywords=Weredeer#customerReviews\" target=\"_blank\">I was a Teenage Weredeer</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Straight-Outta-Fangton-Comedic-Vampire-ebook/dp/B01KNHICCC/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982774&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Straight+Outta+Fangton\" target=\"_blank\">Straight Outta Fangton</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Lucifers-Star-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01MDM9MCT/ref=mt_kindle?_encoding=UTF8&amp;me=&amp;qid=\" target=\"_blank\">Lucifer's Star</a>, </i>and the <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Rules-Supervillainy-Saga-Book-ebook/dp/B07MB89S33/\" target=\"_blank\">Supervillainy Saga</a>.</i><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":12002,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","user":"CTPhipps","date":". 04-20-2021, 02:55 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","name":"CTPhipps","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12002_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13933"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-04-20T11:49:22-07:00","id":1444882,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>BadFurryFanFic</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1443592-the-official-v5-vs-v20-thread?p=1444813#post1444813\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The Origin Awards win keeps getting brought up like it means something so its probably worth looking at the company V5 is keeping with its win:<br /> <br /> 2020- Teens in Space.....has anyone ever heard of this game?<br /> 2019- V5.<br /> 2018- Adventures in Middle Earth. 5e adaption of the The One Ring rpg. A solid book in my experience.<br /> 2017- No Thank You, Evil.....nope, never heard of this either.<br /> 2016- Star Wars: Force and Destiny. Solid performer from Fantasy Flight.<br /> 2015- D&amp;D 5th Ed- Pretty sure we all know this one.<br /> 2014- Numenera- seems to get mentioned fairly often as having good ideas but the execution is lacking. A mid-range performer.<br /> <br /> So thats 1 800lb gorilla, 2 solid games, 1 middling and 2 that are essentially unknowns........so Origin Awards can be given to pretty much anything and for a game to win it doesn't have to be either popular, particularly high quality or selling very well.<br /> <br /> So winning the award doesn't really tell us anything more than that some people on the jury ( 90% weighting) liked the game.</div> </div> </div> </div>Like winning the Oscars, it indicates at least professionals in the industry the actor or actress is awesome.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Author of <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Cthulhu-Armageddon-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01KUOM7SI/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982844&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Cthulhu+Armageddon\" target=\"_blank\">Cthulhu Armageddon</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Teenage-Weredeer-Bright-Falls-Mysteries-ebook/dp/B075TTN2FN/ref=sr_1_2?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982717&amp;sr=1-2&amp;keywords=Weredeer#customerReviews\" target=\"_blank\">I was a Teenage Weredeer</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Straight-Outta-Fangton-Comedic-Vampire-ebook/dp/B01KNHICCC/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982774&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Straight+Outta+Fangton\" target=\"_blank\">Straight Outta Fangton</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Lucifers-Star-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01MDM9MCT/ref=mt_kindle?_encoding=UTF8&amp;me=&amp;qid=\" target=\"_blank\">Lucifer's Star</a>, </i>and the <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Rules-Supervillainy-Saga-Book-ebook/dp/B07MB89S33/\" target=\"_blank\">Supervillainy Saga</a>.</i><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","name":"CTPhipps","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12002_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13933"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-04-20T12:17:32-07:00","id":1444894,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CTPhipps</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1443592-the-official-v5-vs-v20-thread?p=1444880#post1444880\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">As a note about what I like most about the V5 rules updates if anyone cares:<br /> <br /> <u>What I really like</u><br /> <br /> * The generation tied to what sort of blood you can drink.<br /> * Blood Potency tied to age.<br /> * Moving Humanity away from one single inflexible code of ethics to a more flexible series of personal convictions.<br /> * Thin Bloods having permanent Blush of Life.<br /> * Blush of Life just requiring one single rouse check versus a bunch of blood spent.<br /> * The changes to the Malkavian, Gangrel, and Ventrue weaknesses.<br /> * The updated Tzimisce rules.<br /> * Merging Serpentis, Vicisstitude, and Protean.<br /> * Combining the Abyss of Wraith and Lasombra.<br /> * Getting rid of Thaumaturgy Paths to be replaced with Rituals. Thaumathurgy Paths felt like they didn't want to make new Disciplines.<br /> * Loresheets allowing player characters to get much more hardcore into the Lore.<br /> * Being able to choose your own Generation as related to prey style and power level<br /> * Stains as a replacement for just automatic Humanity Loss.<br /> * Having a human ties or loved one to guard against Humanity loss. I had similar &amp;quot;True Love&amp;quot; rules that helped vampires guard against the Beast.<br /> * The revised rules so you can't blood bond someone without them knowing by spiking their drinks.<br /> * Ditto ghouldom.<br /> * The fact that Dominating mortals doesn't cost Blood and is automatic for the most part.<br /> * I like that Hunger never goes away unless you kill someone.<br /> * I like that Hunger is more erratic and unpredictable versus resource management.<br /> * Chronicle Tenet morality allows more flexibility whether you want to run a pacifist angst-ridden weepy game versus an action game with hundreds of bodies.<br /> <br /> <u>What I'm okay with</u><br /> <br /> * More flexibility about Nosferatu appearance is a good thing.<br /> * Loresheets as a means of tying Bloodlines to existing Clans indicates we may be getting a lot more variety on these without removing them from Clans entirely. After all, a lot of Bloodlines feel like they should be part of Clans but just &amp;quot;off center.&amp;quot;<br /> * Predator Types incentivize roleplaying out your feeding style.<br /> <br /> <u>What I don't like</u><br /> <br /> * I hate the Lasombra technology weakness.<br /> * I am not a big fan of giving vampires literal mental compulsions related to their Clan's stereotype.<br /> * The limit of 5 dots in Attributes and Disciplines is lore breaking and makes no goddamned sense.<br /> * The Amalgam purchase limitations are needlessly limiting and make no sense as well.<br /> * Healing ghouls should be allowed to be done by giving them blood.<br /> * Thin Bloods should be able to have at least one dot in Disciplines and not just as a Merit.<br /> * Thin Blooded Alchemy should not be their only thing.<br /> * I think Touchstones don't need to be linked with Convictions whatsoever.<br /> * I don't get the appeal of Resonances and think its a weird thing to introduce this late in the game.</div> </div> </div> </div>I agree with almost all of this assessment apart from the mergers between Protean &amp; Vicissitude and Obtenebration &amp; necromancy.<br /> <br /> Participants of the [V5] Lasombra thread delved into the Obten/Necro merger better that could already, but Vicissitude and Protean are just as different. <br /> <br /> Protean is a way of pulling the Beast to the surface and temporarily recreating apex predator features on the base human frame. Protean powers have to be activated and only last a set amount of time; if you &quot;pop claws&quot; for a scene eventually the claws have to retract and be &quot;popped&quot; again at a cost. <br /> <br /> Vicissitude is a means of re-writing the actual Pattern in flesh; if a limb is modified, the change is permanent even if the limb is removed and regrown. Only stronger magic can address the changes. <br /> <br /> Protean and Vicissitude have vastly different sources, themes, powers and ramifications.<br /> <br /> I do understand that they were simply trying to reduce \u201cDiscipline bloat,\u201d but I think they may have had other options. I think Necromancy and Vicissitude could have been folded better into Blood Sorcery, but then again, that was another area they were looking to curtail.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24351-garygeneric","name":"Garygeneric","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24351_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"108"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-04-20T12:22:15-07:00","id":1444896,"title":"","content":"Understandable.<br /> <br /> However, for me Protean is purely &quot;shapechanging&quot; and Vicissitude was overpowered. If I was in charge, I would have divided Vicissitude:<br /> <br /> 1. The shapechanging of YourselfTM would be Protean. You can morph your face into new visages and later your body. Frankly, Protean should have this power to begin with.<br /> <br /> 2. Then I would make the mad science experiment on OTHER Kindred a Blood Sorcery/Protean mix. Mind you, I would also homebrew so you could have that and other powers because I've mentioned I hate Amalgams taking away from your Discipline lists.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Author of <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Cthulhu-Armageddon-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01KUOM7SI/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982844&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Cthulhu+Armageddon\" target=\"_blank\">Cthulhu Armageddon</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Teenage-Weredeer-Bright-Falls-Mysteries-ebook/dp/B075TTN2FN/ref=sr_1_2?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982717&amp;sr=1-2&amp;keywords=Weredeer#customerReviews\" target=\"_blank\">I was a Teenage Weredeer</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Straight-Outta-Fangton-Comedic-Vampire-ebook/dp/B01KNHICCC/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982774&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Straight+Outta+Fangton\" target=\"_blank\">Straight Outta Fangton</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Lucifers-Star-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01MDM9MCT/ref=mt_kindle?_encoding=UTF8&amp;me=&amp;qid=\" target=\"_blank\">Lucifer's Star</a>, </i>and the <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Rules-Supervillainy-Saga-Book-ebook/dp/B07MB89S33/\" target=\"_blank\">Supervillainy Saga</a>.</i><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","name":"CTPhipps","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12002_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13933"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-04-20T12:50:37-07:00","id":1444901,"title":"","content":"I care &lt;3 <br /> <br /> <br /> I thought loresheets were very... some of them leaned far too much into the realm of fanservice. The execution (and often the writing) felt poor. The concept is... well, I'd rather have merits and flaws, and while I suppose it's nice to have related merits and flaws put together, it feels a bit too much to throw so much story information infront of new players that aren't familiar with the setting. Personally, I think you should actively avoid trying to inform your players of all the things they've missed out on, not only are their characters unlikely to know such things, but it just feels like you're creating first and second class players by presenting mechanical benefits for players comfortable enough with some old city books to say &quot;they know Tyler&quot;. <br /> <br /> Thaumaturgy having paths is something that makes more sense the more you read into it. Thaumaturgy isn't really distinct from hedgemagic and isn't part of the vampire condition. It's a discipline &quot;for humans&quot; (everyone), only as a vampire it works a little better because vitae is a much more convenient sacrifice than your health. Thaumaturgy is a product of the soul, and WoD runs with the idea that we all have amazing potential and can make miracles and shape reality as we please if we unlock that power (cue massive Tremere ego) Thus it makes sense that thaumaturgy has a myriad of powers because there's so many ways to shape reality, whilst vampire disciplines are rather limited because they're more... tied to your physical body/the beast. <br /> <br /> Literally everything about the way V5 does generation/Blood potency undermines the Jyhad. Why eat my way up when that's not a path to God or God-like status, but just a shortcut to more XP; you'll gain potency over time so you don't need to eat-up for it (and also Blood potency 5+ is really bad for you so you absolutely should not try to eat your way up because that'll increase the time you'll want to spend in torpor.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":7}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25794-mywifeisscary","name":"MyWifeIsScary","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25794_2.png","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3711"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-04-20T15:30:59-07:00","id":1444930,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CTPhipps</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1443592-the-official-v5-vs-v20-thread?p=1444880#post1444880\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">As a note about what I like most about the V5 rules updates if anyone cares:<br /> <br /> <u>What I really like</u><br /> * The generation tied to what sort of blood you can drink.<br /> * Blood Potency tied to age.</div> </div> </div> </div>And I dislike this because it really limits your options. If you're a 4th Gen you're always sucking on fellow vampires or murdering humans because you can't get full any other way. No options for a high humanity Methuselah who goes out of their way to stay connected with Humanity and thus needs only non-lethal amounts of human blood or can even drink from a bag or animals. Nope... ALL the Elders must be monsters with limited options while the young thinbloods get all the coolness.<br /> <br /> Seriously, its like V5 was written by 50 year olds trying to write what they THINK teens and twenty-somethings would find cool. Just another way V5 feels like the &quot;Dork Age&quot; (not a typo) of Comics.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> * Moving Humanity away from one single inflexible code of ethics to a more flexible series of personal convictions.<br /> * Stains as a replacement for just automatic Humanity Loss.<br /> * Chronicle Tenet morality allows more flexibility whether you want to run a pacifist angst-ridden weepy game versus an action game with hundreds of bodies. </div> </div> </div>See and I find the &quot;inflexibility&quot; of Humanity to be appealing as it gives reasons for those who really can't live up to concepts like &quot;Don't steal from people&quot; and &quot;Don't deliberately kill people&quot; to look at the Paths of Enlightenment.<br /> <br /> And what's so inflexible about &quot;Don't hurt other people and don't take/destroy other people's things?&quot; Those are pretty damned universal concepts in human society and the further down you go on Humanity the more universally bad the things are regarded as.<br /> <br /> Further, to actually risk losing that last dot of Humanity in V20 you basically have to start fucking people's dismembered corpses.<br /> <br /> V20 Humanity doesn't even remark on sexual ethics or &quot;must go to Church&quot; so you're free to hold whatever beliefs in those categories as fit your personal ethics without risking your Humanity.<br /> <br /> And that's what you seem to be missing about how Humanity works in older editions; first the loss is NEVER automatic. You get a Conscience check to see whether you lose the dot.<br /> <br /> Second, you only check if the sin is worse than your current humanity. If a professional thief can hold at Humanity 6 without ever needing to even make a roll for Humanity loss no matter how many people they rob or how many guards they knock unconscious in the process of doing so. Once a professional hitman reaches Humanity 2, he's unlikely to ever need to make another check for Humanity loss again unless he starts murdering people just for the funzies.<br /> <br /> By contrast, using the stain system, having someone you love shot in the head could turn you into a wight because there is no floor to Humanity loss in V5. Its not a scale of morality where your actions determine where you fall... its Morality Hit Points.<br /> <br /> So, I'd say the V20 Humanity system (and Paths of Enlightenment) are far more flexible in terms of morality and do a better job at keeping a PC from completely falling off the bottom of the scale than V5's Stains.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> * Having a human ties or loved one to guard against Humanity loss. I had similar &quot;True Love&quot; rules that helped vampires guard against the Beast. </div> </div> </div>And yet requiring these to be specific mortal humans vs. allowing people to define their own ties to Humanity is another example of V5's &quot;You WILL play the way we tell you to play&quot; that's frankly been a problem ever since Revised when the writers got ticked that people weren't playing the games the way they thought they should (imagine games of Mage devoted to wonder and exploring strange otherworlds... can't have that; turn up the GRIMDARK; kill all the archmages, destroy any way of reaching the spirit world, make magic harder, paradox nastier, and introduce a never existed before Armageddon event to ensure everyone is playing a hopeless street level game of wankery).<br /> <br /> One True Way-ist bullshit can die in a fire.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> * Blush of Life just requiring one single rouse check versus a bunch of blood spent. </div> </div> </div>And yet the more potency you have, the more that rouse check costs you. With a 50/50 shot at gaining a level of Hunger and only limited ways to remove it, it becomes much more costly.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> * Loresheets allowing player characters to get much more hardcore into the Lore. </div> </div> </div>&quot;You must be connected to this piece of other people's stories that have fuck all to do with the place and time your current game is set in order to gain X benefit. Never mind that your current campaign is set in Rome c. AD 300 so none of these people are even born yet.<br /> <br /> Nope... V20 Merits are 1500% better than Loresheets. Give us the mechanical widgets and let the players and GMs figure out what they mean to their present story. We've got the purple prose of the books and all sorts of Wikis if you actually care about Lore. <br /> <br /> Making me have to be a &quot;Childe of Hardestadt&quot; or something to get some extra resilience power is just lame design that, as I've pointed out before, presupposes that 99% of players and GMs give two wet farts about how cool the book authors think their snowflake GMPCs are.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> * Ditto ghouldom.<br /> * The fact that Dominating mortals doesn't cost Blood and is automatic for the most part. </div> </div> </div>Ghouls in V5 are lame and unplayable as PCs, in part because Dominate is basically automatic... so half their utility is gone and its again in service to the &quot;One True Way to Play VtM.&quot;<br /> <br /> Also, Dominate, at least ranks 1-5, never cost Blood to begin with in V20. So that part is a wash.<br /> <br /> I, for one, hate that mortals are basically fodder. It runs completely counter to the idea that they're supposed to be important enough to attach convictions to (except not so much... as the Touchstone system is creepy and manipulative without house-ruled interpretations of how its written).<br /> <br /> But then, I play games that are often bigger than just vampire on vampire politics again and again and where humans can actually fucking matter.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> * I like that Hunger never goes away unless you kill someone.<br /> * I like that Hunger is more erratic and unpredictable versus resource management. </div> </div> </div>And I say that only being able to satiate hunger with death has profound implications that make it a game I'm never interested in playing. You can drink a sip from a thousand mortals until you're bloated like a tick and still be hungry in V5, but suck the blood out of a single five-year old child and you're satiated.<br /> <br /> You're not a vampire... you don't drink blood. You drink MURDER, blood is just a stand-in for the real thing.<br /> <br /> And its another &quot;You must play Vampire the way we tell you it should be played&quot; vs. the previous editions where it was a toolbox and playing someone like Angel was just as possible as playing pre-ensouled Spike.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> * Predator Types incentivize roleplaying out your feeding style. </div> </div> </div>Except they're so poorly written as to be almost unusable as they don't just make it &quot;you do this way BETTER&quot; its &quot;you can't do it any other way.&quot;<br /> <br /> * * * *<br /> <br /> Basically, everything you like about V5 is why I strongly prefer V20 by a wide margin.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":8}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1328-chris24601","name":"Chris24601","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"520"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-04-20T15:35:40-07:00","id":1444932,"title":"","content":"<span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Frankly, </span><span style=\"color:#FF0000\"> a lot of those are flat out not true and verging on insulting of the gameline in the very specific way I requested this thread NOT to go.<br /> <br /> So I'll be clear.<br /> <br /> The moment anyone ever says, &quot;One True Way-ism&quot; again outside of the Golconda book, then this thread will be not only shut down but erased. The people involved will also be temporarily banned.<br /> <br /> If you can't be polite about the work of developers then this thread has no place on this forum and it was a bad idea to not ban this topic completely. This thread exists only at the idea that people can be respectful of other posters and the work of developers even if it's not to their taste.<br /> <br /> This is the only warning.</span>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Author of <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Cthulhu-Armageddon-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01KUOM7SI/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982844&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Cthulhu+Armageddon\" target=\"_blank\">Cthulhu Armageddon</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Teenage-Weredeer-Bright-Falls-Mysteries-ebook/dp/B075TTN2FN/ref=sr_1_2?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982717&amp;sr=1-2&amp;keywords=Weredeer#customerReviews\" target=\"_blank\">I was a Teenage Weredeer</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Straight-Outta-Fangton-Comedic-Vampire-ebook/dp/B01KNHICCC/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982774&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Straight+Outta+Fangton\" target=\"_blank\">Straight Outta Fangton</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Lucifers-Star-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01MDM9MCT/ref=mt_kindle?_encoding=UTF8&amp;me=&amp;qid=\" target=\"_blank\">Lucifer's Star</a>, </i>and the <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Rules-Supervillainy-Saga-Book-ebook/dp/B07MB89S33/\" target=\"_blank\">Supervillainy Saga</a>.</i><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":12002,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","user":"CTPhipps","date":". 04-20-2021, 06:41 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","name":"CTPhipps","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12002_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13933"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-04-20T16:26:16-07:00","id":1444952,"title":"","content":"Also losing one (or two) point of humanity was never the end of the world... until V5.<br /> <br /> I don't understand where this mentality comes from (one should never lose syndrome?). Sure a Humanity 8 vampire set himself to very high and difficult standard... as he should! Because playing high humanity vampire should never be easy... otherwise what's even the point of the ladder? What differentiate a more Humane vampire than a human from a serial killer? A righteous ideology? Please... I thought this wasn't a superhero katana kind of game.<br /> <br /> That does not mean however that a Humanity 8 vampire can not fail or that he always was a good person. He may even have been a rather bad person before reaching an epiphany. That was a cool aspect of Vampire. That cool and affable elder? Well he may have some skeleton in the closet and he may still become again THAT dude if push come to shove.<br /> <br /> I feel like that add another layer of morality to the setting. First things are not always black and white. Yes the beast will rouse should you commit a wrong act and that may (and should) spurs some drama but nothing is final as long as the pc doesn't completely or partially give up to the beast. Which gives us the second layer: acceptance.<br /> <br /> So yes Humanity was hard. Because damn right it should be! A player that can maintain a humane vampire for as long as a chronicle (or more) should and is entitiled to feel some sort of achievement for taking the high road with all its bumps. And no, he does not get a game over for losing once. Only a new bonus stage. Which may or may not lead him to defeat.<br /> <br /> So yes I very much prefer the way Humanity was handled before V5. First because regaining Humanity was both easier to lose and regain. Stains are worse in that they only delay the inevitable... unless the player purposefully choose the &quot;Tenets of what I wanted to do anyway&quot; In which case Humanity is made completely useless.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":24936,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24936-morbus","user":"Morbus","date":". 04-20-2021, 07:31 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":9}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24936-morbus","name":"Morbus","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"119"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-04-20T16:41:34-07:00","id":1444955,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MyWifeIsScary</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1443592-the-official-v5-vs-v20-thread?p=1444901#post1444901\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I care &lt;3<br /> <br /> <br /> I thought loresheets were very... some of them leaned far too much into the realm of fanservice. The execution (and often the writing) felt poor. The concept is... well, I'd rather have merits and flaws, and while I suppose it's nice to have related merits and flaws put together, it feels a bit too much to throw so much story information infront of new players that aren't familiar with the setting. Personally, I think you should actively avoid trying to inform your players of all the things they've missed out on, not only are their characters unlikely to know such things, but it just feels like you're creating first and second class players by presenting mechanical benefits for players comfortable enough with some old city books to say &quot;they know Tyler&quot;.<br /> <br /> Thaumaturgy having paths is something that makes more sense the more you read into it. Thaumaturgy isn't really distinct from hedgemagic and isn't part of the vampire condition. It's a discipline &quot;for humans&quot; (everyone), only as a vampire it works a little better because vitae is a much more convenient sacrifice than your health. Thaumaturgy is a product of the soul, and WoD runs with the idea that we all have amazing potential and can make miracles and shape reality as we please if we unlock that power (cue massive Tremere ego) Thus it makes sense that thaumaturgy has a myriad of powers because there's so many ways to shape reality, whilst vampire disciplines are rather limited because they're more... tied to your physical body/the beast.<br /> <br /> Literally everything about the way V5 does generation/Blood potency undermines the Jyhad. Why eat my way up when that's not a path to God or God-like status, but just a shortcut to more XP; you'll gain potency over time so you don't need to eat-up for it (and also Blood potency 5+ is really bad for you so you absolutely should not try to eat your way up because that'll increase the time you'll want to spend in torpor.</div> </div> </div> </div>1. My bias toward in-game lore is probably showing but I really appreciate Loresheets making a chance to intertwine your characters with the settings NPCs and major plot threads without being accused of being a Gary Stu. It also rewards players who do want to become involved with the lore and make their characters as part of the larger, richer tapestry of characters that is part of the setting. Mind you, I admit some of the rewards are crazy like being part of the new Council of Seven.<br /> <br /> 2. Part of the problem that presents is that Thaumaturgy/Blood Sorcery becomes an entirely different Discipline from the rest of them and encourages you to spend everything on Thaumaturgy paths versus your regular Disciplines. Making it just divided into rituals and the main campaign allows you to still develop powers but doesn't necessarily dominate your point spread. Mind you, I think it also underscores how stupid the Amalgam rules are right now. You can get all the Blood Sorcery rituals you want but not two 4th Dot Powers in Dominate.<br /> <br /> 3. Because you don't have 200 years to become Prince and be powerful. You need power NOW. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Author of <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Cthulhu-Armageddon-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01KUOM7SI/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982844&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Cthulhu+Armageddon\" target=\"_blank\">Cthulhu Armageddon</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Teenage-Weredeer-Bright-Falls-Mysteries-ebook/dp/B075TTN2FN/ref=sr_1_2?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982717&amp;sr=1-2&amp;keywords=Weredeer#customerReviews\" target=\"_blank\">I was a Teenage Weredeer</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Straight-Outta-Fangton-Comedic-Vampire-ebook/dp/B01KNHICCC/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982774&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Straight+Outta+Fangton\" target=\"_blank\">Straight Outta Fangton</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Lucifers-Star-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01MDM9MCT/ref=mt_kindle?_encoding=UTF8&amp;me=&amp;qid=\" target=\"_blank\">Lucifer's Star</a>, </i>and the <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Rules-Supervillainy-Saga-Book-ebook/dp/B07MB89S33/\" target=\"_blank\">Supervillainy Saga</a>.</i><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","name":"CTPhipps","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12002_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13933"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-04-21T00:09:15-07:00","id":1445002,"title":"","content":"1- Good you can admit that, but I think it's fair to say you have a minority opinion, again.<br /> <br /> 2-That's not a problem, that's a feature. The whole point of thaumaturgy was to be &quot;The Wizard&quot;. It was to go against your vampiric nature and instead focus on enlightenment and secrets. The fact that you, a thaumaturge has access to all maner of strange and wonderful power ,and that you insist this power is because you've got a big brain and you're from a big-brain school, is something that inspires jealousy and plotting; people will kill to get your secrets, and you either need to fortify or hide as a result. It's a game of Haves and Have-nots which, like anything, inspires conflict. Thaumaturgy in V5, being hardly distinguishable from any other discipline, doesn't have that push towards conflict. A five bloody powers and some rituals don't really justify the effort and drama to learn thaumaturgy nearly as well as the ability to fly, throw fireballs or change the weather at will.<br /> (also V20 did a lot to give you thaumaturgy possibilities without neccessarily having to be Tremere, Settite or AsSoc)<br /> <br /> 3- This really encourages princes to be nicer so that nobody feels pressured enough to scramble for power like that. Really softens the idea of the Jyhad. In V20, Being the only 7th gen in a city with multiple 8th gens, however, means there's never any time to relax.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":7}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25794-mywifeisscary","name":"MyWifeIsScary","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25794_2.png","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3711"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-04-21T00:10:52-07:00","id":1445004,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MyWifeIsScary</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1443592-the-official-v5-vs-v20-thread?p=1445002#post1445002\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">3- This really encourages princes to be nicer so that nobody feels pressured enough to scramble for power like that. Really softens the idea of the Jyhad. In V20, Being the only 7th gen in a city with multiple 8th gens, however, means there's never any time to relax.</div> </div> </div> </div>Eh, if you're nice then you're perceived as weak. One of the lore bits that I actually liked-liked was the Prince of Berlin descalating the violence with the Anarchs and leaving them alone.<br /> <br /> So the Camarilla replaces him with someone to crack the whip and the city falls.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Author of <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Cthulhu-Armageddon-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01KUOM7SI/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982844&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Cthulhu+Armageddon\" target=\"_blank\">Cthulhu Armageddon</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Teenage-Weredeer-Bright-Falls-Mysteries-ebook/dp/B075TTN2FN/ref=sr_1_2?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982717&amp;sr=1-2&amp;keywords=Weredeer#customerReviews\" target=\"_blank\">I was a Teenage Weredeer</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Straight-Outta-Fangton-Comedic-Vampire-ebook/dp/B01KNHICCC/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982774&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Straight+Outta+Fangton\" target=\"_blank\">Straight Outta Fangton</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Lucifers-Star-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01MDM9MCT/ref=mt_kindle?_encoding=UTF8&amp;me=&amp;qid=\" target=\"_blank\">Lucifer's Star</a>, </i>and the <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Rules-Supervillainy-Saga-Book-ebook/dp/B07MB89S33/\" target=\"_blank\">Supervillainy Saga</a>.</i><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","name":"CTPhipps","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12002_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13933"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-04-21T00:23:28-07:00","id":1445007,"title":"","content":"So there's a popular misconception that &quot;Alphas&quot; in nature are the biggest, strongest, meanest wolf/ape. But in reality, the chimp who gets the top spot is more often the most charming, generous, charismatic guy who rewards his followers well. Kings used to hunt with their nobles as a way of becoming BFF with everyone.... there's nothing wrong with a &quot;nice&quot; prince (especially since he's often a puppet, but not exclusively because he's a puppet. If you're really powerful, you can certainly afford to be nice.)<br /> <br /> The Threat of being a desirable diablerie target is the reason why princes want to keep distances. Actually, In V5, it's better to diablerize people of higher gen because you're more likely to get more XP than lose excess humanity.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":8}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25794-mywifeisscary","name":"MyWifeIsScary","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25794_2.png","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3711"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-04-21T00:28:26-07:00","id":1445008,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MyWifeIsScary</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1443592-the-official-v5-vs-v20-thread?p=1445007#post1445007\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">So there's a popular misconception that &quot;Alphas&quot; in nature are the biggest, strongest, meanest wolf/ape. But in reality, the chimp who gets the top spot is more often the most charming, generous, charismatic guy who rewards his followers well. Kings used to hunt with their nobles as a way of becoming BFF with everyone.... there's nothing wrong with a &quot;nice&quot; prince (especially since he's often a puppet, but not exclusively because he's a puppet. If you're really powerful, you can certainly afford to be nice.)<br /> <br /> The Threat of being a desirable diablerie target is the reason why princes want to keep distances. Actually, In V5, it's better to diablerize people of higher gen because you're more likely to get more XP than lose excess humanity.</div> </div> </div> </div>Yep and that is why the tyranny of Princes fails.<br /> <br /> They will not be able to do the things that work best for everyone because the Camarilla not built on game theory and mutual advancement. It is built around the oppression of the young and violence as the only method of achieving victory. If you need a biological reason for it other the fact that historically tyrantsl, cults of personality, and corruption ruins governments that &quot;should&quot; be smarter then I suppose we can blame the Beast. Vampires are innately drawn to violence and domination. The Beast will always ruin what is good and sensible in exchange for what is violent as well as self-serving.<br /> <br /> Mind you, this isn't a natural phenomenon either. In the 1st Edition of V:TM it was also made clear that the better natures of Princes are suppressed by their masters. Even if Lodin wants to be a good ruler, he doesn't have that option because Lodin is going to be a slave of Helena and her desire will be to stir shit up whether because of boredom or a simple desire to regularly thin the herd of lesser vampires.<br /> <br /> The Antediluvians as well are purely evil monsters and they, too, are always playing other vampires against one another.<br /> <br /> Ah, what a glorious time to be dead,<br /> <br /> Unlife is always interesting!","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Author of <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Cthulhu-Armageddon-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01KUOM7SI/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982844&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Cthulhu+Armageddon\" target=\"_blank\">Cthulhu Armageddon</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Teenage-Weredeer-Bright-Falls-Mysteries-ebook/dp/B075TTN2FN/ref=sr_1_2?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982717&amp;sr=1-2&amp;keywords=Weredeer#customerReviews\" target=\"_blank\">I was a Teenage Weredeer</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Straight-Outta-Fangton-Comedic-Vampire-ebook/dp/B01KNHICCC/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982774&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Straight+Outta+Fangton\" target=\"_blank\">Straight Outta Fangton</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Lucifers-Star-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01MDM9MCT/ref=mt_kindle?_encoding=UTF8&amp;me=&amp;qid=\" target=\"_blank\">Lucifer's Star</a>, </i>and the <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Rules-Supervillainy-Saga-Book-ebook/dp/B07MB89S33/\" target=\"_blank\">Supervillainy Saga</a>.</i><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":12002,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","user":"CTPhipps","date":". 04-21-2021, 03:32 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","name":"CTPhipps","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12002_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13933"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-04-21T00:53:37-07:00","id":1445011,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CTPhipps</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1443592-the-official-v5-vs-v20-thread?p=1444932#post1444932\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">I'll fucking kill ya all</span></div> </div> </div> </div>While it might be an exaggeration to ascribe everything to malicious and intentional -shallNotBeNamed- , I do think V5 does a significant job in lowering the scope of genres available, and emphasizing some aspects of the game at the expense of others;<br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#252C2F\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:13px\">The moves towards simplified, cinematic combat also remove the more simulationist possibilities that could've been undertaken in v20 <br /> <br /> losing control all the time eliminates the possibility of playing a cool vampire, at least in my view. Clan compulsions... I wanna be in control, and the idea that I can do absolutely nothing to mitigate the prospect of losing control (other than murder people before I want to do something) is problematic both on a personal level and on the level that it effects the setting and actions of everyone involved. (There's also a degree of agentic shift here; If the Beast fucks shit up, and I can't do anything reasonable to control the Beast, then I'm not responsible; my loss of control is what bothers me, not that the Beast used my body and killed a baby or whatever. End of discussion.) </span></span></span><br /> <br /> I don't feel &quot;political horror&quot; works so well in a setting where the Vampires are so deep in &quot;personal horror&quot; that they struggle to feed each night and don't have the time to fuck up the planet or arange schemes that can't be destroyed by their own Beast rebelling against them or their touchstones going out of whack. Political horror also doesn't work so well when the gap between prince and hunter has been shrunk to an extent that the coterie can wipe the city through teamwork and a semi-good plan and we don't have to overmuch worry about the possibility that one old sixth gen can wipe the party before they can even make a proper move. <i>Also I can't dominate the president into executing order 66 because dominate doesn't work the way it used to</i>. <br /> <br /> Gaining power (influence resources, domain, retainers etc) is hampered by my own inability, while gaining personal power (disciplines) is a dead-end where once it could be a goal in of itself. <span style=\"color:#252C2F\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:13px\">I can't be a wizard anymore/wizards have had their powers reduced and their beliefs largely invalidated. </span></span></span><br /> <br /> The Sabbat, and their themes, literally left the game. <br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":8}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25794-mywifeisscary","name":"MyWifeIsScary","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25794_2.png","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3711"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-04-21T02:31:35-07:00","id":1445016,"title":"","content":"I also recall V5 openly says something like &quot; If you consider yourself alt-right go home and rethink your life, this game is not for you&quot;<br /> <br /> I would probably be considered &quot;left&quot; enough to be put on a list, but you simply can't have the kind of attitude to write something like that in something that's A: A commercial product that you hope will be successful and B: a satirical work of literature that you hope will bring people around to your point of view. That &quot;my way or the highway&quot; attitude is really significant enough that it's effects are felt on the rest of the work. Even if you don't mean to hurt &quot;political horror&quot; with &quot;personal horror&quot; the fact that you've taken such a strong stance with who can't play your game makes it feel like it's not such a stretch that you're taking a strong stance there too. Hell, the reduction of strong hierarchies and power disparities (IE Generation isn't that desirable and humans are a credible threat), which are important aspects of fascism, kinda gives rise to the idea that the previously exaggerated gaps in power have been reduced in order to make sure that such hierarchies aren't legitimized and everyone feels equal so that the game doesn't support fascist ideas (which is, to me at least, obviously counterproductive since those hierarchies were exaggerated for the purpose of satirical ridicule, but it's not unknown for supposedly liberal narratives to backfire and become counterproductive, like how the &quot;strong women&quot; in recent Star-Wars movies have been an object of some scorn. If someone's game enough to write &quot;fascists stop reading&quot; on a product you can expect little good)<br /> <br /> In short, if you're dictating who is allowed to play it's not much of a stretch to believe you're also going to dictate how they should play. I'm not saying they are engaging in a 1TW approach, just that it's understandable that some people have suspicions.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":25794,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25794-mywifeisscary","user":"MyWifeIsScary","date":". 04-21-2021, 05:34 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":6}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25794-mywifeisscary","name":"MyWifeIsScary","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25794_2.png","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3711"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-04-21T03:01:13-07:00","id":1445018,"title":"","content":"That's in there because of the clusterfuck of PR disasters nWW made before Paradox pulled the plug on them. It's really no deeper than that.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-04-21T04:48:29-07:00","id":1445020,"title":"","content":"Yeah, that was kind of necessary in light of the fallout over what happened with that.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/741-anubisxy","name":"AnubisXy","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar741_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5693"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-04-21T09:38:47-07:00","id":1445061,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MyWifeIsScary</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1443592-the-official-v5-vs-v20-thread?p=1445016#post1445016\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I also recall V5 openly says something like &quot; If you consider yourself alt-right go home and rethink your life, this game is not for you&quot;</div> </div> </div> </div><span style=\"color:#FF0000\"><b>For the sake of clarification, Jason Carl telling white supremacists to fuck off is considered both reasonable and humane.<br /> <br /> Also, that he wasn't misusing the term but in the same sense as the Dead Kennedy's.</b></span><br /> <br /> <div class=\"videocontainer with-aspect-ratio videocontainer-horizontal\" style=\"aspect-ratio: 16/9;\"> <a class=\"video-frame\" href=\"https://youtu.be/iyc62g7YQM0\" data-code=\"iyc62g7YQM0\" data-provider=\"youtube_share\" data-height=\"0\" data-width=\"0\" itemprop=\"video\"> <div class=\"videothumbnail\" style=\"\"> <img src=\"https://img.youtube.com/vi/iyc62g7YQM0/maxresdefault.jpg\" alt=\"\" /> <div class=\"videothumbnailoverlay\"></div> </div> </a> </div><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#FF0000\"><b>But I promise not to kill everyone, My Wife is Scary. Probably.</b></span>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Author of <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Cthulhu-Armageddon-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01KUOM7SI/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982844&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Cthulhu+Armageddon\" target=\"_blank\">Cthulhu Armageddon</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Teenage-Weredeer-Bright-Falls-Mysteries-ebook/dp/B075TTN2FN/ref=sr_1_2?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982717&amp;sr=1-2&amp;keywords=Weredeer#customerReviews\" target=\"_blank\">I was a Teenage Weredeer</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Straight-Outta-Fangton-Comedic-Vampire-ebook/dp/B01KNHICCC/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982774&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Straight+Outta+Fangton\" target=\"_blank\">Straight Outta Fangton</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Lucifers-Star-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01MDM9MCT/ref=mt_kindle?_encoding=UTF8&amp;me=&amp;qid=\" target=\"_blank\">Lucifer's Star</a>, </i>and the <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Rules-Supervillainy-Saga-Book-ebook/dp/B07MB89S33/\" target=\"_blank\">Supervillainy Saga</a>.</i><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":12002,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","user":"CTPhipps","date":". 04-21-2021, 12:42 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","name":"CTPhipps","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12002_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13933"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-04-21T09:45:59-07:00","id":1445064,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Heavy Arms</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1443592-the-official-v5-vs-v20-thread?p=1445018#post1445018\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">That's in there because of the clusterfuck of PR disasters nWW made before Paradox pulled the plug on them. It's really no deeper than that.</div> </div> </div> </div><div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>AnubisXy</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1443592-the-official-v5-vs-v20-thread?p=1445020#post1445020\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Yeah, that was kind of necessary in light of the fallout over what happened with that.</div> </div> </div> </div>The sad fact is that White Wolf and the World of Darkness have actually had to deal with white supremacist appropriatioin several times in the past. One of the most famous incidents being the Sword of Heimdall one in Werewolf: The Apocalypse. Ethan Skemp, way back when, basically said that they had a white supremacy problem among Werewolf: The Apocalypse &quot;fans&quot; with it being appropriated by them and people showing up at LARPs or games claiming to be just playing in character while embracing the (meant to be villains) Swords of Heimdall. This is notably why the Werewolf camp was exterminated to the last Garou in Werewolf Revised.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Author of <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Cthulhu-Armageddon-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01KUOM7SI/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982844&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Cthulhu+Armageddon\" target=\"_blank\">Cthulhu Armageddon</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Teenage-Weredeer-Bright-Falls-Mysteries-ebook/dp/B075TTN2FN/ref=sr_1_2?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982717&amp;sr=1-2&amp;keywords=Weredeer#customerReviews\" target=\"_blank\">I was a Teenage Weredeer</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Straight-Outta-Fangton-Comedic-Vampire-ebook/dp/B01KNHICCC/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982774&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Straight+Outta+Fangton\" target=\"_blank\">Straight Outta Fangton</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Lucifers-Star-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01MDM9MCT/ref=mt_kindle?_encoding=UTF8&amp;me=&amp;qid=\" target=\"_blank\">Lucifer's Star</a>, </i>and the <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Rules-Supervillainy-Saga-Book-ebook/dp/B07MB89S33/\" target=\"_blank\">Supervillainy Saga</a>.</i><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":12002,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","user":"CTPhipps","date":". 04-21-2021, 12:48 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","name":"CTPhipps","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12002_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13933"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-04-21T09:48:02-07:00","id":1445066,"title":"","content":"Agreed both reasonable and humane but mostly grandstanding. Once you release a product into the wild you cant control who will purchase it or how they will chose to interpret the text.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>The Hecata are a sect not a clan.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24211-frontline989","name":"Frontline989","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24211_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"152"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-04-21T09:56:29-07:00","id":1445067,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Frontline989</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1443592-the-official-v5-vs-v20-thread?p=1445066#post1445066\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Agreed both reasonable and humane but mostly grandstanding. Once you release a product into the wild you cant control who will purchase it or how they will chose to interpret the text.</div> </div> </div> </div>True, but the news cycle has a tendency to get ahead of itself so that it is important to be extremely clear--especially in a game that is meant to be politically charged. I appreciate White Wolf didn't decide to lie like Ubisoft (which had much darker issues going on) and say, &quot;our games aren't political&quot; while using the Tom Clancy logo and militant terrorist religious cults as the basis fo its games. White Wolf embracing its original punk progressive ethos (at least in terms of anti-racism and anti-homophobia) is both a valid artistic choice as well as just good business sense.<br /> <br /> Sadly, V5's early troubles prove there is such a thing as bad publicity and I do think Jason's statement, whether you take it as grandstanding or sincere articulation of belief like me, at least made an impression.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Author of <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Cthulhu-Armageddon-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01KUOM7SI/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982844&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Cthulhu+Armageddon\" target=\"_blank\">Cthulhu Armageddon</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Teenage-Weredeer-Bright-Falls-Mysteries-ebook/dp/B075TTN2FN/ref=sr_1_2?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982717&amp;sr=1-2&amp;keywords=Weredeer#customerReviews\" target=\"_blank\">I was a Teenage Weredeer</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Straight-Outta-Fangton-Comedic-Vampire-ebook/dp/B01KNHICCC/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982774&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Straight+Outta+Fangton\" target=\"_blank\">Straight Outta Fangton</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Lucifers-Star-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01MDM9MCT/ref=mt_kindle?_encoding=UTF8&amp;me=&amp;qid=\" target=\"_blank\">Lucifer's Star</a>, </i>and the <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Rules-Supervillainy-Saga-Book-ebook/dp/B07MB89S33/\" target=\"_blank\">Supervillainy Saga</a>.</i><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","name":"CTPhipps","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12002_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13933"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-04-21T10:27:38-07:00","id":1445070,"title":"","content":"&quot;There's no such thing as bad publicity,&quot; is both questionable as a concept, and only really works on a corporate scale well above were most RPGs live. Bad publicity is bad because it has a cost. The bigger you are, the easier it is to absorb that cost and spin things to your benefit in the long run (ex: New Coke). Smaller companies frequently do not have that ability, let alone individuals.<br /> <br /> As for Jason Carl's comment, it is both possible to feel it was sincere for him personally, but find it to be grandstanding by the company as they trot out someone that honestly feels strongly about it without necessarily demonstrating any corporate culture changes that would keep the same situation from happening again.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-04-21T10:35:09-07:00","id":1445073,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MyWifeIsScary</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1443592-the-official-v5-vs-v20-thread?p=1445011#post1445011\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">While it might be an exaggeration to ascribe everything to malicious and intentional -shallNotBeNamed- , I do think V5 does a significant job in lowering the scope of genres available, and emphasizing some aspects of the game at the expense of others; <span style=\"color:#252C2F\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:13px\">The moves towards simplified, cinematic combat also remove the more simulationist possibilities that could've been undertaken in v20</span></span></span></div> </div> </div> </div><span style=\"color:#252C2F\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:13px\">Honestly, I think the biggest benefit of V5 is the fact that it dramatically broadens the scope of underutilized genres in the vampire game. Not only is combat and mechanics more simplified but it really does give a lot of incentive for doing street level gaming that didn't exist there before. I used to be very hostile to MAGE REVISED due to the extensiveness of use that I made of the Umbra in my games, almost to the point of being Nobilis, but when I actually tried out a street mage game, it proved to be incredibly fun.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> losing control all the time eliminates the possibility of playing a cool vampire, at least in my view. Clan compulsions... I wanna be in control, and the idea that I can do absolutely nothing to mitigate the prospect of losing control (other than murder people before I want to do something) is problematic both on a personal level and on the level that it effects the setting and actions of<br /> everyone involved. </div> </div> </div>Honestly, I think perception is the cause of the problem here because if you play the rules as is, the V20 vampires are the ones that should be frenzying all the time. I believe that a lot of Storytellers got out of the habit of calling for frenzy checks when in danger, when angry, when there was any fire larger than a cigarette, when injured, or the scent of blood nearby. The rules make it very clear that this is meant to be an extremely common thing. I note that I actually think that the ability to manage the Beast goes up with the fact that the mind is &quot;quieted&quot; when you kill someone in the game. Plus, Compulsions mean that you are LESS likely to go on a killing spree but just have your behavior altered.<br /> <br /> But there are ample ways of managing the Beast in-game, not the least bit keeping that Hunger at 1 and only having to deal with the threat if confronted with great provocation. Let's not pretend that V20's rules don't make it clear that if you spend that last Blood Point, you won't carve up your own coterie and the nearest baby. When you don't, that was because the ST made a decision to not do so because it wouldn't be fun. V5 has solidified that lessened tendency to go on a murder spree into the rules.<br /> <br /> Even the Bestial Failures have been designed to move AWAY from random murder.<br /> <br /> RANDOM COMPULSIONS<br /> <br /> 1-3: Hunger<br /> 4-5: Dominance<br /> 6-7: Harm<br /> 8-9: Paranoia<br /> 0: Clan Compulsion*<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> (There's also a degree of agentic shift here; If the Beast fucks shit up, and I can't do anything reasonable to control the Beast, then I'm not responsible; my loss of control is what bothers me, not that the Beast used my body and killed a baby or whatever. End of discussion.) </div> </div> </div></span></span></span><br /> <br /> I don't think that in the entirety of the genre of vampires has ever made this an attitude of a protagonist. Vampires may be cursed in the literal sense with an uncontrollable lust for blood but when they do something horrible under duress they still carry that traumatizing memory. I once got a 1-star review by a poor woman who was HORRIFIED that there was a scene in my STRAIGHT OUTTA FANGTON book where the protagonist was locked up in a basement with a little girl to be starved until he fed on her.<br /> <br /> I'm like, &quot;Yes, it's meant to be horrifying.&quot;<br /> <br /> It obviously traumatized the protagonist despite having no control.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> I don't feel &quot;political horror&quot; works so well in a setting where the Vampires are so deep in &quot;personal horror&quot; that they struggle to feed each night and don't have the time to fuck up the planet or arange schemes that can't be destroyed by their own Beast rebelling against them or their touchstones going out of whack. Political horror also doesn't work so well when the gap between prince and hunter has been shrunk to an extent that the coterie can wipe the city through teamwork and a semi-good plan and we don't have to overmuch worry about the possibility that one old sixth gen can wipe the party before they can even make a proper move. <i>Also I can't dominate the president into executing order 66 because dominate doesn't work the way it used to</i>. </div> </div> </div>Totally disagree.<br /> <br /> Political horror is something that I think has been modified primarily for this game based around the decades of lessons of LARP and material. The loss of Elders and focus on jockeying for power has taken front stage so we do have people like Kevin Jackson actually able to move into the big seat. However, it's because the power vacuum that currently exists low-wise is open to them. It's not like there's more frenzy opportunities than Elysium than there were before either and when you frenzy, you might NOT rip out the throat of Annabelle as you would before but instead just be a real asshole.<br /> <br /> I'm not entirely down with that but let's not pretend the Compulsion system doesn't downgrade the dangers of frenzy.<br /> <br /> As for Princes and Hunters, unless you use the overpowered &quot;Wake with Mornings' Freshness, virtually any vampire caught with hunters in the daytime will be only able to flee. Its why minions exist.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Gaining power (influence resources, domain, retainers etc) is hampered by my own inability, while gaining personal power (disciplines) is a dead-end where once it could be a goal in of itself. <span style=\"color:#252C2F\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:13px\">I can't be a wizard anymore/wizards have had their powers reduced and their beliefs largely invalidated. </span></span></span> </div> </div> </div>Frankly, I feel like Rituals as a replacement for Paths make vampires stronger not weaker.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> The Sabbat, and their themes, literally left the game. </div> </div> </div>Yes, their absence was a mistake and I'm glad they're finally &quot;coming back.&quot;","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Author of <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Cthulhu-Armageddon-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01KUOM7SI/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982844&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Cthulhu+Armageddon\" target=\"_blank\">Cthulhu Armageddon</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Teenage-Weredeer-Bright-Falls-Mysteries-ebook/dp/B075TTN2FN/ref=sr_1_2?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982717&amp;sr=1-2&amp;keywords=Weredeer#customerReviews\" target=\"_blank\">I was a Teenage Weredeer</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Straight-Outta-Fangton-Comedic-Vampire-ebook/dp/B01KNHICCC/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982774&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Straight+Outta+Fangton\" target=\"_blank\">Straight Outta Fangton</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Lucifers-Star-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01MDM9MCT/ref=mt_kindle?_encoding=UTF8&amp;me=&amp;qid=\" target=\"_blank\">Lucifer's Star</a>, </i>and the <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Rules-Supervillainy-Saga-Book-ebook/dp/B07MB89S33/\" target=\"_blank\">Supervillainy Saga</a>.</i><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","name":"CTPhipps","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12002_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13933"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-04-21T10:47:49-07:00","id":1445076,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MyWifeIsScary</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1443592-the-official-v5-vs-v20-thread?p=1445016#post1445016\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I also recall V5 openly says something like &quot; If you consider yourself alt-right go home and rethink your life, this game is not for you&quot;<br /> <br /> I would probably be considered &quot;left&quot; enough to be put on a list, but you simply can't have the kind of attitude to write something like that in something that's A: A commercial product that you hope will be successful and B: a satirical work of literature that you hope will bring people around to your point of view. That &quot;my way or the highway&quot; attitude is really significant enough that it's effects are felt on the rest of the work. Even if you don't mean to hurt &quot;political horror&quot; with &quot;personal horror&quot; the fact that you've taken such a strong stance with who can't play your game makes it feel like it's not such a stretch that you're taking a strong stance there too. Hell, the reduction of strong hierarchies and power disparities (IE Generation isn't that desirable and humans are a credible threat), which are important aspects of fascism, kinda gives rise to the idea that the previously exaggerated gaps in power have been reduced in order to make sure that such hierarchies aren't legitimized and everyone feels equal so that the game doesn't support fascist ideas (which is, to me at least, obviously counterproductive since those hierarchies were exaggerated for the purpose of satirical ridicule, but it's not unknown for supposedly liberal narratives to backfire and become counterproductive, like how the &quot;strong women&quot; in recent Star-Wars movies have been an object of some scorn. If someone's game enough to write &quot;fascists stop reading&quot; on a product you can expect little good)<br /> <br /> In short, if you're dictating who is allowed to play it's not much of a stretch to believe you're also going to dictate how they should play. I'm not saying they are engaging in a 1TW approach, just that it's understandable that some people have suspicions.</div> </div> </div> </div>Yes, that certainly made what could be called a &quot;bad first impression&quot; on me. It seemed counter to the idea of mature games for mature players or the idea that real world issues could be addressed with WoD games. <br /> <br /> Of course, looking back, WW had all kinds of crazy politically charged and biased stuff in their games through the decades. I think when I was younger it didn't phase me quite as much as it would (and does) now.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1129-sergeant-brother","name":"Sergeant Brother","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1129_3.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1620"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-04-21T12:08:36-07:00","id":1445089,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Frontline989</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1443592-the-official-v5-vs-v20-thread?p=1445066#post1445066\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Agreed both reasonable and humane but mostly grandstanding. Once you release a product into the wild you cant control who will purchase it or how they will chose to interpret the text.</div> </div> </div> </div>Very much this. The average dude or dudette (and me) isn't going to know the intricate rational and history behind telling a portion of the fanbase to fuck off, we just see the authors telling that portion to fuck off. While that might be gratifying for some, it's no solution. <br /> Crazed alt-right types aren't going to get any better by further marginalizing them, by excluding them from normalcy and letting them fester and radicalize in the echo chambers that accept them. It might be too painful for larp, but you've got plenty of oppertunity to show them the error of their ways in tabletop ; sympathetic minorities, Charismatic, Successful and powerful minority vampires; elders using the player's beliefs to exploit them for chumps before casting them off like a used condom, fellow white supremicist characters being exploitable losers, Surprise 'he was jewish all along' when they get close to someone...","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25794-mywifeisscary","name":"MyWifeIsScary","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25794_2.png","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3711"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-04-21T12:17:29-07:00","id":1445093,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MyWifeIsScary</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1443592-the-official-v5-vs-v20-thread?p=1445089#post1445089\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Very much this. The average dude or dudette (and me) isn't going to know the intricate rational and history behind telling a portion of the fanbase to fuck off, we just see the authors telling that portion to fuck off. While that might be gratifying for some, it's no solution.</div> </div> </div> </div>I dunno, I feel like telling Nazis to fuck off is something that is very hard to criticize.<br /> <br /> It's like the Neo-Nazi fans of Star Wars.<br /> <br /> &quot;Dude, read the room.&quot;<br /> <br /> Part of the issue is the fact that Neo-Nazi World of Darkness fans aren't a weird hypothetical to me. They actually exist in my area and I don't mean this as a kind of, &quot;You are using that as an insult.&quot; I mean the guys with swastika tattoos, Neo Confederate paraphernalia, and openly talking about their fear of white genocide as well as disgust for LGBT people.<br /> <br /> Kicking them out of the Huntington, WV LARP community was a thing.<br /> <br /> In some parts of the country, these guys are openly active. Look at what they FINALLY did in the Kentucky State Fair two years ago: <a href=\"https://www.courier-journal.com/story/news/2018/11/15/sales-nazi-and-kkk-items-banned-kentucky-expo-center/2003010002/\" target=\"_blank\">https://www.courier-journal.com/stor...er/2003010002/</a>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Author of <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Cthulhu-Armageddon-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01KUOM7SI/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982844&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Cthulhu+Armageddon\" target=\"_blank\">Cthulhu Armageddon</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Teenage-Weredeer-Bright-Falls-Mysteries-ebook/dp/B075TTN2FN/ref=sr_1_2?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982717&amp;sr=1-2&amp;keywords=Weredeer#customerReviews\" target=\"_blank\">I was a Teenage Weredeer</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Straight-Outta-Fangton-Comedic-Vampire-ebook/dp/B01KNHICCC/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982774&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Straight+Outta+Fangton\" target=\"_blank\">Straight Outta Fangton</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Lucifers-Star-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01MDM9MCT/ref=mt_kindle?_encoding=UTF8&amp;me=&amp;qid=\" target=\"_blank\">Lucifer's Star</a>, </i>and the <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Rules-Supervillainy-Saga-Book-ebook/dp/B07MB89S33/\" target=\"_blank\">Supervillainy Saga</a>.</i><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":12002,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","user":"CTPhipps","date":". 04-21-2021, 03:44 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","name":"CTPhipps","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12002_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13933"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-04-21T12:19:39-07:00","id":1445094,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CTPhipps</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1443592-the-official-v5-vs-v20-thread?p=1445073#post1445073\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Honestly, I think the biggest benefit of V5 is the fact that it dramatically broadens the scope of underutilized genres in the vampire game.</div> </div> </div> </div>I really don't see how it practically accomplishes this. For example, all the negative talk about &quot;superheores with fangs,&quot; is just taking mechanics to a specific genre extreme, while those same mechanics also V20 functional for a number of other things. The more detailed V20 combat mechanics help street level games where vampires are looking for every edge to survive, so even the minor bonus of wearing low rated hidden armor is worth pursuing. Meanwhile V5 makes armor completely worthless to vampires, to the point where a vampire wearing bright yellow spandex has a combat edge over one wearing heavy riot gear. Simple isn't always better when trying to enable multiple genre playstyles.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Honestly, I think perception is the cause of the problem here because if you play the rules as is, the V20 vampires are the ones that should be frenzying all the time. I believe that a lot of Storytellers got out of the habit of calling for frenzy checks when in danger, when angry, when there was any fire larger than a cigarette, when injured, or the scent of blood nearby. The rules make it very clear that this is meant to be an extremely common thing. </div> </div> </div>I have no idea where you're getting this from. V20 still has automatic success rules, which STs are more than free to apply to Frenzy/Rotschreck checks. So cutting out the low level triggers when it isn't a dramatically appropriate scene is 100% how the rules are written.<br /> <br /> V20 is very clear that vampires <b>feel</b> these urges commonly, but the vast majority of the time they easily keep the Beast in check. For example, hunger checks only set in if your character has too little vitae in their system at all. It doesn't mean the sight or smell of blood doesn't rouse the Beast to feed, it just means that unless your low, and have relatively low Self-Control by PC standards, vampires can control themselves without even needing to roll.<br /> <br /> To cite, V20 page 299:<br /> <br /> &quot;Relatively innocuous stimuli, or stimuli directly under the character\u2019s control, are unlikely to induce R\u00f6tschreck. For example, a character who sees a lit cigarette in a nightclub, or a screened-in fireplace in an ally\u2019s home, might grow uneasy, but is unlikely to succumb to the Red Fear. If that same cigarette is pointed threateningly at the vampire, though, or the fireplace suddenly flares up\u2026&quot;<br /> <br /> Vampires, in V20 rules, do not flip out over things just because they're there. It's established that a certain level of narrative escalation be present.<br /> <br /> I note that I actually think that the ability to manage the Beast goes up with the fact that the mind is &quot;quieted&quot; when you kill someone in the game. Plus, Compulsions mean that you are LESS likely to go on a killing spree but just have your behavior altered.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Let's not pretend that V20's rules don't make it clear that if you spend that last Blood Point, you won't carve up your own coterie and the nearest baby. When you don't, that was because the ST made a decision to not do so because it wouldn't be fun. V5 has solidified that lessened tendency to go on a murder spree into the rules. </div> </div> </div>Um, you seem to be skipping that V5 still has Frenzy rules in it on top of Compulsions, with pretty much the same provocations as V20 as (if adjusted for things like blood points vs. Hungry levels). Compulsions from Bestial Failures might not have a high risk of random murder, but they have a risk of that which adds to the risk of flipping out via Frenzy. That doesn't really paint a picture of more &quot;calm&quot; vampires. A Hunger 5 V5 vampire is extremely at risk of murdering people for blood, and isn't likely to care who.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":9}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-04-21T12:32:50-07:00","id":1445099,"title":"","content":"Important note:<br /> <br /> Alt-righters, Neo-Nazis, and so on, espouse a philosophy that explicitly calls for my whole family to be murdered. It's not on a RPG to fix that. A RPG company doesn't have the resources to both ensure me that they aren't making such ideologies welcome in their fans, and do outreach to the individuals that hold those views to make the spaces needed for them to feel comfortable and create room for reevaluation.<br /> <br /> And if anyone is serious about these things:<br /> <br /> 1) The best way to help people is to pull them away before they go down that rabbit hole.<br /> <br /> 2) Helping people abandon bigoted world views is a form of psychological therapy. We as individuals might be presented with difficult chances to catalyze a desire in someone to change, but guiding that change is the realm of experts, not a gaming circle.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":9}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-04-21T12:38:31-07:00","id":1445100,"title":"","content":"My simple strategy for that is to get them away from my groups and communities. Reaching out is something that endangers the gay, trans, and other minorities in my groups. I would never invite Far Right gamers to my table where they could endanger my players or even just ruin their evening. Even if I were so inclined to play with them myself, which I would not be as I only play with friends.<br /> <br /> White Wolf helped break me out of my fundamentalist homophobic background in high school and was a net positive in my life as well as an introduction to liberal Christianity.<br /> <br /> But I also knew a guy who (literally-no hyperbole) burned all of his books because he thought they were leading him to Satanism.<br /> <br /> He was a <i>Changeling: the Dreaming</i> fan.<br /> <br /> Later he got involved in, well, worse stuff. Breaking off that association was a good idea.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Author of <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Cthulhu-Armageddon-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01KUOM7SI/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982844&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Cthulhu+Armageddon\" target=\"_blank\">Cthulhu Armageddon</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Teenage-Weredeer-Bright-Falls-Mysteries-ebook/dp/B075TTN2FN/ref=sr_1_2?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982717&amp;sr=1-2&amp;keywords=Weredeer#customerReviews\" target=\"_blank\">I was a Teenage Weredeer</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Straight-Outta-Fangton-Comedic-Vampire-ebook/dp/B01KNHICCC/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982774&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Straight+Outta+Fangton\" target=\"_blank\">Straight Outta Fangton</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Lucifers-Star-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01MDM9MCT/ref=mt_kindle?_encoding=UTF8&amp;me=&amp;qid=\" target=\"_blank\">Lucifer's Star</a>, </i>and the <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Rules-Supervillainy-Saga-Book-ebook/dp/B07MB89S33/\" target=\"_blank\">Supervillainy Saga</a>.</i><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":12002,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","user":"CTPhipps","date":". 04-21-2021, 03:45 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","name":"CTPhipps","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12002_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13933"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-04-21T12:54:15-07:00","id":1445104,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CTPhipps</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1443592-the-official-v5-vs-v20-thread?p=1445093#post1445093\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I dunno, I feel like telling Nazis to fuck off is something that is very hard to criticize.</div> </div> </div> </div>Eh, anything less than a.... spanking, is a waste of breath. <br /> One cannot advocate real world violence on the forum. So the spanking is of course a metaphorical one. <br /> Anyhow, the issue isn't the message, it's the quality of the message. Maybe you're surrounded by more nazis than a prison cell's aryan brotherhood meeting so it's nice to vent a little. I found it offputting and supercilious. it evoked the idea of a smug middle-class american looking down on the redneck peasantry. I didn't like it as someone wanting to consume the wealthy, I don't imagine it'll be very well received by those seeing themselves as 'centrists' <br /> <br /> More on topic:<br /> Still, I also remember that the sample convictions were all &quot;good&quot; convictions; even a career criminal's gotta be a nice guy deep down. All together it just feels like V5 is far more heavy handed with morality. It's just not organic or intuitive to tie convictions up with touchstones. Hell everything in V5 feels less organic and intuitive than prior editions.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25794-mywifeisscary","name":"MyWifeIsScary","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25794_2.png","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3711"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-04-21T12:59:43-07:00","id":1445105,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MyWifeIsScary</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1443592-the-official-v5-vs-v20-thread?p=1445104#post1445104\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Eh, anything less than a.... spanking, is a waste of breath.<br /> One cannot advocate real world violence on the forum. So the spanking is of course a metaphorical one.<br /> Anyhow, the issue isn't the message, it's the quality of the message. Maybe you're surrounded by more nazis than a prison cell's aryan brotherhood meeting so it's nice to vent a little. I found it offputting and supercilious. it evoked the idea of a smug middle-class american looking down on the redneck peasantry. I didn't like it as someone wanting to consume the wealthy, I don't imagine it'll be very well received by those seeing themselves as 'centrists'</div> </div> </div> </div>So noted.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> More on topic:<br /> Still, I also remember that the sample convictions were all &quot;good&quot; convictions; even a career criminal's gotta be a nice guy deep down. All together it just feels like V5 is far more heavy handed with morality. It's just not organic or intuitive to tie convictions up with touchstones. Hell everything in V5 feels less organic and intuitive than prior editions. </div> </div> </div>* Obey authority<br /> * My country, right or wrong<br /> * None may control me<br /> * From each according to their<br /> abilities, to each according to<br /> their needs<br /> * Never act against another (insert<br /> own group/faith/sect)<br /> <br /> I dunno, there's a lot of questionable Convictions here. A Sabbat could very well have &quot;Never act against another Sabbat&quot; even when they're eating the hypothetical baby.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Author of <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Cthulhu-Armageddon-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01KUOM7SI/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982844&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Cthulhu+Armageddon\" target=\"_blank\">Cthulhu Armageddon</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Teenage-Weredeer-Bright-Falls-Mysteries-ebook/dp/B075TTN2FN/ref=sr_1_2?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982717&amp;sr=1-2&amp;keywords=Weredeer#customerReviews\" target=\"_blank\">I was a Teenage Weredeer</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Straight-Outta-Fangton-Comedic-Vampire-ebook/dp/B01KNHICCC/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982774&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Straight+Outta+Fangton\" target=\"_blank\">Straight Outta Fangton</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Lucifers-Star-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01MDM9MCT/ref=mt_kindle?_encoding=UTF8&amp;me=&amp;qid=\" target=\"_blank\">Lucifer's Star</a>, </i>and the <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Rules-Supervillainy-Saga-Book-ebook/dp/B07MB89S33/\" target=\"_blank\">Supervillainy Saga</a>.</i><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","name":"CTPhipps","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12002_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13933"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-04-21T14:40:06-07:00","id":1445126,"title":"","content":"That alt-right comment was in poor taste simply because it was pandering to a very specific (american) political group who fairly often demand such things from businesses they are customer to.<br /> <br /> That's all. The writer may have really believed what he said but let's not pretend that this was the main reason. And yes for anyone else that do not belong to that very specific cultural group that comment was jarring. Especially when you put it back into its proper context when white wolf was criticized because... they wrote in a nazi brujah. Yes first edition had a skinhead brujah as a freaking PLAYER CHARACTER CONCEPT but that did not matter.<br /> <br /> So white wolf had to demonstrate that they were not nazis by writing this line. By the way I am not criticizing White Wolf for choosing to write this. But let's not pretend that this was a courageous move or a real morale statement. When the truth is anything but. It's that culture of ignorance, censorship and submission that is so prevalent in the United States that is concerning for the rest of us outsiders.<br /> <br /> Buy what you believe in. Not sure I subscribe to that kind of socialism.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":24936,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24936-morbus","user":"Morbus","date":". 04-21-2021, 05:42 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24936-morbus","name":"Morbus","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"119"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-04-21T14:55:45-07:00","id":1445129,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Morbus</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1443592-the-official-v5-vs-v20-thread?p=1445126#post1445126\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">That alt-right comment was in poor taste simply because it was pandering to a very specific (american) political group who fairly often demand such things from businesses they are customer to</div> </div> </div> </div>It is also saying that Far Right white supremacist fans are not welcome at a pro-gay, pro diverse RPG community. Which is not a bad thing, LGBT and other fans helped make White Wolf.<br /> <br /> That statement has gone well over and beyond anyone concerned about Skinheads being listed among Brujah Concepts.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Author of <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Cthulhu-Armageddon-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01KUOM7SI/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982844&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Cthulhu+Armageddon\" target=\"_blank\">Cthulhu Armageddon</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Teenage-Weredeer-Bright-Falls-Mysteries-ebook/dp/B075TTN2FN/ref=sr_1_2?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982717&amp;sr=1-2&amp;keywords=Weredeer#customerReviews\" target=\"_blank\">I was a Teenage Weredeer</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Straight-Outta-Fangton-Comedic-Vampire-ebook/dp/B01KNHICCC/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982774&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Straight+Outta+Fangton\" target=\"_blank\">Straight Outta Fangton</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Lucifers-Star-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01MDM9MCT/ref=mt_kindle?_encoding=UTF8&amp;me=&amp;qid=\" target=\"_blank\">Lucifer's Star</a>, </i>and the <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Rules-Supervillainy-Saga-Book-ebook/dp/B07MB89S33/\" target=\"_blank\">Supervillainy Saga</a>.</i><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":12002,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","user":"CTPhipps","date":". 04-21-2021, 05:58 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","name":"CTPhipps","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12002_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13933"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-04-21T15:00:39-07:00","id":1445132,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CTPhipps</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1443592-the-official-v5-vs-v20-thread?p=1445129#post1445129\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> It is also saying that Far Right white supremacist fans are not welcome at a pro-gay, pro diverse RPG community. Which is not a bad thing, LGBT and other fans helped make White Wolf.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> As I said its not the content that was the issue. The reason for that was. And as always context matters.<br /> <br /> If WW had wrote this after being attacked by the alt-right, things would have been very different. And I would have been the first to applaud them. But no. That's not what happened. Admittedly it was a pretty insignificant concession to cave into. But it was still what it was.<br /> <br /> And I am not going to applaud posturing.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":24936,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24936-morbus","user":"Morbus","date":". 04-21-2021, 06:03 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24936-morbus","name":"Morbus","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"119"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-04-21T15:07:17-07:00","id":1445134,"title":"","content":"To each their own. For me, all that matters is that they made their position abundantly clear and it stands starkly against less forward claims like Ubisoft that their games are &quot;not political.&quot;<br /> <br /> But that's just me and its probably a bit off topic.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Author of <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Cthulhu-Armageddon-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01KUOM7SI/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982844&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Cthulhu+Armageddon\" target=\"_blank\">Cthulhu Armageddon</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Teenage-Weredeer-Bright-Falls-Mysteries-ebook/dp/B075TTN2FN/ref=sr_1_2?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982717&amp;sr=1-2&amp;keywords=Weredeer#customerReviews\" target=\"_blank\">I was a Teenage Weredeer</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Straight-Outta-Fangton-Comedic-Vampire-ebook/dp/B01KNHICCC/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982774&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Straight+Outta+Fangton\" target=\"_blank\">Straight Outta Fangton</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Lucifers-Star-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01MDM9MCT/ref=mt_kindle?_encoding=UTF8&amp;me=&amp;qid=\" target=\"_blank\">Lucifer's Star</a>, </i>and the <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Rules-Supervillainy-Saga-Book-ebook/dp/B07MB89S33/\" target=\"_blank\">Supervillainy Saga</a>.</i><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","name":"CTPhipps","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12002_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13933"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-04-21T15:10:31-07:00","id":1445136,"title":"","content":"Yes. Selling politics is a popular marketing tool in the US, apparently. It's very strange anywhere else. Corporations do no belong in the political sphere. At least in all the countries I lived. Which include a few countries in Europe and the Middle East.<br /> <br /> But yes to each their own.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24936-morbus","name":"Morbus","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"119"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-04-21T15:19:26-07:00","id":1445138,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Morbus</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1443592-the-official-v5-vs-v20-thread?p=1445136#post1445136\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Yes. Selling politics is a popular marketing tool in the US, apparently. It's very strange anywhere else. Corporations do no belong in the political sphere. At least in all the countries I lived. Which include a few countries in Europe and the Middle East.<br /> <br /> But yes to each their own.</div> </div> </div> </div>It's interesting to believe corporations denouncing white supremacy is considered bad to me. US or not. Mind you, the obvious reason is that with hate crime laws, promoting white supremacy is ILLEGAL in most of Europe.<br /> <br /> So its not necessary.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Author of <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Cthulhu-Armageddon-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01KUOM7SI/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982844&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Cthulhu+Armageddon\" target=\"_blank\">Cthulhu Armageddon</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Teenage-Weredeer-Bright-Falls-Mysteries-ebook/dp/B075TTN2FN/ref=sr_1_2?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982717&amp;sr=1-2&amp;keywords=Weredeer#customerReviews\" target=\"_blank\">I was a Teenage Weredeer</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Straight-Outta-Fangton-Comedic-Vampire-ebook/dp/B01KNHICCC/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982774&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Straight+Outta+Fangton\" target=\"_blank\">Straight Outta Fangton</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Lucifers-Star-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01MDM9MCT/ref=mt_kindle?_encoding=UTF8&amp;me=&amp;qid=\" target=\"_blank\">Lucifer's Star</a>, </i>and the <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Rules-Supervillainy-Saga-Book-ebook/dp/B07MB89S33/\" target=\"_blank\">Supervillainy Saga</a>.</i><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","name":"CTPhipps","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12002_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13933"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-04-21T15:27:45-07:00","id":1445142,"title":"","content":"Ad Hominem.<br /> <br /> I never said what was said was bad. But nice try nonetheless.<br /> <br /> No. As you admitted yourself you are not insensitive to such marketing, and buying your politics. Which is okay. Do you.<br /> <br /> Me personally this kind of marketing does not appeal to me. I am even kind of wary of the potential slippery slope here. The US seems to veer dangerously close to a sort of corpocracy. Maybe that's why it's so important that brands appeal to political sensitivities?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":24936,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24936-morbus","user":"Morbus","date":". 04-21-2021, 06:30 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24936-morbus","name":"Morbus","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"119"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-04-21T15:29:46-07:00","id":1445143,"title":"","content":"Out of curiosity:<br /> <br /> What is everyone's favorite V20 supplement and favorite V5?<br /> <br /> Why?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Author of <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Cthulhu-Armageddon-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01KUOM7SI/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982844&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Cthulhu+Armageddon\" target=\"_blank\">Cthulhu Armageddon</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Teenage-Weredeer-Bright-Falls-Mysteries-ebook/dp/B075TTN2FN/ref=sr_1_2?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982717&amp;sr=1-2&amp;keywords=Weredeer#customerReviews\" target=\"_blank\">I was a Teenage Weredeer</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Straight-Outta-Fangton-Comedic-Vampire-ebook/dp/B01KNHICCC/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982774&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Straight+Outta+Fangton\" target=\"_blank\">Straight Outta Fangton</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Lucifers-Star-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01MDM9MCT/ref=mt_kindle?_encoding=UTF8&amp;me=&amp;qid=\" target=\"_blank\">Lucifer's Star</a>, </i>and the <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Rules-Supervillainy-Saga-Book-ebook/dp/B07MB89S33/\" target=\"_blank\">Supervillainy Saga</a>.</i><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","name":"CTPhipps","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12002_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13933"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-04-21T15:58:01-07:00","id":1445147,"title":"","content":"Making your position clear is bad when it's making you look not-great.<br /> And yes, thankyou morbus. For someone who could marginally be considered a european, it's just a really weird thing to say. Mind you, I've spent the last year in the parts of europe where bigotry is normal and uncontroversial and the big issue of the last election was whether or not gays were acceptable. The year before I was living in one of the most liberal countries europe has. It's weird here and it's weird there, for mostly the same reasons. If you &quot;need&quot; to make a statement typically you say &quot;We support X,Y and Z&quot; not &quot;We don't like X and if you're X go home and rethink your life&quot;. That's just giving your opponents ammo. It looks like you're overcompensating for something. If you're in a country filled with biggoted conservatives but nobody's actually challenged enough to be a neo-nazi because the nation's 99% white and non jewish because the actual historic nazis over-performed (here) then all you're doing by condemning the alt-right in such a posturing maner is confirming their negative beliefs about &quot;The left&quot;.<br /> It's tone-deaf counterproductive.<br /> <br /> Corporations can get &quot;political&quot; in their message but it's weird and usually not a good idea. (paying politicians as a corporation for favours however is very very normal)<br /> <br /> Anyhow I think that's more than need said about the topic but... I don't know, if I'm with a good group who trusts me, I kinda like playing very right-wing characters. V5 as a game seems to push too much &quot;right wing&quot; ideas like religiosity on the cam and too many zany liberal ideas (the ministry) onto the Anarchs. When you take it all in together it feels like they really are trying to hamfist you with a very specific political outlook. V20 was great because it gave you a lot more freedom to interpret the political philosophy of each sect, even if sometimes players come up with obviously wrong stuff like the Anarchs being the good guys or the Sabbat being the good guys or the Cam not being the best sect since Haquim founded all the assamite bloodlines and gave them jobs.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":25794,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25794-mywifeisscary","user":"MyWifeIsScary","date":". 04-21-2021, 07:20 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25794-mywifeisscary","name":"MyWifeIsScary","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25794_2.png","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3711"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-04-21T16:12:24-07:00","id":1445149,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CTPhipps</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1443592-the-official-v5-vs-v20-thread?p=1445143#post1445143\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Out of curiosity:<br /> <br /> What is everyone's favorite V20 supplement and favorite V5?<br /> <br /> Why?</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> V20 wise I'd list them like so<br /> <br /> <b>Perfect</b>: Alas, I'm picky. <br /> <br /> <b>Great</b>: <br /> Core book<br /> Rites Of the Blood<br /> Hunters hunted II<br /> LotC<br /> <br /> <b>Good</b><br /> Ghouls<br /> Anarchs unbound<br /> <br /> <b>Eh, mostly can't remember it. </b><br /> Red list. <br /> Edit; TBH<br /> <br /> <b>Eh, can't remember it (but fairly sure I read it) </b><br /> V20 Companion. <br /> Children of the Revolution<br /> <br /> <b>Bad:</b> LotB<br /> <br /> <b>Haven't read</b>: <br /> The rest. I plan to read Becket's someday. <br /> <br /> I'm less favourable to DAV20. But honestly I don't remember much beyond the corebook, like which book had the realistic weapon table?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":25794,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25794-mywifeisscary","user":"MyWifeIsScary","date":". 04-22-2021, 02:28 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25794-mywifeisscary","name":"MyWifeIsScary","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25794_2.png","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3711"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-04-21T16:37:53-07:00","id":1445156,"title":"","content":"On the whole calling out alt-righters thing:<br /> <br /> I think this thread has lost a lot of context. There was not one misstep by nWW, but a series of them.<br /> <br /> People are not getting upset at the idea of neo-Nazi Brujah, but the phrasing in the book equating their status as outsiders and rebels (despite a rise in political power by the far-right in both the US and Europe) to non-politically charged groups.<br /> <br /> Then there's things like the accidental use of numbers in a mechanics example that are used in alt-right iconography. And Martin's incredibly poorly worded statement on FaceBook about how there's nothing they can do but accept the reality that with so many Swedes voting for a far-right political party with Nazi sympathies means they have lots of Nazi customers (which... might make Jason's statement a bit more sensible when you look at his specific phrasing as a way to refute Martin's).<br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CTPhipps</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1443592-the-official-v5-vs-v20-thread?p=1445143#post1445143\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Out of curiosity:<br /> <br /> What is everyone's favorite V20 supplement and favorite V5?<br /> <br /> Why?</div> </div> </div> </div>V20: I'll got out on a weird limb here, The Black Hand: A Guide to the Tal'Mahe'Ra. It stands out for embracing some of the early weirdness of the game, and does a very good job updating the material to something that still works with a more modern sensibility.<br /> <br /> V5: The free V5 Companion. Kind of a weak answer, but I've only read four V5 books in full, and the other three are core, Anarchs and Camarilla.... and I'm not picking a book I haven't read even I'm sure I'd probably take Cults if I was going to take the time to read more of V5.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-04-21T17:17:32-07:00","id":1445161,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CTPhipps</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1443592-the-official-v5-vs-v20-thread?p=1445143#post1445143\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Out of curiosity:<br /> <br /> What is everyone's favorite V20 supplement and favorite V5?<br /> <br /> Why?</div> </div> </div> </div>For V20 this is a hard battle between, Compendium, BJD, LotC, LotB and the Ghoul book.<br /> BJD because it has rules for Dhampirs and it has many flavour text and it looks very good in limited but those stories are more for long time fans and in German Beckett speaks still ingame about the wrong transleted term Kainskind (Kaine's child) for Kindred.<br /> V20 Compendium has on the plus point good descriptions about modern Kainite live in the 2010s and Caitiff but sadly this boring talk about all this titles and depts which is from my opinion unneeded.<br /> Lore of the Clans has the much needed in-depth going to the clans but Lore of the Bloodlines is in my eyes way better written. Ghoul20 book is very well written and give of fantastic insight about the live of a ghoul but I would not say it is the best supplementory because you would more need one of the previous mentiened books more.<br /> If I have to choose I would say my favourite supplement book for V20 is DAV20 because it opens a whole new world.<br /> For V5 because beside core rules anarchs and cam book is only just now Fall of London come out in german which I whas unable to buy right now cause of Lockdown so I would say Cam book because in comparison to the Anarch book it feels like it is not only style but has substance too.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>As I am from Austria I need to clarify two things.<br /> First my native language is german and so please point out if the english I write is broken so I can improve.<br /> Second I do not own VTMV beyond first three books nor any line after M20 Corebook because it is not out there and I wait for the translation.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26160-koronus","name":"Koronus","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2020"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"366"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-04-21T18:46:15-07:00","id":1445174,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CTPhipps</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1443592-the-official-v5-vs-v20-thread?p=1445143#post1445143\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Out of curiosity:<br /> <br /> What is everyone's favorite V20 supplement and favorite V5?<br /> <br /> Why?</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> DAV20 Core, and V20 Core I mix and match Discipline rules, If I had to choose just one I'd have a hard time.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24221-vamps-like-us","name":"Vamps Like Us","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"390"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-04-21T18:58:07-07:00","id":1445177,"title":"","content":"I'm noticing some people not mentioning the second part of the question. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/biggrin.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Big Grin\" smilieid=\"3\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> Edit:<br /> <br /> I'm just kidding, guys. Seriously. Loving the answers so far.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Author of <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Cthulhu-Armageddon-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01KUOM7SI/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982844&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Cthulhu+Armageddon\" target=\"_blank\">Cthulhu Armageddon</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Teenage-Weredeer-Bright-Falls-Mysteries-ebook/dp/B075TTN2FN/ref=sr_1_2?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982717&amp;sr=1-2&amp;keywords=Weredeer#customerReviews\" target=\"_blank\">I was a Teenage Weredeer</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Straight-Outta-Fangton-Comedic-Vampire-ebook/dp/B01KNHICCC/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982774&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Straight+Outta+Fangton\" target=\"_blank\">Straight Outta Fangton</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Lucifers-Star-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01MDM9MCT/ref=mt_kindle?_encoding=UTF8&amp;me=&amp;qid=\" target=\"_blank\">Lucifer's Star</a>, </i>and the <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Rules-Supervillainy-Saga-Book-ebook/dp/B07MB89S33/\" target=\"_blank\">Supervillainy Saga</a>.</i><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":12002,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","user":"CTPhipps","date":". 04-21-2021, 10:07 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","name":"CTPhipps","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12002_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13933"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-04-21T19:04:28-07:00","id":1445178,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CTPhipps</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1443592-the-official-v5-vs-v20-thread?p=1445177#post1445177\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I'm noticing some people not mentioning the second part of the question. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/biggrin.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Big Grin\" smilieid=\"3\" class=\"inlineimg\" /></div> </div> </div> </div>v20: Lore of the Clans,DAV20.<br /> V5: Chicago by Night","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4621-nicolas-milioni","name":"Nicolas Milioni","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4621_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3605"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-04-21T19:30:26-07:00","id":1445184,"title":"","content":"I've really grown to like the Messy Critical and Bestial Failure mechanics. Very fun to roleplay the results.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3598-cajunkhan","name":"CajunKhan","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3598_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1700"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-04-21T20:21:12-07:00","id":1445199,"title":"","content":"One thing I don't think gets brought up very much is the removal of Generation as a background in V5. I love as a ST picking the type of game you want to play either beginner(fledgling), experienced(neonate) and advanced(ancillae). Keeping everyone at the same general power level and you don't have the one player who puts all his backgrounds into generation to get a super character with no ties to anything else in the game.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>The Hecata are a sect not a clan.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24211-frontline989","name":"Frontline989","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24211_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"152"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-04-22T01:25:28-07:00","id":1445240,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CTPhipps</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1443592-the-official-v5-vs-v20-thread?p=1445073#post1445073\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Honestly, I think the biggest benefit of V5 is the fact that it dramatically broadens the scope of underutilized genres in the vampire game. Not only is combat and mechanics more simplified but it really does give a lot of incentive for doing street level gaming that didn't exist there before. I used to be very hostile to MAGE REVISED due to the extensiveness of use that I made of the Umbra in my games, almost to the point of being Nobilis, but when I actually tried out a street mage game, it proved to be incredibly fun.</div> </div> </div> </div>I can't see how this is true. It's not broadening if it's only in one area. 'Honing in' may be more accurate. V20 definitely allows for a broader style of play. I think traditional roleplaying games are better for that sort of play. Modern indie game design attempts to express theme and genre through mechanics, which is fine for games that offer a very specific experience, but I don't think a game such as VTM has ever been that narrow. It has never focused on just one experience. By making it narrow, it does gut a lot of the opportunities from the world.<br /> <br /> To be honest, I play VTM for that world. I like rules that support a range of themes and don't get in the way. Bells and whistles can be good, but I prefer them as something in my toolbox I can pull out if I need them for a specific chronicle with a specific tone. <br /> <br /> I'm extremely comfortable creating theme, tone and mood through narrative and roleplaying. I don't need systems to do that. I get that others do, though. So the best solution is one that caters to me as well as those other players. You give a basic system and then provide a bunch of dials for those who need to tweak things or need extra support building a cohesive ambience.<br /> <br /> When I think of the games I return to all the time, they're games like Warhammer, Fading Suns, Shadowrun and anything World of Darkness. Even D&amp;D and Exalted are not as narrow as V5. I don't play hyper specialised games that always play the same because that's not my bag. I like games to surprise me and go in new directions, not always play the same.<br /> <br /> In this case, I don't think the combat rules are actually better either. Simpler is not necessarily better. The new rules put way more on the ST to adjudicate, due to basic things like not having a definite initiative system. V20DA provided a much faster, deadlier and more versatile combat system that's usually done in fewer than three rounds anyway, but with enough dials that you can have more intricate options or you can keep it simple.<br /> <br /> CTD2e also had one-roll combat, which I still think was better than V5's, and that was two decades earlier.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Honestly, I think perception is the cause of the problem here because if you play the rules as is, the V20 vampires are the ones that should be frenzying all the time. I believe that a lot of Storytellers got out of the habit of calling for frenzy checks when in danger, when angry, when there was any fire larger than a cigarette, when injured, or the scent of blood nearby. The rules make it very clear that this is meant to be an extremely common thing. I note that I actually think that the ability to manage the Beast goes up with the fact that the mind is &quot;quieted&quot; when you kill someone in the game. Plus, Compulsions mean that you are LESS likely to go on a killing spree but just have your behavior altered. </div> </div> </div>Heavy Arms dealt with this, but this is your misperception, I think. V20 and Revised are both clear that these rolls are for exceptional circumstances. It's there in black and white.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> But there are ample ways of managing the Beast in-game, not the least bit keeping that Hunger at 1 and only having to deal with the threat if confronted with great provocation. Let's not pretend that V20's rules don't make it clear that if you spend that last Blood Point, you won't carve up your own coterie and the nearest baby. When you don't, that was because the ST made a decision to not do so because it wouldn't be fun. V5 has solidified that lessened tendency to go on a murder spree into the rules. </div> </div> </div>I mean, you explicitly don't need to kill anyone to avoid getting hungry in V20 or earlier. You can sip little but often and be fine. It's really not the same at all. Even one Hunger Die can cause havoc in play.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Even the Bestial Failures have been designed to move AWAY from random murder.<br /> <br /> RANDOM COMPULSIONS<br /> <br /> 1-3: Hunger<br /> 4-5: Dominance<br /> 6-7: Harm<br /> 8-9: Paranoia<br /> 0: Clan Compulsion* </div> </div> </div>Murder is already baked into Hunger, so the fact that Bestial Failures don't mandate murder doesn't reduce the murder requirement. It just stops it from being even higher. <br /> <br /> But overall, Messy Criticals and Bestial Failures do increase the risk of bad things happening significantly, and you're rarely free of them. And I actually like the idea of them; I just think, as is, they're a bit of a narrative straitjacket. They ensure a certain style of play at all times.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> I don't think that in the entirety of the genre of vampires has ever made this an attitude of a protagonist. Vampires may be cursed in the literal sense with an uncontrollable lust for blood but when they do something horrible under duress they still carry that traumatizing memory. I once got a 1-star review by a poor woman who was HORRIFIED that there was a scene in my STRAIGHT OUTTA FANGTON book where the protagonist was locked up in a basement with a little girl to be starved until he fed on her. </div> </div> </div>That's where content warnings can come in handy. Personally, I'd find that gratuitous, too. I'm not into that sort of story. <br /> <br /> That said, it's clear we have different tastes as to what we want to play. I like low levels of squick, even when I'm playing Sabbat vampires. Vampires can be dicks to each other and adults without involving minors, pets, vulnerable people, etc.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> I'm like, &quot;Yes, it's meant to be horrifying.&quot;<br /> <br /> It obviously traumatized the protagonist despite having no control. </div> </div> </div>Honestly, this anecdote makes me uncomfortable. What's the effect of such traumatic incidents on the reader or, in a game, on the player? It sounds to me like the person who complained in her review didn't feel there was adequate warning about what was in store, and that's a legitimate critique.<br /> <br /> To bring that back on track, there are different levels of horror. I'm hugely into classic horror movies, but I've never been into things like Hostel or Saw because I think they're gratuitous. Horror isn't just one thing. VTM doesn't need to be gratuitous either, just because horror sometimes is.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Political horror is something that I think has been modified primarily for this game based around the decades of lessons of LARP and material. The loss of Elders and focus on jockeying for power has taken front stage so we do have people like Kevin Jackson actually able to move into the big seat. However, it's because the power vacuum that currently exists low-wise is open to them. It's not like there's more frenzy opportunities than Elysium than there were before either and when you frenzy, you might NOT rip out the throat of Annabelle as you would before but instead just be a real asshole. </div> </div> </div>Most of us aren't LARPers, which is again why this feels like the game wasn't written for us. I get the intent, but it makes more sense that the things LARP needs happen to the LARP version of the game (and V20 MET does have a separate metaplot and rules for that precise system). Merging the two disadvantages both groups, really.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> I'm not entirely down with that but let's not pretend the Compulsion system doesn't downgrade the dangers of frenzy. </div> </div> </div>It absolutely does not. Compulsions do not replace Frenzy. They are in addition to it. How is that not *adding* to the dangers? 3+1=4, not 2.<br /> <br /> Now, if you could opt to take a Compulsion instead of Frenzying in certain low-threshold situations, that would reduce the dangers of the Frenzy system, IMO. And actually, that might be a neat way for me to port Compulsions into V20.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Writer, publisher, performer<br /> Mostly he/his, sometimes she/her IRL <a href=\"https://adam-lowe.com\" target=\"_blank\">https://adam-lowe.com</a>","edited":{"userid":5291,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5291-adambeyoncelowe","user":"adambeyoncelowe","date":". 04-22-2021, 04:31 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":11}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5291-adambeyoncelowe","name":"adambeyoncelowe","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5291_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2802"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-04-22T01:37:22-07:00","id":1445241,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>adambeyoncelowe</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1443592-the-official-v5-vs-v20-thread?p=1445240#post1445240\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I can't see how this is true. It's not broadening if it's only in one area. 'Honing in' may be more accurate. V20 definitely allows for a broader style of play. I think traditional roleplaying games are better for that sort of play. Modern indie game design attempts to express theme and genre through mechanics, which is fine for games that offer a very specific experience, but I don't think a game such as VTM has ever been that narrow. It has never focused on just one experience. By making it narrow, it does gut a lot of the opportunities from the world.</div> </div> </div> </div>Totally disagree.<br /> <br /> I feel like a lot of people have zoomed in on the idea of personal horror as the only thing that V5 can do but I've very much enjoyed the action-focused campaigns as well as the political games I've been enjoying with it. I think the setting for V5 does politics better than V20 and it also is excellent at action. I feel like V20 is perfectly serviceable and is a great jack of all trades game but I think that with modification, it could be better at the styles you're likely to play with the setting.<br /> <br /> You've addressed a lot of what I considered to be the improvements of V5 in terms of combat and action, though. I feel like it has a more cinematic and faster paced action rules set. Its a lot faster and more dynamic rules set.<br /> <br /> I also feel like the Humanity and Tenet system being more adjustable for Chronicle means that the game is incentivized to allow maximum flexibility for storytelling and mood. Now there's not going to be any confusion on what sort of game you'll be experiencing with players. Whether you're playing Louis, Lestat, or Selene.<br /> <br /> But YMMV I guess.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Author of <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Cthulhu-Armageddon-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01KUOM7SI/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982844&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Cthulhu+Armageddon\" target=\"_blank\">Cthulhu Armageddon</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Teenage-Weredeer-Bright-Falls-Mysteries-ebook/dp/B075TTN2FN/ref=sr_1_2?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982717&amp;sr=1-2&amp;keywords=Weredeer#customerReviews\" target=\"_blank\">I was a Teenage Weredeer</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Straight-Outta-Fangton-Comedic-Vampire-ebook/dp/B01KNHICCC/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982774&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Straight+Outta+Fangton\" target=\"_blank\">Straight Outta Fangton</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Lucifers-Star-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01MDM9MCT/ref=mt_kindle?_encoding=UTF8&amp;me=&amp;qid=\" target=\"_blank\">Lucifer's Star</a>, </i>and the <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Rules-Supervillainy-Saga-Book-ebook/dp/B07MB89S33/\" target=\"_blank\">Supervillainy Saga</a>.</i><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","name":"CTPhipps","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12002_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13933"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-04-22T02:39:56-07:00","id":1445246,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CTPhipps</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1443592-the-official-v5-vs-v20-thread?p=1445241#post1445241\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Totally disagree.<br /> <br /> I feel like a lot of people have zoomed in on the idea of personal horror as the only thing that V5 can do but I've very much enjoyed the action-focused campaigns as well as the political games I've been enjoying with it. I think the setting for V5 does politics better than V20 and it also is excellent at action. I feel like V20 is perfectly serviceable and is a great jack of all trades game but I think that with modification, it could be better at the styles you're likely to play with the setting.<br /> <br /> You've addressed a lot of what I considered to be the improvements of V5 in terms of combat and action, though. I feel like it has a more cinematic and faster paced action rules set. Its a lot faster and more dynamic rules set.<br /> <br /> I also feel like the Humanity and Tenet system being more adjustable for Chronicle means that the game is incentivized to allow maximum flexibility for storytelling and mood. Now there's not going to be any confusion on what sort of game you'll be experiencing with players. Whether you're playing Louis, Lestat, or Selene.<br /> <br /> But YMMV I guess.</div> </div> </div> </div>I don't see how politics is easier in V5. Would you mind elaborating on that? Is it a matter of setting or mechanics? Because, to me, the Hunger mechanic forces a very narrow focus on feeding and blood, which actually lends itself to a street-level focus rather than a political focus. And yes, street-level can be political, but it's only, again, a small fraction of the politicking you could do in V20.<br /> <br /> For example, V20 has super-powerful elders, so you are quite often forced to think really cleverly about how to take an opponent down or make them lose prestige in your city. Games can also have a global as well as a street-level focus quite easily, which expands the politicking.<br /> <br /> If anything, the kind of politics in V5 is more about turf wars but otherwise *avoiding* the politics.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Writer, publisher, performer<br /> Mostly he/his, sometimes she/her IRL <a href=\"https://adam-lowe.com\" target=\"_blank\">https://adam-lowe.com</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":10}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5291-adambeyoncelowe","name":"adambeyoncelowe","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5291_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2802"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-04-22T03:08:05-07:00","id":1445248,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>adambeyoncelowe</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1443592-the-official-v5-vs-v20-thread?p=1445240#post1445240\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I can't see how this is true. It's not broadening if it's only in one area. 'Honing in' may be more accurate. V20 definitely allows for a broader style of play. I think traditional roleplaying games are better for that sort of play. Modern indie game design attempts to express theme and genre through mechanics, which is fine for games that offer a very specific experience, but I don't think a game such as VTM has ever been that narrow. It has never focused on just one experience. By making it narrow, it does gut a lot of the opportunities from the world.<br /> <br /> To be honest, I play VTM for that world. I like rules that support a range of themes and don't get in the way. Bells and whistles can be good, but I prefer them as something in my toolbox I can pull out if I need them for a specific chronicle with a specific tone. <br /> <br /> I'm extremely comfortable creating theme, tone and mood through narrative and roleplaying. I don't need systems to do that. I get that others do, though. So the best solution is one that caters to me as well as those other players. You give a basic system and then provide a bunch of dials for those who need to tweak things or need extra support building a cohesive ambience.<br /> <br /> When I think of the games I return to all the time, they're games like Warhammer, Fading Suns, Shadowrun and anything World of Darkness. Even D&amp;D and Exalted are not as narrow as V5. I don't play hyper specialised games that always play the same because that's not my bag. I like games to surprise me and go in new directions, not always play the same.<br /> <br /> In this case, I don't think the combat rules are actually better either. Simpler is not necessarily better. The new rules put way more on the ST to adjudicate, due to basic things like not having a definite initiative system. V20DA provided a much faster, deadlier and more versatile combat system that's usually done in fewer than three rounds anyway, but with enough dials that you can have more intricate options or you can keep it simple.<br /> <br /> CTD2e also had one-roll combat, which I still think was better than V5's, and that was two decades earlier.<br /> <br /> <br /> Heavy Arms dealt with this, but this is your misperception, I think. V20 and Revised are both clear that these rolls are for exceptional circumstances. It's there in black and white.<br /> <br /> <br /> I mean, you explicitly don't need to kill anyone to avoid getting hungry in V20 or earlier. You can sip little but often and be fine. It's really not the same at all. Even one Hunger Die can cause havoc in play.<br /> <br /> <br /> Murder is already baked into Hunger, so the fact that Bestial Failures don't mandate murder doesn't reduce the murder requirement. It just stops it from being even higher. <br /> <br /> But overall, Messy Criticals and Bestial Failures do increase the risk of bad things happening significantly, and you're rarely free of them. And I actually like the idea of them; I just think, as is, they're a bit of a narrative straitjacket. They ensure a certain style of play at all times.<br /> <br /> <br /> That's where content warnings can come in handy. Personally, I'd find that gratuitous, too. I'm not into that sort of story. <br /> <br /> That said, it's clear we have different tastes as to what we want to play. I like low levels of squick, even when I'm playing Sabbat vampires. Vampires can be dicks to each other and adults without involving minors, pets, vulnerable people, etc.<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> Honestly, this anecdote makes me uncomfortable. What's the effect of such traumatic incidents on the reader or, in a game, on the player? It sounds to me like the person who complained in her review didn't feel there was adequate warning about what was in store, and that's a legitimate critique.<br /> <br /> To bring that back on track, there are different levels of horror. I'm hugely into classic horror movies, but I've never been into things like Hostel or Saw because I think they're gratuitous. Horror isn't just one thing. VTM doesn't need to be gratuitous either, just because horror sometimes is.<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> Most of us aren't LARPers, which is again why this feels like the game wasn't written for us. I get the intent, but it makes more sense that the things LARP needs happen to the LARP version of the game (and V20 MET does have a separate metaplot and rules for that precise system). Merging the two disadvantages both groups, really.<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> It absolutely does not. Compulsions do not replace Frenzy. They are in addition to it. How is that not *adding* to the dangers? 3+1=4, not 2.<br /> <br /> Now, if you could opt to take a Compulsion instead of Frenzying in certain low-threshold situations, that would reduce the dangers of the Frenzy system, IMO. And actually, that might be a neat way for me to port Compulsions into V20.</div> </div> </div> </div>Fully Agree.<br /> <br /> We gave up on ever going to Elysium in our games as the combination of MCs, BFs, Willpower Damage etc. made interactions with other vampires a losing proposition where social damage was certain, mental damage extremely likely and any plans you made could be randomly sidetracked when your nature betrayed you. If SPCs used the same rules as PCs the place would be a bloodbath every time.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":9}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/479-damian-may","name":"Damian May","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar479_1.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1199"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-04-22T03:49:01-07:00","id":1445250,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CTPhipps</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">I think the setting for V5 does politics better than V20</div> </div> </div> </div>.............lol","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Jade Kingdom Warrior","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25523-shakanaka","name":"Shakanaka","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25523_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"951"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-04-22T04:00:38-07:00","id":1445251,"title":"","content":"Oi don't get nasty. The community doesn't want the thread to close.'<br /> <br /> That said, CTPhipps, you really do have a strange view of V20. Maybe it's your long experience playing the game with housrules, or prior editions muddling your view a bit, but sometimes when I read your posts I'm wondering if we read the same books. (and Indeed, you do often write down your fan-changes as if they were the product, as you have admited) Maybe try and forget everything you know and re-read V20. Try put yourself as someone who's playing vampire for the first time. I understand that V5's politics may align with your own personal views more, but I don't understand how you could think that politics is &quot;done better&quot;. Could you explain? It's clearly not as &quot;realistic&quot;, nor as central, nor as.. well, a lot of things. I will grant that V5 actually has a pretty solid section on how kindred society is fuedal, but mechanically, and given how the sects have changed, it's clearly more loses than gains.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":12}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25794-mywifeisscary","name":"MyWifeIsScary","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25794_2.png","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3711"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-04-22T07:58:59-07:00","id":1445266,"title":"","content":"Yeah, things like his repeated insistence that \u201cyou automatically lose Humanity when you kill in V20\u201d and his headcanon about how Viniculum worked oved the Lasombra thread it really does feel like Phipps\u2019 actual experience with V20 is rather superficial and/or based on someone\u2019s heavily homebrewed campaign.<br /> <br /> The result is that a lot his arguments/explanations really fail to connect like it seems he think they should be doing because his attempts to show how V5\u2019s mechanics are superior to V20\u2019s aren\u2019t even referencing an actual rule in V20.<br /> <br /> And part of it too is just a massive disconnect between people\u2019s definitions of horror and drama. For example, I consider the whole \u201clocked in a room with a child and starved until I lose control and feed\u201d to be neither horror (evoking fear or dread) nor dramatic (those involved must have some choice to make that affects the outcome). For me such a scene is what I\u2019d call \u201cmisery porn.\u201d<br /> <br /> And because my frame of reference is heroism and drama, if I were writing the same scene the protagonist would either find a way to escape with the child (a more heroic outcome) or, if wanting something more tragic, find a way to cripple or kill himself before Hunger would drive him to eat the child. Because just suffering until you give in doesn\u2019t make for an interesting protagonist to me. If I wanted misery porn I\u2019d just turn on the news.<br /> <br /> And I don\u2019t play to be victimized by some force beyond my control; I play characters who fight to maintain control and not harm innocents. With its hunger dice only being completely mitigated by murder, the ONLY enjoyable vampire I could play in V5 is one who, upon learning what they are, took an immediate sunbath.<br /> <br /> As written V5 is utterly unable to deliver an experience I\u2019d find enjoyable while V20\u2019s toolbox approach can. Being a consensualist in V20 is a viable approach. You can keep yourself satiated and therefore in virtually no danger of losing control when feeding. In V5 it\u2019s a recipe for misery as there\u2019s always going to be that one hunger die that will rob you of your agency and leave a consensual vessel drained... and again, that\u2019s when the only viable option for me in terms of character interest is a sunbath.<br /> <br /> Not saying people who like that stuff shouldn\u2019t have options for it, but it\u2019s absolutely not for me.<br /> <br /> As to which products I like. For VtM preferences it ranks...<br /> <br /> 1) p. 144 of BJD (V20 Dhampir rules).<br /> 2) V20 Core<br /> 3) Ghouls and Revenants<br /> 4) Hunter\u2019s Hunted II<br /> 5) Rites of the Blood<br /> 6) The Rest of Beckett\u2019s Jyhad Diary<br /> 7) The rest of the V20 books<br /> <br /> 8) Revised and 2e VtM materials<br /> 9) the other X20 game lines (and Revised HtR, DtF, KotE and 2e Mummy and Bygone Bestiary)<br /> 10) select Vampire the Requiem products (ex. Damnation City had its section on \u201cOne Hundred People You Haven\u2019t Met Before\u201d and \u201cFifty Things People Want\u201d that I turned into some precentile tables for introducing random NPCs when the players are just going out on the town).<br /> <br /> 11) V5 Core (because it\u2019s where I\u2019ve scraped a few useful houserules for V20 from).<br /> <br /> 12) various World of Darkness wikis where I can get a semblance of the metaplot without having to read the first-person purple prose (for reference, my preference in approach to lore about events is pg. 125-127 of Time of Thin Blood where they just lay it out 3rd person omniscient style).<br /> <br /> 13) V5 Companion for being free.<br /> 14) Almost every other V5 book. <br /> 15) Non-Word of Darkness systems.<br /> 666) Cults of the Blood Gods for reasons I will not discuss lest I get this thread shut down.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1328,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1328-chris24601","user":"Chris24601","date":". 04-22-2021, 11:03 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":9}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1328-chris24601","name":"Chris24601","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"520"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-04-22T09:39:11-07:00","id":1445280,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MyWifeIsScary</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1443592-the-official-v5-vs-v20-thread?p=1445251#post1445251\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Oi don't get nasty. The community doesn't want the thread to close.'<br /> <br /> That said, CTPhipps, you really do have a strange view of V20. Maybe it's your long experience playing the game with housrules, or prior editions muddling your view a bit, but sometimes when I read your posts I'm wondering if we read the same books. (and Indeed, you do often write down your fan-changes as if they were the product, as you have admited) Maybe try and forget everything you know and re-read V20. Try put yourself as someone who's playing vampire for the first time. I understand that V5's politics may align with your own personal views more, but I don't understand how you could think that politics is &quot;done better&quot;. Could you explain? It's clearly not as &quot;realistic&quot;, nor as central, nor as.. well, a lot of things. I will grant that V5 actually has a pretty solid section on how kindred society is fuedal, but mechanically, and given how the sects have changed, it's clearly more loses than gains.</div> </div> </div> </div>I don't write down fan changes canon, I write down suggestions for how to do things. I think interpretations are very different at tables, though, which is something that needs to be considered.<br /> <br /> I will confess to flat out getting a couple of rules wrong like V5's Dominate, though. That was embarrassing. I also appreciate when corrected. Fans who have a better grasp of things are guys I owe a boon to.<br /> <br /> Happy to explain why I think V5 politics are better, though.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>adambeyoncelowe</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1443592-the-official-v5-vs-v20-thread?p=1445246#post1445246\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I don't see how politics is easier in V5. Would you mind elaborating on that? Is it a matter of setting or mechanics? Because, to me, the Hunger mechanic forces a very narrow focus on feeding and blood, which actually lends itself to a street-level focus rather than a political focus. And yes, street-level can be political, but it's only, again, a small fraction of the politicking you could do in V20.<br /> <br /> For example, V20 has super-powerful elders, so you are quite often forced to think really cleverly about how to take an opponent down or make them lose prestige in your city. Games can also have a global as well as a street-level focus quite easily, which expands the politicking.<br /> <br /> If anything, the kind of politics in V5 is more about turf wars but otherwise *avoiding* the politics.</div> </div> </div> </div>In terms of both but in terms of mechanics, I think that people who attempt to state that the Hunger Mechanics ruins politics just flat out are doing it wrong. They've let their own interpretation of the rules get in the way of actually running the game and the politica are not in any way shape or form affected the way they think.<br /> <br /> Mechanically, just a few of the benefits that I think have been helped by the game are:<br /> <br /> * The adjustments to Mental Disciplines that emphasize more freedom for vampires in roleplay over Disciplines.<br /> * Rouse checks limiting the use of abilities on fellow vampires to dramatically appropriate moments.<br /> * Loresheets allowing the player characters to be neck deep in the politics of the game from the get go.<br /> * The transformation to appearance and how it functions being no longer a Attribute sink.<br /> * The de-emphaziing of powerful Elder Disciplines and focus much more on prestige and alliances.<br /> * The bigger focus on coterie-power and shared backgrounds.<br /> * Feeding changes mean that the Tradition of Domain is now something much more important to fight over when it was previously the ignored Tradition.<br /> * CbN and Cults of the Blood Gods also give other great optional rules sets.<br /> <br /> Lore wise, the differences are also beneficial for politics:<br /> <br /> * The allowance of Ancilla and Neonates to higher positions in the setting.<br /> * The conflict between Anarchs and Camarilla in the same city.<br /> * The limitation of Elder and Methuselah power, which I don't necessarily AGREE with but makes for more exciting politics.<br /> * The rise of cults and hidden sect allegiance.<br /> * Cities now can have a lot more variety in their structure and makeup.<br /> <br /> I'm gonna be honest, yeah, a lot of my praise is, &quot;I think Requiem was always the better social game and V5 is now more like that.&quot; But it really was. However, it combines the best of V:TM with V:TR and the results are impressive.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Damian May</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1443592-the-official-v5-vs-v20-thread?p=1445248#post1445248\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Fully Agree.<br /> <br /> We gave up on ever going to Elysium in our games as the combination of MCs, BFs, Willpower Damage etc. made interactions with other vampires a losing proposition where social damage was certain, mental damage extremely likely and any plans you made could be randomly sidetracked when your nature betrayed you. If SPCs used the same rules as PCs the place would be a bloodbath every time.</div> </div> </div> </div>Really, I would have thought the Willpower benefits far outweigh the costs because if you can reroll a particularly bad dice in social situations you can avoid a lot of the horribly embarrassing situations you can in others.<br /> <br /> It's another reason I like the revision to combat as Willpower expenditures are great ways to make sure embarrassing failures are not going to disrupt the flow of a story.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Author of <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Cthulhu-Armageddon-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01KUOM7SI/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982844&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Cthulhu+Armageddon\" target=\"_blank\">Cthulhu Armageddon</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Teenage-Weredeer-Bright-Falls-Mysteries-ebook/dp/B075TTN2FN/ref=sr_1_2?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982717&amp;sr=1-2&amp;keywords=Weredeer#customerReviews\" target=\"_blank\">I was a Teenage Weredeer</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Straight-Outta-Fangton-Comedic-Vampire-ebook/dp/B01KNHICCC/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982774&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Straight+Outta+Fangton\" target=\"_blank\">Straight Outta Fangton</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Lucifers-Star-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01MDM9MCT/ref=mt_kindle?_encoding=UTF8&amp;me=&amp;qid=\" target=\"_blank\">Lucifer's Star</a>, </i>and the <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Rules-Supervillainy-Saga-Book-ebook/dp/B07MB89S33/\" target=\"_blank\">Supervillainy Saga</a>.</i><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":12002,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","user":"CTPhipps","date":". 04-22-2021, 01:06 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","name":"CTPhipps","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12002_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13933"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-04-22T10:08:51-07:00","id":1445284,"title":"","content":"If it's easy to become prince, becoming prince is worth a lot less; thats half the crux of v5. You can all get fancy titles but they all mean far less now than they did then. This is compounded further when there's no one dominant sect to hold a monopoly over everyone and if people don't like you then it's free and easy for them to junp ship. Everyone is so weak you really aught to just form a coterie/gang and declare your own barony through threat of violence if necessary.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":6}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25794-mywifeisscary","name":"MyWifeIsScary","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25794_2.png","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3711"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-04-22T10:15:39-07:00","id":1445288,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Chris24601</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1443592-the-official-v5-vs-v20-thread?p=1445266#post1445266\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Yeah, things like his repeated insistence that \u201cyou automatically lose Humanity when you kill in V20\u201d and his headcanon about how Viniculum worked oved the Lasombra thread it really does feel like Phipps\u2019 actual experience with V20 is rather superficial and/or based on someone\u2019s heavily homebrewed campaign.</div> </div> </div> </div>I confess to having made a couple of mistakes on the lore and if you think I have no credibility discussing issues, I'll drop out. I'll still moderate the thread.<br /> <br /> But let's just say I strongly disagree.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Chris24601</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">And part of it too is just a massive disconnect between people\u2019s definitions of horror and drama. For example, I consider the whole \u201clocked in a room with a child and starved until I lose control and feed\u201d to be neither horror (evoking fear or dread) nor dramatic (those involved must have some choice to make that affects the outcome). For me such a scene is what I\u2019d call \u201cmisery porn.\u201d</div> </div> </div> </div>I'll be honest, I think it basically boils down to your inability to engage with the material. This isn't your fault because you are aren't the player character in question and you aren't the one who agreed to the involvement in the game. Really, every table is different but if you agree to the game's themes and darkness ahead of time then you are willing to explore the darkness of the game.<br /> <br /> In this case, the effects of the event and the inspiring tabletop incident were roleplayed extensively out and had longlasting effects. It allowed us to explore issues of revenge, self-hatred, loathing, questioning the nature of whether the Kindred condition is something worth surviving or not or if it's better that they be wiped out completely. It was a dark, rich, and extremely well done campaign because we could do deal with the fact that the character could never atone or forgive himself for what had happened to himself. It alienated him from his fellow Kindred and informed a lot of really get moments.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Chris24601</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">And because my frame of reference is heroism and drama, if I were writing the same scene the protagonist would either find a way to escape with the child (a more heroic outcome) or, if wanting something more tragic, find a way to cripple or kill himself before Hunger would drive him to eat the child. Because just suffering until you give in doesn\u2019t make for an interesting protagonist to me. If I wanted misery porn I\u2019d just turn on the news.</div> </div> </div> </div>Being the player character rather than the Storyteller at this point and writing the scene with my Storyteller, the point of the scene is to emphasize that being a vampire is a horrifying curse. That it will compell you to do something unforgivable and nightmarish that cannot be forgiven or forgotten. I wanted to define the character by a moment that would certainly carry through other moments and deal with the consequences.<br /> <br /> In short, he didn't escape or rescue the girl because the scenario was designed by me<u> and</u> the Storyteller for him to be unable to. If he did, then there's nothing really for him to be tortured by. Gwen Stacy and Uncle Ben have to die.<br /> <br /> The ST was very good to work with me and I've since had a lot of really good use for my <b>Dark Personal Horror</b> campaigns where they deal with the terrible deeds they done and try to atone or live with the guilt.<br /> <br /> So I'll throw this back at you, &quot;How many innocent people have your PCs killed? Is the answer none? If so, are you really enjoying the full potential of being an antihero or villain protagonist? This isn't to everyone's tastes and I clear it with my players ahead of time but I've enjoyed roleplaying PCs who are murderers and guilty of horrible crimes because it makes the world more bleak.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Chris24601</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">And I don\u2019t play to be victimized by some force beyond my control; I play characters who fight to maintain control and not harm innocents. With its hunger dice only being completely mitigated by murder, the ONLY enjoyable vampire I could play in V5 is one who, upon learning what they are, took an immediate sunbath.</div> </div> </div> </div>I think this is definitely the best and most rewarding playstyle and certainly why killing an innocent has any meaning whatsoever. If your player character doesn't CARE when they kill an innocent then it's not going to have any dramatic tension or guilt whatsoever. However, I should note that Hunger 1 is being treated differently than the rules of V20.<br /> <br /> You're ALWAYS hungry as a vampire and that's what Hunger 1 represents. You will always be tempted by that extra bit of Blood and to kill unless you have killed for the Night. It is however very managable.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Author of <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Cthulhu-Armageddon-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01KUOM7SI/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982844&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Cthulhu+Armageddon\" target=\"_blank\">Cthulhu Armageddon</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Teenage-Weredeer-Bright-Falls-Mysteries-ebook/dp/B075TTN2FN/ref=sr_1_2?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982717&amp;sr=1-2&amp;keywords=Weredeer#customerReviews\" target=\"_blank\">I was a Teenage Weredeer</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Straight-Outta-Fangton-Comedic-Vampire-ebook/dp/B01KNHICCC/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982774&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Straight+Outta+Fangton\" target=\"_blank\">Straight Outta Fangton</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Lucifers-Star-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01MDM9MCT/ref=mt_kindle?_encoding=UTF8&amp;me=&amp;qid=\" target=\"_blank\">Lucifer's Star</a>, </i>and the <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Rules-Supervillainy-Saga-Book-ebook/dp/B07MB89S33/\" target=\"_blank\">Supervillainy Saga</a>.</i><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":12002,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","user":"CTPhipps","date":". 04-22-2021, 01:21 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","name":"CTPhipps","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12002_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13933"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-04-22T10:39:39-07:00","id":1445294,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MyWifeIsScary</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1443592-the-official-v5-vs-v20-thread?p=1445284#post1445284\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">If it's easy to become prince, becoming prince is worth a lot less; thats half the crux of v5. You can all get fancy titles but they all mean far less now than they did then. This is compounded further when there's no one dominant sect to hold a monopoly over everyone and if people don't like you then it's free and easy for them to junp ship. Everyone is so weak you really aught to just form a coterie/gang and declare your own barony through threat of violence if necessary.</div> </div> </div> </div>Unsurprisingly, disagree.<br /> <br /> 1. Being a Prince is still being able to enforce your will over the vampires of your city. Kevin Jackson is the most powerful Prince that has ever existed in Chicago because he has the Primogen under his thumb due to Critias' personality change and the loss of several members. Even so, he's still under Helena's control and if he ever wants to be the ruler that he could be then he has to get out from under that too (and that may be possible). Similarly, the Barons of LA are the most powerful because they've no longer got Christopher pulling their strings but have had to form a Council of Barons that means that they're more like a Primogen now.<br /> <br /> 2. The Camarilla used to enforce a free-travel between its states in the same way that Europe did before Brexit and as such a vampire could leave any city they had committed diablerie in or had a Blood Hunt without much difficulty. The Justicars were not keeping a list of every crime your chaarcters committed. Now there's no telling what sort of government exists in any given city and what sort of reception you'll receive when you arrive. Now plenty of Princes are going to just flat out say, &quot;No&quot; if they don't like you and you'll have to live on the outskirts or in defiance.<br /> <br /> 3. Travel is meant to be pretty hard in this setting with the Second Inquisition and usual troubles of moving around during the daytime. I recommend the V:TR supplement &quot;Nomads&quot; for a pretty good discussion of how to make travel between domains a hard rough struggle.<br /> <br /> 4. Taking over a Domain and Managing it feels like it's a lot more interesting as a prospect in V5 as well as &quot;realistic&quot; than in previous Editons. I'm currently running my first ongoing Prince Game and its working very well.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Author of <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Cthulhu-Armageddon-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01KUOM7SI/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982844&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Cthulhu+Armageddon\" target=\"_blank\">Cthulhu Armageddon</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Teenage-Weredeer-Bright-Falls-Mysteries-ebook/dp/B075TTN2FN/ref=sr_1_2?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982717&amp;sr=1-2&amp;keywords=Weredeer#customerReviews\" target=\"_blank\">I was a Teenage Weredeer</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Straight-Outta-Fangton-Comedic-Vampire-ebook/dp/B01KNHICCC/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982774&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Straight+Outta+Fangton\" target=\"_blank\">Straight Outta Fangton</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Lucifers-Star-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01MDM9MCT/ref=mt_kindle?_encoding=UTF8&amp;me=&amp;qid=\" target=\"_blank\">Lucifer's Star</a>, </i>and the <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Rules-Supervillainy-Saga-Book-ebook/dp/B07MB89S33/\" target=\"_blank\">Supervillainy Saga</a>.</i><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","name":"CTPhipps","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12002_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13933"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-04-22T11:05:23-07:00","id":1445297,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CTPhipps</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">I'm gonna be honest, yeah, a lot of my praise is, &quot;I think Requiem was always the better social game and V5 is now more like that.&quot; But it really was.</div> </div> </div> </div>This is the exact reason why V5 is bad in the first place. oWoD VTM and CofD VTR are supposed to be whole different styles of play, different mechanics, everything. Then when you try to take a bunch of stuff from the latter, but then keep a minutiae of things from the former, then you get things that SIMPLY don't mesh <i>at all</i>.<br /> <br /> From Blood Potency nonsensically being added despite Generation (now instead of intrigue and planning for a greater power ceiling through Diablerie, just wait it out);<br /> <br /> The removal of Perception, Charisma, and Appearance for: Resolve, Presence, Composure respectively (when it wasn't needed at all, essentially doing away with Attributes from oWoD and confirming that the rest of the other oWoD lines will be using CofD attributes);<br /> <br /> Capping Disciplines so now PCs or STNPCs from V20 and before aren't compatible, unless you just continue using the characters whilst only taking heed of V5's &quot;lore/meta updates&quot; (and basically in general, no fun allowed; along with the fact they probably scrapped Elders and above wholesale because of these changes they made);<br /> <br /> The whole Touchstone drama and destroying off the old Morality system. It could've just used some adjustments, but changing it for the Twilight Bella simulator wasn't good at all. And now you're telling me some theoretical 127 year old Sabbat Gangrel on the Path of the Feral Heart suddenly is or rather compelled to now have somesort of strange relation with some human due to forced mechanic? Even if they've been entirely absconded from caring about humanity at all and even before their embrace, was basically a loner?<br /> <br /> Putting two systems together that are very incompatible and achieves different things doesn't make sense at all. That's not imply some things can't be burrowed or influenced from the source, but when doing so, make sure it's actually adapted in a GOOD way; because even people who main and like VTR who view V5, don't even like how V5 has implemented inspirations from the former.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Jade Kingdom Warrior","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":7}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25523-shakanaka","name":"Shakanaka","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25523_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"951"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-04-22T11:59:07-07:00","id":1445303,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Shakanaka</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1443592-the-official-v5-vs-v20-thread?p=1445297#post1445297\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> This is the exact reason why V5 is different in ways which are not preferable to me in the first place.</div> </div> </div> </div>Just a suggestion","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24351-garygeneric","name":"Garygeneric","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24351_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"108"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-04-22T12:00:36-07:00","id":1445304,"title":"","content":"1. Anecdotal, and irrelevant to the point. <br /> 2. where does it say the cam allowed freedom of movement... ever? The cam follows the traditions, the prince can interpret all but one of them how he sees fit. If he doesn't like the way you've presented yourself, he's under no obligation to accept you. Hell he can even throw you in custody while he conducts a background check, and destroy you if he has an excuse (or not, if he has the power to get away with it)<br /> 3. Travel is something the book says is hard. sure. but is it actually hard when you think about it enough? no. Are the SI causing taffic as they search the motorways? not likely. <br /> 4. Thats pure conjecture. Back it up.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25794-mywifeisscary","name":"MyWifeIsScary","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25794_2.png","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3711"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-04-22T12:05:44-07:00","id":1445306,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MyWifeIsScary</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1443592-the-official-v5-vs-v20-thread?p=1445304#post1445304\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">1. Anecdotal, and irrelevant to the point.<br /> 2. where does it say the cam allowed freedom of movement... ever? The cam follows the traditions, the prince can interpret all but one of them how he sees fit. If he doesn't like the way you've presented yourself, he's under no obligation to accept you. Hell he can even throw you in custody while he conducts a background check, and destroy you if he has an excuse (or not, if he has the power to get away with it)<br /> 3. Travel is something the book says is hard. sure. but is it actually hard when you think about it enough? no. Are the SI causing taffic as they search the motorways? not likely.<br /> 4. Thats pure conjecture. Back it up.</div> </div> </div> </div>1. No, just showing that Princes are more powerful potentially.<br /> <br /> 2. Uh, because the Camarilla established a universal shared set of laws among Princes that were united under the Traditions. The Traditions are the agreed upon laws of the Camarilla and with them, you have to violate the Traditions to have the authority of destruction. The Camarilla also enforced the idea that all Kindred were part of the Camarilla and thus under its protection. Its not quite freedom of movement but its pretty damn close.<br /> <br /> 3. Depends on if they have car photos.<br /> <br /> 4. How would you like me to back it up? What would it take to convince you V5 is better in terms of Domain and running Princedoms. I want to know your criteria so I can prove it.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Author of <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Cthulhu-Armageddon-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01KUOM7SI/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982844&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Cthulhu+Armageddon\" target=\"_blank\">Cthulhu Armageddon</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Teenage-Weredeer-Bright-Falls-Mysteries-ebook/dp/B075TTN2FN/ref=sr_1_2?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982717&amp;sr=1-2&amp;keywords=Weredeer#customerReviews\" target=\"_blank\">I was a Teenage Weredeer</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Straight-Outta-Fangton-Comedic-Vampire-ebook/dp/B01KNHICCC/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982774&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Straight+Outta+Fangton\" target=\"_blank\">Straight Outta Fangton</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Lucifers-Star-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01MDM9MCT/ref=mt_kindle?_encoding=UTF8&amp;me=&amp;qid=\" target=\"_blank\">Lucifer's Star</a>, </i>and the <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Rules-Supervillainy-Saga-Book-ebook/dp/B07MB89S33/\" target=\"_blank\">Supervillainy Saga</a>.</i><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","name":"CTPhipps","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12002_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13933"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-04-22T12:10:47-07:00","id":1445307,"title":"","content":"To answer a question earlier:<br /> <br /> <u>Favorite V20</u><br /> <br /> <b>Beckett's Jyhad Diary</b>: I am spectacularly in love with this book and it may be my all-time favorite V:TM supplement ever, even more so than Chicago by Night 1st Edition. Compiling a massive amount of lore and updating characters ranging from Christof to Byzantium's Black Mary. This is a book I am absolutely in love with and I can't wait for the Werewolf 20 installment. At last we can learn the fate of Evan-Heals-The-Past! A character dying for an update!<br /> <br /> <u>Runner Up</u><br /> <br /> <b>Anarchs Unbound</b><br /> <br /> I mentioned I felt that Revised did the Anarchs dirty with the destruction of the Anarch Free States and the de-emphasizing of the sect for the sake of the Sabbat as well as Kuei-Jin. I like how they showed them as a powerful alternative sect opposed to the Camarilla. Also, I liked how they tied the Brujah Council to the Anarchs as well as the French Revolution. Good continuity.<br /> <br /> <u>Favorite V5</u><br /> <br /> <b>Chicago by Night</b><br /> <br /> Chicago by Night is where I think V5 had its course correction after making some serious mistakes to go along with the benefits of the Core book. In my opinion, Chicago By Night deserves kudos for the fact that it did what the others books failed to do and that's <i>illustrate how games are meant to be played</i>. Despite having two books on the subject, people didn't know how the Anarchs were supposed to act with the Camarilla, how the Princedom was handling, how many Elders were left, and so on. Chicago gave us an example and we're all grateful for it, I think. OPP deserves an award for it.<br /> <br /> Plus, I'm a huge Chicago junkie.<br /> <br /> <u>Runner Up</u><br /> <br /> <b>Let the Streets Run Red</b><br /> <br /> Just because it is an awesome set of flexible Chronicles and books that gives a real sense of how V5 cities run and could change under the new circumstances. Milwaukee's update to be a Camarilla police state and Gary's new Anarch domain.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Author of <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Cthulhu-Armageddon-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01KUOM7SI/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982844&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Cthulhu+Armageddon\" target=\"_blank\">Cthulhu Armageddon</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Teenage-Weredeer-Bright-Falls-Mysteries-ebook/dp/B075TTN2FN/ref=sr_1_2?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982717&amp;sr=1-2&amp;keywords=Weredeer#customerReviews\" target=\"_blank\">I was a Teenage Weredeer</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Straight-Outta-Fangton-Comedic-Vampire-ebook/dp/B01KNHICCC/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982774&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Straight+Outta+Fangton\" target=\"_blank\">Straight Outta Fangton</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Lucifers-Star-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01MDM9MCT/ref=mt_kindle?_encoding=UTF8&amp;me=&amp;qid=\" target=\"_blank\">Lucifer's Star</a>, </i>and the <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Rules-Supervillainy-Saga-Book-ebook/dp/B07MB89S33/\" target=\"_blank\">Supervillainy Saga</a>.</i><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","name":"CTPhipps","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12002_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13933"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-04-22T12:15:59-07:00","id":1445308,"title":"","content":"1- What does -canon character- have to do with the power and respect a player can gain as prince? Fact is, in V5, princes are weaker, and you've said nothing to refute that. <br /> 2- That's not freedom of movement. You're confused. <br /> 3- If they have car photos, you're not safe without traveling, nevermind traveling. <br /> 4- Like any convincing argument. Subjectively you might find the weaker power curve more interesting in terms of taking territory and holding it, but how can V5 be more &quot;Realistic&quot; than V20 in this aspect? Being more &quot;realistic&quot; is definitely not a strong suit of V5 after all, Note that &quot;magical realism&quot; is not realism.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25794-mywifeisscary","name":"MyWifeIsScary","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25794_2.png","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3711"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-04-22T12:28:17-07:00","id":1445311,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MyWifeIsScary</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1443592-the-official-v5-vs-v20-thread?p=1445308#post1445308\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">1- What does -canon character- have to do with the power and respect a player can gain as prince? Fact is, in V5, princes are weaker, and you've said nothing to refute that.<br /> 2- That's not freedom of movement. You're confused.<br /> 3- If they have car photos, you're not safe without traveling, nevermind traveling.<br /> 4- Like any convincing argument. Subjectively you might find the weaker power curve more interesting in terms of taking territory and holding it, but how can V5 be more &quot;Realistic&quot; than V20 in this aspect? Being more &quot;realistic&quot; is definitely not a strong suit of V5 after all, Note that &quot;magical realism&quot; is not realism.</div> </div> </div> </div>1. Except I've given an example and you have yet to provide a counter example. Name a canon Prince who is weaker. Otherwise you have no argument.<br /> <br /> 2. I disagree. Every Camarilla Kindred can petition a Prince for entering new territory and under the laws of the Traditons the Prince can refuse or not, Now it's much harder.<br /> <br /> 3. There's a lot of reasons why travel is difficult and they made an entire game about it in Night Road. But yes, it is possible to travel. Even then you have to make contact with the local power structure before acceptance.<br /> <br /> 4. Just checking what exactly you're looking for in an argument about better rules for running Domains.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Author of <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Cthulhu-Armageddon-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01KUOM7SI/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982844&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Cthulhu+Armageddon\" target=\"_blank\">Cthulhu Armageddon</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Teenage-Weredeer-Bright-Falls-Mysteries-ebook/dp/B075TTN2FN/ref=sr_1_2?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982717&amp;sr=1-2&amp;keywords=Weredeer#customerReviews\" target=\"_blank\">I was a Teenage Weredeer</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Straight-Outta-Fangton-Comedic-Vampire-ebook/dp/B01KNHICCC/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982774&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Straight+Outta+Fangton\" target=\"_blank\">Straight Outta Fangton</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Lucifers-Star-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01MDM9MCT/ref=mt_kindle?_encoding=UTF8&amp;me=&amp;qid=\" target=\"_blank\">Lucifer's Star</a>, </i>and the <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Rules-Supervillainy-Saga-Book-ebook/dp/B07MB89S33/\" target=\"_blank\">Supervillainy Saga</a>.</i><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","name":"CTPhipps","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12002_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13933"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-04-22T12:38:59-07:00","id":1445314,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Chris24601</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1443592-the-official-v5-vs-v20-thread?p=1445266#post1445266\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Yeah, things like his repeated insistence that \u201cyou automatically lose Humanity when you kill in V20\u201d.</div> </div> </div> </div>I only know this if you state that you are not feeling any remourse for your actions. Like saying you steel someone an important heirloom back that a scrupulous tax taker has taken with force or you killed a serial raper.<br /> Turned out RAW is saying you can even then do a conscience roll and if you succeed you either feel remorse or can justify your actions enough.<br /> It is even encouraged that the ST should modify the difficulty depending on the situation so that killing in self defense where you really got forced could have easily be only a dif 4 roll while ST could say too that every feeding where the person is not herself cutting her wrist and forces you into your mouth would be a Tier 7 wrongdoing.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>As I am from Austria I need to clarify two things.<br /> First my native language is german and so please point out if the english I write is broken so I can improve.<br /> Second I do not own VTMV beyond first three books nor any line after M20 Corebook because it is not out there and I wait for the translation.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26160-koronus","name":"Koronus","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2020"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"366"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-04-22T12:43:14-07:00","id":1445316,"title":"","content":"Hey guys with regards to point 1, you're not even having the same argument.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/9015-zee-patrick","name":"zee PaTrick","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"56"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-04-22T12:52:00-07:00","id":1445317,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Koronus</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1443592-the-official-v5-vs-v20-thread?p=1445314#post1445314\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I only know this if you state that you are not feeling any remourse for your actions. Like saying you steel someone an important heirloom back that a scrupulous tax taker has taken with force or you killed a serial raper.<br /> Turned out RAW is saying you can even then do a conscience roll and if you succeed you either feel remorse or can justify your actions enough.<br /> It is even encouraged that the ST should modify the difficulty depending on the situation so that killing in self defense where you really got forced could have easily be only a dif 4 roll while ST could say too that every feeding where the person is not herself cutting her wrist and forces you into your mouth would be a Tier 7 wrongdoing.</div> </div> </div> </div>I said that killing was an exceptionally harshly punished act in the system and that Conscience rolls were a poor substitute vs. Stains. I feel that Stains are more forgiving and work better for Humanity based stories.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Author of <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Cthulhu-Armageddon-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01KUOM7SI/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982844&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Cthulhu+Armageddon\" target=\"_blank\">Cthulhu Armageddon</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Teenage-Weredeer-Bright-Falls-Mysteries-ebook/dp/B075TTN2FN/ref=sr_1_2?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982717&amp;sr=1-2&amp;keywords=Weredeer#customerReviews\" target=\"_blank\">I was a Teenage Weredeer</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Straight-Outta-Fangton-Comedic-Vampire-ebook/dp/B01KNHICCC/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982774&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Straight+Outta+Fangton\" target=\"_blank\">Straight Outta Fangton</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Lucifers-Star-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01MDM9MCT/ref=mt_kindle?_encoding=UTF8&amp;me=&amp;qid=\" target=\"_blank\">Lucifer's Star</a>, </i>and the <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Rules-Supervillainy-Saga-Book-ebook/dp/B07MB89S33/\" target=\"_blank\">Supervillainy Saga</a>.</i><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","name":"CTPhipps","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12002_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13933"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-04-22T12:52:35-07:00","id":1445318,"title":"","content":"1: So our back and forth is like this: <br /> My argument: Princes are weaker because the Cam doesn't have a monopoly over vampires as a sect (the anarchs are strong) and the curve of power levels (No elder disciplines and such) is lower. <br /> Your argument: Kevin jackson is doing well. <br /> If this debate had a panel of judges, I don't imagine you'd be winning now. <br /> Also you've pointed out that in LA they're doing a council of barons which really... is a point in my favour is it not? One strong prince replaced by an alliance of lords. Being a prince is obviously on the downswing. <br /> <br /> 2. You're asking for a pass, a visa. That's not &quot;freedom of movement&quot;. Freedom of movement is when you waltz right in and never bother to visit &quot;the one who ruleth there&quot;. Now, perhaps, if you visit multiple cities to get your visas, you can travel between them without bothering the prince again, but you've still gotta collect your pass. <br /> <br /> 3. yes, contact with the local power structure before acceptance. What was that &quot;freedom of movement&quot; thing you were talking about again?. Real talk: the chance of you finding danger is pretty low, and in modern nights, you've got very easy access to excelent transportation. A walk from vegas to LA supposedly takes 93 hours, and... well, for vampires you could sprint without tiring but you've only got eight hours a day so... I don't want to calculate that; anyhow, a car drive takes four hours. You could do it in a night. <br /> <br /> 4: ?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":7}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25794-mywifeisscary","name":"MyWifeIsScary","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25794_2.png","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3711"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-04-22T13:12:31-07:00","id":1445322,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MyWifeIsScary</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1443592-the-official-v5-vs-v20-thread?p=1445318#post1445318\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">1: So our back and forth is like this:<br /> My argument: Princes are weaker because the Cam doesn't have a monopoly over vampires as a sect (the anarchs are strong) and the curve of power levels (No elder disciplines and such) is lower.<br /> Your argument: Kevin jackson is doing well.<br /> If this debate had a panel of judges, I don't imagine you'd be winning now.<br /> Also you've pointed out that in LA they're doing a council of barons which really... is a point in my favour is it not? One strong prince replaced by an alliance of lords. Being a prince is obviously on the downswing.</div> </div> </div> </div>Well your argument isn't exactly... an argument.<br /> <br /> The argument you present is the Camarilla had a monopoly over vampires except that was never actually the case except their dogma, which undermined them rather than other Clans. The Camarilla didn't have 4 Independent Clans, the Sabbat, and while they claimed the Anarchs as members--the Anarchs themselves were not likely to accept this. The Camarilla also undermined Princes by being able to remove them as well as execute their citizens. Princes now have much broader authority over their Domains due to the fact that they no longer have to tolerate Anarchs in their Domains or those without Camarilla representation.<br /> <br /> They are &quot;off the leash&quot; so to speak.<br /> <br /> Now would you please kindly provide EXAMPLES of your idea that Princes are weaker. Your dismissal is noted but Kevin Jackson is what we call EVIDENCE.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Author of <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Cthulhu-Armageddon-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01KUOM7SI/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982844&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Cthulhu+Armageddon\" target=\"_blank\">Cthulhu Armageddon</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Teenage-Weredeer-Bright-Falls-Mysteries-ebook/dp/B075TTN2FN/ref=sr_1_2?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982717&amp;sr=1-2&amp;keywords=Weredeer#customerReviews\" target=\"_blank\">I was a Teenage Weredeer</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Straight-Outta-Fangton-Comedic-Vampire-ebook/dp/B01KNHICCC/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982774&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Straight+Outta+Fangton\" target=\"_blank\">Straight Outta Fangton</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Lucifers-Star-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01MDM9MCT/ref=mt_kindle?_encoding=UTF8&amp;me=&amp;qid=\" target=\"_blank\">Lucifer's Star</a>, </i>and the <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Rules-Supervillainy-Saga-Book-ebook/dp/B07MB89S33/\" target=\"_blank\">Supervillainy Saga</a>.</i><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","name":"CTPhipps","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12002_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13933"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-04-22T14:00:09-07:00","id":1445330,"title":"","content":"My argument is based on logic; If the Camarilla is weaker, princes are going to be weaker. If elders are weaker, elder princes are going to be weaker.<br /> Truly, i doubt anyone would call KJ evidence. At the least, why's he stronger than he was in V20 (I don't read city books generally so maybe you'll have to point out he isn't a prince in V20 or something.) It's also a bit of a stretch to ask me to search for examples of princes in V5 suffering as a result of the sectarian and mechanical changes of v5... because it's a very &quot;have cake and eat it too&quot; kinda game. I might suggest that LA being lead by a confederation than an individual may be points for &quot;individuals are weaker in terms of political clout&quot; I mean, if you're Barron No.7 you're obviously not going to have the clout of the one-and-only prince.<br /> <br /> RE: Camarilla monopoly.<br /> The Brujah and Toreador together probably have more members than the six least populous clans combined, and the other five members of the original seven clans are all on the larger side of things. Anarchs might've lamented the camarilla, but they were members mostly too weak to throw off the rule of princes all the same. While exact details aren't given, by the 21st century the Camarilla would've been absolutely Dominant in the overwhelming majority of the Old World, with their main contenders being a few archaic holdouts rather than Sabbat (all in the new world) or Anarchs (princes are stronger in the old world)<br /> <br /> Ultimately though, it's on a local level that they have monopoly. What does it matter that Medina is Ashira? You' don't live in medina, you live in Cologne, where your choices of sect are Camarilla, Camarilla, Camarilla or the Inconnu if you're over three hundred, never diablerized, sixth gen or better. Even if you join the local Setite cult, you're still under Camarilla rule. Claiming you're an anarch is, in most places, like claiming you vote Green in national elections.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":25794,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25794-mywifeisscary","user":"MyWifeIsScary","date":". 04-22-2021, 05:03 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":7}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25794-mywifeisscary","name":"MyWifeIsScary","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25794_2.png","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3711"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-04-22T14:03:40-07:00","id":1445331,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MyWifeIsScary</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1443592-the-official-v5-vs-v20-thread?p=1445330#post1445330\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">My argument is based on logic; If the Camarilla is weaker, princes are going to be weaker.</div> </div> </div> </div>Let me refute that in one sentence: &quot;A Prince who answers to less people above them is stronger.&quot;<br /> <br /> The Camarilla has always been a check and binding on the behavior of Princes with the original Dark Ages princes being much stronger and more powerful than the ones that would come out of the Camarilla. A good example is Mithras in London. We're not talking V5 now but V12,3,20. Mithras HATED the Camarilla because he saw it as a massive impediment to ruling his domain the way he wanted to and removed his own Seneschal from power due to the fact that he swore the British Isles under their rule while he was in torpor.<br /> <br /> His ban on Tremere was also considered to be something that infuriated the Camarilla and broke their rules on passage.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> RE: Camarilla monopoly.<br /> The Brujah and Toreador together probably have more members than the six least populous clans combined, and the other five members of the original seven clans are all on the larger side of things. Anarchs might've lamented the camarilla, but they were members mostly too weak to throw off the rule of princes all the same. While exact details aren't given, by the 21st century the Camarilla would've been absolutely Dominant in the overwhelming majority of the Old World, with their main contenders being a few archaic holdouts rather than Sabbat (all in the new world) or Anarchs (princes are stronger in the old world)<br /> <br /> Ultimately though, it's on a local level that they have monopoly. What does it matter that Medina is Ashira? You' don't live in medina, you live in Cologne, where your choices of sect are Camarilla, Camarilla, Camarilla or the Inconnu if you're over three hundred, never diablerized, sixth gen or better. Even if you join the local Setite cult, you're still under Camarilla rule </div> </div> </div>One thing to note about the Camarilla in V20 is that its setting agnostic but by Revised, the Camarilla had already lost vast numbers of holdings. The Gangrel had already left by Revised and whatever your opinion was on that, it was not a decision of V5. Anarchs Unbound had also already established that the Anarchs were making large gains so V20 had begun the idea that the Anarchs were a sect separate from the Camarilla and actively seizing territory. The canonical ending of Bloodlines also had California retaken by the Anarchs.<br /> <br /> Even in editions other than V5, the Camarilla's monopoly was shrinking not growing. Possibly because the writers realized the Anarchs as loyal opposition didn't fit the characters or ideology.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Author of <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Cthulhu-Armageddon-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01KUOM7SI/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982844&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Cthulhu+Armageddon\" target=\"_blank\">Cthulhu Armageddon</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Teenage-Weredeer-Bright-Falls-Mysteries-ebook/dp/B075TTN2FN/ref=sr_1_2?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982717&amp;sr=1-2&amp;keywords=Weredeer#customerReviews\" target=\"_blank\">I was a Teenage Weredeer</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Straight-Outta-Fangton-Comedic-Vampire-ebook/dp/B01KNHICCC/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982774&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Straight+Outta+Fangton\" target=\"_blank\">Straight Outta Fangton</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Lucifers-Star-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01MDM9MCT/ref=mt_kindle?_encoding=UTF8&amp;me=&amp;qid=\" target=\"_blank\">Lucifer's Star</a>, </i>and the <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Rules-Supervillainy-Saga-Book-ebook/dp/B07MB89S33/\" target=\"_blank\">Supervillainy Saga</a>.</i><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":12002,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","user":"CTPhipps","date":". 04-22-2021, 05:11 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","name":"CTPhipps","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12002_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13933"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-04-22T15:01:58-07:00","id":1445348,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CTPhipps</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1443592-the-official-v5-vs-v20-thread?p=1445280#post1445280\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Really, I would have thought the Willpower benefits far outweigh the costs because if you can reroll a particularly bad dice in social situations you can avoid a lot of the horribly embarrassing situations you can in others.<br /> <br /> It's another reason I like the revision to combat as Willpower expenditures are great ways to make sure embarrassing failures are not going to disrupt the flow of a story.</div> </div> </div> </div>I'm talking specifically about Elysium here where social combat is inevitable as you attempt to negotiate with other Kindred. Remember there are on average 5-6 Willpower points in V5 and as you said you need those to reroll, however you are extremely likely to end up Impaired at which point you don't have anything to reroll with. And if you've already used one or two of your Willpower for rerolls already then your absolutely guaranteed to hit Impaired and be basically useless at anything for quite some time.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":479,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/479-damian-may","user":"Damian May","date":". 04-22-2021, 08:14 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/479-damian-may","name":"Damian May","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar479_1.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1199"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-04-22T15:12:55-07:00","id":1445352,"title":"","content":"<u>Oops, forgot to do this:</u><br /> <br /> <u>Favorite V20</u><br /> <br /> <b>V20 Corebook</b><br /> <br /> <u>Runner Up</u><br /> <br /> <b>Lore of the Bloodlines</b><br /> <br /> <u>Favorite V5</u><br /> <br /> <b>V5 Companion- it was free? <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /></b><br /> <br /> <u>Runner Up</u><br /> <br /> <b>There is no runner up. ( Perhaps Chicago by Night? If I had any use for a city book, which I don't. It was well written and seems to have viscerally offended a large swathe of the more aggresive V5 fans by existing).</b><br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":479,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/479-damian-may","user":"Damian May","date":". 04-22-2021, 06:21 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/479-damian-may","name":"Damian May","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar479_1.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1199"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-04-22T15:28:24-07:00","id":1445356,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Damian May</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1443592-the-official-v5-vs-v20-thread?p=1445352#post1445352\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><u>Runner Up</u><br /> <br /> <b>There is no runner up. ( Perhaps Chicago by Night? If I had any use for a city book, which I don't. It was well written and seems to have viscerally offended a large swathe of the more aggresive V5 fans by existing).</b></div> </div> </div> </div>I know a lot of gamers who viscerally hated Chicago by Night 5th Edition for having Lasombra detailed within. They not only didn't want to buy a city book, they HATED THE CONCEPT OF CITY BOOKS and were angered that non-city book information was inside so they'd have to buy it.<br /> <br /> I didn't win any friends by saying, &quot;So what you're saying is it was a good marketing decision.&quot;","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Author of <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Cthulhu-Armageddon-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01KUOM7SI/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982844&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Cthulhu+Armageddon\" target=\"_blank\">Cthulhu Armageddon</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Teenage-Weredeer-Bright-Falls-Mysteries-ebook/dp/B075TTN2FN/ref=sr_1_2?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982717&amp;sr=1-2&amp;keywords=Weredeer#customerReviews\" target=\"_blank\">I was a Teenage Weredeer</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Straight-Outta-Fangton-Comedic-Vampire-ebook/dp/B01KNHICCC/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982774&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Straight+Outta+Fangton\" target=\"_blank\">Straight Outta Fangton</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Lucifers-Star-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01MDM9MCT/ref=mt_kindle?_encoding=UTF8&amp;me=&amp;qid=\" target=\"_blank\">Lucifer's Star</a>, </i>and the <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Rules-Supervillainy-Saga-Book-ebook/dp/B07MB89S33/\" target=\"_blank\">Supervillainy Saga</a>.</i><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","name":"CTPhipps","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12002_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13933"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-04-22T15:51:37-07:00","id":1445358,"title":"","content":"Yikes, you get some sleep and go do some adult things and boom the thread goes all over the place.<br /> <br /> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar12002_2.jpeg');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"12002\" data-vbnamecard=\"12002\">CTPhipps</a> <br /> <br /> On the whole &quot;credibility&quot; thing? I think part of the problem is that you are not phrasing things as strongly as you could to differentiate between &quot;what's said in the books,&quot; &quot;what I think the books are trying to say,&quot; and, &quot;how I would do things.&quot; I feels like you're leaving way too much to subtext to be clear in a fashion that works in a purely text-based (and an especially mutlifaceted) discussion.<br /> <br /> It does not help that, even when the text is directly cited to you, you have a habit of not responding to the correction. I don't just mean things like, &quot;oh, thanks I misremembered that,&quot; but also not incorporating that into further discussion. I cited multiple editions of VtM on how homicide is treated by the Humanity system pre-V5 as not being what you said it was, and later, you changed your wording slightly, but still made a statement largely holding to the same point that pre-V5 Humanity is very harsh with killing people (even though it has a wide range of responses to killing people depending on the circumstances).<br /> <br /> At a certain point &quot;no matter how many times I make mistakes about what the books actually say, and it gets cited at me, but I still hold that the evidence is in my favor,&quot; gets frustrating. It makes it very hard to have the discussion you want this to be.<br /> <br /> --------------------<br /> <br /> On the &quot;power of Princes&quot; thing:<br /> <br /> I think there's a big disconnect over the vague concept of power. Pre-V5, Princes were not the top of the ladder, because the Camarilla above them could boss them around (and that's true in most of the Sects with whatever names they use for things). But that also meant they had more practical power as a trade in that they could call on Camarilla resources if necessary. &quot;Hey, I have a serious Sabbat problem here, if you want this city to stay in our hands, send me some heavy hitters,&quot; is nothing to scoff at in terms of what having power means. V5 Princes have more freedom with a weaker Camarilla oversight, which is another form of power, but one that's coming at the cost of another.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":8}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-04-22T15:55:10-07:00","id":1445359,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Heavy Arms</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1443592-the-official-v5-vs-v20-thread?p=1445358#post1445358\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Yikes, you get some sleep and go do some adult things and boom the thread goes all over the place.<br /> <br /> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar12002_2.jpeg');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"12002\" data-vbnamecard=\"12002\">CTPhipps</a><br /> <br /> On the whole &quot;credibility&quot; thing? I think part of the problem is that you are not phrasing things as strongly as you could to differentiate between &quot;what's said in the books,&quot; &quot;what I think the books are trying to say,&quot; and, &quot;how I would do things.&quot; I feels like you're leaving way too much to subtext to be clear in a fashion that works in a purely text-based (and an especially mutlifaceted) discussion.<br /> <br /> <b>It does not help that, even when the text is directly cited to you, you have a habit of not responding to the correction. I don't just mean things like, &quot;oh, thanks I misremembered that,&quot; but also not incorporating that into further discussion. I cited multiple editions of VtM on how homicide is treated by the Humanity system pre-V5 as not being what you said it was, and later, you changed your wording slightly, but still made a statement largely holding to the same point that pre-V5 Humanity is very harsh with killing people (even though it has a wide range of responses to killing people depending on the circumstances).</b><br /> <br /> At a certain point &quot;no matter how many times I make mistakes about what the books actually say, and it gets cited at me, but I still hold that the evidence is in my favor,&quot; gets frustrating. It makes it very hard to have the discussion you want this to be.<br /> <br /> --------------------<br /> <br /> On the &quot;power of Princes&quot; thing:<br /> <br /> I think there's a big disconnect over the vague concept of power. Pre-V5, Princes were not the top of the ladder, because the Camarilla above them could boss them around (and that's true in most of the Sects with whatever names they use for things). But that also meant they had more practical power as a trade in that they could call on Camarilla resources if necessary. &quot;Hey, I have a serious Sabbat problem here, if you want this city to stay in our hands, send me some heavy hitters,&quot; is nothing to scoff at in terms of what having power means. V5 Princes have more freedom with a weaker Camarilla oversight, which is another form of power, but one that's coming at the cost of another.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Thank you for explaining all the Humanity points, though. I stand corrected. I should have mentioned that earlier.<br /> <br /> I'm actually worried about this because the thread is moving so incredibly fast and I can't respond to everything before it moves on. It doesn't help that there doesn't seem to be that many V5 fans participating so it feels like I'm responding to several posters at once.<br /> <br /> Shame.<br /> <br /> It seems like I'm going to have to drop out soon in fact because I don't have the time to partcipate in this thread as well as doing my other posts. I do appreciate everyone who has participated in this thread and I'm sure there's plenty of other people who will carry on this delightful discussion.<br /> <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Author of <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Cthulhu-Armageddon-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01KUOM7SI/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982844&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Cthulhu+Armageddon\" target=\"_blank\">Cthulhu Armageddon</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Teenage-Weredeer-Bright-Falls-Mysteries-ebook/dp/B075TTN2FN/ref=sr_1_2?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982717&amp;sr=1-2&amp;keywords=Weredeer#customerReviews\" target=\"_blank\">I was a Teenage Weredeer</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Straight-Outta-Fangton-Comedic-Vampire-ebook/dp/B01KNHICCC/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982774&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Straight+Outta+Fangton\" target=\"_blank\">Straight Outta Fangton</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Lucifers-Star-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01MDM9MCT/ref=mt_kindle?_encoding=UTF8&amp;me=&amp;qid=\" target=\"_blank\">Lucifer's Star</a>, </i>and the <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Rules-Supervillainy-Saga-Book-ebook/dp/B07MB89S33/\" target=\"_blank\">Supervillainy Saga</a>.</i><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","name":"CTPhipps","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12002_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13933"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-04-22T16:12:10-07:00","id":1445362,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CTPhipps</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1443592-the-official-v5-vs-v20-thread?p=1445356#post1445356\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I know a lot of gamers who viscerally hated Chicago by Night 5th Edition for having Lasombra detailed within. They not only didn't want to buy a city book, they HATED THE CONCEPT OF CITY BOOKS and were angered that non-city book information was inside so they'd have to buy it.<br /> <br /> I didn't win any friends by saying, &amp;quot;So what you're saying is it was a good marketing decision.&amp;quot;</div> </div> </div> </div>Seriously they hate city books so much that they are pissed that non city content is in a city book? As a german Shadowrun fan* this would be awesome and if I would be Methuselah or Syndicate rich I would finance that every state and their capital would get a region book.<br /> <br /> <br /> *DACHL and US diffef from world building. In US you are used to tell what is the big meta situation and how would a standard city look like with mayby one big showrunner that regulary get updates and descriptions if you do not want to do everything yourself. In DACHL you get instead only descriptions about Meta Situations if the event is big enough for the whole country to be affected and instead mostly you got more and regular bits of information of your local hub so you have many different small local playpoints that differ so for everyone is something there.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>As I am from Austria I need to clarify two things.<br /> First my native language is german and so please point out if the english I write is broken so I can improve.<br /> Second I do not own VTMV beyond first three books nor any line after M20 Corebook because it is not out there and I wait for the translation.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26160-koronus","name":"Koronus","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2020"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"366"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-04-22T16:12:40-07:00","id":1445363,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CTPhipps</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1443592-the-official-v5-vs-v20-thread?p=1445356#post1445356\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I know a lot of gamers who viscerally hated Chicago by Night 5th Edition for having Lasombra detailed within. They not only didn't want to buy a city book, they HATED THE CONCEPT OF CITY BOOKS and were angered that non-city book information was inside so they'd have to buy it.<br /> <br /> I didn't win any friends by saying, &quot;So what you're saying is it was a good marketing decision.&quot;</div> </div> </div> </div>I like the Chicago by Night book (and the other Onyx Path productions), but I think the main issue with the Lasombra inclusion in it was that they weren\u2019t also detailed in an official core book too. They were included in Chicago by Night mainly because of the chronicle outlined within. They were mooted to be included in the Vampire Player\u2019s Guide but it wasn\u2019t released, with the Vampire Companion a hint of what could have been included. Right now, I think having a Sabbat book - where Lasombra are detailed again from the perspective of loyalists, Tzmisce (and possibly the Ravnos as a new inclusion? Why not?) it would mean that all the 13 Clans are fully in print somewhere.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2517-trippy","name":"Trippy","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2517_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1018"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-04-22T16:17:13-07:00","id":1445366,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Trippy</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1443592-the-official-v5-vs-v20-thread?p=1445363#post1445363\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I like the Chicago by Night book (and the other Onyx Path productions), but I think the main issue with the Lasombra inclusion in it was that they weren\u2019t also detailed in an official core book too. They were included in Chicago by Night mainly because of the chronicle outlined within. They were mooted to be included in the Vampire Player\u2019s Guide but it wasn\u2019t released, with the Vampire Companion a hint of what could have been included. Right now, I think having a Sabbat book - where Lasombra are detailed again from the perspective of loyalists, Tzmisce (and possibly the Ravnos as a new inclusion? Why not?) it would mean that all the 13 Clans are fully in print somewhere.</div> </div> </div> </div>I don't think they should use space to republish rules that could be used for other material but I do want them to assemble all the Companion information into a new Players Guide someday, even though I'm pretty sure the Companion is just what Modiphius wrote for it already.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Author of <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Cthulhu-Armageddon-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01KUOM7SI/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982844&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Cthulhu+Armageddon\" target=\"_blank\">Cthulhu Armageddon</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Teenage-Weredeer-Bright-Falls-Mysteries-ebook/dp/B075TTN2FN/ref=sr_1_2?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982717&amp;sr=1-2&amp;keywords=Weredeer#customerReviews\" target=\"_blank\">I was a Teenage Weredeer</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Straight-Outta-Fangton-Comedic-Vampire-ebook/dp/B01KNHICCC/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982774&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Straight+Outta+Fangton\" target=\"_blank\">Straight Outta Fangton</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Lucifers-Star-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01MDM9MCT/ref=mt_kindle?_encoding=UTF8&amp;me=&amp;qid=\" target=\"_blank\">Lucifer's Star</a>, </i>and the <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Rules-Supervillainy-Saga-Book-ebook/dp/B07MB89S33/\" target=\"_blank\">Supervillainy Saga</a>.</i><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","name":"CTPhipps","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12002_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13933"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-04-22T16:17:51-07:00","id":1445367,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Damian May</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">Remember there are only 5 Willpower points in V5</div> </div> </div> </div>They capped Willpower only to 5 in V5? WTF","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Jade Kingdom Warrior","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25523-shakanaka","name":"Shakanaka","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25523_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"951"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-04-22T16:18:53-07:00","id":1445369,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Shakanaka</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1443592-the-official-v5-vs-v20-thread?p=1445367#post1445367\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> They capped Willpower only to 5 in V5? WTF</div> </div> </div> </div>That is explictly not true. The Willpower number on the character sheet is 10.<br /> <br /> A character\u2019s maximum Willpower rating equals their Composure + Resolve. You cannot raise Willpower with EXP but you can by raising your Composure or Resolve, thus saving EXP and making your Willpower benefit your overall control and courage.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Author of <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Cthulhu-Armageddon-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01KUOM7SI/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982844&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Cthulhu+Armageddon\" target=\"_blank\">Cthulhu Armageddon</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Teenage-Weredeer-Bright-Falls-Mysteries-ebook/dp/B075TTN2FN/ref=sr_1_2?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982717&amp;sr=1-2&amp;keywords=Weredeer#customerReviews\" target=\"_blank\">I was a Teenage Weredeer</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Straight-Outta-Fangton-Comedic-Vampire-ebook/dp/B01KNHICCC/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982774&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Straight+Outta+Fangton\" target=\"_blank\">Straight Outta Fangton</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Lucifers-Star-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01MDM9MCT/ref=mt_kindle?_encoding=UTF8&amp;me=&amp;qid=\" target=\"_blank\">Lucifer's Star</a>, </i>and the <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Rules-Supervillainy-Saga-Book-ebook/dp/B07MB89S33/\" target=\"_blank\">Supervillainy Saga</a>.</i><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":12002,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","user":"CTPhipps","date":". 04-22-2021, 07:21 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","name":"CTPhipps","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12002_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13933"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-04-22T16:25:12-07:00","id":1445371,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Shakanaka</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1443592-the-official-v5-vs-v20-thread?p=1445367#post1445367\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> They capped Willpower only to 5 in V5? WTF</div> </div> </div> </div>Willpower doesn\u2019t cap at 5 in V5. It is generally scaled 1-10 (calculated by Composure + Resolve), although it could theoretically go higher.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2517-trippy","name":"Trippy","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2517_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1018"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-04-22T16:32:52-07:00","id":1445373,"title":"","content":"My Wish List for V5 is:<br /> <br /> * More rules for Predator Types Rules<br /> * More rules for Convictions, both gaining and changing<br /> * Elder Discipline Rules to replace the old ones<br /> * The Sabbat book<br /> * The Second Inquisition Book<br /> * A Fall of Vienna Chronicle book<br /> * A Council of Prague Chronicle<br /> * A Chronicle book updating DC, Berlin, New York, and Los Angeles<br /> * A Players Handbook that includes the Companion, Hecata, and Lasombra rules<br /> <br /> I pitched a Chicago Novel Trilogy to Jason Carl written by me but he didn't take it.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Author of <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Cthulhu-Armageddon-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01KUOM7SI/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982844&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Cthulhu+Armageddon\" target=\"_blank\">Cthulhu Armageddon</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Teenage-Weredeer-Bright-Falls-Mysteries-ebook/dp/B075TTN2FN/ref=sr_1_2?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982717&amp;sr=1-2&amp;keywords=Weredeer#customerReviews\" target=\"_blank\">I was a Teenage Weredeer</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Straight-Outta-Fangton-Comedic-Vampire-ebook/dp/B01KNHICCC/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982774&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Straight+Outta+Fangton\" target=\"_blank\">Straight Outta Fangton</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Lucifers-Star-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01MDM9MCT/ref=mt_kindle?_encoding=UTF8&amp;me=&amp;qid=\" target=\"_blank\">Lucifer's Star</a>, </i>and the <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Rules-Supervillainy-Saga-Book-ebook/dp/B07MB89S33/\" target=\"_blank\">Supervillainy Saga</a>.</i><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":12002,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","user":"CTPhipps","date":". 09-21-2021, 09:12 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","name":"CTPhipps","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12002_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13933"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-04-22T16:45:33-07:00","id":1445374,"title":"","content":"V5 Willpower is equal to your Resolve + Composure, which means it starts between 3 and 7, with 5 or 6 being the most likely range (putting your one 4 in either is a lot for the more &quot;passive&quot; Attributes, but most people aren't going to be their 1 in something that important either).<br /> <br /> I'm not sure where the &quot;capped at 5&quot; thing came from, but I know in previous discussions about the V5 advanced social conflict rules, 5 was frequently used as the &quot;minimum&quot; damage because that's 1 success on the roll to socially attack, and +4 from being in front of a major figure like the Prince. The idea of starting with 5 WP and facing 5 WP damage in Elysium was a quick shorthand for why a lot of us don't like the impact of that specific subsystem on vampire social life.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-04-22T16:52:44-07:00","id":1445376,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CTPhipps</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1443592-the-official-v5-vs-v20-thread?p=1445373#post1445373\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">My Wish List for V5 is:<br /> <br /> * More rules for Predator Types Rules<br /> * More rules for Convictions, both gaining and changing<br /> * Elder Discipline Rules to replace the old ones<br /> * The Sabbat book<br /> * The Second Inquisition Book<br /> * A Fall of Vienna Chronicle book<br /> * A Council of Prague Chronicle<br /> * A Chronicle book updating DC, Berlin, New York, and Los Angeles<br /> * A Players Handbook that includes the Companion, Hecate, and Lasombra rules<br /> <br /> I pitched a Chicago Novel Trilogy to Jason Carl written by me but he didn't take it.</div> </div> </div> </div>The Sabbat book is already on the way, apparently, and it would be pretty awful if The Second Inquisition isn\u2019t also because it is such a core development in the game as it is.<br /> <br /> If they did a Players Guide, then they could indeed include all the extra Clans, and possibly some more Bloodlines, along with more Predator Types, Convictions, Elder rules, etc. It would essentially be a book of advanced rules, I think - and I believe it could be very popular.<br /> <br /> A Fall of Vienna Chronicle would be awesome and, to be honest, I would only be interested in Chronicle or City-based material after the core rules have been established. Indeed, what could be an idea is publishing some mini-chronicles (30 pages or so) or some more character-based story books - maybe to replace the type of thing we used to get at the back of the old splatbooks.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":2517,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2517-trippy","user":"Trippy","date":". 04-22-2021, 08:00 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2517-trippy","name":"Trippy","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2517_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1018"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-04-22T17:11:42-07:00","id":1445379,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CTPhipps</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1443592-the-official-v5-vs-v20-thread?p=1445356#post1445356\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I know a lot of gamers who viscerally hated Chicago by Night 5th Edition for having Lasombra detailed within. They not only didn't want to buy a city book, they HATED THE CONCEPT OF CITY BOOKS and were angered that non-city book information was inside so they'd have to buy it.<br /> <br /> I didn't win any friends by saying, &quot;So what you're saying is it was a good marketing decision.&quot;</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> The ones that I've run into mostly hate it for &quot; rolling back&quot; V5 to &quot; cater to older fans&quot;.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/479-damian-may","name":"Damian May","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar479_1.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1199"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-04-22T17:13:23-07:00","id":1445380,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Heavy Arms</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1443592-the-official-v5-vs-v20-thread?p=1445374#post1445374\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">V5 Willpower is equal to your Resolve + Composure, which means it starts between 3 and 7, with 5 or 6 being the most likely range (putting your one 4 in either is a lot for the more &quot;passive&quot; Attributes, but most people aren't going to be their 1 in something that important either).<br /> <br /> I'm not sure where the &quot;capped at 5&quot; thing came from, but I know in previous discussions about the V5 advanced social conflict rules, 5 was frequently used as the &quot;minimum&quot; damage because that's 1 success on the roll to socially attack, and +4 from being in front of a major figure like the Prince. The idea of starting with 5 WP and facing 5 WP damage in Elysium was a quick shorthand for why a lot of us don't like the impact of that specific subsystem on vampire social life.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Yeah, my fault for shorthanding. have edited.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/479-damian-may","name":"Damian May","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar479_1.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1199"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-04-22T17:19:03-07:00","id":1445382,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Damian May</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1443592-the-official-v5-vs-v20-thread?p=1445379#post1445379\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The ones that I've run into mostly hate it for &quot; rolling back&quot; V5 to &quot; cater to older fans&quot;.</div> </div> </div> </div>Weird, I've not encountered a single V5 fan who didn't love it except for the &quot;forcing you to buy it&quot; aspect.<br /> <br /> I certainly think it did clarify a lot of the changes to be less extreme but hadn't ever seen any complaints about such.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Author of <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Cthulhu-Armageddon-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01KUOM7SI/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982844&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Cthulhu+Armageddon\" target=\"_blank\">Cthulhu Armageddon</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Teenage-Weredeer-Bright-Falls-Mysteries-ebook/dp/B075TTN2FN/ref=sr_1_2?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982717&amp;sr=1-2&amp;keywords=Weredeer#customerReviews\" target=\"_blank\">I was a Teenage Weredeer</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Straight-Outta-Fangton-Comedic-Vampire-ebook/dp/B01KNHICCC/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982774&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Straight+Outta+Fangton\" target=\"_blank\">Straight Outta Fangton</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Lucifers-Star-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01MDM9MCT/ref=mt_kindle?_encoding=UTF8&amp;me=&amp;qid=\" target=\"_blank\">Lucifer's Star</a>, </i>and the <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Rules-Supervillainy-Saga-Book-ebook/dp/B07MB89S33/\" target=\"_blank\">Supervillainy Saga</a>.</i><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","name":"CTPhipps","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12002_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13933"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-04-22T17:25:41-07:00","id":1445383,"title":"","content":"I\u2019ve not encountered any hatred for V5 Chicago by Night. V5, yes (too much!), but not the Onyx Path supplements.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2517-trippy","name":"Trippy","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2517_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1018"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-04-22T17:31:15-07:00","id":1445386,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CTPhipps</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1443592-the-official-v5-vs-v20-thread?p=1445382#post1445382\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Weird, I've not encountered a single V5 fan who didn't love it except for the &quot;forcing you to buy it&quot; aspect.<br /> <br /> I certainly think it did clarify a lot of the changes to be less extreme but hadn't ever seen any complaints about such.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Are you on reddit much? Its pretty common there.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/479-damian-may","name":"Damian May","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar479_1.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1199"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-04-22T17:42:32-07:00","id":1445388,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Damian May</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1443592-the-official-v5-vs-v20-thread?p=1445386#post1445386\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Are you on reddit much? Its pretty common there.</div> </div> </div> </div>The White Wolf reddit.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Author of <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Cthulhu-Armageddon-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01KUOM7SI/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982844&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Cthulhu+Armageddon\" target=\"_blank\">Cthulhu Armageddon</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Teenage-Weredeer-Bright-Falls-Mysteries-ebook/dp/B075TTN2FN/ref=sr_1_2?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982717&amp;sr=1-2&amp;keywords=Weredeer#customerReviews\" target=\"_blank\">I was a Teenage Weredeer</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Straight-Outta-Fangton-Comedic-Vampire-ebook/dp/B01KNHICCC/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982774&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Straight+Outta+Fangton\" target=\"_blank\">Straight Outta Fangton</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Lucifers-Star-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01MDM9MCT/ref=mt_kindle?_encoding=UTF8&amp;me=&amp;qid=\" target=\"_blank\">Lucifer's Star</a>, </i>and the <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Rules-Supervillainy-Saga-Book-ebook/dp/B07MB89S33/\" target=\"_blank\">Supervillainy Saga</a>.</i><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","name":"CTPhipps","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12002_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13933"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-04-22T20:56:24-07:00","id":1445409,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CTPhipps</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1443592-the-official-v5-vs-v20-thread?p=1445388#post1445388\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> The White Wolf reddit.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Maybe we just read different threads? Theres a bunch of &quot; OPP ruined V5 &quot; posters active there that I butt heads with.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/479-damian-may","name":"Damian May","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar479_1.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1199"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-04-22T21:00:16-07:00","id":1445412,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Damian May</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1443592-the-official-v5-vs-v20-thread?p=1445409#post1445409\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Maybe we just read different threads? Theres a bunch of &quot; OPP ruined V5 &quot; posters active there that I butt heads with.</div> </div> </div> </div>Wow, makes no sense to me.<br /> <br /> OPP is the best pony.<br /> <br /> I suppose there's no end of fans with dramatically different tastes.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Author of <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Cthulhu-Armageddon-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01KUOM7SI/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982844&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Cthulhu+Armageddon\" target=\"_blank\">Cthulhu Armageddon</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Teenage-Weredeer-Bright-Falls-Mysteries-ebook/dp/B075TTN2FN/ref=sr_1_2?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982717&amp;sr=1-2&amp;keywords=Weredeer#customerReviews\" target=\"_blank\">I was a Teenage Weredeer</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Straight-Outta-Fangton-Comedic-Vampire-ebook/dp/B01KNHICCC/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982774&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Straight+Outta+Fangton\" target=\"_blank\">Straight Outta Fangton</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Lucifers-Star-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01MDM9MCT/ref=mt_kindle?_encoding=UTF8&amp;me=&amp;qid=\" target=\"_blank\">Lucifer's Star</a>, </i>and the <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Rules-Supervillainy-Saga-Book-ebook/dp/B07MB89S33/\" target=\"_blank\">Supervillainy Saga</a>.</i><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","name":"CTPhipps","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12002_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13933"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-04-22T21:44:29-07:00","id":1445422,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Damian May</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1443592-the-official-v5-vs-v20-thread?p=1445409#post1445409\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> Maybe we just read different threads? Theres a bunch of &quot; OPP ruined V5 &quot; posters active there that I butt heads with.</div> </div> </div> </div>I\u2019ve not seen them, but I can\u2019t even fathom the mentality. OPP don\u2019t produce V5 - only some supplements. From everything I\u2019ve seen, they\u2019ve all been well received.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2517-trippy","name":"Trippy","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2517_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1018"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-04-22T21:52:44-07:00","id":1445425,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Trippy</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1443592-the-official-v5-vs-v20-thread?p=1445422#post1445422\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I\u2019ve not seen them, but I can\u2019t even fathom the mentality. OPP don\u2019t produce V5 - only some supplements. From everything I\u2019ve seen, they\u2019ve all been well received.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> I think its more that OPP V5 books are seen as ' walking back' V5s setting to be more like previous VtM settings. It mostly seems to be centred around CbN but there is a fair bit of the same sentiment regarding CotBG and the Companion.<br /> <br /> I can't really relate to them personally as I pretty much ignore all the V5 metaplot changes in my V20 games anyway.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/479-damian-may","name":"Damian May","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar479_1.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1199"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-04-22T21:56:52-07:00","id":1445426,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Damian May</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1443592-the-official-v5-vs-v20-thread?p=1445425#post1445425\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> I think its more that OPP V5 books are seen as ' walking back' V5s setting to be more like previous VtM settings. It mostly seems to be centred around CbN but there is a fair bit of the same sentiment regarding CotBG and the Companion.<br /> <br /> I can't really relate to them personally as I pretty much ignore all the V5 metaplot changes in my V20 games anyway.</div> </div> </div> </div>Well, I just see that as a misconception on what V5 was doing. V5 was always written as a starting point, or a re-callibration, for the line to be built on. The OPP supplements do that.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2517-trippy","name":"Trippy","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2517_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1018"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-04-22T23:48:58-07:00","id":1445441,"title":"","content":"Thing is, Camarilla oversight has always been very lax, in part because they own too much territory. They would rarely stoop to bother a prince (and in most cases, that's going to be on a personal mission rather than something the inner circle agreed on). There's no rules saying mithras needs to have Tremere, the Tremere are just using the Camarilla as high-ground to bother mithras about it. So long as you don't break the masquerade or show off your Gehenna cults, the Cam can at most send strongly worded letters (or send resources to your opposition) <br /> <br /> In V5, it's very likely the Camarilla is actually going to be more overbearing to it's princes. They don't own that much territory and they're in a state of crisis; a period in which the consolidation of power is expected. The only consolation is that Methuselahs are weaker now.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":6}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25794-mywifeisscary","name":"MyWifeIsScary","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25794_2.png","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3711"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-04-23T02:15:51-07:00","id":1445450,"title":"","content":"Ok, many things going on and a very heated discussion. I won't address all the topics that have shown up but will go with my take. My background is the one of someone that has read and played a bit of V20, later run the V5 Chicago by Night setting for a while as a ST and currently playing a Berlin by Night Campaign with a Ministry PC.<br /> <br /> Writting this I realized the V5 Companion errata addresses or reinforces some of what is being questioned, so kudos for them!<br /> <br /> Personal Horror: I love the hunger dice and what they accomplish:<ul><li>You cannot calculate how many times you can rely on powers, relying to them is a temptation that may come to a cost. On Blood Surges, this has been reinforced with the V5 Companion errata</li> <li>You are always hungry unless you kill. That mostly means, as mentioned before, that you will be mostly always hungry. You are a Vampire after all.</li> <li>And yes, that single die may cause catastrophic damage. This means that yes, you are playing a vampire, and even the nicest of vampires cannot escape the curse. This does NOT mean you are to Frenzy in every roll, and you can still play the cool vampire. Hunger, Rage, Clan compulsions, Messy Crits... are for you to play out or the ST to decide.</li> <li>Players unable to keep their cool: as an example, my PC made his final argument in a tense political conversation doing a manipulation roll that Messy Critted. The ST decreed Hunger Compulsion. My PC took, as a remark of his arguments, a vessel to dance and feed. The target of my machinations joined and fed on the same vessel as well. The scene called for some eerie waltz music to start playing and the camera to zoom out while the two vampires nearly drained their victim. Hey, a Messy Crit turned a mostly &quot;cool&quot; attitude into a &quot;larger than life cool&quot; attitude. Of course, when leaving the room, my PC discreetly called a retainer and urged him to call a doctor.</li> </ul>All the possible outcomes from such rolls need both the player and ST to &quot;read the room&quot; to decide for the most appropriate one, whether to shake the whole scene or reinforce it as dramatically appropriate. To me, they are not a bug but a feature. They can boost the history and enhance the themes. I understand some players may not like it and keep the control at any time on both resources and PC behavior, but to me making them juggle constantly with their beasts is a benefit. After all, this is a vampire game.<br /> <br /> Political Horror:<ul><li>I guess depends on your campaign. If you want to play an elder's game you'll struggle. V20 may work better.</li> <li>If you want to play Neonates or Ancilla though... Princes have Absolute power in their cities, they need to reinforce it more ruthlessly, both at the &quot;play nice&quot; and &quot;make them fear you&quot; levels to keep it since they are not so old, and Ancilla and Neonate players are in the game. There is still a lot of power to get, but more dynamism. To me, this benefits political games, doesn't hinder them.</li> <li>We haven't played by the Social Conflict rules so not much to say there, but to my understanding, they do nothing else but add tension to whatever is at stake, including the PCs themselves. That calls itself for Political Horror as well.</li> </ul>So, in my opinion V5 boosts this &quot;vampiriness&quot;, and I can understand that the ones that don't want the system to get in their way doesn't like it. I personally do.<br /> <br /> On Blood potency, I like that higher generation vampires are not stuck on a power level and age can make them stronger - to a point. Also I like how the higher Blood Potency levels make Elders much more powerful rather than neonates rather than higher disciplines. I am not fan of the 5 powers per discipline restriction though, and I think it would need to be balanced with higher BP granting more powers, but that is a minor complain.<br /> <br /> About ease of travel, movement and many other stuff... I find it is very relative to the interpretations of the setting. I might be wrong, but to me, it depends more on ST interpretation than system per se.<br /> <br /> My favorite V20 books:<ul><li>The Core book</li> <li>Anarchs Unbound</li> <li>The Black Hand: A Guide to the Tal\u2019Mahe\u2019Ra</li> </ul>My favorite V5 books:<ul><li>The Core book</li> <li>Chicago By Night</li> <li>Cults of the Blood Goods</li> <li>V5 Companion, with some cool ideas, although I take it more as a completion of the core book (that is, Companion :P)</li> </ul>Oh, and one last thing... I feel that in this thread there are more V20 defenders than V5 because... V5 are just happy with what they've got. We may like V20 and not feel like criticizing it because it is a cool setting and rules. In my case, I just like the changes introduced with V5.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":17974,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/17974-strangelove","user":"Strangelove","date":". 04-23-2021, 05:20 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/17974-strangelove","name":"Strangelove","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar17974_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"56"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-04-23T10:39:12-07:00","id":1445493,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Strangelove</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1443592-the-official-v5-vs-v20-thread?p=1445450#post1445450\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">[/LIST]Oh, and one last thing... I feel that in this thread there are more V20 defenders than V5 because... V5 are just happy with what they've got. We may like V20 and not feel like criticizing it because it is a cool setting and rules. In my case, I just like the changes introduced with V5.</div> </div> </div> </div>While that's a point one should consider, I also remember that when I first got into VTM i wanted to tell everybody about it, and a lot of people had that experience. Surely you should rant and rave about how great the game is, and yet few do that with V5. Furthermore for everybody who cares enough to go on the forums there's hundreds who are as passionate that don't for a variety of reasons; real people to talk to, general forum aversion, or perhaps they don't feel like, or don't know how to effectively articulate their points of views. There are also lots of little reasons why you might not like one game as much as another.<br /> <br /> Say, for a lot of reasons Fallout NV is seen as better than Fallout 3, but Fallout 3 was more popular and I enjoyed it more.. and I'm fairly sure it's 90% because the way exploration is paced. NV has better writing, a better story, you can aim down the sights... but the map is difficult (the other 10% is cazadors) . V5 has so many small issues with it, like the overchoice of disciplines; not many people are going to realize why it's worse, but they're going to have less fun working with that. A lot of factions are opened up in V5, but a lot can be said for overcoming difficulties. <br /> It's never good to believe that there's a &quot;silent majority&quot; out there that support your ideas. But critically speaking, V5 has a lot more problems than V20, Some big, some small, but unless you're hooked on the hunger die and fluctuating willpower (honestly the latter's a good feature) it's just not as mindblowingly Caine-damned awesome as prior edition.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":6}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25794-mywifeisscary","name":"MyWifeIsScary","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25794_2.png","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3711"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-04-23T14:15:46-07:00","id":1445540,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MyWifeIsScary</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1443592-the-official-v5-vs-v20-thread?p=1445493#post1445493\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">While that's a point one should consider, I also remember that when I first got into VTM i wanted to tell everybody about it, and a lot of people had that experience. Surely you should rant and rave about how great the game is, and yet few do that with V5. Furthermore for everybody who cares enough to go on the forums there's hundreds who are as passionate that don't for a variety of reasons; real people to talk to, general forum aversion, or perhaps they don't feel like, or don't know how to effectively articulate their points of views. There are also lots of little reasons why you might not like one game as much as another.<br /> <br /> Say, for a lot of reasons Fallout NV is seen as better than Fallout 3, but Fallout 3 was more popular and I enjoyed it more.. and I'm fairly sure it's 90% because the way exploration is paced. NV has better writing, a better story, you can aim down the sights... but the map is difficult (the other 10% is cazadors) . V5 has so many small issues with it, like the overchoice of disciplines; not many people are going to realize why it's worse, but they're going to have less fun working with that. A lot of factions are opened up in V5, but a lot can be said for overcoming difficulties.<br /> It's never good to believe that there's a &quot;silent majority&quot; out there that support your ideas. But critically speaking, V5 has a lot more problems than V20, Some big, some small, but unless you're hooked on the hunger die and fluctuating willpower (honestly the latter's a good feature) it's just not as mindblowingly Caine-damned awesome as prior edition.</div> </div> </div> </div>There are plenty of people who speak enthusiastically about V5. They don\u2019t necessarily congregate around these forums, but I can account for that insofar that its not the most welcoming experience to express your enthusiasm for a game when you may get dog-piled by detractors. The various communities generally end up being self selected. Personally, most of my V5 discussions occur on the V5 Facebook page, where most fans are...fans. <br /> <br /> It\u2019s not a phenomena that is unusual to Vampire either. There are loads of self named \u201cgrognards\u201d who reject Mongoose\u2019s Traveller or \u2018OSR\u2019 D&amp;D players who reject 5E. It doesn\u2019t mean that both aren\u2019t successful, well designed games though. Back in the day, there were big \u2018flame wars\u2019 regarding the transition of WoD games from 2nd edition to Revised. It is not a new phenomena or exclusive to any particular edition.<br /> <br /> And I reject the notion that V5 has \u2018a lot more problems\u2019. I think it is a substantially better and more focussed design than V20 - which we have all discussed before.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":2517,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2517-trippy","user":"Trippy","date":". 04-23-2021, 05:22 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2517-trippy","name":"Trippy","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2517_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1018"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-04-23T15:25:38-07:00","id":1445554,"title":"","content":"<b>V5 Pros</b><br /> Bestial Failures and Messy Criticals are very fun new mechanics that are fun to roleplay.<br /> Compulsions are fun to roleplay, and provide a vast improvement over the old black and white, frenzy or fine mechanics.<br /> <br /> They also more accurately portray how vampires seem to lose control in fiction, where they visably lose it, but rarely go completely berzerk. As I post in another thread, Jerry Dandrige's behavior in the nightclub perfectly fits into the Bestial Failure and Messy Critical system, not the Frenzy-or-Nothing system.<br /> <br /> It fits in with Barlow's behavior in &quot;Salem's Lot&quot; as well, where he can't resist executing his servant very cruelly over one mistake, despite immediately thereafter calling him the best servant he's ever had. There's a definite &quot;I should have let that slide. Why couldn't I let that slide?&quot; vibe of regret to that part of his letter. This is just a wonderfully inventive mechanic for portraying the lack of self-control various fictional vampires possess.<br /> ----------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------<br /> Combat is much faster and cleaner. One roll per round instead of four. And no picking out all the damned 1's.<br /> ----------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------<br /> <br /> Animalism and Fortitude are vastly improved. Animalism used to be garbage after level 2. I always hated that it didn't give you more power over swarms of beasts after level 2, when ever increasing control over swarms of beasts is the whole reason I wanted Animalism in the first place.<br /> <br /> Fortitude now has cool powers that allow you to either duplicate the living-statue nature of old Anne Ricepires and Twilightpires, or the berzerker ferocity of the more animalistic vampires. Huge improvement over a handful of bland and waayyy overpriced for their usefulness soak dice.<br /> <b>----------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------</b><br /> <br /> <b>V5 Cons</b><br /> You blew up lots of institutions and characters I didn't want blown up. I liked visiting the great halls of power in vampire. It was kind of like playing superhero video games and visiting Stark Tower, and the JLA Hall of Justice and the Hall of Doom and Arkham Asylum. You blew up Mexico City and Montreal and a great many NPCs I liked meeting. I can't express how much that angered me without a stream of curses and rude gestures. And I don't for the life of me understand why. It's not like their existence interfered with games in local cities. They just provided a cool richness to the world at large.<br /> <br /> <br /> ----------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------<br /> <br /> <br /> Mooning over Bella Swans. I hate human touchstones. I hate them with a passion. They make my skin crawl. Every time I'm forced to interact with them I want to kill them in such a cruel manner that even a Tzimisce would be taken aback.<br /> <br /> ----------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------<br /> <br /> <br /> The absence of Paths of Enlightenment. Without the Long Road Out of Hell homebrew, I would have had no means of running/playing Paths of Enlightenment. I adore Paths of Enlightenment. They allow for truly varied character types, instead of every single character being the Louis/Night Knight type, just with a different powerset.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":3598,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3598-cajunkhan","user":"CajunKhan","date":". 04-23-2021, 06:27 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3598-cajunkhan","name":"CajunKhan","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3598_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1700"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-04-23T15:37:56-07:00","id":1445557,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CajunKhan</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">You blew up lots of institutions and characters I didn't want blown up. I liked visiting the great halls of power in vampire. It was kind of like playing superhero video games and visiting Stark Tower, and the JLA Hall of Justice and the Hall of Doom and Arkham Asylum. You blew up Mexico City and Montreal and a great many NPCs I liked meeting. I can't express how much that angered me without a stream of curses and rude gestures. And I don't for the life of me understand why. It's not like their existence interfered with games in local cities. They just provided a cool richness to the world at large</div> </div> </div> </div>We actually have answers for this and they're kind of hilarious.<br /> <br /> 1. <b>Mexico City </b>has a thriving Vampire: The Masquerade Spanish language LARP and gaming community that don't like playing Sabbat or their hometown as discount Mordor.<br /> <br /> 2. <b>Montreal </b>was picked as the setting for CHAPTERS by the creators....in Montreal. That wanted to do a Camarilla game.<br /> <br /> Its pretty much the same reason that Kuei-Jin are in trouble. The locals of a lot of these places include World of Darkness fans but they don't want to play as the exotic weird guys.<br /> <br /> They're playing Alliance not Horde.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Author of <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Cthulhu-Armageddon-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01KUOM7SI/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982844&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Cthulhu+Armageddon\" target=\"_blank\">Cthulhu Armageddon</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Teenage-Weredeer-Bright-Falls-Mysteries-ebook/dp/B075TTN2FN/ref=sr_1_2?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982717&amp;sr=1-2&amp;keywords=Weredeer#customerReviews\" target=\"_blank\">I was a Teenage Weredeer</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Straight-Outta-Fangton-Comedic-Vampire-ebook/dp/B01KNHICCC/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982774&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Straight+Outta+Fangton\" target=\"_blank\">Straight Outta Fangton</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Lucifers-Star-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01MDM9MCT/ref=mt_kindle?_encoding=UTF8&amp;me=&amp;qid=\" target=\"_blank\">Lucifer's Star</a>, </i>and the <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Rules-Supervillainy-Saga-Book-ebook/dp/B07MB89S33/\" target=\"_blank\">Supervillainy Saga</a>.</i><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","name":"CTPhipps","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12002_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13933"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-04-23T15:40:25-07:00","id":1445558,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Strangelove</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1443592-the-official-v5-vs-v20-thread?p=1445450#post1445450\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">You are a Vampire after all.<br /> ...<br /> After all, this is a vampire game.<br /> ...<br /> So, in my opinion V5 boosts this &quot;vampiriness&quot;, and I can understand that the ones that don't want the system to get in their way doesn't like it. I personally do.</div> </div> </div> </div>I'm sure you don't intend it, but this is probably one of the biggest sources of negative feelings from the V20 camp towards the V5 camp: the attitude that those of us that have playing VtM and other games with vampires in them that aren't close to what V5 does, haven't been playing &quot;real&quot; vampire games. This whole way of phrasing the conversation tends to raise hackles because you, again giving you the benefit of the doubt that you don't mean to come off this way, are basically saying that in my near 25 years of playing vampires in RPGs, I don't appreciate what a &quot;vampire game&quot; should actually be because I don't like the specific way V5 does vampires.<br /> <br /> I hope you can see how off-putting that can be when seen from the other side of it.<br /> <br /> Vampires are fictional creatures. Of thousands of years they've seen countless variations in different mythologies and folklore. Even in pop-culture there is a huge range of what vampires are, what they do, what dominates their concerns, and what narrative point their creators are trying to make. Blade or Morbius are two very different vampire stories (as much as one can sum up comic books as stories like that), but they're both vampire stories. There is no platonic ideal of vampires to appeal to when saying &quot;this is good because you're playing a vampire,&quot; or, &quot;this makes the game more vampire-like.&quot;<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Oh, and one last thing... I feel that in this thread there are more V20 defenders than V5 because... V5 are just happy with what they've got. We may like V20 and not feel like criticizing it because it is a cool setting and rules. In my case, I just like the changes introduced with V5. </div> </div> </div>As someone that's been rather involved in the discussions around V5 here since they started, I think there's a somewhat rosy picture of history.<br /> <br /> When V5 was announced, and first few playtests were out, things felt rather the opposite. V5 was all the hype, expressing negativity about it put you firmly in the minority in most threads; though the flames were plenty heated and I'm sure lots of people just avoided those threads on both sides. Plenty of us felt like it was turning from the VtM forum into the V5 forum. Then the core dropped. Then the Cam and Anarch books dropped. That's when the mood of this forum started swinging towards where it is now. There were some very serious V5 supporters that jumped back to V20 during that period here as a sign of, at least on this forum, the reaction wasn't so positive once the product got in people's hands.<br /> <br /> Lots of V5 posters here spent a lot of time actively posting about how much better V5 is; not just &quot;being happy with what they got.&quot; It's just that after the hype settled, these forums settled more on the V20 side than the V5 side, and that's colored discussions since.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":8}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-04-23T15:50:40-07:00","id":1445561,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Heavy Arms</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1443592-the-official-v5-vs-v20-thread?p=1445558#post1445558\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I'm sure you don't intend it, but this is probably one of the biggest sources of negative feelings from the V20 camp towards the V5 camp: the attitude that those of us that have playing VtM and other games with vampires in them that aren't close to what V5 does, haven't been playing &quot;real&quot; vampire games. This whole way of phrasing the conversation tends to raise hackles because you, again giving you the benefit of the doubt that you don't mean to come off this way, are basically saying that in my near 25 years of playing vampires in RPGs, I don't appreciate what a &quot;vampire game&quot; should actually be because I don't like the specific way V5 does vampires.</div> </div> </div> </div>I find this doubly ironic since the reverse is usually encountered.<br /> <br /> &quot;V5 isn't REALLY Vampire: The Masquerade. It's too different. It's an alternate universe!&quot; is an expression I've heard far too many times.<br /> <br /> As if I don't know what real V:TM is.<br /> <br /> It's also ridiculous as it should be one community with different preferences.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Heavy Arms</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1443592-the-official-v5-vs-v20-thread?p=1445558#post1445558\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Lots of V5 posters here spent a lot of time actively posting about how much better V5 is; not just &quot;being happy with what they got.&quot; It's just that after the hype settled, these forums settled more on the V20 side than the V5 side, and that's colored discussions since.</div> </div> </div> </div>As guilty as I am for feeling like V5 needs defending, I do think that everyone should be able to play the game they want.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Author of <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Cthulhu-Armageddon-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01KUOM7SI/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982844&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Cthulhu+Armageddon\" target=\"_blank\">Cthulhu Armageddon</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Teenage-Weredeer-Bright-Falls-Mysteries-ebook/dp/B075TTN2FN/ref=sr_1_2?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982717&amp;sr=1-2&amp;keywords=Weredeer#customerReviews\" target=\"_blank\">I was a Teenage Weredeer</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Straight-Outta-Fangton-Comedic-Vampire-ebook/dp/B01KNHICCC/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982774&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Straight+Outta+Fangton\" target=\"_blank\">Straight Outta Fangton</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Lucifers-Star-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01MDM9MCT/ref=mt_kindle?_encoding=UTF8&amp;me=&amp;qid=\" target=\"_blank\">Lucifer's Star</a>, </i>and the <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Rules-Supervillainy-Saga-Book-ebook/dp/B07MB89S33/\" target=\"_blank\">Supervillainy Saga</a>.</i><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","name":"CTPhipps","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12002_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13933"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-04-23T16:14:15-07:00","id":1445564,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CTPhipps</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1443592-the-official-v5-vs-v20-thread?p=1445557#post1445557\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> We actually have answers for this and they're kind of hilarious.<br /> <br /> 1. <b>Mexico City </b>has a thriving Vampire: The Masquerade Spanish language LARP and gaming community that don't like playing Sabbat or their hometown as discount Mordor.<br /> <br /> 2. <b>Montreal </b>was picked as the setting for CHAPTERS by the creators....in Montreal. That wanted to do a Camarilla game.<br /> <br /> Its pretty much the same reason that Kuei-Jin are in trouble. The locals of a lot of these places include World of Darkness fans but they don't want to play as the exotic weird guys.<br /> <br /> They're playing Alliance not Horde.</div> </div> </div> </div>So <b>THAT'S </b>it?? The Cammies are the majority in real life, so they also get to completely conquer the WOD in the gameverse? Just when I thought I couldn't possibly hate the Cammies more than I already do. Reminds me of one of the early LARPs I was in, when the Sabbat were on the verge of conquering New Orleans, and the guys running the game just declared that they didn't envision the Sabbat winning, and weren't going to allow us to do it. All the work we had spent all game converting people to Paths, getting them to see how much better unlife would be as Sabbat, undone by God fiat.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":3598,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3598-cajunkhan","user":"CajunKhan","date":". 04-23-2021, 07:36 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":8}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3598-cajunkhan","name":"CajunKhan","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3598_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1700"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-04-23T16:19:26-07:00","id":1445565,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CajunKhan</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1443592-the-official-v5-vs-v20-thread?p=1445564#post1445564\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> So <b>THAT'S </b>it?? The Cammies are the majority in real life, so they also get to completely conquer the WOD in the gameverse? Just when I thought I couldn't possibly hate the Cammies more than I already do. Reminds me of one of the early LARPs I was in, when the Sabbat were on the verge of conquering the city, and the guys running the game just declared that they didn't envision the Sabbat winning, and weren't going to allow us to do it. All the work we had spent all game converting people to Paths, getting them to see how much better unlife would be as Sabbat, undone by God fiat.</div> </div> </div> </div>I'm not even extrapolating. The Montreal Chapters guys said that that why they did it and looked forward to updating the setting to something similar to what they played an interview. The Mexico thing I heard from a developer.<br /> <br /> And yes, basically the reason that the Camarilla is in Tokyo is because there's WOD fans there too playing Camarilla.<br /> <br /> That does sound lame, though. The least they could do is make the city contested.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Author of <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Cthulhu-Armageddon-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01KUOM7SI/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982844&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Cthulhu+Armageddon\" target=\"_blank\">Cthulhu Armageddon</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Teenage-Weredeer-Bright-Falls-Mysteries-ebook/dp/B075TTN2FN/ref=sr_1_2?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982717&amp;sr=1-2&amp;keywords=Weredeer#customerReviews\" target=\"_blank\">I was a Teenage Weredeer</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Straight-Outta-Fangton-Comedic-Vampire-ebook/dp/B01KNHICCC/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982774&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Straight+Outta+Fangton\" target=\"_blank\">Straight Outta Fangton</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Lucifers-Star-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01MDM9MCT/ref=mt_kindle?_encoding=UTF8&amp;me=&amp;qid=\" target=\"_blank\">Lucifer's Star</a>, </i>and the <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Rules-Supervillainy-Saga-Book-ebook/dp/B07MB89S33/\" target=\"_blank\">Supervillainy Saga</a>.</i><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":12002,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","user":"CTPhipps","date":". 04-23-2021, 07:24 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","name":"CTPhipps","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12002_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13933"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-04-23T16:27:56-07:00","id":1445568,"title":"","content":"Well then they should give the Sabbat Houma and Thibodaux, if they are giving cities to the vampire characters of the humans who play there. Heck, give us Terrebone Parish, since it's basically one city pretending to be a bunch of little towns. It's not a lot, but at least we would have our own canon territories again.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":3598,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3598-cajunkhan","user":"CajunKhan","date":". 04-23-2021, 08:12 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3598-cajunkhan","name":"CajunKhan","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3598_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1700"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-04-23T16:37:54-07:00","id":1445571,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CajunKhan</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1443592-the-official-v5-vs-v20-thread?p=1445568#post1445568\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Well then they should give the Sabbat Houma and Thibodaux, if they are giving cities to the vampire characters of the humans who play there. It's not a lot, but at least we would have our own canon territories again.</div> </div> </div> </div>V5 afficiciando that I am, I still have the Sabbat control Miami, Saint Louis, Baltimore, and Detroit.<br /> <br /> In one of the weirdest digressions I've made, I imagined them like the Fortress Worlds from the Old West End Game Star Wars' Expanded Universe. Places where the Sabbat are still in charge and the leaders deny that it is suffering ANY collapse or failures.<br /> <br /> Big Brother says that there's victory on all fronts!","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Author of <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Cthulhu-Armageddon-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01KUOM7SI/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982844&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Cthulhu+Armageddon\" target=\"_blank\">Cthulhu Armageddon</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Teenage-Weredeer-Bright-Falls-Mysteries-ebook/dp/B075TTN2FN/ref=sr_1_2?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982717&amp;sr=1-2&amp;keywords=Weredeer#customerReviews\" target=\"_blank\">I was a Teenage Weredeer</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Straight-Outta-Fangton-Comedic-Vampire-ebook/dp/B01KNHICCC/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982774&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Straight+Outta+Fangton\" target=\"_blank\">Straight Outta Fangton</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Lucifers-Star-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01MDM9MCT/ref=mt_kindle?_encoding=UTF8&amp;me=&amp;qid=\" target=\"_blank\">Lucifer's Star</a>, </i>and the <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Rules-Supervillainy-Saga-Book-ebook/dp/B07MB89S33/\" target=\"_blank\">Supervillainy Saga</a>.</i><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","name":"CTPhipps","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12002_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13933"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-04-23T17:43:05-07:00","id":1445574,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Strangelove</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1443592-the-official-v5-vs-v20-thread?p=1445450#post1445450\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">[*]You are always hungry unless you kill. That mostly means, as mentioned before, that you will be mostly always hungry. You are a Vampire after all.<br /> (...)<br /> On Blood potency, I like that higher generation vampires are not stuck on a power level and age can make them stronger - to a point. Also I like how the higher Blood Potency levels make Elders much more powerful rather than neonates rather than higher disciplines. I am not fan of the 5 powers per discipline restriction though, and I think it would need to be balanced with higher BP granting more powers, but that is a minor complain.</div> </div> </div> </div>I just quote those things that I have a gripe with and the easiest answer would be that I should stay a V20.<br /> <br /> Well first my problem is less the endless hunger but more why should it be only fixed when killing.<br /> Mayby here shows my mage solution where my PC where the blood donor for his TL Tremere GF but it should possible to either fill the first with enough drinking or that no matter how much you drink you will always feel thirsty. For example one vampire would drink a person only mayby just half empty and then calls ambulance and run away.<br /> Meanwhile the half dead person will get drunken empty by a vampire with even bigger hunger and this vampire is suddenly saturated? Or for example because of an event the cainite is suddenly the only (un)living person in a room and everyone is dead. From what I understood the vampire would not get saturated because he did not killed any person despite there are like 100 fresh dead persons. I mean what big difference is there if he drinks empty the poor guy that whas just shot in the head and get drunken empty and being shout in heart/stomach/neck and is getting drained while still being alive? This is just alogical which has nothing to do with how much can you saturate blood and more like the beast force you to kill while beasts should care about if they are getting enough feed.<br /> <br /> About the second personally I am not a big fan from this change because it whas a big difference to Requiem, that you can only get mightier with eating souls or other heinous acts then just waiting to get older and needing to stay awake. I am not a fan either that it limits you in what feed you.<br /> <br /> Honestly I repeat myself but with all this big changes from my opinion they should have rather just created a second spin off like Vampire The Inquisition or Vampire The Hunger because in V5 the Masquerade whas a broken and from my opinion V5 masquerades more as VtM.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>As I am from Austria I need to clarify two things.<br /> First my native language is german and so please point out if the english I write is broken so I can improve.<br /> Second I do not own VTMV beyond first three books nor any line after M20 Corebook because it is not out there and I wait for the translation.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26160-koronus","name":"Koronus","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2020"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"366"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-04-23T17:57:58-07:00","id":1445576,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Koronus</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1443592-the-official-v5-vs-v20-thread?p=1445574#post1445574\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I just quote those things that I have a gripe with and the easiest answer would be that I should stay a V20.<br /> <br /> Well first my problem is less the endless hunger but more why should it be only fixed when killing.<br /> Mayby here shows my mage solution where my PC where the blood donor for his TL Tremere GF but it should possible to either fill the first with enough drinking or that no matter how much you drink you will always feel thirsty. For example one vampire would drink a person only mayby just half empty and then calls ambulance and run away.<br /> Meanwhile the half dead person will get drunken empty by a vampire with even bigger hunger and this vampire is suddenly saturated? Or for example because of an event the cainite is suddenly the only (un)living person in a room and everyone is dead. From what I understood the vampire would not get saturated because he did not killed any person despite there are like 100 fresh dead persons. I mean what big difference is there if he drinks empty the poor guy that whas just shot in the head and get drunken empty and being shout in heart/stomach/neck and is getting drained while still being alive? This is just alogical which has nothing to do with how much can you saturate blood and more like the beast force you to kill while beasts should care about if they are getting enough feed.<br /> <br /> About the second personally I am not a big fan from this change because it whas a big difference to Requiem, that you can only get mightier with eating souls or other heinous acts then just waiting to get older and needing to stay awake. I am not a fan either that it limits you in what feed you.<br /> <br /> Honestly I repeat myself but with all this big changes from my opinion they should have rather just created a second spin off like Vampire The Inquisition or Vampire The Hunger because in V5 the Masquerade whas a broken and from my opinion V5 masquerades more as VtM.</div> </div> </div> </div>My view is that it isn't supposed to be logical, but rather magical. Vampires are the child of murder-incarnate. Caine's curse was to embody murder in all things. He can only create children by murdering them, and feeding them blood he got by murdering someone else. His children can commit murder-beyond-murder on each other, and are constantly tempted by the power of doing so. Giving in to their urge to murder gradually murders their own soul. So it makes mystical sense that they can only satiate their hunger fully by committing murder.<br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3598-cajunkhan","name":"CajunKhan","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3598_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1700"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-04-23T18:03:31-07:00","id":1445577,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CTPhipps</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1443592-the-official-v5-vs-v20-thread?p=1445561#post1445561\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I find this doubly ironic since the reverse is usually encountered.</div> </div> </div> </div>I'm not sure it's ironic at all. The idea that there are phrases on both sides that tend to set the other side's emotions on edge is fairly usual with any divisive issue (hell it happens all the time even in far less contentious settings).<br /> <br /> V20 fans are perfectly capable of phrasing things in ways that get under V5 fans' skin too. That's not irony that just.. human.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> &quot;V5 isn't REALLY Vampire: The Masquerade. It's too different. It's an alternate universe!&quot; is an expression I've heard far too many times. </div> </div> </div>I don't particularly like this thing either. I'd like to think it's one I've generally avoided using personally; mostly because I'm a bigger fan of VtR than VtM, and VtR got hit with all sorts of this sort of thing.<br /> <br /> However, I do think these are meaningfully different in terms of what's being expressed even if not so different in how annoying the phrasing is.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> It's also ridiculous as it should be one community with different preferences. </div> </div> </div>The problem is that it feels like a lot of those preferences get expressed to the point of seeming to be mutually incompatible. Should it be one community? I don't know really. Should implies things I'm not sure about. It could be one community with different preferences, but I'm not sure enough stakeholders are invested in that outcome to naturally generate it in current conditions.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":6}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-04-23T18:03:42-07:00","id":1445578,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Koronus</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1443592-the-official-v5-vs-v20-thread?p=1445574#post1445574\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I just quote those things that I have a gripe with and the easiest answer would be that I should stay a V20.<br /> <br /> Well first my problem is less the endless hunger but more why should it be only fixed when killing.<br /> Mayby here shows my mage solution where my PC where the blood donor for his TL Tremere GF but it should possible to either fill the first with enough drinking or that no matter how much you drink you will always feel thirsty. For example one vampire would drink a person only mayby just half empty and then calls ambulance and run away.<br /> Meanwhile the half dead person will get drunken empty by a vampire with even bigger hunger and this vampire is suddenly saturated? Or for example because of an event the cainite is suddenly the only (un)living person in a room and everyone is dead. From what I understood the vampire would not get saturated because he did not killed any person despite there are like 100 fresh dead persons. I mean what big difference is there if he drinks empty the poor guy that whas just shot in the head and get drunken empty and being shout in heart/stomach/neck and is getting drained while still being alive? This is just alogical which has nothing to do with how much can you saturate blood and more like the beast force you to kill while beasts should care about if they are getting enough feed.<br /> <br /> About the second personally I am not a big fan from this change because it whas a big difference to Requiem, that you can only get mightier with eating souls or other heinous acts then just waiting to get older and needing to stay awake. I am not a fan either that it limits you in what feed you.<br /> <br /> Honestly I repeat myself but with all this big changes from my opinion they should have rather just created a second spin off like Vampire The Inquisition or Vampire The Hunger because in V5 the Masquerade whas a broken and from my opinion V5 masquerades more as VtM.</div> </div> </div> </div>I think it's because they want to emphasize you're not Hungry for blood but hungry for life.<br /> <br /> Trying to emphasize that being a vampire is a curse not a blessing or just a different state of being.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Author of <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Cthulhu-Armageddon-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01KUOM7SI/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982844&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Cthulhu+Armageddon\" target=\"_blank\">Cthulhu Armageddon</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Teenage-Weredeer-Bright-Falls-Mysteries-ebook/dp/B075TTN2FN/ref=sr_1_2?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982717&amp;sr=1-2&amp;keywords=Weredeer#customerReviews\" target=\"_blank\">I was a Teenage Weredeer</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Straight-Outta-Fangton-Comedic-Vampire-ebook/dp/B01KNHICCC/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982774&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Straight+Outta+Fangton\" target=\"_blank\">Straight Outta Fangton</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Lucifers-Star-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01MDM9MCT/ref=mt_kindle?_encoding=UTF8&amp;me=&amp;qid=\" target=\"_blank\">Lucifer's Star</a>, </i>and the <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Rules-Supervillainy-Saga-Book-ebook/dp/B07MB89S33/\" target=\"_blank\">Supervillainy Saga</a>.</i><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","name":"CTPhipps","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12002_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13933"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-04-23T18:25:58-07:00","id":1445582,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Heavy Arms</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1443592-the-official-v5-vs-v20-thread?p=1445577#post1445577\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> <br /> The problem is that it feels like a lot of those preferences get expressed to the point of seeming to be mutually incompatible. Should it be one community? I don't know really. Should implies things I'm not sure about. It could be one community with different preferences, but I'm not sure enough stakeholders are invested in that outcome to naturally generate it in current conditions.</div> </div> </div> </div>I think it's partly because there are only so many vampire players to go around, so those of us with different visions are in competition for those handful of players.<br /> <br /> I mean, you look on Roll20, and it's One page of WOD games, and thirty-four pages of DnD games. If you have a different vision for DnD, you will still find a game, or players for your game, pretty quickly. Maybe you spend five minutes weeding out the applications that don't fit your vision. Or ten minutes finding a game to join that fits your vision.<br /> <br /> If you don't like the vision of your applications for your Vampire game, you might not find another group of applicants for weeks. And if you don't like the vision of the ST's you find today, you might not find an ST for months.<br /> <br /> So we are in competition for control over our tiny world in a way that DnD players never will be.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3598-cajunkhan","name":"CajunKhan","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3598_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1700"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-04-23T18:31:02-07:00","id":1445584,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Heavy Arms</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1443592-the-official-v5-vs-v20-thread?p=1445577#post1445577\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The problem is that it feels like a lot of those preferences get expressed to the point of seeming to be mutually incompatible. Should it be one community? I don't know really. Should implies things I'm not sure about. It could be one community with different preferences, but I'm not sure enough stakeholders are invested in that outcome to naturally generate it in current conditions.</div> </div> </div> </div>I think it should be one community the same way that comic fans should be one community or DC Universe ones. People who like Bloodlines may not play the tabletop games but I think of them as still fans of Vampire: The Masquerade.<br /> <br /> I also feel like the same should be the case for Requiem.<br /> <br /> Its why I'm very excited about branching out into comic fans, board games, and more. Those people brought in by the Live Plays are new fans but still fans of the same universe.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Author of <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Cthulhu-Armageddon-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01KUOM7SI/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982844&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Cthulhu+Armageddon\" target=\"_blank\">Cthulhu Armageddon</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Teenage-Weredeer-Bright-Falls-Mysteries-ebook/dp/B075TTN2FN/ref=sr_1_2?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982717&amp;sr=1-2&amp;keywords=Weredeer#customerReviews\" target=\"_blank\">I was a Teenage Weredeer</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Straight-Outta-Fangton-Comedic-Vampire-ebook/dp/B01KNHICCC/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982774&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Straight+Outta+Fangton\" target=\"_blank\">Straight Outta Fangton</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Lucifers-Star-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01MDM9MCT/ref=mt_kindle?_encoding=UTF8&amp;me=&amp;qid=\" target=\"_blank\">Lucifer's Star</a>, </i>and the <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Rules-Supervillainy-Saga-Book-ebook/dp/B07MB89S33/\" target=\"_blank\">Supervillainy Saga</a>.</i><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","name":"CTPhipps","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12002_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13933"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-04-23T19:30:29-07:00","id":1445588,"title":"","content":"To an extent, that's moving beyond &quot;one community&quot; and just being positive people in general.<br /> <br /> To expand on CajunKhan's point: RPG.net is &quot;one community&quot; in a sense, but there are multiple major sub-forums that are also their own sub-communities (large enough and old enough that they have lingo that most people don't know). They have a separate d20 subforum so D&amp;D and Pathfinder discussions don't drown out everything else, and due to the edition wars that have happened in the d20 umbrella, have different rules to manage different needs.<br /> <br /> Even here, we split things up because there's a level of practicality involved.<br /> <br /> Communities exist, in a web of concentric circles of Venn-diagrams. Every user here is part of the Onyx Path community by virtue of participating here, but that doesn't mean everyone here sees themselves are a part of the Scared Lands community just because it falls under the Onyx Path umbrella.<br /> <br /> Whatever the ideal state of everyone being supportive of everyone else is, we're going to self-segregate into sub-units.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-04-23T19:35:03-07:00","id":1445589,"title":"","content":"First I\u2019d like to say that I have lots of older edition books (haven\u2019t read them all) and most V20 books but, unlike most of the people on this forum I haven\u2019t played it enough to know the ins and outs of the different clans and sects and what it means to be this or that. I have, what I feel, is a superficial engagement with the game. The commenters here are way above me when it comes to the knowledge of all things VtM. But I also feel like surely there are others like me that enjoy it on a minimal level. Surely people like me matter with how a game fares. I am possibly wrong about the following things but I might possess the ignorance that unfortunately other people might have about the game.<br /> <br /> V20 to me, embraces the essence of the time period of when VtM was released. While it has modern stuff in what the characters can do. The art, the look, the clans and sects all still invoke the sense of the early 90s. A time period I think fondly of that has a texture about it. The music, the fashion, the movies, the vibe. VtM came out at a time when all these things gelled and became part of the game. Part of me wants to recapture those great times in a game that belongs in that decade. Any game I run is set in the 90s. I\u2019m a grognard.<br /> <br /> In contrast V5 contains none of those things. Because of the decision to place the game in modern times the game suffers from it. Personally I feel no attachment to the past 20 years. It could be my age, in my early 40s. Modern times have no \u201ctexture\u201d that enhances the mood of the game. Music? Movies? Fashion? Nothing. While yes I could play V5 set in the 90s why would I when V20 has the look and feel of those times.<br /> <br /> The \u201cfashion magazine\u201d photos is one of the most pretentious cringe inducing things I\u2019ve seen in a rpg. A huge nail in coffin. Overall the book physically is a huge negative. The Anarch book cover literally has 2 people walking on the sidewalk. Terrible.<br /> <br /> The changes of publisher seem to hurt the release schedule.<br /> <br /> The anarchs are so modern politics, pass. Don\u2019t want to spotlight something that we are inundated with daily. The Sabbat rules. I know they are coming but oh well. Also goes into the political horror (actual politics not the jyhad) angle which I don\u2019t want. See also the delving into modern historical drama that makes me roll my eyes and go \u201cSee? That\u2019s what you get for being modern and politically edgy.\u201d<br /> <br /> The lack of focus on elders. I love the generations, the elders, the lore and history.<br /> <br /> The lack of feeling unique and uniquely powerful. I guess I prefer superheroes with fangs.<br /> <br /> The Hunger mechanic seems gimmicky and I don\u2019t want it to influence my actions. Also it seems to force a certain type of play.<br /> <br /> I didn\u2019t like Gangrel leaving the Camarilla back in the day so obviously I don\u2019t like any other big clan changes.<br /> <br /> Again I might be ignorant but that\u2019s my 2 cents and I can\u2019t help to think others share my ignorance and are staying away for the same issues.<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":13440,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13440-savagegm","user":"SavageGM","date":". 04-23-2021, 10:47 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":10}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13440-savagegm","name":"SavageGM","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar13440_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"26"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-04-23T19:48:30-07:00","id":1445592,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>SavageGM</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1443592-the-official-v5-vs-v20-thread?p=1445589#post1445589\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">V20 to me, embraces the essence of the time period of when VtM was released. While it has modern stuff in what the characters can do. The art, the look, the clans and sects all still invoke the sense of the early 90s. A time period I think fondly of that has a texture about it. The music, the fashion, the movies, the vibe. VtM came out at a time when all these things gelled and became part of the game. Part of me wants to recapture those great times in a game that belongs in that decade. Any game I run is set in the 90s. I\u2019m a grognard.</div> </div> </div> </div>Well that's fine for you but I don't understand this argument at all. The only reason to play V20 rather than play one of the Older Edition is to play it in the Modern Times.<br /> <br /> All of the Sourcebooks are period appropriate except the main book, which is setting agnostic.<br /> <br /> Or to put it another way, &quot;V20 to me is distinct and not the same as the Previous Three Editions. It is its own thing from the 2000s.&quot;<br /> <br /> But yes, if you don't like it, that's fine. Shame you can't find something enjoyable in it, though, but it happens.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Author of <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Cthulhu-Armageddon-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01KUOM7SI/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982844&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Cthulhu+Armageddon\" target=\"_blank\">Cthulhu Armageddon</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Teenage-Weredeer-Bright-Falls-Mysteries-ebook/dp/B075TTN2FN/ref=sr_1_2?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982717&amp;sr=1-2&amp;keywords=Weredeer#customerReviews\" target=\"_blank\">I was a Teenage Weredeer</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Straight-Outta-Fangton-Comedic-Vampire-ebook/dp/B01KNHICCC/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982774&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Straight+Outta+Fangton\" target=\"_blank\">Straight Outta Fangton</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Lucifers-Star-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01MDM9MCT/ref=mt_kindle?_encoding=UTF8&amp;me=&amp;qid=\" target=\"_blank\">Lucifer's Star</a>, </i>and the <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Rules-Supervillainy-Saga-Book-ebook/dp/B07MB89S33/\" target=\"_blank\">Supervillainy Saga</a>.</i><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","name":"CTPhipps","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12002_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13933"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-04-23T20:58:08-07:00","id":1445595,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CTPhipps</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1443592-the-official-v5-vs-v20-thread?p=1445584#post1445584\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I think it should be one community the same way that comic fans should be one community or DC Universe ones. People who like Bloodlines may not play the tabletop games but I think of them as still fans of Vampire: The Masquerade.<br /> <br /> I also feel like the same should be the case for Requiem.<br /> <br /> Its why I'm very excited about branching out into comic fans, board games, and more. Those people brought in by the Live Plays are new fans but still fans of the same universe.</div> </div> </div> </div>This is the most peculiar way of thinking to me. I can understand why you would consider the other VTM mediums being fans, but to me Requiem and VTM are about as different as Star Trek and Star Wars. And I know plenty of people who love one of those and absolutely hate the other even though they are both space sci-fi universes.<br /> <br /> So if someone loves say Watchmen (and only Watchmen) but hates every other DC character and comic line with a passion would you consider them a DC fan?<br /> <br /> I personally HATE the mechanics of Requiem(I liked the lore and felt the books were well written for the most part) and consider them non-functional to run a game (1st ed I have no experience with 2nd), but I loved DA1-V20. Not a super fan of the discipline changes in DA20, except for obfuscate dot one no longer being a useless power once you got the 2nd dot.<br /> <br /> It is enlightening to see how different our two thought processes are from each other even if I disagree with with most of your opinions. Which I am sure stems from your focus tending to be more on the Narrative aspects and my focus on the Game Mechanics aspects of rpgs.<br /> <br /> <b>Liked about V5:</b><br /> Lore sheets in concept--I would have rather had the levels build up (the way backgrounds do) than be bought as separate independent levels though.<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25664-gubenyochi","name":"Gubenyochi","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"50"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-04-23T21:00:17-07:00","id":1445596,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Gubenyochi</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1443592-the-official-v5-vs-v20-thread?p=1445595#post1445595\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> This is the most peculiar way of thinking to me. I can understand why you would consider the other VTM mediums being fans, but to me Requiem and VTM are about as different as Star Trek and Star Wars. And I know plenty of people who love one of those and absolutely hate the other even though they are both space sci-fi universes.<br /> <br /> So if someone loves say Watchmen (and only Watchmen) but hates every other DC character and comic line with a passion would you consider them a DC fan?<br /> <br /> I personally HATE the mechanics of Requiem(I liked the lore and felt the books were well written for the most part) and consider them non-functional to run a game (1st ed I have no experience with 2nd), but I loved DA1-V20. Not a super fan of the discipline changes in DA20, except for obfuscate dot one no longer being a useless power once you got the 2nd dot.<br /> <br /> It is enlightening to see how different our two thought processes are from each other even if I disagree with with most of your opinions. Which I am sure stems from your focus tending to be more on the Narrative aspects and my focus on the Game Mechanics aspects of rpgs.<br /> <br /> <b>Liked about V5:</b><br /> Lore sheets in concept--I would have rather had the levels build up (the way backgrounds do) than be bought as separate independent levels though.<br /></div> </div> </div> </div>I suspect I might be a bad market here because I've played Requiem games with the V:TM setting and stolen bits from Requiem for Masquerade like the Ordo Dracul and Crones.<br /> <br /> Basically, I feel like once I got past the fact that Antediluvians weren't a thing in V:TM or Clans as we knew them but the focus was on street level vampires with very questionable histories, it became a very interesting new setting. It's not something I warmed too quickly but I thought there was a lot of interesting rules that helped explore the idea of being a vampire in the &quot;real&quot; world. Where the conflict wasn't over billion dollar industries, the Apocalypse, world banks, and nacient relics but over 14th street as well as the gas station there.<br /> <br /> Its a grungier, darker, and uglier setting but that's what makes it work.<br /> <br /> <img src=\"https://images-na.ssl-images-amazon.com/images/I/61zXZWVqv-L._SX258_BO1,204,203,200_.jpg\" class=\"bbcode-attachment bbcode-attachment--lightbox js-lightbox\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" itemprop=\"image\" loading=\"lazy\"/><br /> <br /> You could meet a 2000 year old vampire in Requiem that's not much more powerful than you and you could ask him about the origins of Vampiredom and he'd have no clue or say he was the first vampire. The uncertainty really added to the Anne Rice sense of, &quot;Why are we here? What are we doing?&quot; and the answer is, &quot;I have no idea and there is never going to be a satisfactory answer.&quot;<br /> <br /> Which was how I liked Anne Rice's first two books before answered everything in Queen of the Damned.<br /> <br /> The power levels of the game were GREATLY different and I think really enforced the mood that you could be powerful as a vampire but you'd never be OMNIPOTENT. You capped out at a certain level and even then, it might be better if you gave away some of that power.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Author of <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Cthulhu-Armageddon-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01KUOM7SI/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982844&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Cthulhu+Armageddon\" target=\"_blank\">Cthulhu Armageddon</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Teenage-Weredeer-Bright-Falls-Mysteries-ebook/dp/B075TTN2FN/ref=sr_1_2?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982717&amp;sr=1-2&amp;keywords=Weredeer#customerReviews\" target=\"_blank\">I was a Teenage Weredeer</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Straight-Outta-Fangton-Comedic-Vampire-ebook/dp/B01KNHICCC/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982774&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Straight+Outta+Fangton\" target=\"_blank\">Straight Outta Fangton</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Lucifers-Star-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01MDM9MCT/ref=mt_kindle?_encoding=UTF8&amp;me=&amp;qid=\" target=\"_blank\">Lucifer's Star</a>, </i>and the <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Rules-Supervillainy-Saga-Book-ebook/dp/B07MB89S33/\" target=\"_blank\">Supervillainy Saga</a>.</i><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":12002,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","user":"CTPhipps","date":". 04-24-2021, 12:07 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","name":"CTPhipps","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12002_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13933"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-04-23T21:39:58-07:00","id":1445601,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>SavageGM</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1443592-the-official-v5-vs-v20-thread?p=1445589#post1445589\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">V20 to me, embraces the essence of the time period of when VtM was released. While it has modern stuff in what the characters can do. The art, the look, the clans and sects all still invoke the sense of the early 90s. A time period I think fondly of that has a texture about it. The music, the fashion, the movies, the vibe. VtM came out at a time when all these things gelled and became part of the game. Part of me wants to recapture those great times in a game that belongs in that decade. Any game I run is set in the 90s. I\u2019m a grognard.</div> </div> </div> </div>To me, the look and feel of V20 was the same as that of Vampire Revised, from the very late 1990s moving into the early 2000s. It felt like an expanded version of Vampire Revised really, especially without the original Tim Bradsheet art or the original art to illustrate the clans (not Leif Jones). In actuality, the original two editions of Vampire actually evoke the tone of the 1980s in many ways, when goth-punk was a genuine alternative counter-culture in music and style. In the early 1990s, basically, the alternative became mainstream - so the general public started listening to Nirvana, watching The Crow - and playing Vampire: The Masquerade - in greater numbers.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> In contrast V5 contains none of those things. Because of the decision to place the game in modern times the game suffers from it. Personally I feel no attachment to the past 20 years. It could be my age, in my early 40s. Modern times have no \u201ctexture\u201d that enhances the mood of the game. Music? Movies? Fashion? Nothing. While yes I could play V5 set in the 90s why would I when V20 has the look and feel of those times. </div> </div> </div>Well, I disagree with this because one of the major features of the original game was that it was set in modern nights - not the past. So, if a new company were going to make a new edition of the game, it shouldn\u2019t be fixated on a historical period but in the here and now. The past is \u2019safer\u2019 for the game - but the original game was provocative and this created the energy for much of its appeal. In the early 1990s, most RPGs were giving you historical or futuristic fantasies to escape into - Vampire was a jarring exception when it first came out, in that it reflected a dark, dangerous modern world. <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> The \u201cfashion magazine\u201d photos is one of the most pretentious cringe inducing things I\u2019ve seen in a rpg. A huge nail in coffin. Overall the book physically is a huge negative. The Anarch book cover literally has 2 people walking on the sidewalk. Terrible. </div> </div> </div>Again, I like this because it blurs the sense of the real world being infused with supernatural conspiracy. Moreover, White Wolf games of old were using photo art ever since they were producing live action games and supplements. It isn\u2019t a new style. <br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2517-trippy","name":"Trippy","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2517_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1018"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-04-23T21:48:11-07:00","id":1445602,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CTPhipps</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1443592-the-official-v5-vs-v20-thread?p=1445596#post1445596\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><img src=\"https://images-na.ssl-images-amazon.com/images/I/61zXZWVqv-L._SX258_BO1,204,203,200_.jpg\" class=\"bbcode-attachment bbcode-attachment--lightbox js-lightbox\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" itemprop=\"image\" loading=\"lazy\"/></div> </div> </div> </div>This image was always a bit jarring for me, but it was explained at the time that the USA and UK both understand different meanings for \u2019New Wave\u2019 music.<br /> <br /> In the UK, \u2019New Wave\u2019 was another name for \u2018post-punk\u2019 music from the late 1970s - probably most embodied by groups like Joy Division/New Order, The Slits, Souxie and the Banshees, etc - where groups originally influenced by punk rock, or actual punk bands, were moving on from it and experimenting with forms. In my view, gothic-punk originates in these groups - notably Bauhaus\u2019 Bela Lugosi\u2019s Dead was the song that had the term \u2018Goth Rock\u2019 coined for it. The Cure also came from this type of music. It is also where you saw a trend of independent labels, or \u2018Indie Rock\u2019 becoming prevalent and would later on include bands like The Smiths or The Jesus and Mary Chain. In America, they basically refer to this as Alternative rock, these days.<br /> <br /> In the USA, though \u2019New Wave' was sort of what people in the UK would refer to as 'New Romantic\u2019. It was more encapsulated in 80s ostentatiousness and a glam style.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":2517,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2517-trippy","user":"Trippy","date":". 04-24-2021, 01:13 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2517-trippy","name":"Trippy","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2517_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1018"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-04-23T22:07:09-07:00","id":1445604,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Trippy</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1443592-the-official-v5-vs-v20-thread?p=1445602#post1445602\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> This image was always a bit jarring for me, but it was explained at the time that the USA and UK both understand different meanings for \u2019New Wave\u2019 music.<br /> <br /> In the UK, \u2019New Wave\u2019 was another name for \u2018post-punk\u2019 music from the late 1970s - probably most embodied by groups like Joy Division/New Order, The Slits, Souxie and the Banshees, etc - where groups originally influenced by punk rock, or actual punk bands, were moving on from it and experimenting with forms. In my view, gothic-punk originates in these groups - notably Bauhaus\u2019 Bela Lugosi\u2019s Dead was the song that had the term \u2018Goth Rock\u2019 termed for it. The Cure also came from this type of music. It is also where you saw a trend of independent labels, or \u2018Indie Rock\u2019 becoming prevalent and would later on include bands like The Smiths or The Jesus and Mary Chain. In America, they basically refer to this as Alternative rock, these days.<br /> <br /> In the USA, though \u2019New Wave' was sort of what people in the UK would refer to as 'New Romantic\u2019. It was more encapsulated in 80s ostentatiousness and a glam style.</div> </div> </div> </div>NEW WAVE REQUIEM was a book that disappointed me in other ways because it was so thin and barely touched on what could have been a fascinating alternative setting. Even so, it had great bits spread around with more questionable bits. I admit, I bought the book because of the cover and glamorous colorful image of a vampiress, high as a kite, and her tacky oversexed outfit.<br /> <br /> Funnily, this ties into your statement about how V:TM 1st Edition felt more 80s than 90s. I think this is distinctly because of the fact that V:TM was very much a product of the Bible Belt. You can't actually differentiate Vampire: The Masquerade from the American South even if it was set in Chicago initially. It was created and printed up in the counterculture district of Atlanta during the early 90s but strongly influenced by the vibe there that is always a little behind the rest of the countries trendsetters.<br /> <br /> I've always noted that the themes of Damnation, Pseudo-Christianity, Goth, rebellion, and tradition vs. punk of early V:TM are things that indulate the American South in a way that is probably quite queer to people outside of the region. However, Anne Rice pretty much created the Vampire Chronicles around growing up in that exact sort of environment. Its why V5 came at a great time and if it could reach the right audience in rural America, I think it could have a second boom because there is no end of people silently screaming during the Trump era.<br /> <br /> <b>Revised vs. Requiem vs. V20 vs. V5</b><br /> <br /> I think part of the problem was that White Wolf had gotten somewhat sick of the old World of Darkness and wanted to play in new environments (plus some bad financial decisions) that they couldn't just make a new setting for. I think if they'd made Requiem while the regular World of Darkness was still going strong, it would have avoided much of the original flack. Basically, make it Eberron to Dragonlance to Forgotten Realms, which is how I see this.<br /> <br /> Requiem fans are the Eberron fans of the intellectual property and just the same as Dragonlance (V20) or Realms fans (V5).","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Author of <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Cthulhu-Armageddon-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01KUOM7SI/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982844&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Cthulhu+Armageddon\" target=\"_blank\">Cthulhu Armageddon</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Teenage-Weredeer-Bright-Falls-Mysteries-ebook/dp/B075TTN2FN/ref=sr_1_2?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982717&amp;sr=1-2&amp;keywords=Weredeer#customerReviews\" target=\"_blank\">I was a Teenage Weredeer</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Straight-Outta-Fangton-Comedic-Vampire-ebook/dp/B01KNHICCC/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982774&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Straight+Outta+Fangton\" target=\"_blank\">Straight Outta Fangton</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Lucifers-Star-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01MDM9MCT/ref=mt_kindle?_encoding=UTF8&amp;me=&amp;qid=\" target=\"_blank\">Lucifer's Star</a>, </i>and the <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Rules-Supervillainy-Saga-Book-ebook/dp/B07MB89S33/\" target=\"_blank\">Supervillainy Saga</a>.</i><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","name":"CTPhipps","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12002_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13933"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-04-23T22:14:36-07:00","id":1445607,"title":"","content":"For me the here and now sucks. Hard. I\u2019m sure many people are still setting their games in the 90s and have been for 20 years. I\u2019d say playing a game of VtM that\u2019s always in modern times is far down the list of must haves in people\u2019s games, but maybe I\u2019m wrong. <br /> <br /> Using photo art for years I understand. Not sure that makes it good or not. For me it\u2019s not preferable to actual art. Also I have issue more with the depictions in the photos themselves rather than actually using photo art.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13440-savagegm","name":"SavageGM","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar13440_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"26"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-04-23T22:21:45-07:00","id":1445608,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>SavageGM</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1443592-the-official-v5-vs-v20-thread?p=1445607#post1445607\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">For me the here and now sucks. Hard. I\u2019m sure many people are still setting their games in the 90s and have been for 20 years. I\u2019d say playing a game of VtM that\u2019s always in modern times is far down the list of must haves in people\u2019s games, but maybe I\u2019m wrong.<br /> <br /> Using photo art for years I understand. Not sure that makes it good or not. For me it\u2019s not preferable to actual art. Also I have issue more with the depictions in the photos themselves rather than actually using photo art.</div> </div> </div> </div>I dunno, what exactly is appealing about the 90s to a vampire versus now? Either decade I'm still a sexy immortal creature of the night.<br /> <br /> Anecdotal or not, I've never heard of anyone setting their game perpetually in the 90s versus staying current or the far past.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Author of <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Cthulhu-Armageddon-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01KUOM7SI/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982844&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Cthulhu+Armageddon\" target=\"_blank\">Cthulhu Armageddon</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Teenage-Weredeer-Bright-Falls-Mysteries-ebook/dp/B075TTN2FN/ref=sr_1_2?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982717&amp;sr=1-2&amp;keywords=Weredeer#customerReviews\" target=\"_blank\">I was a Teenage Weredeer</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Straight-Outta-Fangton-Comedic-Vampire-ebook/dp/B01KNHICCC/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982774&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Straight+Outta+Fangton\" target=\"_blank\">Straight Outta Fangton</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Lucifers-Star-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01MDM9MCT/ref=mt_kindle?_encoding=UTF8&amp;me=&amp;qid=\" target=\"_blank\">Lucifer's Star</a>, </i>and the <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Rules-Supervillainy-Saga-Book-ebook/dp/B07MB89S33/\" target=\"_blank\">Supervillainy Saga</a>.</i><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","name":"CTPhipps","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12002_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13933"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-04-23T22:30:52-07:00","id":1445610,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CTPhipps</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1443592-the-official-v5-vs-v20-thread?p=1445608#post1445608\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I dunno, what exactly is appealing about the 90s to a vampire versus now? Either decade I'm still a sexy immortal creature of the night.<br /> <br /> Anecdotal or not, I've never heard of anyone setting their game perpetually in the 90s versus staying current or the far past.</div> </div> </div> </div>I believe part of it is escapism back to the 90s in their own lives as well as the game. I remember it as better times and would like to revisit it how ever I can. To me V20 embraces the past by making it a \u201cgreatest hits\u201d, as it\u2019s often called, by looking and playing like the game we played in the 90s. So not only do I want the setting in the 90s I want to \u201crelive\u201d the 90s. It may be a strange way of reminiscing but that\u2019s what I want out of VtM game.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13440-savagegm","name":"SavageGM","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar13440_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"26"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-04-23T22:33:53-07:00","id":1445611,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>SavageGM</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1443592-the-official-v5-vs-v20-thread?p=1445607#post1445607\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">For me the here and now sucks. Hard. I\u2019m sure many people are still setting their games in the 90s and have been for 20 years. I\u2019d say playing a game of VtM that\u2019s always in modern times is far down the list of must haves in people\u2019s games, but maybe I\u2019m wrong.</div> </div> </div> </div>Well, put it this way: Vampire: The Masquerade is listed as one of the 100 Best Hobby Games (published by Green Ronin) - along with a bunch of other awards - in a ranking chosen by other industry professionals and is pretty much a gold standard nomination.<br /> <br /> It was nominated by George Vasilakos, noted as the driving force behind games like Eden Studios\u2019 All Flesh Must Be Eaten and Buffy The Vampire Slayer, among a lot of other credits. In his essay to explain what <i>he</i> found compelling about the game - one of things he clearly cites is the fact that it is set in modern nights. Now, I am not saying you are wrong, but is a clearly identifying aspect of the game and, to be sure, <u>all </u>of the VTM editions have defaulted to be set in modern nights - even V20. You can get supplemental games, like Dark Ages, for different eras and you can always take the option of using historical settings, but the core default game is deliberately set in the here and now.<br /> <br /> Now, to flip this criticism on its head, if fans are arguing that V20 is preferable to them because it <i>feels like it is set in the past (in the 1990s)</i>, then I\u2019d say this is a flaw of the design. That is, <i>it\u2019s intent </i>is to be set in modern nights, but apparently it doesn\u2019t feel that way. It isn\u2019t a major problem for me, in as much as my general take on V20 is that it is a \u2018Greatest Hits compilation\u2019 edition that celebrates past editions and supplements. V5 however, is an attempt to recapture the spirit of the original game in tone and style - but updated to the modern nights of the 21st century. By contrast, it is a \u2018Remastered\u2019 edition.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":2517,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2517-trippy","user":"Trippy","date":". 04-24-2021, 01:36 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2517-trippy","name":"Trippy","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2517_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1018"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-04-23T22:40:57-07:00","id":1445612,"title":"","content":"Really one of the biggest things about V5, for better or worse, is dealing with the War on Terror as well as the Surveillance State that was created post-9/11. That needed to be addressed if you wanted to maintain some sort of realism.<br /> <br /> Its why vampires are just magically impossible to know about in Requiem.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Author of <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Cthulhu-Armageddon-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01KUOM7SI/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982844&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Cthulhu+Armageddon\" target=\"_blank\">Cthulhu Armageddon</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Teenage-Weredeer-Bright-Falls-Mysteries-ebook/dp/B075TTN2FN/ref=sr_1_2?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982717&amp;sr=1-2&amp;keywords=Weredeer#customerReviews\" target=\"_blank\">I was a Teenage Weredeer</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Straight-Outta-Fangton-Comedic-Vampire-ebook/dp/B01KNHICCC/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982774&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Straight+Outta+Fangton\" target=\"_blank\">Straight Outta Fangton</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Lucifers-Star-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01MDM9MCT/ref=mt_kindle?_encoding=UTF8&amp;me=&amp;qid=\" target=\"_blank\">Lucifer's Star</a>, </i>and the <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Rules-Supervillainy-Saga-Book-ebook/dp/B07MB89S33/\" target=\"_blank\">Supervillainy Saga</a>.</i><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","name":"CTPhipps","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12002_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13933"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-04-23T22:47:42-07:00","id":1445614,"title":"","content":"I understand Trippy. I guess because all 3 original editions were released in the 90s, their modern nights are the 90s to me. If that makes sense.<br /> <br /> Also I don\u2019t think V5 should have been set in the 90s. V5\u2019s modern nights is nothing that can be helped. The times are as they are. So, to me, it\u2019s unfortunate that the modern times just aren\u2019t as compelling as the previous editions set in the 90s.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13440-savagegm","name":"SavageGM","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar13440_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"26"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-04-23T23:21:16-07:00","id":1445618,"title":"","content":"Modern nights are kind of the trickiest setting (in any medium) to write for thanks to smartphones. About 90% of Buffy the Vampire Slayer plots could have been solved with cell phones (even without internet) and &quot;Harold and Kumar Doordash White Castle&quot; would be a very different movie.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25664-gubenyochi","name":"Gubenyochi","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"50"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-04-23T23:32:42-07:00","id":1445620,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Gubenyochi</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1443592-the-official-v5-vs-v20-thread?p=1445618#post1445618\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Modern nights are kind of the trickiest setting (in any medium) to write for thanks to smartphones. About 90% of Buffy the Vampire Slayer plots could have been solved with cell phones (even without internet) and &quot;Harold and Kumar Doordash White Castle&quot; would be a very different movie.</div> </div> </div> </div>I wonder if banning cell-phones save for Anarchs was an attempt to do it, even though that's silly.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Author of <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Cthulhu-Armageddon-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01KUOM7SI/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982844&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Cthulhu+Armageddon\" target=\"_blank\">Cthulhu Armageddon</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Teenage-Weredeer-Bright-Falls-Mysteries-ebook/dp/B075TTN2FN/ref=sr_1_2?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982717&amp;sr=1-2&amp;keywords=Weredeer#customerReviews\" target=\"_blank\">I was a Teenage Weredeer</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Straight-Outta-Fangton-Comedic-Vampire-ebook/dp/B01KNHICCC/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982774&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Straight+Outta+Fangton\" target=\"_blank\">Straight Outta Fangton</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Lucifers-Star-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01MDM9MCT/ref=mt_kindle?_encoding=UTF8&amp;me=&amp;qid=\" target=\"_blank\">Lucifer's Star</a>, </i>and the <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Rules-Supervillainy-Saga-Book-ebook/dp/B07MB89S33/\" target=\"_blank\">Supervillainy Saga</a>.</i><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","name":"CTPhipps","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12002_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13933"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-04-23T23:37:46-07:00","id":1445621,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Trippy</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1443592-the-official-v5-vs-v20-thread?p=1445601#post1445601\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">To me, the look and feel of V20 was the same as that of Vampire Revised, from the very late 1990s moving into the early 2000s. It felt like an expanded version of Vampire Revised really, especially without the original Tim Bradsheet art or the original art to illustrate the clans (not Leif Jones). In actuality, the original two editions of Vampire actually evoke the tone of the 1980s in many ways, when goth-punk was a genuine alternative counter-culture in music and style. In the early 1990s, basically, the alternative became mainstream - so the general public started listening to Nirvana, watching The Crow - and playing Vampire: The Masquerade - in greater numbers.</div> </div> </div> </div>Given that the first edition of <i>Vampire: the Masquerade</i> was published in 1991, I think that it's natural that it reflects the 1980s more than the 1990s; it was a book about how people felt at the end of the 1980s, looking back on what was, in essence, the very recent past. This is, of course, a feature of any book, that it will never properly reflect the present, in that the formative experiences of the author will have occurred in the past. I would also argue that <i>Vampire: the Masquerade </i>is a better book about the 1980s that <i>New Wave Requiem</i>, as the former is a very immediate reflection, whilst the latter is a pastiche of the period, which would appear to be written by people too young to have properly experienced the decade...<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":6}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/317-james_willoughby","name":"James_Willoughby","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar317_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"297"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-04-23T23:45:25-07:00","id":1445622,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CTPhipps</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1443592-the-official-v5-vs-v20-thread?p=1445612#post1445612\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Really one of the biggest things about V5, for better or worse, is dealing with the War on Terror as well as the Surveillance State that was created post-9/11. That needed to be addressed if you wanted to maintain some sort of realism.<br /> <br /> Its why vampires are just magically impossible to know about in Requiem.</div> </div> </div> </div>There's actually a massive gulf between &quot;Hollywood intelligence and surveillance state&quot; and the real world. Having worked in what might euphemistically be known as some interesting career areas, I wouldn't think vampires have much to fear from the security services. Of course, the suspension of disbelief from people whose primary experience comes from television and movies might be hard to bridge, regardless of the reality of the situation.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":7}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/317-james_willoughby","name":"James_Willoughby","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar317_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"297"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-04-24T00:08:08-07:00","id":1445624,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CTPhipps</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1443592-the-official-v5-vs-v20-thread?p=1445612#post1445612\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Its why vampires are just magically impossible to know about in Requiem.</div> </div> </div> </div>Um... huh?<br /> <br /> VtR's only thing here is that vampires are magically hard to capture with cameras clearly. Nothing else magically protects them from being known about.<br /> <br /> The CofD as a whole opts for a different approach to the status quo of the setting where the majority of humanity subconsciously rejects intellectual idea of the existence of the supernatural as a self-defense mechanism. Safety in ignorance has been ingrained in humanity over thousands of years of supernatural violence, but if you really want you can drag anyone into the reality of the darkness kicking and screaming (being a Hunter in the CofD is a rough job). Task Force Valkyrie, which absolutely knows vampires are real, also knows that vampires aren't the only thing out there that would love to turn a senator into a pawn, and if they put all their resources into trying to wipe out vampires, then some other nasty would take over the country in the meantime; so they focus on keeping the all supernaturals away from the highest ranks of political power to ensure humans run the country, instead of trying to get rid of supernaturals as a whole.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":7}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-04-24T00:37:47-07:00","id":1445626,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Heavy Arms</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1443592-the-official-v5-vs-v20-thread?p=1445558#post1445558\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I'm sure you don't intend it, but this is probably one of the biggest sources of negative feelings from the V20 camp towards the V5 camp: the attitude that those of us that have playing VtM and other games with vampires in them that aren't close to what V5 does, haven't been playing &amp;quot;real&amp;quot; vampire games. This whole way of phrasing the conversation tends to raise hackles because you, again giving you the benefit of the doubt that you don't mean to come off this way, are basically saying that in my near 25 years of playing vampires in RPGs, I don't appreciate what a &amp;quot;vampire game&amp;quot; should actually be because I don't like the specific way V5 does vampires.<br /> <br /> I hope you can see how off-putting that can be when seen from the other side of it.<br /> <br /> Vampires are fictional creatures. Of thousands of years they've seen countless variations in different mythologies and folklore. Even in pop-culture there is a huge range of what vampires are, what they do, what dominates their concerns, and what narrative point their creators are trying to make. Blade or Morbius are two very different vampire stories (as much as one can sum up comic books as stories like that), but they're both vampire stories. There is no platonic ideal of vampires to appeal to when saying &amp;quot;this is good because you're playing a vampire,&amp;quot; or, &amp;quot;this makes the game more vampire-like.&amp;quot;<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> As someone that's been rather involved in the discussions around V5 here since they started, I think there's a somewhat rosy picture of history.<br /> <br /> When V5 was announced, and first few playtests were out, things felt rather the opposite. V5 was all the hype, expressing negativity about it put you firmly in the minority in most threads; though the flames were plenty heated and I'm sure lots of people just avoided those threads on both sides. Plenty of us felt like it was turning from the VtM forum into the V5 forum. Then the core dropped. Then the Cam and Anarch books dropped. That's when the mood of this forum started swinging towards where it is now. There were some very serious V5 supporters that jumped back to V20 during that period here as a sign of, at least on this forum, the reaction wasn't so positive once the product got in people's hands.<br /> <br /> Lots of V5 posters here spent a lot of time actively posting about how much better V5 is; not just &amp;quot;being happy with what they got.&amp;quot; It's just that after the hype settled, these forums settled more on the V20 side than the V5 side, and that's colored discussions since.</div> </div> </div> </div>This is pretty much exactly how I feel.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Writer, publisher, performer<br /> Mostly he/his, sometimes she/her IRL <a href=\"https://adam-lowe.com\" target=\"_blank\">https://adam-lowe.com</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5291-adambeyoncelowe","name":"adambeyoncelowe","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5291_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2802"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-04-24T01:16:28-07:00","id":1445627,"title":"","content":"Yeah the Masquerade was still a thing in Requiem. There's even a whole faction who's dedicated to its preservation (among other things).<br /> <br /> The fact that vampires could not be caught on tape just meant that said faction did not need to be a global conspiracy powerful enough to prevent a worldwide breach if needed (and a video on the net could quickly become such a thing). At least until v5 when the Masquerade shattered but not really because... no reason given.<br /> And conveniently enough the Camarilla is no longer a global superpower because... well who need to maintain the Masquerade if Humans can gatekeep other humans by themselves?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":24936,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24936-morbus","user":"Morbus","date":". 04-24-2021, 04:19 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":8}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24936-morbus","name":"Morbus","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"119"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-04-24T02:06:42-07:00","id":1445631,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Trippy</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1443592-the-official-v5-vs-v20-thread?p=1445611#post1445611\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Well, put it this way: Vampire: The Masquerade is listed as one of the 100 Best Hobby Games (published by Green Ronin) - along with a bunch of other awards - in a ranking chosen by other industry professionals and is pretty much a gold standard nomination.<br /> <br /> It was nominated by George Vasilakos, noted as the driving force behind games like Eden Studios\u2019 All Flesh Must Be Eaten and Buffy The Vampire Slayer, among a lot of other credits. In his essay to explain what <i>he</i> found compelling about the game - one of things he clearly cites is the fact that it is set in modern nights. Now, I am not saying you are wrong, but is a clearly identifying aspect of the game and, to be sure, <u>all </u>of the VTM editions have defaulted to be set in modern nights - even V20. You can get supplemental games, like Dark Ages, for different eras and you can always take the option of using historical settings, but the core default game is deliberately set in the here and now.<br /> <br /> Now, to flip this criticism on its head, if fans are arguing that V20 is preferable to them because it <i>feels like it is set in the past (in the 1990s)</i>, then I\u2019d say this is a flaw of the design. That is, <i>it\u2019s intent </i>is to be set in modern nights, but apparently it doesn\u2019t feel that way. It isn\u2019t a major problem for me, in as much as my general take on V20 is that it is a \u2018Greatest Hits compilation\u2019 edition that celebrates past editions and supplements. V5 however, is an attempt to recapture the spirit of the original game in tone and style - but updated to the modern nights of the 21st century. By contrast, it is a \u2018Remastered\u2019 edition.</div> </div> </div> </div>Ah nope Remastering means the gameplay feels the same but it is only more resolution. For roleplay Books this means Hardcover instead of Softcover, Art and Book in Colour instead of B/W and Bugfixing. I think it means for RP Settings too, that the description is slightly improved too. So V20 is actually more Remaster then V5.<br /> I would say V5 is a Reboot where Setting and Gameplay are only vague the same and mostly only name stays the same.<br /> Btw I took the actual descriptions of Definitions from here:<br /> <div class=\"b-bbcode b-bbcode__url b-bbcode__url--preview\"> <a href=\"https://praxistipps.chip.de/remake-remaster-co-so-unterscheiden-sie-die-neuauflagen-von-games_125480\" target=\"_blank\" class=\"urlimg_container\"> <img class=\"js-img-fallback\" src=\"https://quadro.burda-forward.de/ctf/f34e5f12-71e8-41df-8aea-eb4cb99ba957.b1b53737-3ddf-46ad-8ed2-79b5ce5367c3.jpeg?im=RegionOfInterestCrop=(1200,630),regionOfInterest=(960,540)&amp;hash=e5531c90ea1e091cac25d9f1ee0c3068ff41f48989e94afc128ebfb4a1dc5e3e\"> </a> <div class=\"urlinfo\"> <div class=\"title ellipsis\"> <a href=\"https://praxistipps.chip.de/remake-remaster-co-so-unterscheiden-sie-die-neuauflagen-von-games_125480\" target=\"_blank\"> Remake, Remaster &amp; Co.: So unterscheiden Sie die Neuauflagen von Games </a> </div> <div class=\"url ellipsis\"> <a href=\"https://praxistipps.chip.de/remake-remaster-co-so-unterscheiden-sie-die-neuauflagen-von-games_125480\" target=\"_blank\"> https://praxistipps.chip.de/remake-remaster-co-so-unterscheiden-sie-die-neuauflagen-von-games_125480 </a> </div> <div class=\"meta\"> Bei Begriffen wie Remake, Remaster, Reboot und Port herrscht h&auml;ufig Verwirrung. In diesem Praxistipp kl&auml;ren wir, wie Sie sie am besten erkennen und voneinander unterscheiden k&ouml;nnen. </div> </div> </div>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>As I am from Austria I need to clarify two things.<br /> First my native language is german and so please point out if the english I write is broken so I can improve.<br /> Second I do not own VTMV beyond first three books nor any line after M20 Corebook because it is not out there and I wait for the translation.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":6}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26160-koronus","name":"Koronus","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2020"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"366"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-04-24T02:34:09-07:00","id":1445633,"title":"","content":"Ah there's too much for me to adress to make a post on my phone, but my kid would start demading youtube if i turn my computer on. She's young. I am young. I'm 26; sometimes I get the impression you're all in your 50's. <br /> V20 is not a 90's game. It can be a 90's game. But it is not a 90's game. V20 isn't quite timeless; It assumes we've got computers, but it's pretty close. There's a healthy level of seperation between Immortal, resistant-to-change vampire society and mortal events. It's not entirely static; Rites of the blood gives us a nice runover of evolving anarch sorcery, but it's certainly not so stupid as to claim SYRIA IS GEHENNA. V20 works for 1995, 2005, 2015, and assuming nothing apocalyptic it'll work for 2025, 2035, 2045 and 2125. V20, Ignoring east Asia if you're adverse to a sensible retcon, v20 works anywhere. It feels like it was written for everyone. V5, in contrast, is a 2018 product haunted by the USA's 2016. <br /> <br /> RE LARP. <br /> LARP is fine, you do you, but I'm gonna be honest; I deeply resent the Idea of LARP impacting tabletop. Everyone is welcome to their own little word, but I refuse to have the power of Imagination shackled down by a medium highly limited by a bunch of actors. Unless you all work out how to throw cars at eachother or accept the cruelties of Dominate, you shouldn't impose your problems on the tabletop majority. Keep your canon seperate. V5 takes too many cues from LARP, and it suffers from it. <br /> <br /> RE How Vampires are supposed to be. <br /> Maybe it's because its the first 'vampire' thing I really clicked with, being a &quot;youth&quot; and all, but nothing seemed to do Vampires better than VTM, so I don't see the need to immitate other vampires with compulsions, especially so because doing so goes against two of the most important themes vampies have going for them in VTM:<br /> <br /> 1-The Masquerade. How can we keep this thing up if the beast is constantly making clowns of us through messy criticals, beastial failures, compulsions on top of the rare frenzy? What V5 does is interesting for a few games or so, but it really stretches suspension of disbelief that such clowns could ever maintain a conspiracy for a few months, nevermind five hundred years, especially since blood potency makes you even more clownishly incompetent and thus elders are a comedic disaster only mitigated by having more backgrounds. <br /> <br /> Second, VtM is all about control;&quot; a Beast I am lest a Beast I become&quot;; you do mean things of your own voalition so you don't lose control and do worse. V5 has us do mean things outside of our control regardless of how well we approach things. Why should I take responsibility for something the red dice made me do? In V20, I would be to blame for putting myself in a possition where i am likely to frenzy. In V5 the Beast will rear its head any time I try and do something; my only recourse is to stay at home and have bloodbags delivered to me, or suicide; that's no fun is it? Anytime I screw up in V5 it's probably because 'the beast made me do it&quot;. Compulsions might work great for an alternative Malkavian or Brujah weakness but it doesn't work at all for the vampires who're trying to build businesses around themselves.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":8}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25794-mywifeisscary","name":"MyWifeIsScary","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25794_2.png","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3711"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-04-24T02:43:47-07:00","id":1445634,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Koronus</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1443592-the-official-v5-vs-v20-thread?p=1445631#post1445631\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Ah nope Remastering means the gameplay feels the same but it is only more resolution. For roleplay Books this means Hardcover instead of Softcover, Art and Book in Colour instead of B/W and Bugfixing. I think it means for RP Settings too, that the description is slightly improved too. So V20 is actually more Remaster then V5.<br /> I would say V5 is a Reboot where Setting and Gameplay are only vague the same and mostly only name stays the same.<br /> Btw I took the actual descriptions of Definitions from here:<br /> <a href=\"https://praxistipps.chip.de/remake-remaster-co-so-unterscheiden-sie-die-neuauflagen-von-games_125480\" target=\"_blank\">https://praxistipps.chip.de/remake-r...n-games_125480</a></div> </div> </div> </div>I had a longer post written up before but gave up on it as pointless. Since you bring this up, and I agree, I'll put some of those thoughts here.<br /> <br /> For instance, VTR2e adds Kindred Senses to account for the fluff saying that vamps have keener senses than humans. Something like that getting added into VTM would make sense, since the fluff in all editions has made similar claims.<br /> <br /> Likewise, VTR has systems for changing food sources, which were a bit woollier before in VTM (there are rules for developing Methuselah's Thirst, but they weren't in the core rules). Something like that isn't inappropriate, and so while I think Blood Potency in V5 is too granular (there should only be small fluctuations in power within a Generation, and changing food sources should be influenced more by your behaviour than it is in V5), it's also not a huge bugbear of mine.<br /> <br /> Those things alone would be remastering. Making the game as it was more accurate.<br /> <br /> But then V5 adds in things that were never there before: Resonances, You Are What You Eat, trait caps at 5, restrictive Feeding Styles, etc. One or two of these things might be okay, but all of them together make it feel more like a reboot or reimagining. Combine that with a big shake up of the metaplot, rather than tweaks, and it does feel like a different game. <br /> <br /> Maybe it's a remix, since it borrows liberally from VTR and VTM, with loads of stuff from MET, as though it were a collection of someone's homebrew rules that have been made official. There's nothing wrong with learning from different iterations of the game, but OPP always acknowledged that VTM players and VTR players often had different priorities.<br /> <br /> Obviously, if you wanted a different game with V5, that's good. If you didn't, then it makes sense you wouldn't like what's there.<br /> <br /> TBH, I think if V5 had been presented as an alternate timeline setting, that would have avoided lots of the aggro. But I can see why, from a business perspective, they didn't.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Writer, publisher, performer<br /> Mostly he/his, sometimes she/her IRL <a href=\"https://adam-lowe.com\" target=\"_blank\">https://adam-lowe.com</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":6}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5291-adambeyoncelowe","name":"adambeyoncelowe","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5291_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2802"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-04-24T03:25:49-07:00","id":1445635,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Koronus</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1443592-the-official-v5-vs-v20-thread?p=1445631#post1445631\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Ah nope Remastering means the gameplay feels the same but it is only more resolution. ]</div> </div> </div> </div>I think it does.<br /> <br /> I think V5 hones in, with laser focus, on all the themes outlined in the original, with the same attitude, tone and intent. System-wise it does it better with less ambiguity and looseness in the mechanics. It is the game that Mark Rein-Hagen set out to make in 1991 - a reversal of some of the softening/bloat that had accrued over the years and found its way in to V20 - and his contribution/influence was acutely felt in the making of V5.<br /> <br /> So we disagree on that.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":2517,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2517-trippy","user":"Trippy","date":". 04-24-2021, 06:33 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2517-trippy","name":"Trippy","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2517_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1018"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-04-24T03:36:22-07:00","id":1445637,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MyWifeIsScary</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1443592-the-official-v5-vs-v20-thread?p=1445633#post1445633\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">1-The Masquerade. How can we keep this thing up if the beast is constantly making clowns of us through messy criticals, beastial failures, compulsions on top of the rare frenzy? What V5 does is interesting for a few games or so, but it really stretches suspension of disbelief that such clowns could ever maintain a conspiracy for a few months, nevermind five hundred years, especially since blood potency makes you even more clownishly incompetent and thus elders are a comedic disaster only mitigated by having more backgrounds.<br /> <br /> Second, VtM is all about control;&quot; a Beast I am lest a Beast I become&quot;; you do mean things of your own voalition so you don't lose control and do worse. V5 has us do mean things outside of our control regardless of how well we approach things. Why should I take responsibility for something the red dice made me do? In V20, I would be to blame for putting myself in a possition where i am likely to frenzy. In V5 the Beast will rear its head any time I try and do something; my only recourse is to stay at home and have bloodbags delivered to me, or suicide; that's no fun is it? Anytime I screw up in V5 it's probably because 'the beast made me do it&quot;. Compulsions might work great for an alternative Malkavian or Brujah weakness but it doesn't work at all for the vampires who're trying to build businesses around themselves.</div> </div> </div> </div>That's technically correct, but the idea of messy criticals and bestial failures seems to be trying to duplicate the behavior of fictional vampires like Jerry Dandrige and Barlow and various True Blood vampires rather than being a realistic portrayal of creatures who would own the world of finance and politics. It's a mechanic to represent characters who lack self-control but rarely go absolutely berzerk. Hence the frenzy checks in this edition being really quite forgiving, and the results of messy crits and bestial failures being far more common.<br /> <br /> Now me, I like playing Dandrige and Barlow and Erik Northman with all their routine failures at self-control. I adore it, actually. So I have zero, absolutely zero complaints about the messy/bestial mechanic. That I couldn't realistically rule the world as this character is...whatever...shrug...to me.<br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3598-cajunkhan","name":"CajunKhan","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3598_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1700"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-04-24T04:15:46-07:00","id":1445638,"title":"","content":"Issue is you could easily make -compulsions- a bloodline weakness in V20, perhaps make it a malkavian problem. You can enjoy that if you want to without stepping on everyone else's fun. In V5, you're all beholden to compulsions, even if you have concepts that make it a terrible and stupid idea. V20 is inclusive. V5 is exclusive.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":7}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25794-mywifeisscary","name":"MyWifeIsScary","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25794_2.png","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3711"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-04-24T04:23:54-07:00","id":1445639,"title":"","content":"I enjoy it regardless of the clan I am playing. Being forced to play a Malk if I want to enjoy messy crits/bestials would be exclusive to me, forcing me to play a clan I am not fond of in order to get at a mechanic I enjoy.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3598-cajunkhan","name":"CajunKhan","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3598_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1700"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-04-24T04:43:38-07:00","id":1445642,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MyWifeIsScary</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1443592-the-official-v5-vs-v20-thread?p=1445638#post1445638\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Issue is you could easily make -compulsions- a bloodline weakness in V20, perhaps make it a malkavian problem. You can enjoy that if you want to without stepping on everyone else's fun. In V5, you're all beholden to compulsions, even if you have concepts that make it a terrible and stupid idea. V20 is inclusive. V5 is exclusive.</div> </div> </div> </div>For, me, V5 is an authentic experience of dealing with the emotions and drives of being a vampire. It does what it says on the tin - a game of personal horror. V20 is watering down that experience, by comparison.You can call that inclusive if you want, but if wanted inclusive, I\u2019d play GURPS.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":2517,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2517-trippy","user":"Trippy","date":". 04-24-2021, 07:53 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2517-trippy","name":"Trippy","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2517_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1018"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-04-24T04:54:34-07:00","id":1445644,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Morbus</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1443592-the-official-v5-vs-v20-thread?p=1445627#post1445627\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Yeah the Masquerade was still a thing in Requiem. There's even a whole faction who's dedicated to its preservation (among other things).<br /> <br /> The fact that vampires could not be caught on tape just meant that said faction did not need to be a global conspiracy powerful enough to prevent a worldwide breach if needed (and a video on the net could quickly become such a thing). <b>At least until v5 when the Masquerade shattered but not really because... no reason given.</b><br /> And conveniently enough the Camarilla is no longer a global superpower because... well who need to maintain the Masquerade if Humans can gatekeep other humans by themselves?</div> </div> </div> </div>I feel preventing a global panic and upending the world order is a pretty decent reason itself.<br /> <br /> <i>&quot;Listen. Every week there's a panic about some puny little bug. Now how do you think it would be if this got out? Hm? You'll have paranoia, you'll have vigilantes, you'll have people running back to religion in droves. The next thing you know, you'll have the Archbishop up for Prime Minister. I don't fancy living in Iran, do you?&quot; </i>- Vaughn, Ultraviolet<br /> <br /> I feel that the idea the government wouldn't do it kind of loses its strength when the most recent RL administration was full of lies at every conceivable level about a global yet undeniable threat.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Author of <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Cthulhu-Armageddon-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01KUOM7SI/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982844&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Cthulhu+Armageddon\" target=\"_blank\">Cthulhu Armageddon</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Teenage-Weredeer-Bright-Falls-Mysteries-ebook/dp/B075TTN2FN/ref=sr_1_2?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982717&amp;sr=1-2&amp;keywords=Weredeer#customerReviews\" target=\"_blank\">I was a Teenage Weredeer</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Straight-Outta-Fangton-Comedic-Vampire-ebook/dp/B01KNHICCC/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982774&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Straight+Outta+Fangton\" target=\"_blank\">Straight Outta Fangton</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Lucifers-Star-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01MDM9MCT/ref=mt_kindle?_encoding=UTF8&amp;me=&amp;qid=\" target=\"_blank\">Lucifer's Star</a>, </i>and the <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Rules-Supervillainy-Saga-Book-ebook/dp/B07MB89S33/\" target=\"_blank\">Supervillainy Saga</a>.</i><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":12002,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","user":"CTPhipps","date":". 04-24-2021, 07:57 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","name":"CTPhipps","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12002_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13933"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-04-24T04:55:31-07:00","id":1445645,"title":"","content":"You know if I have to roll for emotions they're not really mine now, are they?<br /> <br /> <i>Yes, I'm aware V20 isn't perfect for that, but it's a whole lot better. *Rolls conscience* </i>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":25794,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25794-mywifeisscary","user":"MyWifeIsScary","date":". 04-24-2021, 08:00 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":7}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25794-mywifeisscary","name":"MyWifeIsScary","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25794_2.png","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3711"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-04-24T05:01:56-07:00","id":1445646,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MyWifeIsScary</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1443592-the-official-v5-vs-v20-thread?p=1445645#post1445645\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">You know if I have to roll for emotions they're not really mine now, are they?<br /> <br /> <i>Yes, I'm aware V20 isn't perfect for that, but it's a whole lot better. *Rolls conscience* </i></div> </div> </div> </div>I think V5 is pretty good at generating real emotions, going on these threads at least.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2517-trippy","name":"Trippy","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2517_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1018"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-04-24T05:02:02-07:00","id":1445647,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CajunKhan</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1443592-the-official-v5-vs-v20-thread?p=1445639#post1445639\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I enjoy it regardless of the clan I am playing. Being forced to play a Malk if I want to enjoy messy crits/bestials would be exclusive to me, forcing me to play a clan I am not fond of in order to get at a mechanic I enjoy.</div> </div> </div> </div>Make up a bloodline, or consider it a 5 point flaw then.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":7}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25794-mywifeisscary","name":"MyWifeIsScary","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25794_2.png","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3711"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-04-24T05:30:01-07:00","id":1445651,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Trippy</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1443592-the-official-v5-vs-v20-thread?p=1445635#post1445635\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I think it does.<br /> <br /> I think V5 hones in, with laser focus, on all the themes outlined in the original, with the same attitude, tone and intent. System-wise it does it better with less ambiguity and looseness in the mechanics. It is the game that Mark Rein-Hagen set out to make in 1991 - a reversal of some of the softening/bloat that had accrued over the years and found its way in to V20 - and his contribution/influence was acutely felt in the making of V5.<br /> <br /> So we disagree on that.</div> </div> </div> </div>It is totally different. For example that with Blood Power 3 alone you can not get saturated by animals or blood conserves anymore is a BIG Retcon. For one it makes it impossible to play an ethical vampire that stays away from humans and it makes the Seagangrel impossible.<br /> The sea gangrel are Gangrels that are very old and stay away from the world exisiting in the deepest sea where no more light shines feeding from animals like whales.<br /> <br /> Then as it whas mentioned before you can not really do disciples anymore because of this constant hunger and potence is now costing and not just being passive anymore.<br /> The hunger is messing up things too.<br /> Then the new humanity system actually forces you to fawn over a human and micromanage his live.<br /> In V5 is the Beast made me do it a common and accepted excuse while before if you lost controll it is your own fault.<br /> <br /> The whole telling is even different. Even if we ignore the lore things like Pyramid exist not anymore, the Ivory Tower is an exclusive society instead being like Rom claiming to rule over everyone, vampire hunters everywhere.<br /> Alone from Blood Potency the telling is that the eldest are neither powerfull enough to enforce getting some pure neonates full and served to them as dinner because for filling them two normal humans needs to get drained.<br /> While technically in V20 and before you would need twice as much humans for getting completely saturated it is because they have so much that goes inside and not that human blood does not fill them.<br /> Methusalahs first where more of a spook story because the Methusalah are so old and powerfull.<br /> Now they are not as powerfull anymore.<br /> Sorry but V5 is clearly a Reboot or as adambeyoncelowe said a remix.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>As I am from Austria I need to clarify two things.<br /> First my native language is german and so please point out if the english I write is broken so I can improve.<br /> Second I do not own VTMV beyond first three books nor any line after M20 Corebook because it is not out there and I wait for the translation.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":6}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26160-koronus","name":"Koronus","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2020"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"366"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-04-24T05:36:42-07:00","id":1445652,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Koronus</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1443592-the-official-v5-vs-v20-thread?p=1445651#post1445651\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> It is totally different. For example that with Blood Power 3 alone you can not get saturated by animals or blood conserves anymore is a BIG Retcon. For one it makes it impossible to play an ethical vampire that stays away from humans and it makes the Seagangrel impossible.<br /> The sea gangrel are Gangrels that are very old and stay away from the world exisiting in the deepest sea where no more light shines feeding from animals like whales.<br /> <br /> Then as it whas mentioned before you can not really do disciples anymore because of this constant hunger and potence is now costing and not just being passive anymore.<br /> The hunger is messing up things too.<br /> Then the new humanity system actually forces you to fawn over a human and micromanage his live.<br /> In V5 is the Beast made me do it a common and accepted excuse while before if you lost controll it is your own fault.<br /> <br /> The whole telling is even different. Even if we ignore the lore things like Pyramid exist not anymore, the Ivory Tower is an exclusive society instead being like Rom claiming to rule over everyone, vampire hunters everywhere.<br /> Alone from Blood Potency the telling is that the eldest are neither powerfull enough to enforce getting some pure neonates full and served to them as dinner because for filling them two normal humans needs to get drained.<br /> While technically in V20 and before you would need twice as much humans for getting completely saturated it is because they have so much that goes inside and not that human blood does not fill them.<br /> Methusalahs first where more of a spook story because the Methusalah are so old and powerfull.<br /> Now they are not as powerfull anymore.<br /> Sorry but V5 is clearly a Reboot or as adambeyoncelowe said a remix.</div> </div> </div> </div>1. Random Interjection but there's a big irony for Gangrel, Nosferatu, and Tzimisce of all people. <b>Animalism</b> has been adjusted to be FAR more important to be an ethical vampire than it was in previous editions. <b>Animal Succulence</b> allows you feed on the blood of animals even if you're a much-much older and powerful vampire. So being an &quot;ethical&quot; vampire is either a matter of choosing to play a High Generation vampire, a Thin Blood, or getting the Animalism Discipline versus being an impossibility.<br /> <br /> Consensualists are also people that are both incredible morons in-universe and also apparently common enough to be a thing among ethical undead too.<br /> <br /> 2. The Ivory Tower claiming all vampires were members of the Camarilla but not including:<br /> <br /> * Independents (ESPECIALLY the Giovanni)<br /> * Sabbat<br /> * Caitiff<br /> * Thin Bloods<br /> * Inconnu<br /> * Kuei Jin, Ashirra, Laibon<br /> <br /> is a thing that wasn't created by V5. The only real difference is the Anarchs are officially expelled now.<br /> <br /> 3. It was canon that even when &quot;full&quot; that vampires still lusted for blood before V5. That was due to it always being an Addiction Metaphor.<br /> <br /> 4. Its more complex but Blood Potency still makes Methusalehs ridiculously powerful. But I've stated my issues with Amalgams and lack of Elder Disciplines.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Author of <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Cthulhu-Armageddon-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01KUOM7SI/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982844&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Cthulhu+Armageddon\" target=\"_blank\">Cthulhu Armageddon</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Teenage-Weredeer-Bright-Falls-Mysteries-ebook/dp/B075TTN2FN/ref=sr_1_2?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982717&amp;sr=1-2&amp;keywords=Weredeer#customerReviews\" target=\"_blank\">I was a Teenage Weredeer</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Straight-Outta-Fangton-Comedic-Vampire-ebook/dp/B01KNHICCC/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982774&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Straight+Outta+Fangton\" target=\"_blank\">Straight Outta Fangton</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Lucifers-Star-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01MDM9MCT/ref=mt_kindle?_encoding=UTF8&amp;me=&amp;qid=\" target=\"_blank\">Lucifer's Star</a>, </i>and the <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Rules-Supervillainy-Saga-Book-ebook/dp/B07MB89S33/\" target=\"_blank\">Supervillainy Saga</a>.</i><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":12002,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","user":"CTPhipps","date":". 04-24-2021, 08:44 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","name":"CTPhipps","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12002_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13933"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-04-24T06:31:18-07:00","id":1445659,"title":"","content":"My problem with using high Blood Potency to make elders/methuselahs more powerful is that it's too complicated for people to intuitively grasp. Pre-V5 rules were very simple. Traits for elders can range from 6 to 10, and they can store/spend more blood points. Boom, done.<br /> <br /> I honestly have no idea why Blood Potency makes V5 elders so powerful; something about surge bonuses being bigger? I don't have the inclination to look it up in the V5 book, as I don't use V5's rules and it doesn't make a difference to me either way, so I'm largely taking Matthew Dawkins' word that it's true (I remember him also saying somewhere that elders are still more powerful than people give them credit for). But even if it is true, the fact that &quot;V5 elders are weak&quot; could be so many people's takeaway is a serious problem with the mechanics. Your mechanics are supposed to clearly illustrate how the world functions, not obfuscate it. They can be the best mechanics in the world and I'd still consider them bad game design if they lead to such prevalent misconceptions among the fandom.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://blood-and-bourbon.obsidianportal.com/\" target=\"_blank\">Blood and Bourbon</a>, my New Orleans-based Vampire chronicle.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":10}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3110-false-epiphany","name":"False Epiphany","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3110_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"748"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-04-24T06:44:31-07:00","id":1445660,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>False Epiphany</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1443592-the-official-v5-vs-v20-thread?p=1445659#post1445659\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">My problem with using high Blood Potency to make elders/methuselahs more powerful is that it's too complicated for people to intuitively grasp. Pre-V5 rules were very simple. Traits for elders can range from 6 to 10, and they can store/spend more blood points. Boom, done.<br /> <br /> I honestly have no idea why Blood Potency makes V5 elders so powerful; something about surge bonuses being bigger? I don't have the inclination to look it up in the V5 book, as I don't use V5's rules and it doesn't make a difference to me either way, so I'm largely taking Matthew Dawkins' word that it's true (I remember him also saying somewhere that elders are still more powerful than people give them credit for). But even if it is true, the fact that &quot;V5 elders are weak&quot; could be so many people's takeaway is a serious problem with the mechanics. Your mechanics are supposed to clearly illustrate how the world functions, not obfuscate it. They can be the best mechanics in the world and I'd still consider them bad game design if they lead to such prevalent misconceptions among the fandom.</div> </div> </div> </div>The short version is that you can pump up your stats a large amount, heal a lot more damage, and require far less effort when using Disciplines. Theoretically, this does eliminate most of the problems of Attributes over 5 if not Disciplines.<br /> <br /> Example:<br /> <br /> According to V5 rules, Helena has Blood Potency 7. This means that she can add 4 dice during a Blood Surge.<br /> <br /> Which means that she naturally has Strength 5 and Dexterity 9 but goes up to Strength 9, Dexterity 9, and so on. The big difference from other is you Blood Surge one Attribute Pool at a time versus one Attribute. So you improve ALL your Physicals, Socials, or whatnot with one use of it.<br /> <br /> If we still had appearance, she'd &quot;normally&quot; be Appearance 5 and naturally one of the most beautiful women on Earth (I use Angelina Jolie as a basis because why not) and yet would be Appearance 9. However, she can still up her Socials with a Blood Surge to the superhuman level she's famous for.<br /> <br /> The big difference is that supernatural potency is not &quot;on&quot; for Methuselahs like them at all times. They have to activate it.<br /> <br /> So V5 rules wise, Helena hasn't actually &quot;lost&quot; any of her Superhuman Attributes. Just Disciplines.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Author of <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Cthulhu-Armageddon-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01KUOM7SI/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982844&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Cthulhu+Armageddon\" target=\"_blank\">Cthulhu Armageddon</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Teenage-Weredeer-Bright-Falls-Mysteries-ebook/dp/B075TTN2FN/ref=sr_1_2?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982717&amp;sr=1-2&amp;keywords=Weredeer#customerReviews\" target=\"_blank\">I was a Teenage Weredeer</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Straight-Outta-Fangton-Comedic-Vampire-ebook/dp/B01KNHICCC/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982774&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Straight+Outta+Fangton\" target=\"_blank\">Straight Outta Fangton</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Lucifers-Star-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01MDM9MCT/ref=mt_kindle?_encoding=UTF8&amp;me=&amp;qid=\" target=\"_blank\">Lucifer's Star</a>, </i>and the <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Rules-Supervillainy-Saga-Book-ebook/dp/B07MB89S33/\" target=\"_blank\">Supervillainy Saga</a>.</i><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":12002,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","user":"CTPhipps","date":". 04-24-2021, 09:47 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","name":"CTPhipps","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12002_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13933"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-04-24T07:44:54-07:00","id":1445663,"title":"","content":"<a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar12002_2.jpeg');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"12002\" data-vbnamecard=\"12002\">CTPhipps</a> actually Animalism only allows you mearly to survive without feeding from humans but not that feeding from Animals is more effective then from humans like before.<br /> The Tier 3 power only unlocks for Ancilla from 5-9. Generation what whas possible before by default before and makes it that Elder merely being able to survive without using blood while before it actually allowed you by feeding from animals not merely to survive but to flourish. Sorry but I am not convinced.<br /> This forced feels like having to play as a Humanity 9+ vampire which is for long not really funny.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>As I am from Austria I need to clarify two things.<br /> First my native language is german and so please point out if the english I write is broken so I can improve.<br /> Second I do not own VTMV beyond first three books nor any line after M20 Corebook because it is not out there and I wait for the translation.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26160-koronus","name":"Koronus","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2020"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"366"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-04-24T07:56:04-07:00","id":1445664,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CTPhipps</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1443592-the-official-v5-vs-v20-thread?p=1445660#post1445660\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> The short version is that you can pump up your stats a large amount, heal a lot more damage, and require far less effort when using Disciplines. Theoretically, this does eliminate most of the problems of Attributes over 5 if not Disciplines.<br /> <br /> Example:<br /> <br /> According to V5 rules, Helena has Blood Potency 7. This means that she can add 4 dice during a Blood Surge.<br /> <br /> Which means that she naturally has Strength 5 and Dexterity 9 but goes up to Strength 9, Dexterity 9, and so on. The big difference from other is you Blood Surge one Attribute Pool at a time versus one Attribute. So you improve ALL your Physicals, Socials, or whatnot with one use of it.<br /> <br /> If we still had appearance, she'd &amp;quot;normally&amp;quot; be Appearance 5 and naturally one of the most beautiful women on Earth (I use Angelina Jolie as a basis because why not) and yet would be Appearance 9. However, she can still up her Socials with a Blood Surge to the superhuman level she's famous for.<br /> <br /> The big difference is that supernatural potency is not &amp;quot;on&amp;quot; for Methuselahs like them at all times. They have to activate it.<br /> <br /> So V5 rules wise, Helena hasn't actually &amp;quot;lost&amp;quot; any of her Superhuman Attributes. Just Disciplines.</div> </div> </div> </div>Unless you\u2019re talking House Rules, Blood Surge only adds dice to a single Attribute for a single roll. On the next turn, you can rouse check for another Surge to bump an Attribute for another single roll.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":7}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24351-garygeneric","name":"Garygeneric","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24351_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"108"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-04-24T08:47:49-07:00","id":1445671,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Garygeneric</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1443592-the-official-v5-vs-v20-thread?p=1445664#post1445664\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Unless you\u2019re talking House Rules, Blood Surge only adds dice to a single Attribute for a single roll. On the next turn, you can rouse check for another Surge to bump an Attribute for another single roll.</div> </div> </div> </div>It said Mental, Social, and Physical so I took it for all three. Odd as a single dice roll to include multiple ones may be.<br /> <br /> And I wouldn't present House Rules as the canon rules.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Author of <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Cthulhu-Armageddon-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01KUOM7SI/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982844&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Cthulhu+Armageddon\" target=\"_blank\">Cthulhu Armageddon</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Teenage-Weredeer-Bright-Falls-Mysteries-ebook/dp/B075TTN2FN/ref=sr_1_2?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982717&amp;sr=1-2&amp;keywords=Weredeer#customerReviews\" target=\"_blank\">I was a Teenage Weredeer</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Straight-Outta-Fangton-Comedic-Vampire-ebook/dp/B01KNHICCC/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982774&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Straight+Outta+Fangton\" target=\"_blank\">Straight Outta Fangton</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Lucifers-Star-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01MDM9MCT/ref=mt_kindle?_encoding=UTF8&amp;me=&amp;qid=\" target=\"_blank\">Lucifer's Star</a>, </i>and the <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Rules-Supervillainy-Saga-Book-ebook/dp/B07MB89S33/\" target=\"_blank\">Supervillainy Saga</a>.</i><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":12002,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","user":"CTPhipps","date":". 04-24-2021, 11:51 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","name":"CTPhipps","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12002_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13933"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-04-24T08:54:19-07:00","id":1445672,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Garygeneric</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1443592-the-official-v5-vs-v20-thread?p=1445664#post1445664\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Unless you\u2019re talking House Rules, Blood Surge only adds dice to a single Attribute for a single roll. On the next turn, you can rouse check for another Surge to bump an Attribute for another single roll.</div> </div> </div> </div>Does high blood potency let you reroll rouse checks for attributes?If not,Helena risks hitting hunger 5 quite quickly and be unable to rouse at all.<br /> <br /> <br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":6}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25477-perisa","name":"Perisa","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-04-24T09:34:14-07:00","id":1445678,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Perisa</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1443592-the-official-v5-vs-v20-thread?p=1445672#post1445672\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Does high blood potency let you reroll rouse checks for attributes?If not,Helena risks hitting hunger 5 quite quickly and be unable to rouse at all.</div> </div> </div> </div>The benefits of Blood Potency 7 mean Helena can re-roll Discilpline Rouse checks of 4 or below. She also gets three extra dice when using DIsciplines.<br /> <br /> In other words, Helena can use most of her powers without ever gaining Hunger.<br /> <br /> The rules are a bit complex but generally the stronger you are as a Kindred, the less Hungry you are for the more stuff you do.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Author of <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Cthulhu-Armageddon-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01KUOM7SI/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982844&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Cthulhu+Armageddon\" target=\"_blank\">Cthulhu Armageddon</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Teenage-Weredeer-Bright-Falls-Mysteries-ebook/dp/B075TTN2FN/ref=sr_1_2?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982717&amp;sr=1-2&amp;keywords=Weredeer#customerReviews\" target=\"_blank\">I was a Teenage Weredeer</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Straight-Outta-Fangton-Comedic-Vampire-ebook/dp/B01KNHICCC/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982774&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Straight+Outta+Fangton\" target=\"_blank\">Straight Outta Fangton</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Lucifers-Star-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01MDM9MCT/ref=mt_kindle?_encoding=UTF8&amp;me=&amp;qid=\" target=\"_blank\">Lucifer's Star</a>, </i>and the <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Rules-Supervillainy-Saga-Book-ebook/dp/B07MB89S33/\" target=\"_blank\">Supervillainy Saga</a>.</i><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":12002,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","user":"CTPhipps","date":". 04-24-2021, 12:37 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","name":"CTPhipps","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12002_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13933"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-04-24T09:57:31-07:00","id":1445680,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CTPhipps</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1443592-the-official-v5-vs-v20-thread?p=1445660#post1445660\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The short version is that you can pump up your stats a large amount, heal a lot more damage, and require far less effort when using Disciplines. Theoretically, this does eliminate most of the problems of Attributes over 5 if not Disciplines.<br /> <br /> Example:<br /> <br /> According to V5 rules, Helena has Blood Potency 7. This means that she can add 4 dice during a Blood Surge.<br /> <br /> Which means that she naturally has Strength 5 and Dexterity 9 but goes up to Strength 9, Dexterity 9, and so on. The big difference from other is you Blood Surge one Attribute Pool at a time versus one Attribute. So you improve ALL your Physicals, Socials, or whatnot with one use of it.<br /> <br /> If we still had appearance, she'd &quot;normally&quot; be Appearance 5 and naturally one of the most beautiful women on Earth (I use Angelina Jolie as a basis because why not) and yet would be Appearance 9. However, she can still up her Socials with a Blood Surge to the superhuman level she's famous for.<br /> <br /> The big difference is that supernatural potency is not &quot;on&quot; for Methuselahs like them at all times. They have to activate it.<br /> <br /> So V5 rules wise, Helena hasn't actually &quot;lost&quot; any of her Superhuman Attributes. Just Disciplines.</div> </div> </div> </div>This, IMO, is fairly poor mechanics design.<br /> <br /> First, it's less intuitive. Appearance 9 is four more dice over Appearance 5. Got it. I can read that off the NPC's statblock in a single line. The bonus from Blood Surge at Blood Potency 7 is... what? Also, I have to remember that new rule is a thing, when this is a new edition for a very old game. It just doesn't do as good a job conveying the NPC's capabilities at a glance. Helena's stats say Charisma 5, and my gut reaction is, &quot;Oh, so the fabled Helen of Troy isn't leagues beyond mortal women. Even though that's what the developers want.&quot;<br /> <br /> Second, it's much less cool to have to activate a power, or to pay a cost for a power, than to have it free/always on. In my experience, free/always on powers are VASTLY more appealing to players. If I were playing a superhumanly beautiful elder PC, I would much rather have Appearance 6 than be able to spend blood to roll extra Appearance dice to the same numeric effect. Or even to better numeric effect. It's just inherently cooler to always have the bigger number, no fuss no muss. There is 30 years of history and sense of scale behind those numbers.<br /> <br /> All of this would be one thing, if V5's developers were designing a brand new game. (I don't think a <i>good</i> thing, but it'd still be one thing.) But when it comes on the heel of 6+ traits getting nuked... the fan reaction of &quot;so elders are weaker&quot; was fairly predictable, even if it wasn't true. Paradox ignored the social aspect of these rules changes, and the fact they would foster a misconception among the player base that more attentive/devoted fans would have to correct.<br /> <br /> Just a bad decision on numerous levels. Should've kept 6+ traits. Way simpler.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://blood-and-bourbon.obsidianportal.com/\" target=\"_blank\">Blood and Bourbon</a>, my New Orleans-based Vampire chronicle.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":7}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3110-false-epiphany","name":"False Epiphany","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3110_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"748"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-04-24T10:07:28-07:00","id":1445682,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CTPhipps</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1443592-the-official-v5-vs-v20-thread?p=1445678#post1445678\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> The benefits of Blood Potency 7 mean Helena can re-roll Discilpline Rouse checks of 4 or below. She also gets three extra dice when using DIsciplines.<br /> <br /> In other words, Helena can use most of her powers without ever gaining Hunger.<br /> <br /> The rules are a bit complex but generally the stronger you are as a Kindred, the less Hungry you are for the more stuff you do.</div> </div> </div> </div>Yes I know that that is true for disciplines but Is it the same for attributes?If not,I would say that that makes a difference.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25477-perisa","name":"Perisa","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-04-24T12:25:42-07:00","id":1445692,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Perisa</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1443592-the-official-v5-vs-v20-thread?p=1445682#post1445682\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Yes I know that that is true for disciplines but Is it the same for attributes?If not,I would say that that makes a difference.</div> </div> </div> </div>Re-rolls are for Disciplines only. So yes, she only gets her enhanced beauty for a short period of time. It's not a realistic alternative to 5+ stats in the long run. Maybe in combat, though.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Writer, publisher, performer<br /> Mostly he/his, sometimes she/her IRL <a href=\"https://adam-lowe.com\" target=\"_blank\">https://adam-lowe.com</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5291-adambeyoncelowe","name":"adambeyoncelowe","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5291_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2802"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-04-24T12:45:07-07:00","id":1445696,"title":"","content":"Here's the V5 wording if it helps:<br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Any vampire can call upon their <br /> Blood to temporarily augment their Attributes, whether Physical, <br /> Social, or Mental. When the character wills a Blood Surge, the player <br /> can add a number of dice to a dice <br /> pool incorporating an Attribute. <br /> The number of dice a Blood Surge <br /> adds depends on the character\u2019s <br /> Blood Potency; characters can only <br /> use Blood Surge once per roll.<br /> <br /> [...]<br /> <br /> Blood Surge applies only to a <br /> single roll of the dice. </div> </div> </div>The key bits being Physical, Mental OR Social, A dice pool incorporating AN Attribute, ONCE per roll and A SINGLE roll.<br /> <br /> So it only applies to one roll using any one Attribute. That doesn't even mean it lasts for all Strength checks on a turn. That means it lasts for one Strength check on a single turn and that's it.<br /> <br /> This is another one of those examples where the RAW are different to what has been claimed. It does make me wonder if everyone is playing house rules and just glosses over what's actually in the books? It happens!","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Writer, publisher, performer<br /> Mostly he/his, sometimes she/her IRL <a href=\"https://adam-lowe.com\" target=\"_blank\">https://adam-lowe.com</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":7}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5291-adambeyoncelowe","name":"adambeyoncelowe","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5291_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2802"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-04-24T12:57:57-07:00","id":1445700,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>adambeyoncelowe</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1443592-the-official-v5-vs-v20-thread?p=1445692#post1445692\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Re-rolls are for Disciplines only. So yes, she only gets her enhanced beauty for a short period of time. It's not a realistic alternative to 5+ stats in the long run. Maybe in combat, though.</div> </div> </div> </div>I see,thank you,the upper end of the power scale does seem to have come down a bit.More powerful elder than \u201dblood god\u201d.It makes sense for V5 though.<br /> Has anyone run a game with higher blood potency?The reason I ask is that my group is mostly interested in Vampire for the historical aspects and the ability to run \u201dhighlander-like\u201d games.<br /> We are reluctant to move to V5 because difficulty of handling hunger with a blood potency of 4+.<br /> It`s mostly the randomness that feels like it could be a problem and I was wondering if there was a way to make it follow the narrative more,rather than shape it?<br /> I`m not sure how to explain it well.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25477-perisa","name":"Perisa","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-04-24T13:12:50-07:00","id":1445703,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>adambeyoncelowe</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1443592-the-official-v5-vs-v20-thread?p=1445696#post1445696\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">This is another one of those examples where the RAW are different to what has been claimed. It does make me wonder if everyone is playing house rules and just glosses over what's actually in the books? It happens!</div> </div> </div> </div>I mean, I do. V5's mechanics have... a lot of issues (though some pretty great ideas), and Masquerade's are now 30 years old, so I've just played with Requiem rules. Heavily house ruled, the point of now being its own game system.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CTPhipps</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">The benefits of Blood Potency 7 mean Helena can re-roll Discilpline Rouse checks of 4 or below. She also gets three extra dice when using DIsciplines.<br /> <br /> In other words, Helena can use most of her powers without ever gaining Hunger.<br /> <br /> The rules are a bit complex but generally the stronger you are as a Kindred, the less Hungry you are for the more stuff you do.</div> </div> </div> </div>This is too complex for my tastes. I introduced Hunger and Rouse checks into my game, but I modeled bigger blood pools by removing Rouse costs from (most) Disciplines with a lower rating than the vampire's Blood Potency.<br /> <br /> Players have loved it. Very easy to understand, and cool to be able to call on your weaker powers without any costs or rolls.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://blood-and-bourbon.obsidianportal.com/\" target=\"_blank\">Blood and Bourbon</a>, my New Orleans-based Vampire chronicle.","edited":{"userid":3110,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3110-false-epiphany","user":"False Epiphany","date":". 04-24-2021, 04:15 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3110-false-epiphany","name":"False Epiphany","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3110_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"748"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-04-24T13:18:09-07:00","id":1445704,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Koronus</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1443592-the-official-v5-vs-v20-thread?p=1445651#post1445651\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> It is totally different. For example that with Blood Power 3 alone you can not get saturated by animals or blood conserves anymore is a BIG Retcon. For one it makes it impossible to play an ethical vampire that stays away from humans and it makes the Seagangrel impossible.<br /> The sea gangrel are Gangrels that are very old and stay away from the world exisiting in the deepest sea where no more light shines feeding from animals like whales.<br /> <br /> Then as it whas mentioned before you can not really do disciples anymore because of this constant hunger and potence is now costing and not just being passive anymore.<br /> The hunger is messing up things too.<br /> Then the new humanity system actually forces you to fawn over a human and micromanage his live.<br /> In V5 is the Beast made me do it a common and accepted excuse while before if you lost controll it is your own fault.<br /> <br /> The whole telling is even different. Even if we ignore the lore things like Pyramid exist not anymore, the Ivory Tower is an exclusive society instead being like Rom claiming to rule over everyone, vampire hunters everywhere.<br /> Alone from Blood Potency the telling is that the eldest are neither powerfull enough to enforce getting some pure neonates full and served to them as dinner because for filling them two normal humans needs to get drained.<br /> While technically in V20 and before you would need twice as much humans for getting completely saturated it is because they have so much that goes inside and not that human blood does not fill them.<br /> Methusalahs first where more of a spook story because the Methusalah are so old and powerfull.<br /> Now they are not as powerfull anymore.<br /> Sorry but V5 is clearly a Reboot or as adambeyoncelowe said a remix.</div> </div> </div> </div>There is actually predatory types in V5 that has vampires staying away from humans, and in my chronicle we have a player who does that exactly too. So what you are saying about that is incorrect.<br /> <br /> And no, it isn\u2019t retconning. It is providing a mechanical representation of what has always been talked about in the game - discussions of the Hunger and the Beast are one of the most prominent aspects of the game in its writing. So, again, I just totally disagree with your assessment of V5, its intent and its mechanics in practice. The \u2018remastering\u2019 was my metaphor and it is the one that fits my experience. I cannot account for everybody\u2019s tastes - but for me, V5 realises aspects of the game that were <i>always </i>intended - and the endorsement/contributions of Mark Rein-Hagen, as the original creator, is enough proof of that.<br /> <br /> When people complain about how Hunger and Humanity are now prominent in their decision making as a character, to me that is the whole point of playing a vampire. If they didn\u2019t feel compelled to play the game in reference to these things in V20, well again, that shows up as a flaw for V20. The criticism, much stated in reviews for VTM, that &quot;<span style=\"font-family:Arial, Helvetica, sans-serif\"><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-size:12px\">the rules pay only lip service to their stated purpose\u201d is basically what people are claiming they like about V20 here. When I play Vampire, I want the experience, directly through the mechanics, of all the drives and pressures of vampiric existence. If I wanted to play something with less of that stuff, I\u2019d probably play something else instead.</span></span></span>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":2517,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2517-trippy","user":"Trippy","date":". 04-24-2021, 04:32 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2517-trippy","name":"Trippy","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2517_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1018"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-04-24T14:21:42-07:00","id":1445708,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>adambeyoncelowe</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1443592-the-official-v5-vs-v20-thread?p=1445696#post1445696\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The key bits being Physical, Mental OR Social, A dice pool incorporating AN Attribute, ONCE per roll and A SINGLE roll.</div> </div> </div> </div>Yep. This is one of the bigger points on the &quot;weaker elders&quot; thing, because while the WoD games have never been kind to powerful individuals trying to fend off a group of weaker foes, this is a massive reduction in capability.<br /> <br /> Helena, back in pre-V5 rules, could pump herself up to Str 12/Dex 12/Stam 12 for a scene and still have more vitae left than starting PCs can top up at (35/50). That means she could, with Attributes and blood alone, roll more combat dice than mortals can hope to achieve... and she wasn't a slouch in combat even if she was far from maxed out. Five starting level PCs, min-maxed to hell would still be massively over their heads trying to fight her (and surprising her Auspex 7 wasn't happening any time soon).<br /> <br /> In V5, since she's rolling 8 or 10 dice base depending how she's fighting, her raw stats aren't above what PCs can hit (and she lost a bunch of Discipline dots, in combat of note: Fort 5 to Fort 3, and all her Potence), unless she surges... but she'd have to surge against every attack individually to ensure she's appropriately spanking some neonate upstarts... which means she'd be gaining Hunger at around 2-3 per turn. No exactly sustainable.<br /> <br /> It's not that she wouldn't win most of the time or something (esp. if she, being the social powerhouse she's supposed to be, doesn't get into a melee in the first place), but it's still a massive reduction in her ability to deal with getting jumped by packs of Sabbat.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":7}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-04-24T14:43:59-07:00","id":1445713,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Heavy Arms</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1443592-the-official-v5-vs-v20-thread?p=1445708#post1445708\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Yep. This is one of the bigger points on the &quot;weaker elders&quot; thing, because while the WoD games have never been kind to powerful individuals trying to fend off a group of weaker foes, this is a massive reduction in capability.<br /> <br /> Helena, back in pre-V5 rules, could pump herself up to Str 12/Dex 12/Stam 12 for a scene and still have more vitae left than starting PCs can top up at (35/50). That means she could, with Attributes and blood alone, roll more combat dice than mortals can hope to achieve... and she wasn't a slouch in combat even if she was far from maxed out. Five starting level PCs, min-maxed to hell would still be massively over their heads trying to fight her (and surprising her Auspex 7 wasn't happening any time soon).<br /> <br /> In V5, since she's rolling 8 or 10 dice base depending how she's fighting, her raw stats aren't above what PCs can hit (and she lost a bunch of Discipline dots, in combat of note: Fort 5 to Fort 3, and all her Potence), unless she surges... but she'd have to surge against every attack individually to ensure she's appropriately spanking some neonate upstarts... which means she'd be gaining Hunger at around 2-3 per turn. No exactly sustainable.<br /> <br /> It's not that she wouldn't win most of the time or something (esp. if she, being the social powerhouse she's supposed to be, doesn't get into a melee in the first place), but it's still a massive reduction in her ability to deal with getting jumped by packs of Sabbat.</div> </div> </div> </div>While true, combat doesn't work in the area of Strength/Dex/Stam the same either. Ergo that amount of expenditure isn't necessary anymore. Also, I'm pretty sure that your physical atttributes were limited to your Generation back then as well.<br /> <br /> You couldn't physically pump your stats as a 8th generation vampire above 5. Helena would be limited to 9 in her Attributes (or 10).<br /> <br /> Edit:<br /> <br /> With an additional +1 above your generation. Sorry, relatives are visiting.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Author of <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Cthulhu-Armageddon-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01KUOM7SI/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982844&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Cthulhu+Armageddon\" target=\"_blank\">Cthulhu Armageddon</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Teenage-Weredeer-Bright-Falls-Mysteries-ebook/dp/B075TTN2FN/ref=sr_1_2?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982717&amp;sr=1-2&amp;keywords=Weredeer#customerReviews\" target=\"_blank\">I was a Teenage Weredeer</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Straight-Outta-Fangton-Comedic-Vampire-ebook/dp/B01KNHICCC/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982774&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Straight+Outta+Fangton\" target=\"_blank\">Straight Outta Fangton</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Lucifers-Star-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01MDM9MCT/ref=mt_kindle?_encoding=UTF8&amp;me=&amp;qid=\" target=\"_blank\">Lucifer's Star</a>, </i>and the <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Rules-Supervillainy-Saga-Book-ebook/dp/B07MB89S33/\" target=\"_blank\">Supervillainy Saga</a>.</i><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":12002,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","user":"CTPhipps","date":". 04-24-2021, 06:42 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","name":"CTPhipps","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12002_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13933"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-04-24T15:18:33-07:00","id":1445718,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CTPhipps</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1443592-the-official-v5-vs-v20-thread?p=1445713#post1445713\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> While true, combat doesn't work in the area of Strength/Dex/Stam the same either. Ergo that amount of expenditure isn't necessary anymore. Also, I'm pretty sure that your physical atttributes were limited to your Generation back then as well.<br /> <br /> You couldn't physically pump your stats as a 8th generation vampire above 5. Helena would be limited to 9 in her Attributes.</div> </div> </div> </div>Wuh? No. You could pump your stats to your gen max plus one for a scene, and up to ten for three rounds. For player generations, this meant you could pump your stats to 6 for a scene, and 10 for three rounds. For Helena, she could pump her stats to 10 for a scene.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3598-cajunkhan","name":"CajunKhan","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3598_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1700"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-04-24T15:24:46-07:00","id":1445719,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CajunKhan</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1443592-the-official-v5-vs-v20-thread?p=1445718#post1445718\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Wuh? No. You could pump your stats to your gen max plus one for a scene, and up to ten for three rounds. For player generations, this meant you could pump your stats to 6 for a scene, and 10 for three rounds. For Helena, she could pump her stats to 10 for a scene.</div> </div> </div> </div>Right, sorry.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Author of <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Cthulhu-Armageddon-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01KUOM7SI/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982844&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Cthulhu+Armageddon\" target=\"_blank\">Cthulhu Armageddon</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Teenage-Weredeer-Bright-Falls-Mysteries-ebook/dp/B075TTN2FN/ref=sr_1_2?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982717&amp;sr=1-2&amp;keywords=Weredeer#customerReviews\" target=\"_blank\">I was a Teenage Weredeer</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Straight-Outta-Fangton-Comedic-Vampire-ebook/dp/B01KNHICCC/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982774&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Straight+Outta+Fangton\" target=\"_blank\">Straight Outta Fangton</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Lucifers-Star-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01MDM9MCT/ref=mt_kindle?_encoding=UTF8&amp;me=&amp;qid=\" target=\"_blank\">Lucifer's Star</a>, </i>and the <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Rules-Supervillainy-Saga-Book-ebook/dp/B07MB89S33/\" target=\"_blank\">Supervillainy Saga</a>.</i><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","name":"CTPhipps","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12002_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13933"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-04-24T15:26:12-07:00","id":1445720,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CTPhipps</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1443592-the-official-v5-vs-v20-thread?p=1445713#post1445713\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> While true, combat doesn't work in the area of Strength/Dex/Stam the same either. Ergo that amount of expenditure isn't necessary anymore. Also, I'm pretty sure that your physical atttributes were limited to your Generation back then as well.<br /> <br /> You couldn't physically pump your stats as a 8th generation vampire above 5. Helena would be limited to 9 in her Attributes.</div> </div> </div> </div>The rule is you can pump up to 1 above your generational limit (to a maximum of 10) for one scene at a cost of 1 blood point per +1 bump. They can also pump any of the physical stats to as high as 10, but only for three turns after they stop spending blood on increasing their attributes.<br /> <br /> So a 13th Gen with Strength 5 could burn 1 point to go to 6 for a scene. On the next four turns they could spend another to bump it to 7, 8, 9 and then 10, but unless they spend another blood point on pumping stats, that level will fade back to six after more three turns... and they've burned half their blood pool getting to 10 so they can only keep spending for five more turns if they started at full.<br /> <br /> Helena thus could pump her stats to as high as 10... the limit of a mortal human dice pool and maintain that level for an entire scene... and could add +10 in a single turn due to her generational spending limit being so high.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1328-chris24601","name":"Chris24601","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"520"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-04-24T18:02:16-07:00","id":1445754,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CTPhipps</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1443592-the-official-v5-vs-v20-thread?p=1445644#post1445644\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I feel preventing a global panic and upending the world order is a pretty decent reason itself.<br /> <br /> <i>&quot;Listen. Every week there's a panic about some puny little bug. Now how do you think it would be if this got out? Hm? You'll have paranoia, you'll have vigilantes, you'll have people running back to religion in droves. The next thing you know, you'll have the Archbishop up for Prime Minister. I don't fancy living in Iran, do you?&quot; </i>- Vaughn, Ultraviolet<br /> <br /> I feel that the idea the government wouldn't do it kind of loses its strength when the most recent RL administration was full of lies at every conceivable level about a global yet undeniable threat.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> I <i>feel</i> differently. But hey, at least that's an explanation provided. Something V5 has yet to provide after 3 years of production.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24936-morbus","name":"Morbus","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"119"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-04-24T18:11:36-07:00","id":1445755,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Morbus</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1443592-the-official-v5-vs-v20-thread?p=1445754#post1445754\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I <i>feel</i> differently. But hey, at least that's an explanation provided. Something V5 has yet to provide after 3 years of production.</div> </div> </div> </div>I thought the Camarilla book's SI section was quite clear. It's the best part of the book aside from its handling of cults, IMHO.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Author of <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Cthulhu-Armageddon-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01KUOM7SI/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982844&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Cthulhu+Armageddon\" target=\"_blank\">Cthulhu Armageddon</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Teenage-Weredeer-Bright-Falls-Mysteries-ebook/dp/B075TTN2FN/ref=sr_1_2?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982717&amp;sr=1-2&amp;keywords=Weredeer#customerReviews\" target=\"_blank\">I was a Teenage Weredeer</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Straight-Outta-Fangton-Comedic-Vampire-ebook/dp/B01KNHICCC/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982774&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Straight+Outta+Fangton\" target=\"_blank\">Straight Outta Fangton</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Lucifers-Star-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01MDM9MCT/ref=mt_kindle?_encoding=UTF8&amp;me=&amp;qid=\" target=\"_blank\">Lucifer's Star</a>, </i>and the <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Rules-Supervillainy-Saga-Book-ebook/dp/B07MB89S33/\" target=\"_blank\">Supervillainy Saga</a>.</i><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","name":"CTPhipps","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12002_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13933"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-04-24T18:15:53-07:00","id":1445758,"title":"","content":"What I remember from that book is that the SI is such a disjointed faction that ultimately any human being involved in the hunting can fairly easily break the Masquerade if he grows the moral fortitude to bring the truth to the rest of Humanity. Not that difficult because even a loner with some well hidden gopros can do a lot of damage considering whole states are run by vampiric anarch gangs with no global conspiracy covering their asses.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":24936,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24936-morbus","user":"Morbus","date":". 04-24-2021, 09:18 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24936-morbus","name":"Morbus","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"119"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-04-24T18:46:15-07:00","id":1445759,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Morbus</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1443592-the-official-v5-vs-v20-thread?p=1445758#post1445758\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">What I remember from that book is that the SI is such a disjointed faction that ultimately any human being involved in the hunting can fairly easily break the Masquerade if he grows the moral fortitude to bring the truth to the rest of Humanity. Not that difficult because even a loner with some well hidden gopros can do a lot of damage considering whole states are run by vampiric anarch gangs with no global conspiracy covering their asses.</div> </div> </div> </div>I don't get this argument.<br /> <br /> A guy says vampires are real.<br /> <br /> And?<br /> <br /> Oddly the big thing I took from the SI is the government DOES know vampires are real but they're now invested in protecting the secret and while that's bad for the Masquerade, helps explain its maintainance into 2020. Mind you, the fact that 20 million Qanon people believe the Democrats are Satanist vampires now show that the Masquerade is unnecessary.<br /> <br /> People will believe lunacy and the world will go on.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Author of <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Cthulhu-Armageddon-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01KUOM7SI/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982844&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Cthulhu+Armageddon\" target=\"_blank\">Cthulhu Armageddon</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Teenage-Weredeer-Bright-Falls-Mysteries-ebook/dp/B075TTN2FN/ref=sr_1_2?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982717&amp;sr=1-2&amp;keywords=Weredeer#customerReviews\" target=\"_blank\">I was a Teenage Weredeer</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Straight-Outta-Fangton-Comedic-Vampire-ebook/dp/B01KNHICCC/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982774&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Straight+Outta+Fangton\" target=\"_blank\">Straight Outta Fangton</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Lucifers-Star-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01MDM9MCT/ref=mt_kindle?_encoding=UTF8&amp;me=&amp;qid=\" target=\"_blank\">Lucifer's Star</a>, </i>and the <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Rules-Supervillainy-Saga-Book-ebook/dp/B07MB89S33/\" target=\"_blank\">Supervillainy Saga</a>.</i><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","name":"CTPhipps","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12002_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13933"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-04-24T18:50:22-07:00","id":1445760,"title":"","content":"And some people believe him and start to join in the uncovering/hunting. And it snowballs from here.<br /> <br /> One dude obviously can only do so much. But 20 millions? that's a lot of people to day hunt and day shoot further evidence and day burn the monsters.<br /> <br /> Frankly I don't even think you need the majority of mankind to wipe at the very least the Anarch. 10% of the US population seems indeed more than enough to genocide most vampires.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":24936,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24936-morbus","user":"Morbus","date":". 04-24-2021, 09:53 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24936-morbus","name":"Morbus","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"119"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-04-24T18:51:38-07:00","id":1445761,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Morbus</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1443592-the-official-v5-vs-v20-thread?p=1445760#post1445760\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">And some people believe him and start to join in the uncovering. And it snowballs from here.<br /> <br /> One dude obviously can do much. But 20 millions? that's a lot of people.</div> </div> </div> </div>I'm using the 20 million as an example of people believing something utterly insane and achieving nothing with it despite powerful support in the government.<br /> <br /> (Yes, I mean Qanon)<br /> <br /> <img src=\"ht