e:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13933"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-04-24T18:56:00-07:00","id":1445762,"title":"","content":"I know.<br /> <br /> People can believe crazy conspiracy theory without much evidence provided. Now imagine if you can bring them a vampire in flesh? (probably a thin blood since they are about as strong as a regular human being. If not weaker during daytime.)<br /> <br /> The sky is the limit. I tell you.<br /> <br /> One hero is all you need.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24936-morbus","name":"Morbus","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"119"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-04-24T19:49:38-07:00","id":1445769,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Morbus</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1443592-the-official-v5-vs-v20-thread?p=1445762#post1445762\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I know.<br /> <br /> People can believe crazy conspiracy theory without much evidence provided. Now imagine if you can bring them a vampire in flesh? (probably a thin blood since they are about as strong as a regular human being. If not weaker during daytime.)<br /> <br /> The sky is the limit. I tell you.<br /> <br /> One hero is all you need.</div> </div> </div> </div>Listen, I saw the vampire autopsy tape. It was obviously faked. Now maybe if we saw it in the flesh. Oh it's gone now? Pffft. Conveinant.<br /> <br /> But good example. Probably great for a hunter game.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Author of <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Cthulhu-Armageddon-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01KUOM7SI/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982844&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Cthulhu+Armageddon\" target=\"_blank\">Cthulhu Armageddon</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Teenage-Weredeer-Bright-Falls-Mysteries-ebook/dp/B075TTN2FN/ref=sr_1_2?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982717&amp;sr=1-2&amp;keywords=Weredeer#customerReviews\" target=\"_blank\">I was a Teenage Weredeer</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Straight-Outta-Fangton-Comedic-Vampire-ebook/dp/B01KNHICCC/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982774&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Straight+Outta+Fangton\" target=\"_blank\">Straight Outta Fangton</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Lucifers-Star-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01MDM9MCT/ref=mt_kindle?_encoding=UTF8&amp;me=&amp;qid=\" target=\"_blank\">Lucifer's Star</a>, </i>and the <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Rules-Supervillainy-Saga-Book-ebook/dp/B07MB89S33/\" target=\"_blank\">Supervillainy Saga</a>.</i><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","name":"CTPhipps","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12002_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13933"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-04-25T00:02:21-07:00","id":1445786,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>False Epiphany</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1443592-the-official-v5-vs-v20-thread?p=1445703#post1445703\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I mean, I do. V5's mechanics have... a lot of issues (though some pretty great ideas), and Masquerade's are now 30 years old, so I've just played with Requiem rules. Heavily house ruled, the point of now being its own game system.</div> </div> </div> </div>V5 has driven me right into the arms of VTR and... I'm happy about it. I love the VTM setting, but there are so many things I've now pinched from VTR (aforementioned Kindred Senses, the rewrites of Protean and Auspex, etc).<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> This is too complex for my tastes. I introduced Hunger and Rouse checks into my game, but I modeled bigger blood pools by removing Rouse costs from (most) Disciplines with a lower rating than the vampire's Blood Potency. </div> </div> </div>That's a really simple, elegant fix. One of my pet peeves about rouses and Blood Potency is that the table is way more complicated than it needs to be, with re-rolls, blood surge, variable heal costs, etc. All those things were simply achievable with blood points before. <br /> <br /> Having simple rules is, IMO, better. E.g., if blood surge equalled Blood Potency, too, and it lasted for one scene in one Attribute, that might be better. Or maybe you allocate dice across Attributes equal to your BP for the scene, so you can have +1 Strength, +2 Dexterity and +1 Stamina if you have BP 4. <br /> <br /> To me, that's preferable to making blood surge basically a slightly better version of WP expenditure. (Also, am I alone in thinking Netchuch's name for this, the Quickening, is better than blood surge? I also prefer VTR's Devotions as a term than V5's Amalgams, which sound like dental work. But that's another tangent...)<br /> <br /> Re: Compulsions, which some people have had a problem with but which others like but not as written, I wondered whether you could make Frenzies a bit different, so that you only roll once (rather than making it an extended test), with the following outcomes: when you score 5+ successes on your roll, you avoid Frenzy; if you pass with 1-4 successes, you gain a Compulsion (perhaps with an onset delayed by one turn per success, if you're generous); if you fail, you Frenzy; if you botch, you Frenzy and lose a dot in a Virtue or develop a Derangement. <br /> <br /> (You might need to tweak the number of successes based on how many dice people are rolling. With V20 Virtues, it might be better to set the bar at 3+ successes, since you'll be rolling 1-5 dice. Maybe add Humanity/3 like in V5 to push those dice pools up a bit or give a bonus for vampires who are fully fed.)<br /> <br /> That way, Compulsions are the default, but only when you'd normally test for Frenzy. You trade losing complete control for acting more like a vampire, as mediated by clan and concept. <br /> <br /> If you botch when subject to a Compulsion, only then would you get a Bestial Failure; if you score 5+ successes, only then would you get a Messy Critical. These are less common as a result, and therefore more meaningful. You could reward the player by letting them resolve the Compulsions when they BF or MC, or by allowing them to regain WP by turning over control to the Beast for these brief moments.<br /> <br /> That gives you the seasoning, as it were, from V5, without so much loss of control. For more danger, you can simply add Bestial Failures and Messy Crits as outcomes when you botch or crit when hungry, but not in any other state. This way, it's a dial you can turn up or down.<br /> <br /> Boom! Simple. It works with blood points or rouses. It loses Hunger Dice. It gives everyone more chance to get the tone right for their tables.<br /> <br /> We use VTR Beats anyway, so the simple fix for us is letting PCs convert any botch or crit to a Bestial Failure or Messy Critical for a Beat, in addition to the options above. Making those options a choice with a reward makes things more appealing than making them all stick.<br /> <br /> Finally (and this isn't something I'm interested in as much but others might be), if you want more dynamic blood points, I'd do the following: for every health level you inflict upon a human while feeding (you can normally inflict three per turn; humans only have seven HLs, as usual), roll two dice; or take 10 points if you are willing to drain someone dry instead. For each success, you gain one blood point. On average, that means a human gives you seven blood points and you can leave them on the cusp of life or death, but they give you 10 if you don't care about leaving them totally dry.<br /> <br /> Each time you spend blood, instead roll two dice per blood point. Each die that fails, you lose a blood point. Each die that botches also triggers a Compulsion. This way, you can't quite gauge how much blood you'll spend at a given time but you lose all the re-rolls, variable heal costs and variable blood surge on the Blood Potency table. If you want things a bit more reliable, have all humans provide a fixed number blood points (up to 10 as usual) and just randomise the expenditure.<br /> <br /> In this way, you can take a lot of the new stuff from V5 while still using the core V20 chassis.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Writer, publisher, performer<br /> Mostly he/his, sometimes she/her IRL <a href=\"https://adam-lowe.com\" target=\"_blank\">https://adam-lowe.com</a>","edited":{"userid":5291,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5291-adambeyoncelowe","user":"adambeyoncelowe","date":". 04-25-2021, 03:24 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5291-adambeyoncelowe","name":"adambeyoncelowe","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5291_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2802"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-04-25T00:10:57-07:00","id":1445787,"title":"","content":"I will say that I think they attempted to nerf vampires to be <i>Vampire: The Requiem</i> style, which is NOT BAD but it is not <i>Vampire: The Masquerade</i>.<br /> <br /> V:TM vampires are trenchcoats, katanas, and dragonsbreath shotguns doing<i> Underworld </i>and having to deal with ancient powerful gods as well as Noddist conspiracies. <i>Vampire: The Requiem</i> is a bunch of dirty bikers slicing the throats of people in a dive bar and a rich businessman struggling to maintain control over one city block's kindred due to the fact that a bunch of religious fanatics moved in and started converting some of his friends.<br /> <br /> I love V:TR and think V:TM was wise to incorporate many of its better parts.<br /> <br /> HOWEVER, it needs to have the rules for the big supersplashy stuff as well as the gritty dark street level stuff. Which is my biggest criticism of the game. They need to un-nerf vampires with disciplines and the ability to do fantastical comic book weirdness.<br /> <br /> They're not WEAK by any stretch of the imagination but need to be able to do godlike, at least in theory.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Author of <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Cthulhu-Armageddon-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01KUOM7SI/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982844&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Cthulhu+Armageddon\" target=\"_blank\">Cthulhu Armageddon</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Teenage-Weredeer-Bright-Falls-Mysteries-ebook/dp/B075TTN2FN/ref=sr_1_2?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982717&amp;sr=1-2&amp;keywords=Weredeer#customerReviews\" target=\"_blank\">I was a Teenage Weredeer</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Straight-Outta-Fangton-Comedic-Vampire-ebook/dp/B01KNHICCC/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982774&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Straight+Outta+Fangton\" target=\"_blank\">Straight Outta Fangton</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Lucifers-Star-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01MDM9MCT/ref=mt_kindle?_encoding=UTF8&amp;me=&amp;qid=\" target=\"_blank\">Lucifer's Star</a>, </i>and the <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Rules-Supervillainy-Saga-Book-ebook/dp/B07MB89S33/\" target=\"_blank\">Supervillainy Saga</a>.</i><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":7}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","name":"CTPhipps","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12002_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13933"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-04-25T00:23:31-07:00","id":1445788,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CTPhipps</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1443592-the-official-v5-vs-v20-thread?p=1445787#post1445787\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I will say that I think they attempted to nerf vampires to be <i>Vampire: The Requiem</i> style, which is NOT BAD but it is not <i>Vampire: The Masquerade</i>.<br /> <br /> V:TM vampires are trenchcoats, katanas, and dragonsbreath shotguns doing<i> Underworld </i>and having to deal with ancient powerful gods as well as Noddist conspiracies. <i>Vampire: The Requiem</i> is a bunch of dirty bikers slicing the throats of people in a dive bar and a rich businessman struggling to maintain control over one city block's kindred due to the fact that a bunch of religious fanatics moved in and started converting some of his friends.<br /> <br /> I love V:TR and think V:TM was wise to incorporate many of its better parts.<br /> <br /> HOWEVER, it needs to have the rules for the big supersplashy stuff as well as the gritty dark street level stuff. Which is my biggest criticism of the game. They need to un-nerf vampires with disciplines and the ability to do fantastical comic book weirdness.<br /> <br /> They're not WEAK by any stretch of the imagination but need to be able to do godlike, at least in theory.</div> </div> </div> </div>Yes to this, so much! Like I say, I love VTR's rules, but I lean more towards VTM's power levels in V20 and earlier. So for Presence, I use Majesty 1 to replace Awe, then mostly use the V20 version of the Discipline.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Writer, publisher, performer<br /> Mostly he/his, sometimes she/her IRL <a href=\"https://adam-lowe.com\" target=\"_blank\">https://adam-lowe.com</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5291-adambeyoncelowe","name":"adambeyoncelowe","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5291_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2802"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-04-25T00:41:00-07:00","id":1445790,"title":"","content":"I feel like vamps were weakened in part to make the SI a more credible threat.<br /> Nobody kills players by setting them on fire while they sleep during the day. That might be the smart choice for dealing with NPCS, but not players. The one time I saw a player die during rest was because the player was sloppy and found an emergency resting place not too far from a &quot;crime scene&quot; while being followed. Hunters generally need to hunt players when they're active, and should only use clever techniques (like Car bombings) when the players have the Auspex to warn them of it. The current rules heavily favour mortals; Armour only works for mortals, Dominate, Potence, auspex, celerity and obfuscate got nerfed hard. A single vamp can't stomp a cell like they could in V20.<br /> <br /> <i>If you have to fundamentally upend large chunks of the game's mechanics to make your story work, it's not a good story</i>.<br /> <br /> Really, to make hunters more of a threat, you could've just gone with <i>MORE DAKKA</i>.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":6}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25794-mywifeisscary","name":"MyWifeIsScary","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25794_2.png","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3711"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-04-25T00:46:40-07:00","id":1445791,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MyWifeIsScary</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1443592-the-official-v5-vs-v20-thread?p=1445790#post1445790\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I feel like vamps were weakened in part to make the SI a more credible threat.<br /> Nobody kills players by setting them on fire while they sleep during the day. That might be the smart choice for dealing with NPCS, but not players. The one time I saw a player die during rest was because the player was sloppy and found an emergency resting place not too far from a &quot;crime scene&quot; while being followed. Hunters generally need to hunt players when they're active, and should only use clever techniques (like Car bombings) when the players have the Auspex to warn them of it. The current rules heavily favour mortals; Armour only works for mortals, Dominate, Potence, auspex, celerity and obfuscate got nerfed hard. A single vamp can't stomp a cell like they could in V20.<br /> <br /> <i>If you have to fundamentally upend large chunks of the game's mechanics to make your story work, it's not a good story</i>.<br /> <br /> Really, to make hunters more of a threat, you could've just gone with <i>MORE DAKKA</i>.</div> </div> </div> </div>Well that's because it's a boring story to kill the players during the day. However, vampires are helpless during the day if they have Low Humanity. It probably took a couple of hours to clean out Mexico City once they located their dens. I also think that its stupid, cinematic but stupid, to imagine the Second Inquisition would attack the PCs at night. It seems that overconfidence is meant to be a thing that the Inquisitors would display an abundance of.<br /> <br /> Any Inquisitor who does that is like a vampire who attacks a Garou head on, not named Karsh.<br /> <br /> Stupid. Brave but stupid.<br /> <br /> Of course the biggest advantage the Second Inquisition has over vampires is not any nerfing but the fact that SI have military grade weapons. The Frog Brothers wouldn't have been nearly as overwhelmed if they'd had grenade launchers and MI16s. If I was writing the SI, I'd say the greatest benefit from the changing paradigm is not the international conspiracy of intelligence agencies but the fact that the Department of Homeland Security will bail you out of jail whenever you're caught next to a burning house and a family of dead ghouls.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Author of <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Cthulhu-Armageddon-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01KUOM7SI/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982844&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Cthulhu+Armageddon\" target=\"_blank\">Cthulhu Armageddon</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Teenage-Weredeer-Bright-Falls-Mysteries-ebook/dp/B075TTN2FN/ref=sr_1_2?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982717&amp;sr=1-2&amp;keywords=Weredeer#customerReviews\" target=\"_blank\">I was a Teenage Weredeer</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Straight-Outta-Fangton-Comedic-Vampire-ebook/dp/B01KNHICCC/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982774&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Straight+Outta+Fangton\" target=\"_blank\">Straight Outta Fangton</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Lucifers-Star-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01MDM9MCT/ref=mt_kindle?_encoding=UTF8&amp;me=&amp;qid=\" target=\"_blank\">Lucifer's Star</a>, </i>and the <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Rules-Supervillainy-Saga-Book-ebook/dp/B07MB89S33/\" target=\"_blank\">Supervillainy Saga</a>.</i><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":12002,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","user":"CTPhipps","date":". 04-25-2021, 03:49 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","name":"CTPhipps","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12002_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13933"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-04-25T00:51:35-07:00","id":1445792,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CTPhipps</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1443592-the-official-v5-vs-v20-thread?p=1445787#post1445787\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I will say that I think they attempted to nerf vampires to be <i>Vampire: The Requiem</i> style, which is NOT BAD but it is not <i>Vampire: The Masquerade</i>.<br /> <br /> V:TM vampires are trenchcoats, katanas, and dragonsbreath shotguns doing<i> Underworld </i>and having to deal with ancient powerful gods as well as Noddist conspiracies. <i>Vampire: The Requiem</i> is a bunch of dirty bikers slicing the throats of people in a dive bar and a rich businessman struggling to maintain control over one city block's kindred due to the fact that a bunch of religious fanatics moved in and started converting some of his friends.<br /> <br /> I love V:TR and think V:TM was wise to incorporate many of its better parts.<br /> <br /> HOWEVER, it needs to have the rules for the big supersplashy stuff as well as the gritty dark street level stuff. Which is my biggest criticism of the game. They need to un-nerf vampires with disciplines and the ability to do fantastical comic book weirdness.<br /> <br /> They're not WEAK by any stretch of the imagination but need to be able to do godlike, at least in theory.</div> </div> </div> </div>I think one of the stated design goals in the making of V5, was expressed through the repeated line of \u2018One World of Darkness\u2019.<br /> <br /> In one respect, this meant that White Wolf changed the name of the 'New World of Darkness\u2019 to 'Chronicles of Darkness\u2019 to avoid brand confusion. I think it was also the case of attempting to bring together ideas from both lines in the making of V5, in order to move forward as a unifying line. Whether it was successful at that is open to question, but I think that was the intent - take the brio of VTM and the polish of VTR, and build on both of them. <br /> <br /> Personally, I don\u2019t see it as an issue, and creative game designers take ideas from all sources. As such, I don\u2019t really buy into the whole VTM vs VTR division either. They had different design goals to suit their times, but a good idea in a game is a good idea no matter where it is sourced from. I\u2019d quite happily use VTR books as sources of ideas in V5 (or any other edition).","signature":"","edited":{"userid":2517,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2517-trippy","user":"Trippy","date":". 04-25-2021, 03:53 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2517-trippy","name":"Trippy","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2517_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1018"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-04-25T01:13:36-07:00","id":1445794,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CTPhipps</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1443592-the-official-v5-vs-v20-thread?p=1445787#post1445787\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I love V:TR and think V:TM was wise to incorporate many of its better parts.<br /> <br /> HOWEVER, it needs to have the rules for the big supersplashy stuff as well as the gritty dark street level stuff. Which is my biggest criticism of the game. They need to un-nerf vampires with disciplines and the ability to do fantastical comic book weirdness.<br /> <br /> They're not WEAK by any stretch of the imagination but need to be able to do godlike, at least in theory.</div> </div> </div> </div>Requiem 2e vampires are stronger than Masquerade vampires in many ways, honestly.<br /> <br /> Elder Disciplines may not be a thing, but 1-5 Disciplines all got huge boosts, especially at the low levels. Dominate 1 lets you command people to do whatever you can cram into four words and rewrite their memories of the current scene. Dominate 2 turns someone into your slave for all night with one roll (and a weighted dice pool that favors the attacker). Dominate 4 lets you rewrite an entire <i>lifetime's</i> worth of a victim's memories, even inventing families who never existed. Auspex 1-2 let you look into people's heads with explicitly no way for them to tell someone is reading their mind. Many of the 6-7 Masquerade powers got folded into 4-5 Requiem 2e powers.<br /> <br /> The increased power level of those Disciplines is okay in Requiem's setting, which in many ways is less political. Or at least more dynamic. The War of Ages between elders and neonates isn't really a thing and power shakeups are more common in cities. But in a Masquerade game, I found the 2e Disciplines to be much too powerful. And by &quot;powerful&quot; I mean, they tended to cut through layers of intrigue and social interaction, and made players devote more time and thought than I liked towards how to counter adversaries' Disciplines. My Ventrue player cheered when I nerfed Dominate. (I found V5's caveat that Dominate can't be used for interrogation purposes to be <i>incredibly</i> wise.)<br /> <br /> Requiem 2e has a lot of cool ideas. I love how all vampires can see in the dark by default. (They are nocturnal, the Beast doesn't play well with fire, and electricity is a comparatively modern invention.) Many Disciplines with &quot;meh&quot; powers got seriously beefed up. But they're designed for a different setting than Masquerade and need tweaking when they're used in it.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://blood-and-bourbon.obsidianportal.com/\" target=\"_blank\">Blood and Bourbon</a>, my New Orleans-based Vampire chronicle.","edited":{"userid":3110,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3110-false-epiphany","user":"False Epiphany","date":". 04-25-2021, 04:16 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3110-false-epiphany","name":"False Epiphany","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3110_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"748"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-04-25T10:28:54-07:00","id":1445844,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>adambeyoncelowe</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1443592-the-official-v5-vs-v20-thread?p=1445786#post1445786\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">V5 has driven me right into the arms of VTR and... I'm happy about it. I love the VTM setting, but there are so many things I've now pinched from VTR (aforementioned Kindred Senses, the rewrites of Protean and Auspex, etc).</div> </div> </div> </div>The new Protean is fantastic. Earth Meld/Unmarked Grace isn't <i>that</i> powerful and works okay at one dot, I've found.<br /> <br /> Auspex is basically the same as Masquerade's at levels 3+. Levels 1-2 in Masquerade are lame, but 1-2 in Requiem are too good. I changed them to only work against mortals or vampires whose blood the character has recently tasted, and found that to reduce &quot;everyone could be reading my mind&quot; paranoia levels. <br /> <br /> One of the biggest things I like about 2e VtR Disciplines is how many of them no longer take dice rolls. You just say &quot;this cool thing happens,&quot; no fuss no muss. I've increasingly trended away from requiring dice rolls for powers that don't directly harm or influence other characters. <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Having simple rules is, IMO, better. E.g., if blood surge equalled Blood Potency, too, and it lasted for one scene in one Attribute, that might be better. Or maybe you allocate dice across Attributes equal to your BP for the scene, so you can have +1 Strength, +2 Dexterity and +1 Stamina if you have BP 4.<br /> <br /> Scene-long physical boosts is basically paying blood to use Potence, IMO. I liked the way Requiem did it with spending a Vitae giving you a +2 bonus on a single Physical roll (IIRC?), no messy generational caps or diminishing bonuses past X threshold. Just spend the blood, get a +2 bonus. Boom.<br /> <br /> Conceptually, I like Physical Intensity/Blood Surge/whatever as a brief, desperate surge of blood-fueled strength. It can let any vampire pull off incredible physical feats, if they really want to, but it's not something they can use all the time like Potence. <br /> <br /> [qupte]I also prefer VTR's Devotions as a term than V5's Amalgams, which sound like dental work. But that's another tangent...) </div> </div> </div>Me too. I just use Devotions as the name for individual powers within a larger Discipline. <br /> <br /> This was another design idea of V5's that I really, really liked, as an aside. Multiple powers per Discipline level. I can't believe earlier editions didn't think of this. <br /> <br /> The big thing I've changed is not restricting players to only one power per Discipline level: they can take as many they like, though every power beyond the first at the same Discipline level costs extra XP. Players have loved it. It's also allowed me to open up many high-level Disciplines at lower levels by inventing scaled-down versions. For instance, Beast Shape works just fine at Protean 1 if you limit it to a non-flying, non-dangerous animal for only a scene. My player with Protean 2 loves being able to turn into a cat. <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Re: Compulsions, which some people have had a problem with but which others like but not as written, I wondered whether you could make Frenzies a bit different, so that you only roll once (rather than making it an extended test), with the following outcomes: when you score 5+ successes on your roll, you avoid Frenzy; if you pass with 1-4 successes, you gain a Compulsion (perhaps with an onset delayed by one turn per success, if you're generous); if you fail, you Frenzy; if you botch, you Frenzy and lose a dot in a Virtue or develop a Derangement. </div> </div> </div>I like this idea. Messy criticals, bestial failures, and hunger dice were a prolix and non-intuitive part of the rules, but bestial compulsions were cool. Easiest way to insert them into a game is to just attach them to other dice rolls as a consequence for not rolling high enough. Don't even have to be just frenzy rolls.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://blood-and-bourbon.obsidianportal.com/\" target=\"_blank\">Blood and Bourbon</a>, my New Orleans-based Vampire chronicle.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3110-false-epiphany","name":"False Epiphany","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3110_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"748"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-04-25T15:10:37-07:00","id":1445876,"title":"","content":"Something I think VtR 2e did well (esp. since it redeemed one of the worst rules in VtR 1e) relates to the idea of having something between VtM 1e-20th's &quot;nothing or frenzy&quot; and V5's &quot;here's a half a dozen ways the Beast might screw up your character's plans,&quot; approaches: Lashing Out.<br /> <br /> When VtR 2e vampires go Beast to Beast, the loser effectively gets smacked with a Compulsion in V5 terms (though there are just three universal ones instead of Clan ones and all that). It has that &quot;Beast gets under your skin and you do not so smart things without a full blown Frenzy&quot; part that the earlier games lack, but isn't as agency ignoring as V5's mechanics tend to be. It's never an accident, because there's always at least one vampires that is purposefully making it happen. <br /> <br /> It's easy to picture how street level politics are full of Lashing Out as vampires push each other around for dominance and control, but polite high political vampire society considers such antics beneath them (not that they aren't all ready to do it at the drop of a hat if cornered or need to put a youngster in their place without drawn out conflict) and uncouth to maintain the appearances of civil vampire society.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-04-26T10:27:29-07:00","id":1445982,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Heavy Arms</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1443592-the-official-v5-vs-v20-thread?p=1445876#post1445876\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Something I think VtR 2e did well (esp. since it redeemed one of the worst rules in VtR 1e) relates to the idea of having something between VtM 1e-20th's &quot;nothing or frenzy&quot; and V5's &quot;here's a half a dozen ways the Beast might screw up your character's plans,&quot; approaches: Lashing Out.<br /> <br /> When VtR 2e vampires go Beast to Beast, the loser effectively gets smacked with a Compulsion in V5 terms (though there are just three universal ones instead of Clan ones and all that). It has that &quot;Beast gets under your skin and you do not so smart things without a full blown Frenzy&quot; part that the earlier games lack, but isn't as agency ignoring as V5's mechanics tend to be. It's never an accident, because there's always at least one vampires that is purposefully making it happen. <br /> <br /> It's easy to picture how street level politics are full of Lashing Out as vampires push each other around for dominance and control, but polite high political vampire society considers such antics beneath them (not that they aren't all ready to do it at the drop of a hat if cornered or need to put a youngster in their place without drawn out conflict) and uncouth to maintain the appearances of civil vampire society.</div> </div> </div> </div>I really like Lashing Out, too. I've been thinking about how to pinch it in my V20/V30 hack.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Writer, publisher, performer<br /> Mostly he/his, sometimes she/her IRL <a href=\"https://adam-lowe.com\" target=\"_blank\">https://adam-lowe.com</a>","edited":{"userid":5291,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5291-adambeyoncelowe","user":"adambeyoncelowe","date":". 04-27-2021, 07:45 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5291-adambeyoncelowe","name":"adambeyoncelowe","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5291_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2802"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-04-27T04:31:02-07:00","id":1446091,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Heavy Arms</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1443592-the-official-v5-vs-v20-thread?p=1445558#post1445558\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I'm sure you don't intend it, but this is probably one of the biggest sources of negative feelings from the V20 camp towards the V5 camp: the attitude that those of us that have playing VtM and other games with vampires in them that aren't close to what V5 does, haven't been playing &quot;real&quot; vampire games. This whole way of phrasing the conversation tends to raise hackles because you, again giving you the benefit of the doubt that you don't mean to come off this way, are basically saying that in my near 25 years of playing vampires in RPGs, I don't appreciate what a &quot;vampire game&quot; should actually be because I don't like the specific way V5 does vampires.<br /> <br /> I hope you can see how off-putting that can be when seen from the other side of it.</div> </div> </div> </div>I definitely didn't intend it and I apologize if that offended anyone. I didn't mean anyone playing and enjoying VtM games before did it the wrong way. I just to acknowledge that V5 stresses out some of the aspects of roleplaying a vampire in a way that I find appropriate.<br /> <br /> And I see there's a lot of discussions to catch up on, this is actually a heated subject!<br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/17974-strangelove","name":"Strangelove","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar17974_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"56"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-04-30T10:22:02-07:00","id":1446627,"title":"","content":"I can play an unstable character if I choose. I don't need nor want rules making it crude and mandatory.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25794-mywifeisscary","name":"MyWifeIsScary","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25794_2.png","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3711"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-04-30T10:23:26-07:00","id":1446628,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MyWifeIsScary</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1443592-the-official-v5-vs-v20-thread?p=1446627#post1446627\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I can play an unstable character if I choose. I don't need nor want rules making it crude and mandatory.</div> </div> </div> </div>Like the Beast?<br /> <br /> *rimshot*","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Author of <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Cthulhu-Armageddon-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01KUOM7SI/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982844&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Cthulhu+Armageddon\" target=\"_blank\">Cthulhu Armageddon</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Teenage-Weredeer-Bright-Falls-Mysteries-ebook/dp/B075TTN2FN/ref=sr_1_2?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982717&amp;sr=1-2&amp;keywords=Weredeer#customerReviews\" target=\"_blank\">I was a Teenage Weredeer</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Straight-Outta-Fangton-Comedic-Vampire-ebook/dp/B01KNHICCC/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982774&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Straight+Outta+Fangton\" target=\"_blank\">Straight Outta Fangton</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Lucifers-Star-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01MDM9MCT/ref=mt_kindle?_encoding=UTF8&amp;me=&amp;qid=\" target=\"_blank\">Lucifer's Star</a>, </i>and the <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Rules-Supervillainy-Saga-Book-ebook/dp/B07MB89S33/\" target=\"_blank\">Supervillainy Saga</a>.</i><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","name":"CTPhipps","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12002_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13933"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-04-30T10:42:52-07:00","id":1446633,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CTPhipps</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1443592-the-official-v5-vs-v20-thread?p=1446628#post1446628\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Like the Beast?<br /> <br /> *rimshot*</div> </div> </div> </div>er... what?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25794-mywifeisscary","name":"MyWifeIsScary","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25794_2.png","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3711"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-04-30T12:07:52-07:00","id":1446642,"title":"","content":"I think the joke is that there have been rules in vampire since first edition where the Beast takes control of your character and causes them to act in ways outside the players control.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11637-gryffon15","name":"Gryffon15","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11637_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"900"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-04-30T16:32:44-07:00","id":1446681,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Gryffon15</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1443592-the-official-v5-vs-v20-thread?p=1446642#post1446642\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I think the joke is that there have been rules in vampire since first edition where the Beast takes control of your character and causes them to act in ways outside the players control.</div> </div> </div> </div>Such as? Because all I remember is frenzy. It was always frenzy-or-nothing, which doesn't really fit with how vampires in fiction tend to be represented.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3598-cajunkhan","name":"CajunKhan","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3598_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1700"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-04-30T17:20:28-07:00","id":1446692,"title":"","content":"That is, at least, Gryffon's interpretation? That the Beast has always been a way for the rules to render your character unstable and take away control.<br /> <br /> I'm still not getting the joke either though.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-04-30T17:26:30-07:00","id":1446694,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CajunKhan</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1443592-the-official-v5-vs-v20-thread?p=1446681#post1446681\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Such as? Because all I remember is frenzy. It was always frenzy-or-nothing, which doesn't really fit with how vampires in fiction tend to be represented.</div> </div> </div> </div>Also, Rotschrek.<br /> <br /> Also, if you're a Malkavian fan....<br /> <br /> Just sayin.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Author of <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Cthulhu-Armageddon-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01KUOM7SI/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982844&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Cthulhu+Armageddon\" target=\"_blank\">Cthulhu Armageddon</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Teenage-Weredeer-Bright-Falls-Mysteries-ebook/dp/B075TTN2FN/ref=sr_1_2?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982717&amp;sr=1-2&amp;keywords=Weredeer#customerReviews\" target=\"_blank\">I was a Teenage Weredeer</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Straight-Outta-Fangton-Comedic-Vampire-ebook/dp/B01KNHICCC/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982774&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Straight+Outta+Fangton\" target=\"_blank\">Straight Outta Fangton</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Lucifers-Star-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01MDM9MCT/ref=mt_kindle?_encoding=UTF8&amp;me=&amp;qid=\" target=\"_blank\">Lucifer's Star</a>, </i>and the <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Rules-Supervillainy-Saga-Book-ebook/dp/B07MB89S33/\" target=\"_blank\">Supervillainy Saga</a>.</i><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","name":"CTPhipps","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12002_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13933"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-04-30T20:44:01-07:00","id":1446725,"title":"","content":"I think it's a point of mixed strength given that even though pre-V5 always had Frenzy/Rotschrek as a consideration, you can choose to make characters that struggle with those, or have a relatively easy time with them (basically how much you invest in Virtues), as well as things like the Brujah and Malkavian Clan weaknesses being something you choose to deal with but don't have to because you can always make a member of a different Clan.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-05-02T06:50:53-07:00","id":1446967,"title":"","content":"currently 36:7<br /> That's slightly better than 5:1<br /> <br /> Maybe V20 is just better. For All the reasons. So, do people thing a 5.5 is in order to sort the mess out or is it beyond hope and the next vampire game should look more like 20th.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25794-mywifeisscary","name":"MyWifeIsScary","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25794_2.png","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3711"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-05-02T07:39:35-07:00","id":1446975,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MyWifeIsScary</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1443592-the-official-v5-vs-v20-thread?p=1446967#post1446967\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">currently 36:7<br /> That's slightly better than 5:1<br /> <br /> Maybe V20 is just better. For All the reasons. So, do people thing a 5.5 is in order to sort the mess out or is it beyond hope and the next vampire game should look more like 20th.</div> </div> </div> </div>5.5<br /> this notion that V5 is bad because it isn't V20 is just silly<br /> V5 is conceptually fine but the execution of it all is just why? it's generally just unfinnished and most V5 fans usually are relying on homebrewing or are banking on future releases to finish the system. for me however several of the big problems are the type you just can't fix by building on top of it in future releases, they're just too ingrained for that, it needs a redo.<br /> if it all is doable with the current ppl, resources and just the general state of the world is a different discussion that's more speculation then anything.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25992-archderd","name":"archderd","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25992_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2020"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"205"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-05-02T09:22:53-07:00","id":1446993,"title":"","content":"I need to get back to it but that\u2019s kind of why I have my 20.5 project on the back burner. I prefer 20 but I do appreciate that there\u2019s a lot of interesting concepts put forth in the fifth edition, which I do think can be adapted and put on a slider of personal preferences.<br /> <br /> I\u2019m happy for the V5 folks who enjoy it and I probably will learn it at some point but I do personally prefer V20.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11637-gryffon15","name":"Gryffon15","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11637_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"900"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-05-02T11:09:59-07:00","id":1447004,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MyWifeIsScary</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1443592-the-official-v5-vs-v20-thread?p=1446967#post1446967\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">currently 36:7<br /> That's slightly better than 5:1<br /> <br /> Maybe V20 is just better. For All the reasons. So, do people thing a 5.5 is in order to sort the mess out or is it beyond hope and the next vampire game should look more like 20th.</div> </div> </div> </div>Depend on what V5.5 should actually be?<br /> V20 rules with lore from V5?<br /> Yes please. Because as Phipps has shown many things from the lore change where already part of revised or V20.<br /> <br /> v5.5 just being V5 with some big flaws like low gen vampires has not automatically to feed from other vampires or do a big mess then I think a new Edition would be better.<br /> Because yesterday in the night when I read through the STV Rom book I recocnized what whas my biggest flaw for the blood power system. It is actually an inuniverse contradiction comming up from the idea, that every vampire with low gen is extrem old. While those 4th and 5th Gen whas back then Neonates too. So Methusalahs thirst should not tied with generation but with age. But because with Blood power is now tied with Generation the feeding restriction need either to put so that BP 6 is not allowing you to feed from Animals anymore, BP 7 not more from Blood Bags BP 8+ only from vampires and now more decreasing from Blood Power. Because decreasing BP is not really fitting with that you should fear the old ones if those old ones are after their aeon long sleep only mayby as dangerous as an acilla or mayby an elder.<br /> Or what I would prefer, we just throw out the Blood Power system and if we want to keep the hunger system too, the lower the generation the more maximum hunger roles one could have so that Gen 7- you get one more maximum hunger dice for each gen while from 14+ you get one less maximum hunger dice per gen and can not use actions that would go above your maximum hunger<br /> and Blood Power 0 with 1 Hunger Dice is reserved for Dhampires and Ghoules.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>As I am from Austria I need to clarify two things.<br /> First my native language is german and so please point out if the english I write is broken so I can improve.<br /> Second I do not own VTMV beyond first three books nor any line after M20 Corebook because it is not out there and I wait for the translation.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26160-koronus","name":"Koronus","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2020"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"366"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-05-02T14:28:26-07:00","id":1447035,"title":"","content":"I don't believe accusing people of headcanon is a very good thing to say, especially as making rules up for your game is homebrew not headcanon.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Author of <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Cthulhu-Armageddon-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01KUOM7SI/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982844&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Cthulhu+Armageddon\" target=\"_blank\">Cthulhu Armageddon</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Teenage-Weredeer-Bright-Falls-Mysteries-ebook/dp/B075TTN2FN/ref=sr_1_2?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982717&amp;sr=1-2&amp;keywords=Weredeer#customerReviews\" target=\"_blank\">I was a Teenage Weredeer</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Straight-Outta-Fangton-Comedic-Vampire-ebook/dp/B01KNHICCC/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982774&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Straight+Outta+Fangton\" target=\"_blank\">Straight Outta Fangton</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Lucifers-Star-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01MDM9MCT/ref=mt_kindle?_encoding=UTF8&amp;me=&amp;qid=\" target=\"_blank\">Lucifer's Star</a>, </i>and the <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Rules-Supervillainy-Saga-Book-ebook/dp/B07MB89S33/\" target=\"_blank\">Supervillainy Saga</a>.</i><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","name":"CTPhipps","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12002_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13933"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-05-02T15:09:03-07:00","id":1447040,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MyWifeIsScary</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1443592-the-official-v5-vs-v20-thread?p=1446967#post1446967\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Maybe V20 is just better.</div> </div> </div> </div>It's just a poll of people here. For all my obvious feelings about which is better for me, a poll in one relatively small (in user base and social media footprint) forum isn't really enough to get to this point.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> So, do people thing a 5.5 is in order to sort the mess out or is it beyond hope and the next vampire game should look more like 20th. </div> </div> </div>Honestly, I think we need to see what W5 look like, and how the response to that goes. I don't think the WtA fans are going to be nearly as happy with a W5 that hews relatively closely to V5's lead (though we might get a preview of things to come as we're getting the W20 equivalent to BJD sooner); and the WtA fans already have a significant factor of WW messing with Shattered Dreams and Changing Ways in a fashion that generally pissed people off.<br /> <br /> If W5 manages to thread the needle between making the potential in V5 reality, without radically changing the core systems, and doing a better job of appealing to people that like the original run style of the game? I think it leads to V5 getting minor updates like it's getting now rather than a fully acknowledged V5.5. Paradox can chalk it up to learning pains, and mollify enough fans to just backport in fixes from W5/etc.<br /> <br /> After all, Scion 2e had a pretty messy start, but fans largely overlook it because the later Storypath games address a lot of the flaws with the first game that uses it, increasing the tolerance for those flaws. Modiphius's 2d20 system had a similarly iffy first outing, but has survived as newer implementations of the core system have clearly learn and gotten better. There's no plans for a Scion 2.5 or Mutant Chronicles 3.5, and no serious backlash over the lack of plans.<br /> <br /> If W5 ends up being either divisive or bombs (as is a distinct possibility as the non-VtM WoD games never hit the same level of wide scale cultural significance and are less likely to pull in sales numbers on brand alone), I think it would be a strong reason for Paradox to reconsider how they wan to approach the TTRPG side of their business.<br /> <br /> Speaking as someone that considers Exalted 3e the best edition of Exalted.... Exalted needs a 3.5 or 4th badly. But it's not getting that for a long time because 3e has a massive number of main books to get out first, and Exalted is too massive of a system to just tweak some core rules here and there without lots of unintended consequences for all the Charms built on those rules. Exalted: Essence is going to help keep the Exalted fandom intact, but it's not really a good place for the game-line to be in.<br /> <br /> V5 is quickly moving towards a point of no return: either commit to WoD5 and get out at least the original five core WoD games in the V5 model, or take the hit of ending WoD5 soon, and doing 5.5 or 6 or whatever you want to call it. The delays with Bloodlines 2 could actually help here as they could announce a revamped (ha) VtM to release with it (assuming it makes it out of development hell).<br /> <br /> Of course, they still have to thread that needle. The chance to capitalize on a PR moment only really pays off if you can deliver.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-05-02T15:39:51-07:00","id":1447048,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MyWifeIsScary</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1443592-the-official-v5-vs-v20-thread?p=1446967#post1446967\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">currently 36:7<br /> That's slightly better than 5:1<br /> <br /> <b>Maybe V20 is just better. </b>For All the reasons. So, do people thing a 5.5 is in order to sort the mess out or is it beyond hope and the next vampire game should look more like 20th.</div> </div> </div> </div><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">One rule. There's just ONE rule and you can't abide by it.<br /> <br /> Seriously?</span><br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Heavy Arms</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1443592-the-official-v5-vs-v20-thread?p=1447040#post1447040\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Speaking as someone that considers Exalted 3e the best edition of Exalted.... Exalted needs a 3.5 or 4th badly. But it's not getting that for a long time because 3e has a massive number of main books to get out first, and Exalted is too massive of a system to just tweak some core rules here and there without lots of unintended consequences for all the Charms built on those rules. Exalted: Essence is going to help keep the Exalted fandom intact, but it's not really a good place for the game-line to be in.</div> </div> </div> </div>Sadly, I just can't get into 3EE<br /> <br /> I love all the work they've done but I want gonzo R-rated sexy post-apocalypse anime world and they're going a bit too &quot;realistic&quot; for me.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Heavy Arms</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">V5 is quickly moving towards a point of no return: either commit to WoD5 and get out at least the original five core WoD games in the V5 model, or take the hit of ending WoD5 soon, and doing 5.5 or 6 or whatever you want to call it. The delays with Bloodlines 2 could actually help here as they could announce a revamped (ha) VtM to release with it (assuming it makes it out of development hell).<br /> <br /> Of course, they still have to thread that needle. The chance to capitalize on a PR moment only really pays off if you can deliver.</div> </div> </div> </div>I believe that point passed when 5th Edition was presented for the television shows and video games.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Author of <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Cthulhu-Armageddon-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01KUOM7SI/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982844&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Cthulhu+Armageddon\" target=\"_blank\">Cthulhu Armageddon</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Teenage-Weredeer-Bright-Falls-Mysteries-ebook/dp/B075TTN2FN/ref=sr_1_2?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982717&amp;sr=1-2&amp;keywords=Weredeer#customerReviews\" target=\"_blank\">I was a Teenage Weredeer</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Straight-Outta-Fangton-Comedic-Vampire-ebook/dp/B01KNHICCC/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982774&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Straight+Outta+Fangton\" target=\"_blank\">Straight Outta Fangton</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Lucifers-Star-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01MDM9MCT/ref=mt_kindle?_encoding=UTF8&amp;me=&amp;qid=\" target=\"_blank\">Lucifer's Star</a>, </i>and the <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Rules-Supervillainy-Saga-Book-ebook/dp/B07MB89S33/\" target=\"_blank\">Supervillainy Saga</a>.</i><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":12002,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","user":"CTPhipps","date":". 05-02-2021, 06:43 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","name":"CTPhipps","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12002_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13933"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-05-02T19:28:11-07:00","id":1447085,"title":"","content":"The only thing that is unsalvageable in V5 is Humanity. Just throw in the trash.<br /> <br /> - Reintroduce old Humanity.<br /> <br /> - Make touchstone completely optional and an investment like Contact and Allies. Mostly beneficial for your humanity with the possibility for complications.<br /> <br /> - Touchstones should have higher Humanity than the character rather than having to be human. So an Elder can choose a Ghoul or a Neonate as Touchstone rather than retconning their detachment from human society. It also creates more interesting rp for intrigue and for the PC than a banal human that nobody really cares about except as a target. Make that target a PC instead or a friend of the PC's.<br /> <br /> - Finally for those who cannot play Vampire in other fashion than the Justice League. But with murder and without the Justice part.<br /> Introduce the banes from VTR so they can get sort of get away with it but with a cost. Not ideal imo but certainly better than the Tenets of what I wanted to do anyway.<br /> <br /> <br /> Everything else can simply be adjusted. 6+ powers/attribute, the 5 discipline power limit, the stupid amalgam/discipline etc.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24936-morbus","name":"Morbus","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"119"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-05-02T19:30:39-07:00","id":1447086,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Morbus</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1443592-the-official-v5-vs-v20-thread?p=1447085#post1447085\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The only thing that is unsalvageable in V5 is Humanity. Just throw in the trash.</div> </div> </div> </div>I think that whatever you think of it, the old Humanity system was TERRIBLE for anything resembling actual moral systems and needlessly locked characters into black and white moral decisions by an arbitrary system. You can't change SOME of your views as a vampire. You have to either be Humanity or some alien bizarre system. The new Humanity system has its flaws but it is much-much flexible and even if you hate it, there's NO way anyone should ever want to go back to the old one.<br /> <br /> We need a system that allows player characters to be able to choose their own values, really, rather than getting locked into them.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> - Finally for those who cannot play Vampire in other fashion than the Justice League. But with murder and without the Justice part. Introduce the banes from VTR so they can get sort of get away with it but with a cost. Not ideal imo but certainly better than the Tenets of what I wanted to do anyway. </div> </div> </div>To rebuttal the &quot;Justice League with fangs&quot; thing, I'd like to point out that violence is inherent to vampire. Their lives are full of death, blood, gore, and murder.<br /> <br /> It's no more &quot;Justice League&quot; than the Godfather and violence.<br /> <br /> A gangster movie without violence is just silly.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Author of <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Cthulhu-Armageddon-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01KUOM7SI/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982844&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Cthulhu+Armageddon\" target=\"_blank\">Cthulhu Armageddon</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Teenage-Weredeer-Bright-Falls-Mysteries-ebook/dp/B075TTN2FN/ref=sr_1_2?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982717&amp;sr=1-2&amp;keywords=Weredeer#customerReviews\" target=\"_blank\">I was a Teenage Weredeer</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Straight-Outta-Fangton-Comedic-Vampire-ebook/dp/B01KNHICCC/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982774&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Straight+Outta+Fangton\" target=\"_blank\">Straight Outta Fangton</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Lucifers-Star-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01MDM9MCT/ref=mt_kindle?_encoding=UTF8&amp;me=&amp;qid=\" target=\"_blank\">Lucifer's Star</a>, </i>and the <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Rules-Supervillainy-Saga-Book-ebook/dp/B07MB89S33/\" target=\"_blank\">Supervillainy Saga</a>.</i><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":12002,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","user":"CTPhipps","date":". 05-02-2021, 10:41 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","name":"CTPhipps","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12002_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13933"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-05-02T19:37:34-07:00","id":1447088,"title":"","content":"That's because you don't understand how old Humanity worked.<br /> <br /> You can kill once or twice in self-defense in a campaign and remain on a High Humanity track. Either you succeed your Conscience rolls or you regain your Humanity with time after the ST judged you deserve it.<br /> <br /> Going on a murdering spree however was not okay. It proves that the vampire has grown detached from life and does not really value it, ready to murder anyone in his path.<br /> <br /> And I specifically mentioned murder because I know this is what bothers you and many others with Humanity. No murder is not okay. I don't know any reasonable Human being who think that murder is ever justifiable. Sure there are some edge case where you would be justified in killing someone, but they are rarer than you realize. Torpor is a thing afterall.<br /> <br /> Even super-heroes do not go on a murdering rampage. They arrest criminals.<br /> <br /> Sure you can play the Punisher but you do not deserve a good score in Humanity. Because two wrongs do not make right.<br /> <br /> Edit: But I am open-minded. Which is why I suggested a way for murderers to keep a good Humanity score.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":24936,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24936-morbus","user":"Morbus","date":". 05-02-2021, 10:42 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24936-morbus","name":"Morbus","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"119"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-05-02T19:42:14-07:00","id":1447089,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Morbus</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1443592-the-official-v5-vs-v20-thread?p=1447088#post1447088\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">That's because you don't understand how old Humanity worked.</div> </div> </div> </div>I think I understand it just fine, thank you.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Sure you can play the Punisher but you do not deserve a good score in Humanity. Because you two wrongs do not make right. </div> </div> </div>To explain my logic, Old Humanity was not very good for reflecting, say a Roman centurion or other morality which is human but not necessarily reflective of the Humanity Road.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Author of <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Cthulhu-Armageddon-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01KUOM7SI/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982844&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Cthulhu+Armageddon\" target=\"_blank\">Cthulhu Armageddon</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Teenage-Weredeer-Bright-Falls-Mysteries-ebook/dp/B075TTN2FN/ref=sr_1_2?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982717&amp;sr=1-2&amp;keywords=Weredeer#customerReviews\" target=\"_blank\">I was a Teenage Weredeer</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Straight-Outta-Fangton-Comedic-Vampire-ebook/dp/B01KNHICCC/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982774&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Straight+Outta+Fangton\" target=\"_blank\">Straight Outta Fangton</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Lucifers-Star-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01MDM9MCT/ref=mt_kindle?_encoding=UTF8&amp;me=&amp;qid=\" target=\"_blank\">Lucifer's Star</a>, </i>and the <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Rules-Supervillainy-Saga-Book-ebook/dp/B07MB89S33/\" target=\"_blank\">Supervillainy Saga</a>.</i><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","name":"CTPhipps","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12002_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13933"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-05-02T19:45:48-07:00","id":1447090,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> To rebuttal the &quot;Justice League with fangs&quot; thing, I'd like to point out that violence is inherent to vampire. Their lives are full of death, blood, gore, and murder.<br /> <br /> It's no more &quot;Justice League&quot; than the Godfather and violence.<br /> <br /> A gangster movie without violence is just silly. </div> </div> </div>Exactly. Which is why you do not deserve to be rewarded for acting like a vampire should.<br /> <br /> It's called HUMANITY. Not the path of the perfect Cainite.<br /> <br /> Resisting your nature is the whole point. And what is your nature? Violence.<br /> <br /> If you cannot maintain the morality of a normal human being, your score should reflect that. Plain and simple.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CTPhipps</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1443592-the-official-v5-vs-v20-thread?p=1447089#post1447089\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I think I understand it just fine, thank you.</div> </div> </div> </div>If you did then you would understand that Tenets are far less flexible and more black and white than Humanity ever was. Which is why you can do &quot;Tenets of what I wanted to do anyway&quot; in the first place.<br /> <br /> Doesn't sound very gray to me.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> To explain my logic, Old Humanity was not very good for reflecting, say a Roman centurion or other morality which is human but not necessarily reflective of the Humanity Road. </div> </div> </div>I agree to a certain point that Humanity had limitation for older eras. Which is why other road were conceptualized. And I am fine with those.<br /> Note that even in Rome a centurion that goes on a murdering rampage a la &quot;gangsters&quot; was not really well seen to say the least.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":24936,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24936-morbus","user":"Morbus","date":". 05-02-2021, 10:50 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24936-morbus","name":"Morbus","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"119"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-05-02T20:55:40-07:00","id":1447097,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Morbus</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1443592-the-official-v5-vs-v20-thread?p=1447085#post1447085\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> - Make touchstone completely optional and an investment like Contact and Allies. Mostly beneficial for your humanity with the possibility for complications.<br /></div> </div> </div> </div>Personally I like touchstones, but only non-human ones, and only in conjunction with the Beast Marks system from the Long Road Out Of Hell homebrew. Really, once I got a taste of roleplaying Beast Marks, I immediately became converted into an all-in touchstone enthusiast. So if the game-designers ever make that homebrew canon, I'll be all in.<br /> <br /> On the other hand, the current insistence that we stalk Bella Swans just makes me feel like I'm putting up with Scrappy-Do, or Navi saying, &quot;Hey! Link! Listen! Hey!&quot; ad nauseaum.<br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3598-cajunkhan","name":"CajunKhan","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3598_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1700"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-05-02T21:14:56-07:00","id":1447099,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CajunKhan</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1443592-the-official-v5-vs-v20-thread?p=1447097#post1447097\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Personally I like touchstones, but only non-human ones, and only in conjunction with the Beast Marks system from the Long Road Out Of Hell homebrew. Really, once I got a taste of roleplaying Beast Marks, I immediately became converted into an all-in touchstone enthusiast. So if the game-designers ever make that homebrew canon, I'll be all in.<br /> <br /> On the other hand, the current insistence that we stalk Bella Swans just makes me feel like I'm putting up with Scrappy-Do, or Navi saying, &quot;Hey! Link! Listen! Hey!&quot; ad nauseaum.<br /></div> </div> </div> </div>There is one weird thing that I don't understand and I think is a failure to communicate about Touchstones. I believe they should be people, places, or things since there's no point in making Humanity unlinked from being GOOD while also making Touchstones hyper-focused on people. Humanity, in V5, is linked to being able to keep the Beast down. It doesn't mean being moral, it means being in control of yourself whatever your values be they &quot;I am a devoted fascist&quot; or a &quot;I am a Saint who loves killing fascists.&quot; I find this to be a much more interesting set of possibilities than the strict Road of Humanity. However, they have you laser focused on a Human embodying your convictions which doesn't make any sense, especially if your Convictions and Ambitions are, &quot;Be the best vampire you can possibly be.&quot;<br /> <br /> The thing about Touchstones is that it's clear the authors thought the primary fear that people would have about them would be that it made their vampires into wusses. The Touchstone description overemphasizes vampires not using them as things that make them &quot;good.&quot; They emphasize the crazy murder stalker thing like Dracula and Mina, Edward and Bella, or so on. Now everyone acts like Touchstones have to be horrifying and exploitative versus legitimate friendships or inspirations.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Author of <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Cthulhu-Armageddon-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01KUOM7SI/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982844&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Cthulhu+Armageddon\" target=\"_blank\">Cthulhu Armageddon</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Teenage-Weredeer-Bright-Falls-Mysteries-ebook/dp/B075TTN2FN/ref=sr_1_2?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982717&amp;sr=1-2&amp;keywords=Weredeer#customerReviews\" target=\"_blank\">I was a Teenage Weredeer</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Straight-Outta-Fangton-Comedic-Vampire-ebook/dp/B01KNHICCC/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982774&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Straight+Outta+Fangton\" target=\"_blank\">Straight Outta Fangton</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Lucifers-Star-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01MDM9MCT/ref=mt_kindle?_encoding=UTF8&amp;me=&amp;qid=\" target=\"_blank\">Lucifer's Star</a>, </i>and the <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Rules-Supervillainy-Saga-Book-ebook/dp/B07MB89S33/\" target=\"_blank\">Supervillainy Saga</a>.</i><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","name":"CTPhipps","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12002_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13933"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-05-02T21:31:30-07:00","id":1447101,"title":"","content":"Personally, I like both. Both of them are games I played and enjoyed. Neither is \u201cbetter\u201d honestly, as they both have a lot of merits and flaws.<br /> When I first started playing tabletop roleplaying games back in 2016, I feel in love. I started out with 5th edition Dungeons and Dragons, but grew bored with the lack of character creativity mechanically and started seeking new games. I ended up trying 4th edition (v20) before 5th was even a pipe dream. Or rather, I tried to try it. See, when several groups wouldn\u2019t let you play at all because they weren\u2019t willing to teach news players, you kind of can\u2019t play. And when the few groups I could play end up going bottom up session 2 because of sudden life changes, which are understandable by the way, I kind of just gave up trying. The gaming pool was so very limited for me, so I gave up and moved on.<br /> In 2019 or 2020, I can\u2019t remember, I heard about 5th edition and was more experienced with RPGs, so I found a group and play. It was great, and the mechanics were easy to learn. Also, it was just easier to find a game, so that helped. However, I looked back at 20th, and it\u2019s just at cool. Obviously V5 is a hell of a lot more streamlined, which I love, but V20 has a lot to work with.<br /> I would say stuff like how I love the diverse options in V20, or how V5 does mortality a lot better in their core book, waiting for Sabbat to see if that continues. However, I\u2019d rather leave you off with the best rule in the books:<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> This is the most important rule of all, and the only real rule worth following: There are no rules. This game should be whatever you want it to be, whether that\u2019s a nearly dice-less chronicle of in-character socialization or a long-running tactical campaign with each player controlling a small coterie of vampires. If the rules in this book interfere with your enjoyment of the game, change them. The world is far too big, no set of inflexible rules can possibly reflect it. Think of this book as a collection of guidelines: suggested but not mandatory ways of capturing the World of Darkness in the format of a game. You decide what works best in your game. And you may freely use, alter, abuse, or ignore these rules at your whim <br /> Page 130 of V5, and page 245 of V20 (Just worded Differently) </div> </div> </div>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\"><div align=\"left\"><a href=\"http://www.nodiatis.com/personality.htm\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://www.nodiatis.com/pub/7.jpg\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a></div></div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26764-vilenecromancer","name":"Vilenecromancer","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar26764_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"247"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-05-02T21:58:12-07:00","id":1447106,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MyWifeIsScary</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1443592-the-official-v5-vs-v20-thread?p=1446967#post1446967\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">currently 36:7<br /> That's slightly better than 5:1<br /> <br /> Maybe V20 is just better. For All the reasons. So, do people thing a 5.5 is in order to sort the mess out or is it beyond hope and the next vampire game should look more like 20th.</div> </div> </div> </div>Or maybe V20 is not better? 'All the reasons' seem to depend on who we are talking about making the objections - for me, many of the objections just boil down to \u201cI just don\u2019t like the way things are now done\u201d. When people start saying they want it to be more like V20, which isn\u2019t very specific, the counter to that is that it would be a backwards step.<br /> <br /> It\u2019s all a bit moot anyway because there isn\u2019t going to be any new edition any time soon.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2517-trippy","name":"Trippy","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2517_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1018"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-05-02T22:04:26-07:00","id":1447107,"title":"","content":"In regards to W5 for me if they start fundamentally changing the tribes and cosmology in a significant way that doesnt hew closely to tradition then W5 is DOA for me anyway. I can handle most of the changes in the V5 metaplot since besides Clans kindred society can be very fluid. WTA is far more strict in where each tribe draws its culture and traditions from. Change anything significantly and it ceases to be WTA.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>The Hecata are a sect not a clan.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24211-frontline989","name":"Frontline989","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24211_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"152"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-05-02T22:11:26-07:00","id":1447109,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Frontline989</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1443592-the-official-v5-vs-v20-thread?p=1447107#post1447107\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">In regards to W5 for me if they start fundamentally changing the tribes and cosmology in a significant way that doesnt hew closely to tradition then W5 is DOA for me anyway. I can handle most of the changes in the V5 metaplot since besides Clans kindred society can be very fluid. WTA is far more strict in where each tribe draws its culture and traditions from. Change anything significantly and it ceases to be WTA.</div> </div> </div> </div>I'm hoping HEART OF THE FOREST was a good peak into W:TA 5th Edition society.<br /> <br /> &quot;The Apocalypse is over. What now?&quot;","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Author of <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Cthulhu-Armageddon-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01KUOM7SI/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982844&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Cthulhu+Armageddon\" target=\"_blank\">Cthulhu Armageddon</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Teenage-Weredeer-Bright-Falls-Mysteries-ebook/dp/B075TTN2FN/ref=sr_1_2?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982717&amp;sr=1-2&amp;keywords=Weredeer#customerReviews\" target=\"_blank\">I was a Teenage Weredeer</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Straight-Outta-Fangton-Comedic-Vampire-ebook/dp/B01KNHICCC/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982774&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Straight+Outta+Fangton\" target=\"_blank\">Straight Outta Fangton</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Lucifers-Star-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01MDM9MCT/ref=mt_kindle?_encoding=UTF8&amp;me=&amp;qid=\" target=\"_blank\">Lucifer's Star</a>, </i>and the <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Rules-Supervillainy-Saga-Book-ebook/dp/B07MB89S33/\" target=\"_blank\">Supervillainy Saga</a>.</i><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","name":"CTPhipps","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12002_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13933"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-05-02T22:17:41-07:00","id":1447111,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CTPhipps</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1443592-the-official-v5-vs-v20-thread?p=1447109#post1447109\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I'm hoping HEART OF THE FOREST was a good peak into W:TA 5th Edition society.<br /> <br /> &quot;The Apocalypse is over. What now?&quot;</div> </div> </div> </div>Thats the WTA BJD analog? Im very interested as well.<br /> <br /> I wish they'd taken more from BJD for V5 into account. I know I can still use it in my games and I have been but its such a wasted opportunity.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>The Hecata are a sect not a clan.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24211-frontline989","name":"Frontline989","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24211_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"152"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-05-02T22:20:51-07:00","id":1447112,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Frontline989</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1443592-the-official-v5-vs-v20-thread?p=1447111#post1447111\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Thats the WTA BJD analog? Im very interested as well.<br /> <br /> I wish they'd taken more from BJD for V5 into account. I know I can still use it in my games and I have been but its such a wasted opportunity.</div> </div> </div> </div>No, it's a Visual Novel that was released last year.<br /> <br /> <a href=\"https://store.steampowered.com/app/1342620/Werewolf_The_Apocalypse__Heart_of_the_Forest/\" target=\"_blank\">https://store.steampowered.com/app/1...of_the_Forest/</a><br /> <br /> It takes place in 2020 and is talks about how the Garou are recovering from the events of 2004 when a large number of them went into the Umbra then never came back. The Garou have been rebuilding ever since.<br /> <br /> It got criticized for shitting on the Get of Fenris, though.<br /> <br /> I am very excited about the BJD equivalent.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Author of <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Cthulhu-Armageddon-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01KUOM7SI/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982844&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Cthulhu+Armageddon\" target=\"_blank\">Cthulhu Armageddon</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Teenage-Weredeer-Bright-Falls-Mysteries-ebook/dp/B075TTN2FN/ref=sr_1_2?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982717&amp;sr=1-2&amp;keywords=Weredeer#customerReviews\" target=\"_blank\">I was a Teenage Weredeer</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Straight-Outta-Fangton-Comedic-Vampire-ebook/dp/B01KNHICCC/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982774&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Straight+Outta+Fangton\" target=\"_blank\">Straight Outta Fangton</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Lucifers-Star-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01MDM9MCT/ref=mt_kindle?_encoding=UTF8&amp;me=&amp;qid=\" target=\"_blank\">Lucifer's Star</a>, </i>and the <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Rules-Supervillainy-Saga-Book-ebook/dp/B07MB89S33/\" target=\"_blank\">Supervillainy Saga</a>.</i><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","name":"CTPhipps","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12002_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13933"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-05-02T23:21:04-07:00","id":1447120,"title":"","content":"VTR Humanity does what V5 Humanity intends to do, but better. And it has the old Hierarchy of Sins as well as Touchstones. So I don't think the problem was the old Hierarchy of Sins or that throwing that out is the solution.<br /> <br /> Re: Centurions, you would just give them a different Path. Humanity isn't supposed to be universal throughout all time periods and cultures. It was created for the modern day, and that's why Dark Ages has alternate Paths of Humanity.<br /> <br /> Really, VTM should've just acknowledged that the Path of Humanity is merely culturally prevalent (among vampires) and relative easy to follow, rather than being the default for everyone, and therefore allowed you to pick any of the other Paths on the Road instead.<br /> <br /> Which would also mean humans never have Humanity either, because it's not really a mark of how human you are but how much you stave off the Beast by following a moral code similar enough to the dominant ethics of the culture you lived in to make it easy to learn.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Writer, publisher, performer<br /> Mostly he/his, sometimes she/her IRL <a href=\"https://adam-lowe.com\" target=\"_blank\">https://adam-lowe.com</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5291-adambeyoncelowe","name":"adambeyoncelowe","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5291_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2802"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-05-02T23:27:20-07:00","id":1447122,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>adambeyoncelowe</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1443592-the-official-v5-vs-v20-thread?p=1447120#post1447120\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">VTR Humanity does what V5 Humanity intends to do, but better. And it has the old Hierarchy of Sins as well as Touchstones. So I don't think the problem was the old Hierarchy of Sins or that throwing that out is the solution.<br /> <br /> Re: Centurions, you would just give them a different Path. Humanity isn't supposed to be universal throughout all time periods and cultures. It was created for the modern day, and that's why Dark Ages has alternate Paths of Humanity.<br /> <br /> Really, VTM should've just acknowledged that the Path of Humanity is merely culturally prevalent (among vampires) and relative easy to follow, rather than being the default for everyone, and therefore allowed you to pick any of the other Paths on the Road instead.<br /> <br /> Which would also mean humans never have Humanity either, because it's not really a mark of how human you are but how much you stave off the Beast by following a moral code similar enough to the dominant ethics of the culture you lived in to make it easy to learn.</div> </div> </div> </div>Paths are not something that should be handed out willy nilly to humans. I'm a Revised guy and they're meant to be alien and unknowable.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Author of <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Cthulhu-Armageddon-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01KUOM7SI/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982844&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Cthulhu+Armageddon\" target=\"_blank\">Cthulhu Armageddon</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Teenage-Weredeer-Bright-Falls-Mysteries-ebook/dp/B075TTN2FN/ref=sr_1_2?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982717&amp;sr=1-2&amp;keywords=Weredeer#customerReviews\" target=\"_blank\">I was a Teenage Weredeer</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Straight-Outta-Fangton-Comedic-Vampire-ebook/dp/B01KNHICCC/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982774&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Straight+Outta+Fangton\" target=\"_blank\">Straight Outta Fangton</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Lucifers-Star-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01MDM9MCT/ref=mt_kindle?_encoding=UTF8&amp;me=&amp;qid=\" target=\"_blank\">Lucifer's Star</a>, </i>and the <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Rules-Supervillainy-Saga-Book-ebook/dp/B07MB89S33/\" target=\"_blank\">Supervillainy Saga</a>.</i><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","name":"CTPhipps","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12002_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13933"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-05-02T23:38:58-07:00","id":1447123,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CTPhipps</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1443592-the-official-v5-vs-v20-thread?p=1447122#post1447122\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Paths are not something that should be handed out willy nilly to humans. I'm a Revised guy and they're meant to be alien and unknowable.</div> </div> </div> </div>Most of them really aren't that alien. They are only alien the way that Predators and Klingons are alien: as an exaggeration of a common culture or mindset. Honorable Accord is an exaggeration of those people who believe that the rules are the rules, personal feelings be damned. Feral Heart is an exaggeration of people who belief in family and tribe above all else blended with primitivist cults. Power/Inner Voice is an exaggeration of various forms of social darwinism such as Ayn Randism. Most of the others are exaggerations of some form of real world religion.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":3598,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3598-cajunkhan","user":"CajunKhan","date":". 05-03-2021, 02:41 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3598-cajunkhan","name":"CajunKhan","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3598_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1700"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-05-03T02:08:34-07:00","id":1447130,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CTPhipps</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1443592-the-official-v5-vs-v20-thread?p=1447122#post1447122\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Paths are not something that should be handed out willy nilly to humans. I'm a Revised guy and they're meant to be alien and unknowable.</div> </div> </div> </div>I agree, but perhaps for a slightly different reason: humans don't need Paths, and that includes the Path of Humanity.<br /> <br /> Though I think we're talking at least partly at cross-purposes. When you say 'Path', I think you mean 'Path of Enlightenment'. When I say 'Path', I mean in the broader sense of Roads and Paths as they are in DA (and from which the present day Paths, including Humanity, are descended).<br /> <br /> I include Humanity as a Path, even though the source material is ambivalent about that (except in DA). Because I think it is by dint of what it aims to do. You lose a lot of the supposed confusion around Humanity if you see it as just another Path (albeit the most popular one), rather than as something distinct.<br /> <br /> Paths are specifically there as an anchor against the Beast. They're iterations (or perversions?) of the path to Golconda/redemption laid down by one of the Archangels, on behalf of God, when Caine was cursed.<br /> <br /> The books always sort of fudged it by saying that humans only have Humanity scores as a relative thing. They don't actually have to follow the Path of Humanity, though.<br /> <br /> But it was always confusing, and that's partly where the misunderstanding about what Humanity actually is comes from. Humanity should be a Path, no more and no less, and therefore only for beings who actively have to resist the Beast.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Writer, publisher, performer<br /> Mostly he/his, sometimes she/her IRL <a href=\"https://adam-lowe.com\" target=\"_blank\">https://adam-lowe.com</a>","edited":{"userid":5291,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5291-adambeyoncelowe","user":"adambeyoncelowe","date":". 05-03-2021, 05:15 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5291-adambeyoncelowe","name":"adambeyoncelowe","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5291_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2802"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-05-03T02:14:51-07:00","id":1447131,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>adambeyoncelowe</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1443592-the-official-v5-vs-v20-thread?p=1447130#post1447130\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> But it was always confusing, and that's partly where the misunderstanding about what Humanity actually is comes from. Humanity should be a Path, no more and no less, and therefore only for beings who actively have to resist the Beast.</div> </div> </div> </div>I suppose that depends on how you are meant to view the &quot;morality&quot; of the game and whether Golconda is a thing or even relevant to most players. Making Humanity just another Path or Road has kind of always been interpreted by some players as saying that Paths were &quot;better&quot; due to the fact that Humanity is so inherently contradictory to the Life of the UndeadTM. Which led to the view that I think undermines the Paths that they're &quot;easier&quot; to be on than Humanity. Which I think does them a disservice even in the Sabbat.<br /> <br /> So I favored, while in Revised to V20 to make Paths hard to get on and Humanity the &quot;default.&quot; However, I admit that was always imperfect to me and Roads was something most of my players favored with the idea of Humanity as just another.<br /> <br /> But yes, not giving humanity a Humanity score may have been a better idea. You're probably right.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Author of <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Cthulhu-Armageddon-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01KUOM7SI/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982844&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Cthulhu+Armageddon\" target=\"_blank\">Cthulhu Armageddon</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Teenage-Weredeer-Bright-Falls-Mysteries-ebook/dp/B075TTN2FN/ref=sr_1_2?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982717&amp;sr=1-2&amp;keywords=Weredeer#customerReviews\" target=\"_blank\">I was a Teenage Weredeer</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Straight-Outta-Fangton-Comedic-Vampire-ebook/dp/B01KNHICCC/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982774&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Straight+Outta+Fangton\" target=\"_blank\">Straight Outta Fangton</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Lucifers-Star-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01MDM9MCT/ref=mt_kindle?_encoding=UTF8&amp;me=&amp;qid=\" target=\"_blank\">Lucifer's Star</a>, </i>and the <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Rules-Supervillainy-Saga-Book-ebook/dp/B07MB89S33/\" target=\"_blank\">Supervillainy Saga</a>.</i><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","name":"CTPhipps","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12002_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13933"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-05-03T02:18:09-07:00","id":1447132,"title":"","content":"Roads are swell. Part of the strength of the DA lines were how accessible roads were without you needing to be a crazed extremist in a cult like the sabbat. <br /> <br /> The things that bother me most about V5 are Generation/Blood potency and disciplines, and the resulting impact they have on the story. These are hard retcons that fly in the face of what VTM is all about, and they're a lesser system than what came before. Touchstones can just be dismissed as a one-off misjudgement, but changing generation and the new system for disciplines is a fundamental misunderstanding of the source material. It kills my desire to diablerize, and if it kills my desire, it kills everyone's desire, and the Jyhad is going to be chill because you're only fighting people you don't like so it's in everyone's best interests for everyone to get along. It kills my occult theorizing and the mindfulness the old system had towards the philosophies of several clans and sects; Gnostics used to be right, now their views are no more valid than anyone elses. Hermetics used to be right, and now their views are less valid than anyone elses. The Sabbat are preparing for war with rare but somewhat stronger vampires, rather than apocalyptic blood-gods... <br /> <br /> Also all these discipline 1-5 choices suck. I'm not choosing which power to have, i'm choosing what power to deny myself. OWOD is built around the idea that everyone can be 10/10/10 10/10/10/ 10/10/10... they just need to rise above their material circumstances and challenge gods, or ascend like in Mage. V5 doesn't give you that. V5 gives you a setting where it's wrong to have ambition, where it's wrong to want something more, where the best thing a vampire could hope for is to become human.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25794-mywifeisscary","name":"MyWifeIsScary","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25794_2.png","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3711"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-05-03T02:24:31-07:00","id":1447135,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MyWifeIsScary</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1443592-the-official-v5-vs-v20-thread?p=1447132#post1447132\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The Sabbat are preparing for war with rare but somewhat stronger vampires, rather than apocalyptic blood-gods...</div> </div> </div> </div>Hasn't it been a thing since 2nd Edition [when they were first introduced in any real way] onward that the Sabbat's war on the Antediluvians was stupid? I mean, it was always a suspicion that the Antediluvians were playing them for chumps but it was confirmed as early as The Dark Ages.<br /> <br /> The Sabbat never had any chance against the Ancients and that was part of the point. It was just a scam to get the young to die for them.<br /> <br /> Sort of like the Kuei Jin and the Great Leap Outward.<br /> <br /> &quot;Go fight the Yama Kings/Antediluvians by killing the Camarilla?&quot;<br /> <br /> &quot;What do the Camarilla have to do with either?&quot;<br /> <br /> &quot;SHUT UP!&quot;<br /> <br /> I mean, Lasombra and Tzimisce being alive was established pretty early.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Author of <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Cthulhu-Armageddon-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01KUOM7SI/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982844&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Cthulhu+Armageddon\" target=\"_blank\">Cthulhu Armageddon</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Teenage-Weredeer-Bright-Falls-Mysteries-ebook/dp/B075TTN2FN/ref=sr_1_2?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982717&amp;sr=1-2&amp;keywords=Weredeer#customerReviews\" target=\"_blank\">I was a Teenage Weredeer</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Straight-Outta-Fangton-Comedic-Vampire-ebook/dp/B01KNHICCC/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982774&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Straight+Outta+Fangton\" target=\"_blank\">Straight Outta Fangton</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Lucifers-Star-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01MDM9MCT/ref=mt_kindle?_encoding=UTF8&amp;me=&amp;qid=\" target=\"_blank\">Lucifer's Star</a>, </i>and the <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Rules-Supervillainy-Saga-Book-ebook/dp/B07MB89S33/\" target=\"_blank\">Supervillainy Saga</a>.</i><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":12002,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","user":"CTPhipps","date":". 05-03-2021, 05:26 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","name":"CTPhipps","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12002_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13933"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-05-03T02:25:37-07:00","id":1447136,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CTPhipps</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1443592-the-official-v5-vs-v20-thread?p=1447131#post1447131\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I suppose that depends on how you are meant to view the &amp;quot;morality&amp;quot; of the game and whether Golconda is a thing or even relevant to most players. Making Humanity just another Path or Road has kind of always been interpreted by some players as saying that Paths were &amp;quot;better&amp;quot; due to the fact that Humanity is so inherently contradictory to the Life of the UndeadTM. Which led to the view that I think undermines the Paths that they're &amp;quot;easier&amp;quot; to be on than Humanity. Which I think does them a disservice even in the Sabbat.<br /> <br /> So I favored, while in Revised to V20 to make Paths hard to get on and Humanity the &amp;quot;default.&amp;quot; However, I admit that was always imperfect to me and Roads was something most of my players favored with the idea of Humanity as just another.<br /> <br /> But yes, not giving humanity a Humanity score may have been a better idea. You're probably right.</div> </div> </div> </div>Making Humanity the 'default' doesn't mean it's inherently a separate thing, though. I live in a nominally Anglican country. The Church of England is the default (or supposed to be). That makes it easier to be an Anglican, for sure, but it's still just one of many religions.<br /> <br /> I see Humanity in the same way. Humanity is the most common and easily accessible Path in Western (European and N. American) cultures. It might even be the closest Path to the original one that leads to Golconda, as you can only reach Golconda via Humanity (though there may be equivalent transcendent states for other Paths).<br /> <br /> That doesn't mean we should have Humanity and Paths as two entirely separate things. That's where VTM has sometimes got things muddled, and why V5 has made Humanity about pretending to be human rather than a Biblical moral code that leads you to redemption. <br /> <br /> I don't think making Humanity another Path detracts from Humanity at all. Actually, the fact Humanity is the only Path that leads to Golconda (and perhaps regaining your mortality, at least in 1e) still makes it a good choice. Having more choices doesn't dilute that.<br /> <br /> I actually think Humanity becomes more important, even if I rarely play characters who follow it, because it's the only real 'out'. If you follow one of the other Paths, you are likely to just find different flavours of damnation. Sometimes playing that is more interesting, though.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Writer, publisher, performer<br /> Mostly he/his, sometimes she/her IRL <a href=\"https://adam-lowe.com\" target=\"_blank\">https://adam-lowe.com</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5291-adambeyoncelowe","name":"adambeyoncelowe","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5291_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2802"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-05-03T02:25:53-07:00","id":1447137,"title":"","content":"Things are pretty clear in VTM. Most humans are on the Path of Humanity even if they do not know it. Because it's the path of being a human. And holding human values. It doesn't really matter for Humans specifically tough because they do not have a Beast so they can even hit 0 with no consequence whatsoever.<br /> <br /> It's also possible for Human to be on another path but it's rare because it would require a Human to go against their very nature. They have to really strive to be monsters to change paths. And thus it's mostly ghouls and Revenants who follows non humanity paths. And in my headcanon, infernalist mortals as well.<br /> <br /> In Dark Age tough, things are more complicated. As morality was slightly different back then. A Crusader for exemple is one of the few archetype that can reliably hit wassail using Humanity despite them being a heroic figure in the past and the present.<br /> Unfortunately purging the Heathens, Killing the Heretics, and burning the Witches and other heinous crimes against humanity are not supported by the Road. So others were created to cater to those archetype. Paradise or Knight work much better in those cases.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24936-morbus","name":"Morbus","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"119"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-05-03T02:27:09-07:00","id":1447138,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MyWifeIsScary</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1443592-the-official-v5-vs-v20-thread?p=1447132#post1447132\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Also all these discipline 1-5 choices suck. I'm not choosing which power to have, i'm choosing what power to deny myself. OWOD is built around the idea that everyone can be 10/10/10 10/10/10/ 10/10/10... they just need to rise above their material circumstances and challenge gods, or ascend like in Mage. V5 doesn't give you that. V5 gives you a setting where it's wrong to have ambition, where it's wrong to want something more, where the best thing a vampire could hope for is to become human.</div> </div> </div> </div>New Fortitude and Animalism are wildly superior to the old versions. Fortitude and Animalism used to suck.<br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3598-cajunkhan","name":"CajunKhan","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3598_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1700"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-05-03T02:28:26-07:00","id":1447139,"title":"","content":"Eh, there's some logic to it. <br /> The Vauldrie breaks bonds and keeps the sabbat safe from the control of the Antideluvians. <br /> All those who don't partake in the vauldrie are ready to be puppets for the antideluvians, and therefore must be destroyed. <br /> <br /> Also the cam occupying most cities prevents the sabbat from searching for antideluvians to devour.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25794-mywifeisscary","name":"MyWifeIsScary","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25794_2.png","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3711"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-05-03T02:28:37-07:00","id":1447140,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Morbus</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1443592-the-official-v5-vs-v20-thread?p=1447137#post1447137\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Things are pretty clear in VTM. Most humans are on the Path of Humanity even if they do not know it. Because it's the path of being a human. And holding human values. It doesn't really matter for Humans specifically tough because they do not have a Beast so they can even hit 0 with no consequence whatsoever.</div> </div> </div> </div>As of Hunter's Hunted (1st Edition) a human who hits 0 gets a Derangement then slots back up to Humanity 1.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MyWifeIsScary</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1443592-the-official-v5-vs-v20-thread?p=1447139#post1447139\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Eh, there's some logic to it.<br /> The Vauldrie breaks bonds and keeps the sabbat safe from the control of the Antideluvians.<br /> All those who don't partake in the vauldrie are ready to be puppets for the antideluvians, and therefore must be destroyed.<br /> <br /> Also the cam occupying most cities prevents the sabbat from searching for antideluvians to devour.</div> </div> </div> </div>Yep, the Sabbat have got a pretty sweet scam going. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /> Then the Antediluvians had to ruin it by proving to be real.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Author of <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Cthulhu-Armageddon-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01KUOM7SI/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982844&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Cthulhu+Armageddon\" target=\"_blank\">Cthulhu Armageddon</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Teenage-Weredeer-Bright-Falls-Mysteries-ebook/dp/B075TTN2FN/ref=sr_1_2?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982717&amp;sr=1-2&amp;keywords=Weredeer#customerReviews\" target=\"_blank\">I was a Teenage Weredeer</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Straight-Outta-Fangton-Comedic-Vampire-ebook/dp/B01KNHICCC/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982774&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Straight+Outta+Fangton\" target=\"_blank\">Straight Outta Fangton</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Lucifers-Star-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01MDM9MCT/ref=mt_kindle?_encoding=UTF8&amp;me=&amp;qid=\" target=\"_blank\">Lucifer's Star</a>, </i>and the <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Rules-Supervillainy-Saga-Book-ebook/dp/B07MB89S33/\" target=\"_blank\">Supervillainy Saga</a>.</i><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":12002,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","user":"CTPhipps","date":". 05-03-2021, 05:31 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","name":"CTPhipps","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12002_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13933"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-05-03T02:34:03-07:00","id":1447141,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CTPhipps</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1443592-the-official-v5-vs-v20-thread?p=1447135#post1447135\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Hasn't it been a thing since 2nd Edition [when they were first introduced in any real way] onward that the Sabbat's war on the Antediluvians was stupid? I mean, it was always a suspicion that the Antediluvians were playing them for chumps but it was confirmed as early as The Dark Ages.<br /> <br /> The Sabbat never had any chance against the Ancients and that was part of the point. It was just a scam to get the young to die for them.<br /> <br /> Sort of like the Kuei Jin and the Great Leap Outward.<br /> <br /> &quot;Go fight the Yama Kings/Antediluvians by killing the Camarilla?&quot;<br /> <br /> &quot;What do the Camarilla have to do with either?&quot;<br /> <br /> &quot;SHUT UP!&quot;<br /> <br /> I mean, Lasombra and Tzimisce being alive was established pretty early.</div> </div> </div> </div>Players Guide to the Sabbat was 1e, so define 'any real way'? Also, although your question is framed rhetorically, I don't think the war on the Antediluvians is stupid. Suicidal, yes. But there's a very real reason why you'd do it, because if you don't, they will come along and eat you up sooner or later.<br /> <br /> It might seem stupid for America and Britain to fight Godzilla, given he's only currently stomping around Tokyo, but it's actually the wiser choice. Because Godzilla is a threat to everyone.<br /> <br /> Okay, in this scenario, Godzilla hasn't hatched yet, but the Sabbat knows there are eggs hidden all over the world (their elders have seen these eggs hatching before!) and they strongly suspect what will happen if one of those eggs does hatch again. So it makes sense to burn those eggs before they do. Or at least to be prepared.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Writer, publisher, performer<br /> Mostly he/his, sometimes she/her IRL <a href=\"https://adam-lowe.com\" target=\"_blank\">https://adam-lowe.com</a>","edited":{"userid":5291,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5291-adambeyoncelowe","user":"adambeyoncelowe","date":". 05-03-2021, 05:36 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5291-adambeyoncelowe","name":"adambeyoncelowe","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5291_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2802"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-05-03T02:40:18-07:00","id":1447143,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>adambeyoncelowe</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1443592-the-official-v5-vs-v20-thread?p=1447141#post1447141\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Players Guide to the Sabbat was 1e, so define 'any real way'?</div> </div> </div> </div><a href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/List_of_Vampire:_The_Masquerade_books\" target=\"_blank\">https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/List_o...squerade_books</a><br /> <br /> Second Edition actually.<br /> <br /> <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> Second Edition was when things went international and away from Chicago.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>adambeyoncelowe</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1443592-the-official-v5-vs-v20-thread?p=1447141#post1447141\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I don't think the war on the Antediluvians is stupid. Suicidal, yes. But there's a very real reason why you'd do it, because if you don't, they will come along and eat you up sooner or later.<br /> <br /> It might seem stupid for America and Britain to fight Godzilla, given he's only currently stomping around Tokyo, but it's actually the wiser choice. Because Godzilla is a threat to everyone.<br /> <br /> Okay, in this scenario, Godzilla hasn't hatched yet, but the Sabbat knows there are eggs hidden all over the world (their elders have seen these eggs hatching before!) and they strongly suspect what will happen if one of those eggs does hatch again. So it makes sense to burn those eggs before they do. Or at least to be prepared.</div> </div> </div> </div>My take is significantly more cynical and that the Sabbat have never actually had any real interest in fighting the Antediluvians. It's why I was initially taken aback by the Gehenna Crusade since from my perspective it would have come off as a Snipe Hunt even with the rise of the Ravnos Antediluvian. Mind you, as any reader of my posts will know, I have a very cynical interpretation of every single one of the sects. Basically, I went with the impression the Sabbat is a coarser rougher version of the Camarilla but not really different at the core being about land, power, and wealth.<br /> <br /> After all, the Sabbats justification for fighting the Camarilla is that they're the Antediluvians pawns--when we know they're no more pawns than the Sabbat,<br /> <br /> No, the only way to deal with the antediluvains is to FEED THEM OTHER VAMPIRES!<br /> <br /> *puts on Cthulhu cultist robe*<br /> <br /> PRAISE THE DARK FATHERS!<br /> <br /> PRAISE THE TRUE HAND!<br /> <br /> <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/biggrin.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Big Grin\" smilieid=\"3\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Author of <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Cthulhu-Armageddon-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01KUOM7SI/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982844&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Cthulhu+Armageddon\" target=\"_blank\">Cthulhu Armageddon</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Teenage-Weredeer-Bright-Falls-Mysteries-ebook/dp/B075TTN2FN/ref=sr_1_2?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982717&amp;sr=1-2&amp;keywords=Weredeer#customerReviews\" target=\"_blank\">I was a Teenage Weredeer</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Straight-Outta-Fangton-Comedic-Vampire-ebook/dp/B01KNHICCC/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982774&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Straight+Outta+Fangton\" target=\"_blank\">Straight Outta Fangton</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Lucifers-Star-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01MDM9MCT/ref=mt_kindle?_encoding=UTF8&amp;me=&amp;qid=\" target=\"_blank\">Lucifer's Star</a>, </i>and the <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Rules-Supervillainy-Saga-Book-ebook/dp/B07MB89S33/\" target=\"_blank\">Supervillainy Saga</a>.</i><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":12002,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","user":"CTPhipps","date":". 05-03-2021, 05:45 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","name":"CTPhipps","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12002_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13933"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-05-03T02:42:18-07:00","id":1447144,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CajunKhan</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1443592-the-official-v5-vs-v20-thread?p=1447138#post1447138\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> New Fortitude and Animalism are wildly superior to the old versions. Fortitude and Animalism used to suck.<br /></div> </div> </div> </div>1: OG Animalism's great, it's just misunderstood by a lot of people.<br /> 2-Fortitude was a LOT better before revised fucked the balance of it and V20 copy-pasted revised without really thinking about it sometimes (or perhaps they did put the thought in and decided to used revised rules... which is weird and I don't see why you'd wanna do that but I suppose revised did it for a reason). If we use V1/V2 rules for fortitude, it's actually... well, V5 fort has emotional Fortitude and that's strong, but in actually physical preventing damage pre-revised fort is significantly better level-by-level, especially since V5 magically makes body armour completely useless for vampires. It's also a nicer discipline to look at because it's a lot simpler and you don't need to remember so much stuff, leaving you more brain-space for dealing with disciplines that are actually meant to have active effects.<br /> 3- You should also mention that Presence is mildly better than prior editions, because it doesn't cost as much blood.<br /> <br /> But then let's remember<br /> -Auspex is &quot;wildly inferior&quot; in V5<br /> Celerity is &quot;wildly inferior&quot; in V5<br /> -Dominate is &quot;wildly inferior&quot; in V5<br /> Obfuscate is &quot;wildly inferior&quot; in V5<br /> Potence is &quot;wildly inferior&quot; in V5<br /> <br /> Chimestry is wildly inferior in V5<br /> Necromancy is &quot;wildly inferior&quot; in V5<br /> Obtenebration is &quot;wildly inferior&quot; in V5<br /> Thaumaturgy is &quot;wildly inferior&quot; in V5<br /> Vicissitude is &quot;wildly inferior&quot; in V5<br /> <br /> And honestly I'd say most of these have more weight on the story than Animalism/Fortitude","signature":"","edited":{"userid":25794,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25794-mywifeisscary","user":"MyWifeIsScary","date":". 05-03-2021, 05:57 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25794-mywifeisscary","name":"MyWifeIsScary","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25794_2.png","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3711"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-05-03T02:43:46-07:00","id":1447145,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CTPhipps</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1443592-the-official-v5-vs-v20-thread?p=1447140#post1447140\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> As of Hunter's Hunted (1st Edition) a human who hits 0 gets a Derangement then slots back up to Humanity 1.</div> </div> </div> </div>Well I don't know about that. But as far as I played it, Humanity score for Human is only useful should they ever get embraced. A mobster for example would start much closer to wassail than a charity worker. <br /> <br /> And maybe for some side rule like being tainted by the worm.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24936-morbus","name":"Morbus","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"119"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-05-03T02:47:25-07:00","id":1447147,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Morbus</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1443592-the-official-v5-vs-v20-thread?p=1447145#post1447145\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Well I don't know about that. But as far as I played it, Humanity score for Human is only useful should they ever get embraced. A mobster for example would start much closer to wassail than a charity worker.<br /> <br /> And maybe for some side rule like being tainted by the worm.</div> </div> </div> </div>Eh, it's close enough to no consequences as Humanity 0 has always been the most heinous crazy acts.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Author of <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Cthulhu-Armageddon-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01KUOM7SI/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982844&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Cthulhu+Armageddon\" target=\"_blank\">Cthulhu Armageddon</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Teenage-Weredeer-Bright-Falls-Mysteries-ebook/dp/B075TTN2FN/ref=sr_1_2?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982717&amp;sr=1-2&amp;keywords=Weredeer#customerReviews\" target=\"_blank\">I was a Teenage Weredeer</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Straight-Outta-Fangton-Comedic-Vampire-ebook/dp/B01KNHICCC/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982774&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Straight+Outta+Fangton\" target=\"_blank\">Straight Outta Fangton</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Lucifers-Star-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01MDM9MCT/ref=mt_kindle?_encoding=UTF8&amp;me=&amp;qid=\" target=\"_blank\">Lucifer's Star</a>, </i>and the <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Rules-Supervillainy-Saga-Book-ebook/dp/B07MB89S33/\" target=\"_blank\">Supervillainy Saga</a>.</i><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","name":"CTPhipps","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12002_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13933"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-05-03T02:49:14-07:00","id":1447148,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CTPhipps</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1443592-the-official-v5-vs-v20-thread?p=1447143#post1447143\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <a href=\"http://&quot;https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/List_of_Vampire:_The_Masquerade_books&quot;\" target=\"_blank\">https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/List_o...squerade_books</a><br /> <br /> Second Edition actually.<br /> <br /> <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> Second Edition was when things went international and away from Chicago.</div> </div> </div> </div>The Wiki has it before V2e in 1992 (though, actually, it seems to put it in before V2e and then after the V2e Screen, so it's confused there, too). Wikipedia has it in 1993. Google has it as December 1994. I will take your word for it, though, as there seems to be more evidence for it after 1992.<br /> <br /> You did ignore the rest of my post, though.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Morbus</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1443592-the-official-v5-vs-v20-thread?p=1447137#post1447137\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Things are pretty clear in VTM. Most humans are on the Path of Humanity even if they do not know it. Because it's the path of being a human. And holding human values. It doesn't really matter for Humans specifically tough because they do not have a Beast so they can even hit 0 with no consequence whatsoever.</div> </div> </div> </div>I don't think it actually is 'clear', or we wouldn't all have different interpretations. <br /> <br /> To me, the fact humans have Humanity is just a mechanical conceit to show how callous or jaded they are, and so they can interact with vampires in the VTM system.<br /> <br /> Paths in DA can be taken by humans, but I don't think that means it's the same thing vampires are doing. In the Book of Nod, an archangel literally tells Caine there is a path to redemption (Golconda), and it's heavily implied that is the Path of Humanity (or a precursor).<br /> <br /> Humans who follow Humanity or any other Path will not achieve Golconda. They won't become mortal again (even if this was dropped after 1e). Humans who follow any Path are just believing a cult they don't really get the benefit of.<br /> <br /> Vampires, meanwhile, have a tangible benefit from following a Path. At the highest levels, if sustained for a long period of time, there's supposed to be some exalted state that occurs (though, naturally, mostly never does, because vampires are incredibly flawed).<br /> <br /> Humans don't get that benefit. For them it's just a moral code. For vampires, it's something more.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Writer, publisher, performer<br /> Mostly he/his, sometimes she/her IRL <a href=\"https://adam-lowe.com\" target=\"_blank\">https://adam-lowe.com</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5291-adambeyoncelowe","name":"adambeyoncelowe","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5291_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2802"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-05-03T02:50:11-07:00","id":1447149,"title":"","content":"I edited in my response to the rest of it.<br /> <br /> It was a humorous response but underlines that a lot of what I feel people love about the game can be determined to what sort of moods and themes the game approve. Which in my case is that I tend to prefer gritty street-level games and things limited to one city.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Author of <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Cthulhu-Armageddon-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01KUOM7SI/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982844&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Cthulhu+Armageddon\" target=\"_blank\">Cthulhu Armageddon</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Teenage-Weredeer-Bright-Falls-Mysteries-ebook/dp/B075TTN2FN/ref=sr_1_2?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982717&amp;sr=1-2&amp;keywords=Weredeer#customerReviews\" target=\"_blank\">I was a Teenage Weredeer</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Straight-Outta-Fangton-Comedic-Vampire-ebook/dp/B01KNHICCC/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982774&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Straight+Outta+Fangton\" target=\"_blank\">Straight Outta Fangton</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Lucifers-Star-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01MDM9MCT/ref=mt_kindle?_encoding=UTF8&amp;me=&amp;qid=\" target=\"_blank\">Lucifer's Star</a>, </i>and the <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Rules-Supervillainy-Saga-Book-ebook/dp/B07MB89S33/\" target=\"_blank\">Supervillainy Saga</a>.</i><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","name":"CTPhipps","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12002_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13933"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-05-03T02:52:06-07:00","id":1447150,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CTPhipps</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1443592-the-official-v5-vs-v20-thread?p=1447135#post1447135\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Hasn't it been a thing since 2nd Edition [when they were first introduced in any real way] onward that the Sabbat's war on the Antediluvians was stupid?</div> </div> </div> </div>IMO after Ravnos woke up and ate his clan, it pretty much proved the Sabbat <i>are</i> correct and <i>not</i> trying to murder the ancients is stupid. Ravnos made no distinction between its Childer and killed all of them (or would have if he hadn't been stopped by Space Lasers\u2122) and it stands to reason the others won't either. Sticking ones head in the sand and pretending the Antedeluvians aren't a threat, or trying to convince yourself you'll be spared, or sitting around hoping the Technocracy blows up the Antedeluvian before it eats you are all even dumber things. <br /> <br /> So suicidally fighting a hungry elder God is stupid, but still probably less stupid than slathering yourself in BBQ sauce and then waiting for it to wake up, at any rate.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/741-anubisxy","name":"AnubisXy","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar741_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5693"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-05-03T02:56:10-07:00","id":1447151,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CTPhipps</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1443592-the-official-v5-vs-v20-thread?p=1447149#post1447149\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I edited in my response to the rest of it.</div> </div> </div> </div>Great. I see it now. <br /> <br /> I agree with you that the Sect is managed deeply cynically. In spirit, though, I think the Sabbat is objectively right, even if the day to day running of the sect results in something completely different to its stated aims. <br /> <br /> That's the reality of pretty much every RL institution too -- honourable intent, but it doesn't always work out that way. That's very in-keeping with the World of Darkness.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Morbus</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">Well I don't know about that. But as far as I played it, Humanity score for Human is only useful should they ever get embraced. A mobster for example would start much closer to wassail than a charity worker.</div> </div> </div> </div>CT is right here. I think it's in Demon Hunter X, too, that if you would fall to Humanity 0, you instead gain a Derangement and stay at Humanity 1.<br /> <br /> I use Humanity for mortals for the same reasons you do, though. Because yes, it probably helps with where they start out when Embraced. Though I still think there are no mystical consequences or benefits of following a Path while a human is a human (only once they become a vampire).","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Writer, publisher, performer<br /> Mostly he/his, sometimes she/her IRL <a href=\"https://adam-lowe.com\" target=\"_blank\">https://adam-lowe.com</a>","edited":{"userid":5291,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5291-adambeyoncelowe","user":"adambeyoncelowe","date":". 05-03-2021, 05:58 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5291-adambeyoncelowe","name":"adambeyoncelowe","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5291_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2802"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-05-03T02:58:15-07:00","id":1447152,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>AnubisXy</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1443592-the-official-v5-vs-v20-thread?p=1447150#post1447150\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> IMO after Ravnos woke up and ate his clan, it pretty much proved the Sabbat <i>are</i> correct and <i>not</i> trying to murder the ancients is stupid. Ravnos made no distinction between its Childer and killed all of them (or would have if he hadn't been stopped by Space Lasers\u2122) and it stands to reason the others won't either. Sticking ones head in the sand and pretending the Antedeluvians aren't a threat, or trying to convince yourself you'll be spared, or sitting around hoping the Technocracy blows up the Antedeluvian before it eats you are all even dumber things. <br /> <br /> So suicidally fighting a hungry elder God is stupid, but still probably less stupid than slathering yourself in BBQ sauce and then waiting for it to wake up, at any rate.</div> </div> </div> </div>Also, yes, Revised made it clear the Sabbat were objectively right, even if they're the worst sect to pull it off (although, maybe they're all equally bad).<br /> <br /> The stupidest sect, in my view, is the Tal'mahe'Ra (though I still love those guys).","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Writer, publisher, performer<br /> Mostly he/his, sometimes she/her IRL <a href=\"https://adam-lowe.com\" target=\"_blank\">https://adam-lowe.com</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5291-adambeyoncelowe","name":"adambeyoncelowe","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5291_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2802"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-05-03T03:04:37-07:00","id":1447153,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>adambeyoncelowe</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1443592-the-official-v5-vs-v20-thread?p=1447148#post1447148\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I don't think it actually is 'clear', or we wouldn't all have different interpretations.<br /> <br /> To me, the fact humans have Humanity is just a mechanical conceit to show how callous or jaded they are, and so they can interact with vampires in the VTM system.<br /> <br /> Paths in DA can be taken by humans, but I don't think that means it's the same thing vampires are doing. In the Book of Nod, an archangel literally tells Caine there is a path to redemption (Golconda), and it's heavily implied that is the Path of Humanity (or a precursor).<br /> <br /> Humans who follow Humanity or any other Path will not achieve Golconda. They won't become mortal again (even if this was dropped after 1e). Humans who follow any Path are just believing a cult they don't really get the benefit of.<br /> <br /> Vampires, meanwhile, have a tangible benefit from following a Path. At the highest levels, if sustained for a long period of time, there's supposed to be some exalted state that occurs (though, naturally, mostly never does, because vampires are incredibly flawed).<br /> <br /> Humans don't get that benefit. For them it's just a moral code. For vampires, it's something more.</div> </div> </div> </div>I pretty much agree with you. Yes Human gets no benefit for following Humanity or any other path for that matter because they have no Beast to fend off. Humans are on Humanity in VTM because it's pretty much the universal code of Humanity as a whole<br /> <br /> Don't hurt. Don't steal. Don't kill. Those are Humanity (the path) three axioms. Only Humanity 10 is an outlier here.<br /> <br /> Dark Age is indeed different as I conceded. Albeit even then Humanity is considered the default for human. And thus for vampire too.<br /> <br /> I think this is where we diverge. For me, most vampire start on Humanity because they already were subconsciously following that path when they were mortals. Those who somehow followed another moral code start immediately on that particular road. Which is why it was also more common for Vampire in Dark Age to start on another road than Humanity.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24936-morbus","name":"Morbus","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"119"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-05-03T03:05:55-07:00","id":1447155,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>AnubisXy</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1443592-the-official-v5-vs-v20-thread?p=1447150#post1447150\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> IMO after Ravnos woke up and ate his clan, it pretty much proved the Sabbat <i>are</i> correct and <i>not</i> trying to murder the ancients is stupid. Ravnos made no distinction between its Childer and killed all of them (or would have if he hadn't been stopped by Space Lasers\u2122) and it stands to reason the others won't either. Sticking ones head in the sand and pretending the Antedeluvians aren't a threat, or trying to convince yourself you'll be spared, or sitting around hoping the Technocracy blows up the Antedeluvian before it eats you are all even dumber things.<br /> <br /> So suicidally fighting a hungry elder God is stupid, but still probably less stupid than slathering yourself in BBQ sauce and then waiting for it to wake up, at any rate.</div> </div> </div> </div>Ehhhhh, yes and no.<br /> <br /> Because Ravnos was destroyed and the result was the end of the Ravnos Clan. That means destroying the Antediluvians if they're suffering wassail is the same as covering yourself in BBQ sauce.<br /> <br /> The thing is that while Ravnos had hit wightdom, we also knew that Tzimisce was intelligent, active, and apparently immortal.<br /> <br /> If you nuked New York, it wouldn't mean a thing.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>adambeyoncelowe</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1443592-the-official-v5-vs-v20-thread?p=1447152#post1447152\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Also, yes, Revised made it clear the Sabbat were objectively right, even if they're the worst sect to pull it off (although, maybe they're all equally bad).<br /> <br /> The stupidest sect, in my view, is the Tal'mahe'Ra (though I still love those guys).</div> </div> </div> </div>I mean, it was pretty likely the Tal'Mah'Ra was serving the Baali founders in those coffins rather than the Antediluvians. So, yes, they were the dumbest clan and I have the funniest idea the V20 ones had members running away when they invited Moloch's get to join.<br /> <br /> However, as of Revised, the Antediluvians showing up on screen were very much NOT like Ravnos. Baba Yaga gets eaten by a Nikutu without any problems. Tzimisce is now merged with the Earth. Lasombra is apparently a demon abyss thing. They'd evolved into demon gods beyond any vampire's ability to destroy and super-intelligent. You might nuke Ur-Shulgi but I wasn't sure who else might beat him so statting him was an odd choice.<br /> <br /> Victory is impossible unless God sends Wormword to end the world's vampires.<br /> <br /> Which....no one saw that coming. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Author of <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Cthulhu-Armageddon-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01KUOM7SI/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982844&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Cthulhu+Armageddon\" target=\"_blank\">Cthulhu Armageddon</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Teenage-Weredeer-Bright-Falls-Mysteries-ebook/dp/B075TTN2FN/ref=sr_1_2?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982717&amp;sr=1-2&amp;keywords=Weredeer#customerReviews\" target=\"_blank\">I was a Teenage Weredeer</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Straight-Outta-Fangton-Comedic-Vampire-ebook/dp/B01KNHICCC/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982774&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Straight+Outta+Fangton\" target=\"_blank\">Straight Outta Fangton</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Lucifers-Star-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01MDM9MCT/ref=mt_kindle?_encoding=UTF8&amp;me=&amp;qid=\" target=\"_blank\">Lucifer's Star</a>, </i>and the <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Rules-Supervillainy-Saga-Book-ebook/dp/B07MB89S33/\" target=\"_blank\">Supervillainy Saga</a>.</i><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":12002,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","user":"CTPhipps","date":". 05-03-2021, 06:09 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","name":"CTPhipps","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12002_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13933"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-05-03T03:13:40-07:00","id":1447159,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>AnubisXy</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1443592-the-official-v5-vs-v20-thread?p=1447150#post1447150\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> IMO after Ravnos woke up and ate his clan, it pretty much proved the Sabbat <i>are</i> correct and <i>not</i> trying to murder the ancients is stupid. Ravnos made no distinction between its Childer and killed all of them (or would have if he hadn't been stopped by Space Lasers\u2122) and it stands to reason the others won't either. Sticking ones head in the sand and pretending the Antedeluvians aren't a threat, or trying to convince yourself you'll be spared, or sitting around hoping the Technocracy blows up the Antedeluvian before it eats you are all even dumber things.<br /> <br /> So suicidally fighting a hungry elder God is stupid, but still probably less stupid than slathering yourself in BBQ sauce and then waiting for it to wake up, at any rate.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Yup this is the tragedy of the Sabbat. They are fighting the real fight. Anarchs rebelling against their elders is well and good but there's no point as long as the Ante the ultimate Elders are still standing. You still remain a pawn and a slave. And eventually food.<br /> <br /> Which is why the Sabbat is the logical conclusion of the Anarch spirit. Akin to bolshevism to communism. To win the war againt the Ante, you have to become an army or a sword.<br /> <br /> But CTPhilipps is also right in that while the cause is righteous, many Sabbat elder have stopped believing in it and are more interested in politicking and warring the Camarilla. So there's many way to see the Sect.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24936-morbus","name":"Morbus","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"119"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-05-03T03:25:32-07:00","id":1447161,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Morbus</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1443592-the-official-v5-vs-v20-thread?p=1447153#post1447153\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I pretty much agree with you. Yes Human gets no benefit for following Humanity or any other path for that matter because they have no Beast to fend off. Humans are on Humanity in VTM because it's pretty much the universal code of Humanity as a whole<br /> <br /> Don't hurt. Don't steal. Don't kill. Those are Humanity (the path) three axioms. Only Humanity 10 is an outlier here.<br /> <br /> Dark Age is indeed different as I conceded. Albeit even then Humanity is considered the default for human. And thus for vampire too.<br /> <br /> I think this is where we diverge. For me, most vampire start on Humanity because they already were subconsciously following that path when they were mortals. Those who somehow followed another moral code start immediately on that particular road. Which is why it was also more common for Vampire in Dark Age to start on another road than Humanity.</div> </div> </div> </div>I think we agree. <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CTPhipps</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1443592-the-official-v5-vs-v20-thread?p=1447155#post1447155\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Ehhhhh, yes and no.<br /> <br /> Because Ravnos was destroyed and the result was the end of the Ravnos Clan. That means destroying the Antediluvians if they're suffering wassail is the same as covering yourself in BBQ sauce.</div> </div> </div> </div>Yes, but previous Ante-murders didn't have the same outcome. It's debatable whether that happens to everyone, or if it's because you need Maharet and Makare to take the 'Core' (as in The Vampire Chronicles) to avoid that destruction, or whether Ravnos was simply so mad his destruction drove his descendants to madness too.<br /> <br /> I'm thinking the answer is probably to be Troile and eat your Ante, so that you don't annihilate your own clan. That's how most of the Antes who actually died did so, without killing their entire clans in the process (though whether they all really died is another thing, as most survived). <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> The thing is that while Ravnos had hit wightdom, we also knew that Tzimisce was intelligent, active, and apparently immortal.<br /> <br /> If you nuked New York, it wouldn't mean a thing. </div> </div> </div>I agree. But also, you have to try. Otherwise, are you complicit in letting this thing happen?<br /> <br /> Maybe you at least need to find Caine and ask him to fix this. Or Lilith, I guess.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> I mean, it was pretty likely the Tal'Mah'Ra was serving the Baali founders in those coffins rather than the Antediluvians. So, yes, they were the dumbest clan and I have the funniest idea the V20 ones had members running away when they invited Moloch's get to join. </div> </div> </div>That seems to be the V20 interpretation, but Revised pretty much stated that the Aralu were the Messengers of Hunter (in Ends of Empire and The Time of Thin Blood, I think). I also find that quite ironic.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> However, as of Revised, the Antediluvians showing up on screen were very much NOT like Ravnos. Baba Yaga gets eaten by a Nikutu without any problems. Tzimisce is now merged with the Earth. Lasombra is apparently a demon abyss thing. They'd evolved into demon gods beyond any vampire's ability to destroy and super-intelligent. You might nuke Ur-Shulgi but I wasn't sure who else might beat him so statting him was an odd choice.<br /> <br /> Victory is impossible unless God sends Wormword to end the world's vampires.<br /> <br /> Which....no one saw that coming. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /> </div> </div> </div>Resistance is futile, but if you don't resist, what's the alternative? Covering yourself in BBQ sauce while fighting to the death seems to me the more noble option than covering yourself in BBQ sauce and reclining on the ground until it happens.<br /> <br /> As for the Baali, I liked their treatment in TBH:GttTMR. I do like their joining the TMR. I think it's an interesting idea to have their founders in Enoch, too. That's probably how I'd run it if we didn't have the Imbued in our games (which we haven't yet). That has the potential for all sorts of shenanigans.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Writer, publisher, performer<br /> Mostly he/his, sometimes she/her IRL <a href=\"https://adam-lowe.com\" target=\"_blank\">https://adam-lowe.com</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5291-adambeyoncelowe","name":"adambeyoncelowe","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5291_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2802"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-05-03T03:36:32-07:00","id":1447165,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CTPhipps</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1443592-the-official-v5-vs-v20-thread?p=1447089#post1447089\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">To explain my logic, Old Humanity was not very good for reflecting, say a Roman centurion or other morality which is human but not necessarily reflective of the Humanity Road.</div> </div> </div> </div>That is why I am big fan of the optional rule that beside Road of Humanity, Road of Enlightenment, those religious roades and Road of the Kings with his subroades should eligable for Golconda too.<br /> Because this shows that there can be more than one good moral system. That is one of the biggest flaws in my opinion from Modern Nights VTM and that DAV20 did not took over the optional rule.<br /> The problem is in my opinion that modern paths of Enlightenment are automatically evil.<br /> Where DA Knight Path is, that you are a protector of the weak is modern Knight path, that your are a professional massmurderer with honor.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>As I am from Austria I need to clarify two things.<br /> First my native language is german and so please point out if the english I write is broken so I can improve.<br /> Second I do not own VTMV beyond first three books nor any line after M20 Corebook because it is not out there and I wait for the translation.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26160-koronus","name":"Koronus","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2020"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"366"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-05-03T03:40:42-07:00","id":1447166,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Koronus</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1443592-the-official-v5-vs-v20-thread?p=1447165#post1447165\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> That is why I am big fan of the optional rule that beside Road of Humanity, Road of Enlightenment, those religious roades and Road of the Kings with his subroades should eligable for Golconda too.<br /> Because this shows that there can be more than one good moral system. That is one of the biggest flaws in my opinion from Modern Nights VTM and that DAV20 did not took over the optional rule.<br /> The problem is in my opinion that modern paths of Enlightenment are automatically evil.<br /> Where DA Knight Path is, that you are a protector of the weak is modern Knight path, that your are a professional massmurderer with honor.</div> </div> </div> </div>Which is why I do think V5 has the right idea that you can switch moralities too to an extent.<br /> <br /> Nicholas Knight, Patron Saint of Canadian Vampire Detectives, was a Crusader who murdered hundreds of Muslims for his faith and as a result lost it because it was so devastatingly evil. Then he proceeded to become a vampire and was disgusted with it as well.<br /> <br /> So switching Convictions should be much easier than Paths or Roads.<br /> <br /> However, I think that the rules don't presently give rules for Switching Convictions or getting New Touchstones save implying, &quot;Oh, in roleplay.&quot; I think we need to rectify that. A Players Guide would have helped.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Author of <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Cthulhu-Armageddon-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01KUOM7SI/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982844&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Cthulhu+Armageddon\" target=\"_blank\">Cthulhu Armageddon</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Teenage-Weredeer-Bright-Falls-Mysteries-ebook/dp/B075TTN2FN/ref=sr_1_2?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982717&amp;sr=1-2&amp;keywords=Weredeer#customerReviews\" target=\"_blank\">I was a Teenage Weredeer</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Straight-Outta-Fangton-Comedic-Vampire-ebook/dp/B01KNHICCC/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982774&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Straight+Outta+Fangton\" target=\"_blank\">Straight Outta Fangton</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Lucifers-Star-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01MDM9MCT/ref=mt_kindle?_encoding=UTF8&amp;me=&amp;qid=\" target=\"_blank\">Lucifer's Star</a>, </i>and the <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Rules-Supervillainy-Saga-Book-ebook/dp/B07MB89S33/\" target=\"_blank\">Supervillainy Saga</a>.</i><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","name":"CTPhipps","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12002_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13933"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-05-03T06:06:24-07:00","id":1447181,"title":"","content":"I'm still hoping for a Players Guide in the future! I remember during VRev, we were told we shouldn't expect a PG as we had the Guides to the Camarilla and Sabbat instead, and then we got one anyway. (We were also told we'd never get Gehenna, but we got that too.)<br /> <br /> Given that Justin was at the helm for both of those, I wouldn't be surprised if we got a V5 PG too, further down the line.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Writer, publisher, performer<br /> Mostly he/his, sometimes she/her IRL <a href=\"https://adam-lowe.com\" target=\"_blank\">https://adam-lowe.com</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5291-adambeyoncelowe","name":"adambeyoncelowe","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5291_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2802"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-05-03T08:34:05-07:00","id":1447203,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CTPhipps</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1443592-the-official-v5-vs-v20-thread?p=1447089#post1447089\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">To explain my logic, Old Humanity was not very good for reflecting, say a Roman centurion or other morality which is human but not necessarily reflective of the Humanity Road.</div> </div> </div> </div>The Centurion (and a lot of military types throughout history) would probably be either on the equivalent of Honorable Accord (which retains both the \u201chuman\u201d virtues of Conscience and Self-Control) or just on the low side of Humanity (many soldiers talk about how they can feel desensitized to killing and disconnected from loved ones who haven\u2019t been through what they\u2019ve been through... i.e. they are disconnected from their humanity and a lot of the counseling and support groups are methods of reconnecting).<br /> <br /> Basically, I think Humanity actually functions pretty well in modeling the effects of violence and dissociation on people. War should be dehumanizing because it is. Even killing in self-defense is traumatic (which is not the same in a game sense as \u201cautomatically loses Humanity\u201d but is probably going to be a Conscience test depending on your present level... also the number of people who have to kill in self-defense is small and those who have to do so more than once in their entire lives is vanishingly so even if in a game sense a normal person fails Humanity 6 is still a pretty functional individual).<br /> <br /> I know that because it\u2019s a stat in a game that the temptation is that you should always try to max said stat, thus a system like V5\u2019s tenants that make it easier for you to do so is \u201cbetter\u201d, but in just about every situation (daylight dice pools and cost of blush of health being the only common ones) in V20 there\u2019s no functional difference between Humanity 5 and Humanity 10. Only at 4 or less could it possibly affect your Virtue dice pools (making it harder for you to resist frenzies and certain disciplines) and by then, a lot of types of violence/killing don\u2019t even trigger degeneration checks any more).<br /> <br /> Basically, I think a big part of the \u201cproblem\u201d with Humanity is that it\u2019s seen as basically a \u201chealth bar\u201d in the same way your wound track is, so if it\u2019s not at full it\u2019s an issue, when it\u2019s actually something that\u2019s closer to a \u201cupkeep\u201d tracker and as long the number is positive (i.e. your troops are eating less food than your kingdom produces) then you\u2019re good.<br /> <br /> Though in this case \u201cpositive\u201d will vary with concept; a vampire who regularly mingles with mortals and needs Blush of Health may consider \u201cpositive\u201d to be 8+ so it costs no blood to use; a vampire who just doesn\u2019t want to have their virtue tests restricted might consider 4-5+ \u201cpositive\u201d and one who just wants to keep playing their character considers 1+ \u201cpositive.\u201d<br /> <br /> And in that sense, I do think V5 is much harsher than V20 because it added so many additional penalties to the low end and bonuses to the high end of the Humanity scale. In V20 you could just be Humanity 5 and other than needing 3 BP for Blush of Health you\u2019re basically at the same level as the saintly Humanity 10 vampire. In V5 though the Humanity 10 vampire can actually eat certain foods and have sex normally while at 5 you vomit up food, can only fake sex and take penalties to interacting with humans.<br /> <br /> Basically, V5 turned Humanity from an upkeep tracker to a health bar where if you\u2019re not at full then you\u2019re taking penalties... which is also why it needs Tenants so it\u2019s actually possible to fill that health bar even when the campaign themes don\u2019t align with the Hierarchy of Sins in previous editions.<br /> <br /> i.e. in V20 you can run an Archons hunting down Red List targets and the PCs sliding down to Humanity 4-5 is no big deal (you\u2019re probably not using Blush of Health much anyway). In V5 you need to lay down specific Tenants where doing whatever it takes to take out Red Listers doesn\u2019t violate Humanity or they\u2019ll be steadily degenerating as the stains rack up from all the likely collateral damage.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1328-chris24601","name":"Chris24601","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"520"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-05-03T09:14:09-07:00","id":1447211,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> I mean, it was pretty likely the Tal'Mah'Ra was serving the Baali founders in those coffins rather than the Antediluvians. </div> </div> </div>I actually find it far more likely the Aarlu were Angels (likely Slayers), as in Revised there are stories of a witness to the nuking of Enoch and they saw two bright lights appear and reach towards the sky...then you know..the Heralds showed up and made the Imbued almost right after that. The timing pretty much lines up.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3215-supersabbatst","name":"SuperSabbatST","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3215_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"196"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-05-03T09:16:48-07:00","id":1447212,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>SuperSabbatST</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1443592-the-official-v5-vs-v20-thread?p=1447211#post1447211\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I actually find it far more likely the Aarlu were Angels (likely Slayers), as in Revised there are stories of a witness to the nuking of Enoch and they saw two bright lights appear and reach towards the sky...then you know..the Heralds showed up and made the Imbued almost right after that. The timing pretty much lines up.</div> </div> </div> </div>I thought it was three and being, &quot;The nukes just woke up the creatures inside the coffins. Nice job, you Hierarchy <i>assholes</i>.&quot;<br /> <br /> But I suppose I find angels in coffins a bit weird.<br /> <br /> Then again, maybe the Messengers were always Antediluvians or Baali. No one ever said the Hunters had to be GOOD guys.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Author of <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Cthulhu-Armageddon-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01KUOM7SI/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982844&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Cthulhu+Armageddon\" target=\"_blank\">Cthulhu Armageddon</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Teenage-Weredeer-Bright-Falls-Mysteries-ebook/dp/B075TTN2FN/ref=sr_1_2?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982717&amp;sr=1-2&amp;keywords=Weredeer#customerReviews\" target=\"_blank\">I was a Teenage Weredeer</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Straight-Outta-Fangton-Comedic-Vampire-ebook/dp/B01KNHICCC/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982774&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Straight+Outta+Fangton\" target=\"_blank\">Straight Outta Fangton</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Lucifers-Star-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01MDM9MCT/ref=mt_kindle?_encoding=UTF8&amp;me=&amp;qid=\" target=\"_blank\">Lucifer's Star</a>, </i>and the <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Rules-Supervillainy-Saga-Book-ebook/dp/B07MB89S33/\" target=\"_blank\">Supervillainy Saga</a>.</i><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","name":"CTPhipps","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12002_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13933"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-05-03T09:18:32-07:00","id":1447213,"title":"","content":"Nope, 4 Coffins of the Aralu. 2 Bright lights seen over enoch when the nuke went off. Granted, its not spelled out. But if you connect the dots like a Charlie day meme...","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3215-supersabbatst","name":"SuperSabbatST","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3215_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"196"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-05-03T09:42:05-07:00","id":1447217,"title":"","content":"Nope you are right, it was 3. Its under Ambrogino's write up in children of the night. <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <span style=\"color:#3A3A3A\"><span style=\"font-family:Verdana\"><span style=\"font-size:16px\"> witnessed the eruption of the Sixth Great Maelstrom. At that time, he saw glowing angelic figures rise and survey their surroundings, as if taking stock of creation, and then simply vanish.</span></span></span> </div> </div> </div>Still pretty sure thats the Hearlds...just dunno where the 3rd ran off too then hehe","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3215-supersabbatst","name":"SuperSabbatST","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3215_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"196"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-05-03T12:46:02-07:00","id":1447247,"title":"","content":"<br /> Any reasonable discussion would conclude V20 does disciplines better (I mean you're all entitled to your opinions and all BUT THEY'RE WRONG UNLESS THEY'RE MINE FOOLS!!) <br /> <br /> <b>1-Disciplines are more natural because they are broader.</b> What does V20 potence do? Adds strength die. Can I use this strength for damage? Yes. Can I use this strength to jump high? Yes. Can I use this strength to get past my enemy's defences? Yes! Can I use this strength to lift things? Yes! Can I use this strength to break through barricades? Yes! Climb well? Absolutely. V5 on the otherhand, we start with two choices; Jump Good, or more dangerous brawl damage... Very specific no? Reminds me of a perk tree for an arcadey RPG. We have some pretty extreme examples too. Celerity 3 for examble; rush your enemy, and only an enemy, to make an attack or rush in any direction but don't make an attack... I suppose the designers liked Mass effect. There are possibilities V5 presents that V20 doesn't, but V20 gives you more power per level, and a fair few V5 powers really stretch the definition of the Discipline.<br /> <br /> (minor note; the pick'n mix approach of V5 also means I might pick progressions that will seem unnatural, for example I'll want to avoid picking up Dominate 1's &quot;Forget&quot; if I want to take Dominate 3's Forgetful mind to avoid redundancy, even though in a more natural system learning Forget should be a predecessor to Forgetful mind)<br /> <br /> 2- <b>Discipline selection is just more streamlined.</b><br /> In V20, I look at the list of clans, there's a brief summary of what their three disciplines do, and I can make a decision from that alone. There is no 'wrong' path here. If I get Dominate, I'll get every dominate power between 1 and 5 eventually, given enough XP.<br /> In V5, I look at the list of clans, I look at the disciplines, which are varied. I then work through all the disciplines working out what the right path for disciplines are for my character, knowing that my selections will bar me from the other powers. And that's before we get into amalgams.<br /> <br /> <b>3- Brujah are Brujah and Wizards are Wizards. </b><br /> In V5, Potence is as complicated as Presence and only slightly less complicated than Thaumaturgy (Sorry, &quot;Blood Sorcery&quot;)<br /> In V20, Physical disciplines are simple-as, and Thaumaturgy works best if you're prepared to research like an actual-wizard. The Advantages are manifold. First, somepeople just wanna play a Brujah, A mechanically light character; Potence and Celerity are one power with five levels, easy to memorize, meaning you only gotta worry about Presence. It's very satisfying. Let's say I get 5/5/5 in Brujah disciplines. In V20, I gotta keep 7 distinct powers in mind. In V5, I gotta keep 15 distinct powers in mind. Keep It Simple, Sir. conversely, If I'm playing a Tremere, well, I fully intend to geek out about having UNLIMITED POWER!!!! and a lengthly spell list. That's what playing a wizard is for. Imagine if DnD 6e said Fighters, Rogues and monks were too simple, but Bards, Wizards and Clerics were bullshit, so everyone has to play half-casters? Nobody wins there. Rangers are lame and Paladins are just shit clerics misusing a high charisma value.<br /> <br /> <b>4 Elder disciplines. </b><br /> This one's somewhat more subjective, but look; individual powers above level 7 are rarely written well, but the concept of there being levels beyond 5 is fascinating. If I were a conniving vampire (Which I am not) I'd devour someone for the opportunity to develop transcendental power. That's what drives the Jyhad. If everyone caps out at 5, and blood potency is mostly just going to make you both really hungry and really picky, there's no reason to eat eachother (killing eachother's fair game but there's much less incentive for that) From a religious Sabbat/Assamite/Settite/Ravnos perspective, eating up's a reason to exist, it's a religious duty. From the Cam/Inconnu/generic elder perspective, it's a reason to get paranoid and supress the neonates hard, because you've got something they want and they'll only get it over your corpse. There's just a wonderful, sociological impact at play, and it's gone in V5.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":8}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25794-mywifeisscary","name":"MyWifeIsScary","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25794_2.png","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3711"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-05-03T13:33:50-07:00","id":1447256,"title":"","content":"I feel that maybe \u201cnot arbitrarily merging tangentially-related and/or heretofore-completely-unrelated Disciplines\u201d deserves a mention on that list.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24351-garygeneric","name":"Garygeneric","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24351_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"108"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-05-03T14:29:07-07:00","id":1447271,"title":"","content":"Think this is one of the many areas where V5's intentions might have been good, but the execution is sorely lacking<br /> <br /> As the CofD and some 20th books have demonstrated, there's a lot of interesting things you can do when you get off strict the 1-5 dots of powers VtM started with Disciplines. Lots of people have been complaining about Discipline bloat in VtM for decades. So V5 trying to adjust this wasn't wrong... just well.... the execution clearly has flaws and a lot of us feel those flaws don't outweigh the benefits.<br /> <br /> For example, Wr20's dual Arcanoi tracks is a very interesting take on things. While still 1-5 rated powers, there's the common versions that pretty much any wraith can learn, and the Guild versions that requires (at least for modern wraiths) tutelage from someone that knows them; and you can learn both rather than having to pick. One of the major benefits of this is Wraith specific (1e/2e WtO had a weird thing where most of the Guilds were illegal entities but the Arcanoi were also linked to the Guilds, so how could you learn your Arcanoi without becoming a criminal?), but it could also be a model for how to address some of the concerns with V5's setup without completely tossing the benefits.<br /> <br /> While it wouldn't resolve more specific debates about the utility of certain powers, I'd have been much more pleased if we had something like this:<br /> <br /> A set of common Disciplines (basically the classic VtM ones, maybe elevate some of the others to this status). Variant Disciplines that recreate most rarer Disciplines as an additional set of powers ala Wr20 but not inherently limited to just two. So, for example Serpentis and Vicissitude could both be Variants of Protean.<br /> <br /> Amalgams go back to being a separate thing like Combo Disciplines that don't count towards your max number of powers. Some of the really specialized Disciplines can really be reduced to a few of these rather than the bloated 1-5 dot versions in pre-V5, or some of the pretty bland single power Amalgams in V5.<br /> <br /> Clans can extend favored XP bonuses to either a single Variant, or to buying Amalgams. This means our Gangrel that just favors Protean has greater flexibility in learning unique off-shoot powers, while our Tzimisce get the most out of studying the Vicissitude variant instead. This can help mitigate some of urges to pick rare Clan/Bloodlines because they get cool nifty unique powers, since you're explicitly trading one set of nifty powers for another. The choice is more of flexibility vs. specialization instead.<br /> <br /> Not perfect mind you, but I just wrote it up right now. Just an idea of ways to play with the setup that could balance different desires for the game more successfully.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-05-03T15:36:18-07:00","id":1447279,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Garygeneric</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1443592-the-official-v5-vs-v20-thread?p=1447256#post1447256\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I feel that maybe \u201cnot arbitrarily merging tangentially-related and/or heretofore-completely-unrelated Disciplines\u201d deserves a mention on that list.</div> </div> </div> </div>I honestly have always felt that Disciplines should be more flexible like Mage magic. Sadly, V5 only does it halfway. If I were to revised V5 it would be to DOUBLE DOWN on this and add this change:<br /> <br /> 1. You can buy as many powers for a level of Discipline or Combo Discipline as you want.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Author of <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Cthulhu-Armageddon-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01KUOM7SI/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982844&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Cthulhu+Armageddon\" target=\"_blank\">Cthulhu Armageddon</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Teenage-Weredeer-Bright-Falls-Mysteries-ebook/dp/B075TTN2FN/ref=sr_1_2?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982717&amp;sr=1-2&amp;keywords=Weredeer#customerReviews\" target=\"_blank\">I was a Teenage Weredeer</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Straight-Outta-Fangton-Comedic-Vampire-ebook/dp/B01KNHICCC/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982774&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Straight+Outta+Fangton\" target=\"_blank\">Straight Outta Fangton</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Lucifers-Star-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01MDM9MCT/ref=mt_kindle?_encoding=UTF8&amp;me=&amp;qid=\" target=\"_blank\">Lucifer's Star</a>, </i>and the <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Rules-Supervillainy-Saga-Book-ebook/dp/B07MB89S33/\" target=\"_blank\">Supervillainy Saga</a>.</i><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","name":"CTPhipps","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12002_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13933"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-05-03T16:07:42-07:00","id":1447290,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CTPhipps</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1443592-the-official-v5-vs-v20-thread?p=1447279#post1447279\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I honestly have always felt that Disciplines should be more flexible like Mage magic. Sadly, V5 only does it halfway. If I were to revised V5 it would be to DOUBLE DOWN on this and add this change:<br /> <br /> 1. You can buy as many powers for a level of Discipline or Combo Discipline as you want.</div> </div> </div> </div>With that approach, you could just go whole-hog and combine Animalism, Auspex, Chimerstry, Dominete, Obfuscate and Presence into one Mental Powers category; Celerity, Fortitude, Potence, Protean, Serpentis and Vicissitude into one Physical Powers column, etc.<br /> <br /> Sometimes less is more, but sometimes more is more, too. Even the name &quot;Discipline&quot; implies an individual field of study. Just my opinion, but I feel homogenization can be takes too far, especially with RPGs (TT and MMO alike)","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24351-garygeneric","name":"Garygeneric","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24351_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"108"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-05-03T17:40:54-07:00","id":1447309,"title":"","content":"Execution is still a huge aspect of this.<br /> <br /> <br /> Something I've lamented before, is that V5 didn't take more from Beast the Primordial mechanically when it was looking at the CofD for inspirations. Beast does, in fact, combine everything into Atavisms (basically physical powers, though plenty of esoteric things like being able to jump into one shadow and appear in another are in here), and Nightmares (more mental powers where you manipulate emotions, memories, and perceptions.... though you can still kill people with them).<br /> <br /> It works because neither are 1-5 powers. Both types of powers are just a big list of powers you can buy individually. How powerful they are is a mix of how powerful your character is, and how hungry your character is.<br /> <br /> I am extremely confident that you can take Beast the Primordial, take out all the dream-horror stuff, and instead of DIY monsters turn everything into vampires, and I could make a vampire game that might not be VtM or VtR, but would be still be a solid vampire game that would appeal to Vampire fans. Mostly because it's a matter of trimming things out rather than needing to add much.<br /> <br /> For a new edition of a game though, there's a case to be conservative with changes. You need to be sure that if you're going to make a pretty big change, the pay off of a better play experience for a wide range of fans. So for V5.5 or V6 or whatever, I wouldn't do my pared down Beast idea no matter how good of a vampire game I think it'd be. But that doesn't mean there shouldn't be some experimentation to see if there are better models than the original 1-5 Disciplines.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-05-03T22:46:48-07:00","id":1447351,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CTPhipps</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1443592-the-official-v5-vs-v20-thread?p=1447279#post1447279\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I honestly have always felt that Disciplines should be more flexible like Mage magic. Sadly, V5 only does it halfway. If I were to revised V5 it would be to DOUBLE DOWN on this and add this change:<br /> <br /> 1. You can buy as many powers for a level of Discipline or Combo Discipline as you want.</div> </div> </div> </div>I've done this in my group and found it to work out fantastic. I don't know why V5 banned taking multiple powers, but having multiple ones per level was one of the new edition's best ideas.<br /> <br /> I did find things to get slightly out of control at first. Everyone wanted to buy as many powers as they could, and usually higher-level ones.<br /> <br /> So I tweaked buying multiple powers at the same level to have a cumulative XP cost. I found that made things much more balanced, as it incentivizes filling out your powers at each level. I've also, as I mentioned earlier in this thread, waived or reduced Rouse costs for powers with a lower level than a character's Blood Potency. So players have been very happy to continue buying and using weaker powers.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://blood-and-bourbon.obsidianportal.com/\" target=\"_blank\">Blood and Bourbon</a>, my New Orleans-based Vampire chronicle.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3110-false-epiphany","name":"False Epiphany","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3110_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"748"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-05-03T23:02:24-07:00","id":1447353,"title":"","content":"I think, as always, VTR does it well. There you have a core set of Discipline powers but a number of Devotions that, in some cases, are just straight up alternate powers (i.e., they're not Amalgams because they only have one Discipline prerequisite).<br /> <br /> It keeps things elegant and simple. Compare that to, say, Exalted's Charm trees, which are a mess, and I know which option I prefer. So V5 should've been more VTR and less Exalted in that respect.<br /> <br /> I actually think Disciplines should be more static than Mage. Vampires are beings of stasis. It was right to make Changeling Arts more fluid, but Disciplines should be less flexible, in general.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Writer, publisher, performer<br /> Mostly he/his, sometimes she/her IRL <a href=\"https://adam-lowe.com\" target=\"_blank\">https://adam-lowe.com</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5291-adambeyoncelowe","name":"adambeyoncelowe","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5291_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2802"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-05-03T23:35:04-07:00","id":1447357,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>adambeyoncelowe</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1443592-the-official-v5-vs-v20-thread?p=1447353#post1447353\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I actually think Disciplines should be more static than Mage. Vampires are beings of stasis. It was right to make Changeling Arts more fluid, but Disciplines should be less flexible, in general.</div> </div> </div> </div>That I don't agree with. It should be about giving vampires the powers you see in fiction, with complete indifference to whether that fits with being &quot;static&quot; or not. Vampire powers in fiction tend to revolve around animalistic savagery, seduction and mindrape, and dark natural disasters like hurricanes and plagues. Whether that results in a power being &quot;static&quot; or &quot;flexible&quot; is accidental and irrelevant. Vampires rip you apart with animalistc power, take over your mind, and plague you with hurricanes, swarms of rats, rotting zombies, etc.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3598-cajunkhan","name":"CajunKhan","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3598_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1700"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-05-03T23:42:36-07:00","id":1447358,"title":"","content":"Besides, there's hundreds of kinds of vampires in fiction and the point of V:TM is to be able to play time all. You should be able to make Dracula, Hellsing's Alucard, Barlow, and Edward if you want.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Author of <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Cthulhu-Armageddon-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01KUOM7SI/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982844&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Cthulhu+Armageddon\" target=\"_blank\">Cthulhu Armageddon</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Teenage-Weredeer-Bright-Falls-Mysteries-ebook/dp/B075TTN2FN/ref=sr_1_2?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982717&amp;sr=1-2&amp;keywords=Weredeer#customerReviews\" target=\"_blank\">I was a Teenage Weredeer</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Straight-Outta-Fangton-Comedic-Vampire-ebook/dp/B01KNHICCC/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982774&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Straight+Outta+Fangton\" target=\"_blank\">Straight Outta Fangton</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Lucifers-Star-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01MDM9MCT/ref=mt_kindle?_encoding=UTF8&amp;me=&amp;qid=\" target=\"_blank\">Lucifer's Star</a>, </i>and the <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Rules-Supervillainy-Saga-Book-ebook/dp/B07MB89S33/\" target=\"_blank\">Supervillainy Saga</a>.</i><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","name":"CTPhipps","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12002_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13933"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-05-03T23:46:54-07:00","id":1447361,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CTPhipps</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1443592-the-official-v5-vs-v20-thread?p=1447279#post1447279\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I honestly have always felt that Disciplines should be more flexible like Mage magic. Sadly, V5 only does it halfway. If I were to revised V5 it would be to DOUBLE DOWN on this and add this change:<br /> <br /> 1. You can buy as many powers for a level of Discipline or Combo Discipline as you want.</div> </div> </div> </div>But V5 disciplines are LESS flexible. Note the example I've given before; Each dot of potence giving +1 strength grants the player a lot of diverse and intuitive benefits: Jumping, Climbing, Swiming, lifting, throwing, flexing, both getting to the target and doing damage.... V5 gives you a choice of either Hare's Leap or -your bare hands are like weapons, though honestly you'd be better off with a weapon-. Dominate used to be 'Do as I say and think how I tell you to think&quot; and now it's just &quot;I will give you orders and you will sleepwalk to fulfill them immediately, though you can't do anything that requires Cognition which should mean you absolutely can't do anything but it instead means you can't be forced to talk or share bank details because if you could do that the players would have too much of an advantage and it's a pain for an uncreative storyteller to deal with that sometimes....&quot;. Auspex 1 used to give you hiegtened senses, premonitions and seeing the unseen, and now they're three seperate powers. You could pull of some absolutely crazy shenanigans with obfuscate 3 in V20, now you need Obfuscate 5 to get close to that level. <br /> If anything, V20 was far more like mage in how freeform disciplines were. V5 just makes all the powers extremely narrow in focus.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25794-mywifeisscary","name":"MyWifeIsScary","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25794_2.png","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3711"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-05-03T23:49:23-07:00","id":1447363,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MyWifeIsScary</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1443592-the-official-v5-vs-v20-thread?p=1447361#post1447361\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">But V5 disciplines are LESS flexible. Note the example I've given before; Each dot of potence giving +1 strength grants the player a lot of diverse and intuitive benefits: Jumping, Climbing, Swiming, lifting, throwing, flexing, both getting to the target and doing damage....</div> </div> </div> </div>I think that specific powers are more flexible than just an extra dot. Same with Celerity and Fortitude. I've always felt those were the weakest DIsciplines because of their lack of imagination.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Author of <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Cthulhu-Armageddon-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01KUOM7SI/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982844&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Cthulhu+Armageddon\" target=\"_blank\">Cthulhu Armageddon</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Teenage-Weredeer-Bright-Falls-Mysteries-ebook/dp/B075TTN2FN/ref=sr_1_2?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982717&amp;sr=1-2&amp;keywords=Weredeer#customerReviews\" target=\"_blank\">I was a Teenage Weredeer</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Straight-Outta-Fangton-Comedic-Vampire-ebook/dp/B01KNHICCC/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982774&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Straight+Outta+Fangton\" target=\"_blank\">Straight Outta Fangton</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Lucifers-Star-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01MDM9MCT/ref=mt_kindle?_encoding=UTF8&amp;me=&amp;qid=\" target=\"_blank\">Lucifer's Star</a>, </i>and the <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Rules-Supervillainy-Saga-Book-ebook/dp/B07MB89S33/\" target=\"_blank\">Supervillainy Saga</a>.</i><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","name":"CTPhipps","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12002_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13933"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-05-03T23:53:45-07:00","id":1447364,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CajunKhan</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1443592-the-official-v5-vs-v20-thread?p=1447357#post1447357\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> That I don't agree with. It should be about giving vampires the powers you see in fiction, with complete indifference to whether that fits with being &amp;quot;static&amp;quot; or not. Vampire powers in fiction tend to revolve around animalistic savagery, seduction and mindrape, and dark natural disasters like hurricanes and plagues. Whether that results in a power being &amp;quot;static&amp;quot; or &amp;quot;flexible&amp;quot; is accidental and irrelevant. Vampires rip you apart with animalistc power, take over your mind, and plague you with hurricanes, swarms of rats, rotting zombies, etc.</div> </div> </div> </div>I take your point, but I think that's already possible with the V20 Discipline spread, so we're not actually disagreeing there. <br /> <br /> I'm not saying vampires shouldn't have flexibility at all; I just think that well defined Discipline paths with some Devotions is a better, more fitting approach than the Mage style. I compared Disciplines to Mage Spheres intentionally, because those are freeform and others suggested Disciplines should be more like Spheres.<br /> <br /> The whole thing about Clan Tremere is they lost a lot of flexibility when they became vampires. It's there in the lore already.<br /> <br /> That doesn't mean no flexibility; it just means it's more static than Spheres.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Writer, publisher, performer<br /> Mostly he/his, sometimes she/her IRL <a href=\"https://adam-lowe.com\" target=\"_blank\">https://adam-lowe.com</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5291-adambeyoncelowe","name":"adambeyoncelowe","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5291_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2802"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-05-03T23:58:36-07:00","id":1447365,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CTPhipps</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1443592-the-official-v5-vs-v20-thread?p=1447363#post1447363\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I think that specific powers are more flexible than just an extra dot. Same with Celerity and Fortitude. I've always felt those were the weakest DIsciplines because of their lack of imagination.</div> </div> </div> </div>But they literally aren't. I can do so much more with +1 strength than higher jump or more brawl damage. The same is true for Celerity. Now, Social Fortitude is an avenue that fortitude doesn't have and V5 fortitude truly does more, but it's the exception, not the rule.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25794-mywifeisscary","name":"MyWifeIsScary","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25794_2.png","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3711"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-05-04T01:08:42-07:00","id":1447368,"title":"","content":"Personally, I don\u2019t see Disciplines as \u2018powers\u2019 in a Mage sense. I see them as literally disciplines of a vampire\u2019s own instinct to hunt and cultivate their blood supply and prey. As such, they are not meant to be broad, encompassing and creative, like Mage Spheres, but narrower more acute abilities with specific implementation.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2517-trippy","name":"Trippy","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2517_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1018"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-05-04T01:28:48-07:00","id":1447371,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MyWifeIsScary</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1443592-the-official-v5-vs-v20-thread?p=1447365#post1447365\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">But they literally aren't. I can do so much more with +1 strength than higher jump or more brawl damage. The same is true for Celerity. Now, Social Fortitude is an avenue that fortitude doesn't have and V5 fortitude truly does more, but it's the exception, not the rule.</div> </div> </div> </div>Celerity was overpowered. It needed a nerf. Potence I'd say is underpowered. I'd make Prowess a level 1 power requiring no rouse-check. Vampires, in my opinion, should be hella strong, strength of 20 men and all that, and there's just something wrong them needing to jump through hoops xp and bloodwise to become strong.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3598-cajunkhan","name":"CajunKhan","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3598_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1700"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-05-04T01:31:14-07:00","id":1447372,"title":"","content":"i always saw the new discipline system as the devs trying to limit what an individual kindred can do with their disciplines but keep what kindred in general can do with disciplines in an attempt to nerf kindred but not fuck up the lore of what kindred can do with disciplines.<br /> <br /> like most ideas in V5 though fine enough idea, bad execution","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25992-archderd","name":"archderd","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25992_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2020"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"205"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-05-04T02:48:45-07:00","id":1447375,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CajunKhan</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1443592-the-official-v5-vs-v20-thread?p=1447371#post1447371\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Celerity was overpowered. It needed a nerf. Potence I'd say is underpowered. I'd make Prowess a level 1 power requiring no rouse-check. Vampires, in my opinion, should be hella strong, strength of 20 men and all that, and there's just something wrong them needing to jump through hoops xp and bloodwise to become strong.</div> </div> </div> </div>Potence was a very good discipline so long as you make use of it beyond doing more melee damage. Getting Automatic successes when you spend a blood is exceptionally good when you need to get out of dodge and scrambling up the exterior of a building becomes your best option of escape. In V5? I just can't get my head around being able to jump twice my height but being unable to deliver a better kick, or the ability to smash my fist into a mortal and deal more damage but being unable to use that advantage in strength to hit him in the first place. It's a lot of cognitive dissonance. Every Potence power in V5 is specific to an absurd degree. It makes sense for werewolf gifts, but not for vampire powers. <br /> <br /> Celerity Needed a Nerf, sure, but there's plenty of ways to do that while keeping it a nice incremental discipline. Like spending a blood to double the amount of passive Dex dice granted (automatic levels are too strong for Dexterity) or spending blood for half-again the amount of passive dex dice (but letting you spend more blood for diminishing returns) <br /> <br /> Even though V5 fortitude is &quot;stronger&quot; I still prefer OG Fortitude for it's simplicity and universal appeal (plus some houserules, like fortitude making it harder to be pushed around, or fortitude reducing firearm penalties because it literally absorbs your recoil)","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25794-mywifeisscary","name":"MyWifeIsScary","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25794_2.png","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3711"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-05-04T02:50:45-07:00","id":1447376,"title":"","content":"I admit, I love Celerity 1 is needed to dodge bullets. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Author of <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Cthulhu-Armageddon-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01KUOM7SI/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982844&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Cthulhu+Armageddon\" target=\"_blank\">Cthulhu Armageddon</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Teenage-Weredeer-Bright-Falls-Mysteries-ebook/dp/B075TTN2FN/ref=sr_1_2?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982717&amp;sr=1-2&amp;keywords=Weredeer#customerReviews\" target=\"_blank\">I was a Teenage Weredeer</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Straight-Outta-Fangton-Comedic-Vampire-ebook/dp/B01KNHICCC/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982774&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Straight+Outta+Fangton\" target=\"_blank\">Straight Outta Fangton</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Lucifers-Star-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01MDM9MCT/ref=mt_kindle?_encoding=UTF8&amp;me=&amp;qid=\" target=\"_blank\">Lucifer's Star</a>, </i>and the <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Rules-Supervillainy-Saga-Book-ebook/dp/B07MB89S33/\" target=\"_blank\">Supervillainy Saga</a>.</i><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","name":"CTPhipps","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12002_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13933"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-05-04T03:15:39-07:00","id":1447380,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MyWifeIsScary</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1443592-the-official-v5-vs-v20-thread?p=1447375#post1447375\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Potence was a very good discipline so long as you make use of it beyond doing more melee damage. Getting Automatic successes when you spend a blood is exceptionally good when you need to get out of dodge and scrambling up the exterior of a building becomes your best option of escape. In V5? I just can't get my head around being able to jump twice my height but being unable to deliver a better kick, or the ability to smash my fist into a mortal and deal more damage but being unable to use that advantage in strength to hit him in the first place. It's a lot of cognitive dissonance. Every Potence power in V5 is specific to an absurd degree. It makes sense for werewolf gifts, but not for vampire powers.<br /> <br /> Celerity Needed a Nerf, sure, but there's plenty of ways to do that while keeping it a nice incremental discipline. Like spending a blood to double the amount of passive Dex dice granted (automatic levels are too strong for Dexterity) or spending blood for half-again the amount of passive dex dice (but letting you spend more blood for diminishing returns)<br /> <br /> Even though V5 fortitude is &quot;stronger&quot; I still prefer OG Fortitude for it's simplicity and universal appeal (plus some houserules, like fortitude making it harder to be pushed around, or fortitude reducing firearm penalties because it literally absorbs your recoil)</div> </div> </div> </div>Agree about Potence. Disagree about everything else, especially Fortitude. Soak rolls in general are an incredibly boring, clunky mechanic. Five soak dice at max level is garbage. And powers like Prowess from Pain are extremely fun, allowing me to duplicate the berzerker ferocity of the more animalistic vampires such as found in &quot;Necroscope&quot;.. And Flesh of Marble allows people to duplicate the living statue versions of vampires found in &quot;Interview with the Vampire&quot; and &quot;Twilight&quot;. Fortitude is both powerful and fun now.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3598-cajunkhan","name":"CajunKhan","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3598_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1700"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-05-04T03:20:44-07:00","id":1447382,"title":"","content":"Just take half for damage and soak; Boom, combat is twice as good and Fortitude is great. (also use Pre-Revised rules for soaking Non-Bane Agg with stamina)","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25794-mywifeisscary","name":"MyWifeIsScary","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25794_2.png","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3711"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-05-04T05:32:47-07:00","id":1447389,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MyWifeIsScary</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1443592-the-official-v5-vs-v20-thread?p=1447382#post1447382\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Just take half for damage and soak; Boom, combat is twice as good and Fortitude is great. (also use Pre-Revised rules for soaking Non-Bane Agg with stamina)</div> </div> </div> </div>Pre-Revised rules for soaking non-bane damage pretty much solves EVERY problem with V20 Fortitude. Sure, it\u2019s boring, but it\u2019s actually useful. As practical proof I give you the V20 Dhampir whose ability to soak lethal and take agg damage as lethal means with Stamina 5 + Fort 1 they can take Agg damage as well as a 7th Gen with Fortitude 6. In the campaign I\u2019m running the Dhampir is literally the frakking Energizer Bunny; their other abilities are basically capped at neonate vampire level, but they can survive damned near anything.<br /> <br /> And the V20 Dhampir does show the other way to make Fortitude viable (in the boring but practical sense) stop making everything that isn\u2019t an outright bane deal agg damage. If it\u2019s not sunlight, fire or true faith then it\u2019s only lethal and can be soaked as such.<br /> <br /> And yes, extra dice to certain attributes is far more flexible than V5\u2019s specific powers. You can add Potence to every strength test, Celerity to every dexterity test, Auspex 1 to practically every perception test. We found it so incredibly useful we swiped the lowest tier of V5 Presence (which basically overlaps with a good performance test which uses the exact same dice pool and doesn\u2019t cost blood) to make it add to interaction tests the same way Potence does to physical ones.<br /> <br /> Give me extra dice any day and I\u2019ll find ways to leverage them that specific powers simply won\u2019t allow.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1328-chris24601","name":"Chris24601","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"520"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-05-04T09:07:19-07:00","id":1447411,"title":"","content":"The current \u201cscore\u201d from page 1 is 36-7 in favor of V20 (and prior), which seems pretty accurate with how the games are favored with people I know if real life. However, I think that if Twitter\u2019s #Vamily crowd were here, those numbers might look very, very different. <br /> <br /> I don\u2019t have any links on hand, but I have read developer interviews where they\u2019ve stated that V5 changes have been met with more approval than disapproval, and I think there are definitely areas you can look to find that to be accurate. I don\u2019t think any legitimate criticisms or concerns voiced by fans of older versions are really going to be addressed in any meaningful way moving forward. <br /> <br /> That sounds overly pessimistic but what I mean is, there is no meaningful back and forth with the devs anywhere that can see other than Twitter, where Outstar will happily explain why you\u2019re wrong if you don\u2019t love V5 changes.<br /> <br /> I think I finally get how Brujah feel in the Camarilla.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":6}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24351-garygeneric","name":"Garygeneric","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24351_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"108"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-05-04T09:28:34-07:00","id":1447412,"title":"","content":"Eh, I think everyone should be able to appreciate everyone else's tastes on the subject. The big thing for me is I don't understand why it should matter if your opinion is the majority or not.<br /> <br /> An opinion being popular does not make it more valid.<br /> <br /> I like V5 and V1 most.<br /> <br /> That doesn't mean I'm more right than people who like the other editions. It's just the way I prefer my games. There's no wrong answer.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Author of <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Cthulhu-Armageddon-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01KUOM7SI/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982844&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Cthulhu+Armageddon\" target=\"_blank\">Cthulhu Armageddon</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Teenage-Weredeer-Bright-Falls-Mysteries-ebook/dp/B075TTN2FN/ref=sr_1_2?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982717&amp;sr=1-2&amp;keywords=Weredeer#customerReviews\" target=\"_blank\">I was a Teenage Weredeer</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Straight-Outta-Fangton-Comedic-Vampire-ebook/dp/B01KNHICCC/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982774&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Straight+Outta+Fangton\" target=\"_blank\">Straight Outta Fangton</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Lucifers-Star-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01MDM9MCT/ref=mt_kindle?_encoding=UTF8&amp;me=&amp;qid=\" target=\"_blank\">Lucifer's Star</a>, </i>and the <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Rules-Supervillainy-Saga-Book-ebook/dp/B07MB89S33/\" target=\"_blank\">Supervillainy Saga</a>.</i><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","name":"CTPhipps","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12002_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13933"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-05-04T09:33:51-07:00","id":1447413,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CTPhipps</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1443592-the-official-v5-vs-v20-thread?p=1447412#post1447412\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Eh, I think everyone should be able to appreciate everyone else's tastes on the subject. The big thing for me is I don't understand why it should matter if your opinion is the majority or not.<br /> <br /> An opinion being popular does not make it more valid.<br /> <br /> I like V5 and V1 most.<br /> <br /> That doesn't mean I'm more right than people who like the other editions. It's just the way I prefer my games. There's no wrong answer.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> because the more ppl agree that V5 isn't good the bigger the chances are that the ppl working on V5 might actually do something about it","signature":"","edited":{"userid":25992,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25992-archderd","user":"archderd","date":". 05-04-2021, 12:37 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":6}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25992-archderd","name":"archderd","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25992_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2020"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"205"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-05-04T09:35:42-07:00","id":1447414,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>archderd</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1443592-the-official-v5-vs-v20-thread?p=1447413#post1447413\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">because if more ppl agreed that V5 isn't good the bigger the chances are that the ppl working on V5 might actually do something about it</div> </div> </div> </div>Unfortunate because that isn't a very good thing for me as a fan.<br /> <br /> I'd rather than refine V5 than destroy it.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Author of <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Cthulhu-Armageddon-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01KUOM7SI/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982844&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Cthulhu+Armageddon\" target=\"_blank\">Cthulhu Armageddon</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Teenage-Weredeer-Bright-Falls-Mysteries-ebook/dp/B075TTN2FN/ref=sr_1_2?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982717&amp;sr=1-2&amp;keywords=Weredeer#customerReviews\" target=\"_blank\">I was a Teenage Weredeer</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Straight-Outta-Fangton-Comedic-Vampire-ebook/dp/B01KNHICCC/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982774&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Straight+Outta+Fangton\" target=\"_blank\">Straight Outta Fangton</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Lucifers-Star-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01MDM9MCT/ref=mt_kindle?_encoding=UTF8&amp;me=&amp;qid=\" target=\"_blank\">Lucifer's Star</a>, </i>and the <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Rules-Supervillainy-Saga-Book-ebook/dp/B07MB89S33/\" target=\"_blank\">Supervillainy Saga</a>.</i><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","name":"CTPhipps","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12002_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13933"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-05-04T10:22:43-07:00","id":1447418,"title":"","content":"Did people who liked D&amp;D4e like 5e? From the Warhammer forums, I know that those who liked 3e also liked 4e. So I don't think a V6 will necessarily be anathema to fans of V5--it may take the best of all editions and be more popular as a result.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Writer, publisher, performer<br /> Mostly he/his, sometimes she/her IRL <a href=\"https://adam-lowe.com\" target=\"_blank\">https://adam-lowe.com</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5291-adambeyoncelowe","name":"adambeyoncelowe","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5291_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2802"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-05-04T11:55:46-07:00","id":1447426,"title":"","content":"5E is just the best DnD. It's got some problems and subjective issues; I kinda liked putting individual points into skills rather than just getting a universal proficiency bonus to a few skills, and clearly some things are better than others, and also &quot;monk&quot; and &quot;Barbarian&quot; are kinda shit names for classes... so mostly nitpicks. <br /> <br /> It seems pretty clear that going from V5 to something more V20 will hurt a lot less fans than the jump from V20 to V5. V20 is broadly applicable, whilst V5 has a very narrow focus. You can use V20 to run V5 stories, but you can't use V5 to run most V20 stories.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25794-mywifeisscary","name":"MyWifeIsScary","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25794_2.png","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3711"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-05-04T12:03:02-07:00","id":1447428,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Chris24601</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1443592-the-official-v5-vs-v20-thread?p=1447389#post1447389\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Pre-Revised rules for soaking non-bane damage pretty much solves EVERY problem with V20 Fortitude. Sure, it\u2019s boring, but it\u2019s actually useful. As practical proof I give you the V20 Dhampir whose ability to soak lethal and take agg damage as lethal means with Stamina 5 + Fort 1 they can take Agg damage as well as a 7th Gen with Fortitude 6. In the campaign I\u2019m running the Dhampir is literally the frakking Energizer Bunny; their other abilities are basically capped at neonate vampire level, but they can survive damned near anything.<br /> <br /> And the V20 Dhampir does show the other way to make Fortitude viable (in the boring but practical sense) stop making everything that isn\u2019t an outright bane deal agg damage. If it\u2019s not sunlight, fire or true faith then it\u2019s only lethal and can be soaked as such.<br /> <br /> And yes, extra dice to certain attributes is far more flexible than V5\u2019s specific powers. You can add Potence to every strength test, Celerity to every dexterity test, Auspex 1 to practically every perception test. We found it so incredibly useful we swiped the lowest tier of V5 Presence (which basically overlaps with a good performance test which uses the exact same dice pool and doesn\u2019t cost blood) to make it add to interaction tests the same way Potence does to physical ones.<br /> <br /> Give me extra dice any day and I\u2019ll find ways to leverage them that specific powers simply won\u2019t allow.</div> </div> </div> </div>Did we read different rules or since when is Sunlight doing damage for Dhampires? Should Dhampires main advantage not be, they can walk at day like a normal mortal despite being not a mortal?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>As I am from Austria I need to clarify two things.<br /> First my native language is german and so please point out if the english I write is broken so I can improve.<br /> Second I do not own VTMV beyond first three books nor any line after M20 Corebook because it is not out there and I wait for the translation.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26160-koronus","name":"Koronus","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2020"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"366"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-05-04T12:07:08-07:00","id":1447429,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MyWifeIsScary</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1443592-the-official-v5-vs-v20-thread?p=1447426#post1447426\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">5E is just the best DnD. It's got some problems and subjective issues; I kinda liked putting individual points into skills rather than just getting a universal proficiency bonus to a few skills, and clearly some things are better than others, and also &quot;monk&quot; and &quot;Barbarian&quot; are kinda shit names for classes... so mostly nitpicks. <br /> <br /> It seems pretty clear that going from V5 to something more V20 will hurt a lot less fans than the jump from V20 to V5. V20 is broadly applicable, whilst V5 has a very narrow focus. You can use V20 to run V5 stories, but you can't use V5 to run most V20 stories.</div> </div> </div> </div>Since we're on the topic of DnD. Isn't this the same kind of division that made Pathfinder? Granted, it was hell of a lot more complicated then that but still.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\"><div align=\"left\"><a href=\"http://www.nodiatis.com/personality.htm\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://www.nodiatis.com/pub/7.jpg\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a></div></div>","edited":{"userid":26764,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26764-vilenecromancer","user":"Vilenecromancer","date":".  Fixing grammar and spelling 05-04-2021, 03:07 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26764-vilenecromancer","name":"Vilenecromancer","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar26764_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"247"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-05-04T12:27:22-07:00","id":1447431,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Vilenecromancer</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1443592-the-official-v5-vs-v20-thread?p=1447429#post1447429\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Since we're on the topic of DnD. Isn't this the same kind of division that made Pathfinder? Granted, it was hell of a lot more complicated then that but still.</div> </div> </div> </div>Yeah because the players where unhappy, that WotC made 4th Edition like a Videogame and with the Open Game Licence the people took the evolution of their favourite edition<br /> <br /> Another advantage of PF whas, that it whas unlike D&amp;D 4 available in other languages.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>As I am from Austria I need to clarify two things.<br /> First my native language is german and so please point out if the english I write is broken so I can improve.<br /> Second I do not own VTMV beyond first three books nor any line after M20 Corebook because it is not out there and I wait for the translation.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26160-koronus","name":"Koronus","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2020"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"366"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-05-04T13:38:06-07:00","id":1447441,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CTPhipps</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1443592-the-official-v5-vs-v20-thread?p=1447414#post1447414\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Unfortunate because that isn't a very good thing for me as a fan.<br /> <br /> I'd rather than refine V5 than destroy it.</div> </div> </div> </div>While invariably V6 is going to piss off some V5 fans, and fail to bring back some pre-V5 edition fans, I share the lack of pessimism that V6 can't be a more unifying edition that refines V5 and walks back some of the more drastic changes to a happier middle ground. Of course, I'm not sure VtM is in the hands of the right people to be doing this, but I'm at least willing to see if the newest combination of hands do with W5.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Vilenecromancer</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1443592-the-official-v5-vs-v20-thread?p=1447429#post1447429\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Since we're on the topic of DnD. Isn't this the same kind of division that made Pathfinder? Granted, it was hell of a lot more complicated then that but still.</div> </div> </div> </div>We haven't had a real Pathfinder equivalent for VtM. The lack of a WoD OGL is probably a big part of it, as is the tiny WoD fanbase compared to the D&amp;D fanbase to support such a thing.<br /> <br /> Of course D&amp;D 5e basically took the wind out of Paizo's sails. PF1 still has its dedicated fans, but that's not really a growing group, and PF2 is generally perceived as not really having a good market (too many PF1 fans didn't convert because it moved away from the D&amp;D 3.X/PF1 design mentality that made them PF1 fans in the first place, and PF2 isn't really offering anything significantly appealing to the D&amp;D 5e crowd). D&amp;D 5e is still OGL, but nobody's figured out a way to replicate PF1's massive cut into D&amp;D's market because the circumstances just aren't there.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-05-04T14:04:02-07:00","id":1447444,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Koronus</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1443592-the-official-v5-vs-v20-thread?p=1447428#post1447428\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Did we read different rules or since when is Sunlight doing damage for Dhampires? Should Dhampires main advantage not be, they can walk at day like a normal mortal despite being not a mortal?</div> </div> </div> </div>Sun doesn\u2019t do damage to Dhampirs. Where did you read that in my reply?<br /> <br /> My point was, V20 Dhampirs basically have the equivalent of pre-Revised Fortitude because they treat all Agg damage as lethal and can soak lethal with Stamina. This makes them super-tanky vs. other supernaturals (which fits well with real world lore where they often become vampire/monster hunters).<br /> <br /> I referenced Dhampirs because they highlight both main ways that you could tweak the rules to make Fortitude better. The first is to let Stamina add to the soak if you have Fortitude, the second is remove the Agg descriptor from everything that isn\u2019t an outright bane (for vamps that\u2019s sun, fire and true faith) so that they can soak more reliably.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1328-chris24601","name":"Chris24601","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"520"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-05-04T14:12:44-07:00","id":1447445,"title":"","content":"I keep reading people saying that v20 can tell more stories then v5. Name one story please.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\"><div align=\"left\"><a href=\"http://www.nodiatis.com/personality.htm\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://www.nodiatis.com/pub/7.jpg\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a></div></div>","edited":{"userid":26764,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26764-vilenecromancer","user":"Vilenecromancer","date":".  Grammer 05-04-2021, 05:13 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26764-vilenecromancer","name":"Vilenecromancer","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar26764_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"247"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-05-04T14:15:34-07:00","id":1447446,"title":"","content":"<a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1328-chris24601\" style=\"background-image:url('data:image/svg+xml;base64,');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"1328\" data-vbnamecard=\"1328\">Chris24601</a> &quot;And the V20 Dhampir does show the other way to make Fortitude viable (in the boring but practical sense) stop making everything that isn\u2019t an outright bane deal agg damage. <b>If it\u2019s not sunlight</b>, fire or true faith then it\u2019s only lethal and can be soaked as such.&quot;","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>As I am from Austria I need to clarify two things.<br /> First my native language is german and so please point out if the english I write is broken so I can improve.<br /> Second I do not own VTMV beyond first three books nor any line after M20 Corebook because it is not out there and I wait for the translation.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26160-koronus","name":"Koronus","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2020"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"366"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-05-04T14:35:41-07:00","id":1447447,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Vilenecromancer</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1443592-the-official-v5-vs-v20-thread?p=1447445#post1447445\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I keep reading people saying that v20 can tell more stories then v5. Name one story please.</div> </div> </div> </div>While I don't mean this to be personally aimed at you, given how this sort of question has gone repeatedly in the past, can you promise not to respond to any examples with any of the following as reasons V5 really &quot;can&quot; do said stories?<br /> <br /> 1) The Golden Rule.<br /> 2) House rules and/or homebrew.<br /> 3) Trust the future books, including announced ones, are going to solve any issues.<br /> <br /> Because the number of times we've tried to highlight this, and then just got into debates about one or all of the above, has gotten exhausting.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-05-04T14:41:47-07:00","id":1447449,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Vilenecromancer</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1443592-the-official-v5-vs-v20-thread?p=1447429#post1447429\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Since we're on the topic of DnD. Isn't this the same kind of division that made Pathfinder? Granted, it was hell of a lot more complicated then that but still.</div> </div> </div> </div>There were a couple different things that made Pathfinder.<br /> <br /> The first was the OGL, which let basically anyone publish products under the D&amp;D label. At the time, it was a brilliant business decision. You saw <i>White Wolf</i> actually publishing products for another company's settings and game system. Really good products, too. The 3e Sword &amp; Sorcery Ravenloft books were a more than worthy continuation of the setting from 2e. You saw a huge explosion of third party content during the 3.0-3.5 D&amp;D era that helped keep interest in the game alive. <br /> <br /> But the OGL also spawned D&amp;D's biggest competitor when fans didn't like 4e. The new edition butchered too many sacred cows and tried to be too different a game. Way more so, I think, than V5 has departed from V20. I don't remember what the terms of 4e's OGL equivalent were, but they were a lot more restrictive. You didn't really see any third party content. A lot of 4e felt like it was going out of its way to take a dump on the lore of previous editions. Even a WotC April Fool's Day post I remember from the late 2000s felt like it was taking mean-spirited jabs at 3e. <br /> <br /> So between those two factors, fan discontent and the OGL, another game actually outsold D&amp;D for the first time in TTRPG history. Fan discontent created the demand for an alternative, and the OGL let Paizo supply it by essentially taking over publication of 3.5 material from WotC. PF was a direct continuation of a game system lots of people wanted to keep playing. &quot;Backwards compatible&quot; was a big selling point of PF back in the day. You could keep using all of your old 3.5/3.0 books, with a little fiddling. <br /> <br /> It also didn't hurt that Pathfinder was flat-out <i>better</i> than 3.5 (at least in my view). Production value was higher. Rules books had lots of really cool mechanics. Setting books were top quality. Lot of the guys working for Paizo were top tier talent. Their forums were vibrant and active, with lots of participation from the game developers (which I think company policy made mandatory.) The whole game and the community around it was just better.<br /> <br /> Another factor which I think helped Pathfinder sell so well was their emphasis on publishing <i>adventures</i>, rather than rulebooks. By default, D&amp;D isn't a flavor-heavy setting like the WoD. In WoD you can have books on being a ghoul or religious faith among vampires. Eventually you'll start scraping the bottom of the idea barrel, but you can go on for a while. In D&amp;D, the individual settings like Ravenloft, Greyhawk, etc. were essentially sub-brands of a larger and setting-agnostic system. I don't know what sales figures were for them, but the glory days of D&amp;D campaign settings were 2e for me. So that left publishing more rule books as WotC's bread and butter, but past a certain point you suffer from mechanics fatigue and GMs just not wanting to deal with the hassle of learning and using material (some of it poorly balanced) from so many books. <br /> <br /> But adventures? Those never get old. Those are the actual bread and butter of any gaming group. Paizo went ahead and did the lion's share of a GM's prep work for them. And if there was a particular adventure you didn't like, well, there were plenty others. You can have rules bloat, but you can't ever have adventure bloat. Even if you never play them, you can steal stuff to use in your own campaigns, or just enjoy reading them and thinking &quot;ooh, I'd like to run this someday.&quot;<br /> <br /> It's hard to emphasize here just what an excellent business model the AP (adventure path) format was for Paizo. You've seen a few pre-published adventures for the WoD, like Transylvania Chronicles, but nothing on the scale of the Pathfinder APs. The APs were Paizo's vanguard, with setting books and rules books on the side. I know people who continued to buy APs long after they stopped buying rules books. <br /> <br /> But Pathfinder's premise was essentially extending the shelf life of a game system people didn't want stop playing in 2008. (3.5 was published in 2003, so it'd only been around for five years before Wizards tried to pull the plug.) And eventually... people did want to stop playing. RPG design moved on with the years and Paizo was stuck with a system rooted in 2000. Their whole business model was being the direct continuation that WotC wasn't, so they couldn't really make any major overhauls. Option bloat became a thing. APs might have been their bread and butter, but rules books still kept coming, and eventually I had my fill. The new mechanics declined in quality. The APs also seemed to decline in quality. Paizo had already done all of the really cool ideas. <br /> <br /> I stopped playing PF in 2013 and migrated to the WoD. PF had too many warts and I was burned out. <br /> <br /> In 2014, 5e came out. Wizards learned their lesson from 4e. The new edition was more like the third, sacred cows brought back to life, and they reinstated the OGL. People loved it. Lot of PF gamers I know switched to 5e. If I still played D&amp;D/PF, <b>I'd</b> want to play 5e. I like Paizo a lot more as a company. I feel a personal connection with its employees that I don't with Wizards'. I think Paizo's adventures (at their best) are gold. But... at the end of the day, none of that is the actual game system I'm playing with. <br /> <br /> In 2018, Paizo bit the bullet and released their own new edition. I've looked it over casually, and it's not my cup of tea. It looks a lot more prolix and fiddly than 5e is. The fandom seems pretty split. I don't know what the sales figures are for 1e vs. 2e books, but most of the PF games I see advertised online are for 1e, so take that anecdote for what it's worth. I can also say that while I'd be willing to play in a PF 1e game, if one came along, I'd be more likely to pass on a 2e game. I already know the rules for 1e. <br /> <br /> Paizo doesn't seem to be what they were, either. A lot of their most talented people have left, and had been leaving for years before then. A few of their former people now work for Wizards. It's pretty obvious who dominates the TTRPG industry now. There's ultimately no competing with the D&amp;D brand. For all the top-notch product that Paizo delivered, and for all the amazing people they formerly had on their staff, they were only able to compete because Wizards bungled things so badly with 4e. (Even if you like 4e as a system, there's no denying it was a failure from a business standpoint.) The corporate overlords eventually noticed it was hurting their bottom line and demanded a course correction. <br /> <br /> <br /> Long digression coming from a long-time D&amp;D/PF fan.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://blood-and-bourbon.obsidianportal.com/\" target=\"_blank\">Blood and Bourbon</a>, my New Orleans-based Vampire chronicle.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3110-false-epiphany","name":"False Epiphany","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3110_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"748"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-05-04T15:02:33-07:00","id":1447453,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Koronus</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1443592-the-official-v5-vs-v20-thread?p=1447446#post1447446\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><span class=\"b-bbcode-user js-bbcode-user\">Guest</span> &amp;quot;And the V20 Dhampir does show the other way to make Fortitude viable (in the boring but practical sense) stop making everything that isn\u2019t an outright bane deal agg damage. <b>If it\u2019s not sunlight</b>, fire or true faith then it\u2019s only lethal and can be soaked as such.&amp;quot;</div> </div> </div> </div>Yes, I was using Dhampir\u2019s treating everything aggravated as lethal instead as an example of how it could be done for vampires, as in, \u201cif its not sunlight, fire or true faith (the traditional banes of a WoD vampire) then they (vampires) should treat the damage as lethal (ergo, soakable).\u201d<br /> <br /> I didn\u2019t think I\u2019d written it THAT unclearly since the topic was Fortitude for vampires. Dhampirs only got mentioned in this case because their mechanics involving soaking damage showed a clear way for V20 Fortitude to not suck.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1328-chris24601","name":"Chris24601","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"520"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-05-04T15:02:51-07:00","id":1447454,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Heavy Arms</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1443592-the-official-v5-vs-v20-thread?p=1447447#post1447447\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> While I don't mean this to be personally aimed at you, given how this sort of question has gone repeatedly in the past, can you promise not to respond to any examples with any of the following as reasons V5 really &quot;can&quot; do said stories?<br /> <br /> 1) The Golden Rule.<br /> 2) House rules and/or homebrew.<br /> 3) Trust the future books, including announced ones, are going to solve any issues.<br /> <br /> Because the number of times we've tried to highlight this, and then just got into debates about one or all of the above, has gotten exhausting.</div> </div> </div> </div>I'm asking out of genuine curiosity. Even without those factors, how can V20 tell more stories then V5 if we go by RAW? This isn't asked out of anger or anything, I just want to understand both sides here.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\"><div align=\"left\"><a href=\"http://www.nodiatis.com/personality.htm\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://www.nodiatis.com/pub/7.jpg\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a></div></div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26764-vilenecromancer","name":"Vilenecromancer","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar26764_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"247"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-05-04T15:29:50-07:00","id":1447464,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Vilenecromancer</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1443592-the-official-v5-vs-v20-thread?p=1447454#post1447454\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I'm asking out of genuine curiosity. Even without those factors, how can V20 tell more stories then V5 if we go by RAW? This isn't asked out of anger or anything, I just want to understand both sides here.</div> </div> </div> </div>As I said before, V5 whas written from the ingame point, that all the elders are gone and it is just you and all the other fledgelings and Neonates that now shell protect the territory.<br /> For example if your blood power is to high you can not feed from anything more then humans. If we go to the roman empire or even the dark ages there are still a lot of low generation vampires that would depend on humans or starve from their rules. Theoretically you could learn animalism but until you learn it you need to stay close to humanity and so Gangrels that just turn to the wild would be impossible.<br /> Then there is the thing that RAW vampires get weaker if they are to long in torpor. If that would be the case there is no need to fear the ancients nor is Torpor viable because if one would sleep to long they are technically from the power only a freshly embraced anymore so you see sleeping for ages only as an emergency bottom if you are in the middle of nowhere and going to starve so you go into sleep hoping that pray will be unfortunate to walk by.<br /> Then you got no dots from 6-9 in the books. Without those there is no more real fearable thing about an elder.<br /> With the blood thickening and thining there is no real reason for diablery. Because your power naturally grows if you wait long enough so the risk for getting killed if you eat the soul of an older stronger vampire is no longer worth the gain.<br /> Then there is no elder round where the characters made it and are in position of power because there is no really feelable power.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>As I am from Austria I need to clarify two things.<br /> First my native language is german and so please point out if the english I write is broken so I can improve.<br /> Second I do not own VTMV beyond first three books nor any line after M20 Corebook because it is not out there and I wait for the translation.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26160-koronus","name":"Koronus","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2020"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"366"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-05-04T15:30:10-07:00","id":1447465,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Vilenecromancer</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1443592-the-official-v5-vs-v20-thread?p=1447454#post1447454\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I'm asking out of genuine curiosity. Even without those factors, how can V20 tell more stories then V5 if we go by RAW? This isn't asked out of anger or anything, I just want to understand both sides here.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> The &quot;diablerie&quot; chronicles books for exemple. Anything using methuselah and elder powers, blood magic based stories (try making a dual between two sorcerers with merely the path of blood, ritualsand the hunger system). &quot;Katana and trenchcoat&quot; campaigns. That's what comes first to mind to me","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24043-nyremne","name":"Nyremne","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"414"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-05-04T15:35:13-07:00","id":1447466,"title":"","content":"Generation being deemphasized is a plus in my book. I always hated generation, and thought one of the best things about Requiem was dumping that damned stat.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3598-cajunkhan","name":"CajunKhan","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3598_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1700"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-05-04T15:57:31-07:00","id":1447471,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Nyremne</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1443592-the-official-v5-vs-v20-thread?p=1447465#post1447465\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The &quot;diablerie&quot; chronicles books for exemple. Anything using methuselah and elder powers, blood magic based stories (try making a dual between two sorcerers with merely the path of blood, ritualsand the hunger system). &quot;Katana and trenchcoat&quot; campaigns. That's what comes first to mind to me</div> </div> </div> </div>I should point out my biggest issue with V5 is the fact that the katana and trenchcoat campaigns are far too easy in the new system. The combat is excellently fast and fluid here.<br /> <br /> Speaking as someone who also owns Diablerie 1 and 2, the point is the Methuselahs aren't fought at full power either because then they'd annihilate the PCs with a weave of their hand. Their stats were written in 1st Edition so they were all 1-5 anyway.<br /> <br /> You're correct the lack of Elder rules hurts using Ur-Shulgi but Ur-Shulgi should be beyond stats anyway.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CajunKhan</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1443592-the-official-v5-vs-v20-thread?p=1447466#post1447466\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Generation being deemphasized is a plus in my book. I always hated generation, and thought one of the best things about Requiem was dumping that damned stat.</div> </div> </div> </div>I admit, I'm glad they made a reason Players would want to play 11th, 12th, and 13th generation or Thin bloods. There's now mechanical reasons that high generation Cainites aren't necessarily mass murdering monsters the way low generation ones always seem to be.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Author of <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Cthulhu-Armageddon-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01KUOM7SI/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982844&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Cthulhu+Armageddon\" target=\"_blank\">Cthulhu Armageddon</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Teenage-Weredeer-Bright-Falls-Mysteries-ebook/dp/B075TTN2FN/ref=sr_1_2?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982717&amp;sr=1-2&amp;keywords=Weredeer#customerReviews\" target=\"_blank\">I was a Teenage Weredeer</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Straight-Outta-Fangton-Comedic-Vampire-ebook/dp/B01KNHICCC/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982774&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Straight+Outta+Fangton\" target=\"_blank\">Straight Outta Fangton</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Lucifers-Star-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01MDM9MCT/ref=mt_kindle?_encoding=UTF8&amp;me=&amp;qid=\" target=\"_blank\">Lucifer's Star</a>, </i>and the <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Rules-Supervillainy-Saga-Book-ebook/dp/B07MB89S33/\" target=\"_blank\">Supervillainy Saga</a>.</i><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":12002,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","user":"CTPhipps","date":". 05-04-2021, 07:00 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","name":"CTPhipps","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12002_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13933"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-05-04T16:01:39-07:00","id":1447474,"title":"","content":"But it is not. We are playing Masquerade not Requiem. If we want to play in a system where the power ceiling is not artificially constricted we would be at Requim. It is one of the biggest fundaments of Masquerade, that who sired you defined how powerfull you are.<br /> Because it made clear for one thing, that those beyond you always look for a sign of weakness and if you have the &quot;luck&quot; by being sired from a low gen cainite it ment that you REALLY need to look out from the elder because an older more powerfull cainite is mayby seeing you as a thing to gain power so you could easily lose your soul because of someone else.<br /> If you merely need to wait for getting more powerfull it makes it less about vampires and more mundan because you fight merely for ideology and other typical things than on your very being of existance because it is a stepstone that hangs the sky a bit higher for someone else.<br /> It is also the reason why you need to fear those ancient beings. Because they have powerlvl you are unable to reach and where can not do anything against if they set eye on you.<br /> <br /> Edit: Because Phipps Ninjad. I would have had less against it, if a Thaumaturgic ritual would made a generation swap for those low gen cainites that are tired of the inhumanity the blood made them got no salvation of golconda so they could get a bit more mortality as a thinblood. But because Diablery should still be the most effective way they should have made it that you can only swap gens 2:1 so getting 2 more points of generation is needed for one generation lowering.<br /> So could low gen vampires still have a chance for enjoying motherhood.<br /> Male vampires are already covered for procreation with either MYtherica or Necromancy or Bardo.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>As I am from Austria I need to clarify two things.<br /> First my native language is german and so please point out if the english I write is broken so I can improve.<br /> Second I do not own VTMV beyond first three books nor any line after M20 Corebook because it is not out there and I wait for the translation.","edited":{"userid":26160,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26160-koronus","user":"Koronus","date":". 05-04-2021, 07:07 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26160-koronus","name":"Koronus","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2020"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"366"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-05-04T16:06:16-07:00","id":1447475,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Koronus</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1443592-the-official-v5-vs-v20-thread?p=1447474#post1447474\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">But it is not. We are playing Masquerade not Requiem. If we want to play in a system where the power ceiling is not artificially constricted we would be at Requim. It is one of the biggest fundaments of Masquerade, that who sired you defined how powerfull you are.<br /> Because it made clear for one thing, that those beyond you always look for a sign of weakness and if you have the &quot;luck&quot; by being sired from a low gen cainite it ment that you REALLY need to look out from the elder because an older more powerfull cainite is mayby seeing you as a thing to gain power so you could easily lose your soul because of someone else.<br /> If you merely need to wait for getting more powerfull it makes it less about vampires and more mundan because you fight merely for ideology and other typical things than on your very being of existance because it is a stepstone that hangs the sky a bit higher for someone else.<br /> It is also the reason why you need to fear those ancient beings. Because they have powerlvl you are unable to reach and where can not do anything against if they set eye on you.</div> </div> </div> </div>This argument was made by Bob on 25 years of Vampire: The Masquerade and for the life of me, I don't get it. Bob says that you don't need to commit diablerie in Requiem because you can just wait until you're old and powerful. That makes no sense because a vampire will need power NOW, not in 200 or 300 years if he wants to survive. There's countless threats out there gunning for an individual vampire and the only way to live to be 200 or 300 if to seek power held by your Elders.<br /> <br /> Also, mechanically, Blood Potency is not that big of a change from the Linear vs. Quadratic Power Expression of Elders vs. Ancilla vs. Neonates.<br /> <br /> Which if you wonder what I mean is to say, the difference between a High Generation Elder and a Low Generation one in V20 is not that big a deal as 1-5 is what the vast majority of their powers are going to be. Most will never get more than a 6 in a Discipline if even that. The 6+ powers are primarily an expression of Methuselahs. Most Elders were already supposed to be gaining vast power from age and experience anyway.<br /> <br /> Really, the only Elder I can think of affected by the gain of Blood Potency is Lucian who had the &quot;joke&quot; of being 2000 years old and 8th generation.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Author of <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Cthulhu-Armageddon-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01KUOM7SI/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982844&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Cthulhu+Armageddon\" target=\"_blank\">Cthulhu Armageddon</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Teenage-Weredeer-Bright-Falls-Mysteries-ebook/dp/B075TTN2FN/ref=sr_1_2?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982717&amp;sr=1-2&amp;keywords=Weredeer#customerReviews\" target=\"_blank\">I was a Teenage Weredeer</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Straight-Outta-Fangton-Comedic-Vampire-ebook/dp/B01KNHICCC/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982774&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Straight+Outta+Fangton\" target=\"_blank\">Straight Outta Fangton</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Lucifers-Star-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01MDM9MCT/ref=mt_kindle?_encoding=UTF8&amp;me=&amp;qid=\" target=\"_blank\">Lucifer's Star</a>, </i>and the <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Rules-Supervillainy-Saga-Book-ebook/dp/B07MB89S33/\" target=\"_blank\">Supervillainy Saga</a>.</i><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":12002,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","user":"CTPhipps","date":". 05-04-2021, 07:09 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","name":"CTPhipps","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12002_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13933"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-05-04T16:15:50-07:00","id":1447480,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Vilenecromancer</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1443592-the-official-v5-vs-v20-thread?p=1447454#post1447454\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I'm asking out of genuine curiosity. Even without those factors, how can V20 tell more stories then V5 if we go by RAW? This isn't asked out of anger or anything, I just want to understand both sides here.</div> </div> </div> </div>OK, so, I'm going to start a basic VtM story (yes, this is based on play experience), and then get to where V5's mechanics shoot it in the foot:<br /> <br /> The Coterie of PCs have been working to expand their current small Domain, and having been eyeing a Domain controlled by the Brujah Primogen's childe. The Tremere PC's let the rest of the Coterie know that there's an place of occult importance in there they're willing to reward the PCs heavily for access to. It's got a good rack and an established Elysium that the PCs want to use to further grow their power.<br /> <br /> The PCs have been trying to figure out what this Brujah's price is, but they just can't seem to figure out something to get him to budge. He's just stubbornly holding it despite having other areas under his control that would be plenty to keep him a big player in the city. Something is up. So the PC investigate. They actually end up missing that the Brujah's Touchstones are all in that area, because he's been hiding that secret tightly and that's exactly why he's not budging. However, instead they find out that there's Sabbat after that occult spot too, and the Brujah didn't seem to be doing anything about it.<br /> <br /> They take a risk, and ignore his Domain to stop the Sabbat. In the process they find out that the Sabbat had 100% irrefutable proof that the Brujah is a diablerist without permission. Awesome, they've got the Brujah by the balls with some double blackmail. Now he's surely cave!<br /> <br /> So the PCs send their best social type to do the blackmail....<br /> <br /> In my not-V5 game, we blackmailed his dead ass... and then set him up to die anyway.<br /> <br /> But this is where V5 gets directly in the way. Why? How good your blackmail material is <b>doesn't matter</b>. No bonus dice, no difficulty modifiers, no extra successes or whatever. It's a straight roll off between the Brujah and the best social PC, with +0 Willpower damage because its a one-on-one (after all, you don't blackmail someone in front of an audience because that ruins the point).<br /> <br /> The results are going to come down to either the NPC losing the social conflict, taking the WP hit, and then counterattack the PCs on the grounds of Domain violations, or the NPC wins the social conflict and then the PC either has to fork over the blackmail material or taking the WP hit and... the NPC comes after them on the Domain violation since they already played their hand.<br /> <br /> So, basically, you can't actually blackmail people in V5 unless they have extremely low WP, and you have a really big dice-pool over theirs at which point rolling was perfunctory anyway. Anyone worth rolling against turns the situation into a no-win.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-05-04T16:18:42-07:00","id":1447481,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CTPhipps</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1443592-the-official-v5-vs-v20-thread?p=1447475#post1447475\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> This argument was made by Bob on 25 years of Vampire: The Masquerade and for the life of me, I don't get it. Bob says that you don't need to commit diablerie in Requiem because you can just wait until you're old and powerful. That makes no sense because a vampire will need power NOW, not in 200 or 300 years if he wants to survive. There's countless threats out there gunning for an individual vampire and the only way to live to be 200 or 300 if to seek power held by your Elders.<br /> <br /> Also, mechanically, Blood Potency is not that big of a change from the Linear vs. Quadratic Power Expression of Elders vs. Ancilla vs. Neonates.<br /> <br /> Which if you wonder what I mean is to say, the difference between a High Generation Elder and a Low Generation one in V20 is not that big a deal as 1-5 is what the vast majority of their powers are going to be. Most will never get more than a 6 in a Discipline if even that. The 6+ powers are primarily an expression of Methuselahs. Most Elders were already supposed to be gaining vast power from age and experience anyway.<br /> <br /> Really, the only Elder I can think of affected by the gain of Blood Potency is Lucian who had the &amp;quot;joke&amp;quot; of being 2000 years old and 8th generation.</div> </div> </div> </div>This conversation just gave me an idea. Thank you both.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\"><div align=\"left\"><a href=\"http://www.nodiatis.com/personality.htm\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://www.nodiatis.com/pub/7.jpg\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a></div></div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26764-vilenecromancer","name":"Vilenecromancer","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar26764_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"247"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-05-04T16:28:55-07:00","id":1447482,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Vilenecromancer</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1443592-the-official-v5-vs-v20-thread?p=1447481#post1447481\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> This conversation just gave me an idea. Thank you both.</div> </div> </div> </div>Oh, do tell!<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Author of <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Cthulhu-Armageddon-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01KUOM7SI/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982844&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Cthulhu+Armageddon\" target=\"_blank\">Cthulhu Armageddon</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Teenage-Weredeer-Bright-Falls-Mysteries-ebook/dp/B075TTN2FN/ref=sr_1_2?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982717&amp;sr=1-2&amp;keywords=Weredeer#customerReviews\" target=\"_blank\">I was a Teenage Weredeer</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Straight-Outta-Fangton-Com