o where V5's mechanics shoot it in the foot:<br /> <br /> The Coterie of PCs have been working to expand their current small Domain, and having been eyeing a Domain controlled by the Brujah Primogen's childe. The Tremere PC's let the rest of the Coterie know that there's an place of occult importance in there they're willing to reward the PCs heavily for access to. It's got a good rack and an established Elysium that the PCs want to use to further grow their power.<br /> <br /> The PCs have been trying to figure out what this Brujah's price is, but they just can't seem to figure out something to get him to budge. He's just stubbornly holding it despite having other areas under his control that would be plenty to keep him a big player in the city. Something is up. So the PC investigate. They actually end up missing that the Brujah's Touchstones are all in that area, because he's been hiding that secret tightly and that's exactly why he's not budging. However, instead they find out that there's Sabbat after that occult spot too, and the Brujah didn't seem to be doing anything about it.<br /> <br /> They take a risk, and ignore his Domain to stop the Sabbat. In the process they find out that the Sabbat had 100% irrefutable proof that the Brujah is a diablerist without permission. Awesome, they've got the Brujah by the balls with some double blackmail. Now he's surely cave!<br /> <br /> So the PCs send their best social type to do the blackmail....<br /> <br /> In my not-V5 game, we blackmailed his dead ass... and then set him up to die anyway.<br /> <br /> <b><i>But this is where V5 gets directly in the way. Why? How good your blackmail material is doesn't matter. No bonus dice, no difficulty modifiers, no extra successes or whatever. It's a straight roll off between the Brujah and the best social PC, with +0 Willpower damage because its a one-on-one (after all, you don't blackmail someone in front of an audience because that ruins the point).</i></b><br /> <br /> The results are going to come down to either the NPC losing the social conflict, taking the WP hit, and then counterattack the PCs on the grounds of Domain violations, or the NPC wins the social conflict and then the PC either has to fork over the blackmail material or taking the WP hit and... the NPC comes after them on the Domain violation since they already played their hand.<br /> <br /> So, basically, you can't actually blackmail people in V5 unless they have extremely low WP, and you have a really big dice-pool over theirs at which point rolling was perfunctory anyway. Anyone worth rolling against turns the situation into a no-win.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> There's just 1 problem with your story, there are dice bonus and difficulty modifiers. to quote the book on page 120, &quot;The Storyteller might decide to add or subtract a modifier to <b>any</b> dice pool.&quot;<br /> <br /> On that same page, the book then goes on to explain the options for the ST to use. As per RAW, there are potentially bonus dice and difficulty changes to any dice pool based on situational things and RP. Granted, it doesn't list off how much or how little, but that gets into ST preference.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\"><div align=\"left\"><a href=\"http://www.nodiatis.com/personality.htm\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://www.nodiatis.com/pub/7.jpg\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a></div></div>","edited":{"userid":26764,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26764-vilenecromancer","user":"Vilenecromancer","date":".  Bolding part of the quote to show what I am referring to 05-04-2021, 07:30 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26764-vilenecromancer","name":"Vilenecromancer","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar26764_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"247"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-05-04T16:33:20-07:00","id":1447484,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CTPhipps</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1443592-the-official-v5-vs-v20-thread?p=1447482#post1447482\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Oh, do tell!</div> </div> </div> </div>Well VTR had skills higher then 5, AND blood potency. ATM I am thinking of crafting a rule to either adapt hunger and blood potency into V20, or import Elder Powers into V5.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\"><div align=\"left\"><a href=\"http://www.nodiatis.com/personality.htm\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://www.nodiatis.com/pub/7.jpg\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a></div></div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26764-vilenecromancer","name":"Vilenecromancer","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar26764_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"247"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-05-04T16:41:32-07:00","id":1447485,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Vilenecromancer</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1443592-the-official-v5-vs-v20-thread?p=1447484#post1447484\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Well VTR had skills higher then 5, AND blood potency. ATM I am thinking of crafting a rule to either adapt hunger and blood potency into V20, or import Elder Powers into V5.</div> </div> </div> </div>Either would be good.<br /> <br /> I've stated that V5 would be perfect for me if they could do the following:<br /> <br /> * Reincorporate the Sabbat<br /> * Modify the rules so that we can use a form of Paths<br /> * Inhuman Touchstones<br /> * Explain/fix Convictions so we know how to get new ones and change them<br /> * Elder Disciplines 6-10 so we can have godlike Antediluvians<br /> * Make it so that we aren't so restricted with Discipline powers. If you need to limit them at all, have Blood Potency allow you an additional power per level in a Discipline per level of Blood Potency.<br /> <br /> <a href=\"https://www.cardboardrepublic.com/articles/you-should-be-playing/vampire-the-requiem-blood-smoke\" target=\"_blank\">Anyone remember the BLOOD AND SMOKE supplement that was designed around modifying the rules for Requiem to make vampires more badass and cinematic? </a>That could be a cool V5 supplement as well.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Author of <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Cthulhu-Armageddon-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01KUOM7SI/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982844&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Cthulhu+Armageddon\" target=\"_blank\">Cthulhu Armageddon</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Teenage-Weredeer-Bright-Falls-Mysteries-ebook/dp/B075TTN2FN/ref=sr_1_2?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982717&amp;sr=1-2&amp;keywords=Weredeer#customerReviews\" target=\"_blank\">I was a Teenage Weredeer</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Straight-Outta-Fangton-Comedic-Vampire-ebook/dp/B01KNHICCC/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982774&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Straight+Outta+Fangton\" target=\"_blank\">Straight Outta Fangton</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Lucifers-Star-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01MDM9MCT/ref=mt_kindle?_encoding=UTF8&amp;me=&amp;qid=\" target=\"_blank\">Lucifer's Star</a>, </i>and the <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Rules-Supervillainy-Saga-Book-ebook/dp/B07MB89S33/\" target=\"_blank\">Supervillainy Saga</a>.</i><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","name":"CTPhipps","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12002_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13933"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-05-04T16:43:57-07:00","id":1447486,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Vilenecromancer</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1443592-the-official-v5-vs-v20-thread?p=1447483#post1447483\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">There's just 1 problem with your story, there are dice bonus and difficulty modifiers.</div> </div> </div> </div>That is part of the Simple Test section, not the Contest/Conflict section, which doesn't even have difficulties (because it's a roll off).","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-05-04T16:55:05-07:00","id":1447487,"title":"","content":"V20 actually has a functioning Humanity system. Requiem too albeit it's man vs beast conflict is a different struggle. V5 by RAW is utterly broken.<br /> <br /> Either you create Tenets that you will often break and eventually handback you sheet once you finally hit 0, or you create Tenets that you will hardly if ever break and the whole system is pointless.<br /> <br /> V20 also has diff\u00e9rents paths which allows you to play a wide variety of vampire archetype that are impossible to replicate in V5. Like serial diablerists. Or shovelheads creators, or really anything Sabbat.<br /> <br /> DA20 even rewards you for good roleplay and high road score with the aura system.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":24936,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24936-morbus","user":"Morbus","date":". 05-04-2021, 07:58 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24936-morbus","name":"Morbus","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"119"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-05-04T16:57:18-07:00","id":1447488,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Morbus</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1443592-the-official-v5-vs-v20-thread?p=1447487#post1447487\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">V20 actually has a functioning Humanity system. Requiem too albeit it's man vs beast conflict is a different struggle. V5 by RAW is utterly broken.<br /> <br /> Either you create Tenets that you will often break and eventually handback you sheet in a game over or you create Tenets that you will hardly if ever break and the whole system is pointless.<br /> <br /> V20 also has diff\u00e9rents paths which allows you to play a wide variety of vampire archetype that are impossible to replicate in V5. Like serial diablerists. Or shovelheads creators, or really anything Sabbat.</div> </div> </div> </div>Yes, you need a Sabbat book to do the Sabbat, which I trust Justin Achilli to make. So I'm glad that is getting rectified.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Author of <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Cthulhu-Armageddon-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01KUOM7SI/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982844&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Cthulhu+Armageddon\" target=\"_blank\">Cthulhu Armageddon</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Teenage-Weredeer-Bright-Falls-Mysteries-ebook/dp/B075TTN2FN/ref=sr_1_2?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982717&amp;sr=1-2&amp;keywords=Weredeer#customerReviews\" target=\"_blank\">I was a Teenage Weredeer</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Straight-Outta-Fangton-Comedic-Vampire-ebook/dp/B01KNHICCC/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982774&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Straight+Outta+Fangton\" target=\"_blank\">Straight Outta Fangton</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Lucifers-Star-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01MDM9MCT/ref=mt_kindle?_encoding=UTF8&amp;me=&amp;qid=\" target=\"_blank\">Lucifer's Star</a>, </i>and the <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Rules-Supervillainy-Saga-Book-ebook/dp/B07MB89S33/\" target=\"_blank\">Supervillainy Saga</a>.</i><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","name":"CTPhipps","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12002_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13933"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-05-04T16:57:24-07:00","id":1447489,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Heavy Arms</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1443592-the-official-v5-vs-v20-thread?p=1447486#post1447486\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> That is part of the Simple Test section, not the Contest/Conflict section, which doesn't even have difficulties (because it's a roll off).</div> </div> </div> </div>It's in the books, and says ST can do this with any dice pool. That said if you wanna say Contest/Conflicts don't count then I can also point you to page 305 <b>Knives in Their Smiles</b>. While it's more about the surrounding audience, it is still a modifier that can work. However that just gets into Golden Rule territory.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\"><div align=\"left\"><a href=\"http://www.nodiatis.com/personality.htm\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://www.nodiatis.com/pub/7.jpg\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a></div></div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26764-vilenecromancer","name":"Vilenecromancer","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar26764_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"247"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-05-04T17:06:27-07:00","id":1447491,"title":"","content":"Also V5 punishes table that have players who want their vampires to hold different values. In V20, you can easily have a non-violent with a rather murder happy vampire playing together. Even following the same path like say Humanity. Their score will be different but the muderhobo will hardly feel the difference as long as he doesn't commit heinous crimes.<br /> <br /> Now try to create Tenets that encourage both kind of roleplay. Now create a table of not 2 but 5 players with very different vampires. Now make a Sabbat games where each have different path. See how V5 system crashes and burn.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":8}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24936-morbus","name":"Morbus","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"119"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-05-04T17:15:24-07:00","id":1447492,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Morbus</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1443592-the-official-v5-vs-v20-thread?p=1447491#post1447491\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Also V5 punishes table that have players who want their vampires to hold different values. In V20, you can easily have a non-violent with a rather murder happy vampire playing together. Even following the same path like say Humanity. Their score will be different but the muderhobo will hardly feel the difference as long as he doesn't commit heinous crimes.<br /> <br /> Now try to create Tenets that encourage both kind of roleplay. Now create a table of not 2 but 5 players with very different vampires. Now make a Sabbat games where each have different path. See how V5 system crashes and burn.</div> </div> </div> </div>I'd argue that was a major source of tension in previous Chronicles actually. Because a vampire on Humanity and a vampire on a Path confused everyone and led to issues among games.<br /> <br /> Chronicle Tenets let's everypne know &quot;WHAT IS THIS GAME ABOUT?&quot;<br /> <br /> What are its themes?<br /> <br /> What are we dealing with?<br /> <br /> You and I both know some gamers HATE personal horror and run away screaming at any game that tries to do it.<br /> <br /> One of the worst games I ever did was a Technocracy Chronicle I said would be based on Resident Evil and told everyone it would be heavy combat and everyone should make big ass soldier characters. What did they make? A bunch of intellectuals and scientists. I was like, &quot;Did anyone bother checking to see what game this would be?&quot;","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Author of <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Cthulhu-Armageddon-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01KUOM7SI/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982844&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Cthulhu+Armageddon\" target=\"_blank\">Cthulhu Armageddon</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Teenage-Weredeer-Bright-Falls-Mysteries-ebook/dp/B075TTN2FN/ref=sr_1_2?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982717&amp;sr=1-2&amp;keywords=Weredeer#customerReviews\" target=\"_blank\">I was a Teenage Weredeer</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Straight-Outta-Fangton-Comedic-Vampire-ebook/dp/B01KNHICCC/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982774&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Straight+Outta+Fangton\" target=\"_blank\">Straight Outta Fangton</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Lucifers-Star-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01MDM9MCT/ref=mt_kindle?_encoding=UTF8&amp;me=&amp;qid=\" target=\"_blank\">Lucifer's Star</a>, </i>and the <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Rules-Supervillainy-Saga-Book-ebook/dp/B07MB89S33/\" target=\"_blank\">Supervillainy Saga</a>.</i><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":12002,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","user":"CTPhipps","date":". 05-04-2021, 08:18 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","name":"CTPhipps","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12002_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13933"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-05-04T17:23:18-07:00","id":1447493,"title":"","content":"Then we have different players.<br /> <br /> I had once a high humanity Tremere. She never used her powers offensively. In fact she pretty much was useless in combat, and that was on purpose. In everything else, she was a beast. (no pun)<br /> With Path of Blood, Technomancy, Auspex, Dominate (yes Domination was fair game), and high mental stats she was one hell of an investigator. And she was a more than adequate face with Dominate, Presence (yes she had that too) and good social scores.<br /> And of course High Humanity came handy for the social aspects.<br /> <br /> The rest of the group (One Brujah, One Nosferatu, One Gangrel) were more focused on the offensive but nobody thought that the Tremere was deadweight despite not participating in battle. She was just as usefull as the rest of the group. Perhaps the most important member of thre group even.<br /> <br /> I also once seen a Salubri in a Dark Age Sabbat games. Pretty fun. The Salubri was not very comfortable with the rest of the group, but survival make some strange bedfellows.<br /> <br /> Having players in different paths is not really an issue when they understand what they can take from each others. And yes it can lead to some interesting rp moments that V5 is sorely missing.<br /> <br /> Inner conflicts is also part of the personal horror afterall.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":24936,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24936-morbus","user":"Morbus","date":". 05-04-2021, 08:25 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24936-morbus","name":"Morbus","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"119"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-05-04T17:26:13-07:00","id":1447494,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Vilenecromancer</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1443592-the-official-v5-vs-v20-thread?p=1447489#post1447489\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">It's in the books, and says ST can do this with any dice pool. That said if you wanna say Contest/Conflicts don't count then I can also point you to page 305 <b>Knives in Their Smiles</b>. While it's more about the surrounding audience, it is still a modifier that can work. However that just gets into Golden Rule territory.</div> </div> </div> </div>And is, in fact, a central part of the problem. The advanced social conflict rules prejudice the system towards public displays of one upping each other, and against backroom dealing.<br /> <br /> Getting one successes to win a debate in front of the Prince does 6 WP damage, but 1 WP in private.<br /> <br /> This damages V5's ability to facilitate all sorts of political games because so much of politics is behind closed doors.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":6}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-05-04T17:29:15-07:00","id":1447495,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Heavy Arms</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1443592-the-official-v5-vs-v20-thread?p=1447494#post1447494\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> And is, in fact, a central part of the problem. The advanced social conflict rules prejudice the system towards public displays of one upping each other, and against backroom dealing.<br /> <br /> Getting one successes to win a debate in front of the Prince does 6 WP damage, but 1 WP in private.<br /> <br /> This damages V5's ability to facilitate all sorts of political games because so much of politics is behind closed doors.</div> </div> </div> </div>Is there a rule that outright gives you a modifier in V20? I don't know that system as well as V5.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\"><div align=\"left\"><a href=\"http://www.nodiatis.com/personality.htm\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://www.nodiatis.com/pub/7.jpg\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a></div></div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26764-vilenecromancer","name":"Vilenecromancer","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar26764_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"247"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-05-04T17:43:08-07:00","id":1447496,"title":"","content":"Having convincing evidence (real or not actually, but real is better) is a default modifier to the difficult of the Credibility roll to convince someone that you have dirt on them.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-05-04T17:56:17-07:00","id":1447500,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Heavy Arms</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1443592-the-official-v5-vs-v20-thread?p=1447496#post1447496\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Having convincing evidence (real or not actually, but real is better) is a default modifier to the difficult of the Credibility roll to convince someone that you have dirt on them.</div> </div> </div> </div>What page from the V20 book is that? Cause I can't find it.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\"><div align=\"left\"><a href=\"http://www.nodiatis.com/personality.htm\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://www.nodiatis.com/pub/7.jpg\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a></div></div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26764-vilenecromancer","name":"Vilenecromancer","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar26764_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"247"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-05-04T18:09:25-07:00","id":1447503,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CTPhipps</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1443592-the-official-v5-vs-v20-thread?p=1447471#post1447471\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I should point out my biggest issue with V5 is the fact that the katana and trenchcoat campaigns are far too easy in the new system. The combat is excellently fast and fluid here.<br /> <br /> Speaking as someone who also owns Diablerie 1 and 2, the point is the Methuselahs aren't fought at full power either because then they'd annihilate the PCs with a weave of their hand. Their stats were written in 1st Edition so they were all 1-5 anyway.<br /> <br /> You're correct the lack of Elder rules hurts using Ur-Shulgi but Ur-Shulgi should be beyond stats anyway.<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> I admit, I'm glad they made a reason Players would want to play 11th, 12th, and 13th generation or Thin bloods. There's now mechanical reasons that high generation Cainites aren't necessarily mass murdering monsters the way low generation ones always seem to be.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> I'm not mentioning the possible fight with the diner in the chronicles. But the whole dungeon crawling part. It isn't doable with the hunger system.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24043-nyremne","name":"Nyremne","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"414"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-05-04T18:48:12-07:00","id":1447509,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Nyremne</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1443592-the-official-v5-vs-v20-thread?p=1447503#post1447503\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> I'm not mentioning the possible fight with the diner in the chronicles. But the whole dungeon crawling part. It isn't doable with the hunger system.</div> </div> </div> </div>how do you figure?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Author of <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Cthulhu-Armageddon-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01KUOM7SI/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982844&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Cthulhu+Armageddon\" target=\"_blank\">Cthulhu Armageddon</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Teenage-Weredeer-Bright-Falls-Mysteries-ebook/dp/B075TTN2FN/ref=sr_1_2?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982717&amp;sr=1-2&amp;keywords=Weredeer#customerReviews\" target=\"_blank\">I was a Teenage Weredeer</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Straight-Outta-Fangton-Comedic-Vampire-ebook/dp/B01KNHICCC/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982774&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Straight+Outta+Fangton\" target=\"_blank\">Straight Outta Fangton</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Lucifers-Star-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01MDM9MCT/ref=mt_kindle?_encoding=UTF8&amp;me=&amp;qid=\" target=\"_blank\">Lucifer's Star</a>, </i>and the <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Rules-Supervillainy-Saga-Book-ebook/dp/B07MB89S33/\" target=\"_blank\">Supervillainy Saga</a>.</i><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","name":"CTPhipps","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12002_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13933"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-05-04T20:34:36-07:00","id":1447519,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Nyremne</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1443592-the-official-v5-vs-v20-thread?p=1447503#post1447503\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I'm not mentioning the possible fight with the diner in the chronicles. But the whole dungeon crawling part. It isn't doable with the hunger system.</div> </div> </div> </div><div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CTPhipps</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1443592-the-official-v5-vs-v20-thread?p=1447509#post1447509\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">how do you figure?</div> </div> </div> </div>You really don't see how having a quantifiable blood pool of 15 where you only have to start making frenzy checks due to hunger when you're down to about 3 and where you can refill a couple of points without a risk to a mortal would produce a different experience than one where, unless you're starting off a fresh murder, have at least one hunger die compromising your actions with messy crits and bestial failures and an indeterminate number of rouse checks before your hunger absolutely overwhelms you and drives you into situations where you end up slaughtering the people you're trying to protect will affect the type of adventurers you're having?<br /> <br /> I get that personal horror and vampires are monsters are like your most favorite thing ever which is probably why you can't see it, but the Vampions/Dungeon Crawl approach requires PCs with much more self-control than V5 allows the PCs to have. Understand that in such a campaign you're basically playing Angel from the Buffyverse, not someone on the verge of losing it to the Beast and committing an atrocity at any given moment. The mechanics of personal horror built into V5's hunger mechanics get in the way of a good &quot;superheroes with fangs&quot; story and so are a far from an ideal fit for playing in that style.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1328-chris24601","name":"Chris24601","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"520"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-05-04T21:34:19-07:00","id":1447523,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Chris24601</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1443592-the-official-v5-vs-v20-thread?p=1447519#post1447519\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> You really don't see how having a quantifiable blood pool of 15 where you only have to start making frenzy checks due to hunger when you're down to about 3 and where you can refill a couple of points without a risk to a mortal would produce a different experience than one where, unless you're starting off a fresh murder, have at least one hunger die compromising your actions with messy crits and bestial failures and an indeterminate number of rouse checks before your hunger absolutely overwhelms you and drives you into situations where you end up slaughtering the people you're trying to protect will affect the type of adventurers you're having?<br /> <br /> I get that personal horror and vampires are monsters are like your most favorite thing ever which is probably why you can't see it, but the Vampions/Dungeon Crawl approach requires PCs with much more self-control than V5 allows the PCs to have. Understand that in such a campaign you're basically playing Angel from the Buffyverse, not someone on the verge of losing it to the Beast and committing an atrocity at any given moment. The mechanics of personal horror built into V5's hunger mechanics get in the way of a good &quot;superheroes with fangs&quot; story and so are a far from an ideal fit for playing in that style.</div> </div> </div> </div>Yeah, that's what I was wondering because it's long since been proven that Rouse checks don't noticeably mean you're going to be frenzying that much more than before--especially during combat.<br /> <br /> You will probably run out of blood before you fail every single rouse check.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Author of <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Cthulhu-Armageddon-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01KUOM7SI/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982844&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Cthulhu+Armageddon\" target=\"_blank\">Cthulhu Armageddon</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Teenage-Weredeer-Bright-Falls-Mysteries-ebook/dp/B075TTN2FN/ref=sr_1_2?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982717&amp;sr=1-2&amp;keywords=Weredeer#customerReviews\" target=\"_blank\">I was a Teenage Weredeer</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Straight-Outta-Fangton-Comedic-Vampire-ebook/dp/B01KNHICCC/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982774&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Straight+Outta+Fangton\" target=\"_blank\">Straight Outta Fangton</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Lucifers-Star-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01MDM9MCT/ref=mt_kindle?_encoding=UTF8&amp;me=&amp;qid=\" target=\"_blank\">Lucifer's Star</a>, </i>and the <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Rules-Supervillainy-Saga-Book-ebook/dp/B07MB89S33/\" target=\"_blank\">Supervillainy Saga</a>.</i><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","name":"CTPhipps","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12002_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13933"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-05-04T22:25:02-07:00","id":1447525,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Vilenecromancer</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1443592-the-official-v5-vs-v20-thread?p=1447500#post1447500\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">What page from the V20 book is that? Cause I can't find it.</div> </div> </div> </div>Actually, I erred slightly that it's a penalty on the defender not a bonus to the one trying to be convincing. Page 265.<br /> <br /> Anyway, I really am not interesting in a citation debate on this. I wanted to do something I felt was a bit more illustrative than just quick one-line responses to illustrate one of the mechanical areas where V5 puts up a roadblock (and not even a vampire specific one) that didn't exist in the previous takes on the game. I could detail the general V20 rules where Difficulty and how to modify it is kept separate from different kinds of rolls, and even points out that Resisted roll offs can have different difficulties for each character rather than equal rolls where whoever gets the most successes wins.<br /> <br /> But that's really not that point, and this was something I was trying to avoid with my three point initial response. The V20 rules for social conflicts are hardly perfect, but I can actually use them to blackmail someone if in a bit of a clunky fashion. And blackmail and similar backroom manipulations are a staple of the political drama VtM traditionally has as a supported playstyle. V5 doesn't support it. At best the ST can make it work by stretching a rule to something that borders up on the Golden Rule (which is a good use of it for sure, but as noted something we're trying to avoid).","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-05-04T23:58:20-07:00","id":1447529,"title":"","content":"I admit, the biggest regret I have of Modiphius losing their license is the fact that I do think this significantly delayed Werewolf: The Apocalypse V5. I think all of the various books should be updated to 5th Edition with a more crossover-friendly feel.<br /> <br /> Mind you, given my suspicions that the Companion is what was done with the V5 Players Guide, I have the suspicion nothing at all was done for Werewolf.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Author of <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Cthulhu-Armageddon-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01KUOM7SI/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982844&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Cthulhu+Armageddon\" target=\"_blank\">Cthulhu Armageddon</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Teenage-Weredeer-Bright-Falls-Mysteries-ebook/dp/B075TTN2FN/ref=sr_1_2?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982717&amp;sr=1-2&amp;keywords=Weredeer#customerReviews\" target=\"_blank\">I was a Teenage Weredeer</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Straight-Outta-Fangton-Comedic-Vampire-ebook/dp/B01KNHICCC/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982774&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Straight+Outta+Fangton\" target=\"_blank\">Straight Outta Fangton</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Lucifers-Star-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01MDM9MCT/ref=mt_kindle?_encoding=UTF8&amp;me=&amp;qid=\" target=\"_blank\">Lucifer's Star</a>, </i>and the <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Rules-Supervillainy-Saga-Book-ebook/dp/B07MB89S33/\" target=\"_blank\">Supervillainy Saga</a>.</i><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","name":"CTPhipps","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12002_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13933"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-05-05T01:10:08-07:00","id":1447537,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Heavy Arms</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1443592-the-official-v5-vs-v20-thread?p=1447447#post1447447\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> While I don't mean this to be personally aimed at you, given how this sort of question has gone repeatedly in the past, can you promise not to respond to any examples with any of the following as reasons V5 really &quot;can&quot; do said stories?<br /> <br /> 1) The Golden Rule.<br /> 2) House rules and/or homebrew.<br /> 3) Trust the future books, including announced ones, are going to solve any issues.<br /> <br /> Because the number of times we've tried to highlight this, and then just got into debates about one or all of the above, has gotten exhausting.</div> </div> </div> </div><div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Vilenecromancer</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1443592-the-official-v5-vs-v20-thread?p=1447483#post1447483\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> There's just 1 problem with your story, there are dice bonus and difficulty modifiers. to quote the book on page 120, &quot;The Storyteller might decide to add or subtract a modifier to <b>any</b> dice pool.&quot;<br /> <br /> On that same page, the book then goes on to explain the options for the ST to use. As per RAW, there are potentially bonus dice and difficulty changes to any dice pool based on situational things and RP. Granted, it doesn't list off how much or how little, but that gets into ST preference.</div> </div> </div> </div><div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CTPhipps</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1443592-the-official-v5-vs-v20-thread?p=1447488#post1447488\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Yes, you need a Sabbat book to do the Sabbat, which I trust Justin Achilli to make. So I'm glad that is getting rectified.</div> </div> </div> </div><div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Vilenecromancer</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1443592-the-official-v5-vs-v20-thread?p=1447489#post1447489\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">It's in the books, and says ST can do this with any dice pool. That said if you wanna say Contest/Conflicts don't count then I can also point you to page 305 <b>Knives in Their Smiles</b>. While it's more about the surrounding audience, it is still a modifier that can work. However that just gets into Golden Rule territory.</div> </div> </div> </div>Heavy Arms said these types of responses were tiresome, yet you went there anyway. This is why discussing these things gets so fraught because it feels like arguing in bad faith sometimes. The default responses are always, 'You're playing it wrong!' 'Wait for the upcoming supplement!' 'Golden Rule it...'","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Writer, publisher, performer<br /> Mostly he/his, sometimes she/her IRL <a href=\"https://adam-lowe.com\" target=\"_blank\">https://adam-lowe.com</a>","edited":{"userid":5291,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5291-adambeyoncelowe","user":"adambeyoncelowe","date":". 05-05-2021, 04:27 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":10}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5291-adambeyoncelowe","name":"adambeyoncelowe","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5291_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2802"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-05-05T01:15:17-07:00","id":1447539,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CTPhipps</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1443592-the-official-v5-vs-v20-thread?p=1447529#post1447529\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Mind you, given my suspicions that the Companion is what was done with the V5 Players Guide, I have the suspicion nothing at all was done for Werewolf.</div> </div> </div> </div>The impression I got from the writers on the Hunters entertainment Discord wa that they were very eager to move on it but that Paradox essentially went incommunicado almost immediately after granting them the license.<br /> <br /> Probably because they had at that point already decided to bring things back in house.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26564-badfurryfanfic","name":"BadFurryFanFic","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2020"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"93"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-05-05T01:16:11-07:00","id":1447540,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>adambeyoncelowe</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1443592-the-official-v5-vs-v20-thread?p=1447537#post1447537\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Heavy Arms said these types of responses were tiresome, yet you went there anyway. This is why discussing these things gets so fraught because if feels like arguing in bad faith sometimes. The default responses are always, 'You're playing it wrong!' 'Wait for the upcoming supplement!' 'Golden Rule it...'</div> </div> </div> </div>I think that's a weird way to take it versus, &quot;Yes, it's a problem. We agree. I'm glad it's getting fixed.&quot;<br /> <br /> If no one is defending it, there's no point in arguing about it.<br /> <br /> If you're asking for an opinion, it's pretty universal, &quot;Yeah, the Sabbat should be here.&quot;","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Author of <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Cthulhu-Armageddon-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01KUOM7SI/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982844&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Cthulhu+Armageddon\" target=\"_blank\">Cthulhu Armageddon</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Teenage-Weredeer-Bright-Falls-Mysteries-ebook/dp/B075TTN2FN/ref=sr_1_2?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982717&amp;sr=1-2&amp;keywords=Weredeer#customerReviews\" target=\"_blank\">I was a Teenage Weredeer</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Straight-Outta-Fangton-Comedic-Vampire-ebook/dp/B01KNHICCC/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982774&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Straight+Outta+Fangton\" target=\"_blank\">Straight Outta Fangton</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Lucifers-Star-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01MDM9MCT/ref=mt_kindle?_encoding=UTF8&amp;me=&amp;qid=\" target=\"_blank\">Lucifer's Star</a>, </i>and the <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Rules-Supervillainy-Saga-Book-ebook/dp/B07MB89S33/\" target=\"_blank\">Supervillainy Saga</a>.</i><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","name":"CTPhipps","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12002_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13933"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-05-05T01:28:57-07:00","id":1447542,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CTPhipps</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1443592-the-official-v5-vs-v20-thread?p=1447540#post1447540\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I think that's a weird way to take it versus, &amp;quot;Yes, it's a problem. We agree. I'm glad it's getting fixed.&amp;quot;<br /> <br /> If no one is defending it, there's no point in arguing about it.<br /> <br /> If you're asking for an opinion, it's pretty universal, &amp;quot;Yeah, the Sabbat should be here.&amp;quot;</div> </div> </div> </div>I'll admit it's hard to read the tone of your posts sometimes. If I made a mistake reading it there, then I apologise. If we're agreed, then all the better.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Writer, publisher, performer<br /> Mostly he/his, sometimes she/her IRL <a href=\"https://adam-lowe.com\" target=\"_blank\">https://adam-lowe.com</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5291-adambeyoncelowe","name":"adambeyoncelowe","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5291_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2802"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-05-05T01:42:34-07:00","id":1447544,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>adambeyoncelowe</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1443592-the-official-v5-vs-v20-thread?p=1447537#post1447537\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> Heavy Arms said these types of responses were tiresome, yet you went there anyway. This is why discussing these things gets so fraught because if feels like arguing in bad faith sometimes. The default responses are always, 'You're playing it wrong!' 'Wait for the upcoming supplement!' 'Golden Rule it...'</div> </div> </div> </div>Annoyingly I think Vilemancer is in the right there. That's not the golden rule, that's a rule. <br /> <br /> But as to his original question? How can it not be obvious? <br /> <br /> A high stakes political game with Suave vampires working among mortals? Can't do it. Messy criticals pose too much of a problem. <br /> <br /> wanna gain money and power fast? do you have the XP? want to deprive someone else of their resources? Well I'll have you know they spent XP on those dots, so good luck there. <br /> <br /> Want to reach 10 humanity and then Golconda/becomeHuman? Hahahahahahahahaha GO FUCK YOURSELF. That's at least 190xp for the best two dots, and you better not screw it up. <br /> <br /> want to Diablerise your way to ultimate power? Think again, blood potency will make you starve. <br /> <br /> Want to play a Samedi? You got Hecata'd. <br /> Brujah in the cam? You can kinda do it, as a second class citizen. <br /> Settite? Heretic either way. <br /> <br /> Wanna play a farmer who isnt a vegan? nah. <br /> <br /> want to wear body armour to give you an advantage in a realisti combat? No benefits. rules say Steel is air when you wear it. <br /> Wanna trade blows and take advantage of your immortal physique? Combat is all or nothing.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":7}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25794-mywifeisscary","name":"MyWifeIsScary","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25794_2.png","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3711"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-05-05T02:08:27-07:00","id":1447546,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MyWifeIsScary</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1443592-the-official-v5-vs-v20-thread?p=1447544#post1447544\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Annoyingly I think Vilemancer is in the right there. That's not the golden rule, that's a rule.</div> </div> </div> </div>I think the point about social modifiers in V5 is that they privilege public humiliation. Vilemancer was incorrect about those, as adding modifiers for private blackmail would be strictly Golden Rule territory. <br /> <br /> From p.305:<br /> <br /> 'Willpower damage hurts most when others see <br /> your weakness. Add a damage modifier depending on the audience (just being present doesn\u2019t cut it, they also need to be interested in the outcome).'<br /> <br /> RAW, p.120 allows you to modify the 'difficulty' of a social roll, but that implies a simple test (not a contest), as you don't use difficulties for opposed rolls, as Heavy Arms said. It says nothing about adding dice for contests. Perhaps it was RAI and has been clarified elsewhere, but the CRB text doesn't support that, as written.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Writer, publisher, performer<br /> Mostly he/his, sometimes she/her IRL <a href=\"https://adam-lowe.com\" target=\"_blank\">https://adam-lowe.com</a>","edited":{"userid":5291,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5291-adambeyoncelowe","user":"adambeyoncelowe","date":". 05-05-2021, 05:13 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5291-adambeyoncelowe","name":"adambeyoncelowe","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5291_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2802"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-05-05T02:52:46-07:00","id":1447553,"title":"","content":"Also, you know, if you accept that the ST can just give you bonus dice for having blackmail material, the ST can just give you bonus dice on defensive rolls to make up for armor doing jack shit in a large number of circumstances even though that's nowhere in the advanced combat rules.<br /> <br /> And I could have stacked the deck in all sorta of ways here (given the NPCs 5s in Att + Skill + Presence with Daunt as the level 1 power so they're rolling 15 dice + Surge and completely over shadowed some bonus dice) too. But that's the tedium I'm trying to avoid.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-05-05T02:54:53-07:00","id":1447554,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>adambeyoncelowe</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1443592-the-official-v5-vs-v20-thread?p=1447542#post1447542\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I'll admit it's hard to read the tone of your posts sometimes. If I made a mistake reading it there, then I apologise. If we're agreed, then all the better.</div> </div> </div> </div>Well for clarity's sake, I feel that the biggest flaw of V5 has always been not having all Clans available in the main book.<br /> <br /> The second biggest being the Sabbat not being developed for V5.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Author of <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Cthulhu-Armageddon-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01KUOM7SI/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982844&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Cthulhu+Armageddon\" target=\"_blank\">Cthulhu Armageddon</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Teenage-Weredeer-Bright-Falls-Mysteries-ebook/dp/B075TTN2FN/ref=sr_1_2?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982717&amp;sr=1-2&amp;keywords=Weredeer#customerReviews\" target=\"_blank\">I was a Teenage Weredeer</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Straight-Outta-Fangton-Comedic-Vampire-ebook/dp/B01KNHICCC/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982774&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Straight+Outta+Fangton\" target=\"_blank\">Straight Outta Fangton</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Lucifers-Star-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01MDM9MCT/ref=mt_kindle?_encoding=UTF8&amp;me=&amp;qid=\" target=\"_blank\">Lucifer's Star</a>, </i>and the <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Rules-Supervillainy-Saga-Book-ebook/dp/B07MB89S33/\" target=\"_blank\">Supervillainy Saga</a>.</i><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","name":"CTPhipps","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12002_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13933"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-05-05T03:28:36-07:00","id":1447556,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CTPhipps</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1443592-the-official-v5-vs-v20-thread?p=1447523#post1447523\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">You will probably run out of blood before you fail every single rouse check.</div> </div> </div> </div>Also.... got caught up in other thoughts but... what? When was this ever &quot;proven?&quot;<br /> <br /> A Hunger 1 vampire has a ~6% chance of hitting Hunger 5 with just four Rouses. At seven Rouses it's a dead 50/50 on hitting Hunger 5. At nine Rouses it's ~75%. You are absolutely more likely to hit Hunger 5 via Rousing faster you'd run out of vitae with Blood Points even with just 10 of them. There's a chance you might come out without your Hunger maxed out, but the odds are not in your favor. Also, a bad series of rolls means you can hit Hunger 5 way before a per-V5 vampire would be feeling any sort of pressure.<br /> <br /> And it's not like Hunger 3-4 are walks in the park either with the massively increased odds of Messy Crits and any failures you get becoming Bestial ones.<br /> <br /> Yeah, you might not Frenzy as often because V5 made Frenzies more rare to make room for Messy Crits and Compulsions, but that's not because Rousing is &quot;safe.&quot;","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":6}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-05-05T05:46:19-07:00","id":1447566,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CTPhipps</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1443592-the-official-v5-vs-v20-thread?p=1447554#post1447554\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Well for clarity's sake, I feel that the biggest flaw of V5 has always been not having all Clans available in the main book.<br /> <br /> The second biggest being the Sabbat not being developed for V5.</div> </div> </div> </div>You're right and you've said this before, which I did know because I've seen you say it in this very thread. So I apologise for misreading what you said.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Writer, publisher, performer<br /> Mostly he/his, sometimes she/her IRL <a href=\"https://adam-lowe.com\" target=\"_blank\">https://adam-lowe.com</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5291-adambeyoncelowe","name":"adambeyoncelowe","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5291_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2802"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-05-05T05:59:00-07:00","id":1447568,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Heavy Arms</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1443592-the-official-v5-vs-v20-thread?p=1447556#post1447556\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Also.... got caught up in other thoughts but... what? When was this ever &quot;proven?&quot;<br /> <br /> A Hunger 1 vampire has a ~6% chance of hitting Hunger 5 with just four Rouses. At seven Rouses it's a dead 50/50 on hitting Hunger 5. At nine Rouses it's ~75%. You are absolutely more likely to hit Hunger 5 via Rousing faster you'd run out of vitae with Blood Points even with just 10 of them. There's a chance you might come out without your Hunger maxed out, but the odds are not in your favor. Also, a bad series of rolls means you can hit Hunger 5 way before a per-V5 vampire would be feeling any sort of pressure.<br /> <br /> And it's not like Hunger 3-4 are walks in the park either with the massively increased odds of Messy Crits and any failures you get becoming Bestial ones.<br /> <br /> Yeah, you might not Frenzy as often because V5 made Frenzies more rare to make room for Messy Crits and Compulsions, but that's not because Rousing is &quot;safe.&quot;</div> </div> </div> </div>There\u2019s also just the flat-out uncertainty of it.<br /> <br /> I don\u2019t know how familiar Phipps is with dungeon-crawl style play, but a key element of it is resource management. You only have X spells, arrows, torches, etc. so you have to evaluate when is the best time to use them.<br /> <br /> That works with Blood Points. It does not work with Rouse checks. Starting from Hunger 1 (because you\u2019re a Vampion, not a murderer) there is a non-trivial chance someone at your table will be sucking Hunger 5 in just four checks (6% may not sound like much, but factor in multiple players across multiple sessions and that 6% quickly becomes absolute certainty... like the night I was GMing D&amp;D and my d20s wouldn\u2019t roll above a 4 the entire night; flukes happen in probability) while another player might get twenty or more before because their dice keep coming up 6+.<br /> <br /> Rouse checks rob you of the ability to plan and manage resources because you cannot manage your resources. Even if sometimes it lasts longer than a specified number of blood points, sometimes it doesn\u2019t and you can\u2019t know which it will be.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CTPhipps</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1443592-the-official-v5-vs-v20-thread?p=1447471#post1447471\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I should point out my biggest issue with V5 is the fact that the katana and trenchcoat campaigns are far too easy in the new system. The combat is excellently fast and fluid here.</div> </div> </div> </div>Too fast and too abstract for a combat focused game really. V20 didn\u2019t include combat manuevers with modifiers for no reason. M20 didn\u2019t massively expand on those basic manuevers for both Martial Arts and Do because they expected everyone to brush past combat in just three rolls. \u201cCombat: The Big Book of Beating Ass\u201d is not sitting on my shelf because I want abstract combat resolution.<br /> <br /> As the excellent genre game Feng Shui advises for a fighting game \u201cdesign three interesting fights, then wrap a plot around them.\u201d To put it another way... we don\u2019t watch Godzilla vs. Kong for the human plotlines. We\u2019re there to watch giant monsters wreck stuff.<br /> <br /> I\u2019m sure V5\u2019s combat system works fantastically for LARPs and non-combat focused campaigns where the only interest is in resolving the fight to get back to what most people are interested in. But when you\u2019re there FOR the fights its thin gruel at best.<br /> <br /> This is why people say that V5\u2019s mechanics are tailored primarily to only one type of play; street level (which is why Elders don\u2019t need the big flashy powers), non-combat focused (which is why combat is focused on being resolved in, at most, three tests) with a focus on personal horror (messy criticals and bestial failures emphasizing your lack of control over yourself that only murder can fully quell).<br /> <br /> The more a campaign\u2019s play deviates from those, the harder time V5 has producing satisfying results; so a combat-focused elder Vampions game is just not going to play well with V5\u2019s mechanics which are tuned to cater to the opposite.<br /> <br /> ETA: there\u2019s nothing wrong with a very focused system. I generally prefer them to generic systems when playing a specific genre as the mechanics are designed to support the genre. But they are NOT generic systems that can handle all genres nearly as well. V20 is more of a generic toolkit approach to the vampire genre and so does specific sub-genres less well because it has to support the others. V5 is hyper-focused on one particular vampire subgenre and does that very well, but at the expense of handling other subgenres as well.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1328,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1328-chris24601","user":"Chris24601","date":". 05-05-2021, 09:12 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":7}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1328-chris24601","name":"Chris24601","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"520"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-05-05T07:35:04-07:00","id":1447574,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>adambeyoncelowe</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1443592-the-official-v5-vs-v20-thread?p=1447546#post1447546\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I think the point about social modifiers in V5 is that they privilege public humiliation. Vilemancer was incorrect about those, as adding modifiers for private blackmail would be strictly Golden Rule territory. <br /> <br /> From p.305:<br /> <br /> 'Willpower damage hurts most when others see <br /> your weakness. Add a damage modifier depending on the audience (just being present doesn\u2019t cut it, they also need to be interested in the outcome).'<br /> <br /> RAW, p.120 allows you to modify the 'difficulty' of a social roll, but that implies a simple test (not a contest), as you don't use difficulties for opposed rolls, as Heavy Arms said. It says nothing about adding dice for contests. Perhaps it was RAI and has been clarified elsewhere, but the CRB text doesn't support that, as written.</div> </div> </div> </div>You can also modify the dice pool itself per the rules of 120, aka the dice an attacker or defender's rolls. This isn't part of the golden rule, but true to the RAW. However, the conversation went from a conversation or debate to what feels like an argument. I just wanted to understand more about another pov, but have to say I am even more confused then before.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\"><div align=\"left\"><a href=\"http://www.nodiatis.com/personality.htm\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://www.nodiatis.com/pub/7.jpg\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a></div></div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26764-vilenecromancer","name":"Vilenecromancer","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar26764_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"247"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-05-05T08:55:31-07:00","id":1447582,"title":"","content":"From p.120:<br /> <br /> 'Especially when dealing with social actions, such as seduction or diplomacy, don\u2019t force the dice into the path of the roleplaying. If a player has their character say something particularly inspired (or painfully wrong), open with a truly tempting (or utterly insulting) gambit, or offer a cunning (or transparently false) explanation, the Storyteller should feel free to modify the Difficulty or even let the character succeed (or fail) without involving dice and Traits.'<br /> <br /> So there's some of the usual WoD thing of 'make this up if you like', but the only concrete rule here is that you can change the Difficulty (which means changing the target number of successes). Crucially, that whole section is titled 'Simple Tests', so doesn't cover contests.<br /> <br /> Difficulty is a capitalised game term and is described on the very next page thus: 'The Storyteller determines the Difficulty of the action you\u2019re attempting, expressed in terms of how many successes you need to win, i.e. to accomplish that action.'<br /> <br /> Now, you can make a simple test instead of a contest if the ST rules it, and wants to simplify things. But again, that's an invitation to use your discretion as the ST rather than a solid rule.<br /> <br /> WoD games have always done this, of course. They often say 'wing it'. But this does seem to be an oversight, pointed out by Heavy Arms to make the point specifically because you asked for examples.<br /> <br /> I think there are other examples given in this thread, though. For example, hunting elders a la the Diablerie books is significantly different now. Before, they often had Disciplines and Traits at 6+ and woke up from torpor with pretty devastating traits already. Heck, the impulse to diablerise was much stronger because there was no Blood Potency.<br /> <br /> At the moment, you also can't really play the Sabbat. Though we have the two main pillar clans, we have no explicit info about what state the Sabbat is in, except 'put on a bus (for now)'. You can't play the Paths of Enlightenment. At all. Or the Tal'mahe'Ra. Or most Bloodlines. Those are all very specific things you can't do with V5 yet. <br /> <br /> You also can't do the same things with many Disciplines, since they've given loads of them the chop or rolled them into others, and you're specifically only allowed one power per dot (so it's impossible to have a Tzimisce who also knows Protean, since those are the same Discipline now, and you have to choose between Fleshcrafting or melding with the Earth and turning into a wolf, etc).<br /> <br /> These are all options removed from the game. Not just fixed or cleared up but removed. So games that made use of these elements aren't possible RAW. And there's been a slow pace of output, so it's not necessarily happening soon.<br /> <br /> This has all been said before, but you said you wanted examples so I assume you haven't read everything posted on this topic (it is 34 pages after all!).","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Writer, publisher, performer<br /> Mostly he/his, sometimes she/her IRL <a href=\"https://adam-lowe.com\" target=\"_blank\">https://adam-lowe.com</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5291-adambeyoncelowe","name":"adambeyoncelowe","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5291_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2802"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-05-05T09:32:47-07:00","id":1447586,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>adambeyoncelowe</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1443592-the-official-v5-vs-v20-thread?p=1447582#post1447582\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><b>From p.120:</b><br /> <br /> 'Especially when dealing with social actions, such as seduction or diplomacy, don\u2019t force the dice into the path of the roleplaying. If a player has their character say something particularly inspired (or painfully wrong), open with a truly tempting (or utterly insulting) gambit, or offer a cunning (or transparently false) explanation, the Storyteller should feel free to modify the Difficulty or even let the character succeed (or fail) without involving dice and Traits.'<br /> <br /> So there's some of the usual WoD thing of 'make this up if you like', but the only concrete rule here is that you can change the Difficulty (which means changing the target number of successes). Crucially, that whole section is titled 'Simple Tests', so doesn't cover contests.<br /> <br /> Difficulty is a capitalised game term and is described on the very next page thus: 'The Storyteller determines the Difficulty of the action you\u2019re attempting, expressed in terms of how many successes you need to win, i.e. to accomplish that action.'<br /> <br /> Now, you can make a simple test instead of a contest if the ST rules it, and wants to simplify things. But again, that's an invitation to use your discretion as the ST rather than a solid rule.<br /> <br /> WoD games have always done this, of course. They often say 'wing it'. But this does seem to be an oversight, pointed out by Heavy Arms to make the point specifically because you asked for examples.<br /> <br /> I think there are other examples given in this thread, though. For example, hunting elders a la the Diablerie books is significantly different now. Before, they often had Disciplines and Traits at 6+ and woke up from torpor with pretty devastating traits already. Heck, the impulse to diablerise was much stronger because there was no Blood Potency.<br /> <br /> At the moment, you also can't really play the Sabbat. Though we have the two main pillar clans, we have no explicit info about what state the Sabbat is in, except 'put on a bus (for now)'. You can't play the Paths of Enlightenment. At all. Or the Tal'mahe'Ra. Or most Bloodlines. Those are all very specific things you can't do with V5 yet.<br /> <br /> You also can't do the same things with many Disciplines, since they've given loads of them the chop or rolled them into others, and you're specifically only allowed one power per dot (so it's impossible to have a Tzimisce who also knows Protean, since those are the same Discipline now, and you have to choose between Fleshcrafting or melding with the Earth and turning into a wolf, etc).<br /> <br /> These are all options removed from the game. Not just fixed or cleared up but removed. So games that made use of these elements aren't possible RAW. And there's been a slow pace of output, so it's not necessarily happening soon.<br /> <br /> This has all been said before, but you said you wanted examples so I assume you haven't read everything posted on this topic (it is 34 pages after all!).</div> </div> </div> </div>Hmmm, a lot more enlightening thank you. However, you misquoted where that quote was from. That quote is from page 118, which leads me to believe that the section I was referencing wasn't even read at all, which is on page 120 which is: <br /> <i>&quot;Change the size of the dice pool. This modifier reflects a change or circumstance for the character: they are drugged, they use a specialty, they appear terrifying, etc.&quot;</i><br /> <br /> However the other parts of your argument do make some sense. I do ultimately agree with you that V20 has more options, and as a result can tell more stories without relying on the Golden Rule. However, V20 isn't &quot;better&quot; and neither is V5, because V20 has just as many flaws as V5 if you don't look at the Golden Rule. Neither system is &quot;better&quot;, and that's okay.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\"><div align=\"left\"><a href=\"http://www.nodiatis.com/personality.htm\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://www.nodiatis.com/pub/7.jpg\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a></div></div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26764-vilenecromancer","name":"Vilenecromancer","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar26764_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"247"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-05-05T10:58:55-07:00","id":1447599,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Chris24601</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1443592-the-official-v5-vs-v20-thread?p=1447568#post1447568\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Rouse checks rob you of the ability to plan and manage resources because you cannot manage your resources. Even if sometimes it lasts longer than a specified number of blood points, sometimes it doesn\u2019t and you can\u2019t know which it will be.</div> </div> </div> </div>I don't think randomized resource results are incompatible with management as a concept. Rouses are just far too statistically punishing for any sort of endurance biased scenario.<br /> <br /> Ammo checks are a fairly common replacement for counting each arrow/bullet/etc. these days because a simple test is a lot less work than tracking every shot and then whatever mechanics to recover ammo if that's possible (either arrows that can be reused, or looting, or whatever). But deciding how many reloads your character has (which can be a combination of character aptitudes and equipment limitations), as well as ammo checks being trait based instead of a flat roll for all characters (so if you're making a ranged weapon fighter, you can make sure to invest in things that boost your ammo checks to make them more reliable and easier to manage).<br /> <br /> The problem with Rousing is that there's extremely little you can do about how harsh the default math is. Increasing your BP only helps with Discipline based Rouses, and makes it harder to keep your base level Hunger as low as possible. You can't do things like buy Stamina to make your Rousing more efficient. A 13th Gen neonate, and a 4th Gen methuselah that surge four times in a row are looking at the exact same math (and that's with the 4th gen is actually worse because if they don't murder people, they're at Hunger 2 instead of Hunger 1 by default and that's if they keep their BP at its lowest).<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Vilenecromancer</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1443592-the-official-v5-vs-v20-thread?p=1447586#post1447586\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"> However, V20 isn't &quot;better&quot; and neither is V5, because V20 has just as many flaws as V5 if you don't look at the Golden Rule. Neither system is &quot;better&quot;, and that's okay.</div> </div> </div> </div>Have you actually counted all the flaws in both? I know, it's an absurdity.<br /> <br /> The point isn't some sort of &quot;objective better&quot; because you can't objectively count flaws like that either. Subjectively, based on what people want out of the game, there are different better and worse choices for them.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-05-05T11:38:11-07:00","id":1447606,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Heavy Arms</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1443592-the-official-v5-vs-v20-thread?p=1447599#post1447599\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Have you actually counted all the flaws in both? I know, it's an absurdity.<br /> <br /> The point isn't some sort of &quot;objective better&quot; because you can't objectively count flaws like that either. Subjectively, based on what people want out of the game, there are different better and worse choices for them.</div> </div> </div> </div>That's what I was trying to say mate.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\"><div align=\"left\"><a href=\"http://www.nodiatis.com/personality.htm\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://www.nodiatis.com/pub/7.jpg\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a></div></div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26764-vilenecromancer","name":"Vilenecromancer","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar26764_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"247"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-05-05T11:47:03-07:00","id":1447609,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Vilenecromancer</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1443592-the-official-v5-vs-v20-thread?p=1447586#post1447586\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I do ultimately agree with you that V20 has more options, and as a result can tell more stories without relying on the Golden Rule. However, V20 isn't &amp;quot;better&amp;quot; and neither is V5, because V20 has just as many flaws as V5 if you don't look at the Golden Rule. Neither system is &amp;quot;better&amp;quot;, and that's okay.</div> </div> </div> </div>I think you can fairly say that V20 is better at being a generic toolkit for many types of vampire stories and V5 is better at the particular subgenre its developers chose to focus on... and therefore you can make a judgement on which will be better for the campaign you wish to run.<br /> <br /> I think if you had to only pick one or the other then V20 is the better choice because it can do okay with a V5-themed campaign in addition to doing okay at many others which gives you flexibility for making later campaigns not feel as repetitive. But barring some extreme \u201ctrapped on a desert island\u201d with only one RPG*\u201d circumstances you don\u2019t have to pick one or the other so its almost always a non-issue.<br /> <br /> * in which case I\u2019d pick an even more generic systems like Mutants &amp; Masterminds anyway.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1328-chris24601","name":"Chris24601","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"520"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-05-05T14:02:39-07:00","id":1447625,"title":"","content":"Honestly I find V5 worse for personal horror. Messy criticals scare me... out of wanting to roll dice. They make vampires very, very passive. Or you can accept you have no control and laugh at the storyteller every time he describes what might otherwise have been your character screwing things up. You can't reasonably lower your hunger dice to 0, so it's not your fault when one goes off and you screw things up. Hell, If you kill someone to cover it up, it's still better than killing to avoid the problem in the forst place. <br /> <br /> Oh yeah and elders aren't so scary anymore and vampire society isnt plagued with a lack of upward mobility so that's a kick in the balls to this idea of 'horror'","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25794-mywifeisscary","name":"MyWifeIsScary","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25794_2.png","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3711"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-05-05T15:09:34-07:00","id":1447639,"title":"","content":"That somewhat depends what you want out of a personal horror <b>game</b>.<br /> <br /> In terms of the general concepts of personal horror, V5 produces genre appropriate results. &quot;I am horrified by the things I was forced to do under mind control,&quot; is a staple of personal horror stories, because the key aspect of personal horror is the negative emotional reaction of a character towards themselves; they don't have to be directly responsible.<br /> <br /> The problems that you're talking about are in the process of gamifying personal horror. In a game, agency is important to having a fulfilling experience; even in situations where the character might not have much agency, the player expects to be able to exercise decision making powers (otherwise they're just listening to the ST narrate what happens).<br /> <br /> So, it's a bit less the in-universe issues of the characters being able to say, &quot;the Beast made me do it!&quot; and having a point, or that Elders aren't there to be scary, but that the players have no real say in how this occurs. The inability to meaningfully engage withe the horror elements as a player makes it very hard to create a personal horror game, even if the system produces valid personal horror stories.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":6}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-05-05T16:37:59-07:00","id":1447657,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Heavy Arms</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1443592-the-official-v5-vs-v20-thread?p=1447639#post1447639\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">That somewhat depends what you want out of a personal horror <b>game</b>.<br /> <br /> In terms of the general concepts of personal horror, V5 produces genre appropriate results. &quot;I am horrified by the things I was forced to do under mind control,&quot; is a staple of personal horror stories, because the key aspect of personal horror is the negative emotional reaction of a character towards themselves; they don't have to be directly responsible.<br /> <br /> The problems that you're talking about are in the process of gamifying personal horror. In a game, agency is important to having a fulfilling experience; even in situations where the character might not have much agency, the player expects to be able to exercise decision making powers (otherwise they're just listening to the ST narrate what happens).<br /> <br /> So, it's a bit less the in-universe issues of the characters being able to say, &quot;the Beast made me do it!&quot; and having a point, or that Elders aren't there to be scary, but that the players have no real say in how this occurs. The inability to meaningfully engage withe the horror elements as a player makes it very hard to create a personal horror game, even if the system produces valid personal horror stories.</div> </div> </div> </div>I have sadly to agree her. With all these messy crits I am really horrifyed. Problem is it too effective. It really makes me unconfortable playing near humans. Which is a problem because with new feeding restrictions I can not really stay in wildnis and even if I can, it really affects the game I could play.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>As I am from Austria I need to clarify two things.<br /> First my native language is german and so please point out if the english I write is broken so I can improve.<br /> Second I do not own VTMV beyond first three books nor any line after M20 Corebook because it is not out there and I wait for the translation.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26160-koronus","name":"Koronus","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2020"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"366"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-05-05T17:07:24-07:00","id":1447663,"title":"","content":"It\u2019s kind of a pity that the Beast is so animalistic, because I think a lot of mileage on Personal Horror could be gained from an approach similar to how Wraith has other players run a PC\u2019s Shadow so it\u2019s NOT just the GM dictating what happens, another player is deciding what the Beast is doing.<br /> <br /> On the more \u201cI trust my players to roleplay properly\u201d is just allow the player to control their PC even as they lose control with the understanding that they\u2019re supposed to be roleplaying someone who has lost control.<br /> <br /> It\u2019s a shame that frenzies and messy crits/bestial fails are so binary. Having the Beast instead manifest as stacking penalties to rational acts while predatory acts don\u2019t take penalties and burn off the penalties to rational acts. So the PC maintains control, but can either flail about ineffectively due to penalties or burn off the penalities by taking predatory acts.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1328-chris24601","name":"Chris24601","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"520"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-05-05T17:17:39-07:00","id":1447665,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Chris24601</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1443592-the-official-v5-vs-v20-thread?p=1447663#post1447663\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">It\u2019s kind of a pity that the Beast is so animalistic, because I think a lot of mileage on Personal Horror could be gained from an approach similar to how Wraith has other players run a PC\u2019s Shadow so it\u2019s NOT just the GM dictating what happens, another player is deciding what the Beast is doing.<br /> <br /> On the more \u201cI trust my players to roleplay properly\u201d is just allow the player to control their PC even as they lose control with the understanding that they\u2019re supposed to be roleplaying someone who has lost control.<br /> <br /> It\u2019s a shame that frenzies and messy crits/bestial fails are so binary. Having the Beast instead manifest as stacking penalties to rational acts while predatory acts don\u2019t take penalties and burn off the penalties to rational acts. So the PC maintains control, but can either flail about ineffectively due to penalties or burn off the penalities by taking predatory acts.</div> </div> </div> </div>Jason Carl notably has been doing that in LA BY NIGHT as he has the Beast's internal dialogue take the form of people that terrify the players.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Author of <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Cthulhu-Armageddon-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01KUOM7SI/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982844&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Cthulhu+Armageddon\" target=\"_blank\">Cthulhu Armageddon</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Teenage-Weredeer-Bright-Falls-Mysteries-ebook/dp/B075TTN2FN/ref=sr_1_2?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982717&amp;sr=1-2&amp;keywords=Weredeer#customerReviews\" target=\"_blank\">I was a Teenage Weredeer</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Straight-Outta-Fangton-Comedic-Vampire-ebook/dp/B01KNHICCC/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982774&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Straight+Outta+Fangton\" target=\"_blank\">Straight Outta Fangton</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Lucifers-Star-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01MDM9MCT/ref=mt_kindle?_encoding=UTF8&amp;me=&amp;qid=\" target=\"_blank\">Lucifer's Star</a>, </i>and the <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Rules-Supervillainy-Saga-Book-ebook/dp/B07MB89S33/\" target=\"_blank\">Supervillainy Saga</a>.</i><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","name":"CTPhipps","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12002_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13933"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-05-05T17:33:39-07:00","id":1447669,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Chris24601</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1443592-the-official-v5-vs-v20-thread?p=1447663#post1447663\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">It\u2019s kind of a pity that the Beast is so animalistic, because I think a lot of mileage on Personal Horror could be gained from an approach similar to how Wraith has other players run a PC\u2019s Shadow so it\u2019s NOT just the GM dictating what happens, another player is deciding what the Beast is doing.<br /></div> </div> </div> </div>Ulch, no. Every attempt I've seen of something like that has been super-cringey, and not fun at all. Maybe if you have an absolute top-tier group of improvisers, the sort of people you see on youtube series, you can do that. But with an average or even above average group? Super-cringey.<br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3598-cajunkhan","name":"CajunKhan","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3598_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1700"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-05-05T17:39:06-07:00","id":1447672,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CajunKhan</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1443592-the-official-v5-vs-v20-thread?p=1447669#post1447669\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Ulch, no. Every attempt I've seen of something like that has been super-cringey, and not fun at all. Maybe if you have an absolute top-tier group of improvisers, the sort of people you see on youtube series, you can do that. But with an average or even above average group? Super-cringey.<br /></div> </div> </div> </div>My Wraith Storyteller and I think some of the products suggest that the best way to do that is to have the player roleplay their Beast. Similarly, in my personal horror games, asking my players to come up with horrible things to do to their characters goes WAY further than I would ever be comfortable doing.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Author of <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Cthulhu-Armageddon-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01KUOM7SI/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982844&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Cthulhu+Armageddon\" target=\"_blank\">Cthulhu Armageddon</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Teenage-Weredeer-Bright-Falls-Mysteries-ebook/dp/B075TTN2FN/ref=sr_1_2?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982717&amp;sr=1-2&amp;keywords=Weredeer#customerReviews\" target=\"_blank\">I was a Teenage Weredeer</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Straight-Outta-Fangton-Comedic-Vampire-ebook/dp/B01KNHICCC/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982774&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Straight+Outta+Fangton\" target=\"_blank\">Straight Outta Fangton</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Lucifers-Star-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01MDM9MCT/ref=mt_kindle?_encoding=UTF8&amp;me=&amp;qid=\" target=\"_blank\">Lucifer's Star</a>, </i>and the <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Rules-Supervillainy-Saga-Book-ebook/dp/B07MB89S33/\" target=\"_blank\">Supervillainy Saga</a>.</i><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","name":"CTPhipps","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12002_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13933"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-05-05T23:10:54-07:00","id":1447695,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Vilenecromancer</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1443592-the-official-v5-vs-v20-thread?p=1447586#post1447586\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Hmmm, a lot more enlightening thank you. However, you misquoted where that quote was from. That quote is from page 118, which leads me to believe that the section I was referencing wasn't even read at all, which is on page 120 which is: <br /> <i>&quot;Change the size of the dice pool. This modifier reflects a change or circumstance for the character: they are drugged, they use a specialty, they appear terrifying, etc.&quot;</i></div> </div> </div> </div>Mea culpa. You're right there. I'm using the PDF, so page '120' is actually page 118. That's super embarrassing! \ud83e\udd23<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> However the other parts of your argument do make some sense. I do ultimately agree with you that V20 has more options, and as a result can tell more stories without relying on the Golden Rule. However, V20 isn't &quot;better&quot; and neither is V5, because V20 has just as many flaws as V5 if you don't look at the Golden Rule. Neither system is &quot;better&quot;, and that's okay. </div> </div> </div>I think we're mostly in agreement. 'Better' is a subjective term. For me, 'better' is whatever gives me more ability to run the kinds of stories I like to run in the WoD. <br /> <br /> And, of course, having played WoD since I was 14, I have two decades' experience and therefore won't necessarily want to play street-level games every time. <br /> <br /> The games I played when I first encountered the core rulebook are often very different to the games I play now, because I'm aware of the wider world and so prefer to explore new parts which we haven't explored before (or old parts in new ways).","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Writer, publisher, performer<br /> Mostly he/his, sometimes she/her IRL <a href=\"https://adam-lowe.com\" target=\"_blank\">https://adam-lowe.com</a>","edited":{"userid":5291,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5291-adambeyoncelowe","user":"adambeyoncelowe","date":". 05-06-2021, 02:17 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5291-adambeyoncelowe","name":"adambeyoncelowe","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5291_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2802"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-05-06T09:43:06-07:00","id":1447721,"title":"","content":"I find V5's rules harmful for streetlevel play. <br /> <br /> Combat is all or nothing, so it's either really easy or you've lost. At a low level of power, that's not how combat should be. Combat should either be -I have a cunning plan- or -he took a few hits but he won out in the end-. If you're playing entry level vampires, your advantages are that nobody knows your coming, and freakish endurance. In V5, it doesn't matter how durable you are, you're going to lose if the guy has a bigger single combat pool than you, and win if your pool is best, and the impact and capability to pull off shenigans is greatly deminished. Your ability to prepare for conflict is peanuts because weapons are trivialized and armour doesn't exist for vampires, and also the retainer background was gutted so good luck playing a Ventrue commander. <br /> <br /> Meanwhile the social game doesn't matter so much because with your coterie, if you assume everyone's playing the same rules as you, can totally wipe the city if elysium really displeases them so much. As stated before, willpower damage relies on public shame, which is a good way to get you killed and weirdly off for a game about vampires since the politics of parasites is going to be mostly backroom deals and friendship with benefits. <br /> <br /> And, well, since I don't want to diablerize anybody, and the players, if they're half-smart, are going to start with a good domain beetween them, there's not really much reason to be an instigator. If I wanna get rich, the method to do so in V5 is to pay XP. If I want less garbage retainers, I spend more XP. Players become passive, waiting for something to happen to them so they can get XP, perhaps that's what touchstones are for, while in V20 the scramble for backgrounds is very real. The rules of V5 encourage the players and characters to move because of Touchstones or because messy criticals and the messy attempts to cover them are spiralling out of control, whilst in V20 the -oh fuck he frenzied/screwed the masquerade- is certainly prevailent in newbie games, but a good chunk of things are the players trying to get backgrounds and the consequences of their consciously chosen actions. (Of course, the storyteller can throw plot at them in both games, but if your players are instigators, it's generally means a lot less work and a lot more fun for the ST, at least from my experience)","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":7}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25794-mywifeisscary","name":"MyWifeIsScary","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25794_2.png","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3711"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-05-06T12:10:58-07:00","id":1447724,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MyWifeIsScary</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1443592-the-official-v5-vs-v20-thread?p=1447721#post1447721\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I find V5's rules harmful for streetlevel play.<br /> <br /> Combat is all or nothing, so it's either really easy or you've lost. At a low level of power, that's not how combat should be. Combat should either be -I have a cunning plan- or -he took a few hits but he won out in the end-. If you're playing entry level vampires, your advantages are that nobody knows your coming, and freakish endurance. In V5, it doesn't matter how durable you are, you're going to lose if the guy has a bigger single combat pool than you, and win if your pool is best, and the impact and capability to pull off shenigans is greatly deminished. Your ability to prepare for conflict is peanuts because weapons are trivialized and armour doesn't exist for vampires, and also the retainer background was gutted so good luck playing a Ventrue commander.<br /> <br /> Meanwhile the social game doesn't matter so much because with your coterie, if you assume everyone's playing the same rules as you, can totally wipe the city if elysium really displeases them so much. As stated before, willpower damage relies on public shame, which is a good way to get you killed and weirdly off for a game about vampires since the politics of parasites is going to be mostly backroom deals and friendship with benefits.<br /> <br /> And, well, since I don't want to diablerize anybody, and the players, if they're half-smart, are going to start with a good domain beetween them, there's not really much reason to be an instigator. If I wanna get rich, the method to do so in V5 is to pay XP. If I want less garbage retainers, I spend more XP. Players become passive, waiting for something to happen to them so they can get XP, perhaps that's what touchstones are for, while in V20 the scramble for backgrounds is very real. The rules of V5 encourage the players and characters to move because of Touchstones or because messy criticals and the messy attempts to cover them are spiralling out of control, whilst in V20 the -oh fuck he frenzied/screwed the masquerade- is certainly prevailent in newbie games, but a good chunk of things are the players trying to get backgrounds and the consequences of their consciously chosen actions. (Of course, the storyteller can throw plot at them in both games, but if your players are instigators, it's generally means a lot less work and a lot more fun for the ST, at least from my experience)</div> </div> </div> </div>The converse of all this is that the combat system in V20 increases the level of randomness in the system to the point that it doesn\u2019t really matter what your skill levels are at fighting, you will still usually end up with a protracted slog, with buckets of dice being rolled for incremental effect. Because of the randomness, it is often the case that a statistical advantage in fighting stats often has only a limited effect on the outcome of the conflict.<br /> <br /> In V5, the action is acute to the abilities on display, swift and dramatic. You can use more advanced systems on offer, if you want to add detail.<br /> <br /> The social game absolutely matters in a politically themed game like Vampire, and the systems in V5 are more detailed and more in line with the systems used in physical conflict. V20 still has the traditional breakdown of combat having all the detail in its own subsystem and the other forms of conflict essentially an afterthought. The same is often true in cases of simulating the vampiric condition - because there aren\u2019t as many well defined systems in V20 play, a lot of things can be potentially ignored in the game. Having a robust mechanical system enhances roleplaying, it doesn\u2019t mean you cannot utilize them for actual roleplaying scenes.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":2517,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2517-trippy","user":"Trippy","date":". 05-06-2021, 03:16 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2517-trippy","name":"Trippy","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2517_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1018"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-05-06T12:16:07-07:00","id":1447725,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CajunKhan</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1443592-the-official-v5-vs-v20-thread?p=1447669#post1447669\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Ulch, no. Every attempt I've seen of something like that has been super-cringey, and not fun at all. Maybe if you have an absolute top-tier group of improvisers, the sort of people you see on youtube series, you can do that. But with an average or even above average group? Super-cringey.</div> </div> </div> </div>To be fair, I don\u2019t think it work in this context either precisely because The Beast is not a Shadow; it\u2019s Fight/Flight/Feed and little else; there\u2019s not much to roleplay there at all.<br /> <br /> No, my preference would be, rather than making Frenzies and such akin to blackouts where the GM takes over, instead do stacking penalties.<br /> <br /> Say rank the Fight/Feed/Flight stressors from 1-5 and when they come up you roll your Self-Control (Fight/Feed) or Courage (Flight) to subtract from that. If you get it down to zero you remain in complete control. For each point you fail to remove you take a +1 difficulty penalty to all your actions unless the action is one that aligns with the Beast. If you do take an action in accord with the Beast then the penalty is reduced by one.<br /> <br /> So say the stressor is you\u2019re being publicly humiliated and we\u2019ll say it\u2019s a 4. You roll Self-Control and get 2 successes. You now have a +2 difficultly penalty to any action that\u2019s not lashing out in some way at those humiliating you. If you do lash out the penalty goes to +1, lash out a second time and it drops to +0... or you don\u2019t and keep trying to interact with a +2 difficultly penalty to every non-violent attempt you make.<br /> <br /> Then you make it stack. So after several rounds of verbal abuse you might be at +5 or 6 difficultly and any attempts at trying to do anything remotely controlled are just sputtering failures and the only way out is to either give in to the Beast and do something violent or, say, spending willpower to drive the Beast back down.<br /> <br /> Maybe the Beast even offers bonuses to Fight, Feed or Flight actions to further incentivize giving in (say you get a -2 difficultly bonus and your built-up Fight reflex drops by 2 or more instead of 1 if you physically strike the person who triggering you).<br /> <br /> I\u2019m still messing around with the idea in my head, but the gist would be instead of just ceding control to the GM, you just get progressively more penalties for trying to hold the Beast in check and progressively more benefits from just giving in (and having to deal with the fallout).<br /> <br /> The fact that it\u2019s ALWAYS your choice to give in in order to remove the penalties I think would better reinforce the concept of personal horror because it\u2019s never \u201cthe Beast MADE me do it\u201d it\u2019s \u201cI GAVE IN to the Beast because it was easier than trying to keep fighting it.\u201d","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1328-chris24601","name":"Chris24601","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"520"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-05-06T12:55:43-07:00","id":1447726,"title":"","content":"I've had a similar thought with regard to stains. How about having stains increase your strength by half the stains round down? So if you have five stains, you get +2 strength? The beast rewards you for feeding it. This also somewhat fixes a minor thing that's annoyed me: that I think vampires should be superhumanly strong by default, and I've never liked that you can easily have vampires who are weaker than humans.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3598-cajunkhan","name":"CajunKhan","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3598_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1700"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-05-06T14:44:30-07:00","id":1447733,"title":"","content":"People have already sang VtR 2e's praises, and to do that some more:<br /> <br /> Frenzying vampires in VtR 2e add their Blood Potency to all Physical rolls. A BP 4 vampire with 3 Strength becomes 7 Strength while frenzying. Add Potence/Vigor dots and they can get up to some pretty scary levels.<br /> <br /> Vampires also take the Tempted Condition whenever they pass a frenzy roll, which gives a cumulative -1 to future frenzy rolls (removed when they finally snap and frenzy). One house rule I like is that feeding or indulging with a dark deed can also remove the penalty. <i>&quot;A beast I am, lest a beast I become.&quot;</i>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://blood-and-bourbon.obsidianportal.com/\" target=\"_blank\">Blood and Bourbon</a>, my New Orleans-based Vampire chronicle.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3110-false-epiphany","name":"False Epiphany","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3110_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"748"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-05-06T23:08:12-07:00","id":1447770,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Trippy</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1443592-the-official-v5-vs-v20-thread?p=1447724#post1447724\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The converse of all this is that the combat system in V20 increases the level of randomness in the system to the point that it doesn\u2019t really matter what your skill levels are at fighting, you will still usually end up with a protracted slog, with buckets of dice being rolled for incremental effect. Because of the randomness, it is often the case that a statistical advantage in fighting stats often has only a limited effect on the outcome of the conflict.<br /> <br /> In V5, the action is acute to the abilities on display, swift and dramatic. You can use more advanced systems on offer, if you want to add detail.<br /> <br /> The social game absolutely matters in a politically themed game like Vampire, and the systems in V5 are more detailed and more in line with the systems used in physical conflict. V20 still has the traditional breakdown of combat having all the detail in its own subsystem and the other forms of conflict essentially an afterthought. The same is often true in cases of simulating the vampiric condition - because there aren\u2019t as many well defined systems in V20 play, a lot of things can be potentially ignored in the game. Having a robust mechanical system enhances roleplaying, it doesn\u2019t mean you cannot utilize them for actual roleplaying scenes.</div> </div> </div> </div>I'm not sure I prefer V5's 'whittle away WP' system for social combat. It wasn't great in Exalted 2e and it's not great here either. I think V20 also needed something meatier, too.<br /> <br /> For a game that often has politics, the social influence system should be really evocative and robust. As I've said before, I've ported in Exalted 3e's Intimacies system, which works incredibly well here. You could probably use that with Backgrounds, Convictions and Touchstones instead, if you don't want to add new traits to V5. The idea being that you'd leverage what's important to a character to get them to do things.<br /> <br /> VTR2e's social system would work, too, but I've got less experience of that. Once I tried Intimacies, I was hooked, as it's so easy to make plot points off them. I have even shared some of those plot points with the players so they can earn extra XP if they make any of them happen (and I can intentionally build conflict into those plot points, by giving players goals that oppose and interact).","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Writer, publisher, performer<br /> Mostly he/his, sometimes she/her IRL <a href=\"https://adam-lowe.com\" target=\"_blank\">https://adam-lowe.com</a>","edited":{"userid":5291,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5291-adambeyoncelowe","user":"adambeyoncelowe","date":". 05-08-2021, 02:13 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5291-adambeyoncelowe","name":"adambeyoncelowe","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5291_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2802"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-05-07T13:54:25-07:00","id":1447839,"title":"","content":"I don't think anyone's actually happy with V20's combat or social mechanics. Just that a lot of us will take the flaws in those over the flaws in V5's attempts.<br /> <br /> The CofD approach is also to have multiple subsystems that can address social interactions, not just one. The big one is the Social Maneuvering system, which is the most important for vampires because it's all about trying to get other people to do favors for you (either by developing a relationship with them over time and improving their opinion of you aka Soft Leverage, or trying to force action immediately through threats/extortionetc. aka Hard Leverage). But the Investigation system has rules for using it to get dirt on people rather than actually solving crimes or mysteries, which can then be used to supplement social actions (either simple ones or ones as part of other systems), the Crafting rules covers non-physical concepts like building a plan for a group to follow (taking over constructive social systems like leadership), and the Chase system - while never really flushed out in how to do it - can be used for non-physical conflicts and draws heavily from the CofD 1e Debate system (making it good for anything that's two or more parties competing over the same social prize).<br /> <br /> While somewhat disjointed compared to the &quot;one social system to do everything&quot; approach, it has a big advantage in that each one can be simpler by having less ground to cover, and therefore create better results for the specific focus you want to put on something.<br /> <br /> Though, as I plugged in the porting from V5 to V20 or vice versa thread, the CofD 2e rules have a lot of good idea for working stuff into V20 or V5. That applies to things like Intimacies too. If you don't want to completely port Intimacies over to VtM, the CofD 2e social mechanics use existing Traits like Anchors (this covers things like Nature/Demeanor in V20, or Convictions, Touchstones, and Aspirations in V5) to fill in the same basic role in social systems. Trying to get a mortal investigator who has a strong sense of justice (Virtue: Justice) and is specifically trying to take down the head of a crime syndicate (Long Term Aspiration: Dismantle [name of gang]), social maneuvers against them can be really easy, or really hard depending on if you sell what your asking as moving towards those goals, or accidentally try to push against them.<br /> <br /> Intimacies are one of the highlights of Exalted 3e, but they're integrated on a pretty broad level; not just the core of the social mechanics that they are. You can get a lot in VtM by taking advantage over the traits that are already there.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-05-07T15:51:17-07:00","id":1447856,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Heavy Arms</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1443592-the-official-v5-vs-v20-thread?p=1447839#post1447839\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I don't think anyone's actually happy with V20's combat or social mechanics. Just that a lot of us will take the flaws in those over the flaws in V5's attempts.</div> </div> </div> </div>I\u2019m not sure anybody has established on this thread, however, what specifically is wrong with V5\u2019s social mechanics. What I\u2019ve read, to date, is how people prefer V20 because of its lack of structure in this area, while also suggesting social mechanics from other games that may be great, but without detail it is hard to establish why they are better.<br /> <br /> The reason why I like V5\u2019s social mechanics is because they are seamless in play to every other conflict mechanic, including physical combat, they are flexible in their interpretation - so you could use them to simulate an internet flame war over months as well as quick interpersonal exchanges - and finally because the mechanic is so intuitive in play that you don\u2019t have to keep referencing the book to implement them in practice. To me, this qualifies them as an excellent set of rules. What precisely is wrong with them? <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2517-trippy","name":"Trippy","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2517_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1018"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-05-07T16:46:26-07:00","id":1447862,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Trippy</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1443592-the-official-v5-vs-v20-thread?p=1447856#post1447856\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I\u2019m not sure anybody has established on this thread, however, what specifically is wrong with V5\u2019s social mechanics.</div> </div> </div> </div>Eh, some people have stated at great length their problems with the social mechanics across the last few pages. But I feel preference is a pretty good reason for either way.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Author of <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Cthulhu-Armageddon-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01KUOM7SI/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982844&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Cthulhu+Armageddon\" target=\"_blank\">Cthulhu Armageddon</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Teenage-Weredeer-Bright-Falls-Mysteries-ebook/dp/B075TTN2FN/ref=sr_1_2?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982717&amp;sr=1-2&amp;keywords=Weredeer#customerReviews\" target=\"_blank\">I was a Teenage Weredeer</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Straight-Outta-Fangton-Comedic-Vampire-ebook/dp/B01KNHICCC/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982774&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Straight+Outta+Fangton\" target=\"_blank\">Straight Outta Fangton</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Lucifers-Star-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01MDM9MCT/ref=mt_kindle?_encoding=UTF8&amp;me=&amp;qid=\" target=\"_blank\">Lucifer's Star</a>, </i>and the <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Rules-Supervillainy-Saga-Book-ebook/dp/B07MB89S33/\" target=\"_blank\">Supervillainy Saga</a>.</i><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","name":"CTPhipps","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12002_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13933"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-05-07T17:19:59-07:00","id":1447871,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CTPhipps</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1443592-the-official-v5-vs-v20-thread?p=1447862#post1447862\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Eh, some people have stated at great length their problems with the social mechanics across the last few pages. But I feel preference is a pretty good reason for either way.</div> </div> </div> </div>Well, I could re-read a bunch of posts - and admittedly, a lot of it is speed reading so I may have missed something - but a lot of what I read is basically saying people\u2019s <i>preference</i> for a given games way of doing something, rather than a specific criticism of the game mechanics in question. So, rather than just saying, for example, 'I don\u2019t like social conflict mechanics that are x, y and z', my question is 'what is actually wrong with social conflict mechanics that are x, y and z, beyond your own personal preference?\u2019.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":2517,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2517-trippy","user":"Trippy","date":". 05-07-2021, 11:07 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2517-trippy","name":"Trippy","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2517_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1018"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-05-07T19:13:31-07:00","id":1447880,"title":"","content":"OK.... let me try to summarize:<br /> <br /> 1) The V5 social mechanics eliminate any advantage to planning or trying to put your opponent on the back foot before you confront them. You roll your best roll against their best roll, and the major result modifier to determine the winner of a round, with no other circumstantial effects in play (ex: combat has cover modifiers against ranged attack that social conflict does not, and there are penalties for called shots).<br /> <br /> Though something I've become aware of to correct a previous assertion: You can get bonus dice in advanced social conflicts through the Maneuver action. However, this uses up one of your three actions, and you can't attack that turn. Thus it's only really safe to use if (a) you have large numbers on your side so someone can defend you or threat to attack if your opponent would otherwise take the chance to All-Out Attack you (b) you have the dice on your side meaning the extra dice are highly unlikely to get you more damage than attacking two turns in a row.<br /> <br /> And that presumes the ST doesn't decide your Maneuver takes setting up, as a Maneuver might not general bonus dice if the ST decides it's necessary to even try your intended action, or that you need to do a setup Maneuver and then you can do a dice-bonus Maneuver, and then you can finally attack.<br /> <br /> 2) The V5 social mechanics models audience as weapon modifiers. What your social attack is, doesn't actually matter. If you have a devastating insult, but you only get 1 success total and it's just you vs. your target? They take 1 WP damage. If you put a whoopie cushion under a Primogen's seat and get one success, and it goes off in front of the Prince, it does 6 WP damage. The Prince finds this childish behavior completely unbecoming of a vampire and isn't at all amused? Doesn't matter, being mocked in front of the Prince is what does the damage. <br /> <br /> What's wrong with that? The mechanics don't model what they say they model. It's not just a matter of preference for style of rules, but the V5 mechanics are heavily biased towards specific social conflict options and not others with no stated rationale (and in fact contradiction to stated points of using social conflicts).<br /> <br /> Calling this &quot;personal preference&quot; is just deflecting. You can claim anything is personal preference is you're going to ignore what the goal of the mechanics are:<br /> <br /> &quot;These combat rules are horrible, this is supposed to be a real world setting, but punches automatically hit, and automatically incapacitate targets, and you get to pick between non-lethal and lethal results, but guns never do more than one non-lethal damage no matter what, and if you successfully hit someone with a gun you lose all your health to lethal damage save one last health and you can't mitigate that at all!&quot;<br /> <br /> &quot;Well, that's just your preference about combat, I like it because my preference is for combat to be up close and personal and not for shooting people from range.&quot;<br /> <br /> It's not actually engaging with the rules in the context of what they're supposed to be doing. If combat tells me it's supposed to be results that resemble real world results fists should not be insanely superior to guns, fists even being close to competitive to guns is a concession to game over reality. If the social conflict rules are supposed to help me play out interesting political intrigue, back room one-on-one social conflicts need to have enough mechanical weight to actually force a result instead of giving one side no reason to take it seriously.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":7}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-05-07T20:53:47-07:00","id":1447886,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Heavy Arms</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1443592-the-official-v5-vs-v20-thread?p=1447880#post1447880\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">OK.... let me try to summarize:<br /> <br /> 1) The V5 social mechanics eliminate any advantage to planning or trying to put your opponent on the back foot before you confront them. You roll your best roll against their best roll, and the major result modifier to determine the winner of a round, with no other circumstantial effects in play (ex: combat has cover modifiers against ranged attack that social conflict does not, and there are penalties for called shots).<br /> <br /> Though something I've become aware of to correct a previous assertion: You can get bonus dice in advanced social conflicts through the Maneuver action. However, this uses up one of your three actions, and you can't attack that turn. Thus it's only really safe to use if (a) you have large numbers on your side so someone can defend you or threat to attack if your opponent would otherwise take the chance to All-Out Attack you (b) you have the dice on your side meaning the extra dice are highly unlikely to get you more damage than attacking two turns in a row.<br /> <br /> And that presumes the ST doesn't decide your Maneuver takes setting up, as a Maneuver might not general bonus dice if the ST decides it's necessary to even try your intended action, or that you need to do a setup Maneuver and then you can do a dice-bonus Maneuver, and then you can finally attack.<br /> <br /> 2) The V5 social mechanics models audience as weapon modifiers. What your social attack is, doesn't actually matter. If you have a devastating insult, but you only get 1 success total and it's just you vs. your target? They take 1 WP damage. If you put a whoopie cushion under a Primogen's seat and get one success, and it goes off in front of the Prince, it does 6 WP damage. The Prince finds this childish behavior completely unbecoming of a vampire and isn't at all amused? Doesn't matter, being mocked in front of the Prince is what does the damage.<br /> <br /> What's wrong with that? The mechanics don't model what they say they model. It's not just a matter of preference for style of rules, but the V5 mechanics are heavily biased towards specific social conflict options and not others with no stated rationale (and in fact contradiction to stated points of using social conflicts).<br /> <br /> Calling this &quot;personal preference&quot; is just deflecting. You can claim anything is personal preference is you're going to ignore what the goal of the mechanics are:<br /> <br /> &quot;These combat rules are horrible, this is supposed to be a real world setting, but punches automatically hit, and automatically incapacitate targets, and you get to pick between non-lethal and lethal results, but guns never do more than one non-lethal damage no matter what, and if you successfully hit someone with a gun you lose all your health to lethal damage save one last health and you can't mitigate that at all!&quot;<br /> <br /> &quot;Well, that's just your preference about combat, I like it because my preference is for combat to be up close and personal and not for shooting people from range.&quot;<br /> <br /> It's not actually engaging with the rules in the context of what they're supposed to be doing. If combat tells me it's supposed to be results that resemble real world results fists should not be insanely superior to guns, fists even being close to competitive to guns is a concession to game over reality. If the social conflict rules are supposed to help me play out interesting political intrigue, back room one-on-one social conflicts need to have enough mechanical weight to actually force a result instead of giving one side no reason to take it seriously.</div> </div> </div> </div>So, I will just note that on the previous discussion of V20 physical combat, that is also the major mark against it. It basically doesn\u2019t model what it says it models - you roll lots of dice in a way that renders combat to a randomized and protracted outcome, where abilities do not actually provide as much advantage as they should. Additionally, the V20 system for social conflict is basically non existent by comparison to V5.<br /> <br /> That said, your criticisms of V5 social conflict can be analyzed too.<br /> <br /> It is not clear that they centre on the advanced rules of social conflict or the basic rules (that of simply having a contested role based on appropriate traits, and subtracting the number of excess successes to the Willpower total)? Some people won\u2019t necessarily be using the advanced rules all the time. I won\u2019t dig the hole of making any suggestions about 'fixing\u2019 any rule - just state how they work.<br /> <br /> Point 1). Is there any reason why you cannot take an Advance to break down the advantage of putting the opponent on the back foot (as an Extended test)? It doesn\u2019t have to be a single roll test, and you could bring in planning elements into the extension rolls. You could also use teamwork for a similar effect, and while the extended tests could be rolled as Maneuvers they don\u2019t necessarily have to be handled that way. They don\u2019t even necessarily require an opposed roll directly. You wouldn\u2019t need to take an action turn to use it as the rolls are done in preparation to the conflict. It would be a prior Maneuver (p296) - not during the conflict.<br /> <br /> Point 2). The stakes of any given social conflict are defined before any dice pools are collected or rolled. That is, your actual social attack can be at any level - if the impact of an attacking insult is supposed to be devastating as a stake, then that outcome can be landed in a differentiated way to the whoops cushion prank. It may be measured through Willpower loss - but the outcome can be as differentiated as the difference between non-lethal and lethal physical weapons.<br /> <br /> Moreover, if you only roll a single success, that is the nature of rolling dice pools isn\u2019t it? You can\u2019t guarantee the outcome of any dice pool roll. If you have a particularly good dice pool, you <i>increase your chances</i> to get more successes, but there is still a chance that your killer insult dice roll will be low and the outcome could be interpreted as being maybe a stuttered delivery or distraction that scuppered the full impact of it? You may, conversely, roll high successes on the whoopee cushion prank - reducing Willpower quickly with the Audience bonus - but the stake may not be as high when the WP runs out. There is still a lot of ST/player negotiation on what the dice rolls represent - with the caveat that the stakes need to be determined beforehand. The Audience modifiers can reflect higher circumstantial stakes as well as 'weapon modifiers\u2019 to the stats involved.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":2517,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2517-trippy","user":"Trippy","date":". 05-08-2021, 01:40 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2517-trippy","name":"Trippy","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2517_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1018"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-05-07T23:01:37-07:00","id":1447895,"title":"","content":"I enjoy V20s social combat simply because of how bare-bones it is. You can't precisely model social conflict to a satisfactory degree without an unreasonable amount of pages, so why bother? V20 does you a favour with the amount of leeway you get. It trusts in storytellers to do right by their players. The only actual problem, aside from an inept st (which is always a potential problem) is that Presence 1 and 3 are horrendously vague.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25794-mywifeisscary","name":"MyWifeIsScary","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25794_2.png","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3711"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-05-07T23:14:05-07:00","id":1447896,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Trippy</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1443592-the-official-v5-vs-v20-thread?p=1447886#post1447886\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">So, I will just note that on the previous discussion of V20 physical combat, that is also the major mark against it. It basically doesn\u2019t model what it says it models - you roll lots of dice in a way that renders combat to a randomized and protracted outcome, where abilities do not actually provide as much advantage as they should. Additionally, the V20 system for social conflict is basically non existent by comparison to V5.</div> </div> </div> </div>You asked what the complaints about V5's mechanics are. As I already said, most V20 fans don't particularly like the V20 combat/social mechanics, and that vast majority I've talked to would prefer something we consider better. The problem is that what we consider better are things more like Exalted 3e, CofD 2e, or the Storypath system: games where these systems that can get out of the way for people that want quick and fast resolutions, but keep enough meat on the bones for players that want mechanical support for a much more tactically minded experience.<br /> <br /> A lot of us have also had a lot of negative experience so &quot;social combat&quot; models where all social situations try to work like combat, instead of recognizing how silly that is. It's one thing for a game like Fate where everything uses the same framework except for having a more than one &quot;health&quot; track to damage if that's relevant, but if you model all advanced social mechanics on combat, you fall short because &quot;social&quot; is as broad as &quot;physical&quot; and combat is not all physical action.<br /> <br /> The utility of easy to remember fast resolution is when you do simple conflict resolutions. Advanced resolution systems are when you want to keep to the core idea of how the game works, but expand it out. Trying to keep all the advanced systems the same in the name of keeping how thy work simple inherently means selling parts of those conflicts short.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Point 1). Is there any reason why you cannot take an Advance to break down the advantage of putting the opponent on the back foot (as an Extended test)? </div> </div> </div>All an Advance does is more towards a narrative that doesn't involved head-to-head conflict. Trying to circumvent getting into a social conflict with a political opponent by doing favors for a mutual superior is when you use an Advance. It isn't for taking on an opponent directly (as noted, you generally don't use Advance in combat because once you're in combat you have to be contesting your foe(s) directly).<br /> <br /> Basically, in my whole example story from before, the making an Advance part was all the stuff that lead up to a blackmail attempt and the NPC making an Advance to gather evidence the PCs broke the laws of Domain to counter them (because just Blocking them would have been kinda boring), that then stalls in V5 because trying to blackmail people doesn't really work in V5 (no audience - since you don't want an audience to blackmail - means it's significantly hard to do enough WP damage do get a meaningful opponent to concede).<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> It would be a prior Maneuver (p296) - not during the conflict. </div> </div> </div>A prior Maneuver is one that you have to take before you can take another conflict action. If you have a gun that's disassembled in a case, you take a Maneuver to put it together before you can use it. Investigating a political to discover a hidden vice that you want to exploit is a prior Maneuver to Advances to corrupt said politician to your employ. They are not stated as rolls that happen before an advanced conflict itself begins. <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> The stakes of any given social conflict are defined before any dice pools are collected or rolled. </div> </div> </div>Winning a social conflict requires one side to concede. If you only do 1 WP damage to them, and they don't concede, you have to keep at them. As V5 states, the only want to ensure concession is to fill them with Aggravated Willpower damage, so do Willpower x 2 damage, which you're not going to achieve in most cases without the audience damage bonus. After three rounds, since you're not supposed to roll more than three rounds and all, you have to be significantly ahead of your opponent so it doesn't get narrated as a tie, or a win in their favor. Which is, again, only really functional with meaningful audiences to give you the damage needed to show that things are decisively going your way (of course at the risk of that going against you too).<br /> <br /> Lets say over three rounds it's looking like you're just going back and forth. You do 1 WP, they do 1 WP, etc. You're only up 2 to 1 because you got the first win. But they have two more Willpower than you - lets say 8 to 6 - so neither character is really done much. So, in deciding what should happen to narrate out the rest, the path set forward is an even verbal back and forth, but you'd come up short on endurance and the ST declares you end up conceding the social conflict and the stake go to your opponent.<br /> <br /> Now we change up to having a +3 audience. After three rounds with the exact some rolls, they're impaired (down 8 WP out of 8) and you're doing not hot but OK (down 4 WP out of 6), with the impairment they might concede anyway, and the impairment penalty swings the even roll off in your favor rather than a coin flip, so suddenly the narrative switches in your favor and you get your stakes instead.<br /> <br /> So, yes, that audience factor really does matter. Whatever stakes you set, you have to be in a position to win the conflict to get them, or your foe gets theirs instead.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Moreover, if you only roll a single success, that is the nature of rolling dice pools isn\u2019t it? </div> </div> </div>Social conflict attack rolls are two characters rolling against each other. It's 1 success total after your opponents successes are subtracted from your own. It's still the nature of dice, but the issue remains the same with 1 success vs. 0, or 5 successes vs. 4; it might matter in terms of how to narrate the details of the actions, but the mechanical results are the same.<br /> <br /> The reason to stress the &quot;just 1 total success&quot; part is how much the audience factor skews what is and isn't effective in V5 social conflicts. That cutting insult could be 5 vs. 4, and so however well delivered the retort blunted it significantly; but you only do 1 damage because nobody else was around. If the harpies were involved, it would jump to 5 WP damage not because the insult was batter, or the retort was worse, but because losing a verbal exchange in front of important people cuts deeper.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-05-07T23:42:09-07:00","id":1447898,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CTPhipps</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1443592-the-official-v5-vs-v20-thread?p=1447862#post1447862\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Eh, some people have stated at great length their problems with the social mechanics across the last few pages. But I feel preference is a pretty good reason for either way.</div> </div> </div> </div>Exactly this. Thanks, CT.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Writer, publisher, performer<br /> Mostly he/his, sometimes she/her IRL <a href=\"https://adam-lowe.com\" target=\"_blank\">https://adam-lowe.com</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5291-adambeyoncelowe","name":"adambeyoncelowe","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5291_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2802"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-05-08T00:24:41-07:00","id":1447899,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Heavy Arms</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1443592-the-official-v5-vs-v20-thread?p=1447896#post1447896\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> You asked what the complaints about V5's mechanics are. As I already said, most V20 fans don't particularly like the V20 combat/social mechanics, and that vast majority I've talked to would prefer something we consider better. The problem is that what we consider better are things more like Exalted 3e, CofD 2e, or the Storypath system: games where these systems that can get out of the way for people that want quick and fast resolutions, but keep enough meat on the bones for players that want mechanical support for a much more tactically minded experience.</div> </div> </div> </div>I am reiterating the points about V20 because of the context of this thread being \u2018V5 vs V20\u2019. If we have a critical eye put upon V5, the context is how it measures up against V20. While it is useful to consider other games for comparison, I also feel that the comparisons are taken out of context of how other fanbases are critical of these other games\u2019 systems too. The 'grass is greener on the other side', in that respect, but I\u2019ve actually read a lot of criticisms of the game systems used in Exalted, for example, that it isn\u2019t a given to me that it is a better system than what we are discussing about. <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> A lot of us have also had a lot of negative experience so &quot;social combat&quot; models where all social situations try to work like combat, instead of recognizing how silly that is. It's one thing for a game like Fate where everything uses the same framework except for having a more than one &quot;health&quot; track to damage if that's relevant, but if you model all advanced social mechanics on combat, you fall short because &quot;social&quot; is as broad as &quot;physical&quot; and combat is not all physical action. </div> </div> </div>Why is it silly? Physical combat systems operate on abstractions in the same way that social conflict can be modeled also. Indeed, most RPG combat systems are not very accurate simulations of real world combat - and aren\u2019t even designed to be - they are interpreted primarily by the outcome. The systems used in V5 is still abstracted to the degree that they are flexible in interpretation towards specified outcomes. Moreover it isn\u2019t just an argument as to whether all this is a realistic simulation or not, a group could employ systems like these because they might actually just be fun to play out as a game within a game - in the same way physical combat is. <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> The utility of easy to remember fast resolution is when you do simple conflict resolutions. Advanced resolution systems are when you want to keep to the core idea of how the game works, but expand it out. Trying to keep all the advanced systems the same in the name of keeping how thy work simple inherently means selling parts of those conflicts short. </div> </div> </div>The advanced systems are not all the same though - they have certain similarities, but also clear differences. The time taken for conflict resolution is a good example of this, and the fact that there are different trackers is another. <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> All an Advance does is more towards a narrative that doesn't involved head-to-head conflict. Trying to circumvent getting into a social conflict with a political opponent by doing favors for a mutual superior is when you use an Advance. It isn't for taking on an opponent directly (as noted, you generally don't use Advance in combat because once you're in combat you have to be contesting your foe(s) directly).<br /> <br /> Basically, in my whole example story from before, the making an Advance part was all the stuff that lead up to a blackmail attempt and the NPC making an Advance to gather evidence the PCs broke the laws of Domain to counter them (because just Blocking them would have been kinda boring), that then stalls in V5 because trying to blackmail people doesn't really work in V5 (no audience - since you don't want an audience to blackmail - means it's significantly hard to do enough WP damage do get a meaningful opponent to concede).<br /> <br /> A prior Maneuver is one that you have to take before you can take another conflict action. If you have a gun that's disassembled in a case, you take a Maneuver to put it together before you can use it. Investigating a political to discover a hidden vice that you want to exploit is a prior Maneuver to Advances to corrupt said politician to your employ. They are not stated as rolls that happen before an advanced conflict itself begins. </div> </div> </div>I think that is a misinterpretation of what an \u2018Advance' is. It clearly is part of a narrative that involves head-to-conflict, because the rule is listed and stated as being \u201cAn Additional Conflict Option\u201d right before Maneuvers. It is precisely about taking on a conflict as part of an extended task. A 'prior maneuver\u2019 is exactly what you were describing as lacking before - it is something you can do in preparation for a conflict and as, it does not impinge on any action during the conflict itself. This isn\u2019t me trying to give you house rule, this is actually what is written in the rules of the text. <br /> <br /> In your story example, you would make an extended set of Advances towards the blackmailing goal, and these would potentially accumulate dice to add to the final roll. If that final roll only ends up in one success, then that is just the luck of dice rolling, but accumulated dice certainly gives advantages to the chances of the final blackmail roll being successful. The impact of Audience isn\u2019t really in context, because it is a different type of social conflict. With the WP thing, you can simply rule it that the stakes are higher than a single WP loss - if that is agreed previously as an outcome. You are missing out on an awful lot of flexibility incorporated into the system. <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Winning a social conflict requires one side to concede. If you only do 1 WP damage to them, and they don't concede, you have to keep at them. As V5 states, the only want to ensure concession is to fill them with Aggravated Willpower damage, so do Willpower x 2 damage, which you're not going to achieve in most cases without the audience damage bonus. After three rounds, since you're not supposed to roll more than three rounds and all, you have to be significantly ahead of your opponent so it doesn't get narrated as a tie, or a win in their favor. Which is, again, only really functional with meaningful audiences to give you the damage needed to show that things are decisively going your way (of course at the risk of that going against you too).<br /> <br /> Lets say over three rounds it's looking like you're just going back and forth. You do 1 WP, they do 1 WP, etc. You're only up 2 to 1 because you got the first win. But they have two more Willpower than you - lets say 8 to 6 - so neither character is really done much. So, in deciding what should happen to narrate out the rest, the path set forward is an even verbal back and forth, but you'd come up short on endurance and the ST declares you end up conceding the social conflict and the stake go to your opponent.<br /> <br /> Now we change up to having a +3 audience. After three rounds with the exact some rolls, they're impaired (down 8 WP out of 8) and you're doing not hot but OK (down 4 WP out of 6), with the impairment they might concede anyway, and the impairment penalty swings the even roll off in your favor rather than a coin flip, so suddenly the narrative switches in your favor and you get your stakes instead.<br /> <br /> So, yes, that audience factor really does matter. Whatever stakes you set, you have to be in a position to win the conflict to get them, or your foe gets theirs instead.<br /> <br /> Social conflict attack rolls are two characters rolling against each other. It's 1 success total after your opponents successes are subtracted from your own. It's still the nature of dice, but the issue remains the same with 1 success vs. 0, or 5 successes vs. 4; it might matter in terms of how to narrate the details of the actions, but the mechanical results are the same.<br /> <br /> The reason to stress the &quot;just 1 total success&quot; part is how much the audience factor skews what is and isn't effective in V5 social conflicts. That cutting insult could be 5 vs. 4, and so however well delivered the retort blunted it significantly; but you only do 1 damage because nobody else was around. If the harpies were involved, it would jump to 5 WP damage not because the insult was batter, or the retort was worse, but because losing a verbal exchange in front of important people cuts deeper. </div> </div> </div>Winning a social conflict does require one side to concede, but it doesn\u2019t require that WP points have to be tracked incrementally till somebody is zero first. As you point out, people can concede strategically to preserve their WP. If agreed, also, it can simply be that someone who scores more social conflict successes than another can win that particular stake as an outcome. The Audience factor really is for a particular type of social conflict where a character\u2019s confidence, reputation or face is at stake - and where the Audience clearly raises that stake - like a public debate as an obvious example. It doesn\u2019t necessarily apply to every type of social conflict. <br /> <br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2517-trippy","name":"Trippy","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2517_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1018"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-05-08T00:28:51-07:00","id":1447900,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>adambeyoncelowe</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1443592-the-official-v5-vs-v20-thread?p=1447898#post1447898\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Exactly this. Thanks, CT.</div> </div> </div> </div>The question is whether the reasons cited are valid or not, and a preference without a valid reason is, basically, prejudicial. <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2517-trippy","name":"Trippy","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2517_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1018"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-05-08T00:38:52-07:00","id":1447901,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MyWifeIsScary</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1443592-the-official-v5-vs-v20-thread?p=1447895#post1447895\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I enjoy V20s social combat simply because of how bare-bones it is. You can't precisely model social conflict to a satisfactory degree without an unreasonable amount of pages, so why bother? V20 does you a favour with the amount of leeway you get. It trusts in storytellers to do right by their players. The only actual problem, aside from an inept st (which is always a potential problem) is that Presence 1 and 3 are horrendously vague.</div> </div> </div> </div>Well, this just suggests that the game shouldn\u2019t have any social conflict mechanics - which I think short changes a game that is supposedly built on playing out politics and various other forms of social conflict. It don\u2019t accept the notion that a game cannot model social conflict any more than the notion that a game cannot model physical conflict. Both things are perfectly feasible in game terms. It isn\u2019t just about having literal simulations, either - it is about providing game systems that can model interactions in a fun way - even they are abstracted in some way.<br /> <br /> I don\u2019t think that the V20 system provides enough support towards running social conflicts in a game, with anywhere near the level of emphasis that is given to physical conflict. This is a shame, because many vampire stories place a lot more emphasis on social conflict rather than physical combat - and this is where V5 shines.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":2517,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2517-trippy","user":"Trippy","date":". 05-08-2021, 03:45 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2517-trippy","name":"Trippy","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2517_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1018"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-05-08T01:43:29-07:00","id":1447907,"title":"","content":"V20 is great.<br /> You make an argument*<br /> Either it's solid enough that it doesn't need a roll, so fucking terrible it doesn't need a roll (perhaps a roll to save face?), or it's worth rolling for. *If the player isn't particularly good at articulating arguments, or he'd have far too much to say, he can just ask to roll.<br /> <i>I'll also try to be lenient on people who're obviously not 4-dots in X trying to play 4-dots in X, though It is easy to forget sometimes. </i><br /> <br /> You can contest another person's roll, or you can make it singly. The issue that V5 flops it's face at is what to do when someone 'wins' a roll. social conflicts aren't about fucking willpower. Either you make your opponent concede, or if he's never going to concede, you make yourself look great and them terrible, or you're just fooling people. It's not about making someone depressed and sullen, that's the least important thing here. What If I know full well that my petitioning the prince will fail, but I'm doing so to galvanize a quietly resentful populace? What if I desperately WANT the story that makes me look like a fool to get out, so that what really happened never sees the light of court? Perhaps losing willpower for humuliation might be appropriate on occasion, but the way V5 does it is simplistic at best. V20 at least has the Beast try to frenzy at a public humiliation, that can excuse the willpower loss.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25794-mywifeisscary","name":"MyWifeIsScary","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25794_2.png","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3711"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-05-08T01:55:35-07:00","id":1447910,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MyWifeIsScary</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1443592-the-official-v5-vs-v20-thread?p=1447907#post1447907\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">V20 is great.<br /> You make an argument*<br /> Either it's solid enough that it doesn't need a roll, so fucking terrible it doesn't need a roll (perhaps a roll to save face?), or it's worth rolling for. *If the player isn't particularly good at articulating arguments, or he'd have far too much to say, he can just ask to roll.<br /> <i>I'll also try to be lenient on people who're obviously not 4-dots in X trying to play 4-dots in X, though It is easy to forget sometimes. </i><br /> <br /> You can contest another person's roll, or you can make it singly. The issue that V5 flops it's face at is what to do when someone 'wins' a roll. social conflicts aren't about fucking willpower. Either you make your opponent concede, or if he's never going to concede, you make yourself look great and them terrible, or you're just fooling people. It's not about making someone depressed and sullen, that's the least important thing here. What If I know full well that my petitioning the prince will fail, but I'm doing so to galvanize a quietly resentful populace? What if I desperately WANT the story that makes me look like a fool to get out, so that what really happened never sees the light of court? Perhaps losing willpower for humuliation might be appropriate on occasion, but the way V5 does it is simplistic at best. V20 at least has the Beast try to frenzy at a public humiliation, that can excuse the willpower loss.</div> </div> </div> </div>You can roleplay your way through any aspect of V5 without making any rolls - including social conflicts. You literally have advice for diceless, freeform play to do this and there are different degrees about how much you can integrate dice-based systems - basic and advanced - in order to highlight scenes of play however you want.<br /> <br /> The systems of V5 do not \u2018flop\u2019 as you describe, they are not simplistic as you describe, and if social conflicts have nothing to do with willpower, then how are you persisting now with these arguments? Are you running on autopilot? Losing willpower doesn\u2019t necessarily make someone depressed and sullen - it may just make them aggressive, swear and use capitalized letters when typing.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":2517,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2517-trippy","user":"Trippy","date":". 05-08-2021, 05:10 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2517-trippy","name":"Trippy","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2517_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1018"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-05-08T03:56:29-07:00","id":1447917,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Trippy</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1443592-the-official-v5-vs-v20-thread?p=1447900#post1447900\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The question is whether the reasons cited are valid or not, and a preference without a valid reason is, basically, prejudicial. </div> </div> </div> </div>All opinions on a matter like this are going to ultimately boil down to preference. One shouldn't assume that just because one has a view it's somehow less biased and subjective than others'. <br /> <br /> You didn't engage with any of the points anyone made until Heavy Arms called you on it and reiterated them. That's not about adjudicating what's objectively right or wrong.<br /> <br /> Moving on, though, the claim that you can make things up on the fly, or ignore part of the rules, or simply roleplay through something, is not evidence of the superiority of any edition. Both editions do that, and 'wing it' isn't really a rule but an invitation to, well, wing it.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Writer, publisher, performer<br /> Mostly he/his, sometimes she/her IRL <a href=\"https://adam-lowe.com\" target=\"_blank\">https://adam-lowe.com</a>","edited":{"userid":5291,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5291-adambeyoncelowe","user":"adambeyoncelowe","date":". 05-08-2021, 06:59 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5291-adambeyoncelowe","name":"adambeyoncelowe","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5291_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2802"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-05-08T04:06:49-07:00","id":1447919,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>adambeyoncelowe</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1443592-the-official-v5-vs-v20-thread?p=1447917#post1447917\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> All opinions on a matter like this are going to ultimately boil down to preference. One shouldn't assume that just because one has a view it's somehow less biased and subjective than others'.<br /> <br /> You didn't engage with any of the points anyone made until Heavy Arms called you on it and reiterated them. That's not about adjudicating what's objectively right or wrong.<br /> <br /> Moving on, though, the claim that you can make things up on the fly, or ignore part of the rules, or simply roleplay through something, is not evidence of the superiority of any edition. Both editions do that, and 'wing it' isn't really a rule but an invitation to, well, wing it.</div> </div> </div> </div>Firstly, I have engaged with Heavy Arms on all his points. He hasn\u2019t 'called me' on anything.<br /> <br /> And the point still stands - that preference without valid reason is prejudicial. Rational arguments and debates do not just boil down to preference.<br /> <br /> In V5, it is not being dismissive to point out the fact that the rules explicitly give you different styles of playing through things, including social conflict. You can do it free form, or with one simple roll or with more structured advanced rules or scale these to taste to any degree. V20 does not provide all these options in play. That is one reason why V5 is superior in design to V20.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":2517,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2517-trippy","user":"Trippy","date":". 05-08-2021, 07:15 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2517-trippy","name":"Trippy","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2517_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1018"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-05-08T04:09:05-07:00","id":1447920,"title":"","content":"I think everyone is giving valid arguments and discussions even if they're not persuaded. As stated, a lot of this is subjective and the thread has mostly remained civil because of it.<br /> <br /> Thumbs up on that folks.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>adambeyoncelowe</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1443592-the-official-v5-vs-v20-thread?p=1447917#post1447917\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Moving on, though, the claim that you can make things up on the fly, or ignore part of the rules, or simply roleplay through something, is not evidence of the superiority of any edition. Both editions do that, and 'wing it' isn't really a rule but an invitation to, well, wing it.</div> </div> </div> </div>Yes, the absence of rules is a double edged sword, though.<br /> <br /> 1. If something doesn't have rules then that MIGHT be a sign that the books are incomplete in terms of development.<br /> <br /> 2. OTOH, it might be a sign that rules were not needed for it in the first place.<br /> <br /> Take for instance the fact that Generation is now something that your character can now choose like Clan. It's no longer a sink for your Backgrounds but a matter of how you wish to play the game.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Trippy</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1443592-the-official-v5-vs-v20-thread?p=1447900#post1447900\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The question is whether the reasons cited are valid or not, and a preference without a valid reason is, basically, prejudicial.</div> </div> </div> </div>I think that preference doesn't particularly require reasoning beyond emotional attachment or enthusiasm. If someone says, I like V20 because it's the one I've done with my friends for years and years then that's entirely valid just as if I said that I like V5 because of its heavy focus on the classic Chicago area of V:TM that had been ignored since Second Edition. Part of what I mentioned earlier when starting the thread is I don't think there's such a thing as objective correctness in roleplaying edition preferences. So much depends on your personal experiences, playstyles, and mood.<br /> <br /> A valid reason amounts to, &quot;I like the way it makes me feel.&quot;<br /> <br /> Really, you can only share ones opinion on what is a benefit or flaw. I know some V5 fans who sincerely think the Sabbat being returned to a mysterious thing or take out was a good idea. I believe they are wrong but I can't say for 100% they are because it's what they think and feel.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Author of <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Cthulhu-Armageddon-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01KUOM7SI/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982844&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Cthulhu+Armageddon\" target=\"_blank\">Cthulhu Armageddon</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Teenage-Weredeer-Bright-Falls-Mysteries-ebook/dp/B075TTN2FN/ref=sr_1_2?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982717&amp;sr=1-2&amp;keywords=Weredeer#customerReviews\" target=\"_blank\">I was a Teenage Weredeer</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Straight-Outta-Fangton-Comedic-Vampire-ebook/dp/B01KNHICCC/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982774&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Straight+Outta+Fangton\" target=\"_blank\">Straight Outta Fangton</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Lucifers-Star-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01MDM9MCT/ref=mt_kindle?_encoding=UTF8&amp;me=&amp;qid=\" target=\"_blank\">Lucifer's Star</a>, </i>and the <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Rules-Supervillainy-Saga-Book-ebook/dp/B07MB89S33/\" target=\"_blank\">Supervillainy Saga</a>.</i><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":12002,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","user":"CTPhipps","date":". 05-08-2021, 07:18 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","name":"CTPhipps","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12002_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13933"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-05-08T04:18:12-07:00","id":1447923,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Trippy</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1443592-the-official-v5-vs-v20-thread?p=1447899#post1447899\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I am reiterating the points about V20 because of the context of this thread being \u2018V5 vs V20\u2019.</div> </div> </div> </div>Perhaps you should ask the question, &quot;Why do you consider the flaws in V20's systems to be less troublesome than the flaws in V5's system,&quot; if you wish to have me or someone else expand on that point. The context of the thread also needs to include that edition warring is against the rules.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Why is it silly? </div> </div> </div>To be succinct: The point of combat is to remove the direct physical threat your character is facing (either beating them in combat, or escaping combat). The point of most social actions is to alter another character's course of action. There is an overlap where altering another character's course of action is because they are a threat to you that you need to remove, but everything else one might expect to do with social actions will never work properly if modeled after combat.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> I think that is a misinterpretation of what an \u2018Advance' is. </div> </div> </div>V5, p. 296-297:<br /> <br /> &quot;<b>Advance</b><br /> Working directly towards the goal(s) of the conflict: <u>this could be cozying up to an elder when vying for a seat on the council,</u> destroying evidence before getting over-whelmed, gathering influence in a housing project, hacking a security system before being discovered, Kissing students, etc. Note how-ever, that advance is not applicable to all conflicts. The prime example being combat, where there are no goals except hurting the opposition and/or getting the hell out of there. Depending on the conflict, a prior Maneuver (see below) might be required to advance effectively..Advances are usually run as an extended test (see p. 293) with the player rolling to accumulate as many wins/successes as possible.&quot;<br /> <br /> Emphasis mine: one of the examples is explicitly trying to impress a third party for political gain rather than engaging your opponent for that political position in a debate, or something of the sort.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> It clearly is part of a narrative that involves head-to-conflict, because the rule is listed and stated as being \u201cAn Additional Conflict Option\u201d right before Maneuvers. </div> </div> </div>V5, p. 296:<br /> <br /> &quot;<b>Additional Conflict Options</b><br /> All conflict actions need not be straight attacks on the opposition. In fact, most engagements involve a goal that does not solely rely on removing all enemies, and <u>there is no reason why players should be forced to confront their opponents head-on</u> when they can achieve their ends with other means. Consider the following action variants when engaged in a conflict of any kind:&quot;<br /> <br /> Emphasis mine. The Addition Conflict Options introductory paragraph directly states that one of the goals of the additional options present is to give players methods to avoid head-on confrontations.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> A 'prior maneuver\u2019 is exactly what you were describing as lacking before - it is something you can do in preparation for a conflict and as, it does not impinge on any action during the conflict itself. </div> </div> </div>V5, p. 297:<br /> <br /> &quot;<b>Maneuver</b><br /> This option involves getting into an advantaged position, either in order to be able to take other actions at all or get an advantage, such as flanking a foe, making sure you are alone with the subject of your desire, getting access to important people, finding cover from oncoming shots, etc. Depending on the situation, a successful maneuver should result in one of these benefits:<br /> ...<br /> <u>In some cases a maneuver is required to make an attack or advance towards the goal in the first place. Only after a successful maneuver can the character attack the intended target or advance towards the goal.</u> Example: finding the target in a city-wide conflict, arranging to be alone with the target in a conflict of seduction and intrigue, getting into position to take over a company.&quot;<br /> <br /> Emphasis mine, again. There is no statement in any of these sections that state you can start a Maneuver before the conflict beings.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> This isn\u2019t me trying to give you house rule, this is actually what is written in the rules of the text. </div> </div> </div>Please cite a passage that states that any Additional Conflict Option can be taken before a Conflict begins.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> In your story example, you would make an extended set of Advances towards the blackmailing goal, and these would potentially accumulate dice to add to the final roll. </div> </div> </div>Please cite a passage that allows the extended roll from the Advance option to be put towards a different Conflict action in the forms of a dice bonus. Just to head it off, a Cascading Extended Test, is a variant on a Series Test. The ability to roll successes over into the next roll is contained with the Test, it does not extend beyond the Test. While it is actually directly referenced for being a way to handle blackmail attempts, it is not included in Extended Conflicts, and thus isn't for when you're targeting someone significant enough to roll back at you instead of being abstracted into a Difficulty.<br /> <br /> To that last point, V5, page. 304:<br /> <br /> &quot;Social combat requires an opponent: someone who actively doesn\u2019t want you to succeed and who attempts to defeat you on the same ground on which you attack them. For social actions without such an opponent \u2013 persuasion of a disinterested audience, seduction of a victim, fast-talking your way past a military patrol, etc. \u2013 use normal resolution.&quot;<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> The impact of Audience isn\u2019t really in context, because it is a different type of social conflict. </div> </div> </div>V5, page 305:<br /> <br /> &quot;Willpower damage hurts most when others see your weakness. Add a damage modifier depending on the audience (just being present doesn\u2019t cut it, they also need to be interested in the outcome).&quot;<br /> <br /> Please cite where this different type of social conflict is detailed that changes the context of the above quote.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> With the WP thing, you can simply rule it that the stakes are higher than a single WP loss - if that is agreed previously as an outcome. </div> </div> </div>V5, page 304:<br /> <br /> &quot;As in One-Roll Conflict, it\u2019s important to set the stakes ahead of time; what happens to the winner of the social conflict and what happens to the loser?&quot;<br /> <br /> V5, page 299, under One-Roll Conflict:<br /> <br /> &quot;The more player characters that win, the better the results. If the majority of the player characters win, the opposition might for example break, fall down wounded, storm off in a fit of pique, surrender, or whatever else makes dramatic sense.<br /> ...<br /> Each player character then takes damage equal to the difference between their successes and twice the Difficulty.&quot;<br /> <br /> Please cite a passage that indicates that the setting stakes for advanced social conflict override how WP damage is applied. Please cite a passage that says stakes can be set as mechanical consideration such has who gets the most successes instead of the stakes being in-character goals each side has for the resolution of the conflict which is resolved by the number of successes rolled.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> The Audience factor really is for a particular type of social conflict where a character\u2019s confidence, reputation or face is at stake - and where the Audience clearly raises that stake - like a public debate as an obvious example. It doesn\u2019t necessarily apply to every type of social conflict. </div> </div> </div>Please cite a passage that supports this; esp. considering the Audience chart includes +0 for no audience.<br /> <br /> Though while we're here, V5 p. 305:<br /> <br /> &quot;Combatants roll their respective dice pools and compare numbers of successes. The combatant with more successes subtracts their opponent\u2019s successes and applies the result as damage to Willpower.&quot;<br /> <br /> Since social conflicts - once rolled, always result in Willpower damage if one side wins a roll, and Audience is always considered (even if +0 because nobody is there, or any other people present are not engaged in observing), then the assumption must be that all advanced social conflicts handled by the system are ones, &quot;where a character\u2019s confidence, reputation or face is at stake.&quot; Considering how vital WP is to vampires keeping their Beasts contained, draining a vampire's Willpower is definitely a risk to their confidence and reputation as they might not have the WP necessary to avoid Messy Crits and Beastial Failures if social conflicts don't go their way.<br /> <br /> Though this touches on a whole other issues with V5's social mechanics where engaging in social conflicts in Elysium is a ridiculously bad idea because of the risk of taking a big WP hit in a situation where you need WP the most to avoid breaking the customs of Elysium... which are there to provide a safe place for vampires to engage in social maneuvering without breaking out into violence; which means the social rules my Elysium a self-defeating concept.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-05-08T04:20:32-07:00","id":1447924,"title":"","content":"<span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Just a reminder, also, folks, that a lot of this is opinion and to not get too heated. There are no wrong answers. Which means there's no right answers.</span><br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Author of <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Cthulhu-Armageddon-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01KUOM7SI/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982844&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Cthulhu+Armageddon\" target=\"_blank\">Cthulhu Armageddon</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Teenage-Weredeer-Bright-Falls-Mysteries-ebook/dp/B075TTN2FN/ref=sr_1_2?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982717&amp;sr=1-2&amp;keywords=Weredeer#customerReviews\" target=\"_blank\">I was a Teenage Weredeer</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Straight-Outta-Fangton-Comedic-Vampire-ebook/dp/B01KNHICCC/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982774&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Straight+Outta+Fangton\" target=\"_blank\">Straight Outta Fangton</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Lucifers-Star-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01MDM9MCT/ref=mt_kindle?_encoding=UTF8&amp;me=&amp;qid=\" target=\"_blank\">Lucifer's Star</a>, </i>and the <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Rules-Supervillainy-Saga-Book-ebook/dp/B07MB89S33/\" target=\"_blank\">Supervillainy Saga</a>.</i><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","name":"CTPhipps","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12002_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13933"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-05-08T04:29:31-07:00","id":1447925,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CTPhipps</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1443592-the-official-v5-vs-v20-thread?p=1447920#post1447920\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I think that preference doesn't particularly require reasoning beyond emotional attachment or enthusiasm. If someone says, I like V20 because it's the one I've done with my friends for years and years then that's entirely valid just as if I said that I like V5 because of its heavy focus on the classic Chicago area of V:TM that had been ignored since Second Edition. Part of what I mentioned earlier when starting the thread is I don't think there's such a thing as objective correctness in roleplaying edition preferences. So much depends on your personal experiences, playstyles, and mood.<br /> <br /> A valid reason amounts to, &quot;I like the way it makes me feel.&quot;<br /> <br /> Really, you can only share ones opinion on what is a benefit or flaw. I know some V5 fans who sincerely think the Sabbat being returned to a mysterious thing or take out was a good idea. I believe they are wrong but I can't say for 100% they are because it's what they think and feel.</div> </div> </div> </div>That could be an argument, if people were arguing that. However, the emotional base it seems is often conflated with trying to find reasons to dislike the other, rather than honestly appraising why people feel the way they do.<br /> <br /> There has been a whole bulk of discussion - as the case in point - about V5\u2019s social conflict rules. A lot of the criticism seems to be presenting the rules in a way that is arguably misinterpreted or in some cases just asserting how they are supposedly 'broken\u2019 without any recourse beyond a personal preference for how things were done, or not done at all, in the previous edition. That, in itself, is not a good argument.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2517-trippy","name":"Trippy","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2517_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1018"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-05-08T04:50:08-07:00","id":1447926,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CTPhipps</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1443592-the-official-v5-vs-v20-thread?p=1447920#post1447920\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Yes, the absence of rules is a double edged sword, though.<br /> <br /> 1. If something doesn't have rules then that MIGHT be a sign that the books are incomplete in terms of development.<br /> <br /> 2. OTOH, it might be a sign that rules were not needed for it in the first place.<br /> <br /> Take for instance the fact that Generation is now something that your character can now choose like Clan. It's no longer a sink for your Backgrounds but a matter of how you wish to play the game.</div> </div> </div> </div>I don't think the &quot;just wing it&quot; issue is quite the same as &quot;absence of rules.&quot;<br /> <br /> The Generation example isn't a lack of rules, but a change of rules. Generation being something agreed on by the group is a rule just as much as Generation being a trait bought with char-gen resources is. An absence of rules would be the game saying that Generation is the thing that vampires have, and its very important, but the game never telling you how to determine what your character's Generation is.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-05-08T05:13:53-07:00","id":1447930,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Heavy Arms</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1443592-the-official-v5-vs-v20-thread?p=1447923#post1447923\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Perhaps you should ask the question, &quot;Why do you consider the flaws in V20's systems to be less troublesome than the flaws in V5's system,&quot; if you wish to have me or someone else expand on that point. The context of the thread also needs to include that edition warring is against the rules.</div> </div> </div> </div>Well, I think I have done. In the case of the combat rules, the proliferation of the dice being rolled in V20 means that the outcome is too randomized, too slow and the outcome less determined by character\u2019s nominal Ability levels. In the case of social conflict rules, V20 essentially doesn\u2019t have any, beyond role playing it and some loose ability rolls with indeterminate outcomes called by the ST. In V5, you still have those options, but it also provides a structured advanced set of rules on a par with other forms of conflict.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> To be succinct: The point of combat is to remove the direct physical threat your character is facing (either beating them in combat, or escaping combat). The point of most social actions is to alter another character's course of action. There is an overlap where altering another character's course of action is because they are a threat to you that you need to remove, but everything else one might expect to do with social actions will never work properly if modeled after combat. </div> </div> </div>The first point isn\u2019t necessarily the goal of combat at all. The point of combat is to win a particular outcome - a stake, if you will. A mugger isn\u2019t choosing to remove a direct physical threat, for example, they are looking to engage in a conflict to obtain something from a victim. A boxer in a ring isn\u2019t looking to remove a direct physical threat - they are looking to win a contest for prize money. The point of social conflict is also to win a particular outcome - in this respect it is no different to any conflict.<br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> V5, p. 296-297:<br /> <br /> &quot;<b>Advance</b><br /> Working directly towards the goal(s) of the conflict: <u>this could be cozying up to an elder when vying for a seat on the council,</u> destroying evidence before getting over-whelmed, gathering influence in a housing project, hacking a security system before being discovered, Kissing students, etc. Note how-ever, that advance is not applicable to all conflicts. The prime example being combat, where there are no goals except hurting the opposition and/or getting the hell out of there. Depending on the conflict, a prior Maneuver (see below) might be required to advance effectively..Advances are usually run as an extended test (see p. 293) with the player rolling to accumulate as many wins/successes as possible.&quot;<br /> <br /> Emphasis mine: one of the examples is explicitly trying to impress a third party for political gain rather than engaging your opponent for that political position in a debate, or something of the sort. </div> </div> </div>However, you were asking about how one could use planning to aid in a social conflict contest. This is how - and it is not ambiguous, it is stated in the section of the book providing options for conflict. You can\u2019t necessarily use these rules in every conflict but you can\u2019t plan for every conflict either - if the conflict is spontaneous, for example. I\u2019m not sure what you think you are arguing here - the rules you requested are present and useable.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> V5, p. 296:<br /> <br /> &quot;<b>Additional Conflict Options</b><br /> All conflict actions need not be straight attacks on the opposition. In fact, most engagements involve a goal that does not solely rely on removing all enemies, and <u>there is no reason why players should be forced to confront their opponents head-on</u> when they can achieve their ends with other means. Consider the following action variants when engaged in a conflict of any kind:&quot;<br /> <br /> Emphasis mine. The Addition Conflict Options introductory paragraph directly states that one of the goals of the additional options present is to give players methods to avoid head-on confrontations. </div> </div> </div>Sorry, you have misread your own quote. It says \u201c<i>there is no reason why players should be forced to confront their opponents head on\u201d. </i>It does not say anywhere that it is a \u2018goal' of the rules to avoid conflict but that most engagements involve a goal that doesn\u2019t rely on removing all enemies. What it is saying that you can prepare for a conflict by way of indirect (ie uncontested) extended rolls or simply that you can attack your opponent surreptitiously - by discrediting them for example. This is simply a misinterpretation of what is being said here. These are rules written under the header of \u2018Additional Conflict Options\u2019 - they are not rules designed to avoid conflict.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> V5, p. 297:<br /> <br /> &quot;<b>Maneuver</b><br /> This option involves getting into an advantaged position, either in order to be able to take other actions at all or get an advantage, such as flanking a foe, making sure you are alone with the subject of your desire, getting access to important people, finding cover from oncoming shots, etc. Depending on the situation, a successful maneuver should result in one of these benefits:<br /> ...<br /> <u>In some cases a maneuver is required to make an attack or advance towards the goal in the first place. Only after a successful maneuver can the character attack the intended target or advance towards the goal.</u> Example: finding the target in a city-wide conflict, arranging to be alone with the target in a conflict of seduction and intrigue, getting into position to take over a company.&quot;<br /> <br /> Emphasis mine, again. There is no statement in any of these sections that state you can start a Maneuver before the conflict beings.<br /> Please cite a passage that states that any Additional Conflict Option can be taken before a Conflict begins. Please cite a passage that allows the extended roll from the Advance option to be put towards a different Conflict action in the forms of a dice bonus. </div> </div> </div>It just told you that in the previous Advance section, that you could take an &quot;prior Maneuver\u201d. So it does, unambiguously, state that you can carry out a maneuver prior to combat. The quote is:<br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-size:14px\"><i><b><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Cormorant\">&quot;Depending on the conflict, a <u>prior Maneuver </u>(see below) might be required to advance effectively. </span></span><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Cormorant\">Advances are usually run as </span></span><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Cormorant\">an extended test (see p. 293) with </span></span><span style=\"font-family:Cormorant\"><span style=\"color:#000000\">the player rolling to accumulate as many wins/successes as possible.\u201d (P297 again!) </span></span></b></i></span><br /> <br /> You are quoting a lot of stuff here, but how on earth can you miss that basic point of what an Advance in a conflict is all about? It is an extended task that allows one to carry out prior maneuvers and apply the successes accumulated to the conflict in hand. It doesn\u2019t apply to some examples, like spontaneous conflict (given as an example), but it answers your question - clearly - about being able to plan a social conflict.<br /> <br /> I\u2019m going to have to request that you go back and read the section of the rules properly, before I go on to your other quotes and requests for rules references, because otherwise I think this process is going to be a waste of time.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":2517,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2517-trippy","user":"Trippy","date":". 05-08-2021, 08:57 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2517-trippy","name":"Trippy","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2517_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1018"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-05-08T07:01:29-07:00","id":1447934,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Trippy</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1443592-the-official-v5-vs-v20-thread?p=1447930#post1447930\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Well, I think I have done.</div> </div> </div> </div>No, you've simply bashed the V20 rules, something some of us have acknowledge are perfectly fair criticisms, and when we didn't expand on why that didn't stop us from consider V20 better anyway, you just bashed V20 again. For some reason... probably the bashing part.. people didn't treat it as a request for elaboration.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> The first point isn\u2019t necessarily the goal of combat at all. </div> </div> </div>What combat systems are you aware of that have possible outcomes other than:<br /> <br /> 1) One side does enough damage via physical harm that the other side is unwilling to or unable to fight back any longer.<br /> 2) One side successfully runs away rather than risk being on the losing end of #1.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> The point of combat is to win a particular outcome - a stake, if you will. </div> </div> </div>This is just a broader statement of the same thing to allow equivocations into non-combat examples.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> A mugger isn\u2019t choosing to remove a direct physical threat, for example, they are looking to engage in a conflict to obtain something from a victim. </div> </div> </div>A mugging isn't combat. It is ultimately a social conflict where the mugger attempts to use the threat of force to obtain compliance from a target to scared or too shocked to respond with force in return. If the victim of a mugging chooses to fight back, then it becomes combat, but then both the mugger and the victim are attempting to deal with a direct physical threat.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> A boxer in a ring isn\u2019t looking to remove a direct physical threat - they are looking to win a contest for prize money. </div> </div> </div>Sports, even &quot;combat sports&quot; aren't anything like a real fight. Trying to model sport boxing with combat rules generally fails to be satisfactory (though this is mostly because combat systems aren't tuned to combat sports in terms of pacing of outcomes). Of course, in boxing the way you win, is to neutralize the physical threat your opponent presents. You need to harm them more than they harm you.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> The point of social conflict is also to win a particular outcome - in this respect it is no different to any conflict. </div> </div> </div>Which is fine for general resolution mechanics, but not a convincing or rational argument when discussing the differences between dedicated sub-systems. If you're going to have dedicated social systems in your game, they're there to offer a more fulfilling play experience towards the expected results of social conflicts, rather than just be the generic resolution system restated. What makes them different from any other conflict is the reason to make a subsystem for them (or if you don't think there is, not to do so).<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> This is how - and it is not ambiguous, it is stated in the section of the book providing options for conflict. </div> </div> </div>It's not ambiguous.... but it's the exact opposite of what you're claiming. To point:<br /> <br /> &quot;<b>Additional Conflict Options</b><br /> All conflict actions need not be straight attacks on the opposition. In fact, most engagements involve a goal that does not solely rely on removing all enemies, and there is no reason why players should be forced to confront their opponents head-on when they can achieve their ends with other means. Consider the following action variants <u>when engaged in a conflict of any kind:</u>&quot;<br /> <br /> Change in emphasis mine.<br /> <br /> The Additional Conflict Options, in black and white, plain as day, state as a general rule that they apply &quot;when engaged in a conflict.&quot; Unless you can cite overt exceptions to this statement, you are house ruling the game, not presenting the RAW. The RAW says that an Advance or a Maneuver are things you do during a conflict, not in preparation for a conflict.<br /> <br /> You have also cited no evidence that an Advance can generate bonus dice to a future action (that's literally what a Maneuver does), so that's another house rule, not the RAW.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Sorry, you have misread your own quote. </div> </div> </div>No, you are misrepresenting my statement.<br /> <br /> I did not say, &quot;...that it is a \u2018goal' of the rules to avoid conflict...&quot;<br /> <br /> I said that the Additional Conflict Options explicitly provide options for approaching conflicts without head-on confrontations. This is in direct response to your assertion that, &quot;It clearly is part of a narrative that involves head-to-conflict, because the rule is listed and stated as being \u201cAn Additional Conflict Option\u201d right before Maneuvers.&quot; What you said is directly contradicted by the book. I'm not misreading anything, you're plain wrong here. Again, you're house ruling, not presenting the RAW.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> What it is saying that you can prepare for a conflict by way of indirect (ie uncontested) extended rolls or simply that you can attack your opponent surreptitiously - by discrediting them for example. </div> </div> </div>Please cite anything that supports the assertion that what that passage says means you can prepare for a conflict when, again, it explicitly says the the actions within, including Advance, are done while engaging in a conflict.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> It just told you that in the previous Advance section, that you could take an &quot;prior Maneuver\u201d. So it does, unambiguously, state that you can carry out a maneuver prior to combat. The quote is: </div> </div> </div>Nothing in this says the Maneuver takes place prior to the conflict beginning, and the general rules for this section say all of these options take place during a conflict.<br /> <br /> What the rules are saying, is that if you want to hack a system, but the system is a closed network, you spend your first action(s) of the conflict performing a Maneuver to gain access to the network. Once successful, you can then perform an Advance to hack the system and gain as many wins/successes as possible with you more limited time thanks to the extra step necessary.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> You are quoting a lot of stuff here, but how on earth can you miss that basic point of what an Advance in a conflict is all about? </div> </div> </div>Please demonstrate from the text how I've missed anything. The point of an Advance in a conflict is to try to win without directly engaging with an enemy. All of the examples demonstrate this: sucking up to a superior, engaging in a competition instead of directly opposing each other, hacking without getting noticed, destroying evidence before your home gets raided... the point of an Advance is to Advance towards you goal, but in a fashion that doesn't involve direct head-on conflict with another significant character.<br /> <br /> What in the text actually supports any other interpretation of the words printed?<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> It is an extended task that allows one to carry out prior maneuvers and apply the successes accumulated to the conflict in hand. </div> </div> </div>More house rules, not RAW.<br /> <br /> The rules say the exact opposite of &quot;allow one to carry out prior maneuvers,&quot; because it says you have to perform a prior maneuver before you can start an Advance. This is in both the Advance rules, &quot;Depending on the conflict, a prior Maneuver (see below) might be required to advance effectively.&quot; and the Maneuver rules, &quot;In some cases a maneuver is required to make an attack or advance towards the goal in the first place.&quot;<br /> <br /> Both phrases unambiguously say that sometimes you need to perform a Maneuver first, in order to justify being able to start an Advance.<br /> <br /> You have cited no passage that says you can bank Advance successes to other actions. Advances are treated as Extended tests. Extended tests do not carry over successes into whatever the next thing you're doing is. So, again, more house rules, no RAW.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> I\u2019m going to have to request that you go back and read the section of the rules properly,... </div> </div> </div>As far as I can tell, I've read the rules perfectly, and the only problem here is that for all your protestations about people making statement without any recourse to anything other than personal preference? That's precisely what you're doing. You're not talking about what the book says, you're talking about what you want the book to say.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> ...before I go on to your other quotes and requests for rules references, because otherwise I think this process is going to be a waste of time. </div> </div> </div>Well, that's one hell of a cop out. If this is a waste of time, it is 100% on you for refusing to actually engage in a discussion of the text like you claim you want people to do. You're not rationally analyzing the text, your misrepresenting it to assert how it's not broken without any back up from the words of the book itself.<br /> <br /> Do you have any idea how much of a pain in the ass it is for me to borrow a book during a pandemic just so I can type up what the books say, so I can show I'm talking about what's in the books while you're trying to make it sound like I'm just making it up so I can feel better about not liking V5? I'm lucky my friend is a cool guy and not charging me because I'm pretty sure I've spent more time with his book than he has by now. I'm pretty sure the only reason he takes it back is because he's helping a different friend run a V5 game who hasn't really STed before.<br /> <br /> So yeah, you could, at a bare minimum get to actually citing the text to show what rules you're talking about that say the things you're claiming they say. Because I can't find them in the book.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-05-08T07:06:22-07:00","id":1447935,"title":"","content":"<span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Guys, we're getting personal again. Should we move on or have we reached the thread's conclusion?</span>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Author of <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Cthulhu-Armageddon-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01KUOM7SI/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982844&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Cthulhu+Armageddon\" target=\"_blank\">Cthulhu Armageddon</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Teenage-Weredeer-Bright-Falls-Mysteries-ebook/dp/B075TTN2FN/ref=sr_1_2?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982717&amp;sr=1-2&amp;keywords=Weredeer#customerReviews\" target=\"_blank\">I was a Teenage Weredeer</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Straight-Outta-Fangton-Comedic-Vampire-ebook/dp/B01KNHICCC/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982774&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Straight+Outta+Fangton\" target=\"_blank\">Straight Outta Fangton</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Lucifers-Star-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01MDM9MCT/ref=mt_kindle?_encoding=UTF8&amp;me=&amp;qid=\" target=\"_blank\">Lucifer's Star</a>, </i>and the <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Rules-Supervillainy-Saga-Book-ebook/dp/B07MB89S33/\" target=\"_blank\">Supervillainy Saga</a>.</i><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","name":"CTPhipps","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12002_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13933"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-05-08T07:23:00-07:00","id":1447936,"title":"","content":"If I am missing a rule from V5 that actually addresses what I've asked for citations on, I would very much like to know that. If someone needs to DM it to me so the thread can move on, so be it.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-05-08T07:48:49-07:00","id":1447939,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Trippy</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1443592-the-official-v5-vs-v20-thread?p=1447930#post1447930\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Well, I think I have done. In the case of the combat rules, the proliferation of the dice being rolled in V20 means that the outcome is too randomized, too slow and the outcome less determined by character\u2019s nominal Ability levels.</div> </div> </div> </div>You seem to miss how probability works. More dice REDUCES randomness by pushing the outcome towards a bell curve distribution where relative attributes matter MORE not less.<br /> <br /> This isn\u2019t opinion; it\u2019s just how math works. More dice will always reduce the randomness of the outcome. By reducing the total number of tests in a conflict to just three from each side (and with smaller pools in general) you increase the odds of outlier results occuring. A d20 and 3d6 both have an average result of 10.5, but d20 has 1/20 chance of a 20 and a 1/20 chance of a 10. A roll of 3d6 has a 1/216 chance of an 18, but a 1/14.4 (15 times greater) chance of getting a 10.<br /> <br /> V20\u2019s multiple opposed dice tests may be slower, but they serve to push the results closer to the median outcome where the more skilled will defeat the less skilled more regularly.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1328-chris24601","name":"Chris24601","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"520"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-05-08T07:58:47-07:00","id":1447940,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Chris24601</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1443592-the-official-v5-vs-v20-thread?p=1447939#post1447939\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">By reducing the total number of tests in a conflict to just three from each side (and with smaller pools in general) you increase the odds of outlier results occuring.</div> </div> </div> </div>That by itself can actually be a good thing. Making combat less predictable can make it more fun just by virtue of being more tense. Though devil's in the details and all that when it comes to the total package.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-05-08T09:01:21-07:00","id":1447943,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CTPhipps</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1443592-the-official-v5-vs-v20-thread?p=1447920#post1447920\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I think everyone is giving valid arguments and discussions even if they're not persuaded. As stated, a lot of this is subjective and the thread has mostly remained civil because of it.<br /> <br /> Thumbs up on that folks.<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> Yes, the absence of rules is a double edged sword, though.<br /> <br /> 1. If something doesn't have rules then that MIGHT be a sign that the books are incomplete in terms of development.</div> </div> </div> </div>I absolutely agree. I've seen analysis of VTM1e that talks about how the game was radical at the time for suggesting social influence could essentially be LARPed in a TTRPG, although it was acknowledged in the same essay that very few people actually did this in practice.<br /> <br /> I think that's the origin of the barebones social rules, because people were initially expected to act out these scenes and the assumption it could just be roleplayed has persisted (for better or worse).<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> 2. OTOH, it might be a sign that rules were not needed for it in the first place.<br /> <br /> Take for instance the fact that Generation is now something that your character can now choose like Clan. It's no longer a sink for your Backgrounds but a matter of how you wish to play the game. </div> </div> </div>I quite like that change, too.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> I think that preference doesn't particularly require reasoning beyond emotional attachment or enthusiasm. If someone says, I like V20 because it's the one I've done with my friends for years and years then that's entirely valid just as if I said that I like V5 because of its heavy focus on the classic Chicago area of V:TM that had been ignored since Second Edition. Part of what I mentioned earlier when starting the thread is I don't think there's such a thing as objective correctness in roleplaying edition preferences. So much depends on your personal experiences, playstyles, and mood.<br /> <br /> A valid reason amounts to, &amp;quot;I like the way it makes me feel.&amp;quot;<br /> <br /> Really, you can only share ones opinion on what is a benefit or flaw. I know some V5 fans who sincerely think the Sabbat being returned to a mysterious thing or take out was a good idea. I believe they are wrong but I can't say for 100% they are because it's what they think and feel. </div> </div> </div>Exactly. And taste is always mediated by lots of subjective things--it's not an essential abstract that can be measured. <br /> <br /> Working in publishing, I have seen lots of editors resist diverse voices because 'I'm not seeing the quality I want', without acknowledging that they may have subjective values of quality that are culturally mediated. <br /> <br /> If all the British poetry editors go to, say, Oxford University, and have the same background, it's no surprise they all pick similar things to publish. That doesn't mean their 'canon' is objectively better.<br /> <br /> That said, I think you can justify your preferences. But you still have to acknowledge, at some level, that they're still just that. The critique can also have a constructive benefit.<br /> <br /> One thing that discussing things like the social rules does for me is give me more tools to adapt what is there in all editions. We're currently playing a V20-derived system with lots from VTR2e, some stuff from V5 and a little bit from Exalted 3e and Storypath.<br /> <br /> I think I am more likely to try V5 again in the near future because of, for example, Heavy Arms' posts, which have clarified for me or reminded me about why some things don't quite click. But if I know what the problem is (e.g., WP damage based on audience only), I can consciously address that next time (e.g., by basing the WP damage on more than just who's present).","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Writer, publisher, performer<br /> Mostly he/his, sometimes she/her IRL <a href=\"https://adam-lowe.com\" target=\"_blank\">https://adam-lowe.com</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5291-adambeyoncelowe","name":"adambeyoncelowe","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5291_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2802"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-05-08T09:27:06-07:00","id":1447946,"title":"","content":"<span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Also, to clarify one last thing, I've been extra lenient for this thread but the next time anyone dismisses another posters views or their work then they will be ejected from this thread.<br /> <br /> Disagreements are fine but bashing is not nor are personal attacks.<br /> <br /> Final warning. </span><br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Author of <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Cthulhu-Armageddon-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01KUOM7SI/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982844&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Cthulhu+Armageddon\" target=\"_blank\">Cthulhu Armageddon</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Teenage-Weredeer-Bright-Falls-Mysteries-ebook/dp/B075TTN2FN/ref=sr_1_2?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982717&amp;sr=1-2&amp;keywords=Weredeer#customerReviews\" target=\"_blank\">I was a Teenage Weredeer</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Straight-Outta-Fangton-Comedic-Vampire-ebook/dp/B01KNHICCC/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982774&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Straight+Outta+Fangton\" target=\"_blank\">Straight Outta Fangton</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Lucifers-Star-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01MDM9MCT/ref=mt_kindle?_encoding=UTF8&amp;me=&amp;qid=\" target=\"_blank\">Lucifer's Star</a>, </i>and the <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Rules-Supervillainy-Saga-Book-ebook/dp/B07MB89S33/\" target=\"_blank\">Supervillainy Saga</a>.</i><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","name":"CTPhipps","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12002_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13933"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-05-08T11:24:39-07:00","id":1447956,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Heavy Arms</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1443592-the-official-v5-vs-v20-thread?p=1447940#post1447940\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">That by itself can actually be a good thing. Making combat less predictable can make it more fun just by virtue of being more tense. Though devil's in the details and all that when it comes to the total package.</div> </div> </div> </div>Not disagreeing. D&amp;D uses a d20 for an even distribution across the full range for a reason. The only thing I wished to counter was the idea that more rolling equals more randomness when every textbook on probability will tell you the opposite is true.<br /> <br /> It\u2019s fine to dislike V20 for the sheer number of die rolls required. I\u2019ve played both with smashing attack and damage together (weapon type determined the difficulty... so an unarmed strike is diff 8, a knife is 7, a handgun is 6, a rifle 5-4, a .50 cal would be diff 3) with damage determined by margin over the opposed roll of dodge+soak (soak reducing the difficulty of their test) and adapting Requiem\u2019s LARP rules (add traits to the result of a 1d10 or 1-10 card draw) in place of dice pools simply to reduce the sheer amount of dice required. But I did both of those knowing that this would increase the variance of the outcomes not with the idea that it would reduce the randomness.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1328-chris24601","name":"Chris24601","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"520"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-05-08T12:01:59-07:00","id":1447959,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Chris24601</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1443592-the-official-v5-vs-v20-thread?p=1447939#post1447939\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">You seem to miss how probability works. More dice REDUCES randomness by pushing the outcome towards a bell curve distribution where relative attributes matter MORE not less.<br /> <br /> This isn\u2019t opinion; it\u2019s just how math works. More dice will always reduce the randomness of the outcome. By reducing the total number of tests in a conflict to just three from each side (and with smaller pools in general) you increase the odds of outlier results occuring. A d20 and 3d6 both have an average result of 10.5, but d20 has 1/20 chance of a 20 and a 1/20 chance of a 10. A roll of 3d6 has a 1/216 chance of an 18, but a 1/14.4 (15 times greater) chance of getting a 10.<br /> <br /> V20\u2019s multiple opposed dice tests may be slower, but they serve to push the results closer to the median outcome where the more skilled will defeat the less skilled more regularly.</div> </div> </div> </div>Well, this is wrong - because you are rolling <i>contested</i> dice pools through a chain, with each individual die having a fixed target. If you roll more dice you are changing the range of the potential number of success, not increasing the likelihood of a median point average You are not rolling a bell curve of results - you are rolling dice pools that are weighted towards accumulating lower numbers of success rather than higher number of success. You are citing the wrong mathematical model, because we are not talking about rolling 3D6 like in D&amp;D or GURPS, so this is not how the maths work in dice pool rolling.<br /> <br /> You can talk textbooks if you like, but this statistical anomaly has been analysed mathematically before a number of times before. Here is a spreadsheet link: <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/spreadsheets/d/1OK1pf7N3tIoPYYhX0kL37s-awQ0owwKNZlopwZ4EjHI/edit#gid=0\" target=\"_blank\">https://docs.google.com/spreadsheets...jHI/edit#gid=0</a><br /> <br /> Unlike other rolls in V20, you roll for initiative, then an opposed attack roll and then an opposed damage roll. So, for example, you may have a big attack pool of 8, and might roll 3 or 4 successes, but this will be reduced by the number of successes that the opponent will roll, and then you still have to roll again for another contested roll for damage. It is the number of <i>opposed rolls in the chain</i> that increases the randomness, compared to a single roll. The roll tends towards smaller amounts of damage being incrementally applied despite rolling loads of dice. it means that combat outcomes - ie damage - generally moves forward in small increments. This levies the overall chances of winning towards somebody with less skill but lucky rolls, as opposed to more skill but unlucky rolls. The advantage of having bigger dice pools is reduced by the number of tiers in which you roll them, so the <i>overall outcome</i> is more randomized - and means that the combat is more likely to be protracted regardless.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":2517,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2517-trippy","user":"Trippy","date":". 05-08-2021, 05:16 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2517-trippy","name":"Trippy","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2517_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1018"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-05-08T13:43:47-07:00","id":1447977,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Heavy Arms</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1443592-the-official-v5-vs-v20-thread?p=1447934#post1447934\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> No, you've simply bashed the V20 rules, something some of us have acknowledge are perfectly fair criticisms, and when we didn't expand on why that didn't stop us from consider V20 better anyway, you just bashed V20 again. For some reason... probably the bashing part.. people didn't treat it as a request for elaboration.</div> </div> </div> </div>I haven\u2019t bashed V20 rules. I have given criticisms of V20 rules, compared and contrasted them with V5 and given indication as to why V5 rules are better. If you acknowledge they are fair criticisms, then how can it be bashing as well?<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> What combat systems are you aware of that have possible outcomes other than:<br /> <br /> 1) One side does enough damage via physical harm that the other side is unwilling to or unable to fight back any longer.<br /> 2) One side successfully runs away rather than risk being on the losing end of #1. </div> </div> </div>The V5 system operates on the basis that conflict is based on agreed stakes, so this is one example in hand of a game that can base combat on outcomes that do not require doing enough damage that disables the opposition. There are other games that also work on this basis - Fate, that you have already mentioned and the recent Dune game (combat is based on maneuvering Assets). However, you are shifting the gaol posts here. Your original point was that physical combat is only about reducing the risk of harm, and it isn\u2019t. Stakes and outcomes can vary. It is also an observation that many combat systems in games are not actually reflections of how combat works in real life - they are abstracted into game terms.The same can be true of social conflict systems.<br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> This is just a broader statement of the same thing to allow equivocations into non-combat examples. </div> </div> </div>It is not the same thing as what you said, and the examples given (again below) point to that original statement.<br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> A mugging isn't combat. It is ultimately a social conflict where the mugger attempts to use the threat of force to obtain compliance from a target to scared or too shocked to respond with force in return. If the victim of a mugging chooses to fight back, then it becomes combat, but then both the mugger and the victim are attempting to deal with a direct physical threat. </div> </div> </div>A mugging is combat - it is physical violence based on an ambush of sorts. It can be handled by the combat systems of most games too. In V5 it can be handled through Advances.<br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Sports, even &quot;combat sports&quot; aren't anything like a real fight. Trying to model sport boxing with combat rules generally fails to be satisfactory (though this is mostly because combat systems aren't tuned to combat sports in terms of pacing of outcomes). Of course, in boxing the way you win, is to neutralize the physical threat your opponent presents. You need to harm them more than they harm you. </div> </div> </div>A boxing match is a real fight. The purpose of the bout is not to 'remove the direct physical threat your character is facing\u2019. If they wanted to do that, the boxer simply needs to leave the ring. They don\u2019t do this because there is another objective to the fight than simply removing the physical threat of the opponent.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Which is fine for general resolution mechanics, but not a convincing or rational argument when discussing the differences between dedicated sub-systems. If you're going to have dedicated social systems in your game, they're there to offer a more fulfilling play experience towards the expected results of social conflicts, rather than just be the generic resolution system restated. What makes them different from any other conflict is the reason to make a subsystem for them (or if you don't think there is, not to do so). </div> </div> </div>I think the social conflict system in V5 is a fulfilling play experience. It isn\u2019t generic - the outcome and contests are determined by the ST and players through their predeclared stakes and the mechanics are dynamic in creating drama.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> It's not ambiguous.... but it's the exact opposite of what you're claiming. To point:<br /> <br /> &quot;<b>Additional Conflict Options</b><br /> All conflict actions need not be straight attacks on the opposition. In fact, most engagements involve a goal that does not solely rely on removing all enemies, and there is no reason why players should be forced to confront their opponents head-on when they can achieve their ends with other means. Consider the following action variants <u>when engaged in a conflict of any kind:</u>&quot;<br /> <br /> Change in emphasis mine.<br /> <br /> The Additional Conflict Options, in black and white, plain as day, state as a general rule that they apply &quot;when engaged in a conflict.&quot; Unless you can cite overt exceptions to this statement, you are house ruling the game, not presenting the RAW. The RAW says that an Advance or a Maneuver are things you do during a conflict, not in preparation for a conflict.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> You have also cited no evidence that an Advance can generate bonus dice to a future action (that's literally what a Maneuver does), so that's another house rule, not the RAW. </div> </div> </div>It literally says that in the Advance section, that I have quoted to you RAW.<br /> <br /> No, you are misrepresenting my statement.<br /> <br /> I did not say, &quot;...that it is a \u2018goal' of the rules to avoid conflict...&quot;<br /> <br /> I said that the Additional Conflict Options explicitly provide options for approaching conflicts without head-on confrontations. This is in direct response to your assertion that, &quot;It clearly is part of a narrative that involves head-to-conflict, because the rule is listed and stated as being \u201cAn Additional Conflict Option\u201d right before Maneuvers.&quot; What you said is directly contradicted by the book. I'm not misreading anything, you're plain wrong here. Again, you're house ruling, not presenting the RAW. </div> </div> </div>Your emphasized words point out that you can approach all conflict through alternative, surreptitious means. It isn\u2019t suggesting that Advances are means of avoiding conflict, but that you can win a conflict through alternative means that don\u2019t involve direct opposition. For example, you could stab somebody in the back rather than head on.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Please cite anything that supports the assertion that what that passage says means you can prepare for a conflict when, again, it explicitly says the the actions within, including Advance, are done while engaging in a conflict.<br /> <br /> <br /> Nothing in this says the Maneuver takes place prior to the conflict beginning, and the general rules for this section say all of these options take place during a conflict. </div> </div> </div>It literally says it is a \u2018prior maneuver\u2019, the whole Advance section describes that these actions can be done in preparation for combat, and that they are normally done through accumulating successes over extended rolls.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> What the rules are saying, is that if you want to hack a system, but the system is a closed network, you spend your first action(s) of the conflict performing a Maneuver to gain access to the network. Once successful, you can then perform an Advance to hack the system and gain as many wins/successes as possible with you more limited time thanks to the extra step necessary. </div> </div> </div>You can apply Advance rules this way, but you can also set up a chain to accumulate success - precisely as stated in the RAW. What you are not acknowledging, I think, is that an extended task can be used to accumulate successes against a target and that it can only be used in a chain of discrete rolls. However, RAW states that there are different types of extended rolls, and in this instance, the point of an Advance in a conflict roll is to usually accumulate successes to affect the outcome of the conflict roll. It is precisely how one could use preparation towards a social conflict roll - which is what you were asking about.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Please demonstrate from the text how I've missed anything. The point of an Advance in a conflict is to try to win without directly engaging with an enemy. All of the examples demonstrate this: sucking up to a superior, engaging in a competition instead of directly opposing each other, hacking without getting noticed, destroying evidence before your home gets raided... the point of an Advance is to Advance towards you goal, but in a fashion that doesn't involve direct head-on conflict with another significant character.<br /> <br /> What in the text actually supports any other interpretation of the words printed? </div> </div> </div>Again, I have literally quite that to you already.<br /> <br /> <i><span style=\"font-size:14px\"><b><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Cormorant\">&quot;Depending on the conflict, a <u>prior Maneuver </u>(see below) might be required to advance effectively. </span></span><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Cormorant\">Advances are usually run as </span></span><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Cormorant\">an extended test (see p. 293) with </span></span><span style=\"font-family:Cormorant\"><span style=\"color:#000000\">the player rolling to accumulate as many wins/successes as possible.\u201d (P297 again!)</span></span></b></span></i><br /> <br /> The term \u2018Advance\u2019 literally means you are taking these actions prior to a conflict, but applying them to the conflict<i> in advance </i>and/or taking a maneuver <i>prior </i>to the conflict itself. Again it states that these tests are \u2018usually\u201d run as an extended test with a player rolling to <i>accumulate</i> successes.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> More house rules, not RAW. </div> </div> </div>I\u2019ve not discussed any house rules, whatsoever. This is all in the book - rules as written.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> The rules say the exact opposite of &quot;allow one to carry out prior maneuvers,&quot; because it says you have to perform a prior maneuver before you can start an Advance. This is in both the Advance rules, &quot;Depending on the conflict, a prior Maneuver (see below) might be required to advance effectively.&quot; and the Maneuver rules, &quot;In some cases a maneuver is required to make an attack or advance towards the goal in the first place.&quot;<br /> Both phrases unambiguously say that sometimes you need to perform a Maneuver first, in order to justify being able to start an Advance. </div> </div> </div>No they do not. The quote is directly above and it says, as part of the entree about Advances lest we forget, that a prior maneuver <u>migh</u>t be required <u>in some circumstances</u> to Advance, but goes on to say that Advances are <u>usually</u> run as an extended test with the player rolling to <u>accumulate</u> successes.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> You have cited no passage that says you can bank Advance successes to other actions. Advances are treated as Extended tests. Extended tests do not carry over successes into whatever the next thing you're doing is. So, again, more house rules, no RAW. </div> </div> </div>It is absolutely written in the rules that Extended tests can be done in different ways - Standard, Series, Hard or Cascading (P293-294). One of these ways can be to accumulate successes to reach a target. This is expanded upon by the quote above to show how you can use Extended tests to accumulate successes as Advances towards a particular conflict. That is RAW - not House rules.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> As far as I can tell, I've read the rules perfectly, and the only problem here is that for all your protestations about people making statement without any recourse to anything other than personal preference? That's precisely what you're doing. You're not talking about what the book says, you're talking about what you want the book to say.<br /> <br /> Well, that's one hell of a cop out. If this is a waste of time, it is 100% on you for refusing to actually engage in a discussion of the text like you claim you want people to do. You're not rationally analyzing the text, your misrepresenting it to assert how it's not broken without any back up from the words of the book itself.<br /> <br /> Do you have any idea how much of a pain in the ass it is for me to borrow a book during a pandemic just so I can type up what the books say, so I can show I'm talking about what's in the books while you're trying to make it sound like I'm just making it up so I can feel better about not liking V5? I'm lucky my friend is a cool guy and not charging me because I'm pretty sure I've spent more time with his book than he has by now. I'm pretty sure the only reason he takes it back is because he's helping a different friend run a V5 game who hasn't really STed before.<br /> <br /> So yeah, you could, at a bare minimum get to actually citing the text to show what rules you're talking about that say the things you're claiming they say. Because I can't find them in the book. </div> </div> </div>You haven\u2019t read the rules perfectly - evidently, by the interpretation you are giving here. So it is not a cop out to ask you to go back over this salient point - which is specifically about the point you were disputing - before moving on to other things. Do this and we can.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":2517,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2517-trippy","user":"Trippy","date":". 05-08-2021, 04:56 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2517-trippy","name":"Trippy","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2517_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1018"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-05-08T13:47:26-07:00","id":1447979,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Trippy</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1443592-the-official-v5-vs-v20-thread?p=1447959#post1447959\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Well, this is wrong - because you are rolling <i>contested</i> dice pools through a chain. You are not rolling a bell curve of results - you are rolling dice pools that are weighted towards accumulating lower numbers of success rather than higher number of success. You are citing the wrong mathematical model, because we are not talking about rolling 3D6 like in D&amp;D or GURPS, so this is not how the maths work in dice pool rolling.</div> </div> </div> </div>3d6 vs. 1d20 is just an example of how, despite having the same average result, the more dice you roll the more the results tend towards a bell curve result. And that's the problem with the dataset you linked to, it only shows the average not the full distributions.<br /> <br /> Contested pools actually push things towards the average range of a bell curve distribution faster because its effectively adding both sets into a single outcome... basically X dice result -Y dice result.<br /> <br /> Dice pools by their very nature produce bell curve distributions that favor the average outcome because you have multiple dice rolling for passes and the resultant value is the number of passes you get... i.e. the more dice you roll the closer you will skew on average to the average pass rate. You can actually calculate this out on anydice.com.<br /> <br /> <a href=\"https://anydice.com/program/2211b\" target=\"_blank\">Here's</a> a link for the dice results of 10 dice at difficulty 6 (you can change the number of dice and difficulty in the formula above to check out other distributions). There is not an equal chance of getting 0-10 successes from rolling those 10 dice. More than half of all rolls (52.38%) will fall between 3-5 successes while there is only a 0.1% chance of scoring 10 successes. There is a 13.8% chance of getting 6 successes though.<br /> <br /> When you add in an opposing roll the number of successes countered will similarly fall into a bell curve distribution and subtracting that set from the attackers will push the results even further towards a large percentage of the outcomes falling closer to the average results with those results determined almost entirely by who's traits are higher and/or who can get the lowest difficulty to roll against (because 6 dice at difficulty 4 will score between 3-5 successes 64.55% of the time so a -2 difficulty in V20 can be worth as much as 4 bonus dice in V20).<br /> <br /> So again, its fine to say that you feel rolling so many dice is slower than making fewer checks (I don't even think that's a matter of opinion that it would) and its also fine to say you prefer a system with fewer dice rolls, but the math is the math and the math says the more dice you roll the more the results will conform to the average because the standard deviation is reduced with each additional die involved in the overall resolution.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1328-chris24601","name":"Chris24601","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"520"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-05-08T13:48:43-07:00","id":1447982,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Trippy</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1443592-the-official-v5-vs-v20-thread?p=1447977#post1447977\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">You haven\u2019t read the rules perfectly - evidently, by the interpretation you are giving here. So it is not a cop out to ask you to go back over this salient point - which is specifically about the point you were disputing - before moving on to other things. Do this and we can.</div> </div> </div> </div><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">This is exactly the sort of thing that I was warning repeatedly against. Please leave the thread.</span>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Author of <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Cthulhu-Armageddon-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01KUOM7SI/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982844&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Cthulhu+Armageddon\" target=\"_blank\">Cthulhu Armageddon</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Teenage-Weredeer-Bright-Falls-Mysteries-ebook/dp/B075TTN2FN/ref=sr_1_2?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982717&amp;sr=1-2&amp;keywords=Weredeer#customerReviews\" target=\"_blank\">I was a Teenage Weredeer</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Straight-Outta-Fangton-Comedic-Vampire-ebook/dp/B01KNHICCC/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982774&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Straight+Outta+Fangton\" target=\"_blank\">Straight Outta Fangton</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Lucifers-Star-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01MDM9MCT/ref=mt_kindle?_encoding=UTF8&amp;me=&amp;qid=\" target=\"_blank\">Lucifer's Star</a>, </i>and the <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Rules-Supervillainy-Saga-Book-ebook/dp/B07MB89S33/\" target=\"_blank\">Supervillainy Saga</a>.</i><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","name":"CTPhipps","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12002_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13933"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-05-08T15:09:28-07:00","id":1447989,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Chris24601</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1443592-the-official-v5-vs-v20-thread?p=1447979#post1447979\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">So again, its fine to say that you feel rolling so many dice is slower than making fewer checks (I don't even think that's a matter of opinion that it would) and its also fine to say you prefer a system with fewer dice rolls, but the math is the math and the math says the more dice you roll the more the results will conform to the average because the standard deviation is reduced with each additional die involved in the overall resolution.</div> </div> </div> </div>Something that might be worth analyzing because I don't think I've bothered since Exalted 2e came out, is where V5's infliction point is regarding the diminishing returns of reducing standard deviation.<br /> <br /> One of the things that came out of talking about Ex2 moving to two-roll combat (the attack rolls to hit, and for damage, while resisting both is by static value for the defender), was that there were already so many dice involved in resolving two rolls (Exalted has big dice-pools) that dropping rolling for defense didn't meaningfully change anything. The deviation was already narrowed to the point where changes wouldn't even appear at two sig figs when Exalts were tossing down at full strength.<br /> <br /> Regardless of a desire to keep V5 far away from that because of the aforementioned tensions of it, or for people considering house rules and want to know how far you can push in certain directions before the effort becomes wasted in a practical sense, it would be an interesting data point to have on hand that I don't know of anyone working out.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-05-08T23:50:53-07:00","id":1448024,"title":"","content":"Personally, I wouldn't run a mugging as combat, as that's all geared towards inflicting damage and VTM can be lethal in any edition. I'd rather run it as an extended contest where no to minimal damage is caused. <br /> <br /> E.g., a mugging could be Wits + Stealth v Perception + Alertness to get close enough. Then either Dexterity + Larceny or Dexterity + Brawl to take what you want versus the target's Dexterity + Athletics or Dexterity + Brawl, with the aim being not to injure but to snatch, evade or immobilise, etc.<br /> <br /> Boxing probably would be combat, but you could argue that it obeys stricter rules--the intent isn't an all-out brawl but a slow match of skill and training. So that could also be an extended contest if you wanted. If it were combat, you'd want to pull your punches enough to avoid accidental murder.<br /> <br /> Old school VTM is considerably more lethal when people don't use their action to defend every time. But that favours the person with the higher initiative.<br /> <br /> My players rarely use their action to dodge or block, preferring to save their action for an attack. The exception is social- or mental-focussed characters who prefer to use their turn using all-out defence. But that might just be our table.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Writer, publisher, performer<br /> Mostly he/his, sometimes she/her IRL <a href=\"https://adam-lowe.com\" target=\"_blank\">https://adam-lowe.com</a>","edited":{"userid":5291,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5291-adambeyoncelowe","user":"adambeyoncelowe","date":". 05-09-2021, 02:54 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5291-adambeyoncelowe","name":"adambeyoncelowe","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5291_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2802"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-05-09T01:04:46-07:00","id":1448027,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>adambeyoncelowe</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1443592-the-official-v5-vs-v20-thread?p=1448024#post1448024\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Personally, I wouldn't run a mugging as combat, as that's all geared towards inflicting damage and VTM can be lethal in any edition. I'd rather run it as an extended contest where no to minimal damage is caused.</div> </div> </div> </div>V5's four types of Extended tests is actually one of the better little change to the core mechanics. Using a series or cascading test for a mugging makes a lot of sense if the PCs are doing the mugging. It breaks down a bit if the PCs are getting mugged.... but I'm not sure that's all that common in VtM and most vampires can easily turn a mugging into a chance for a quick snack easily enough however you want to run it.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Boxing probably would be combat, but you could argue that it obeys stricter rules--the intent isn't an all-out brawl but a slow match of skill and training. So that could also be an extended contest if you wanted. If it were combat, you'd want to pull your punches enough to avoid accidental murder. </div> </div> </div>The big problem is pacing. If you ran boxing as combat, it would be over in the first round. Even if you just did one exchange per boxing round, actually making it the distance would be extremely rare even in divisions where TKOs and KOs are extremely rare. You'd need to house rule in something for the rest between rounds to help mitigate the relatively small Health tracks of of WoD characters so they can shed some of the damage inflicted and extend the bout out to a satisfactory length.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> My players rarely use their action to dodge or block, preferring to save their action for an attack. The exception is social- or mental-focussed characters who prefer to use their turn using all-out defence. But that might just be our table. </div> </div> </div>V20 definitely pushed things back into this direction with the return of splitting dice-pools. Attacking and defending IME were more common in Revised where the multiple action penalty wasn't as punishing to combat focused characters. The declaration phase, and aborting to defense option also tend to favor attacking, and if necessary aborting to defense.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-05-09T01:28:34-07:00","id":1448030,"title":"","content":"Yeah, pacing is definitely hard in combat if you're using it to simulate boxing. Does any edition of VTM have actual rules for pulling your punches? <br /> <br /> I guess boxing gloves probably reduce the damage somewhat, and it would be bashing, but it's still going to be over much quicker than most RL boxing matches. And stunning only requires more damage than your Stamina for mortals.<br /> <br /> So I do think extended tests will probably make more sense. Then you can use more tactics and variety (e.g., Intelligence + Brawl, Wits + Athletics, Perception + Medicine, etc).","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Writer, publisher, performer<br /> Mostly he/his, sometimes she/her IRL <a href=\"https://adam-lowe.com\" target=\"_blank\">https://adam-lowe.com</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5291-adambeyoncelowe","name":"adambeyoncelowe","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5291_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2802"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-05-09T02:18:21-07:00","id":1448035,"title":"","content":"For boxing, I'd increase the difficulty to strike/reduce difficulty to block; the enemy knows you can only use a limited number of moves against a limited part of the body, and while the damage potential of gloved hands are disputed, their size does make it slightly harder to get round defences. V20 can do all this, V5 struggles. Mortals might also make stamina checks every few rounds or be at a penalty.<br /> <br /> Most other combat sports don't last nearly as long, so they're fine.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25794-mywifeisscary","name":"MyWifeIsScary","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25794_2.png","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3711"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-05-09T02:31:56-07:00","id":1448037,"title":"","content":"I don't believe pulling your punches is covered in VtM. Though it wouldn't be hard to make rules for.<br /> <br /> Boxing gloves do not do anything to reduce the damage the punches do. They protect the puncher's hand from developing breaks. Having been hit with bare knuckles and gloves? They feel different, and gloved hits can feel like they didn't hit as hard at first. I guess it's kind of like bare knuckle punches sting more upfront and that sudden very intense pain masks the deeper tissue bruising to an extent. Gloved hits kinda go the other way where you don't have that same &quot;wow shit that hurt&quot; reaction, but then you try to use whatever just got hit and then you feel the pain of it.<br /> <br /> That all said, you could say that boxing gloves making it slightly harder to land a blow, at least in a regulation match (in a street fight this wouldn't really matter). A standard modern boxing posture is designed so that the larger surface area created by the glove is more likely to land on your arms, or glance off your arms, making it harder to get solid his on vital areas. But this only works because a lot of areas are off limits to attack. If you look at older boxing stances, and most martial arts stances, the arms are projected much farther out from the body than a modern boxer because they need to defend against a larger number of angles of attack.<br /> <br /> OK... probably went into too much detail there...<br /> <br /> I've had the best luck with modifying the CofD 2e Chase rules for combat sports. Boxing in particular works well because you can use holding onto/taking the Edge as a way to simulate the judge's scoring for a bout to the decision. Boxing abstracted out to this level doesn't need too many roll options, but the players can still get creative. Mostly you'd be picking a Physical Attribute + Brawl: Strength for trying to TKO/KO, Dexterity for trying to land clean hits for the judges or pummel an injury, or Stamina to focus more on trying to exhaust your opponent first (this is basically the Rope-a-Dope). But no reason to not consider other options if they make sense.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-05-09T02:36:15-07:00","id":1448039,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MyWifeIsScary</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1443592-the-official-v5-vs-v20-thread?p=1448035#post1448035\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Most other combat sports don't last nearly as long, so they're fine.</div> </div> </div> </div>That seems hard to generalize about. UFC matches tend to be around half as long as boxing matches... which is still a lot of time. Fencing exchanges tend to be over exceedingly fast (so fast they almost cause problems in the other direction where winning initiative is all that matters).","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-05-09T09:50:12-07:00","id":1448050,"title":"","content":"Eh. I can't claim to know too much about UFC (I've done a <i>lot </i>of martial arts growing up, but not MMA and sitting down to watch competitions? Rarely) , but grappling slows the competition down a lot more than striking, and I think the ring size is larger so striking is slowed down a bit with the extra space. You've also got a lot of bans on moves that would end fights faster, because those moves present a hazard to contestants and few fighters want to risk their careers or even death on dangerous stuff (and I'm given to understand a lot of the rules there to give BJJ an advantage because the founders of UFC were into BJJ and made money from it) <br /> <br /> Mortals doing bashing damage and not hitting the head that much might explain it.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25794-mywifeisscary","name":"MyWifeIsScary","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25794_2.png","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3711"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-05-09T14:00:18-07:00","id":1448065,"title":"","content":"OK.... we're probably getting way off-topic here, so I'll trying to bring things back after a bit more combat sports nerding on my part:<br /> <br /> The pace of combat sports is really complicated because that's just so many factors. Like, I pointed to earlier fencing happens insanely fast. An average fencing exchange lasts around six seconds, and will involve dozens of moves for both fencers. Standard competition fencing is to 5 points. Foil and epee are grueling competitions though, and frequently don't hit 5 points before regulation 3 minutes are up (somewhere between 15-20 exchanges since there are generally pauses of a few seconds as they reset and evaluate tactics). The muscles that let you fight that fast fatigue very quickly, so it takes an insane amount of body condition to actually keep up that long. Sabre tends to go much faster and requires less endurance. The only difference? Sabre lets you slash and thrust, not just thrust, so winning on 5 points before time is way more common. Boxing and martial arts based sports generally would think of 3 minutes as nothing for a competitive fighter, but that's because it's a completely different set of stresses on the body. It's like sprinters vs. marathon runners; the general idea of running from A to B is the same, but what you're asking the body to do in the process is radically different. Then you toss hurdlers into the mix and it gets even more insane to try to model any of this in a way that reflects the differences between them all.<br /> <br /> ----------------<br /> <br /> <br /> This does actually let me come back to answer an question that was lingering though:<br /> <br /> Why put up with V20's clunky combat system and slapdash social mechanics? Because options. V5 does a respectable job of trying to not get bogged down in details that might matter to an enthusiast such as myself, but really don't matter to playing the game, but in the end the advanced systems end up too much of a bad compromise where you're in a middle ground that's not really satisfactory to me. The added details aren't detailed enough to capture enough nuances to make me feel like the extra effort pays off rather than just using the standard resolution mechanics. V20's mechanics give their options enough differentiation that it actually feels like the process feels like a meaningful level of granularity while still abstract.<br /> <br /> For example, in V20, I can make a vampire that's actually good at fighting other vampires with guns. Guns aren't an easy choice for a vampire, because vampires are very resilient to bullets. And I'm not even talking about getting into some of the boardering on sci-fi ammunition VtM has let into the games over the years. But with a lot of system mastery, I once made a character that was basically vampire John Wick. He averaged ~5 Bashing damage after soak and halving in one fight, and a lot people apparently don't realize that if you have the damage output, Bashing torpors vampires just the same as Lethal does. Pulling that off required a constant use of taking advantage of all those little system details that V5 cut out to make things faster. And it wasn't like this was some sort of busted OP build... outside of the advantage of range, you could have easily out DPSed him with close combat attacks and Potence. And this wasn't a trenchcoat and katanas, or Vampions sort of game. My character quickly became a Scourge, and was angling for Sheriff, and his reputation for doing the equivalent of killing three guys with a pencil was part of his political rise to power. Getting him on the Path of Honorable Accord while being a public figure of the Camarilla, so he could have a Path rating over 3 was a much bigger deal to the overall story than all the ghouls he slaughtered.<br /> <br /> I just don't see how to make that character fun in V5. The combat systems just don't have the meat on the bones to make that sort of rise in power through violence anything more than luck. There's no enough rules rewards for fighting smart to ever get a reputation built around wasting dumb licks with a weapon that's a suboptimal choice to most vampires so they think it's a statement of showing off how much he's holding back. The slog of combat was worth it because the resulting power, and struggles with morality, felt earned in a fashion the V5 rules don't seem like they can really manage because the rules framework isn't there.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-05-14T05:35:42-07:00","id":1448497,"title":"","content":"I have pros and cons for both. Generally, V20 has the benefit of inspiring no deep feelings from me and being all around satisfactory. V5, meanwhile, is mixed bag of stuff I either love or<i> loathe. </i>They're different games set in different eras of the same setting, it's like there's Dark Ages, Victorian, the Masquerade (1990s/2000s) and the Masquerade (2020s).<br /> <br /> I compiled a list of pros for both, and then realised they were too long. So here's just the V20 list for now (which is still too long...). Naturally, these are my opinions, not statements of fact.<br /> <br /> Pro V20:<ul><li>- The biggest advantage for V20 is that it's a complete work, all rules and lore available right now. No waiting to see if stuff will be added back in or worrying that stuff won't. Also the corebook had all clans, sects, bloodlines and disciplines from the start. I can play Sabbat and I didn't need to wait for a book for it, because the mechanics hadn't changed so much they were temporarily unplayable.<br /> -</li> <li>- I felt no need to homerule the hell out of V20 all the time. Most of V5 I like conceptually, but I don't like the mechanics. The lore is stuff I almost like sometimes, if you just tweak it a bit... or a lot.<br /> -</li> <li>- I could defy clan stereotypes. V5's clan banes kinda reinforce them.<br /> -</li> <li>- V5 leaves me feeling edgy about what they're going to do in the future metaplot, and not in a good way.<br /> -</li> <li>- Paths, paths, paths, <i>paths, path-</i><br /> Anyway, V5 does not (yet?) allow me to explore the metamorphosis of humanity into an inhuman monster (Camarilla and Anarch elders don't count, their monstrosity is still rooted in a human perspective). I love my inhuman vampire philosophies/religons.<br /> -</li> <li>- The Cappadocian/HoS and Samedi weaknesses. That's another thing I have to homerule. They could at least have merged them or something.<br /> -</li> <li>- The old Camarilla is preferable. I don't like its new exclusive status. Maybe if V5's Cam was present as a special premium membership for the &quot;True Camarilla&quot;. They still claim responsibility/governance of all kindred, but since the Anarchs are such ungrateful shortsighted spoilt brats they're grounded and have to earn their feeding/Elysium/domain privilges back.<br /> So what V5 is doing, basically, but with a different flavour. More like a secretive undead government, less like a VIP undead country club<br /> .-</li> <li>- The disciplines and blood sorcery are much more restrictive. To be a thaumaturge you need to be Tremere, to use vicisitude you need to be Tzimisce. I don't mind the older disciplines being different uses of a handful of core disciplines, but it feels like the clans are losing their distinctions. Dementation is a core part of the Malkavians, but in V5 anyone with dominate and obfuscate can use it. Obviously you can restrict it to the clan at your table, but unless I missed something there's nothing in the rules themselves that says &quot;restriction: must be of/taught to outsiders by x clan&quot;.<br /> -</li> <li>- Elder power levels. Your Elders are and always will be way beyond your leage in terms of power and you will be beneath their heal for eternity, your choices are either to cope or to get good at playing Jyhad.<br /> -</li> <li>- The nature of vampirism in V20 already did a perfectly good job of leaving you alienated from mortal life. You could try, and would almost certainly fuck up because your unlife makes you a monster by circumstance, but it wasn't definite that you would fuck up. There was always the slimest chance you could maybe pull it off if you managed your feeding right and truly cared to try hard enough. That made it worth striving for. There was a much needed light at the end of the road in a grimdark setting.<br /> The way V5 treats vampirism vs humanity is overkill. You're a ticking timebomb who can't ever not be risking killing people without... killing people. Great. There's no <i>point</i> trying to preserve your humanity because there's absolutely no chance of success. Well, guess it's time to embrace damnation and join the Sabbat, because they're right, and the only way not to be a constant danger to everyone around you is to embrace the fact that you're a vampire and humans are food. I prefer the question of &quot;Which sect is right?&quot; to be more ambiguous, thank you.<br /> It's atmospheric, butit goes too far.</li> </ul><br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><sup><i>Prone to hyperbole</i></sup>","edited":{"userid":26836,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26836-rhywbeth","user":"Rhywbeth","date":". 05-14-2021, 08:55 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26836-rhywbeth","name":"Rhywbeth","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar26836_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"377"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-05-14T07:54:20-07:00","id":1448506,"title":"","content":"Oh, and I don't care for the way V5 puts discipline requirements on rituals/ceremonies <i>at all</i>. It's very limiting.<br /> I also silmultaneously miss blood sorcery being split into paths while also enjoying the flexibility of having those restrictions lifted.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><sup><i>Prone to hyperbole</i></sup>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26836-rhywbeth","name":"Rhywbeth","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar26836_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"377"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-05-15T01:02:50-07:00","id":1448570,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Rhywbeth</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1443592-the-official-v5-vs-v20-thread?p=1448497#post1448497\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I have pros and cons for both. Generally, V20 has the benefit of inspiring no deep feelings from me and being all around satisfactory. V5, meanwhile, is mixed bag of stuff I either love or<i> loathe. </i>They're different games set in different eras of the same setting, it's like there's Dark Ages, Victorian, the Masquerade (1990s/2000s) and the Masquerade (2020s).<br /> <br /> I compiled a list of pros for both, and then realised they were too long. So here's just the V20 list for now (which is still too long...). Naturally, these are my opinions, not statements of fact.<br /> <br /> Pro V20:<ul><li>- The biggest advantage for V20 is that it's a complete work, all rules and lore available right now. No waiting to see if stuff will be added back in or worrying that stuff won't. Also the corebook had all clans, sects, bloodlines and disciplines from the start. I can play Sabbat and I didn't need to wait for a book for it, because the mechanics hadn't changed so much they were temporarily unplayable.<br /> -</li> <li>- I felt no need to homerule the hell out of V20 all the time. Most of V5 I like conceptually, but I don't like the mechanics. The lore is stuff I almost like sometimes, if you just tweak it a bit... or a lot.<br /> -</li> <li>- I could defy clan stereotypes. V5's clan banes kinda reinforce them.<br /> -</li> <li>- V5 leaves me feeling edgy about what they're going to do in the future metaplot, and not in a good way.<br /> -</li> <li>- Paths, paths, paths, <i>paths, path-</i><br /> Anyway, V5 does not (yet?) allow me to explore the metamorphosis of humanity into an inhuman monster (Camarilla and Anarch elders don't count, their monstrosity is still rooted in a human perspective). I love my inhuman vampire philosophies/religons.<br /> -</li> <li>- The Cappadocian/HoS and Samedi weaknesses. That's another thing I have to homerule. They could at least have merged them or something.<br /> -</li> <li>- The old Camarilla is preferable. I don't like its new exclusive status. Maybe if V5's Cam was present as a special premium membership for the &amp;quot;True Camarilla&amp;quot;. They still claim responsibility/governance of all kindred, but since the Anarchs are such ungrateful shortsighted spoilt brats they're grounded and have to earn their feeding/Elysium/domain privilges back.<br /> So what V5 is doing, basically, but with a different flavour. More like a secretive undead government, less like a VIP undead country club<br /> .-</li> <li>- The disciplines and blood sorcery are much more restrictive. To be a thaumaturge you need to be Tremere, to use vicisitude you need to be Tzimisce. I don't mind the older disciplines being different uses of a handful of core disciplines, but it feels like the clans are losing their distinctions. Dementation is a core part of the Malkavians, but in V5 anyone with dominate and obfuscate can use it. Obviously you can restrict it to the clan at your table, but unless I missed something there's nothing in the rules themselves that says &amp;quot;restriction: must be of/taught to outsiders by x clan&amp;quot;.<br /> -</li> <li>- Elder power levels. Your Elders are and always will be way beyond your leage in terms of power and you will be beneath their heal for eternity, your choices are either to cope or to get good at playing Jyhad.<br /> -</li> <li>- The nature of vampirism in V20 already did a perfectly good job of leaving you alienated from mortal life. You could try, and would almost certainly fuck up because your unlife makes you a monster by circumstance, but it wasn't definite that you would fuck up. There was always the slimest chance you could maybe pull it off if you managed your feeding right and truly cared to try hard enough. That made it worth striving for. There was a much needed light at the end of the road in a grimdark setting.<br /> The way V5 treats vampirism vs humanity is overkill. You're a ticking timebomb who can't ever not be risking killing people without... killing people. Great. There's no <i>point</i> trying to preserve your humanity because there's absolutely no chance of success. Well, guess it's time to embrace damnation and join the Sabbat, because they're right, and the only way not to be a constant danger to everyone around you is to embrace the fact that you're a vampire and humans are food. I prefer the question of &amp;quot;Which sect is right?&amp;quot; to be more ambiguous, thank you.<br /> It's atmospheric, butit goes too far.</li> </ul></div> </div> </div> </div>Can we see your V5 list now?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Writer, publisher, performer<br /> Mostly he/his, sometimes she/her IRL <a href=\"https://adam-lowe.com\" target=\"_blank\">https://adam-lowe.com</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5291-adambeyoncelowe","name":"adambeyoncelowe","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5291_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2802"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-05-15T10:12:28-07:00","id":1448599,"title":"","content":"Ok, having lost several hours to things that should have taken less than one, here's the pros of V5:<ul><li>- Flexible morality with the chronicle tenets, great fun when i don't want to use paths. The Path of Humanity is fun, but it's not a depiction of humanity, it's about denying the beast a foothold so that you can preserve your humanity. Now I can make preserving your humanity about behaving like a human, instead of a saint. Or utilitse values of different eras, such as a game I'm working on set in Imperial Rome which values duty and military prowess but does not necessarily object to bloodshed and killing (and sets up for interesting encounters with younger modern day kindred raised with values that do).<br /> The characters having their own personal principles, and that those principles can strengthen their sense of self when the beast starts erroding it (ie, lessening stains from tennet violations) is something I also love.<br /> -</li> <li>- The Masquerade, while I don't think it's in danger of total collapse, would definitely need to take a look at itself in the current era. The internet making its way into every inch of our lives, the rapidly vanishing illusion of privacy and government agencies abusing that <i>would </i>be prevalent themes for a piece of media that does social commentary. Plus it's interesting to shake things up with a second Inquisition. The kindred could use the exercise.<br /> -</li> <li>- I also like the SI. They're fighting monsters, but they're also a government agency. There might be heroic individuals amognst them, but as an organisation they're certainly not on the side of the common human. They're vaguely like the Technocracy for vampires, I suppose. It would be interesting to play them.<br /> -</li> <li>- Gehenna is likely misunderstood and most likely not the be-all-and-end-all of apocalypses.<br /> -</li> <li>- More vampire religous cults, I love exploring the effect of becoming a vampire on characters and how they might rationalise and deal with it. A vampire specific religion is good for that, it was why I loved paths and the Setites.<br /> -</li> <li>- Blood Sorcery as its own discipline, with Hermetic Thaumaturgy, Dur-An-Ki, Akhu and so on being different paradigms.<br /> -</li> <li>- Necromancy was found to be too sanitary it seems, I love it. Want to go the shadowlands? No longer do you need to follow the Ash Path to five dots. Nowadays when we get five dots we stain our souls with the essence of Oblivion channeled through<i> human sacrifice.<br /> -</i></li> <li>- The Tzimisce weakness is more interesting and contributes to characterisation. Now you need to think about what the core of this character's identity is and how it manifests, which in V20 was generally devolved into a question of &quot;where is the jar of dirt&quot;?<br /> -</li> <li>With their new, and vastly improved weakness, the Tremere just got a boost to one of the most interesting clans for me. I love it so much, I homeruled it so it was even <i>worse</i> and their blood is totally unable to bind anything anymore. The clan must be falling over itself to guard this knowledge.<br /> You can make a ghoul, but they have no innate loyalty to you and without that they're a walking masquerade breach waiting to happen. You know who could make use of the superhuman powers of ghouls, but without the loyalty to a vampire master? The SI.<br /> You're also a walking snack for elders. They've somehow aquired even more potential enemies, because those who didn't want them staked out for the sun are considering the possibility of opening a cafe with usurper vitae on the menu.<br /> More than even the Tremere need to pull together for safety, but with several different opinions on the way to go and no blood bond to force them together they're having a hard time doing that. I find I can make Tremere plot hooks much easier now.<br /> -</li> <li>- Less bloodline clutter, at the moment.<br /> -</li> <li>- The thin bloods make for a different playstyle when I want a change of pace.<br /> -</li> <li>- I do like the Hecata, albeit as a sect for the necromancers rather than a magically blended together clan. It also makes sense for the Clan of Death to be independent, since death is impartial and that is the theme these guys have going on.<br /> -</li> <li>- Once I remove &quot;must kill to sate the final hunger dot&quot;, I do appreciate how the struggle with the beast is a much bigger presence in a vampire's unlife now. V5 better depicts the concept that you're in an internal nightly battle for your soul.<br /> -</li> <li>- I wasn't fond of discipline powers until I started playing with converting older combo disciplines and VtR devotions into amalgams and got totally different playstyles out of two characters with overlapping disciplines. I'm more sold on them now. Amalgams are great fun and put a lot of clan specific flavour in, turning common disciplines into very different things depending on the clan using them.<br /> I think the current problem is just the limited selection.<br /> -</li> <li>- Touchstones. While I still don't like the human restriction or how they work in game, I adore the concept that there are things, anchors, that resonate so strongly with your sense of self it can beat back the beast. Used in a certain way, they could be a little break of real love and joy - or at least a sense of purpose - in the world of darkness.<br /> -</li> <li>- Here's a possibly contraversial one:<br /> So, there's the view that &quot;V5 is VtR with a VtM paintjob&quot;. While I can see why, V5 isn't VtR. It's not VtM1e-V20. It's V5, it's its own thing. But it does have enough similarities to the two that you can sort of play it that way, which works for me if I'm in the mood to do so. I prefer VtM's clans, paths, sects, blood magic and having vicissitude to VtR, but enjoy the lore flexibility and closer to actually-human default humanity of VtR which can be replicated in the tenets (spend time with people, have a life outside of vampire politics). It's not a one-to-one matchup, but V5 saves me time messing around with the translation guide and the changes to some of the lore makes blending them with VtR covenants easier..</li> </ul><br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><sup><i>Prone to hyperbole</i></sup>","edited":{"userid":26836,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26836-rhywbeth","user":"Rhywbeth","date":". 05-15-2021, 01:19 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26836-rhywbeth","name":"Rhywbeth","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar26836_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"377"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-05-15T11:10:58-07:00","id":1448604,"title":"","content":"There's a common theme of V5 either allowing people to use more things from VTR2e or encouraging them to seek it out, I feel. But this may be confirmation bias, since that's what I did!","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Writer, publisher, performer<br /> Mostly he/his, sometimes she/her IRL <a href=\"https://adam-lowe.com\" target=\"_blank\">https://adam-lowe.com</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5291-adambeyoncelowe","name":"adambeyoncelowe","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5291_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2802"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-05-15T14:03:41-07:00","id":1448621,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MyWifeIsScary</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1448421-v5-so-what-happened-to-the-giovanni-s-potence?p=1448519#post1448519\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"> If the Tremere can't use their blood to bind anything, how do they work rituals?\u2e2e?</div> </div> </div> </div>I just meant the blood bond, in the sense of &quot;drink three times, bind them to your will&quot; specifically, not affecting thaumaturgy because reasons and I like the potential consequences of such a curse. Also after they had the Assamites chasing after a curse breaker for the last however long, it'd be sort of ironic to have the Tremere having to do the same for their new clan curse.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Honestly... No, I can't be honest, but the gist is that I feel like a lot of V5 appreciation comes from either selective reading or a misunderstanding of something crucial. </div> </div> </div>I can certainly say that describes <i>me</i>.<br /> But even if what I'm seeing is my own misinterpretations I'm enjoying I what I can make it into when I twist it around to fit my narratives.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> The SI is a paradoxical existence. You can't have a bunch of agents stay a secret AND communicate across agencies. </div> </div> </div>I don't consider there to actually<i> be</i> an organised unified SI, so much as there was a collosal masquerade breach that triggered an increase of well organised, well informed and well equipped hunter organisations that the more paranoid kindred are insisting are a repeat of the mess that predated the Convention of Thorns because they got some very lucky hits in during the early days (probably due to some inside help looking to take out rivals).<br /> If getting kindred to cooperate across sect, clan, age and generation (or even if they share these things) is like herding cats, getting all these human organisations across the globe to cooperate is asking for a fucking miracle. They're not going to win, but can become a thorn in the side of cainite society usually by the cainites' own doing.<br /> <br /> Although as I write this, I wonder if it's going to turn out later in the metaplot that there's some supernatural force that orchastrated the masquerade breach that caused them to form and is manipulating them behind the scenes. Antediluvian levels of mind control might explain how you would get world governments to work together.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> The rise of celphones and the internet doesn't mean shit because it directly correlates to the rise of computer generated imagery, viral marketing and fake news. As a certain great firewall has shown, if someone doesn't want you looking at something, it's easy to swamp it with enough BS that it disappears. </div> </div> </div>Also true, but from the point where the efforts of the Masquerade and the Technocracy convinced people the supernatural doesn't exist, it hasn't been the random people complimenting the special effects on a YouTube video that vampires would be in danger from. It's the ones who never forgot, keeping their eye out for these things. If the number of well informed (or &quot;well informed&quot;/s) vampire hunter societies with modern lethal-damage-inflicting weaponry like bombs and flamethrowers grows, so does the danger.<br /> <br /> The video, the conspiracy forums, these don't do shit. But it's good practice to bring the hammer down hard on the tiny violations, because sometimes some bright spark might do something like let the humans with nukes find out about Shrecknet or something because they overestimated themselves.<br /> <br /> Getting around the Camarilla stranglehold on information would be the SI's obstacle to face, which I suppose would be a feature of the playstyle if they ever become a playable faction. Most of their information is likely going to come from vampires dropping hints to point the shiny new toys at enemies.<br /> <br /> ...I do admit, I feel like I'm scrambling to cover logic holes here, and I'm not doing well.<br /> <br /> I will also admit that I skimmed the cults and haven't found the time to read them properly, since I was focused on skipping through to the Hecata to find out what'd happened to my necromancers... which was, as with all of V5, a mixed reaction from me.<br /> I'll find a way to blend them back in with previous lore for my table.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> But did you pay attention to the rest of what they did to thaumaturgy? Is there even enough left for us to even create paradigms? Do they even still use Dur-An-Ki to refer to assamite sorcery now? Isn't it Quietus... </div> </div> </div>Streamlining the disciplines into groups and subgroups helps me keep track of it, it's just a personal preference born of accessability to me. That's why I like Blood Sorcery as a discipline with paths for clan-specific paradigms. But yes, they have in the actual material taken out the paradigms, I just live in the V5 of my head where paths remain a thing. I am annoyed by the loss of clan discipline distinctions and sorcery paths. (Also the fact that Silence of Death is under Obfuscate now, <i>it's supposed to be Quietus</i>.)<br /> It sort of went &quot;Oh, they're streamlining the disciplines now.&quot;<br /> And then I saw the mishmash that followed and died inside. Also, pretty much everything is missing at the moment.<br /> <br /> I can see some Anarch Sorcerers using a mix of powers born from bastardising Thaumaturgy into an unregimented new age pagan make-it-up-as-you-go thing though, so it might work for them.<br /> And I just used Dur-An-Ki as a random example of a paradigm off the top of my head. I have no idea. Isn't Quietus the general discipline of the Assamites, and Dur-An-Ki is specific to the Sorcerer caste? I'm not great with Assamite lore..<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> just seems like edge for the sake of edge. Blood magic gotta be bloody right? Wrong. Give me an edition that lets me play an erudite sorcerer who knows what he's doing, rather than an evil magic clown. </div> </div> </div>It absolutely is, I just found it <i>hilarious</i>. ( It's the WoD, I've just accepted that there'll occasionally be over the top edgy stuff that makes me roll my eyes and snort in amusement (&quot;Tzimisce have a flesh warping alien disease, Vampires are all incapable of actual positive emotions no matter what they do, it's so dark and deep you guys!&quot;). I get that others aren't amused though.<br /> If I'm not in the mood for &quot;Necromancy, as performed by the Rosselini&quot;, I'll just edit it to be more like V20's Ex Nihilo instead. As I said, I homerule V5 a lot.<br /> I'm not so keen on it no longer being blood sorcery though. I think I prefer the idea that the Giovanni's necromancy was evil mostly because of the way they used it abusively for bad purposes (making being a monster something you 100% chose, because there was nothing that said you <i>had</i> to do it like that) rather than because it's inherently tied to Oblivion and thus inherenty eats your soul.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><sup><i>Prone to hyperbole</i></sup>","edited":{"userid":26836,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26836-rhywbeth","user":"Rhywbeth","date":". 05-16-2021, 03:34 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26836-rhywbeth","name":"Rhywbeth","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar26836_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"377"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-05-15T16:38:37-07:00","id":1448632,"title":"","content":"I'm not sure how coherent any of that was. It's around midnight and my brains switching off, so I might have confused some lore or gotten stuff wrong and my reasoning probably looks like swiss cheese, but I can't edit the post for some reason.<br /> <br /> Anyway, I guess at the end of the day how tight the Camarilla's grip on the flow of digital information is comes down to storyteller decision. The metaplot storytellers just decided it's not tight enough, I guess.<br /> <br /> Also vampires seem to like seeing conspiracies and secret masters in the shadows. Iconnu this, Antediluvian pawns that. Ventrue elders and their thing about the Secret Masters, or whatever they were called. It's entirely possible that the higher ups are just freaking out too hard over a relatively trivial upsurge in attention and vampire hunter activity.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><sup><i>Prone to hyperbole</i></sup>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26836-rhywbeth","name":"Rhywbeth","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar26836_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"377"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-05-15T23:39:54-07:00","id":1448659,"title":"","content":"I think MWIS broke the forum with the broken code in his post. Whoops!","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Writer, publisher, performer<br /> Mostly he/his, sometimes she/her IRL <a href=\"https://adam-lowe.com\" target=\"_blank\">https://adam-lowe.com</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5291-adambeyoncelowe","name":"adambeyoncelowe","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5291_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2802"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-05-16T00:29:43-07:00","id":1448662,"title":"","content":"Ah, so it's not just me. <br /> It's really bother. i'm rather unhappy with some of the post but can't edit it.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25794-mywifeisscary","name":"MyWifeIsScary","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25794_2.png","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3711"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-05-16T05:00:45-07:00","id":1448675,"title":"","content":"Ok, slightly less sleep deprived and having thought on it.<br /> <br /> VtM wants to explore the themes of privacy invasion, your personal information being available to those who know how to look (and how that can make it harder to hide that you're undead) in an era when companies are<br /> installing their creepy, annoying voiced wiretaps in your house and blah. I accept it makes sense to explore that.<br /> <br /> There were various ways that could've played out that would impact vampiric society, and what V5 did is not the way I would've done it. I would have built on the path of technomancy (whatever happened to that...) and the Anarchs' forays into tech and the web and subsequent evolution of vampire internet culture from V20's Rites of the Blood.<br /> I wouldn't make the SI their prime concern. Worry more about what other vampires are doing with your information and how they'll hold it over your head. Are your secrets really safe? Really? Is the information you have faked? Can you tell? Fangbook scandal?.<br /> This isn't a new worry, it's just gotten worse in recent years.<br /> <br /> But ultimately, while I might not like the exact details of (or flat out scream &quot;put that back!&quot; at) the newest additions/changes to the setting, it offers me enough ideas and toys that I find interesting to play with that it's worth it to use V5 and edit it to my preferences. The masquerade finally slipping badly enough for humans to become vaguely aware on a global level that there's something sharing the night with them and occasionally start poking around is one of them. I know I'm cherry picking stuff, and I'm ok with engaging in suspension of disbelief if it's entertaining me.<br /> Once I'm done moulding things to my will I'll probably end up with a V20-V5 hybrid of some sort. (V25?)<br /> To be honest, that's kind of what I'm hoping for from a sixth edition.<br /> <br /> Also V5's necromancy works fine for playing one of the Rosselini, since these guys love pushing the envelope on torture and pointless cruelty to the point where they're looked down on by a family that has branches who are slaving warlords, cannibals, mafiosi, and of course the infamous necromantic patrician family.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><sup><i>Prone to hyperbole</i></sup>","edited":{"userid":26836,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26836-rhywbeth","user":"Rhywbeth","date":". 05-17-2021, 03:22 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26836-rhywbeth","name":"Rhywbeth","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar26836_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"377"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-05-16T05:02:53-07:00","id":1448676,"title":"","content":"I didn't finish typing, and I still can't edit:<br /> They're looked down on for being puerile, specifically, but still.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><sup><i>Prone to hyperbole</i></sup>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26836-rhywbeth"