/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12002_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13933"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-05-26T15:23:22-07:00","id":1449711,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CTPhipps</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1443592-the-official-v5-vs-v20-thread?p=1449708#post1449708\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Yeah and that means nothing since the rules for NPCs is the same as the rules for PCs.<br /> <br /> There's no rules for Mooks in VTM.</div> </div> </div> </div>let's keep this convo in one thread.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25992-archderd","name":"archderd","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25992_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2020"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"205"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-05-26T15:30:25-07:00","id":1449714,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>archderd</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1443592-the-official-v5-vs-v20-thread?p=1449711#post1449711\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">let's keep this convo in one thread.</div> </div> </div> </div>Good idea. But in terms of comparison, yes, V20 gets a big boost from the idea that Sabbat shouldn't be PCs in V5. I don't see the reasoning there and think its a poor decision.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Author of <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Cthulhu-Armageddon-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01KUOM7SI/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982844&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Cthulhu+Armageddon\" target=\"_blank\">Cthulhu Armageddon</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Teenage-Weredeer-Bright-Falls-Mysteries-ebook/dp/B075TTN2FN/ref=sr_1_2?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982717&amp;sr=1-2&amp;keywords=Weredeer#customerReviews\" target=\"_blank\">I was a Teenage Weredeer</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Straight-Outta-Fangton-Comedic-Vampire-ebook/dp/B01KNHICCC/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982774&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Straight+Outta+Fangton\" target=\"_blank\">Straight Outta Fangton</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Lucifers-Star-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01MDM9MCT/ref=mt_kindle?_encoding=UTF8&amp;me=&amp;qid=\" target=\"_blank\">Lucifer's Star</a>, </i>and the <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Rules-Supervillainy-Saga-Book-ebook/dp/B07MB89S33/\" target=\"_blank\">Supervillainy Saga</a>.</i><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","name":"CTPhipps","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12002_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13933"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-05-26T15:50:32-07:00","id":1449722,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CTPhipps</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1443592-the-official-v5-vs-v20-thread?p=1449702#post1449702\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I think this is a silly action but I'm also 99.99% sure that it will have all the rules for making Sabbat PCs. They'll just be the same rules for making Sabbat NPCs.<br /> <br /> After all, there's no point making Paths of Enlightenment for NPCs.<br /> <br /> No one rolls for Path checks for NPCs.</div> </div> </div> </div>This presumes they'll even include MECHANICS for the Paths of Enlightenment vs. two pages of purple prose where some rando in universe describes what its like so the GM can roleplay them, but with zero actual mechanical support for the paths.<br /> <br /> I get that hope springs eternal for you with V5, but when you really go back and look at all the things you were sure V5 was going to have to include... when was the last time your prognostications were actually on target relative to what was actually delivered?<br /> <br /> My prediction, purple prose and zero mechanics for Paths, but they'll throw in 5-10 new discipline powers and some lore sheets related to having previously been a member of the Sabbat (but are now a brave and noble Anarch) and that will be it for player-facing mechanics.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1328-chris24601","name":"Chris24601","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"520"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-05-26T15:53:56-07:00","id":1449724,"title":"","content":"I think the Sabbat announcement and certain Twitter comments actually highlights a larger issue: Paradox isn't letting V5 escape its original vision even though the people responsible for it aren't working on it were removed from being in charge of it.<br /> <br /> Ultimately, V5 can't reach it's potential no matter who's hands it's placed in, if they're going to follow design principles from the original V5 development team. Switching teams over and over and expecting something to really change in fan reactions is pointless if teams feel compelled to not change the things that are getting negative reactions.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":6}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-05-26T16:25:49-07:00","id":1449727,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Chris24601</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1443592-the-official-v5-vs-v20-thread?p=1449722#post1449722\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">This presumes they'll even include MECHANICS for the Paths of Enlightenment vs. two pages of purple prose where some rando in universe describes what its like so the GM can roleplay them, but with zero actual mechanical support for the paths.<br /> <br /> I get that hope springs eternal for you with V5, but when you really go back and look at all the things you were sure V5 was going to have to include... when was the last time your prognostications were actually on target relative to what was actually delivered?<br /> <br /> My prediction, purple prose and zero mechanics for Paths, but they'll throw in 5-10 new discipline powers and some lore sheets related to having previously been a member of the Sabbat (but are now a brave and noble Anarch) and that will be it for player-facing mechanics.</div> </div> </div> </div>Hope springs eternal isn't the right word. I'm quite satisfied with V5.<br /> <br /> However, it's a bit of the nature of the Beast that I am the guy people generally expects to be the V5 defender because this board has quite a few people with a vocan dislike. Fine, it's not their bag. That's just how it goes.<br /> <br /> I'm not inclined to defend this decision, though, because I'm a big Sabbat fan and disappointed. I do think that it will include the rules for Paths, though.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Heavy Arms</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1443592-the-official-v5-vs-v20-thread?p=1449724#post1449724\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I think the Sabbat announcement and certain Twitter comments actually highlights a larger issue: Paradox isn't letting V5 escape its original vision even though the people responsible for it aren't working on it were removed from being in charge of it.<br /> <br /> Ultimately, V5 can't reach it's potential no matter who's hands it's placed in, if they're going to follow design principles from the original V5 development team. Switching teams over and over and expecting something to really change in fan reactions is pointless if teams feel compelled to not change the things that are getting negative reactions.</div> </div> </div> </div>Well that's unsurprising because they consider it a wide and huge artistic as well as financial success.<br /> <br /> Which is part of the problem I think because a lot of fans just don't believe that because they don't like it and assume that's universal.<br /> <br /> Like that guy who couldn't accept Captain Marvel was a huge success and kept insisting it was a bomb.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Author of <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Cthulhu-Armageddon-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01KUOM7SI/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982844&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Cthulhu+Armageddon\" target=\"_blank\">Cthulhu Armageddon</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Teenage-Weredeer-Bright-Falls-Mysteries-ebook/dp/B075TTN2FN/ref=sr_1_2?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982717&amp;sr=1-2&amp;keywords=Weredeer#customerReviews\" target=\"_blank\">I was a Teenage Weredeer</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Straight-Outta-Fangton-Comedic-Vampire-ebook/dp/B01KNHICCC/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982774&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Straight+Outta+Fangton\" target=\"_blank\">Straight Outta Fangton</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Lucifers-Star-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01MDM9MCT/ref=mt_kindle?_encoding=UTF8&amp;me=&amp;qid=\" target=\"_blank\">Lucifer's Star</a>, </i>and the <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Rules-Supervillainy-Saga-Book-ebook/dp/B07MB89S33/\" target=\"_blank\">Supervillainy Saga</a>.</i><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","name":"CTPhipps","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12002_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13933"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-05-26T18:31:37-07:00","id":1449736,"title":"","content":"If it was such a huge artistic success why did it go from WW, to Modiphius, back to Paradox, and then to Renegade?<br /> <br /> Where's the evidence that the financial success of the initial sales of the core book have carried over into long tail sales or high levels of sales of the supplements?<br /> <br /> You can't compare a single movie to a franchise. The Solo movie was a bomb, but the Star Wars franchise is doing fine as a whole.<br /> <br /> If V5 is meant to be the foundation of a new set of VtM books, and a wider WoD, we're not seeing it work for that purpose.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-05-26T19:16:35-07:00","id":1449737,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Heavy Arms</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1443592-the-official-v5-vs-v20-thread?p=1449736#post1449736\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">If it was such a huge artistic success why did it go from WW, to Modiphius, back to Paradox, and then to Renegade?</div> </div> </div> </div>Because Modiphius wasn't getting their books out fast enough.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Where's the evidence that the financial success of the initial sales of the core book have carried over into long tail sales or high levels of sales of the supplements? </div> </div> </div>The multiple global printings certainly help.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> You can't compare a single movie to a franchise. The Solo movie was a bomb, but the Star Wars franchise is doing fine as a whole. </div> </div> </div>Even then, it's stood the test of time financially after gross grandiose overspending.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> If V5 is meant to be the foundation of a new set of VtM books, and a wider WoD, we're not seeing it work for that purpose. </div> </div> </div>No, it's instead the foundation for video games and mass media including television shows as well as movies.<br /> <br /> Tabletop Games are really just the artifact now.<br /> <br /> Though I do find it weird that this is the point being argued when my point is, &quot;I'm really bummed out by people who think it isn't successful as if that is something they think is even possible to believe at this point.&quot;","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Author of <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Cthulhu-Armageddon-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01KUOM7SI/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982844&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Cthulhu+Armageddon\" target=\"_blank\">Cthulhu Armageddon</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Teenage-Weredeer-Bright-Falls-Mysteries-ebook/dp/B075TTN2FN/ref=sr_1_2?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982717&amp;sr=1-2&amp;keywords=Weredeer#customerReviews\" target=\"_blank\">I was a Teenage Weredeer</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Straight-Outta-Fangton-Comedic-Vampire-ebook/dp/B01KNHICCC/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982774&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Straight+Outta+Fangton\" target=\"_blank\">Straight Outta Fangton</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Lucifers-Star-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01MDM9MCT/ref=mt_kindle?_encoding=UTF8&amp;me=&amp;qid=\" target=\"_blank\">Lucifer's Star</a>, </i>and the <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Rules-Supervillainy-Saga-Book-ebook/dp/B07MB89S33/\" target=\"_blank\">Supervillainy Saga</a>.</i><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","name":"CTPhipps","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12002_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13933"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-05-26T22:34:53-07:00","id":1449759,"title":"","content":"V20 is a lot easier to adapt for a computer game tho. <br /> The disciplines are simple. <br /> Generation is more elegant.<br /> Factions are cleaner and better defined. <br /> Crazy philosophies make for more interesting and timeless narratives than the very mortal politics of v5<br /> The plot's more Deus Ex 2001 than Team Fortress 2, and you can cover a wider aray of genres with it. Did i mention it ages better with its light metaplot?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":6}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25794-mywifeisscary","name":"MyWifeIsScary","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25794_2.png","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3711"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-05-26T22:39:53-07:00","id":1449760,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MyWifeIsScary</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1443592-the-official-v5-vs-v20-thread?p=1449759#post1449759\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">V20 is a lot easier to adapt for a computer game tho.<br /> The disciplines are simple.<br /> Generation is more elegant.<br /> Factions are cleaner and better defined.<br /> Crazy philosophies make for more interesting and timeless narratives than the very mortal politics of v5<br /> The plot's more Deus Ex 2001 than Team Fortress 2, and you can cover a wider aray of genres with it. Did i mention it ages better with its light metaplot?</div> </div> </div> </div>I'm pretty sure that V5 was designed specifically to be a Video Game adaptation.<br /> <br /> Also, quite a few of what is in V5 is an adaptation of what was in Bloodlines.<br /> <br /> * Choose between Anarch and Camarilla<br /> * Sabbat as the murderous bad guys<br /> * Lots of Hunters that kill you if you break the Masquerade<br /> * Generation is an irrelevancy unless its a plot point<br /> * Much simpler Disciplines<br /> * Very fast combat","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Author of <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Cthulhu-Armageddon-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01KUOM7SI/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982844&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Cthulhu+Armageddon\" target=\"_blank\">Cthulhu Armageddon</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Teenage-Weredeer-Bright-Falls-Mysteries-ebook/dp/B075TTN2FN/ref=sr_1_2?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982717&amp;sr=1-2&amp;keywords=Weredeer#customerReviews\" target=\"_blank\">I was a Teenage Weredeer</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Straight-Outta-Fangton-Comedic-Vampire-ebook/dp/B01KNHICCC/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982774&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Straight+Outta+Fangton\" target=\"_blank\">Straight Outta Fangton</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Lucifers-Star-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01MDM9MCT/ref=mt_kindle?_encoding=UTF8&amp;me=&amp;qid=\" target=\"_blank\">Lucifer's Star</a>, </i>and the <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Rules-Supervillainy-Saga-Book-ebook/dp/B07MB89S33/\" target=\"_blank\">Supervillainy Saga</a>.</i><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","name":"CTPhipps","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12002_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13933"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-05-27T00:16:49-07:00","id":1449767,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CTPhipps</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1443592-the-official-v5-vs-v20-thread?p=1449737#post1449737\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Because Modiphius wasn't getting their books out fast enough.</div> </div> </div> </div>That's only one step in the chain. And it certainly doesn't explain a confidence in the product as an artistic success, even if it supports your later point that V5 is, to Paradox, just a hype builder for other more lucrative projects (of course, even if a bunch of the existing transmedia projects are probably more profitable than the TT books just because TT books are shit for profits, it doesn't mean anything in that area has actually returned on the investment yet).<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> The multiple global printings certainly help. </div> </div> </div>Number of printings in a vacuum is a fairly meaningless data point because it's simple to inflate. A company that orders print runs of 1K books, and is on its fifth print run isn't outselling a company that does 10K print runs and is just about to start a second.<br /> <br /> This is also tempered by multiple print runs each coinciding with a significant errata (as in either a major addition such as the safety tools appendix, or a minor change to a core mechanic like tweaking certain values from 0-5 to 1-6) worked in. Even if they're just putting those in each print run, the fact that it keeps happening isn't great, and it gives a negative impression.<br /> <br /> None of the publicly available data backs up the print runs as being equally large as the second on (aka the first main print run after the first initial preorder one). There's nothing wrong with doing small print runs after a books first big push... that's when most physical sales are going to happen and you don't want to carry a large stock if you don't have to. But it means &quot;hey another print run&quot; isn't the same as, &quot;hey another print run that means we sold as many books this time as we did the best time.&quot;<br /> <br /> And it doesn't address anything regarding the performance of the supplements.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Even then, it's stood the test of time financially after gross grandiose overspending. </div> </div> </div>No, it didn't. It's budget was completely in-line with the rest of the Star Wars movies of the same era, and where all the others were massively financially successful, Solo managed to barely squeak over the line in global box office sales to end up with a higher ticket sales than production budget. Which by no means indicates that it actually turned a profit because there's lots of other factors in movies that go into it. Just managing to avoid a project going into the red doesn't mean it &quot;stood the test of time financially.&quot;<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> No, it's instead the foundation for video games and mass media including television shows as well as movies. </div> </div> </div>Then why even bother with the level of investment of TT support? Paradox doesn't need this headache to make video games, shows, and movies. The original VtM run had lots of mass media stuff just fine. They could have easily ask Onyx Path to do this: Onyx Path was already planning a new edition, Paradox just needed one that would be friendly towards their other goals, and then Paradox could have but in the money for marketing, distribution, and so on that Onyx Path doesn't have to push VtM back into the lime light.<br /> <br /> If it's primary purpose is to be a foundation for other media, being an artistic or financial success is, generally, meaningless. It needs to be a PR success first and foremost. Pissing off a bunch of fans in the name of artistic vision is not a strong PR move.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Though I do find it weird that this is the point being argued when my point is, &quot;I'm really bummed out by people who think it isn't successful as if that is something they think is even possible to believe at this point.&quot; </div> </div> </div>Maybe because you make your point in a fashion that invites counterpoints that you don't really intend?<br /> <br /> If all you want to say is, &quot;it doesn't matter that anything after the successful hyping of V5's initial release isn't a major financial success, because VtM is back as a brand now and non-TT products are what really matters,&quot; you shouldn't be making comments about how artistically successful V5 is as a gameline.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CTPhipps</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1443592-the-official-v5-vs-v20-thread?p=1449760#post1449760\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I'm pretty sure that V5 was designed specifically to be a Video Game adaptation.</div> </div> </div> </div>Doubtful. While there are video game influences (Martin literally said some of the V5 ideas were things that were taken from the failed MMO design stages), that game isn't particularly well suited to video-game translation. It actively increases the amount of reliance on GM judgement calls, which is the hardest thing for a video game to handle well. Video game AI is absolute shit for trying to figure out if a fight should be a single roll off, a three round capped conflict, or say &quot;screw the book, Five Act structure is actually a thing to, lets let this combat go a bit longer.&quot; &quot;Keep fighting until a metric is accomplished,&quot; is something much easier on a video game.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Also, quite a few of what is in V5 is an adaptation of what was in Bloodlines. </div> </div> </div>That seems quite the stretch. Lets also remember that the cult darling Bloodlines is the heavily modded and fan-patched Bloodlines that changes some of these things (like options to make the Sabbat a faction you can join...).<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Choose between Anarch and Camarilla </div> </div> </div>And the KotE, and &quot;none,&quot; which don't really work well for V5 right now.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Lots of Hunters that kill you if you break the Masquerade </div> </div> </div>Always been a thing, and they're Society of Leopold hunters, not the SI.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Generation is an irrelevancy unless its a plot point </div> </div> </div>Generation is extremely relevant in V5 even if it's no longer selected individually and all the mess that goes with that.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Much simpler Disciplines </div> </div> </div>Bloodlines kept, and even expanded the number of Disciplines that are a single power that gets better each level like Potence/Celerity/Fortitude. V5 made Disciplines more complicated by having different multiple different powers at each level. This claim makes no sense if you compare Bloodlines's implementation of Auspex or Obfuscate compared to V5's takes on them.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Very fast combat </div> </div> </div>Bloodline's combat isn't particularly fast. You're not storming the SoL stronghold in Bloodlines and only doing three rounds of combat. Now, in Bloodlines, if you spec for stealth/combat you can tear through most enemies like butter and the boss battles aren't too bad on time, but there's still waves and waves of them as some points, and if you try to make a non-combat character... those things can just be utter slog-fests.<br /> <br /> And, of course, they're &quot;fast&quot; in completely different ways. You can be really fast at BL combat be having strong FPS skills (getting lots of head shots and knowing how to avoid attacks without having to care about your stats). This is not the same as, &quot;we capped combat at three rounds to keep things moving.&quot;<br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":7}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-05-27T01:23:27-07:00","id":1449772,"title":"","content":"We have a brand that was ejected by Icv2 charts faster than I can fart.<br /> <br /> A brand that in in less than 4 years has changed developers 3 times.<br /> <br /> A brand whose last iteration is disliked by 4 out 5 people in the historical forum of the brand, and that have a bad reputation in others.<br /> <br /> The main flagship of the multi-media approach, Bloodlines 2, has sink into a development hell : the whole studio fired, the project suspended and delayed without date and the main brain behind the first Bloodlines pushed out from development.<br /> <br /> On Drivethru, the most important digital shop of the sector, V20 Corebook is the 25th best selling entry, while V5 Corebook is the 71th (lower even than the Chronicles of Darkness corebook). Even Planescape 2nd Ed is selling more than V5.<br /> <br /> But we must still assume that it's a success history. I envy the unquestioning and dogmatic faith of some people here, it must be quite reassurring believing something in total spite of evidence.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":12142,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12142-undead-rabbit","user":"Undead rabbit","date":". 05-27-2021, 04:26 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":6}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12142-undead-rabbit","name":"Undead rabbit","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"888"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-05-27T02:39:48-07:00","id":1449775,"title":"","content":"Despite all that, I do think that V5 Core is a financial success. As in, I'm confident that it has long since sold enough copies to recoup the costs of producing it in the first place. It's probably made far more money than most RPG books ever will (which isn't actually saying that much).<br /> <br /> The problems I was highlighting, because I feel it's very relevant to the news about the Sabbat book pushing away even more potential fans, is that V5 as a brand isn't a cashcow. It doesn't have strong long-tail sales (not none, but not a lot for something that's supposed to be the foundation of anything). If the V5 brand is going to continue to serve the purpose of building up a bigger brand, it needs the ability to generate hype. Right now, it can't. The initial hype is gone. The game itself hasn't secured a place in the larger RPG world as standard to measure other games against. The supplements are not generating tons of industry buzz or positive hype outside the existing V5 fans.<br /> <br /> V5's success as a brand, not it's success as a core book, can't afford more disappointments, or else it can't really do it's job of getting people excited about new products (TT RPG books or others).<br /> <br /> Lets say Bloodlines 2 recovers for a Q1 2023 release date. What book does V5 have in the wings to release in Q4 2022 to build up excitement for VtM is that's the job of V5? Nothing really. The major Sects will each have a book out by then. The most prominent city in the game's already been covered. If people are saying they're done with V5 just hearing that the Sabbat book isn't going to include PC rules, how big is the V5 fan community really growing at this point? Is the Storytellers Guide to Elders going to get people pumped up in time to build up a bunch of PR before BL 2 finally hits? I guess maybe a Thinbloods book since that seemed kinda central to BL 2's plot... if that survives.<br /> <br /> That's the problem with all of the changes in developers that aren't being coupled with changes in how the books feel to people. Changing devs is supposed to shut up people like me. It's supposed to say, &quot;this group gets it, gets what the brand needs, and is going to bring back the excitement people had when V5 was first announced by making books people are pumped to get. That lets V5's brand do it's job of promoting VtM (either the TT RPG or in other media). Even mild disappointment is the wrong reaction to a new dev's first big book for the line if the brand is going to mean something when the TV show drops, or BL 2 finally gets made.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":7}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-05-27T04:14:06-07:00","id":1449780,"title":"","content":"What is the appeal of playing a monster if you are not allowed to be a monster? It shouldn't matter in VtM if every Anarch is a Nazi, and every Sabbat is a serial killer. Is it just fear that the game is now too politically incorrect for the 2020's? I wouldn't buy the rights to the Smurfs and then add Rambo Smurf and Pornstar Smurf and make an R rated cartoon. Maybe they should worry less of what people think of VtM and make an R rated game instead of a PG game with Olympic level back peddling on themes.<br /> <br /> And this is from someone who almost exclusively plays the Camarilla games, &quot;the nice faction&quot;.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24221-vamps-like-us","name":"Vamps Like Us","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"390"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-05-27T06:40:31-07:00","id":1449792,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CTPhipps</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1443592-the-official-v5-vs-v20-thread?p=1449760#post1449760\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I'm pretty sure that V5 was designed specifically to be a Video Game adaptation.<br /> <br /> Also, quite a few of what is in V5 is an adaptation of what was in Bloodlines.<br /> <br /> * Choose between Anarch and Camarilla<br /> * Sabbat as the murderous bad guys<br /> * Lots of Hunters that kill you if you break the Masquerade<br /> * Generation is an irrelevancy unless its a plot point<br /> * Much simpler Disciplines<br /> * Very fast combat</div> </div> </div> </div>Please, take a moment to look at your post. Who are you trying to convince here? It seems like yourself. You sure as hell aren't convincing anyone else. <br /> <br /> 1- there are four groups to choose from, if you include yourself. <br /> 2- Sabbat exist in VTMB, while thus far they do not in V5, baring future products. <br /> 3- In V5 the hunters will come even if you aren't messing with the masquerade. <br /> 4- Generation literally drove the plot of VTMB. LaCroix's inferiority complex is what got you into every main quest hassle you find yourself in, all to get him closer to supping on an ancient's blood. <br /> 5- Your statement is absurd. <br /> 6- V5's &quot;fast&quot; combat is &quot;fast&quot; to get it out of the way. VTMB on the otherhand threw you into various dungeon crawls, some of which went on for far too long; Pretty sure you depopulate a chinatown.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25794-mywifeisscary","name":"MyWifeIsScary","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25794_2.png","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3711"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-05-27T07:34:50-07:00","id":1449796,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Undead rabbit</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1443592-the-official-v5-vs-v20-thread?p=1449772#post1449772\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">We have a brand that was ejected by Icv2 charts faster than I can fart.</div> </div> </div> </div>So less than 8 hours after being put in the body? That was fast.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> A brand that in in less than 4 years has changed developers 3 times. </div> </div> </div>I got nothing here.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> A brand whose last iteration is disliked by 4 out 5 people in the historical forum of the brand, and that have a bad reputation in others. </div> </div> </div>Here's where location matters. I feel those numbers would be completely different on Twitter if you asked the #vamily. Or the Twitch subscribers of the actual plays. Echo chambers tend to echo.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> The main flagship of the multi-media approach, Bloodlines 2, has sink into a development hell : the whole studio fired, the project suspended and delayed without date and the main brain behind the first Bloodlines pushed out from development. </div> </div> </div>Again I got nothing here<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> On Drivethru, the most important digital shop of the sector, V20 Corebook is the 25th best selling entry, while V5 Corebook is the 71th (lower even than the Chronicles of Darkness corebook). Even Planescape 2nd Ed is selling more than V5. </div> </div> </div>Why the parenthetical diss of Chronicles of Darkness corebook? It's uncool and uncalled for. Your point is fine with just the V20 and V5 numbers. I am willing to bet that V5 totally outsells V20 in traditional brick and mortar stores though. You should probably mention those numbers for fairness because to reiterate location matters<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> But we must still assume that it's a success history. I envy the unquestioning and dogmatic faith of some people here, it must be quite reassurring believing something in total spite of evidence. </div> </div> </div>I enjoy watching the tribalism and fear of the new of some people here. It must be quite reassuring to be blind to the fact that your beliefs are not monolithic and people have embraced the new. There's evidence. It's like the Truth. It's out there.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/9015-zee-patrick","name":"zee PaTrick","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"56"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-05-27T08:22:25-07:00","id":1449803,"title":"","content":"V20 isn't available in &quot;brick and mortar&quot; stores, of course V5's gonna out-do-it there. That's the sad thing really, V5 can point to sales and pretend it's successful, V20 never got any marketing. people get into V20 because their hardcore friend that not only actually buys books, but obscure books too, introduced them. All of V20 is word of mouth. I really think OPP should've tried their hardest to push V20 out mainstream after it proved successful among hobbyists; I think I heard somewhere that they had their own ideas for V5. Maybe they tried, obviously I'm not privy to the intricacies of publishing. <br /> <br /> Another issue is that a book you buy and use for half a game and never pick up again is often, as a statistic, indistinguishable from the book you'll never put down. Word of mouth, buying suplements.. you can factor them all in, but then you've also got to consider that at your table you'll have one dude that's just happy to slap down money on more books and four others that are happy to use his books.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25794-mywifeisscary","name":"MyWifeIsScary","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25794_2.png","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3711"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-05-27T08:44:33-07:00","id":1449807,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Undead rabbit</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1443592-the-official-v5-vs-v20-thread?p=1449772#post1449772\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">We have a brand that was ejected by Icv2 charts faster than I can fart.<br /> <br /> A brand that in in less than 4 years has changed developers 3 times.<br /> <br /> A brand whose last iteration is disliked by 4 out 5 people in the historical forum of the brand, and that have a bad reputation in others.<br /> <br /> The main flagship of the multi-media approach, Bloodlines 2, has sink into a development hell : the whole studio fired, the project suspended and delayed without date and the main brain behind the first Bloodlines pushed out from development.<br /> <br /> On Drivethru, the most important digital shop of the sector, V20 Corebook is the 25th best selling entry, while V5 Corebook is the 71th (lower even than the Chronicles of Darkness corebook). Even Planescape 2nd Ed is selling more than V5.<br /> <br /> But we must still assume that it's a success history. I envy the unquestioning and dogmatic faith of some people here, it must be quite reassurring believing something in total spite of evidence.</div> </div> </div> </div>Yeah, actually, this is what I mean. The book gets printed in six languages and goes through multiple reprints. It's getting TV shows and video games. The video games hit the Steam Charts even when they're visual novels and the biggest game is still highly hotly anticipated.<br /> <br /> This is just silly to say otherwise.<br /> <br /> Mind you, I've mentioned that the IP has grown beyond tabletop gaming and we should be glad about that.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MyWifeIsScary</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1443592-the-official-v5-vs-v20-thread?p=1449803#post1449803\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">V20 isn't available in &quot;brick and mortar&quot; stores, of course V5's gonna out-do-it there. That's the sad thing really, V5 can point to sales and pretend it's successful,</div> </div> </div> </div>I'm going to be snarky here, I'm sorry. Yes, generally selling more is a sign of being more successful.<br /> <br /> I'm an author. Someone one said that I would never sell as many copies as one guy who sold ebooks exclusive.<br /> <br /> I pointed out that I sold more than him by adding in my audiobook sales.<br /> <br /> He said that didn't count. Why? Because the other guy wasn't available on audiobook.<br /> <br /> My response, &quot;Uh huh.&quot;<br /> <br /> We should be happy that Paradox Entertainment has expanded White Wolf to new markets, new mediums, and put things back in stores. Which is yes, why I think that its OBVIOUS its more successful but that isn't a disparaement on V20. Because the two are EXTENSIONS of one another rather than in direct competition.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Author of <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Cthulhu-Armageddon-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01KUOM7SI/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982844&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Cthulhu+Armageddon\" target=\"_blank\">Cthulhu Armageddon</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Teenage-Weredeer-Bright-Falls-Mysteries-ebook/dp/B075TTN2FN/ref=sr_1_2?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982717&amp;sr=1-2&amp;keywords=Weredeer#customerReviews\" target=\"_blank\">I was a Teenage Weredeer</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Straight-Outta-Fangton-Comedic-Vampire-ebook/dp/B01KNHICCC/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982774&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Straight+Outta+Fangton\" target=\"_blank\">Straight Outta Fangton</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Lucifers-Star-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01MDM9MCT/ref=mt_kindle?_encoding=UTF8&amp;me=&amp;qid=\" target=\"_blank\">Lucifer's Star</a>, </i>and the <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Rules-Supervillainy-Saga-Book-ebook/dp/B07MB89S33/\" target=\"_blank\">Supervillainy Saga</a>.</i><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":12002,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","user":"CTPhipps","date":". 05-27-2021, 03:49 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","name":"CTPhipps","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12002_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13933"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-05-27T10:08:24-07:00","id":1449816,"title":"","content":"This just seems like a pointless wedge to drive among the fandom. Possibly a bad business decision too.<br /> <br /> I mean, I've never played in or GM'd a Sabbat game, and I don't have a ton of interest in doing so. But... all this seems liable to do is piss off people who like Sabbat games. It gains nothing from people who prefer Camarilla or Anarch games. My reaction to this is, &quot;Whatever.&quot; I'll probably still read the book, but I'm not any more excited to do so than I was previously. But I bet there are Sabbat fans who don't want to get the book now.<br /> <br /> I just don't understand why White Wolf would do this. I mean, say the Sabbat they want are a bunch of Gehenna War veterans who've diablerized methuselahs and turned into mysterious and sinister and inordinately powerful bogeymen who don't work well as PCs. Okay. Why not make this group the Black Hand or a breakaway wing of the Sabbat? That would probably be much more palatable to people who want to continue playing them.<br /> <br /> Like, these are the same Revised-era shenanigans as killing off the Tremere <i>antitribu</i> and shaming GMs for letting any survive in their home games. Attempts to retroactively legislate what people should and shouldn't play <b>never</b> go well.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://blood-and-bourbon.obsidianportal.com/\" target=\"_blank\">Blood and Bourbon</a>, my New Orleans-based Vampire chronicle.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":6}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3110-false-epiphany","name":"False Epiphany","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3110_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"748"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-05-27T10:57:41-07:00","id":1449824,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>False Epiphany</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1443592-the-official-v5-vs-v20-thread?p=1449816#post1449816\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">This just seems like a pointless wedge to drive among the fandom. Possibly a bad business decision too.<br /> <br /> I mean, I've never played in or GM'd a Sabbat game, and I don't have a ton of interest in doing so. But... all this seems liable to do is piss off people who like Sabbat games. It gains nothing from people who prefer Camarilla or Anarch games. My reaction to this is, &quot;Whatever.&quot; I'll probably still read the book, but I'm not any more excited to do so than I was previously. But I bet there are Sabbat fans who don't want to get the book now.<br /> <br /> I just don't understand why White Wolf would do this. I mean, say the Sabbat they want are a bunch of Gehenna War veterans who've diablerized methuselahs and turned into mysterious and sinister and inordinately powerful bogeymen who don't work well as PCs. Okay. Why not make this group the Black Hand or a breakaway wing of the Sabbat? That would probably be much more palatable to people who want to continue playing them.<br /> <br /> Like, these are the same Revised-era shenanigans as killing off the Tremere <i>antitribu</i> and shaming GMs for letting any survive in their home games. Attempts to retroactively legislate what people should and shouldn't play <b>never</b> go well.</div> </div> </div> </div>Again, I want to know myself.<br /> <br /> WHY are they doing this?<br /> <br /> Who is this for?<br /> <br /> I'd very much like Justin Achilli's thinking on this and hope it's in the developer's blog. I think it's a bad decision.<br /> <br /> The Sabbat are the third pillar of the setting after all.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Author of <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Cthulhu-Armageddon-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01KUOM7SI/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982844&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Cthulhu+Armageddon\" target=\"_blank\">Cthulhu Armageddon</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Teenage-Weredeer-Bright-Falls-Mysteries-ebook/dp/B075TTN2FN/ref=sr_1_2?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982717&amp;sr=1-2&amp;keywords=Weredeer#customerReviews\" target=\"_blank\">I was a Teenage Weredeer</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Straight-Outta-Fangton-Comedic-Vampire-ebook/dp/B01KNHICCC/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982774&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Straight+Outta+Fangton\" target=\"_blank\">Straight Outta Fangton</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Lucifers-Star-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01MDM9MCT/ref=mt_kindle?_encoding=UTF8&amp;me=&amp;qid=\" target=\"_blank\">Lucifer's Star</a>, </i>and the <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Rules-Supervillainy-Saga-Book-ebook/dp/B07MB89S33/\" target=\"_blank\">Supervillainy Saga</a>.</i><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","name":"CTPhipps","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12002_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13933"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-05-27T11:02:30-07:00","id":1449825,"title":"","content":"Don't get me wrong, sales is sales and money is success. But if we're discussing quality, a book with no marketing doing significantly better in one sales medium than a book with more marketing that has more sales mediums... <br /> That and, well, where's my W5,M5, C5, Wr5? Why does everything look like a fucking mess (except the TV show which we know little about except that it has competent people) ? <br /> <br /> <br /> If you wanted V5 to sell, the trick would actually be to make it as bland an innofensive as possible. Just copy-past V20, streamline and improve some rules, give us a metaplot where the Augustus Giovanni got chomped and the necromancers are all trying to kill one another, because that's cool and we all want it to happen, but it's also safe and it's not going to upset anybody. Every V5 metaplot development feels like it comes from a place of... well, passive agressiveness, to put it mildly; some of them browse these forums, so I can't be too honest, but there's a big sense of trying to flip everything on it's head to make a statement, and it doesn't come across too well; Masquerade? No, Have an Inquisition. You want to play a monster? I've deleted the Sabbat for you. Tremere pyramid? Boom. You want sexy politics? So do I, so I've made everything a mirror of 2016 bipartisanship. Smart camarilla? Ditto. Beast I am lest a Beast I become? Messy criticals. Wanna play a thaumaturge? Well I got rid of paths.... And so on and so forth. Antagonistic seems like an apt description. Doing all this is a risk. Why don't Hollywood movies have profound messages and don't do much original? Because weird creative ideas flop and offend people.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25794-mywifeisscary","name":"MyWifeIsScary","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25794_2.png","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3711"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-05-27T11:07:50-07:00","id":1449829,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MyWifeIsScary</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1443592-the-official-v5-vs-v20-thread?p=1449825#post1449825\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Don't get me wrong, sales is sales and money is success. But if we're discussing quality, a book with no marketing doing significantly better in one sales medium than a book with more marketing that has more sales mediums...<br /> That and, well, where's my W5,M5, C5, Wr5? Why does everything look like a fucking mess (except the TV show which we know little about except that it has competent people) ?</div> </div> </div> </div>Eh, V20 is a very beloved game and very much so. However, I also argue that V5 &quot;competing&quot; with V20 is an illusion made by fans because V5 fans are very often people coming off V20 and the latter having revived the tabletop RPG.<br /> <br /> In short, it's not a competition but an extension.<br /> <br /> It's like saying Dragon Age: Origins is competing with Dragon Age 2 and Inquisition.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <br /> If you wanted V5 to sell, the trick would actually be to make it as bland an innofensive as possible. Just copy-past V20, streamline and improve some rules, give us a metaplot where the Augustus Giovanni got chomped and the necromancers are all trying to kill one another, because that's cool and we all want it to happen, but it's also safe and it's not going to upset anybody. Every V5 metaplot development feels like it comes from a place of... well, passive agressiveness, to put it mildly; some of them browse these forums, so I can't be too honest, but there's a big sense of trying to flip everything on it's head to make a statement, and it doesn't come across too well; Masquerade? No, Have an Inquisition. You want to play a monster? I've deleted the Sabbat for you. Tremere pyramid? Boom. You want sexy politics? So do I, so I've made everything a mirror of 2016 bipartisanship. Smart camarilla? Ditto. Beast I am lest a Beast I become? Messy criticals. Wanna play a thaumaturge? Well I got rid of paths.... And so on and so forth. Antagonistic seems like an apt description. Doing all this is a risk. Why don't Hollywood movies have profound messages and don't do much original? Because weird creative ideas flop and offend people </div> </div> </div>I think it says everything about the differences between us that I didn't buy V20 until Beckett's Jyhad Diary because I realized that it didn't have any metaplot or changes and thus didn't add anything to my game.<br /> <br /> I missed out on a lot of good content as a result.<br /> <br /> But yes, I long held the view that you have no reason to buy a new edition of any game if it doesn't shake things up. Rules mean very little to me versus story.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Author of <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Cthulhu-Armageddon-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01KUOM7SI/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982844&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Cthulhu+Armageddon\" target=\"_blank\">Cthulhu Armageddon</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Teenage-Weredeer-Bright-Falls-Mysteries-ebook/dp/B075TTN2FN/ref=sr_1_2?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982717&amp;sr=1-2&amp;keywords=Weredeer#customerReviews\" target=\"_blank\">I was a Teenage Weredeer</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Straight-Outta-Fangton-Comedic-Vampire-ebook/dp/B01KNHICCC/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982774&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Straight+Outta+Fangton\" target=\"_blank\">Straight Outta Fangton</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Lucifers-Star-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01MDM9MCT/ref=mt_kindle?_encoding=UTF8&amp;me=&amp;qid=\" target=\"_blank\">Lucifer's Star</a>, </i>and the <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Rules-Supervillainy-Saga-Book-ebook/dp/B07MB89S33/\" target=\"_blank\">Supervillainy Saga</a>.</i><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","name":"CTPhipps","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12002_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13933"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-05-27T11:17:58-07:00","id":1449837,"title":"","content":"Have you played DnD 5e? There's no setting there, just updated rules, yet it's wildly successful. Perhaps a good chunk of that is due to more people being into tabletop than before, but there's also... the part where the rules are better and easier to understand. Infact with how light the rules are, it gives you more time with the story. It's not a perfect system and there's little things other editions have done better, but most will agree it's overall the best system that makes stories better.<br /> <br /> V5 is dense rules with dense metaplot. No thank you.<br /> <br /> Edit: <br /> V5 is &quot;competing&quot; with V20 in that it shits on a lot of V20 stuff. Incompatibilities abound. Nobody likes to be told that their stuff doesn't work no more, nobody wants to have their toys taken away.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25794-mywifeisscary","name":"MyWifeIsScary","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25794_2.png","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3711"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-05-27T11:21:25-07:00","id":1449838,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MyWifeIsScary</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1443592-the-official-v5-vs-v20-thread?p=1449837#post1449837\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Have you played DnD 5e? There's no setting there, just updated rules, yet it's wildly successful. Perhaps a good chunk of that is due to more people being into tabletop than before, but there's also... the part where the rules are better and easier to understand. Infact with how light the rules are, it gives you more time with the story. It's not a perfect system and there's little things other editions have done better, but most will agree it's overall the best system that makes stories better.<br /> <br /> V5 is dense rules with dense metaplot. No thank you.<br /> <br /> Edit:<br /> V5 is &quot;competing&quot; with V20 in that it shits on a lot of V20 stuff. Incompatibilities abound. Nobody likes to be told that their stuff doesn't work no more, nobody wants to have their toys taken away.</div> </div> </div> </div>Nope. I have never seen any reason to move past D&amp;D 3rd Edition and Pathfinder. I may buy Forgotten Realms' updated version since they reversed the Spellplague but I have no interest in rules updates.<br /> <br /> The rules supplement the story to me.<br /> <br /> But I am illustrating different STs prioritize different things.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Author of <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Cthulhu-Armageddon-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01KUOM7SI/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982844&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Cthulhu+Armageddon\" target=\"_blank\">Cthulhu Armageddon</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Teenage-Weredeer-Bright-Falls-Mysteries-ebook/dp/B075TTN2FN/ref=sr_1_2?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982717&amp;sr=1-2&amp;keywords=Weredeer#customerReviews\" target=\"_blank\">I was a Teenage Weredeer</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Straight-Outta-Fangton-Comedic-Vampire-ebook/dp/B01KNHICCC/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982774&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Straight+Outta+Fangton\" target=\"_blank\">Straight Outta Fangton</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Lucifers-Star-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01MDM9MCT/ref=mt_kindle?_encoding=UTF8&amp;me=&amp;qid=\" target=\"_blank\">Lucifer's Star</a>, </i>and the <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Rules-Supervillainy-Saga-Book-ebook/dp/B07MB89S33/\" target=\"_blank\">Supervillainy Saga</a>.</i><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","name":"CTPhipps","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12002_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13933"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-05-27T11:31:43-07:00","id":1449842,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>zee PaTrick</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1443592-the-official-v5-vs-v20-thread?p=1449796#post1449796\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I enjoy watching the tribalism and fear of the new of some people here. It must be quite reassuring to be blind to the fact that your beliefs are not monolithic and people have embraced the new. There's evidence. It's like the Truth. It's out there.</div> </div> </div> </div><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">This is pretty much the exact sort of thing I asked people to refrain from. Take a day off from the thread. This is about a nice respectful conversation regarding the merits of both editions.<br /> <br /> At least theoretically.<br /> <br /> Basically, OPP publishes both so it has a vested interest in both sides being happy.</span>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Author of <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Cthulhu-Armageddon-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01KUOM7SI/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982844&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Cthulhu+Armageddon\" target=\"_blank\">Cthulhu Armageddon</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Teenage-Weredeer-Bright-Falls-Mysteries-ebook/dp/B075TTN2FN/ref=sr_1_2?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982717&amp;sr=1-2&amp;keywords=Weredeer#customerReviews\" target=\"_blank\">I was a Teenage Weredeer</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Straight-Outta-Fangton-Comedic-Vampire-ebook/dp/B01KNHICCC/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982774&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Straight+Outta+Fangton\" target=\"_blank\">Straight Outta Fangton</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Lucifers-Star-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01MDM9MCT/ref=mt_kindle?_encoding=UTF8&amp;me=&amp;qid=\" target=\"_blank\">Lucifer's Star</a>, </i>and the <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Rules-Supervillainy-Saga-Book-ebook/dp/B07MB89S33/\" target=\"_blank\">Supervillainy Saga</a>.</i><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","name":"CTPhipps","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12002_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13933"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-05-27T11:46:00-07:00","id":1449845,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>zee PaTrick</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1443592-the-official-v5-vs-v20-thread?p=1449796#post1449796\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Here's where location matters. I feel those numbers would be completely different on Twitter if you asked the #vamily. Or the Twitch subscribers of the actual plays. Echo chambers tend to echo.</div> </div> </div> </div>The problem is when you take V5 out of echo chambers, the conversations look more like things here, and less like #vamily Twitter.<br /> <br /> In general TT RPG spaces, V5 was a game that had a lot of hype, and that all dried up and mostly nobody gives a shit about it anymore because either (1) it's not d20 or (2) it's seen as too &quot;90s&quot; but doesn't actually commit to VtM's 90s aesthetic.<br /> <br /> That's not a problem if you're interesting in pushing a TT RPG that isn't D&amp;D. That is a problem if you're trying to make the VtM brand matter.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> It's like the Truth. It's out there. </div> </div> </div>Citing a poster for believing in UFOs seems questionable. The whole point of that being popularized in the X-Files is that, yes, Mulder is actually right, but no sane person would actually believe him without personally witnessing things, and there's a massive government conspiracy hiding the truth.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CTPhipps</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1443592-the-official-v5-vs-v20-thread?p=1449807#post1449807\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">This is just silly to say otherwise.</div> </div> </div> </div>You're framing it in an actively diametric fashion to exclude middles. I pointed out all the flaws in the &quot;print run&quot; point. V20 is available in multiple languages so what does that mean exactly? The hype for Bloodlines 2 is waaaay down from where it was after Earthblood was meh and the general wider videogame audience seeing lots of red flags.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> I'm going to be snarky here, I'm sorry. Yes, generally selling more is a sign of being more successful. </div> </div> </div>It's one form of success, yes, but you've stated forms of success that are not pure sales as vital. So sales success doesn't back that up.<br /> <br /> Do you have any evidence that, for example, Paradox has even made back the money it paid for the WW IPs yet? That all the investment in developing V5, Earthblood, BL 2, etc. has actually gotten them into making money instead of recovering funds yet?<br /> <br /> You're an author, you understand that raw sales figures are not your bottom line.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> We should be happy that Paradox Entertainment has expanded White Wolf to new markets, new mediums, and put things back in stores. </div> </div> </div>We should be happy with the TT RPG books that they make, instead of swallowing bad design and development choices because the TT RPG books aren't being made to actually be good at being TT RPG books (which is your own claim to be clear).<br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CTPhipps</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1443592-the-official-v5-vs-v20-thread?p=1449824#post1449824\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I'd very much like Justin Achilli's thinking on this and hope it's in the developer's blog. I think it's a bad decision.</div> </div> </div> </div>Is anyone surprised, given Achili's time leading VtM back in the day, by his Twitter comments about this?<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CTPhipps</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1443592-the-official-v5-vs-v20-thread?p=1449829#post1449829\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">In short, it's not a competition but an extension.<br /> <br /> It's like saying Dragon Age: Origins is competing with Dragon Age 2 and Inquisition.</div> </div> </div> </div>Interesting comparison.<br /> <br /> The Dragon Age serious put serious investment into making it so you could have choices you made in previous games carry over into the new games. That was a pretty serious move by them to make each game an extension of the next: you could alter how DA2 played by how you played DAO.<br /> <br /> V5 did pretty much the exact opposite of that. Why is it surprising that people don't feel like it's an extension when V5 keeps cutting out things fans liked about previous editions? Backwards compatibility (even if not strictly so mechanically) is important for giving a sense of extension.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> But yes, I long held the view that you have no reason to buy a new edition of any game if it doesn't shake things up. Rules mean very little to me versus story. </div> </div> </div>TT RPGs are games, hence the G. The rules are going to matter to a lot of people even if not to you personally.<br /> <br /> And there's no point in buying a new edition of you think the shake ups are bad. Buying them just because there's a shake up isn't a great approach to things.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-05-27T12:42:24-07:00","id":1449857,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Heavy Arms</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">Do you have any evidence that, for example, Paradox has even made back the money it paid for the WW IPs yet? That all the investment in developing V5, Earthblood, BL 2, etc. has actually gotten them into making money instead of recovering funds yet?</div> </div> </div> </div>My attitude regarding this is the fact that I think it is blindingly obvious it's a massive success rather than a small scale success let alone a failure. I think it's not worth arguing about and we should be happy for the success. Paradox Entertainment has been full steam ahead on all these projects and been expanding more and more their World of Darkness line. It also helps that they're not actually spending any money on this because people PAY THEM for the license and they get a cut of the profits.<br /> <br /> They get a slice out of every visual novel while paying nothing. Same with Vault comics and Winter's Teeth, which has also been the largest success for that company. And now they've got a huge chunk of change from the Expanse's production company.<br /> <br /> But yes, I admit I'm mostly curious why people are invested in the IDEA of being it a failure. It's like, &quot;what would it mean if it was or wasn't&quot;?<br /> <br /> I said before that I don't think they are in competition and that it is a product of fans trying to make a fight where there is no fight. That is criticizing a certain mindset, yes, but I don't think it's an insult.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Heavy Arms</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">Is anyone surprised, given Achili's time leading VtM back in the day, by his Twitter comments about this?</div> </div> </div> </div>Given he did a fantastic job with the Sabbat in Revised...yes?<br /> <br /> Did people expect something poor out of him regarding this and I didn't know about it?<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Heavy Arms</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">The Dragon Age serious put serious investment into making it so you could have choices you made in previous games carry over into the new games. That was a pretty serious move by them to make each game an extension of the next: you could alter how DA2 played by how you played DAO.<br /> <br /> V5 did pretty much the exact opposite of that. Why is it surprising that people don't feel like it's an extension when V5 keeps cutting out things fans liked about previous editions? Backwards compatibility (even if not strictly so mechanically) is important for giving a sense of extension.</div> </div> </div> </div>My take on the subject is that each game built on the changes of the previous edition so that issues like Gehenna, mortal agencies investigating the undead, and a progresive timeline are important. I'm not a 100% fan of everything they did. The Sabbat not being a Core Book of V5 was a huge mistake. However, I think that the game is interesting for developments rather than remaining static.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Author of <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Cthulhu-Armageddon-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01KUOM7SI/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982844&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Cthulhu+Armageddon\" target=\"_blank\">Cthulhu Armageddon</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Teenage-Weredeer-Bright-Falls-Mysteries-ebook/dp/B075TTN2FN/ref=sr_1_2?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982717&amp;sr=1-2&amp;keywords=Weredeer#customerReviews\" target=\"_blank\">I was a Teenage Weredeer</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Straight-Outta-Fangton-Comedic-Vampire-ebook/dp/B01KNHICCC/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982774&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Straight+Outta+Fangton\" target=\"_blank\">Straight Outta Fangton</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Lucifers-Star-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01MDM9MCT/ref=mt_kindle?_encoding=UTF8&amp;me=&amp;qid=\" target=\"_blank\">Lucifer's Star</a>, </i>and the <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Rules-Supervillainy-Saga-Book-ebook/dp/B07MB89S33/\" target=\"_blank\">Supervillainy Saga</a>.</i><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":12002,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","user":"CTPhipps","date":". 05-27-2021, 03:49 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","name":"CTPhipps","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12002_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13933"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-05-27T13:23:04-07:00","id":1449867,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CTPhipps</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1443592-the-official-v5-vs-v20-thread?p=1449857#post1449857\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">My attitude regarding this is the fact that I think it is blindingly obvious it's a massive success rather than a small scale success let alone a failure.</div> </div> </div> </div>Which is why I asked for evidence, not feelings on the matter.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> It also helps that they're not actually spending any money on this because people PAY THEM for the license and they get a cut of the profits. </div> </div> </div>Paradox spends money on this stuff. They have employees that manage the WoD IP at a minimum. Yes, Paradox is largely operating by licensing as a business model, but that means they have to invest in marketing and PR for the brand to maximize their profits.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> But yes, I admit I'm mostly curious why people are invested in the IDEA of being it a failure. It's like, &quot;what would it mean if it was or wasn't&quot;? </div> </div> </div>You're constantly shifting goal posts about what success means in a fashion that feels like you're less curious about what people think, and more invested in claiming you know what's in our heads.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> I said before that I don't think they are in competition and that it is a product of fans trying to make a fight where there is no fight. That is criticizing a certain mindset, yes, but I don't think it's an insult. </div> </div> </div>Dude, you edited out the part of your own post where you said the exact same thing you just red texted zee PaTrick for: claiming that people don't like V5 because they don't want a new edition.<br /> <br /> Who's trying to turn things into a fight exactly?<br /> <br /> And Paradox is responsible for making it a competition, because they aren't letting the X20 books remain a thing managed by Onyx Path that runs concurrently with V5, while not making V5 an extension of previous VtM games too a large number of fans that aren't you no matter how much you want to inflate your feelings about that.<br /> <br /> If Paradox wasn't clearly quashing more X20 support (like how the WoD and the CofD are being done in parallel now), it wouldn't feel as much like a competition. If Paradox wasn't narrowing the WoD down so fans start feeling excluded by the parts of the WoD they cared about getting kicked to the curb, it wouldn't feel like such a competition.<br /> <br /> When oWW kill the cWoD and replaced it with the nWoD... is was a competition. It wasn't good for either. When V20 revived the cWoD and both lines coexisted, it wasn't a competition and things got better for everyone. Paradox could do that with pre-V5 and V5 if they want to make V5 super focused on a specific play experience. They're choosing not to.<br /> <br /> Ultimately it doesn't matter if the sense of competition is a &quot;product&quot; of fans. It's Paradox's job to understand their audience, and this sort of sense of competition was and is incredibly predictable. So Paradox is not blameless in starting it, or making it worse.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Given he did a fantastic job with the Sabbat in Revised...yes?<br /> <br /> Did people expect something poor out of him regarding this and I didn't know about it? </div> </div> </div>It's not how he did with The Guide to the Sabbat. It's his rather lengthy reputation for &quot;play the game the way we tell you to play it, not all the ways you can play it based on the rules we gave you,&quot; attitudes in Revised. While not 100% deserved (mostly because VtM comes first and the other gameline developers were not bound to VtM's whims), he was the poster child for early 00's WW's negative reputation as talking down to the players and pissing off people that enjoyed the more gonzo side of 2e.<br /> <br /> I don't think anyone was expecting him to make the Sabbat a NPC faction. But I don't think anyone familiar with his Revised work is at all surprised with how he's defended that position after taking it.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> However, I think that the game is interesting for developments rather than remaining static. </div> </div> </div>Mechanical improvements are developments too.<br /> <br /> And you're dodging the point that change for the sake of change is not necessarily good change that makes a new edition valuable to fans.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":6}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-05-27T14:00:52-07:00","id":1449871,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Heavy Arms</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1443592-the-official-v5-vs-v20-thread?p=1449867#post1449867\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Which is why I asked for evidence, not feelings on the matter.</div> </div> </div> </div>Yes. The evidence is the multiple reprintings, the release in multiple languages, the fact that it is carried in stores but V20 isn't, the fact that it has had multiple Visual Novels on steam that have charted, the fact that it is a top selling comic, the fact that it has recently secured the rights for a World of Darkness TV series and rights to more spin offs. The fact there was a video game that was released and recouped its expenditures. The fact that Coteries of New York and Shadows of New York has been released as a physical box release on PS4 due to its success.<br /> <br /> Is that enough? Serious question.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> You're constantly shifting goal posts about what success means in a fashion that feels like you're less curious about what people think, and more invested in claiming you know what's in our heads. </div> </div> </div>I'm not shifting the goal posts because I don't actually believe there's an argument. I think part of the problem is that I started the conversation dismissive of the argument rather than attempting to argue it. I thought it was something everyone accepted.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> And Paradox is responsible for making it a competition, because they aren't letting the X20 books remain a thing managed by Onyx Path that runs concurrently with V5, while not making V5 an extension of previous VtM games too a large number of fans that aren't you no matter how much you want to inflate your feelings about that. </div> </div> </div>This is a weird statement because the V20 books are still on sale and a valuable source of revenue for OPP.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> If Paradox wasn't clearly quashing more X20 support (like how the WoD and the CofD are being done in parallel now), it wouldn't feel as much like a competition. If Paradox wasn't narrowing the WoD down so fans start feeling excluded by the parts of the WoD they cared about getting kicked to the curb, it wouldn't feel like such a competition. </div> </div> </div>That would be unprecedented and weird for a new Edition of a game.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> It's not how he did with The Guide to the Sabbat. It's his rather lengthy reputation for &quot;play the game the way we tell you to play it, not all the ways you can play it based on the rules we gave you,&quot; attitudes in Revised. While not 100% deserved (mostly because VtM comes first and the other gameline developers were not bound to VtM's whims), he was the poster child for early 00's WW's negative reputation as talking down to the players and pissing off people that enjoyed the more gonzo side of 2e.<br /> <br /> I don't think anyone was expecting him to make the Sabbat a NPC faction. But I don't think anyone familiar with his Revised work is at all surprised with how he's defended that position after taking it. </div> </div> </div>Thanks for telling me.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> And you're dodging the point that change for the sake of change is not necessarily good change that makes a new edition valuable to fans. </div> </div> </div>I don't believe any of the authors made &quot;change for change's sake.&quot; They believe it was interesting and wrote it to the best of their abilities, which is why its good, IMHO. You may disagree.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Author of <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Cthulhu-Armageddon-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01KUOM7SI/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982844&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Cthulhu+Armageddon\" target=\"_blank\">Cthulhu Armageddon</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Teenage-Weredeer-Bright-Falls-Mysteries-ebook/dp/B075TTN2FN/ref=sr_1_2?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982717&amp;sr=1-2&amp;keywords=Weredeer#customerReviews\" target=\"_blank\">I was a Teenage Weredeer</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Straight-Outta-Fangton-Comedic-Vampire-ebook/dp/B01KNHICCC/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982774&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Straight+Outta+Fangton\" target=\"_blank\">Straight Outta Fangton</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Lucifers-Star-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01MDM9MCT/ref=mt_kindle?_encoding=UTF8&amp;me=&amp;qid=\" target=\"_blank\">Lucifer's Star</a>, </i>and the <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Rules-Supervillainy-Saga-Book-ebook/dp/B07MB89S33/\" target=\"_blank\">Supervillainy Saga</a>.</i><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":12002,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","user":"CTPhipps","date":". 05-27-2021, 06:34 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","name":"CTPhipps","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12002_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13933"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-05-27T15:09:28-07:00","id":1449875,"title":"","content":"I don't believe Heavy Arms is trying to make a fight where there is no fight. But claims that V5 is a massive financial and artistic success, without any numbers to back it up, are something to be skeptical about. As noted, reprintings don't signify a huge financial success unless you have a number attached to them. Six reprintings is great if there's a million copies per run, but not as much if there was 500.<br /> <br /> You mentioned this person you were arguing with.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CTPhipps</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1443592-the-official-v5-vs-v20-thread?p=1449807#post1449807\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I'm an author. Someone one said that I would never sell as many copies as one guy who sold ebooks exclusive.<br /> <br /> I pointed out that I sold more than him by adding in my audiobook sales.</div> </div> </div> </div>Presumably you compared numbers so you could have some facts to base who &quot;won&quot; off of.<br /> <br /> It doesn't help that in some of your posts you compare posters you're arguing with to Star Wars and Marvel movie trolls. Anyone can point at the budget and sales figures for those movies, they're publicly accessible. Someone arguing about an ephemeral &quot;success&quot; that goes beyond those numbers isn't being respectful to the conversation.<br /> <br /> Also, Paradox Interactive has a License Request Form link on their front page that would allow anyone to get access to the license. There have been no World of Darkness &quot;tv shows&quot; since the 90s, some showrunners issued a press release stating that they want to do something with it. It has a lot more potential than Martin Ericsson saying the same thing a few years ago but it doesn't mean there's a World of Darkness Cinematic Universe. It's great that these games are getting more publicity, but that does not mean everyone has to throw up V5 signs or they're being an irrational troll.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> However, it's a bit of the nature of the Beast that I am the guy people generally expects to be the V5 defender because this board has quite a few people with a vocan dislike. Fine, it's not their bag. That's just how it goes. </div> </div> </div>If people expect you to be the &quot;V5 defender&quot; it's because you're responding to their every post and shutting down their points about the success of the game without any evidence.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-05-27T15:12:44-07:00","id":1449876,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CTPhipps</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1443592-the-official-v5-vs-v20-thread?p=1449871#post1449871\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Is that enough? Serious question.</div> </div> </div> </div>No, because it's answering a different question than the one asked.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> I'm not shifting the goal posts because I don't actually believe there's an argument. </div> </div> </div>These are not mutually exclusive issues. I would say that you're shifting around between different types of success is understandable given your approach to the conversation, but that doesn't change that it comes off as goal post shifting rather than engaging in what people are saying.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> This is a weird statement because the V20 books are still on sale and a valuable source of revenue for OPP. </div> </div> </div>It isn't at all a weird statement because of the wider context of the situation as has been discussed ad nausem.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> That would be unprecedented and weird for a new Edition of a game. </div> </div> </div>Not really. The very first &quot;new edition&quot; in RPGs was when D&amp;D split into AD&amp;D and D&amp;D Basic, which ran parallel to each other.<br /> <br /> There was a period where four different versions of the Storyteller system (2e, Revised, Trinity, Exalted) all had books being made at the same time.<br /> <br /> In the relatively small sample size of &quot;RPGs with a significant number of editions&quot; it's rather well precedented and within the bounds of normal.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> I don't believe any of the authors made &quot;change for change's sake. </div> </div> </div>I'm not trying to say you are. I'm saying you are advocating a position where change for the sake of change is a greater priority than many other considerations. That shaking things up is the measure of justification for a new edition.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-05-27T22:53:00-07:00","id":1449944,"title":"","content":"Six reprintings means something wasn't good enough five times.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25794-mywifeisscary","name":"MyWifeIsScary","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25794_2.png","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3711"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-05-27T23:06:22-07:00","id":1449946,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MyWifeIsScary</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1443592-the-official-v5-vs-v20-thread?p=1449944#post1449944\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Six reprintings means something wasn't good enough five times.</div> </div> </div> </div>*leans in* *whispers* Actually it means that it sold out six times.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Author of <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Cthulhu-Armageddon-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01KUOM7SI/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982844&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Cthulhu+Armageddon\" target=\"_blank\">Cthulhu Armageddon</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Teenage-Weredeer-Bright-Falls-Mysteries-ebook/dp/B075TTN2FN/ref=sr_1_2?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982717&amp;sr=1-2&amp;keywords=Weredeer#customerReviews\" target=\"_blank\">I was a Teenage Weredeer</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Straight-Outta-Fangton-Comedic-Vampire-ebook/dp/B01KNHICCC/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982774&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Straight+Outta+Fangton\" target=\"_blank\">Straight Outta Fangton</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Lucifers-Star-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01MDM9MCT/ref=mt_kindle?_encoding=UTF8&amp;me=&amp;qid=\" target=\"_blank\">Lucifer's Star</a>, </i>and the <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Rules-Supervillainy-Saga-Book-ebook/dp/B07MB89S33/\" target=\"_blank\">Supervillainy Saga</a>.</i><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","name":"CTPhipps","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12002_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13933"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-05-27T23:25:14-07:00","id":1449948,"title":"","content":"Actually it can mean both. Which is part of the problem, in addition to the fact that we don't know what the sizes of the print runs were to have any idea how many actual books it's been.<br /> <br /> The number of reprintings that have included significant errata most times <b>is</b> a sign of major issues in early development; aka &quot;wasn't good enough.&quot;<br /> <br /> But new print runs do mean they sold out of the old print runs too.<br /> <br /> To try an analogy:<br /> <br /> I'm shopping for a new car. I ask someone about their car which they seem to enjoy. I ask how it's been for longevity and so on because a lot of cars are hard to maintain. I get the response of, &quot;Well, I've only had the one.&quot; with a tone of that being a good thing.<br /> <br /> It sounds like a strong endorsement... but logically it's actually meaningless. Has one cost the MSRP of the car five times over in cost-of-ownership? Has it only been one because it's basically brand new? Is there a Ship of Thesus caveat where even if affordable it's still been in the shop so many times everything's been replaced already?<br /> <br /> Like I said, it's not really an answer to the question, it's a contextless number that sounds positive on the surface.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-05-28T00:07:35-07:00","id":1449952,"title":"","content":"Well in lieu of lack of information, I'll drop out. I think the fact that V5 is available on Amazon and in stores means it has the edge but I can't say for 100% certainty it's a massive huge success.<br /> <br /> So I won't bring it up again as a given.<br /> <br /> Only Paradox Entertainment knows for sure.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Author of <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Cthulhu-Armageddon-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01KUOM7SI/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982844&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Cthulhu+Armageddon\" target=\"_blank\">Cthulhu Armageddon</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Teenage-Weredeer-Bright-Falls-Mysteries-ebook/dp/B075TTN2FN/ref=sr_1_2?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982717&amp;sr=1-2&amp;keywords=Weredeer#customerReviews\" target=\"_blank\">I was a Teenage Weredeer</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Straight-Outta-Fangton-Comedic-Vampire-ebook/dp/B01KNHICCC/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982774&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Straight+Outta+Fangton\" target=\"_blank\">Straight Outta Fangton</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Lucifers-Star-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01MDM9MCT/ref=mt_kindle?_encoding=UTF8&amp;me=&amp;qid=\" target=\"_blank\">Lucifer's Star</a>, </i>and the <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Rules-Supervillainy-Saga-Book-ebook/dp/B07MB89S33/\" target=\"_blank\">Supervillainy Saga</a>.</i><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","name":"CTPhipps","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12002_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13933"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-05-28T01:07:48-07:00","id":1449953,"title":"","content":"When WW had games regularly in the top 5 for ICv2, it was for the World of Darkness as a whole. I suspect a big reason why V5 hasn't stayed in the top 5 is that it's out on its own, ATM, without W5 and M5 to back it up. It would be interesting to see how it fares with a complete WoD5 <br /> <br /> I suspect if you play crossovers, or play multiple WoD games, you'd be tempted to play the version of VTM that meshes the most with the others. We play CTD and WTO sometimes, too, which only exist in their 20th Anniversary forms.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Writer, publisher, performer<br /> Mostly he/his, sometimes she/her IRL <a href=\"https://adam-lowe.com\" target=\"_blank\">https://adam-lowe.com</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5291-adambeyoncelowe","name":"adambeyoncelowe","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5291_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2802"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-05-28T03:07:38-07:00","id":1449959,"title":"","content":"Where is W5? surely it should be here by now.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25794-mywifeisscary","name":"MyWifeIsScary","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25794_2.png","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3711"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-05-28T04:06:45-07:00","id":1449963,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MyWifeIsScary</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1443592-the-official-v5-vs-v20-thread?p=1449959#post1449959\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Where is W5? surely it should be here by now.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Perhaps it will be antagonist only so they don't dilute focus from the Anarchs? <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/wink.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Wink\" smilieid=\"4\" class=\"inlineimg\" />*<br /> <br /> <br /> *Joke..........probably.........honestly at this stage who knows? Will Garou have Humanity and Touchstones as well? Fuck knows.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26564-badfurryfanfic","name":"BadFurryFanFic","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2020"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"93"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-05-28T06:10:23-07:00","id":1449970,"title":"","content":"Pretty sure they\u2019re going to repurpose their shiny hunger dice mechanic for all the splats; Rage dice for W5, Paradox dice for M5, Angst dice for Wr5... not sure for Changelings... their innate state is the one more likely to cause chaos so something like \u201cBanality\u201d should be reducing the chaos not increasing it.<br /> <br /> My biggest concern given what they\u2019ve done with Disciplines in V5 and their stated desire for \u201cOne World of Darkness\u201d is that M5\u2019s magic system would be turned into lists of discrete powers with limits on how many you could have to keep it balanced with what V5 characters are capable of.<br /> <br /> Not saying that WILL happen, but given decisions like \u201cNPC Sabbat only\u201d I can\u2019t say I have confidence. My solace is that at the rate they\u2019re going it could be a decade before they get around to doing a M5.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1328-chris24601","name":"Chris24601","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"520"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-05-28T08:04:02-07:00","id":1449978,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CTPhipps</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1443592-the-official-v5-vs-v20-thread?p=1449760#post1449760\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Also, quite a few of what is in V5 is an adaptation of what was in Bloodlines.<br /> <br /> * Choose between Anarch and Camarilla</div> </div> </div> </div>I wanna come back to this because it's so fucking WRONG I just gotta. Obviously, you're wrong because you can clearly choose to side with the Cartoonish Evil Asians or fight for yourself and tell the anarchs to get fucked, but you're also wrong because you're missing the actual arguments the games have. Bloodlines gives you an idiot prince, but otherwise it presents the camarilla in a very favourable light; giving you the option to help strauss in the end, but also having almost all the characters that seem to know what they're doing be pro cam. The first character you can have a good discussion with about politics is Tung, a smart guy, and he's pro cam. The Jeanette/Theresee argument's it's own statement. Meanwhile, three out of four characters at the last round are clowns (the last is a comedian). Strauss is unreasonably cool for a Tremere, and Gary is ostensibly pro cam and the less worldly nosferatu who follow him might have anarch ideas but trust Gary enough. The Baron is anti-cam, but he's a baron. The only good proponents for the Anarchs are Jack and the Baron. The good proponents for the Camarilla is basically everyone Camarilla except the prince himself, and most of the anarchs since Jeanette, Damsel, Nines and Nam are all joke characters that make the Anarchs look bad (Maybe nines wasn't intentional, but Damsel is certainly intentional)<br /> <br /> Opinions on individual characters aside, the straight of it is that, aside from a disaster prince, the Cam is presented mostly pretty well.<br /> <br /> Now in V5, the Cam have taken their stupid pills. They've rejected their monopolies that allowed them to effectively police the masquerade, they've taken up religion because conservatives are religious and the Cam exists to be the conservatives against the Anarch liberals, and... It suprises me that the Cam are still even playable at this point, it seems like playing a rebel fighting the system is mandatory, even if that system is collapsing under it's own ineptitude.<br /> <br /> There's not really good arguments for any sect anymore. Plenty of reasons why they're failures, but nothing for why they'd succeed.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":25794,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25794-mywifeisscary","user":"MyWifeIsScary","date":". 05-28-2021, 11:19 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25794-mywifeisscary","name":"MyWifeIsScary","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25794_2.png","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3711"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-05-28T08:16:29-07:00","id":1449981,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MyWifeIsScary</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1443592-the-official-v5-vs-v20-thread?p=1449978#post1449978\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">It suprises me that the Cam are still even playable at this point, it seems like playing a rebel fighting the system is mandatory, even if that system is collapsing under it's own ineptitude.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> the camarilla is still playable for ppl that want to rebel from the inside","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25992-archderd","name":"archderd","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25992_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2020"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"205"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-05-28T08:21:59-07:00","id":1449982,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>archderd</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1443592-the-official-v5-vs-v20-thread?p=1449981#post1449981\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> the camarilla is still playable for ppl that want to rebel from the inside</div> </div> </div> </div>Indeed. <br /> Before, if you played cam, you probably wanted a better possition, and you'll be happy to politick for one, but you're going to stay cam because it's the best choice for you. Now it's just a clusterfuck and independence is the only viable option. Oh yeah, the independent clans got swallowed up and are now either directly part of Anarchs or the Cam or they perfectly mirror the Anarchs or the Cam.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25794-mywifeisscary","name":"MyWifeIsScary","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25794_2.png","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3711"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-05-28T10:28:46-07:00","id":1450003,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Chris24601</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1443592-the-official-v5-vs-v20-thread?p=1449970#post1449970\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Pretty sure they\u2019re going to repurpose their shiny hunger dice mechanic for all the splats; Rage dice for W5, Paradox dice for M5, Angst dice for Wr5... not sure for Changelings... their innate state is the one more likely to cause chaos so something like \u201cBanality\u201d should be reducing the chaos not increasing it.<br /> <br /> My biggest concern given what they\u2019ve done with Disciplines in V5 and their stated desire for \u201cOne World of Darkness\u201d is that M5\u2019s magic system would be turned into lists of discrete powers with limits on how many you could have to keep it balanced with what V5 characters are capable of.<br /> <br /> Not saying that WILL happen, but given decisions like \u201cNPC Sabbat only\u201d I can\u2019t say I have confidence. My solace is that at the rate they\u2019re going it could be a decade before they get around to doing a M5.</div> </div> </div> </div>Wraith already has Shadow Dice and Changeling has Nightmare Dice. I assume they might just go with those?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Writer, publisher, performer<br /> Mostly he/his, sometimes she/her IRL <a href=\"https://adam-lowe.com\" target=\"_blank\">https://adam-lowe.com</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5291-adambeyoncelowe","name":"adambeyoncelowe","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5291_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2802"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-05-28T11:16:12-07:00","id":1450021,"title":"","content":"I actually like the idea of Rage dice to an extent because WtA has always struggled with the narrative that the Garou are always on edge and ready to flip out and murder things, but the mechanics for enforcing that are really uneven. Rage is supposed to be something that can ruin mundane life and drive Garou towards isolation from the rest of the world (even nature since normal animals are just as scared of Rage and just as at risk of getting slaughtered if a Garou frenzies).<br /> <br /> Even so, CtD's Nightmare dice are a far more appealing mechanical choice to me... here's hoping if &quot;Splat Dice&quot; are a thing some lessons from the games that already have them get worked into future variations.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-05-28T11:18:33-07:00","id":1450024,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Chris24601</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1443592-the-official-v5-vs-v20-thread?p=1449970#post1449970\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Pretty sure they\u2019re going to repurpose their shiny hunger dice mechanic for all the splats; Rage dice for W5, Paradox dice for M5, Angst dice for Wr5... not sure for Changelings... their innate state is the one more likely to cause chaos so something like \u201cBanality\u201d should be reducing the chaos not increasing it.<br /> <br /> My biggest concern given what they\u2019ve done with Disciplines in V5 and their stated desire for \u201cOne World of Darkness\u201d is that M5\u2019s magic system would be turned into lists of discrete powers with limits on how many you could have to keep it balanced with what V5 characters are capable of.<br /> <br /> Not saying that WILL happen, but given decisions like \u201cNPC Sabbat only\u201d I can\u2019t say I have confidence. My solace is that at the rate they\u2019re going it could be a decade before they get around to doing a M5.</div> </div> </div> </div>I doubt they will make Mage a list of discrete powers. Mage just doesn't lend itself to that. I do think they will drop the idea that you can abandon foci as your Arete goes up. They will likely double-down on the idea that you need to justify each spell with your character's practices, and that you always will even at the max arete a player character can achieve. If you need to draw a pentagram, light candles placed on the skulls of a saint or a murderer, and chant a certain language to cast that fireball, then you always will.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3598-cajunkhan","name":"CajunKhan","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3598_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1700"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-05-28T11:24:05-07:00","id":1450026,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Heavy Arms</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1443592-the-official-v5-vs-v20-thread?p=1450021#post1450021\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I actually like the idea of Rage dice to an extent because WtA has always struggled with the narrative that the Garou are always on edge and ready to flip out and murder things, but the mechanics for enforcing that are really uneven. Rage is supposed to be something that can ruin mundane life and drive Garou towards isolation from the rest of the world (even nature since normal animals are just as scared of Rage and just as at risk of getting slaughtered if a Garou frenzies).<br /> <br /></div> </div> </div> </div>Yeah, the Messy-Critical/Bestial failure system is one of the best new mechanics they've created, and will work really well for werewolves. Vampire and werewolf both shared the problem that they were too Frenzy-Or-Nothing. The Messy-Critical/Bestial failure system is a vast improvement, allowing you to portray creatures who rarely completely lose it, but have something in them poisoning their behavior in subtler ways constantly.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3598-cajunkhan","name":"CajunKhan","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3598_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1700"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-05-28T12:17:11-07:00","id":1450034,"title":"","content":"Messy crits don't work with vampires, because Vampires have this whole masquerade thing and can't afford to lose their shit all the time just because they didn't murder a guy before the big meet, and also Vampires in VTM function as metaphores for society's parasitic elite and it doesn't do well to have the parasitic elite be a bunch of barely-functioning mental wrecks who can't hold a socialite gathering without losing their shit. Messy crits might work for other vampire games, where they're secluded nutters sleeping in coffins and unliving in rural castles, and it'll work with werewolves because they're angry fringe members of society living on cult compounds, but it doesn't work at all for modern, urban predators who're expected to hold up a grand conspiracy.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25794-mywifeisscary","name":"MyWifeIsScary","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25794_2.png","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3711"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-05-28T12:34:10-07:00","id":1450037,"title":"","content":"Messy criticals/bestial failures increase the ease and fun of roleplaying the sort of vampires I see in novels/movies.<br /> <div class=\"videocontainer with-aspect-ratio videocontainer-horizontal\" style=\"aspect-ratio: 16/9;\"> <a class=\"video-frame\" href=\"https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=busozfENY0I\" data-code=\"busozfENY0I\" data-provider=\"youtube\" data-height=\"0\" data-width=\"0\" itemprop=\"video\"> <div class=\"videothumbnail\" style=\"\"> <img src=\"https://img.youtube.com/vi/busozfENY0I/maxresdefault.jpg\" alt=\"\" /> <div class=\"videothumbnailoverlay\"></div> </div> </a> </div><br /> Storyteller-&quot;A bouncer blocks your path. He says 'you want chicken, man, you go someplace else&quot;<br /> <br /> Dandrige Player-&quot;I say 'out of my way' forcefully to intimidate him to move aside&quot;.<br /> <br /> Storyteller-&quot;roll Manipulation+Intimidation&quot;<br /> <br /> *Dandrige Player rolls a Bestial Failure*<br /> <br /> Storyteller-&quot;the bouncer is not intimidated. He says 'move me', and his unbearable insolence causes you to gain the Harm Compulsion&quot;<br /> <br /> Dandrige Player-&quot;I bare my fangs, activate my Eyes of the Beast and Protean Claws, and do a called shot to his jugular with my claws&quot;<br /> <br /> Storyteller-*mentally notes that activating both the eyes and claws should take two rounds, but lets it slide for Rule of Cool's sake* &quot;Roll Strength+Brawl&quot;<br /> <br /> *Dandrige Player rolls, scoring four 10's, and three 6's*<br /> <br /> Storyteller-&quot;you land a devastating critical hit to his jugular. The bouncer goes down, mortally wounded. Another bouncer rushes in to help him.&quot;<br /> <br /> Dandrige player-&quot;I blood surge my Strength, pick him up by the throat, and throw him across the room.&quot;<br /> <br /> Storyteller-&quot;roll Strength+Brawl&quot;<br /> <br /> *Dandrige player rolls, scoring a messy critical*<br /> <br /> Storyteller-&quot;you lift him by the throat, crushing his windpipe in the process, and hurl him across the room. Everyone on the dancefloor panics and rushes for the door. In the chaos, you lose track of Amy&quot;","signature":"","edited":{"userid":3598,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3598-cajunkhan","user":"CajunKhan","date":". 05-30-2021, 12:35 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3598-cajunkhan","name":"CajunKhan","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3598_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1700"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-05-28T12:38:29-07:00","id":1450040,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MyWifeIsScary</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1443592-the-official-v5-vs-v20-thread?p=1450034#post1450034\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Messy crits don't work with vampires, because Vampires have this whole masquerade thing and can't afford to lose their shit all the time just because they didn't murder a guy before the big meet, and also Vampires in VTM function as metaphores for society's parasitic elite and it doesn't do well to have the parasitic elite be a bunch of barely-functioning mental wrecks who can't hold a socialite gathering without losing their shit. Messy crits might work for other vampire games, where they're secluded nutters sleeping in coffins and unliving in rural castles, and it'll work with werewolves because they're angry fringe members of society living on cult compounds, but it doesn't work at all for modern, urban predators who're expected to hold up a grand conspiracy.</div> </div> </div> </div>Vampires have always flipped out and murdered people for the slightest reason. It's literally what frenzies mean. They do it for insults, getting blood on their shoes, or just not liking the look of a guy.<br /> <br /> It's like that scene in Goodfellas where Joe Pesci murders a guy for no reason.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"videocontainer with-aspect-ratio videocontainer-horizontal\" style=\"aspect-ratio: 16/9;\"> <a class=\"video-frame\" href=\"https://youtu.be/IDYKslnO0r0\" data-code=\"IDYKslnO0r0\" data-provider=\"youtube_share\" data-height=\"0\" data-width=\"0\" itemprop=\"video\"> <div class=\"videothumbnail\" style=\"\"> <img src=\"https://img.youtube.com/vi/IDYKslnO0r0/maxresdefault.jpg\" alt=\"\" /> <div class=\"videothumbnailoverlay\"></div> </div> </a> </div>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Author of <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Cthulhu-Armageddon-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01KUOM7SI/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982844&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Cthulhu+Armageddon\" target=\"_blank\">Cthulhu Armageddon</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Teenage-Weredeer-Bright-Falls-Mysteries-ebook/dp/B075TTN2FN/ref=sr_1_2?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982717&amp;sr=1-2&amp;keywords=Weredeer#customerReviews\" target=\"_blank\">I was a Teenage Weredeer</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Straight-Outta-Fangton-Comedic-Vampire-ebook/dp/B01KNHICCC/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982774&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Straight+Outta+Fangton\" target=\"_blank\">Straight Outta Fangton</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Lucifers-Star-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01MDM9MCT/ref=mt_kindle?_encoding=UTF8&amp;me=&amp;qid=\" target=\"_blank\">Lucifer's Star</a>, </i>and the <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Rules-Supervillainy-Saga-Book-ebook/dp/B07MB89S33/\" target=\"_blank\">Supervillainy Saga</a>.</i><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","name":"CTPhipps","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12002_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13933"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-05-28T12:53:17-07:00","id":1450043,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CTPhipps</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1443592-the-official-v5-vs-v20-thread?p=1450040#post1450040\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Vampires have always flipped out and murdered people for the slightest reason. It's literally what frenzies mean. They do it for insults, getting blood on their shoes, or just not liking the look of a guy.<br /> <br /> It's like that scene in Goodfellas where Joe Pesci murders a guy for no reason.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"videocontainer with-aspect-ratio videocontainer-horizontal\" style=\"aspect-ratio: 16/9;\"> <a class=\"video-frame\" href=\"https://youtu.be/IDYKslnO0r0\" data-code=\"IDYKslnO0r0\" data-provider=\"youtube_share\" data-height=\"0\" data-width=\"0\" itemprop=\"video\"> <div class=\"videothumbnail\" style=\"\"> <img src=\"https://img.youtube.com/vi/IDYKslnO0r0/maxresdefault.jpg\" alt=\"\" /> <div class=\"videothumbnailoverlay\"></div> </div> </a> </div></div> </div> </div> </div>Yeah, if anything vampires now frenzy LESS than they originally did. The new system makes it easier to succeed than the old extended five successes on five dice or less thing. The all-or-nothing nature of the old system never felt true to vampires. Frenzies are now pretty rare, but in place we've got a system where vampires routinely experience subtler failures of self-control. Fits vampires in fiction waaayyy better.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3598-cajunkhan","name":"CajunKhan","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3598_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1700"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-05-28T13:03:26-07:00","id":1450046,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CajunKhan</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1443592-the-official-v5-vs-v20-thread?p=1450037#post1450037\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Messy criticals/bestial failures increase the ease and fun of roleplaying the sort of vampires I see in novels/movies.</div> </div> </div> </div>Ultimately, the problem is that VtM is not a &quot;vampire movie/TV/novel&quot; emulator that's designed for making whatever kind of vampires you want from pop-culture, It's its owns specific take on vampires, and changes to how they work on a fundamental level is going to piss off people that liked the general idea of how they worked for decades.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Storyteller-&quot;you lift him by the throat, crushing his windpipe in the process, and hurl him across the room. Everyone on the dancefloor panics and rushes for the door. In the chaos, you lose track of Amy&quot;<br /> </div> </div> </div>Then Dandridge is lucky to just get staked by the Sherrif and left to die at dawn by the Prince (instead of worse potential outcomes) after such a flagrant and hard to cover up Masquerade breach.<br /> <br /> Which is part of the problem. While as CT notes, Frenzy has always been part of VtM, the previous editions made it for more extreme situations so players wouldn't feel railroaded by the system into breaking the laws of vampire society over relatively small situations.<br /> <br /> While the <u>idea</u> of having &quot;angry vampire&quot; moments that aren't full Frenzies is good, having them be as random as V5 has them is questionable to the intent of the game.<br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CTPhipps</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1443592-the-official-v5-vs-v20-thread?p=1450040#post1450040\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Vampires have always flipped out and murdered people for the slightest reason. It's literally what frenzies mean. They do it for insults, getting blood on their shoes, or just not liking the look of a guy.</div> </div> </div> </div>You're overstating that quite a lot.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> It's like that scene in Goodfellas where Joe Pesci murders a guy for no reason. </div> </div> </div>I think, unintentionally, you're proving MWiS's point.<br /> <br /> Tommy DeVito isn't cut out to be a real mobster because he's got no self-control. He's not normal even by the violent criminal standards of his gang. While it happens in organized crime (violence is frequently a way to stand out at low levels of an organization and thus unstably violent people can get ahead in that world), they're problems if they get too much power and their gangs turn on them for it once it gets too much.<br /> <br /> It's one thing for a vampire to be Tommy (probably best not a PC, since the PCs are probably going to have to put him down), it's a different thing for every vampire to be Tommy.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":6}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-05-28T13:19:50-07:00","id":1450055,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Heavy Arms</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1443592-the-official-v5-vs-v20-thread?p=1450046#post1450046\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">It's one thing for a vampire to be Tommy (probably best not a PC, since the PCs are probably going to have to put him down), it's a different thing for every vampire to be Tommy.</div> </div> </div> </div>Tommy may be the Brujah of the group but if you don't think that Lodin or other Ventrue have done the EXACT SAME THING then I feel like you've lost a lot of the central horror of vampire.<br /> <br /> You will kill people you don't want to kill.<br /> <br /> It is a status of your existence.<br /> <br /> The Beast is why being a vampire is a CURSE and not a blessing to people who aren't psychopaths. As early as first Edition, the Prince of Milwaukee murdered his wife in a frenzy during a relatively normal fight.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Author of <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Cthulhu-Armageddon-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01KUOM7SI/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982844&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Cthulhu+Armageddon\" target=\"_blank\">Cthulhu Armageddon</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Teenage-Weredeer-Bright-Falls-Mysteries-ebook/dp/B075TTN2FN/ref=sr_1_2?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982717&amp;sr=1-2&amp;keywords=Weredeer#customerReviews\" target=\"_blank\">I was a Teenage Weredeer</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Straight-Outta-Fangton-Comedic-Vampire-ebook/dp/B01KNHICCC/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982774&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Straight+Outta+Fangton\" target=\"_blank\">Straight Outta Fangton</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Lucifers-Star-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01MDM9MCT/ref=mt_kindle?_encoding=UTF8&amp;me=&amp;qid=\" target=\"_blank\">Lucifer's Star</a>, </i>and the <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Rules-Supervillainy-Saga-Book-ebook/dp/B07MB89S33/\" target=\"_blank\">Supervillainy Saga</a>.</i><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","name":"CTPhipps","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12002_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13933"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-05-28T13:41:56-07:00","id":1450062,"title":"","content":"&quot;We all know a guy who...&quot;<br /> Yeah it works for one guy, but when you're all that guy, it doesn't fucking work does it?<br /> <br /> A full frenzy is good for two reasons; First, it's your fault for getting into a situation where you might frenzy, because the Beast is predictable and hates certain things and you can keep it right by making sure those things it hates aren't around when a frenzy would be a big problem. If you frenzy, it's entirely your fault (or entirely your fault for pissing off someone who can get you to frenzy). Secondly, because frenzies are completely controlled by the Beast for the overwhelming majority of vampires, and the Beast is animalistic, it doesn't feel like the storyteller is fucking you by screwing with your character, because it's a completely different character.<br /> <br /> Messy criticals are terrible because first, it's your fault for not hiding in your haven all night every night or murdering a guy, because they can happen at any time and any place unless you murder someone, and secondly every time the dice show you're going to fuck up the storyteller has to lean back and think of some bullshit way you have fucked things up; there isn't a clear divide between beast and man, so it's your character screwing up, and the ST is screwing him up for you.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":25794,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25794-mywifeisscary","user":"MyWifeIsScary","date":". 05-28-2021, 04:44 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25794-mywifeisscary","name":"MyWifeIsScary","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25794_2.png","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3711"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-05-28T13:53:15-07:00","id":1450064,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CTPhipps</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1443592-the-official-v5-vs-v20-thread?p=1450055#post1450055\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Tommy may be the Brujah of the group but if you don't think that Lodin or other Ventrue have done the EXACT SAME THING then I feel like you've lost a lot of the central horror of vampire.</div> </div> </div> </div>I see nothing in the game that suggests Lodin in specific, or Ventrue in general, regularly kill lower ranking members of their organization over minor mistakes that they blow out of proportion.<br /> <br /> I don't see how every vampire being Tommy DeVito is at all demonstrating an understanding of the &quot;central horror&quot; of vampire. The central horror of vampire is supposed to be personal. Personal horror requires agency. The lessons for horror in Goodfellas are the compromises Tommy's friends make because of Tommy's instability, as their emotional bond to Tommy and the requirements of their existence come into conflict, and they have to make choices none of which are &quot;good.&quot; Henry is the main character for a reason, as it's his story of how all of the choices he made ended up sabotaging who he wanted to be.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> You will kill people you don't want to kill. </div> </div> </div>Tommy wanted to kill the guy though.<br /> <br /> Yes, vampires invariably kill someone. But as I bang on about all the time here... execution of the rules matters. Killing people because you rolled bad, they happened to be there, and the Beast made you do it undercuts the horror of this (yes, even in pre-V5 VtM). The people your character kills because the world they live in puts them in a position where they feel killing someone (or at least putting themselves in a situation where they know it's likely that they'll kill someone) are the ones that leave real horror in their wake, because the character had agency and the consequences are on them. The Curse is that vampires are driven into an existence where they are constantly tempted to choose to devalue life, not that they're Cursed to randomly murder people; at least if you want to focus on the horror of &quot;A Beast I am, Least a Beast I become,&quot; and all that.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> As early as first Edition, the Prince of Milwaukee murdered his wife in a frenzy during a relatively normal fight. </div> </div> </div>Yes, we know, Frenzies have always been a thing.<br /> <br /> But this is the difference between writing fiction and playing RPGs: The authors of a NPC's story can make the Frenzy appropriate and dramatic because they don't have to roll the dice to see what happens. It was possible, so it happened, because that's the story that was being told.<br /> <br /> When you're playing the game, you want to be able to differentiate between places where this drama is good for the narrative, and places it isn't. If you want this moment to really work in a game, the PC has to come home in a bad state, so the fight with the NPC loved one is an obvious risk of the Beast coming out. So there's agency: they choose to stay and have the fight instead of leaving and doing something else, so that when that bad roll happens and the Beast slips in, the vampire can't blame the Beast honestly. <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":6}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-05-28T14:43:12-07:00","id":1450074,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>False Epiphany</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">I just don't understand why White Wolf would do this.</div> </div> </div> </div><div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CTPhipps</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1443592-the-official-v5-vs-v20-thread?p=1449824#post1449824\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Again, I want to know myself.<br /> <br /> WHY are they doing this?<br /> <br /> Who is this for?<br /> <br /> I'd very much like Justin Achilli's thinking on this and hope it's in the developer's blog. I think it's a bad decision.<br /> <br /> The Sabbat are the third pillar of the setting after all.</div> </div> </div> </div>My statement was mostly rhetorical, as I think it's fairly plain <b>why</b> they are doing this. They have a very specific vision for V5's setting they're not willing to compromise on. As evidenced by how they're declaring the second-biggest sect in the setting to now be unplayable by PCs, without regard for the number of potential gamers that will leave in the cold or turn off from V5 altogether.<br /> <br /> The only part that's in the air is what their new vision for the Sabbat looks like. Whatever it is, though... I feel 99% confident it was not worth this, and that there were better ways to implement their new vision. Again, I'd have just introduced breakaway wing of the Sabbat that's not for PCs. It is generally much better to <b>add</b> options to new editions than to take them away.<br /> <br /> I can appreciate and enjoy V5's setting for what it is, like I do every other edition. I'll probably get the Sabbat book. I'll use what parts I like and ignore what parts I don't like. But this a terrible, terrible, terrible decision to make for what has already been a very controversial and PR problem-plagued edition.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://blood-and-bourbon.obsidianportal.com/\" target=\"_blank\">Blood and Bourbon</a>, my New Orleans-based Vampire chronicle.","edited":{"userid":3110,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3110-false-epiphany","user":"False Epiphany","date":". 05-28-2021, 06:21 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3110-false-epiphany","name":"False Epiphany","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3110_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"748"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-05-28T15:11:14-07:00","id":1450084,"title":"","content":"Although I've had long periods of forum torpor, I've been on the various incarnations of the VtM forums since the 90s. I think. And there has always been a certain element of... artistic visions perceiving itself as intrinsically above business sense in general. I am at loss to explain many of the decisions made with the new product except to assume that there has been some kind of final victory of artistic vision over the concept of a broad customer base. More and more, it seems like they are trying to pare down the customer base to the group of people that play their style of game.<br /> <br /> I remember around 2004, developers mentioning on the forums that they'd been amazed at the number of people who bought their products for the lore. For a while it has seemed as though the publishing company of the moment took that onboard and tried to sell to the other customer groups (Hello Becketts Jyhad Diary, best product ever!) This feels a bit like backlash against that.<br /> <br /> I am just at a total loss about whatever business reasoning there could be behind these choices.<br /> <br /> On the positive side, V20 now has a great selling comic book and a TV series in the works. Maybe other media if they can get some progress on these things.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2471-trollroot","name":"Trollroot","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"311"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-05-28T20:15:30-07:00","id":1450127,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CajunKhan</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1443592-the-official-v5-vs-v20-thread?p=1450026#post1450026\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Yeah, the Messy-Critical/Bestial failure system is one of the best new mechanics they've created, and will work really well for werewolves..</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> The thing with Rage is its a two-edged sword it can cause Frenzies and The Curse but it can also be used to heal yourself from devastating injury, to move like the wind and to throw off mental impositions. The MC/BF system is just a semi-randomised punishment mechanic that has no upsides, each time you pick up the dice the risk of damaging your character, the story and the play experience increases markedly. There are no upsides.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26564-badfurryfanfic","name":"BadFurryFanFic","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2020"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"93"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-05-28T20:18:41-07:00","id":1450128,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CajunKhan</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1443592-the-official-v5-vs-v20-thread?p=1450037#post1450037\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Messy criticals/bestial failures increase the ease and fun of roleplaying the sort of vampires I see in novels/movies.<br /> <div class=\"videocontainer with-aspect-ratio videocontainer-horizontal\" style=\"aspect-ratio: 16/9;\"> <a class=\"video-frame\" href=\"https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=busozfENY0I\" data-code=\"busozfENY0I\" data-provider=\"youtube\" data-height=\"0\" data-width=\"0\" itemprop=\"video\"> <div class=\"videothumbnail\" style=\"\"> <img src=\"https://img.youtube.com/vi/busozfENY0I/maxresdefault.jpg\" alt=\"\" /> <div class=\"videothumbnailoverlay\"></div> </div> </a> </div><br /> Storyteller-&quot;A bouncer blocks your path. He says 'you want chicken, man, you go someplace else&quot;<br /> <br /> Dandrige Player-&quot;I say 'out of my way' forcefully to intimate him to move aside&quot;.<br /> <br /> Storyteller-&quot;roll Manipulation+Intimidation&quot;<br /> <br /> *Dandrige Player rolls a Bestial Failure*<br /> <br /> Storyteller-&quot;the bouncer is not intimidated. He says 'move me', and his unbearable insolence causes you to gain the Harm Compulsion&quot;<br /> <br /> Dandrige Player-&quot;I bare my fangs, activate my Eyes of the Beast and Protean Claws, and do a called shot to his jugular with my claws&quot;<br /> <br /> Storyteller-*mentally notes that activating both the eyes and claws should take two rounds, but lets it slide for Rule of Cool's sake* &quot;Roll Strength+Brawl&quot;<br /> <br /> *Dandrige Player rolls, scoring four 10's, and three 6's*<br /> <br /> Storyteller-&quot;you land a devastating critical hit to his jugular. The bouncer goes down, mortally wounded. Another bouncer rushes in to help him.&quot;<br /> <br /> Dandrige player-&quot;I blood surge my Strength, pick him up by the throat, and throw him across the room.&quot;<br /> <br /> Storyteller-&quot;roll Strength+Brawl&quot;<br /> <br /> *Dandrige player rolls, scoring a messy critical*<br /> <br /> Storyteller-&quot;you lift him by the throat, crushing his windpipe in the process, and hurl him across the room. Everyone on the dancefloor panics and rushes for the door. In the chaos, you lose track of Amy&quot;</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> *ST tears their hair out as another unnecessary random Masquerade violation utterly derails the plot yet again for the sixth time that session.*<br /> <br /> <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/biggrin.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Big Grin\" smilieid=\"3\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> I mean I don't know about your games but in every Cam game I've ever seen those PCs are getting Blood Hunted sometime in the next 12 hours for fucking up so utterly in public.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":26564,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26564-badfurryfanfic","user":"BadFurryFanFic","date":". 05-28-2021, 11:22 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26564-badfurryfanfic","name":"BadFurryFanFic","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2020"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"93"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-05-28T23:45:54-07:00","id":1450141,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Heavy Arms</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1443592-the-official-v5-vs-v20-thread?p=1450021#post1450021\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I actually like the idea of Rage dice to an extent because WtA has always struggled with the narrative that the Garou are always on edge and ready to flip out and murder things, but the mechanics for enforcing that are really uneven. Rage is supposed to be something that can ruin mundane life and drive Garou towards isolation from the rest of the world (even nature since normal animals are just as scared of Rage and just as at risk of getting slaughtered if a Garou frenzies).<br /> <br /> Even so, CtD's Nightmare dice are a far more appealing mechanical choice to me... here's hoping if &amp;quot;Splat Dice&amp;quot; are a thing some lessons from the games that already have them get worked into future variations.</div> </div> </div> </div>I agree with this. Rage Dice would be really appropriate for WTA, but Nightmare Dice get the balance right when it comes to CTD and could inspire other uses of X Dice. <br /> <br /> Like the whole C20 WP imbalance thing, adding dice to Unleashing, replacing dice with regular powers, etc, feels right. It makes things dangerous but a choice. And often, you are tempted to make that choice.<br /> <br /> That could be adapted for a better representation of the Beast in VTM to me as well, since it's all about temptation and the seductiveness of power. It's not randomly flipping out but making choices which are undermined by your own desire, and those can either work out (rewarding you for temptation but perhaps at the expense of your virtue) or fail spectacularly (giving you consequences that are entirely your own fault).<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MyWifeIsScary</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1443592-the-official-v5-vs-v20-thread?p=1450034#post1450034\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Messy crits don't work with vampires, because Vampires have this whole masquerade thing and can't afford to lose their shit all the time just because they didn't murder a guy before the big meet, and also Vampires in VTM function as metaphores for society's parasitic elite and it doesn't do well to have the parasitic elite be a bunch of barely-functioning mental wrecks who can't hold a socialite gathering without losing their shit. Messy crits might work for other vampire games, where they're secluded nutters sleeping in coffins and unliving in rural castles, and it'll work with werewolves because they're angry fringe members of society living on cult compounds, but it doesn't work at all for modern, urban predators who're expected to hold up a grand conspiracy.</div> </div> </div> </div>I wonder if a way to make Messy Crits less rare is to tie it to Self-Control (this requires V20 Virtues, though). E.g., if you crit (5+ successes) with Hunger Dice, and roll more 10s than your Self-Control, you get a Messy Critical. If you roll 5+ successes without loads of 10s, it's just a regular critical.<br /> <br /> I would probably let you 'upgrade' a crit to a Messy Crit or a botch to a Bestial Failure for +1 XP once per session, too, since that encourages you to roleplay that aspect of your character. <br /> <br /> I think one of the problems with Messy Crits/Bestial Failures is that they're quite random, so not only do they make you lose control as a character, they make you lose control as a player. Empowering the player to have their character lose control seems more enjoyable to me.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Writer, publisher, performer<br /> Mostly he/his, sometimes she/her IRL <a href=\"https://adam-lowe.com\" target=\"_blank\">https://adam-lowe.com</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5291-adambeyoncelowe","name":"adambeyoncelowe","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5291_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2802"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-05-29T03:57:59-07:00","id":1450155,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CTPhipps</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1443592-the-official-v5-vs-v20-thread?p=1449702#post1449702\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I think this is a silly action but I'm also 99.99% sure that it will have all the rules for making Sabbat PCs. They'll just be the same rules for making Sabbat NPCs.<br /> <br /> After all, there's no point making Paths of Enlightenment for NPCs.<br /> <br /> No one rolls for Path checks for NPCs.</div> </div> </div> </div>Umm, what?<br /> <br /> Every game i've played in, the NPCs rolled for path?<br /> <br /> I would be <u><b>pissed</b></u> if they didn't. Like, that's peak ST bullshit there.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Prone to being a Classic Curmudgeon, goshdarned whippersnappers...","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1037-jamiemalk","name":"jamiemalk","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1037_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"399"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-05-29T11:01:28-07:00","id":1450187,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>jamiemalk</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1443592-the-official-v5-vs-v20-thread?p=1450155#post1450155\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Umm, what?<br /> <br /> Every game i've played in, the NPCs rolled for path?<br /> <br /> I would be <u><b>pissed</b></u> if they didn't. Like, that's peak ST bullshit there.</div> </div> </div> </div>That's bizarre.<br /> <br /> I have never in history rolled for a Path or Humanity roll of an NPC.<br /> <br /> Because why would it matter?<br /> <br /> We're not following THEIR journey of self-discovery, enlightenment, and damnation.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Author of <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Cthulhu-Armageddon-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01KUOM7SI/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982844&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Cthulhu+Armageddon\" target=\"_blank\">Cthulhu Armageddon</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Teenage-Weredeer-Bright-Falls-Mysteries-ebook/dp/B075TTN2FN/ref=sr_1_2?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982717&amp;sr=1-2&amp;keywords=Weredeer#customerReviews\" target=\"_blank\">I was a Teenage Weredeer</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Straight-Outta-Fangton-Comedic-Vampire-ebook/dp/B01KNHICCC/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982774&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Straight+Outta+Fangton\" target=\"_blank\">Straight Outta Fangton</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Lucifers-Star-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01MDM9MCT/ref=mt_kindle?_encoding=UTF8&amp;me=&amp;qid=\" target=\"_blank\">Lucifer's Star</a>, </i>and the <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Rules-Supervillainy-Saga-Book-ebook/dp/B07MB89S33/\" target=\"_blank\">Supervillainy Saga</a>.</i><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","name":"CTPhipps","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12002_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13933"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-05-29T11:17:20-07:00","id":1450190,"title":"","content":"Yeah, as ST, I've never rolled a degeneration check for either humanity or path rating on NPCs.<br /> <br /> Then again, I roleplay the NPC as behaving strictly according to their humanity or Path rating, so I wouldn't have to even if that were a thing in my games.<br /> <br /> Humanity and Path-Rating are both blueprints when it comes to NPCs, who are there to fill certain roles: the compassionate mentor leading you towards golconda, the NPC who is ruthless but still has certain moral lines he won't cross to screw you over, the NPC with no moral lines whatsoever, the NPC Path Paragon who has strict moral lines, but those lines are alien and a minefield for players to interact with, etc, etc. Since the humanity or Path Rating is a blueprint for the ST to roleplay them rather than something they struggle with organically, there is no reason to have them violate that humanity level or path rating.<br /> <br /> If anything, having them violate that would be rather odd, like having the wooden chair suddenly be made of marshmallow.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3598-cajunkhan","name":"CajunKhan","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3598_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1700"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-05-29T11:21:48-07:00","id":1450192,"title":"","content":"I gotta go with <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar12002_2.jpeg');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"12002\" data-vbnamecard=\"12002\">CTPhipps</a> on this one. The idea that the ST should use player-facing mechanics like Humanity/Path rolls for NPCs is pretty strange. There's no inherent virtue in randomizing outcomes that have no bearing on the player characters.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1190-elphilm","name":"Elphilm","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1190_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"763"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-05-29T11:27:44-07:00","id":1450194,"title":"","content":"Yeah, I don't decide what an NPC does, then roll to check if it violates his Humanity/Path. I give an NPC a certain Humanity/Path and then use that as a blueprint for its behavior. In other words, Humanity/Path is the programming for a robot, rather than something karmic when it comes to NPCs.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3598-cajunkhan","name":"CajunKhan","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3598_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1700"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-05-29T11:48:14-07:00","id":1450197,"title":"","content":"I don't think you actually need to go to the extent of rolling for NPCs, but it is important they have the same guidelines and capabilities players do. If an NPC is using babies for firearm suppressors like how the postal dude uses cats, a player is going to want to know why that character isn't wassailing. If the players want to hurt an NPC by attacking his morals, then morality for that npc becomes important and the players should have a fair mechanic they can use to take that character down. Vampire before V5 excelled because you followed the same rules as others of your kind; If another vampire can do it, you can learn too, you just need to find the knowledge and experience. It's not DnD where you can expect to take out a magical plot device that only NPCs can use and have the players cool with it. Vampire is &quot;fair&quot; and it does so by holding the NPCs to the same standards as players, even if the storyteller isn't going to roll all the details.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25794-mywifeisscary","name":"MyWifeIsScary","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25794_2.png","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3711"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-05-29T12:16:16-07:00","id":1450201,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MyWifeIsScary</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1443592-the-official-v5-vs-v20-thread?p=1450197#post1450197\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I don't think you actually need to go to the extent of rolling for NPCs, but it is important they have the same guidelines and capabilities players do. If an NPC is using babies for firearm suppressors like how the postal dude uses cats, a player is going to want to know why that character isn't wassailing. If the players want to hurt an NPC by attacking his morals, then morality for that npc becomes important and the players should have a fair mechanic they can use to take that character down. Vampire before V5 excelled because you followed the same rules as others of your kind; If another vampire can do it, you can learn too, you just need to find the knowledge and experience. It's not DnD where you can expect to take out a magical plot device that only NPCs can use and have the players cool with it. Vampire is &quot;fair&quot; and it does so by holding the NPCs to the same standards as players, even if the storyteller isn't going to roll all the details.</div> </div> </div> </div>Except Humanity and Paths are more like Alignment than it is Initiative or THACO. It's a roleplaying tool.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Author of <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Cthulhu-Armageddon-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01KUOM7SI/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982844&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Cthulhu+Armageddon\" target=\"_blank\">Cthulhu Armageddon</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Teenage-Weredeer-Bright-Falls-Mysteries-ebook/dp/B075TTN2FN/ref=sr_1_2?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982717&amp;sr=1-2&amp;keywords=Weredeer#customerReviews\" target=\"_blank\">I was a Teenage Weredeer</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Straight-Outta-Fangton-Comedic-Vampire-ebook/dp/B01KNHICCC/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982774&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Straight+Outta+Fangton\" target=\"_blank\">Straight Outta Fangton</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Lucifers-Star-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01MDM9MCT/ref=mt_kindle?_encoding=UTF8&amp;me=&amp;qid=\" target=\"_blank\">Lucifer's Star</a>, </i>and the <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Rules-Supervillainy-Saga-Book-ebook/dp/B07MB89S33/\" target=\"_blank\">Supervillainy Saga</a>.</i><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","name":"CTPhipps","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12002_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13933"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-05-29T12:41:28-07:00","id":1450206,"title":"","content":"Humanity has (and has always had) mechanical effect. It's not just a role-playing tool. It's an in-universe thing to be manipulated. You can try to help a fellow vampire maintain Humanity, or purposefully try to drive theirs into the dirt. Whether or not the ST rolls out NPC Humanity/Path changes doesn't matter to the fact that the PCs should be able to influence NPCs in this fashion if they choose to. In any of the editions, if you undermine a Prince's Humanity, you can sabotage that Prince's hold on power by making them less capable of leading effectively. The players have every right to expect to be able to engage with that story rather than NPC Humanity just being a number for the ST's reference.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-05-29T12:52:14-07:00","id":1450209,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Heavy Arms</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1443592-the-official-v5-vs-v20-thread?p=1450206#post1450206\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Humanity has (and has always had) mechanical effect. It's not just a role-playing tool. It's an in-universe thing to be manipulated. You can try to help a fellow vampire maintain Humanity, or purposefully try to drive theirs into the dirt. Whether or not the ST rolls out NPC Humanity/Path changes doesn't matter to the fact that the PCs should be able to influence NPCs in this fashion if they choose to. In any of the editions, if you undermine a Prince's Humanity, you can sabotage that Prince's hold on power by making them less capable of leading effectively. The players have every right to expect to be able to engage with that story rather than NPC Humanity just being a number for the ST's reference.</div> </div> </div> </div>Agreed. But it still wouldn't be done the same as a player character. For example, in the game I'm running, I'm going to have the players gradually discover the Prince's Touchstones and snuff those swans. If they destroy the last swan, that Prince will briefly pull out all the stops to destroy the players, then he will become a wight. I'm not going to give him humanity rolls or an opportunity to acquire new touchstones. He's an NPC, a robot. Shortly after his last touchstone dies, he will go wight, because that's his role in the story. I'm treating his Bella Swans like they were Voldemort's Horcruxes. The players gradually destroy his Horcruxes and by doing so destroy him.<br /> <br /> That's very different from how I'd treat a player character, who would get rolls to resist going Wight, and go on a quest for new Touchstones and all that.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3598-cajunkhan","name":"CajunKhan","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3598_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1700"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-05-29T12:58:41-07:00","id":1450212,"title":"","content":"Yeah humanity literally dictates a lot of the symptoms of the Beast. High humanity means you don't have to spend blood for blush of life, Low humanity and you forget how to blush of life. High humanity gives you a bonus for getting sympathy, low humanity makes you sketchy. Your Virtues are capped by your humanity score; you can roll no more dice than your humanity when it comes to ordinary virtue rolls. Lastly, Humanity/path dictates your upper limit when you're awake during the day, and also makes it easier to wake up during danger. <br /> <br /> <br /> There are a few mechanical caveats to alignment in DnD, but not to that extent.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25794-mywifeisscary","name":"MyWifeIsScary","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25794_2.png","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3711"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-05-29T13:04:39-07:00","id":1450213,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CajunKhan</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1443592-the-official-v5-vs-v20-thread?p=1450209#post1450209\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Agreed. But it still wouldn't be done the same as a player character. For example, in the game I'm running, I'm going to have the players gradually discover the Prince's Touchstones and snuff those swans.</div> </div> </div> </div>I am curious what you assume is a typical Touchstone for a vampire in the game. Do the Sabbat assume they're humans that Camarilla vampires inexplicably care for or is it more someone they abuse and hate?<br /> <br /> Like one Touchstone the PCs have in my game is their abusive mortal mother who they keep ghouled and chained up in a nursing home to regularly taunt.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Author of <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Cthulhu-Armageddon-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01KUOM7SI/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982844&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Cthulhu+Armageddon\" target=\"_blank\">Cthulhu Armageddon</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Teenage-Weredeer-Bright-Falls-Mysteries-ebook/dp/B075TTN2FN/ref=sr_1_2?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982717&amp;sr=1-2&amp;keywords=Weredeer#customerReviews\" target=\"_blank\">I was a Teenage Weredeer</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Straight-Outta-Fangton-Comedic-Vampire-ebook/dp/B01KNHICCC/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982774&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Straight+Outta+Fangton\" target=\"_blank\">Straight Outta Fangton</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Lucifers-Star-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01MDM9MCT/ref=mt_kindle?_encoding=UTF8&amp;me=&amp;qid=\" target=\"_blank\">Lucifer's Star</a>, </i>and the <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Rules-Supervillainy-Saga-Book-ebook/dp/B07MB89S33/\" target=\"_blank\">Supervillainy Saga</a>.</i><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","name":"CTPhipps","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12002_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13933"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-05-29T13:16:28-07:00","id":1450218,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CTPhipps</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1443592-the-official-v5-vs-v20-thread?p=1450213#post1450213\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I am curious what you assume is a typical Touchstone for a vampire in the game. Do the Sabbat assume they're humans that Camarilla vampires inexplicably care for or is it more someone they abuse and hate?<br /> <br /> Like one Touchstone the PCs have in my game is their abusive mortal mother who they keep ghouled and chained up in a nursing home to regularly taunt.</div> </div> </div> </div>*sigh* Implicit in the way you phrase that is the assumption that those of us who like Paths just want to be eeeevilll and we should be fine with being forced onto Humanity and having human touchstones so long as we get to do it all in a way that is eeeeeevillllll. I don't want to be an eeeeevillllll human. I want to leave humanity behind completely and play something that doesn't care about humans at all, not even in an eeeeeeevilllllll way. I have no more desire to play something obsessed with tormenting a particular human than a do with playing something that moons over them and angsts over not being like them. And I know, even as I type this, that you won't understand that, and will go right back to talking about how you can make a baby-eater on Humanity with human touchstones. *sigh*","signature":"","edited":{"userid":3598,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3598-cajunkhan","user":"CajunKhan","date":". 05-29-2021, 07:10 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3598-cajunkhan","name":"CajunKhan","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3598_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1700"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-05-29T13:28:05-07:00","id":1450222,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CajunKhan</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1443592-the-official-v5-vs-v20-thread?p=1450218#post1450218\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> *sigh* Implicit in the way you phrase that is the assumption that those of us who like Paths just want to be eeeevilll and we should be fine with being forced onto Humanity and having human touchstones so long as we get to do it all in a way that is eeeeeevillllll. I don't want to be an eeeeevillllll human. I want to leave humanity behind completely and play something that doesn't care about humans at all, not even in an eeeeeeevilllllll way. I have no more desire to play something obsessed with tormenting a particular human than a do with playing something that moons over them and angsts over not being like them. And I know, even as I type this, that won't understand that, and will go right back to talking about how you can make a baby-eater on Humanity with human touchstones. *sigh*</div> </div> </div> </div>You've got a very weird take on me since I play nothing but weird mystics and cultists in my game. I do note that &quot;Bella Swan&quot; implies a very stereotypical Touchstone, though.<br /> <br /> You don't play exclusively Malkavians, Tzimisce, or Setites like me if you want to avoid the esoteric.<br /> <br /> I think the last time I played anything else was 2004.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Author of <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Cthulhu-Armageddon-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01KUOM7SI/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982844&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Cthulhu+Armageddon\" target=\"_blank\">Cthulhu Armageddon</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Teenage-Weredeer-Bright-Falls-Mysteries-ebook/dp/B075TTN2FN/ref=sr_1_2?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982717&amp;sr=1-2&amp;keywords=Weredeer#customerReviews\" target=\"_blank\">I was a Teenage Weredeer</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Straight-Outta-Fangton-Comedic-Vampire-ebook/dp/B01KNHICCC/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982774&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Straight+Outta+Fangton\" target=\"_blank\">Straight Outta Fangton</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Lucifers-Star-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01MDM9MCT/ref=mt_kindle?_encoding=UTF8&amp;me=&amp;qid=\" target=\"_blank\">Lucifer's Star</a>, </i>and the <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Rules-Supervillainy-Saga-Book-ebook/dp/B07MB89S33/\" target=\"_blank\">Supervillainy Saga</a>.</i><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","name":"CTPhipps","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12002_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13933"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-05-29T15:59:35-07:00","id":1450234,"title":"","content":"Leaving humanity behind, human touchstones and inhuman vampires...<br /> <br /> I don't care about rats. I could theoretically eat a rat for sustenance. I could keep one as a pet. I could theoretically kill 'em for fun on account of not liking them. I could kill them for safety reasons. I could use them in lab experiments.<br /> -<br /> But I am indifferent to rats, unless they're threatening me somehow. I know rats share the world with me. They are intelligent, they are social, I am surrounded by thousands at any given time, and I pay them no more mind than is necessary. I don't care, they're nothing to do with me outside of specific circumstances. We don't perceive the world the same way, we don't survive the same way, we are totally different species existing in the same space.<br /> <br /> Said totally other species that I view, at best, as a mild annoyance is hardly going to be a cornerstone of my sanity.<br /> -<br /> Replace the word &quot;rat&quot; with &quot;human&quot; and you get the reason why human touchstones won't work as a universal concept. A vampire divorced from their former species has no kinship with the human animal and views them accordingly. If you want to play a vampire as a member of another species, you do not necessarily want human touchstones.<br /> <br /> Said vampires are also highly unlikely to care about &quot;why&quot; an enemy vampire is keeping rats. Maybe they like them or find them endearing or interesting, maybe they hate them and torture them in a sociopathic fashion. Who cares, except for how you can use it against them.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><sup><i>Prone to hyperbole</i></sup>","edited":{"userid":26836,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26836-rhywbeth","user":"Rhywbeth","date":". 05-29-2021, 07:05 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26836-rhywbeth","name":"Rhywbeth","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar26836_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"377"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-05-29T16:12:34-07:00","id":1450235,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Rhywbeth</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1443592-the-official-v5-vs-v20-thread?p=1450234#post1450234\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Leaving humanity behind, human touchstones and inhuman vampires...<br /> <br /> I don't care about rats. I could theoretically eat a rat for sustenance. I could keep one as a pet. I could theoretically kill 'em for fun on account of not liking them. I could kill them for safety reasons. I could use them in lab experiments.<br /> -<br /> But I am indifferent to rats, unless they're threatening me somehow. I know rats share the world with me. They are intelligent, they are social, I am surrounded by thousands at any given time, and I pay them no more mind than is necessary. I don't care, they're nothing to do with me outside of specific circumstances. We don't perceive the world the same way, we don't survive the same way, we are totally different species existing in the same space.<br /> <br /> Said totally other species that I view, at best, as a mild annoyance is hardly going to be a cornerstone of my sanity.<br /> -<br /> Replace the word &quot;rat&quot; with &quot;human&quot; and you get the reason why human touchstones won't work as a universal concept. A vampire divorced from their former species has no kinship with the human animal and views them accordingly. If you want to play a vampire as a member of another species, you do not necessarily want human touchstones.<br /> <br /> Said vampires are also highly unlikely to care about &quot;why&quot; an enemy vampire is keeping rats. Maybe they like them or find them endearing or interesting, maybe they hate them and torture them in a sociopathic fashion. Who cares, except for how you can use it against them.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Ding! Exactly.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3598-cajunkhan","name":"CajunKhan","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3598_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1700"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-05-29T16:52:09-07:00","id":1450236,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Rhywbeth</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1443592-the-official-v5-vs-v20-thread?p=1450234#post1450234\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Replace the word &quot;rat&quot; with &quot;human&quot; and you get the reason why human touchstones won't work as a universal concept. A vampire divorced from their former species has no kinship with the human animal and views them accordingly. If you want to play a vampire as a member of another species, you do not necessarily want human touchstones</div> </div> </div> </div>Mind you, the question is whether the game should highlight that this is just the usual humans being racist and classicist or an actual point.<br /> <br /> After all, the rat comparison has a lot of RL history.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Author of <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Cthulhu-Armageddon-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01KUOM7SI/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982844&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Cthulhu+Armageddon\" target=\"_blank\">Cthulhu Armageddon</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Teenage-Weredeer-Bright-Falls-Mysteries-ebook/dp/B075TTN2FN/ref=sr_1_2?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982717&amp;sr=1-2&amp;keywords=Weredeer#customerReviews\" target=\"_blank\">I was a Teenage Weredeer</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Straight-Outta-Fangton-Comedic-Vampire-ebook/dp/B01KNHICCC/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982774&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Straight+Outta+Fangton\" target=\"_blank\">Straight Outta Fangton</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Lucifers-Star-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01MDM9MCT/ref=mt_kindle?_encoding=UTF8&amp;me=&amp;qid=\" target=\"_blank\">Lucifer's Star</a>, </i>and the <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Rules-Supervillainy-Saga-Book-ebook/dp/B07MB89S33/\" target=\"_blank\">Supervillainy Saga</a>.</i><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","name":"CTPhipps","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12002_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13933"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-05-29T17:03:22-07:00","id":1450237,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CTPhipps</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1443592-the-official-v5-vs-v20-thread?p=1450236#post1450236\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Mind you, the question is whether the game should highlight that this is just the usual humans being racist and classicist or an actual point.<br /> <br /> After all, the rat comparison has a lot of RL history.</div> </div> </div> </div>As a metaphor it fails me because the vampire is <i>not human</i>. People who view me as subhuman are human and think from a human perspective. Vampires on a path view me the way another animal would. The metaphor hits some rocks. The rat metaphor here isn't the same species creating an artificial divide, it's actually talking about two totally different species.<br /> <br /> -- this is a complicated topic that I shouldn't be getting into while half asleep, and it's 1:30 in the morning, so I'm cutting most of this and maybe get back to it later","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><sup><i>Prone to hyperbole</i></sup>","edited":{"userid":26836,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26836-rhywbeth","user":"Rhywbeth","date":". 05-29-2021, 08:57 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26836-rhywbeth","name":"Rhywbeth","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar26836_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"377"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-05-29T18:08:19-07:00","id":1450245,"title":"","content":"Eh, I think of vampires as human. They're just CURSED humans.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Author of <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Cthulhu-Armageddon-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01KUOM7SI/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982844&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Cthulhu+Armageddon\" target=\"_blank\">Cthulhu Armageddon</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Teenage-Weredeer-Bright-Falls-Mysteries-ebook/dp/B075TTN2FN/ref=sr_1_2?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982717&amp;sr=1-2&amp;keywords=Weredeer#customerReviews\" target=\"_blank\">I was a Teenage Weredeer</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Straight-Outta-Fangton-Comedic-Vampire-ebook/dp/B01KNHICCC/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982774&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Straight+Outta+Fangton\" target=\"_blank\">Straight Outta Fangton</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Lucifers-Star-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01MDM9MCT/ref=mt_kindle?_encoding=UTF8&amp;me=&amp;qid=\" target=\"_blank\">Lucifer's Star</a>, </i>and the <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Rules-Supervillainy-Saga-Book-ebook/dp/B07MB89S33/\" target=\"_blank\">Supervillainy Saga</a>.</i><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","name":"CTPhipps","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12002_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13933"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-05-29T18:24:26-07:00","id":1450247,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CTPhipps</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1443592-the-official-v5-vs-v20-thread?p=1450245#post1450245\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Eh, I think of vampires as human. They're just CURSED humans.</div> </div> </div> </div>They're neither fully inhuman nor still entirely human; most of the game's dramatic tension comes from the conflict between the human and the inhuman elements. After all, their cognition is largely the same as a human being, they grow up in human cultures, mostly retain human morphology, mostly retain human psychology, learn the same way as humans, process their environment in largely the same way, experience all the same emotional responses, internalize memories the same way, etc. Even if you assume the Vampire eventually erases the Man, that process would take a long damn time, and you probably never see the last 10% or so ever being completely erased. No one starts out a vampire.<br /> <br /> A good portion of their perceived inhumanity is the result of a brutally dehumanizing physical and social condition; a lot of it is trauma shock, desensitization, hardening, learned callousness, rather than the result of a genuinely inhuman nature - they're not aliens, after all. Part of the game's horror is how much humanity is &quot;lost&quot; not from the Beast or any other element of vampirism, but the human side itself - all the politicking, occultism, dark religions, the lust for power, sadistic cruelty, the desire for dominance and subjugation, all that stuff is completely in keeping with human behavior under conditions of extreme fear, deprivation, and so forth. The Beast just wants a full belly and a safe place; it's the human side that seeks to avenge a hundred-year-old grudge.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/543-professor-phobos","name":"Professor Phobos","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"237"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-05-29T18:31:39-07:00","id":1450249,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CTPhipps</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1443592-the-official-v5-vs-v20-thread?p=1450245#post1450245\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Eh, I think of vampires as human. They're just CURSED humans.</div> </div> </div> </div>I tend to view vampires as a sort of supernatural liquid zombie fungus. The &quot;spore&quot; gets in the host, spreads and takes over their brain (and thus the entire host). A vampire's true self is the vitae puppeteering the body, somewhat like the real world fungus does to ants. The human host has been magically bioengineered into something else. Though initially they still think like humans (and may continue to, if they stay on humanity)<br /> <br /> But yeah, if you view them as still human, the bigotry angle can come into play.<br /> <br /> To me, the usual vampire games will explore vampirism and monstrosity within the frame of humanity.<br /> Sabbat games are for exploring vampirism from outside the human box.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><sup><i>Prone to hyperbole</i></sup>","edited":{"userid":26836,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26836-rhywbeth","user":"Rhywbeth","date":". 05-29-2021, 09:51 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26836-rhywbeth","name":"Rhywbeth","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar26836_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"377"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-05-30T02:29:14-07:00","id":1450294,"title":"","content":"Vampires are humans given more power than they usually aught to have, and power reveals. If you want to see what a person's really like, give them the power to act like they want. The &quot;curse&quot; aspects aren't there to make the vampire directly miserable, but to push the vampire towards certain aspects of behaviour. Hell, A good enough understanding of human behaviour makes me conclude that the clan weaknesses were probably Deliberate Additions to the blood by the Clan Founders themselves, because shared weakness brings people together and helps them work alongside one another; without the weaknesses, every clan would see themselves as their chief competitors.<br /> <br /> In other words, the &quot;curse&quot; aspects of vampirism are brought about with someone with a keen understanding of human sociology. The weaknesses are designed to make vampires &quot;stronger&quot; as social units and as individuals. On a top down level, making the Nosferatu ugly as sin wins out on a cost-benefit analysis. Obviously I don't think that's the case for all curses; burned by sunlight just sucks and that's probably an outside power hating on vampires, <b>but in the case of the Beast and messy criticals, that's just being fucking stupid. The Person doesn't benefit from it, the Beast doesn't benefit from it, the Vampire as a whole doesn't benefit from it, and the antideluvian puppet master doesn't benefit from it. </b>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":25794,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25794-mywifeisscary","user":"MyWifeIsScary","date":". 05-30-2021, 05:33 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25794-mywifeisscary","name":"MyWifeIsScary","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25794_2.png","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3711"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-05-30T03:44:40-07:00","id":1450299,"title":"","content":"Ok. So your average vampire is not on a path of enlightenment. From humanity 10 - 1, the vampire thinks as a human, and in a way, is.<br /> You have the mind of a social pack animal whose survival is geared around cooperation with other humans suddenly finding themselves with the instincts of a solitary predator, preying on their former &quot;pack&quot;. Neglecting the human needs kills off the human and creates a wight, but neglecting the beast to cultivate your humanity may lead to mess when instinct takes over.<br /> <br /> Sunlight? Gone. (Can vampires get SAD?)<br /> Meaningful relationships? Gone. Kindred society is a paranoid clusterfuck and you can never be truly sure that your relationships are genuine. No human relationships can be safe, honest or lasting.<br /> And paranoia and isolation is so healthy, psychologically<br /> <br /> And the evil that vampires do to sate their hunger is always from the human. The beast simply wants food and safety. The human is the one that achieves it through stuff like human trafficking and murder. The beast doesn't care about your social games at Elysium, the human's doing all the backstabbing mind games. Do wights have governments and politics? Nope, vampire society being a poisonous clusterfuck is down to the human, again.<br /> <br /> Low humanity vampires become callous from cynicism, fear, depression, power, but they are still &quot;human&quot;. The monster in your regular vampire is human.<br /> <br /> But for me, moving on to a path of enlightenment is a controlled destruction of the human psyche - killing off the human thought process without wassailing.<br /> A wight is pure vampire, a vampire on a path hit wight threshold and survived with their higher thought processes intact.<br /> This vampire is not human in instinct, in biology, in needs or in thought. Even if it may seem so at a cursory glance, their behaviour isn't human, observers are simply projecting their humanity onto them. There is nothing human left here, the person it grew out of is officially dead.<br /> (And there's a reason they aren't as common as vampires on humanity)","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><sup><i>Prone to hyperbole</i></sup>","edited":{"userid":26836,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26836-rhywbeth","user":"Rhywbeth","date":". 05-30-2021, 11:50 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26836-rhywbeth","name":"Rhywbeth","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar26836_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"377"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-05-30T14:00:43-07:00","id":1450351,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MyWifeIsScary</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1443592-the-official-v5-vs-v20-thread?p=1449944#post1449944\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Six reprintings means something wasn't good enough five times.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> That's really interesting: so you get to be a best seller by accumulating piles of errata :-D Come on!<br /> <br /> Jokes aside, one of the reason I'm supportive of this edition it's also because it has brought Vampire back in stores. Six reprintings for the english version means quite a number of copies: and to those, you should add the third-party localizations in other languages.<br /> <br /> I can give you a very clear example with the italian market: Italy is a fairly good european market for RPGs.<br /> <br /> Of all V20 wonderful manuals *, we only got the corebook and the companion, and we will get later this year Lore of the Clans. Next year, perhaps, Lore of the Bloodlines. Since 2012.<br /> <br /> When it comes to V5, instead, in the last 2 years a new third-party partner has already translated Corebook, Anarchs, Camarilla, Monsters, Fall of London, Chicago and the Storyteller Screen, has Cult of the Blood Gods translated and waiting for confirmation, and has already announced a translation of Sabbat: the only V5 manuals that so far we are not getting are Let the Streets Run Red and the Chicago Folio, and this is probably due to licensing issues.<br /> <br /> If V5 was the complete commercial failure many think, I highly doubt we'd see this kind of enormous divergence in editorial lines: also, consider that the new third-party partner has a much wider retail network, as I think it has a distribution deal with Asmodee, I can buy V5 manuals also in boardgame stores and even some LEGO / toys shops around the country.<br /> <br /> I'm very sad that V5 has proved this divisive: when it came out, I thought it could have bridged the divide between Requiem and Masquerade fans. I'm very concerned this edition may fail, because I really like what has been done with rules and setting.<br /> <br /> But nonetheless, trying to be as objective as possible, V5 distribution numbers can't possibly be worse than V20: they are, probably, far better. Consider that in many world markets, we got access to V20 and CofD products mostly through Drivethrurpg (an option that, after Brexit, has become much less convenient), whereas I can phisically walk into a huge bookshop or comic shop and buy V5.<br /> <br /> And, speaking of Drivethru, you can't possibly compare the selling position of V20 and V5 PDFs: V20 is selling since late 2011, I think, V5 since late 2018. It's a 7-years gap!<br /> <br /> <br /> <i>* they really are wonderful, it's not meant to be sarcastic</i>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":12590,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12590-manfr","user":"Manfr","date":". 05-30-2021, 05:12 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12590-manfr","name":"Manfr","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"449"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-05-30T14:50:15-07:00","id":1450358,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Manfr</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1443592-the-official-v5-vs-v20-thread?p=1450351#post1450351\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Jokes aside, one of the reason I'm supportive of this edition it's also because it has brought Vampire back in stores. Six reprintings for the english version means quite a number of copies: and to those, you should add the third-party localizations in other languages.</div> </div> </div> </div>The thing is... this really isn't about something fundamental to the editions. This is the result of business decisions by CCP and Paradox.<br /> <br /> If Paradox wanted, it could have put the 20th books in stores, and could have gotten their partners do to official translations into lots of languages for distribution into more places. Paradox is choosing to let V20 stay obscure and hard to get.<br /> <br /> Of course, Paradox wants to promote V5, so it makes sense for them to put more money there since they've already committed to that financially. But saying that VtM is back in stores because of V5 is a bit off base because V20 was never given the resources to try to be back in stores (esp. internationally), it was left in Onyx Path's hands who, despite being started by industry pros, was a brand new company with very little resources and minimal support from CCP at the time.<br /> <br /> The point here is that it's not about content, but about companies on this matter.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> If V5 was the complete commercial failure many think... </div> </div> </div>Nobody really thinks that.<br /> <br /> What people doubt is that V5 is actually much of a successes. Instead there's an impression of more of a loss-leader designed to break even financially while building up the brand.<br /> <br /> When you look at, say, the PS5, it doesn't look like some sort of financial flop. But Sony would lose money if they only made money selling the console itself. They make the vast majority of their money off their cut of video game sales; the console is just to create a captive audience for those games.<br /> <br /> To a lot of us, we see a set of corporate decision making that matches this consideration. The money isn't in the RPG, the movie is in licensing it as much as possible, and to much bigger markets like video games and movies. So the RPG is there to get people talking more than it is about getting people playing the RPG.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> And, speaking of Drivethru, you can't possibly compare the selling position of V20 and V5 PDFs: V20 is selling since late 2011, I think, V5 since late 2018. It's a 7-years gap! </div> </div> </div>DTRPG has metrics that are more fair. The ones general referenced are average sales over time, not total sales. V20 out competing V5 here isn't about total sales, but about V20 averaging more sales a month now than V5 is.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-05-30T15:13:11-07:00","id":1450362,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Heavy Arms</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1443592-the-official-v5-vs-v20-thread?p=1450358#post1450358\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> The thing is... this really isn't about something fundamental to the editions. This is the result of business decisions by CCP and Paradox.<br /> <br /> If Paradox wanted, it could have put the 20th books in stores, and could have gotten their partners do to official translations into lots of languages for distribution into more places. Paradox is choosing to let V20 stay obscure and hard to get.<br /> <br /> Of course, Paradox wants to promote V5, so it makes sense for them to put more money there since they've already committed to that financially. But saying that VtM is back in stores because of V5 is a bit off base because V20 was never given the resources to try to be back in stores (esp. internationally), it was left in Onyx Path's hands who, despite being started by industry pros, was a brand new company with very little resources and minimal support from CCP at the time.<br /> <br /> The point here is that it's not about content, but about companies on this matter.</div> </div> </div> </div>Well, Paradox has arrived in late 2015: that's 4 years of V20 not competing with V5 in someone's marketing strategies, and still V5 has arrived just 3 years later. Also, opening up the Storytellers Vault was hardly a move signaling &quot;boycott V20&quot;.<br /> <br /> It must be noted that V20 was put into stores and translated: problem is, this mostly was confined to corebooks, as CCP wasn't really interested in tabletop RPGs, Onyx Path couldn't possibly lift the brand alone and evidently neither were national distributors.<br /> <br /> And also ... well, 20th editions are not really good starting products, in the age of light game design, I fear. I gladly bought them for nostalgia and for omnibus rules, but I would never try to learn the whole game with a 500-pages thick book (or even a 800-pages one like Mage, I didn't even dare try to study it!).<br /> <br /> A book format (and a lore amount) such as the one of V5 are more manageable: admittedly, this could have been done with a sort of &quot;V20 primer&quot;, but it's evident that, in the context of launching a transversal and easily accessible brand the V20 line was just too ... huge and dense with informations and connections to prior material, to be used as the main product.<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Heavy Arms</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1443592-the-official-v5-vs-v20-thread?p=1450358#post1450358\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> Nobody really thinks that.<br /> <br /> What people doubt is that V5 is actually much of a successes. Instead there's an impression of more of a loss-leader designed to break even financially while building up the brand.<br /> <br /> When you look at, say, the PS5, it doesn't look like some sort of financial flop. But Sony would lose money if they only made money selling the console itself. They make the vast majority of their money off their cut of video game sales; the console is just to create a captive audience for those games.<br /> <br /> To a lot of us, we see a set of corporate decision making that matches this consideration. The money isn't in the RPG, the movie is in licensing it as much as possible, and to much bigger markets like video games and movies. So the RPG is there to get people talking more than it is about getting people playing the RPG.</div> </div> </div> </div>Actually, some pages ago it's full of people saying V5 is going down in flames and arguing that is impossible it has positive results!<br /> <br /> Anyways, what you are describing, is the trans-media strategy that Paradox had outlined when they bought the IP: it's a sound idea, and one which was also widely derided on these pages not long ago (lots of snickering in thread about the failure to get videogames, shows and comics).<br /> <br /> I think that the brand will benefit from reaching pop-culture status: considering it has attracted THE EXPANSE and THE WITCHER people, I'm slightly confident they will pull it off. There's also a huge number of collaterals, especially boardgames, coming out, based on VtM, and this too is good.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":12590,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12590-manfr","user":"Manfr","date":". 05-30-2021, 06:37 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12590-manfr","name":"Manfr","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"449"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-05-30T15:31:41-07:00","id":1450366,"title":"","content":"Essentially, I think that is basically my take on the subject. This is a craps table spread that is not limiting itself to tabletop games.<br /> <br /> We have:<br /> <br /> * Boardgames<br /> * Card games<br /> * Video games (3 Visual Novels, 1 Text based game, 1 video game)<br /> * The Tabletop game<br /> * Multiple free Youtube and Twitch Live Games<br /> * One very successful indie comic book<br /> * The audiobook/novel plus the reprints<br /> * The upcoming television show<br /> <br /> The goal is not to promote <i>Vampire: The Masquerade</i> the tabletop game alone but V:TM the intellectual property as a whole. Because the tabletop game is a niche property now when V5 provides a unified vision and system to operate from. This is actually not that uncommon. One of the funny things about TSR/WOTC was the fact that during the height of Dungeons and Dragons, when it was a national hobby, the Dragonlance books actually made something like 30 times the amount of money that the tabletop games did. That was just Dragonlance too.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Author of <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Cthulhu-Armageddon-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01KUOM7SI/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982844&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Cthulhu+Armageddon\" target=\"_blank\">Cthulhu Armageddon</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Teenage-Weredeer-Bright-Falls-Mysteries-ebook/dp/B075TTN2FN/ref=sr_1_2?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982717&amp;sr=1-2&amp;keywords=Weredeer#customerReviews\" target=\"_blank\">I was a Teenage Weredeer</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Straight-Outta-Fangton-Comedic-Vampire-ebook/dp/B01KNHICCC/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982774&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Straight+Outta+Fangton\" target=\"_blank\">Straight Outta Fangton</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Lucifers-Star-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01MDM9MCT/ref=mt_kindle?_encoding=UTF8&amp;me=&amp;qid=\" target=\"_blank\">Lucifer's Star</a>, </i>and the <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Rules-Supervillainy-Saga-Book-ebook/dp/B07MB89S33/\" target=\"_blank\">Supervillainy Saga</a>.</i><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","name":"CTPhipps","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12002_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13933"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-05-30T21:19:03-07:00","id":1450391,"title":"","content":"The problem is that... none of that really makes sense for justifying a lot of the changes V5 implemented. The pre-V5 WoD has had all of that and more.<br /> <br /> V5 could have been much closer to V20, or even just V20 trimmed back down to VRev in terms of core book stuff and other stuff put into supplements. And it still could have had all the other media stuff. V5 didn't unlock some magical lock that was keeping VtM from such success because VtM already had that success in the past.<br /> <br /> It's not a V20 vs V5 issue, it's a &quot;having a company with resources that wants to invest in the brand,&quot; issue.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-05-30T21:26:11-07:00","id":1450392,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Heavy Arms</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1443592-the-official-v5-vs-v20-thread?p=1450391#post1450391\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The problem is that... none of that really makes sense for justifying a lot of the changes V5 implemented. The pre-V5 WoD has had all of that and more.<br /> <br /> V5 could have been much closer to V20, or even just V20 trimmed back down to VRev in terms of core book stuff and other stuff put into supplements. And it still could have had all the other media stuff. V5 didn't unlock some magical lock that was keeping VtM from such success because VtM already had that success in the past.<br /> <br /> It's not a V20 vs V5 issue, it's a &quot;having a company with resources that wants to invest in the brand,&quot; issue.</div> </div> </div> </div>Yes, and for those of us who prefer the changes, keeping it like V20 is a losing proposition. Why would I pay money for an Edition similar to the one I just bought? An Edition needs heavy updates to justify its purchase.<br /> <br /> But I prefer V5 to V20 as I've stated, some issues aside. I'd rather have something very different than the same even if I don't agree with all the changes.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Author of <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Cthulhu-Armageddon-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01KUOM7SI/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982844&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Cthulhu+Armageddon\" target=\"_blank\">Cthulhu Armageddon</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Teenage-Weredeer-Bright-Falls-Mysteries-ebook/dp/B075TTN2FN/ref=sr_1_2?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982717&amp;sr=1-2&amp;keywords=Weredeer#customerReviews\" target=\"_blank\">I was a Teenage Weredeer</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Straight-Outta-Fangton-Comedic-Vampire-ebook/dp/B01KNHICCC/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982774&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Straight+Outta+Fangton\" target=\"_blank\">Straight Outta Fangton</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Lucifers-Star-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01MDM9MCT/ref=mt_kindle?_encoding=UTF8&amp;me=&amp;qid=\" target=\"_blank\">Lucifer's Star</a>, </i>and the <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Rules-Supervillainy-Saga-Book-ebook/dp/B07MB89S33/\" target=\"_blank\">Supervillainy Saga</a>.</i><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","name":"CTPhipps","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12002_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13933"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-05-30T23:12:04-07:00","id":1450400,"title":"","content":"There are plenty of -probably everybody would have liked this- changes you could've added to V20's ruleset to keep it interesting while not alienating players: <br /> <br /> Mechanically<br /> -Combat gets cleaned up<br /> -Presence gets better documentation. <br /> -Attributes and Abilities get flat XP rates to stop you from powergaming so much<br /> <br /> Fluff<br /> -The Giovanni are in the midst of a coup, and there's a whole adventure book for this. At least half the necromancers will disperse through the mainstream sects, mostly under the purview of the nosferatu. <br /> -The Tremere are making moves to consolidate the future of technomagic, and are also trying to keep the Assamites out of cities. <br /> -The Sabbat can half-collapse due to internal warfare if you want to make them smaller again. <br /> -A baali is found in the inner circle, leading to a grand witchhunt, or something easy to toss out just like that. <br /> -You could do a suplement on vampires during a time of plague. (covid) with a lot of nightclub-dependent vampires not really being able to cope.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25794-mywifeisscary","name":"MyWifeIsScary","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25794_2.png","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3711"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-05-31T01:13:35-07:00","id":1450413,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MyWifeIsScary</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1443592-the-official-v5-vs-v20-thread?p=1450400#post1450400\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">There are plenty of -probably everybody would have liked this- changes you could've added to V20's ruleset to keep it interesting while not alienating players: <br /> <br /> Mechanically<br /> -Combat gets cleaned up<br /> -Presence gets better documentation. <br /> -Attributes and Abilities get flat XP rates to stop you from powergaming so much<br /> <br /> Fluff<br /> -The Giovanni are in the midst of a coup, and there's a whole adventure book for this. At least half the necromancers will disperse through the mainstream sects, mostly under the purview of the nosferatu. <br /> -The Tremere are making moves to consolidate the future of technomagic, and are also trying to keep the Assamites out of cities. <br /> -The Sabbat can half-collapse due to internal warfare if you want to make them smaller again. <br /> -A baali is found in the inner circle, leading to a grand witchhunt, or something easy to toss out just like that. <br /> -You could do a suplement on vampires during a time of plague. (covid) with a lot of nightclub-dependent vampires not really being able to cope.</div> </div> </div> </div>These are some interesting ideas. I admit it's a bit of a missed opportunity to make so many of the setting changes things that happened in the past rather than things you could play through now. <br /> <br /> I loved sourcebooks like The Time of Thin Blood and Nights of Prophecy at the time. You could make a lot of money playing through Transylvania Chronicles: The Fall of Vienna, The Hunters Hunted: Rise of the Second Inquisition, Diablerie: The Gehenna War, etc. <br /> <br /> (They don't need to be part of any earlier series, but I added those as indications for how the new metaplot could feed into and build upon the old, enticing long-standing fans and bringing in new ones, while also selling your backlist.)<br /> <br /> If you want to make the Anarchs more central again, you can still have the Camarilla retreating; you can just have the Anarchs sweep into the vaccum created when the Ivory Tower shrank.<br /> <br /> You can still have the Sabbat civil war and the Gehenna War, but you can make those ongoing things that players can either join in (for more epic, end-of-the-world gaming) or resist (opening up Sabbat cities for the taking by Neonates and Ancillae).","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Writer, publisher, performer<br /> Mostly he/his, sometimes she/her IRL <a href=\"https://adam-lowe.com\" target=\"_blank\">https://adam-lowe.com</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5291-adambeyoncelowe","name":"adambeyoncelowe","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5291_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2802"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-05-31T02:25:32-07:00","id":1450417,"title":"","content":"So that has me brainstorm this idea.<br /> <br /> The Camarilla find a Baali in the Inner circle. They begin a sect wide witchhunt, a good few too many princes, and the Tremere, use this as an excuse to purge rivals. Naturally, a lot of vampires are unhappy with this, and go anarch. The crux is, Infernalists in the Anarchs are fanning the flames against a lot of princes that were really doing a half decent job at purging infernalists. Infernalism's been on the rise for the past hundred years, given the ever-changing environment of modernity creating an increasing pressure on the young, who've turning to devils in increasing numbers in order to survive this tumultuous 'time of thin blood'.<br /> The Followers of Set gain a little power as a group that hate infernalists, being half-trusted as a nuetral arbitrator, only of course they're a bunch of snakes so, while they're definetly killing infernalists, they're making a lot of problems worse than they really aught to be.<br /> <br /> That'd<br /> -Make the Cam smaller, and Anarchs bigger.<br /> -Really emphasize the differences between Anarchs and Camarilla; Abuse of power VS Abuse of freedom.<br /> -would come off as a natural extention of things, thus upsetting nobody because it sounds like something that would happen rather than some writer arbitration.<br /> <br /> <br /> The largest problem with the V5 metaplot is that it seems to be turning heads for the sake of turning heads, with the Tremere imploding because -Book of the Grave Contrivance- and someone casually bombing their hidden, magical, super-fortress-prime. Or the Sabbat all packing up to leave so that the A/C conflict can take up all the space. Or the inquisition being a real big threat because Dominate got nerfed to shit and secret rogue agents can somehow trust secret rogue agents from other agencies along with domestic terrorists to make absolutely sure that they can't ever have a peaceful life or get a lucrative job in the private sector after they leave the service.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25794-mywifeisscary","name":"MyWifeIsScary","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25794_2.png","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3711"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-05-31T02:30:36-07:00","id":1450419,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MyWifeIsScary</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1443592-the-official-v5-vs-v20-thread?p=1450417#post1450417\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">So that has me brainstorm this idea.<br /> <br /> The Camarilla find a Baali in the Inner circle. They begin a sect wide witchhunt, a good few too many princes, and the Tremere, use this as an excuse to purge rivals. Naturally, a lot of vampires are unhappy with this, and go anarch. The crux is, Infernalists in the Anarchs are fanning the flames against a lot of princes that were really doing a half decent job at purging infernalists. Infernalism's been on the rise for the past hundred years, given the ever-changing environment of modernity creating an increasing pressure on the young, who've turning to devils in increasing numbers in order to survive this tumultuous 'time of thin blood'.<br /> The Followers of Set gain a little power as a group that hate infernalists, being half-trusted as a nuetral arbitrator, only of course they're a bunch of snakes so, while they're definetly killing infernalists, they're making a lot of problems worse than they really aught to be.<br /> <br /> That'd<br /> -Make the Cam smaller, and Anarchs bigger.<br /> -Really emphasize the differences between Anarchs and Camarilla; Abuse of power VS Abuse of freedom.<br /> -would come off as a natural extention of things, thus upsetting nobody because it sounds like something that would happen rather than some writer arbitration.<br /> <br /> <br /> The largest problem with the V5 metaplot is that it seems to be turning heads for the sake of turning heads, with the Tremere imploding because -Book of the Grave Contrivance- and someone casually bombing their hidden, magical, super-fortress-prime. Or the Sabbat all packing up to leave so that the A/C conflict can take up all the space. Or the inquisition being a real big threat because Dominate got nerfed to shit and secret rogue agents can somehow trust secret rogue agents from other agencies along with domestic terrorists to make absolutely sure that they can't ever have a peaceful life or get a lucrative job in the private sector after they leave the service.</div> </div> </div> </div>So if you wrote this as an alt-metaplot book, I'd buy it.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Writer, publisher, performer<br /> Mostly he/his, sometimes she/her IRL <a href=\"https://adam-lowe.com\" target=\"_blank\">https://adam-lowe.com</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5291-adambeyoncelowe","name":"adambeyoncelowe","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5291_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2802"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-05-31T02:46:21-07:00","id":1450421,"title":"","content":"I admit, Ido like the Second Inquisition. The idea that vampires are having a harder time keeping up the Masquerade as technology improves is something that's been in the background for years. Obviously there are specific incidents involving the Second Inq that are pretty... questionable, but in broad strokes, having a vampires finding themselves on the defensive because of an increase in vampire hunters is a general plot development I was down with.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/741-anubisxy","name":"AnubisXy","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar741_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5693"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-05-31T02:46:36-07:00","id":1450422,"title":"","content":"I think part of the issue I have is a lot of the suggestions are all things that make sense only to people who have played vampire religiously.<br /> <br /> What's a Baali?<br /> <br /> What's an Inner Circle?<br /> <br /> Tell me, in simple terms, what is a good metaplot for people who have never played a vampire before.<br /> <br /> &quot;The government coming to kill us all&quot; might have been what the writers came up with. Especially with the War on Terror before something everyone experienced.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Author of <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Cthulhu-Armageddon-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01KUOM7SI/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982844&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Cthulhu+Armageddon\" target=\"_blank\">Cthulhu Armageddon</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Teenage-Weredeer-Bright-Falls-Mysteries-ebook/dp/B075TTN2FN/ref=sr_1_2?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982717&amp;sr=1-2&amp;keywords=Weredeer#customerReviews\" target=\"_blank\">I was a Teenage Weredeer</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Straight-Outta-Fangton-Comedic-Vampire-ebook/dp/B01KNHICCC/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982774&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Straight+Outta+Fangton\" target=\"_blank\">Straight Outta Fangton</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Lucifers-Star-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01MDM9MCT/ref=mt_kindle?_encoding=UTF8&amp;me=&amp;qid=\" target=\"_blank\">Lucifer's Star</a>, </i>and the <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Rules-Supervillainy-Saga-Book-ebook/dp/B07MB89S33/\" target=\"_blank\">Supervillainy Saga</a>.</i><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","name":"CTPhipps","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12002_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13933"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-05-31T03:00:19-07:00","id":1450424,"title":"","content":"1 A demon worshiper, a high-end one at that. <br /> 2 &quot;inner circle&quot; is a pretty self explanatory title. &quot;the federal body of the Camarilla&quot; might be an apt description. <br /> <br /> You'd take like, two lines to explain these things. <br /> <br /> V5 is far heavier on this; Gehenna Crusade? Second Inquisition? Giovanni treaties? Banu Haquim? Infact to add extra confusion they went full obtuse with the backgrounds; Mawla? Chasse?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25794-mywifeisscary","name":"MyWifeIsScary","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25794_2.png","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3711"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-05-31T03:06:14-07:00","id":1450427,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CTPhipps</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1443592-the-official-v5-vs-v20-thread?p=1450392#post1450392\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Yes, and for those of us who prefer the changes, keeping it like V20 is a losing proposition.</div> </div> </div> </div>So... back to goal post shifting?<br /> <br /> Seriously, you don't want to get accused of this but you constantly do this sort of thing. How does your preference for game matter, at all, to the idea that &quot;V5 is getting all this stuff besides a TT RPG,&quot; isn't something inherent to V5, but rather something chosen by Paradox to do. Either you're trying to derail the conversation (which I'd like to think you're not trying to do), shifting the goal posts because there isn't a good counter-point to the idea that V5's current transmedia success is all Paradox's choosing to fund that rather than something specific about the nature of V20 vs. V5, or.... some 3rd option I can't for the life of my figure out especially because if it existed I really hope you'd figure out how to come at it better so I stop pointing at your posts and saying, &quot;hey man, goal post shift, not cool.&quot;<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Why would I pay money for an Edition similar to the one I just bought? An Edition needs heavy updates to justify its purchase. </div> </div> </div>That's you. Lots of people buy new editions with a much lower bar for what needs changing than you seem to have. Look at how many people bought V20... and it barely changes anything. 1e to 2e, and 2e to Rev weren't some major overhauls either. <br /> <br /> And this isn't some WoD or WW specific thing, this is true of most RPGs that get a significant number of editions with the same company identity (which is, to be clear, a rarity in the broad view of things). Most new editions are incremental upgrades, not massive changes, unless there's some overriding factor like the new IP holders no longer having the rights to the old system (like Scion 2e).<br /> <br /> New people to existing games also tend to just by the newest edition unless they're warned away in some fashion. To new potential fans, big shake ups between editions are meaningless because they weren't invested in the previous material to care about changes. For them, a Clan changing allegiance isn't some huge new play experience, it's just setting history. For them it's the past, even if for older players it's a major change up, because they never played the other way.<br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-05-31T03:13:09-07:00","id":1450428,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CTPhipps</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1443592-the-official-v5-vs-v20-thread?p=1450422#post1450422\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">&quot;The government coming to kill us all&quot; might have been what the writers came up with. Especially with the War on Terror before something everyone experienced.</div> </div> </div> </div>The War on Terror is almost 20 years old. The US literally has people serving in the War on Terror that weren't born before it started. There is a whole generation of people that only know the War of Terror as &quot;lots of people going off to fight never ending war that just seems to cost lots of lives and money without accomplishing anything because terrorists still exist and do bad stuff,&quot; rather than having lived through the trauma of 9/11 and the geopolitical fallout. This is a generation where the post-Patriot Act surveillance state is the only world they know.<br /> <br /> There are very different experiences here, and &quot;the government coming to kill us all,&quot; doesn't speak to them universally.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-05-31T03:21:59-07:00","id":1450431,"title":"","content":"&quot;govement coming to kill us&quot; doesn't work when they only do that to the poor, and the wealth range for vampires is generally between well-to-do and excessive. If real world goverments start going after their oligarchs, then give us a call. But they don't. So &quot;goverment coming to kill us&quot; is just fucking stupid, especially if you're not an American and thus haven't been blasted with &quot;big gov bad, no gov good&quot; propaganda your whole life. V5 feels even more gratuitously american than the first editions. There's nothing about it that speaks any universal truth.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25794-mywifeisscary","name":"MyWifeIsScary","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25794_2.png","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3711"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-05-31T03:38:12-07:00","id":1450434,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Heavy Arms</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1443592-the-official-v5-vs-v20-thread?p=1450428#post1450428\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> The War on Terror is almost 20 years old. The US literally has people serving in the War on Terror that weren't born before it started. There is a whole generation of people that only know the War of Terror as &quot;lots of people going off to fight never ending war that just seems to cost lots of lives and money without accomplishing anything because terrorists still exist and do bad stuff,&quot; rather than having lived through the trauma of 9/11 and the geopolitical fallout. This is a generation where the post-Patriot Act surveillance state is the only world they know.<br /> <br /> There are very different experiences here, and &quot;the government coming to kill us all,&quot; doesn't speak to them universally.</div> </div> </div> </div>I think you mistake my point. My point being not that it is relevant but something everyone knows.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MyWifeIsScary</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1443592-the-official-v5-vs-v20-thread?p=1450431#post1450431\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">&quot;govement coming to kill us&quot; doesn't work when they only do that to the poor, and the wealth range for vampires is generally between well-to-do and excessive. If real world goverments start going after their oligarchs, then give us a call. But they don't. So &quot;goverment coming to kill us&quot; is just fucking stupid, especially if you're not an American and thus haven't been blasted with &quot;big gov bad, no gov good&quot; propaganda your whole life. V5 feels even more gratuitously american than the first editions. There's nothing about it that speaks any universal truth.</div> </div> </div> </div>Yes, because the Tremere Council is clearly the poor that fall to the Inquisition. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> Mind you, the Camarilla WANTED the Second Inquisition to only wipe out their enemies but they lost control very quickly.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Author of <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Cthulhu-Armageddon-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01KUOM7SI/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982844&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Cthulhu+Armageddon\" target=\"_blank\">Cthulhu Armageddon</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Teenage-Weredeer-Bright-Falls-Mysteries-ebook/dp/B075TTN2FN/ref=sr_1_2?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982717&amp;sr=1-2&amp;keywords=Weredeer#customerReviews\" target=\"_blank\">I was a Teenage Weredeer</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Straight-Outta-Fangton-Comedic-Vampire-ebook/dp/B01KNHICCC/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982774&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Straight+Outta+Fangton\" target=\"_blank\">Straight Outta Fangton</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Lucifers-Star-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01MDM9MCT/ref=mt_kindle?_encoding=UTF8&amp;me=&amp;qid=\" target=\"_blank\">Lucifer's Star</a>, </i>and the <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Rules-Supervillainy-Saga-Book-ebook/dp/B07MB89S33/\" target=\"_blank\">Supervillainy Saga</a>.</i><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","name":"CTPhipps","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12002_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13933"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-05-31T05:14:32-07:00","id":1450437,"title":"","content":"/Woosh<br /> <br /> The Tremere council bombing <i>doesn't </i>work because they're not the poor. Where's the real world parallel? It'd be like if the US goverment nationalized Amazon and Google as punishment for Tax evasion. It's not happening, so why are the Tremere being targeted?<br /> <br /> Good Satire works on some kind of truth.<br /> Vampires work as metaphors for a parasitic elite who benefit from the lifeblood of others. If someone wrote that the Sackler Family (largely responsible for the opiod crisis) were vampires, while a lot of us have reservations about using real people, we'd otherwise be on board with that<br /> The second inquisition functions as a metaphor for... absolutely nothing that is happening in reality. Where's the crackdown? Where's the comeuppance in reality? Where are the police on the side of the little guy?<br /> It's not there. Society remains plagued by untouchables. So the SI comes across as wrong, as a delusion. It runs contrary to the current zeitgeist. It doesn't work at all within the framework of satire. The Tremere being blown up is fucking nonsensical, says doyle and watson. It doesn't fucking work, at least for everyone, because it's not based on a truth, it's based on a lie. It's hard for some people to buy in on an obvious lie, but most people will be happy with truth.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25794-mywifeisscary","name":"MyWifeIsScary","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25794_2.png","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3711"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-05-31T05:20:09-07:00","id":1450438,"title":"","content":"Changes like the ones proposed by <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25794-mywifeisscary\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar25794_2.png');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"25794\" data-vbnamecard=\"25794\">MyWifeIsScary</a> could surely have been a good basis for a less controversial update: the resurgence of the Baali as a threat had also been widely prepared by Onyx Path with V20. I still consider all the rules changes introduced by V5 as positive, but that's a matter of tastes.<br /> <br /> I feel a huge problem is that, while it is sensible that metaplot changes were presented in the Corebook, players would have tremendously benefited of the possibility of playing directly into those events: the controversial introductory adventure set in Berlin did a wonderful job, it's a pity it was buried under shitstorms over the pregen characters.<br /> <br /> A series of &quot;Fall of ...&quot; adventures (Fall of Berlin presenting the rise of the Anarchs; Fall of Wien detailing the crumbling of the Pyramid; Fall of Mexico City or Montreal detailing the Sabbat Civil War, Fall of Venice with the birth of Hecata) would be / have been awesome, and helped people fall in love with new metaplot. Also, the Sabbat book should have come just after the two main splat books, or along with Chicago.<br /> <br /> Also, a Translation Guide such as the one OPP gave us for Requiem-to-Masquerade and viceversa would have been useful.<br /> <br /> Unfortunately, handling the license to Modiphius seems to have been a huge problem: &quot;Fall of London&quot; is really an outlier, in terms of atmosphere (dungeon crawling Ancillae escaping trenchcoat-and-katanas Inquisition agents, and fighting a God-Methuselah), and none of their other projects saw fruition.<br /> <br /> I hope now that Justin and his team, working with OPP, can steer the course of this Edition for good: I really love what has been done so far, and I think it has huge potential.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":12590,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12590-manfr","user":"Manfr","date":". 05-31-2021, 08:23 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12590-manfr","name":"Manfr","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"449"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-05-31T05:30:33-07:00","id":1450439,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MyWifeIsScary</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1443592-the-official-v5-vs-v20-thread?p=1450417#post1450417\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Or the inquisition being a real big threat because Dominate got nerfed to shit and secret rogue agents can somehow trust secret rogue agents from other agencies along with domestic terrorists to make absolutely sure that they can't ever have a peaceful life or get a lucrative job in the private sector after they leave the service.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Dominate nerfed?! You can erase memories with a level 1 power, and at level 5 you can get someone kill himself (something which was clearly excluded in prior editions), and it also insta-works on mortals!<br /> <br /> Mind you, I think Second Inquisition is the only sensible way of still playing &quot;Vampire the Masquerade&quot;, and not &quot;True Blood: the TTRPG&quot;: as for the implausibility of secret rogue agents working with different agencies and domestic terrorists, as an Italian I beg to differ: our whole post-WW2 history is mired with neofascist domestic terrorism influenced, if not orchestrated, by rogue elements of the secret services, that also heavily infiltrated leftwing terrorist groups, possibly with patronage from CIA. We are still discussing former Prime Minister Aldo Moro's kidnapping and assassination by communist Red Brigades, whether they were all alone, or they were manipolated by the Americans, the Russians, both ... so, I find the Second Inquisition pretty plausible.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12590-manfr","name":"Manfr","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"449"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-05-31T05:49:19-07:00","id":1450441,"title":"","content":"Dominate got nerfed hard. Mostly in the form of &quot;Can't do anything which requires cognition&quot; which is... well, even if we give them the benefit of the doubt and don't extend that definition to it's proper extent, is still an extreme nerf. Also It's no longer subtle; people go into a trance when they get targeted and do the thing ASAP.<br /> <br /> Insta working on mortals is hardly an upgrade when mortals were almost universally very easy targets, and the part where you can get people to die at 5th level is more a power-play than an actually useful power for that level. You should also remember that in V20, &quot;implanted directive&quot; was just apart of Dominate 2, not something you needed to buy seperately and.... Yeah man, I've gone through this far too many times before. Just trust me when I say V5 gutted Dominate (and Auspex, and Obfuscate, and Potence, and Thaumaturgy, and the predecessors of oblivion...)<br /> <br /> Respectfully, &quot;Italy is a political clusterfuck&quot; can be the summary of many political discussions with my Italian friends, so, whilst Italy might do that, it's not so much the case for the majority of europe where things are still shit but not to the point that &quot;prohibited&quot; and &quot;extremely prohibited&quot; need to be differentiated. Another way to look at it; would such historically corrupt organization really be against vampires rather than with them? Almost certainly not.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":25794,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25794-mywifeisscary","user":"MyWifeIsScary","date":". 05-31-2021, 09:40 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25794-mywifeisscary","name":"MyWifeIsScary","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25794_2.png","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3711"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-05-31T07:18:11-07:00","id":1450446,"title":"","content":"I always thought it was a missed opportunity not to have the Imbued involved. AFAIK, they haven't appeared yet, but would make sense as antagonists.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Writer, publisher, performer<br /> Mostly he/his, sometimes she/her IRL <a href=\"https://adam-lowe.com\" target=\"_blank\">https://adam-lowe.com</a>","edited":{"userid":5291,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5291-adambeyoncelowe","user":"adambeyoncelowe","date":". 05-31-2021, 01:00 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5291-adambeyoncelowe","name":"adambeyoncelowe","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5291_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2802"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-05-31T09:18:02-07:00","id":1450458,"title":"","content":"The SI works pretty well, in my opinion, if you have them pretty much ineffectual against the vampires in control, but making life a hell for everybody else instead. Especially since they understand nothing about what they're looking for, and treat humans as potentially compromised.<br /> <br /> Humans unwittingly wrapped up in vampire politics, ghouls, thinbloods, caitiff, fledglings and some neonates. These guys are the easy targets, the ones with barely any power who are barely involved in vampire society and got dragged into it without consent or warning and now they're making do.<br /> The SI is forming cults and running experiments on the human populace, they're ruining the careers and lives of people who have unknowingly formed connections to vampires (or who have no connections, and are scapegoats and mistakes)... How many innocents have been kidnapped, killed, tortured and ruined without understanding why?<br /> <br /> And they may well be doing some of these things at the command of elders playing politics. The militant government agency is a tool wielded by those in power trying to get one up over each other and fucking over everyone else in the process.<br /> Actual successful hits against the major powers will have been directed by other elders. The Assamites say (amongst themselves) that they engineered the hit against Vienna, but I suspect there's a long list of candidates privately claiming the same.<br /> <br /> --And considering that a greater power manipulating the SI from behind the scenes would make perfect sense, being Imbued does also make sense...","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><sup><i>Prone to hyperbole</i></sup>","edited":{"userid":26836,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26836-rhywbeth","user":"Rhywbeth","date":". 05-31-2021, 03:23 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26836-rhywbeth","name":"Rhywbeth","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar26836_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"377"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-05-31T12:09:03-07:00","id":1450477,"title":"","content":"I also just think infernalists are cool antagonists/ make kinda interesting antiheroes. I mean if you're playing a vampire an infernalist isn't that much of a stretch. <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>adambeyoncelowe</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1443592-the-official-v5-vs-v20-thread?p=1450419#post1450419\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> So if you wrote this as an alt-metaplot book, I'd buy it.</div> </div> </div> </div>First issue is that I'm a hack writer and too much of an egotist to get an editor or an artist, and also too broke to want to share credit. Second issue is I've already got a project that will be done.... eventually. Third and most relevant issue is that I've paid very little attention to canonical SPCs and wouldn't know what to do with them infront of people who do. I'm not sure how I'd write an in-depth metaplot without throwing names around, whilst the brief summary I've written isn't really worth throwing money at.<br /> <br /> Are big names important to people? Is the inner circle listed? <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25794-mywifeisscary","name":"MyWifeIsScary","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25794_2.png","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3711"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-05-31T12:19:53-07:00","id":1450480,"title":"","content":"I just hope the new Sabbat book gives rules for infernalism. The true Sabbat shouldn't be losers like the Path of Power and the Inner Voice of Honorable Accord. A True Sabbat wields the power of Evil Revelations and will reign after the Antediluvians have eaten their slaves.<br /> <br /> <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Author of <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Cthulhu-Armageddon-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01KUOM7SI/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982844&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Cthulhu+Armageddon\" target=\"_blank\">Cthulhu Armageddon</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Teenage-Weredeer-Bright-Falls-Mysteries-ebook/dp/B075TTN2FN/ref=sr_1_2?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982717&amp;sr=1-2&amp;keywords=Weredeer#customerReviews\" target=\"_blank\">I was a Teenage Weredeer</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Straight-Outta-Fangton-Comedic-Vampire-ebook/dp/B01KNHICCC/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982774&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Straight+Outta+Fangton\" target=\"_blank\">Straight Outta Fangton</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Lucifers-Star-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01MDM9MCT/ref=mt_kindle?_encoding=UTF8&amp;me=&amp;qid=\" target=\"_blank\">Lucifer's Star</a>, </i>and the <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Rules-Supervillainy-Saga-Book-ebook/dp/B07MB89S33/\" target=\"_blank\">Supervillainy Saga</a>.</i><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","name":"CTPhipps","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12002_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13933"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-05-31T12:26:21-07:00","id":1450482,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CTPhipps</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1443592-the-official-v5-vs-v20-thread?p=1450480#post1450480\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I just hope the new Sabbat book gives rules for infernalism. The true Sabbat shouldn't be losers like the Path of Power and the Inner Voice of Honorable Accord. A True Sabbat wields the power of Evil Revelations and will reign after the Antediluvians have eaten their slaves.<br /> <br /> <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /></div> </div> </div> </div>&quot;Yes, Inquisitor, this one over here.&quot;<br /> <br /> I wonder what the Baali are up to in V5...","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><sup><i>Prone to hyperbole</i></sup>","edited":{"userid":26836,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26836-rhywbeth","user":"Rhywbeth","date":". 05-31-2021, 03:32 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26836-rhywbeth","name":"Rhywbeth","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar26836_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"377"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-05-31T12:32:41-07:00","id":1450483,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>adambeyoncelowe</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1443592-the-official-v5-vs-v20-thread?p=1450413#post1450413\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">These are some interesting ideas. I admit it's a bit of a missed opportunity to make so many of the setting changes things that happened in the past rather than things you could play through now.<br /> <br /> I loved sourcebooks like The Time of Thin Blood and Nights of Prophecy at the time. You could make a lot of money playing through Transylvania Chronicles: The Fall of Vienna, The Hunters Hunted: Rise of the Second Inquisition, Diablerie: The Gehenna War, etc.</div> </div> </div> </div>Speaking as someone who's been introducing V5 metaplot into their V20 campaign as current events, it works SO MUCH better than &quot;Oh yeah, this happened 5-10 years ago. Deal with it.&quot;<br /> <br /> Vienna just exploded, the local court is in a tizzy over who was behind it, the Tremere primogen and head of the local chantry left for Vienna to consult with his superiors just a few weeks before and hasn't been heard from since (it's now about three weeks out from the event). The Tremere (including one of the PCs) are currently in a scramble over their leader's resources (the primogen/chantry head played his underlings against each other by using different underlings to be his whip and his second in command for the chantry... which means the acting primogen and acting chantry head are now two different vampires). The other clans see the weakness too and are starting to move in on other Tremere assets throughout the city because &quot;possession is 9/10th of the law&quot; and &quot;as long as the Prince gets his cut it'll be fine.&quot;<br /> <br /> And I haven't even had to touch the actual event directly... that's all just local fallout in a campaign set entirely in a single city.<br /> <br /> The whole Banu Haqim joining the Camarilla has also been going on in the background since the start too with a &quot;goodwill ambassador&quot; from the Banu Haqim (Sorcerer caste) arriving at court and helping out various kindred with their problems and basically ingratiating himself to everyone with any power. Hell yes they have their own agenda, but the PC's haven't figured it out yet. He smiles very much at the misfortune of the Tremere (who are the one faction who wanted nothing to do with the &quot;Assamite&quot; and his offers of assistance).<br /> <br /> Just before the current crazy settles I plan on dropping the Fall of London news on them... because that'll make certain NPCs (and probably some PCs) even MORE paranoid and prone to doing something stupid.<br /> <br /> The V5 metaplot isn't horrible; I think it primarily suffers from being dumped on everyone all at once as past events. If they'd actually occurred through various releases over the last 15 years in real time the way say, the events in Time of Thin Blood did, then I don't think they'd feel nearly so contrived and therefore received nearly the pushback they did from coming all at once and upending so many things, even if, over the course of 15 years of continuing releases, all the same things happened.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1328-chris24601","name":"Chris24601","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"520"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-05-31T12:38:46-07:00","id":1450484,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Rhywbeth</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1443592-the-official-v5-vs-v20-thread?p=1450482#post1450482\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> &quot;Yes, Inquisitor, this one over here.&quot;<br /> <br /> I wonder what the Baali are up to in V5...</div> </div> </div> </div>Why not sell your soul when you're not going to use it? <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Author of <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Cthulhu-Armageddon-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01KUOM7SI/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982844&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Cthulhu+Armageddon\" target=\"_blank\">Cthulhu Armageddon</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Teenage-Weredeer-Bright-Falls-Mysteries-ebook/dp/B075TTN2FN/ref=sr_1_2?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982717&amp;sr=1-2&amp;keywords=Weredeer#customerReviews\" target=\"_blank\">I was a Teenage Weredeer</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Straight-Outta-Fangton-Comedic-Vampire-ebook/dp/B01KNHICCC/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982774&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Straight+Outta+Fangton\" target=\"_blank\">Straight Outta Fangton</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Lucifers-Star-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01MDM9MCT/ref=mt_kindle?_encoding=UTF8&amp;me=&amp;qid=\" target=\"_blank\">Lucifer's Star</a>, </i>and the <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Rules-Supervillainy-Saga-Book-ebook/dp/B07MB89S33/\" target=\"_blank\">Supervillainy Saga</a>.</i><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","name":"CTPhipps","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12002_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13933"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-05-31T12:42:05-07:00","id":1450486,"title":"","content":"One of the big issue with V5's plot is that players will stomp all over the second inquisition with V20 rules. Auspex, Obfuscate and Dominate would really do a number on them (and, y'know, there's no way secret agents are going to be able to co-operate with other groups of secret agents while remaining secret, and secrecy is their only protection)<br /> (and also the Lasombra plot wouldn't mechanically work. And also too many vampires have too many dots in intelligence to really go along with... nevermind)<br /> <br /> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar12002_2.jpeg');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"12002\" data-vbnamecard=\"12002\">CTPhipps</a><br /> Infernalism is probably going to be most prevalent among anarchs.<br /> Your faction are the bad guys (relatively speaking)","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25794-mywifeisscary","name":"MyWifeIsScary","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25794_2.png","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3711"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-05-31T12:43:01-07:00","id":1450487,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CTPhipps</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1443592-the-official-v5-vs-v20-thread?p=1450484#post1450484\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Why not sell your soul when you're not going to use it? <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /></div> </div> </div> </div>Souls are for eating, not currency<br /> Speaking of which, is it possible to diablerise somebody and sell their soul instead? Was that ever covered? Can you get better deals if you have multiple souls?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><sup><i>Prone to hyperbole</i></sup>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26836-rhywbeth","name":"Rhywbeth","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar26836_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"377"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-05-31T12:48:11-07:00","id":1450489,"title":"","content":"It's never explicitly mentioned, but most things point towards no. <br /> However, in some books, you could do &quot;evil&quot; things, ranging from silly to sick, to please demons and gain &quot;points&quot; to get investments. Infernalism has mechanically been changed significantly from each book. In KotE there were even mechanics for lawyering yourself a good contract.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25794-mywifeisscary","name":"MyWifeIsScary","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25794_2.png","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3711"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-05-31T13:04:02-07:00","id":1450490,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CTPhipps</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1443592-the-official-v5-vs-v20-thread?p=1450484#post1450484\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Why not sell your soul when you're not going to use it? <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /></div> </div> </div> </div>Because embracing slavery is for fools and the insane.","signature":"","edite