text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982774&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Straight+Outta+Fangton\" target=\"_blank\">Straight Outta Fangton</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Lucifers-Star-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01MDM9MCT/ref=mt_kindle?_encoding=UTF8&amp;me=&amp;qid=\" target=\"_blank\">Lucifer's Star</a>, </i>and the <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Rules-Supervillainy-Saga-Book-ebook/dp/B07MB89S33/\" target=\"_blank\">Supervillainy Saga</a>.</i><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","name":"CTPhipps","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12002_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13933"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-05-31T13:19:32-07:00","id":1450492,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CTPhipps</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1443592-the-official-v5-vs-v20-thread?p=1450491#post1450491\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I'm sorry, I can't hear you over the fact that I'm an immortal Decani. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /></div> </div> </div> </div>With effectively no will of your own left, no goals or plans of your own, a puppet, or a vessel of an Eldritch being of alien at best goals and desires. Don't get me wrong, those are cool themes, and the weirder and less related to RL myths the Patrons are, the better, but Infernalism should always be a bad deal, a fools trade, the line even the most inhuman Vampire, or power mad Mage finds a step to far, that is it's purpose narratively. <br /> <br /> Bet those games are fun tho, and the cross over mashup potential is epic. Basically I think it's something fun to explore, but you are doing those stories a disservice if you forget how terrible and self destructive (literally, it destroys your Self ,and replaces it with something that serves better) it is.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":25011,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25011-taggie","user":"Taggie","date":". 05-31-2021, 04:24 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25011-taggie","name":"Taggie","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1047"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-06-05T04:05:44-07:00","id":1451035,"title":"","content":"I see infernalism as playing with fire. (hellfire, if you will)<br /> Yeah, you can get burnt, but that's not a garantee unless you're stupid about it. Fire can be incredibly useful if you're using it in a controlled manner. The problem is that the wrong kinds of people are drawn to these flames. Also for some people these flames seem to be the only option for them to gain power or survive so... yeah. <br /> <br /> Infernalism is so hated by vampires because it's the OG method of quick and dirty power, and thus hugely disruptive for undead society. Suddenly a neonate has more spells and abilities than a late-stage ancillae? Shit. We can't be having that. What if it spreads? next thing you know we'll all be equals living in an undead democracy; it's the last thing an elder wants. Sure there's the occasional sick and twisted guy that goes too far with it but that's really anecdotal when we're talking vampires, who all assume themselves to be puppets of the methuselah they don't see anyway.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25794-mywifeisscary","name":"MyWifeIsScary","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25794_2.png","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3711"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-06-19T14:27:52-07:00","id":1452909,"title":"","content":"To illustrate the point i will make i will talk about my current game as a storyteller.<br /> <br /> It is set in southern Germany and it started from being mortal and being in some kind of soft almost non leathel hunger games/highlander type of game to-&gt;becomming a ghoul-&gt;and some of the characters will become kindred.<br /> <br /> I am using -mechanically speaking- almost completely v20. However in terms of Metaplot i have introduced the 2nd Inquisition and the fall of London, maybe even the fall of Vienna. Should i introduce Vienna, i will split the clan, only to have a strong new core forming and trying to reform the old system, hunting down anybody that is not part of it, with a strong camarilla backing. The beckoning is cancelled as well as the Brujah leaving the Cammarilla, but many of the Lasombra did join them, so that the main clan is basically Camarilla now. The Camarilla is NOT scared of the 2nd inquisition and did not go into hiding, in fact they are trying to hit/manipulate/work against the 2nd inquisition instead of the Sabbat. The Sabbat is a bit lifeless due to many, many losses and operates mostly on a street level now, apart from their literal home soils. Another Anarch freestate was created with a heart in Switzerland and southern france (supported by a certain fifth generation Inconnu Brujah). The camarilla still see themselves as the sole representative/sect of Vampires, not a 1% club.<br /> <br /> Should they reach Vampirehood, my player will be able to chose if they want a touchstone (way easier to stay on humanity 7+) as a merit. I will not introduce hunger dies, wil reinterprate Predator type and will stay true to V20 for most mechanical things - apart from combat, which does not happen often in my chronicles, but i would really like an easier way to do it, where V5 is better. No compultions obv.<br /> So basically i will homebrew the stuff from V5 into my chronicle as long as i like it.<br /> <br /> Never had a better game going. Maybe like 10 years ago, but even that game was more sandbox then anything. What V5 showed me was that you dont have to play overpowered elder vamps all the time. The progression we currently enjoy and the escalation that follows is something to be hold.<br /> <br /> For that i am thankful. I wont go over the shortcommings of either edition. I am certain others will create their oWoD the way they want. The only book of V5 that i am interested in is the 2IQ book, as i believe that either Anarch vs 2IQ or Camarilla vs 2IQ should be the new core conflict of the product, in addition to the generational conflict.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>This is me, just forgot my PW and changed my email<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8249-crytash\" target=\"_blank\">http://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8249-crytash</a>","edited":{"userid":25163,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25163-crytash2","user":"Crytash2","date":". 06-19-2021, 05:32 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25163-crytash2","name":"Crytash2","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25163_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"55"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-06-20T05:54:56-07:00","id":1452940,"title":"","content":"The Lasombra shift is such anti-lasombra dickery.<br /> <br /> 1- It's a terrible fucking deal<br /> 2- Social darwinists aren't going to take a bad deal just because it has some appeal to social darwinisim. Social Darwinists want others to die, not themselves. <br /> 3- As a bunch of Ayn Rand fans*, the Anarchs are going to hold more appeal. <br /> 4- as people who see their clan as the OG anarchs, the Anarchs are going to hold more appeal. <br /> 5- the Camarilla is a joke in V5 and the Anarchs are the favoured children, so they hold more appeal. <br /> 6- The cam is too entrenched and stability-loving to really let the lasombra thrive. <br /> 7- vinculum<br /> <br /> <br /> *The ones who aren't Ayn Rand fans are probably going to stay in the sabbat<br /> ** I have never read Ayn Rand's work, however, I did watch an episode of ThugNotes on the fountainhead, which of course makes me informed enough to reference her. <br /> <br /> Out of character:<br /> &quot;replacing the Brujah&quot; is stupid. <br /> <br /> Like, If you wanted to have the Lasombra emerge in the cam, you could just have the Magisters take advantage of the weakening of the sects and using the time to get out of seclusion, embrace and train many new childer, and finally be a force that can stand on their own. But you combine this bullshit move with the new Clan Weakness and it seems pretty self evident that someone really wanted to screw the Lasombra.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25794-mywifeisscary","name":"MyWifeIsScary","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25794_2.png","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3711"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-06-20T06:00:47-07:00","id":1452941,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MyWifeIsScary</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1443592-the-official-v5-vs-v20-thread?p=1452940#post1452940\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">2- Social darwinists aren't going to take a bad deal just because it has some appeal to social darwinisim. Social Darwinists want others to die, not themselves.</div> </div> </div> </div>I don't believe anyone who thinks the Lasombra are making a bad deal are true Lasombra fans.<br /> <br /> After all, the Lasombra are totally briar patching the Camarilla.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Author of <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Cthulhu-Armageddon-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01KUOM7SI/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982844&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Cthulhu+Armageddon\" target=\"_blank\">Cthulhu Armageddon</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Teenage-Weredeer-Bright-Falls-Mysteries-ebook/dp/B075TTN2FN/ref=sr_1_2?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982717&amp;sr=1-2&amp;keywords=Weredeer#customerReviews\" target=\"_blank\">I was a Teenage Weredeer</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Straight-Outta-Fangton-Comedic-Vampire-ebook/dp/B01KNHICCC/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982774&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Straight+Outta+Fangton\" target=\"_blank\">Straight Outta Fangton</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Lucifers-Star-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01MDM9MCT/ref=mt_kindle?_encoding=UTF8&amp;me=&amp;qid=\" target=\"_blank\">Lucifer's Star</a>, </i>and the <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Rules-Supervillainy-Saga-Book-ebook/dp/B07MB89S33/\" target=\"_blank\">Supervillainy Saga</a>.</i><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","name":"CTPhipps","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12002_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13933"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-06-20T06:08:12-07:00","id":1452942,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MyWifeIsScary</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1443592-the-official-v5-vs-v20-thread?p=1452940#post1452940\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Like, If you wanted to have the Lasombra emerge in the cam, you could just have the Magisters take advantage of the weakening of the sects and using the time to get out of seclusion, embrace and train many new childer, and finally be a force that can stand on their own. But you combine this bullshit move with the new Clan Weakness and it seems pretty self evident that someone really wanted to screw the Lasombra.</div> </div> </div> </div>Honestly it felt more like another part of the effort to de-fang the Sabbat rather than a direct stab at the Lasombra. A large number of the Lasombra, one of the two most important clans left, and furthermore murdered a shit ton of the ones who decided to stay on the way out. Other Lasombra probably turned into wights in their attempt to throw off their paths and relearn Humanity to fit into the Camarilla. The Lasombra still remaining the Sabbat are probably outnumbered by several of the antitribu clans. Plus the defecting Lasombra also took a lot of their influence, money, power, etc, with them.<br /> <br /> Having the Lasombra move from the Sabbat to the Camarilla like this really doesn't affect them as player characters, if anything it moves them towards more of a central position in the gameline. <br /> <br /> So I'd hazard someone likes the Lasombra, wanted the Lasombra to have a more significant role in the metaplot, and wanted to mostly pull them out of the Sabbat because they knew the Sabbat were going into full NPC only territory.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/741-anubisxy","name":"AnubisXy","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar741_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5693"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-06-20T06:21:54-07:00","id":1452943,"title":"","content":"My solution to the Lasombra in the Cam is even easier. The elders who\u2019ve been there from the start (or very nearly so) and have been Cam loyalists for centuries have enough childer they finally feel comfortable coming out of the closest and demanding a seat at the table.<br /> <br /> No defections, no bad deals, just an unmasking as part of a power play.<br /> <br /> As to the Brujah, rather than leaving the Cam, the warrior-scholar elders took the opportunity of Hardestadt\u2019s assassination by Bell to rebrand and distance themselves from the street rabble/anarchs and insisting they be called Clan Hellenes as they once were and that the slur of Brujah henceforth only be used in reference to certain \u201cdegenerate\u201d bloodlines.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1328-chris24601","name":"Chris24601","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"520"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-06-20T06:24:57-07:00","id":1452945,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Chris24601</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1443592-the-official-v5-vs-v20-thread?p=1452943#post1452943\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">My solution to the Lasombra in the Cam is even easier. The elders who\u2019ve been there from the start (or very nearly so) and have been Cam loyalists for centuries have enough childer they finally feel comfortable coming out of the closest and demanding a seat at the table.</div> </div> </div> </div>That's what I would have done. With both the Gangrel and Brujah leaving the Cam, the Lasombra antitribu would have been in the perfect position to step in and take one of those seats at the inner table for themselves. But, sadly that isn't what happened.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/741-anubisxy","name":"AnubisXy","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar741_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5693"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-06-20T06:34:07-07:00","id":1452947,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Chris24601</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1443592-the-official-v5-vs-v20-thread?p=1452943#post1452943\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">My solution to the Lasombra in the Cam is even easier. The elders who\u2019ve been there from the start (or very nearly so) and have been Cam loyalists for centuries have enough childer they finally feel comfortable coming out of the closest and demanding a seat at the table.<br /> <br /> No defections, no bad deals, just an unmasking as part of a power play.</div> </div> </div> </div>Which doesn't actually change anything at all and doesn't really lead to any plots as the Antitribu have always been there.<br /> <br /> No offense but what adventures does this inspire and what changes to the power structure? What is the hook?<br /> <br /> The point of edition changes are to make things different than what they were before and throw wrenches into the Jyhad that the PCs can either exploit or roll with.<br /> <br /> At least, IMHO.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Author of <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Cthulhu-Armageddon-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01KUOM7SI/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982844&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Cthulhu+Armageddon\" target=\"_blank\">Cthulhu Armageddon</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Teenage-Weredeer-Bright-Falls-Mysteries-ebook/dp/B075TTN2FN/ref=sr_1_2?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982717&amp;sr=1-2&amp;keywords=Weredeer#customerReviews\" target=\"_blank\">I was a Teenage Weredeer</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Straight-Outta-Fangton-Comedic-Vampire-ebook/dp/B01KNHICCC/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982774&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Straight+Outta+Fangton\" target=\"_blank\">Straight Outta Fangton</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Lucifers-Star-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01MDM9MCT/ref=mt_kindle?_encoding=UTF8&amp;me=&amp;qid=\" target=\"_blank\">Lucifer's Star</a>, </i>and the <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Rules-Supervillainy-Saga-Book-ebook/dp/B07MB89S33/\" target=\"_blank\">Supervillainy Saga</a>.</i><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","name":"CTPhipps","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12002_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13933"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-06-20T09:26:09-07:00","id":1452965,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CTPhipps</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1443592-the-official-v5-vs-v20-thread?p=1452941#post1452941\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I don't believe anyone who thinks the Lasombra are making a bad deal are true Lasombra fans.<br /> <br /> After all, the Lasombra are totally briar patching the Camarilla.</div> </div> </div> </div>If you want a comedic camp game that totally lampoons different archtypes, this Lasombra Farce is excellent. If you want to play with a straight face, No. It doesn't work. It really depends on how serious the tone of your game is; it works for a &quot;beer and pretzels&quot; kinda game but not for a believable setting.<br /> That said, and I know I shouldn't do this, but you writing this is terribly Ironic given your &quot;I love the Tzmisce, and by Tzmisce I strictly refer to the &quot;Old Clan&quot;, who aren't at all normal Tzmisce as most people think of them.&quot; stance.<br /> <br /> There are lots of different kinds of Lasombra. They're not Ventrue who only differ in what fields of business they're interested in. Some examples off the top of my head:<br /> <br /> Edgy kid<br /> Brainwashed kid<br /> Ayn rand.<br /> Bully<br /> Crazy bully<br /> Psychopath<br /> Overcompensator<br /> Obvious meglomaniac<br /> Subtle meglomaniac<br /> lying priest<br /> Evil, but sincere, priest<br /> Good priest.<br /> Occultist<br /> Cthulu cultist.<br /> Cthulu<br /> Vizier,<br /> Slightly more agressive Ventrue<br /> Slightly more vain ventrue<br /> Literally indistinguishable from a Toreador.<br /> Hardly distinguishable from a Malkavian<br /> A Nosferatu but.. shadier. <br /> <br /> How many of these fit the Camarilla, at least more than the Sabbat or Anarchs?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25794-mywifeisscary","name":"MyWifeIsScary","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25794_2.png","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3711"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-06-20T09:46:24-07:00","id":1452969,"title":"","content":"Lasombras are by nature out for their own success. The big problem are the courts and the right to destroy, but as long as they get dispensation, who actually says no? Especially if you think about how the the 2IQ presents a danger that the Sabbat can not really handle. Going to the Camarilla because they might promise a better shot at survival makes sense i my book. Now, should the 2IQ go away, who really knows what the Lasombras long term plan is.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>This is me, just forgot my PW and changed my email<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8249-crytash\" target=\"_blank\">http://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8249-crytash</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25163-crytash2","name":"Crytash2","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25163_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"55"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-06-20T09:48:11-07:00","id":1452970,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MyWifeIsScary</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1443592-the-official-v5-vs-v20-thread?p=1452965#post1452965\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">If you want a comedic camp game that totally lampoons different archtypes, this Lasombra Farce is excellent. If you want to play with a straight face, No. It doesn't work. It really depends on how serious the tone of your game is; it works for a &quot;beer and pretzels&quot; kinda game but not for a believable setting.</div> </div> </div> </div>I'm happy to discuss how I handled it in my game and why I think it works but I should point out that this is not the way to start a dialogue and is in every possible way an attack on fellow posters.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Author of <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Cthulhu-Armageddon-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01KUOM7SI/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982844&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Cthulhu+Armageddon\" target=\"_blank\">Cthulhu Armageddon</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Teenage-Weredeer-Bright-Falls-Mysteries-ebook/dp/B075TTN2FN/ref=sr_1_2?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982717&amp;sr=1-2&amp;keywords=Weredeer#customerReviews\" target=\"_blank\">I was a Teenage Weredeer</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Straight-Outta-Fangton-Comedic-Vampire-ebook/dp/B01KNHICCC/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982774&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Straight+Outta+Fangton\" target=\"_blank\">Straight Outta Fangton</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Lucifers-Star-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01MDM9MCT/ref=mt_kindle?_encoding=UTF8&amp;me=&amp;qid=\" target=\"_blank\">Lucifer's Star</a>, </i>and the <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Rules-Supervillainy-Saga-Book-ebook/dp/B07MB89S33/\" target=\"_blank\">Supervillainy Saga</a>.</i><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","name":"CTPhipps","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12002_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13933"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-06-20T11:43:00-07:00","id":1452976,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CTPhipps</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1443592-the-official-v5-vs-v20-thread?p=1452947#post1452947\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Which doesn't actually change anything at all and doesn't really lead to any plots as the Antitribu have always been there.</div> </div> </div> </div>A) Not every change needs to be an over the top hair-on-fire shattering of the status quo like you\u2019re the showeunner of a crap CW show. A new Clan getting a seat in the inner circle with a vote and justicar/archons throws all the old balances of power into chaos.<br /> <br /> Ex. In my local game the local Lasombra are demanding a seat on the city\u2019s Primogen Council where there were previously seven members and the Prince could only influence the \u201cLegislature\u201d through persuasion and the splits were almost always 3-4. But laws were established the last time the Primogen Council had an even number that, in the event of a tie the Prince acts as tie breaker. So allowing them a seat would vastly increase his influence and person power, so he\u2019s willing to strike bargains he normally wouldn\u2019t that can get the Lasombra a Primogen seat with the expectation of long term gain by being tie breaker.<br /> <br /> And that\u2019s just at the local level. Are you really saying that sort of change; akin to a new political party getting a significant share of the vote; doesn\u2019t change ANYTHING?<br /> <br /> B) The severity of a change is relative.<br /> <br /> Two headlines - \u201cPolitical Outsider wins the Governor\u2019s race, ousting 20 year veteran\u201d and \u201ctwo killed in car accident.\u201d The first is front page headline news, the latter might get a mention in the obituaries in a few days.<br /> <br /> But if your protagonists are the 13 and 12 year old children whose parents just died in a car crash leaving them orphans... the second story is earth shattering and the first an irrelevancy.<br /> <br /> I blew up the Vienna Chantry as a background event in my campaign. It\u2019s irrelevant to the PC\u2019s stories except that the Tremere Primogen went missing at about the same time and the other Tremere are scrambling for his assets in the wake of his presumed death. One of the lesser Tremere, a presumed ally of the PCs (or rather aligned on certain goals), though is getting ready to betray the PCs by squealing to the Prince about certain violations of various edicts the PCs have commited because he hopes that by ingratiating himself to be the best way to get himself a higher position as the Prince has swooped in to basically act as the Executor of the Tremere Primogen\u2019s affairs since the Primogen deliberately set up his underlings to be at each other\u2019s throats without enough resources individually to decisively defeat their rivals.<br /> <br /> C) Ripples can eventually make tidal waves. One of the more subtle effects of the Lasombra coming out and getting a seat at the table has been a loosening of the Camarilla\u2019s traditional secularism, paving the way for widespread acceptance ans adoption of various blood cults in the future.<br /> <br /> Likewise, the Lasombra antitribu felt safe coming out precisely because of the disruption of the Sabbat by the Gehenna War nonsense and since a big part of their staying alive was keeping track of their Clanmates in the Sabbat. So they\u2019ve been scooping up unattended assets of their Sabbat kin has off in the Middle East and sharing key intel to push the remnant Sabbat out of territories they\u2019re claiming in the name of the Camarilla.<br /> <br /> Basically, the Lasombra antitribu are just starting to flex their muscles and the long term effects could be profound.<br /> <br /> Look at that... all sorts of plots where you said none could possibly exist.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1328-chris24601","name":"Chris24601","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"520"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-06-20T14:11:38-07:00","id":1452990,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CTPhipps</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1443592-the-official-v5-vs-v20-thread?p=1452970#post1452970\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I'm happy to discuss how I handled it in my game and why I think it works but I should point out that this is not the way to start a dialogue and is in every possible way an attack on fellow posters.</div> </div> </div> </div>1: you began with &quot; I don't believe anyone who... are true lasombra fans&quot;. That's worse than whatever you think I'm doing. <br /> 2:&quot;beer and pretzel&quot; games are fun and I havent said anything bad about them, though as my body disagrees with hops and I'd rarely get pretzels over an alternative so maybe i should take issue with the term: &quot;Cider and Garlicbread&quot; doesn't have the same ring to it. Anyhows: Fun games are fun, but don't use &quot; just roll with it&quot; politics when writing for a setting people have invested themselves in. Start serious and players can easily make light of the setting. Start silly and its difficult to go back to taking stuff seriously.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25794-mywifeisscary","name":"MyWifeIsScary","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25794_2.png","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3711"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-06-20T15:20:50-07:00","id":1452994,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MyWifeIsScary</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1443592-the-official-v5-vs-v20-thread?p=1452990#post1452990\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> 1: you began with &quot; I don't believe anyone who... are true lasombra fans&quot;. That's worse than whatever you think I'm doing.</div> </div> </div> </div>Well mine is motivated by the fact that I think the Lasombra are smarter than the Camarilla and will cut a very good deal for themselves and you went into an elaborate description of how no game could be serious or mature.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Author of <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Cthulhu-Armageddon-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01KUOM7SI/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982844&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Cthulhu+Armageddon\" target=\"_blank\">Cthulhu Armageddon</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Teenage-Weredeer-Bright-Falls-Mysteries-ebook/dp/B075TTN2FN/ref=sr_1_2?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982717&amp;sr=1-2&amp;keywords=Weredeer#customerReviews\" target=\"_blank\">I was a Teenage Weredeer</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Straight-Outta-Fangton-Comedic-Vampire-ebook/dp/B01KNHICCC/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982774&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Straight+Outta+Fangton\" target=\"_blank\">Straight Outta Fangton</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Lucifers-Star-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01MDM9MCT/ref=mt_kindle?_encoding=UTF8&amp;me=&amp;qid=\" target=\"_blank\">Lucifer's Star</a>, </i>and the <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Rules-Supervillainy-Saga-Book-ebook/dp/B07MB89S33/\" target=\"_blank\">Supervillainy Saga</a>.</i><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","name":"CTPhipps","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12002_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13933"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-06-20T18:03:33-07:00","id":1453001,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Chris24601</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1443592-the-official-v5-vs-v20-thread?p=1452976#post1452976\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Two headlines - \u201cPolitical Outsider wins the Governor\u2019s race, ousting 20 year veteran\u201d and \u201ctwo killed in car accident.\u201d The first is front page headline news, the latter might get a mention in the obituaries in a few days.</div> </div> </div> </div>They are both front page headline news. &quot;If it bleeds it leads!&quot;","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/9015-zee-patrick","name":"zee PaTrick","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"56"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-06-20T23:38:08-07:00","id":1453014,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CTPhipps</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1443592-the-official-v5-vs-v20-thread?p=1452994#post1452994\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Well mine is motivated by the fact that I think the Lasombra are smarter than the Camarilla and will cut a very good deal for themselves and you went into an elaborate description of how no game could be serious or mature.</div> </div> </div> </div>The Lasombra are only &quot;smarter&quot; than the cam in V5, where the cam are routinely making shit choices to give the Anarchs some room. In OG VTM, although they're more interested in raw talent and attitude than other clans, they're not a collective of geniuses: the Malks and Tremere are smarter, the ventrue more socially apt, and the Toreador and Nosferatu are better rounded. The Lasombra work better as muscle, but that's not going to have them running things.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25794-mywifeisscary","name":"MyWifeIsScary","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25794_2.png","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3711"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-06-21T03:39:36-07:00","id":1453017,"title":"","content":"<b>My interpretation of the Lasombra joining the Camarilla</b><br /> <br /> Previous games have paid lip service to the idea that the Lasombra are the ultimate predatory survivors. That the Lasombra have their previous lives destroyed by their sires just so they can make sure that when push comes to shove, when the chips are down, the Lasombra will do anything to survive.<br /> <br /> The premise of the defection is meant to illustrate this attitude of the Keepers better than any previous one in the fact that when the Sabbat becomes more trouble than it is worth, that the Lasombra will turn upon them without a second's hesitation. That the Lasombra really do epitomize the narcissitic psychopath among vampires because they do not feel loyalty to their fellow packmates, the Crusade of Caine, or religious rituals.<br /> <br /> The monumentalness of the betrayal is <b>character development</b> that helps expand the clan in such a way that it develops an even more distinct identity. It also helps develop the Sabbat as well as it shows just what was holding the Sword of Caine back in that a good chunk of its leadership really was composed of traitors and fair weather friends.<br /> <br /> But why join the Camarilla? What could they get out of the Ivory Tower that they weren't getting out of their own sect? Well, the answer boils down to the fact the Camarilla was always the big dog they were up against. They were the 2nd biggest sect but they were the Reno to their Las Vegas and everyone goes to Vegas.<br /> BUT THE CAMARILLA WAS VULNERABLE.<br /> <br /> Having lost the Gangrel and the Brujah, the Camarilla was in need of replacing its two clans and had the Assamites on the hook. The Anarchs and Second Inquisiton had them on the backfoot despite the Sabbat's many defeats. Plus, the Tremere, one of the strongest of Camarilla clans, was temporarily decapitated and disorganized.<br /> <br /> It's a crazy time.<br /> <br /> <img src=\"https://i.imgur.com/jHfd6xe.jpg\" class=\"bbcode-attachment bbcode-attachment--lightbox js-lightbox\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" itemprop=\"image\" loading=\"lazy\"/><br /> <br /> For the Lasombra, that means that there was a power vacuum in need of exploitation. The Lasombra could bring all of their financial holdings and much of their mortal influence with them and the Assamites would be right there for forging new alliances. Never would there be a better time to join and not have the full sum of the Camarilla pressure them to conform or bend the knee.<br /> <br /> The trick, of course, is making the Camarilla think the Lasombra are the ones in a state of weakness. The Lasombra had to look like refugees from the Sabbat and able to conform to ridiculous terms that the Ventrue would impose on them. Except the Lasombra are too smart for this and managed to get terms that would only aid them in the long rum.<br /> <br /> The &quot;kill an older Sabbat vampire to get membership&quot; is the perfect sort of Lasombra trap after all since the Camarilla think its the kind of thing that will leave the Lasombra crippled. However, the Lasombra were going to have to murder a bunch of their Elders (and other Clan's) Elders on their way out anyway. They are also a clan that has no value on loyalty and if a Elder can't protect themselves then they don't deserve their blood.<br /> <br /> Part of what I also like about the Lasombra defection is it increases the menace of the Camarilla. You have a bunch of psychopathic shadow wielders now propping up the Ivory Tower and that makes for better Anarch games.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Author of <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Cthulhu-Armageddon-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01KUOM7SI/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982844&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Cthulhu+Armageddon\" target=\"_blank\">Cthulhu Armageddon</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Teenage-Weredeer-Bright-Falls-Mysteries-ebook/dp/B075TTN2FN/ref=sr_1_2?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982717&amp;sr=1-2&amp;keywords=Weredeer#customerReviews\" target=\"_blank\">I was a Teenage Weredeer</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Straight-Outta-Fangton-Comedic-Vampire-ebook/dp/B01KNHICCC/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982774&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Straight+Outta+Fangton\" target=\"_blank\">Straight Outta Fangton</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Lucifers-Star-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01MDM9MCT/ref=mt_kindle?_encoding=UTF8&amp;me=&amp;qid=\" target=\"_blank\">Lucifer's Star</a>, </i>and the <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Rules-Supervillainy-Saga-Book-ebook/dp/B07MB89S33/\" target=\"_blank\">Supervillainy Saga</a>.</i><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":12002,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","user":"CTPhipps","date":". 06-21-2021, 06:43 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","name":"CTPhipps","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12002_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13933"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-06-21T05:06:05-07:00","id":1453025,"title":"","content":"That entire scenario is based on taking the most important ritual of the pre-V5 Sabbat and burning it out of existence.<br /> <br /> The Sabbat doesn't work without the Vaulderie and the Viniculum If the Lasombra can just all snap their fingers and break the Viniculum whenever they want, than they'd have long since been able to turn the Sabbat into the mindless puppets where all the other Sabbat are ready to die for the Lasombra, but the Lasombra no longer have to reciprocate.<br /> <br /> Either dumping the Sabbat en mass doesn't make sense because the Viniculum would stop them, or it doesn't make sense because it's giving up on a Sect that's effectively blood blood to the Clan without realizing it.<br /> <br /> The Reno vs. Las Vegas analogy is kinda funny in this regard: if you asked anyone that actually lives in Nevada if all else being equal would they rather live in Reno or Vegas, Reno wins by a landslide. Unless you actually like living in a tourist trap, there's nothing about Vegas that's better than Reno. Reno has a higher standard of living (higher median income and lower cost of living), its younger on average which attracts a more vibrate cultural scene, etc. Reno is more resilient. It has a diverse economy that can take a hit to one sector. Vegas doesn't exist without tourists. Without the money the glitz and glamour bring in, Vegas would disappear back into the sand. Reno might be smaller, but it's better for it in the long run. Vegas is basically a giant legal Ponzi scheme waiting to come crashing down someday. Which feels like a great idea of what the Sabbat vs. Camarilla should look like... but not a great example of why the Lasombra would dump the Sabbat.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-06-21T06:02:54-07:00","id":1453029,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Heavy Arms</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1443592-the-official-v5-vs-v20-thread?p=1453025#post1453025\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">That entire scenario is based on taking the most important ritual of the pre-V5 Sabbat and burning it out of existence.<br /> <br /> The Sabbat doesn't work without the Vaulderie and the Viniculum If the Lasombra can just all snap their fingers and break the Viniculum whenever they want, than they'd have long since been able to turn the Sabbat into the mindless puppets where all the other Sabbat are ready to die for the Lasombra, but the Lasombra no longer have to reciprocate.<br /> <br /> Either dumping the Sabbat en mass doesn't make sense because the Viniculum would stop them, or it doesn't make sense because it's giving up on a Sect that's effectively blood blood to the Clan without realizing it.</div> </div> </div> </div>Speaking as someone who loves the Sabbat:<br /> <br /> * The Sabbat Civil Wars<br /> * The Sabbat Infernalist problem<br /> * The Sabbat defection of Milan to the Camairlla<br /> * Monomancy<br /> <br /> The Sabbat fight all the time and the Vaulderie doesn't prevent it.<br /> <br /> It also doesn't have some weird, &quot;But they fight as long as they're working toward the Sabbat's goals.&quot;<br /> <br /> <img src=\"https://cpb-us-w2.wpmucdn.com/sites.gatech.edu/dist/0/249/files/2019/09/thats-not-how-it-works-1.jpg\" class=\"bbcode-attachment bbcode-attachment--lightbox js-lightbox\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" itemprop=\"image\" loading=\"lazy\"/><br /> <br /> The Vinculum it should be remembered DOES NOT MAKE YOU LOYAL TO THE SABBAT. It does not guarantee you want to protect the sect, it does instill within you a desire to obey the Code of Milan, it does not make you loyal to your superior's will.<br /> <br /> It makes you loyal to your PACKMATES and anyone you have shared with at some point during a big Crusade. If your packmates hate the Sabbat, YOU hate the Sabbat because the Sabbat is too complicated a political-economic-religious model for the Junior Mint Blood Bond to affect.<br /> <br /> It has done very little to bring down infighting and if it doesn't make you more loyal to the sect, I'm not sure what makes the Lasombra decision any less likely.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Author of <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Cthulhu-Armageddon-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01KUOM7SI/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982844&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Cthulhu+Armageddon\" target=\"_blank\">Cthulhu Armageddon</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Teenage-Weredeer-Bright-Falls-Mysteries-ebook/dp/B075TTN2FN/ref=sr_1_2?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982717&amp;sr=1-2&amp;keywords=Weredeer#customerReviews\" target=\"_blank\">I was a Teenage Weredeer</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Straight-Outta-Fangton-Comedic-Vampire-ebook/dp/B01KNHICCC/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982774&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Straight+Outta+Fangton\" target=\"_blank\">Straight Outta Fangton</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Lucifers-Star-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01MDM9MCT/ref=mt_kindle?_encoding=UTF8&amp;me=&amp;qid=\" target=\"_blank\">Lucifer's Star</a>, </i>and the <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Rules-Supervillainy-Saga-Book-ebook/dp/B07MB89S33/\" target=\"_blank\">Supervillainy Saga</a>.</i><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":12002,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","user":"CTPhipps","date":". 06-21-2021, 09:05 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","name":"CTPhipps","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12002_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13933"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-06-21T06:23:04-07:00","id":1453032,"title":"","content":"the lasombra joining the cam isn't the issue so much as how the lasombra joined the cam. if they actually gave the lasombra a decent deal instead of the shit they got it might've worked.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0