82774&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Straight+Outta+Fangton\" target=\"_blank\">Straight Outta Fangton</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Lucifers-Star-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01MDM9MCT/ref=mt_kindle?_encoding=UTF8&amp;me=&amp;qid=\" target=\"_blank\">Lucifer's Star</a>, </i>and the <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Rules-Supervillainy-Saga-Book-ebook/dp/B07MB89S33/\" target=\"_blank\">Supervillainy Saga</a>.</i><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","name":"CTPhipps","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12002_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13933"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-06-21T08:21:05-07:00","id":1453039,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CTPhipps</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1443592-the-official-v5-vs-v20-thread?p=1453035#post1453035\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> What's the bad part of the deal?</div> </div> </div> </div>If the previous dozen plus explanations in various threads haven't been able to explain it to you, then why would would anyone believe another attempt at the same would result in a different outcome?<br /> <br /> You ask us to waste our time acting as an insane person because you are so rooted in your own beliefs and ideas that God himself could not budge you from your conviction in your assertions.<br /> <br /> Its pretty plain from the many threads on this forum and which comments receive many likes vs. those who receive virtually none that your ideas are completely out of step with the majority of the readership on this forum (regardless of whatever the majority might actually be across the broader internet, those people who might agree with your sentiments are not here on this forum and those that are here find your explanations and arguments unconvincing).","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":9}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1328-chris24601","name":"Chris24601","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"520"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-06-21T08:50:08-07:00","id":1453042,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Chris24601</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1443592-the-official-v5-vs-v20-thread?p=1453039#post1453039\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">If the previous dozen plus explanations in various threads haven't been able to explain it to you, then why would would anyone believe another attempt at the same would result in a different outcome?</div> </div> </div> </div>At the risk of undermining your statement, I've been arguing why it's a good deal a very long time including the above two posts so I am curious why you bring it up in a discussion thread if you are not interested in discussion.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> You ask us to waste our time acting as an insane person because you are so rooted in your own beliefs and ideas that God himself could not budge you from your conviction in your assertions. </div> </div> </div>Not an attitude conducive for this forum or thread.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Its pretty plain from the many threads on this forum and which comments receive many likes vs. those who receive virtually none that your ideas are completely out of step with the majority of the readership on this forum (regardless of whatever the majority might actually be across the broader internet, those people who might agree with your sentiments are not here on this forum and those that are here find your explanations and arguments unconvincing). </div> </div> </div>This is not a popularity contest. It is not a forum about scoring points against fellow posters. It is a place where fans of a game are to share their love of a subject and broaden their ability to tell stories as well as appreciate the World of Darkness IP. We're supposed to be having threads discussing vampire because we like it and talking to fellow posters give alternative views on the subject.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Author of <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Cthulhu-Armageddon-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01KUOM7SI/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982844&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Cthulhu+Armageddon\" target=\"_blank\">Cthulhu Armageddon</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Teenage-Weredeer-Bright-Falls-Mysteries-ebook/dp/B075TTN2FN/ref=sr_1_2?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982717&amp;sr=1-2&amp;keywords=Weredeer#customerReviews\" target=\"_blank\">I was a Teenage Weredeer</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Straight-Outta-Fangton-Comedic-Vampire-ebook/dp/B01KNHICCC/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982774&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Straight+Outta+Fangton\" target=\"_blank\">Straight Outta Fangton</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Lucifers-Star-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01MDM9MCT/ref=mt_kindle?_encoding=UTF8&amp;me=&amp;qid=\" target=\"_blank\">Lucifer's Star</a>, </i>and the <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Rules-Supervillainy-Saga-Book-ebook/dp/B07MB89S33/\" target=\"_blank\">Supervillainy Saga</a>.</i><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":12002,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","user":"CTPhipps","date":". 06-21-2021, 11:52 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","name":"CTPhipps","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12002_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13933"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-06-21T09:59:20-07:00","id":1453048,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Chris24601</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1443592-the-official-v5-vs-v20-thread?p=1453039#post1453039\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">If the previous dozen plus explanations in various threads haven't been able to explain it to you, then why would would anyone believe another attempt at the same would result in a different outcome?<br /> <br /> You ask us to waste our time acting as an insane person because you are so rooted in your own beliefs and ideas that God himself could not budge you from your conviction in your assertions.<br /> <br /> Its pretty plain from the many threads on this forum and which comments receive many likes vs. those who receive virtually none that your ideas are completely out of step with the majority of the readership on this forum (regardless of whatever the majority might actually be across the broader internet, those people who might agree with your sentiments are not here on this forum and those that are here find your explanations and arguments unconvincing).</div> </div> </div> </div>Just going to +1 the idea that CTPhipps disagreeing with you lot is not a symptom of insanity. I don't agree with everything they say, but your inability to see things from their perspective doesn't warrant dismissing their entire viewpoint as insanity. I don't think the Lasombra Defection is necessarily heresy/madness. Of course, if you really think that truth is just a popularity contest, then one vote doesn't change things. Just think that maybe you should consider that this isn't just a super-obvious anyone-who-disagrees-with-me-must-be-crazy-or-acting-in-bad-faith sort of thing? It's a story, and different kinds of people like different kinds of stories, and different kinds of people are going to see &quot;plot holes&quot; in different places. That's why arguments about riding the Eagles to Mordor are still a thing.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25886-kharnov","name":"Kharnov","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2020"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"683"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-06-21T11:49:15-07:00","id":1453060,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Kharnov</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1443592-the-official-v5-vs-v20-thread?p=1453048#post1453048\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Just going to +1 the idea that CTPhipps disagreeing with you lot is not a symptom of insanity.</div> </div> </div> </div>I never said it was.<br /> <br /> I said that believing that repeating the same arguments ad nauseum will change anyone\u2019s mind is insanity.<br /> <br /> We already HAD the discussion on the Lasombra back when the Chicago book came out and many times since. Phipps already knows all the arguments for why we find his position unconvincing and what he\u2019s posted here is just the same hash reheated.<br /> <br /> There\u2019s no point to repeating the same arguments when no one is going to change their minds. Doing the same thing and expecting a different outcome is the definition of insanity.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1328-chris24601","name":"Chris24601","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"520"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-06-21T11:53:17-07:00","id":1453062,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Chris24601</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1443592-the-official-v5-vs-v20-thread?p=1453060#post1453060\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I never said it was.<br /> <br /> I said that believing that repeating the same arguments ad nauseum will change anyone\u2019s mind is insanity.<br /> <br /> We already HAD the discussion on the Lasombra back when the Chicago book came out and many times since. Phipps already knows all the arguments for why we find his position unconvincing and what he\u2019s posted here is just the same hash reheated.<br /> <br /> There\u2019s no point to repeating the same arguments when no one is going to change their minds. Doing the same thing and expecting a different outcome is the definition of insanity.</div> </div> </div> </div>Have you considered that maybe there will be new posters on this forum or in this thread with new insights?<br /> <br /> Or that people may like debating these issues?<br /> <br /> I certainly want to hear people's thoughts.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Author of <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Cthulhu-Armageddon-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01KUOM7SI/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982844&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Cthulhu+Armageddon\" target=\"_blank\">Cthulhu Armageddon</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Teenage-Weredeer-Bright-Falls-Mysteries-ebook/dp/B075TTN2FN/ref=sr_1_2?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982717&amp;sr=1-2&amp;keywords=Weredeer#customerReviews\" target=\"_blank\">I was a Teenage Weredeer</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Straight-Outta-Fangton-Comedic-Vampire-ebook/dp/B01KNHICCC/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982774&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Straight+Outta+Fangton\" target=\"_blank\">Straight Outta Fangton</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Lucifers-Star-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01MDM9MCT/ref=mt_kindle?_encoding=UTF8&amp;me=&amp;qid=\" target=\"_blank\">Lucifer's Star</a>, </i>and the <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Rules-Supervillainy-Saga-Book-ebook/dp/B07MB89S33/\" target=\"_blank\">Supervillainy Saga</a>.</i><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":12002,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","user":"CTPhipps","date":". 06-21-2021, 02:56 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","name":"CTPhipps","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12002_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13933"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-06-21T11:59:36-07:00","id":1453064,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CTPhipps</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1443592-the-official-v5-vs-v20-thread?p=1453029#post1453029\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The Sabbat fight all the time and the Vaulderie doesn't prevent it.</div> </div> </div> </div>It does, however, contain it, and allow the Sabbat leadership to ensure it doesn't tear the Sect apart.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> ...it does not make you loyal to your superior's will. </div> </div> </div>It certainly should have you loyal to your priest, your ductus, and the local leadership in your default home area (depending on how big it is, and thus how many of them there are). At a minimum the Bishop or Archbishop and their pack should be holding Vaulderies with the packs in their domain often enough that those packs are loyal to them.<br /> <br /> So my point remains, most Lasombra in the Sabbat are yes not bound to the Sect itself, but leaving the Sabbat still means leaving their pack and betraying at least one other pack they've shared blood with. Something that the Viniculum would absolutely interfere with. There's been some Lasombra in the Cam already in every edition, it's not like defections can't happen. But a mass defection that doesn't explain how the Viniculum doesn't impede it doesn't scan.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> It has done very little to bring down infighting and if it doesn't make you more loyal to the sect, I'm not sure what makes the Lasombra decision any less likely. </div> </div> </div>Because the Lasombra aren't a monolith where they just vote on the matter and then they're all cool with the decision even if it's 50%+1.<br /> <br /> As I regularly harp on regarding V5 (and this in the V5 vs. V20 thread, not the Sabbat thread), execution is one of V5's biggest stumbling points. There are lots of ways you could have achieved increased Lasombra presence in the Cam without incredibly heavy handed and sloppy narrative execution of the idea. Even a relatively &quot;cheap&quot; narrative trick like using the Beckoning to cause a ripple in the blood that unevenly and quasi-randomly reduces the strength of the Viniculum could be spun into some interesting high level plot hooks: like say the the Lasombra, Brujah, Ventrue, Salubri, Ravnos, and Harbringers of Skulls are the Sabbat Clans/Bloodlines that seem to be the ones most &quot;freed&quot; by the Beckoning. This doubles up on making faction switches a bit more sensible (since the Harbringers went to the Hecata for some reason), and creates some cool ideas to explore on why Clans that probably lost their Antedeluvian in some form are the ones that have their Viniculum ratings reduced.<br /> <br /> Ignoring the Viniculum is giving up on both helping to bridge edition lore, and giving up on potential plot hooks for characters to explore.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CTPhipps</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1443592-the-official-v5-vs-v20-thread?p=1453042#post1453042\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">At the risk of undermining your statement, I've been arguing why it's a good deal a very long time including the above two posts so I am curious why you bring it up in a discussion thread if you are not interested in discussion.</div> </div> </div> </div>It's very possible to be interested in discussion, and feel frustrated because you don't feel like the other side is interested in discussion as much as talking at you.<br /> <br /> This is especially the case when it feels like you've had the same discussion multiple times, and it seems like even if you feel like you communicated your side of things well, the other side seems to go back to a position where the previous discussions never happened instead of new discussion acknowledging discussions of the past.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Not an attitude conducive for this forum or thread. </div> </div> </div>I don't feel attempts at &quot;pithy&quot; memes is all that conducive to discussions myself. I'm not here to talk to Meme-Morpheus, or be swayed by being compared to Meme-Jesse being chastised by Meme-Walter.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> This is not a popularity contest. </div> </div> </div>Absolutely. And very fortunately so for me!<br /> <br /> That said, it is also a form of feedback. As they say, it's important to read the room. If I'm making an argument, however much I feel I'm right, or saying something important, if I'm getting 0-2 likes, and the main person debating me is getting 5+ likes? I could still be right, but clearly I'm not communicating it successfully enough to a significant number of people participating in/following the thread.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> We're supposed to be having threads discussing vampire because we like it and talking to fellow posters give alternative views on the subject. </div> </div> </div>Allow me to try to rephrase Chris's statement in a less bombastic fashion to this point: the last few posts makes it feel like you want people that don't like the changes made with the Lasombra to have to listen to other opinions, but people that don't have a problem with it/like how it was handled don't have to really pay attention to the other side.<br /> <br /> It makes it feel like an uneven playing field where one side has to do more emotional work to engage than the other, rather than an even place for people to speak their thoughts.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-06-21T12:37:17-07:00","id":1453067,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Heavy Arms</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1443592-the-official-v5-vs-v20-thread?p=1453064#post1453064\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I don't feel attempts at &quot;pithy&quot; memes is all that conducive to discussions myself. I'm not here to talk to Meme-Morpheus, or be swayed by being compared to Meme-Jesse being chastised by Meme-Walter.</div> </div> </div> </div>So noted.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Absolutely. And very fortunately so for me!<br /> <br /> That said, it is also a form of feedback. As they say, it's important to read the room. If I'm making an argument, however much I feel I'm right, or saying something important, if I'm getting 0-2 likes, and the main person debating me is getting 5+ likes? I could still be right, but clearly I'm not communicating it successfully enough to a significant number of people participating in/following the thread. </div> </div> </div>Perhaps, on the other hand I actually don't believe in &quot;right&quot; answers regarding the subject because I tend to take the view that everyone's World of Darkness is different. Currently, V5 is canon and in talking about the subject there is no answer other than, &quot;this is the way it is.&quot; That isn't true for people who are playing V20 or homebrewed campaigns, though, and those are automatically the &quot;correct&quot; ones at your table because Rule Zero is the most important one. <br /> The Storyetller is always right and really no one can tell you what is BETTER for your games. Ergo, the arguments here are not actually arguments over what is correct because we have objective answers to that (whatever the rulebook says) but that doesn't mean it's BETTER for your table. This is basically a discussion of art and preference, IMHO.<br /> <br /> People have strong feelings on the subject regarding the changes of V5, Revised, and other subjects but there's no right answer. There's only the town hall, so to speak, of getting up and talk about what you like or don't like or why.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Allow me to try to rephrase Chris's statement in a less bombastic fashion to this point: the last few posts makes it feel like you want people that don't like the changes made with the Lasombra to have to listen to other opinions, but people that don't have a problem with it/like how it was handled don't have to really pay attention to the other side.<br /> <br /> It makes it feel like an uneven playing field where one side has to do more emotional work to engage than the other, rather than an even place for people to speak their thoughts. </div> </div> </div>I suppose I am going at it from the perspective that the debate is not meant to be arduous. The debate is meant to fun by itself. You listen to people liking or disliking the subject of the Lasombra defection as well as your points because you like discussing it not because you want to win or lose. The journey is the destination.<br /> <br /> The point is not to persuade (albeit that's fun) but to give your perspective and maybe some ideas to enrich their game or other posters or vice versa.<br /> <br /> I know plenty of people for example who have the Second Inquisition in their V20 games but highly modified. Ditto the Gehenna Crusade or Convention of Thorns. Before I was here, I used to be a regular on Candlekeep and there were many discussions of the various Editions changes to the Realms and which were right or wrong.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Author of <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Cthulhu-Armageddon-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01KUOM7SI/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982844&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Cthulhu+Armageddon\" target=\"_blank\">Cthulhu Armageddon</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Teenage-Weredeer-Bright-Falls-Mysteries-ebook/dp/B075TTN2FN/ref=sr_1_2?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982717&amp;sr=1-2&amp;keywords=Weredeer#customerReviews\" target=\"_blank\">I was a Teenage Weredeer</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Straight-Outta-Fangton-Comedic-Vampire-ebook/dp/B01KNHICCC/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982774&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Straight+Outta+Fangton\" target=\"_blank\">Straight Outta Fangton</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Lucifers-Star-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01MDM9MCT/ref=mt_kindle?_encoding=UTF8&amp;me=&amp;qid=\" target=\"_blank\">Lucifer's Star</a>, </i>and the <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Rules-Supervillainy-Saga-Book-ebook/dp/B07MB89S33/\" target=\"_blank\">Supervillainy Saga</a>.</i><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","name":"CTPhipps","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12002_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13933"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-06-21T13:48:23-07:00","id":1453075,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CTPhipps</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1443592-the-official-v5-vs-v20-thread?p=1453062#post1453062\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Have you considered that maybe there will be new posters on this forum or in this thread with new insights?<br /> <br /> Or that people may like debating these issues?<br /> <br /> I certainly want to hear people's thoughts.</div> </div> </div> </div>with others i'd gladly try to have a discussion,just not with you phipps, i've given up on you","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25992-archderd","name":"archderd","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25992_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2020"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"205"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-06-21T14:17:34-07:00","id":1453081,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Chris24601</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1443592-the-official-v5-vs-v20-thread?p=1453060#post1453060\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I never said it was.<br /> <br /> I said that believing that repeating the same arguments ad nauseum will change anyone\u2019s mind is insanity.<br /> <br /> We already HAD the discussion on the Lasombra back when the Chicago book came out and many times since. Phipps already knows all the arguments for why we find his position unconvincing and what he\u2019s posted here is just the same hash reheated.<br /> <br /> There\u2019s no point to repeating the same arguments when no one is going to change their minds. Doing the same thing and expecting a different outcome is the definition of insanity.</div> </div> </div> </div>That's fair. I was still waking up and I misread it, my mistake. And that's something I agree with you on, I just didn't say it earlier because I didn't want to come across as ordering people to move on. But yeah, if people are just talking past each other over irreconcilable differences of opinion, moving on probably is a good idea. Some people might enjoy the back-and-forth, but it does seem to clearly be frustrating some people.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25886-kharnov","name":"Kharnov","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2020"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"683"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-06-21T15:24:16-07:00","id":1453085,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>archderd</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1443592-the-official-v5-vs-v20-thread?p=1453075#post1453075\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">with others i'd gladly try to have a discussion,just not with you phipps, i've given up on you</div> </div> </div> </div>Your loss.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Author of <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Cthulhu-Armageddon-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01KUOM7SI/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982844&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Cthulhu+Armageddon\" target=\"_blank\">Cthulhu Armageddon</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Teenage-Weredeer-Bright-Falls-Mysteries-ebook/dp/B075TTN2FN/ref=sr_1_2?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982717&amp;sr=1-2&amp;keywords=Weredeer#customerReviews\" target=\"_blank\">I was a Teenage Weredeer</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Straight-Outta-Fangton-Comedic-Vampire-ebook/dp/B01KNHICCC/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982774&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Straight+Outta+Fangton\" target=\"_blank\">Straight Outta Fangton</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Lucifers-Star-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01MDM9MCT/ref=mt_kindle?_encoding=UTF8&amp;me=&amp;qid=\" target=\"_blank\">Lucifer's Star</a>, </i>and the <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Rules-Supervillainy-Saga-Book-ebook/dp/B07MB89S33/\" target=\"_blank\">Supervillainy Saga</a>.</i><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","name":"CTPhipps","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12002_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13933"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-06-21T18:05:01-07:00","id":1453095,"title":"","content":"To me whether you can create a plausible excuse for the Lasombra defection is irrelevant. This is a fantasy setting. You can come up with a plausible reason for the Sabbat to all grow rocket feet and fly to Mars if you try hard enough in such a setting. What's more important to me is that I love the Sabbat, and so don't care what explanation you come up with for destroying them. I don't want them destroyed, and won't give you any more of my money because you destroyed them.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3598-cajunkhan","name":"CajunKhan","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3598_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1700"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-06-21T20:47:11-07:00","id":1453109,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CajunKhan</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1443592-the-official-v5-vs-v20-thread?p=1453095#post1453095\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"> To me whether you can create a plausible excuse for the Lasombra defection is irrelevant. This is a fantasy setting. You can come up with a plausible reason for the Sabbat to all grow rocket feet and fly to Mars if you try hard enough in such a setting. What's more important to me is that I love the Sabbat, and so don't care what explanation you come up with for destroying them. I don't want them destroyed, and won't give you any more of my money because you destroyed them.</div> </div> </div> </div>Except a lot of this is actually in CHICAGO BY NIGHT. They have a section about why they have accepted this and joined the Camarilla specifically. It's not me speculating. It's part of canon.<br /> <br /> The Lasombra joining the Camarilla was a suggestion made by the Gentleman Gamer and it was his proposal they adopted.<br /> <br /> I.e. heavily canon driven.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Author of <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Cthulhu-Armageddon-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01KUOM7SI/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982844&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Cthulhu+Armageddon\" target=\"_blank\">Cthulhu Armageddon</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Teenage-Weredeer-Bright-Falls-Mysteries-ebook/dp/B075TTN2FN/ref=sr_1_2?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982717&amp;sr=1-2&amp;keywords=Weredeer#customerReviews\" target=\"_blank\">I was a Teenage Weredeer</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Straight-Outta-Fangton-Comedic-Vampire-ebook/dp/B01KNHICCC/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982774&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Straight+Outta+Fangton\" target=\"_blank\">Straight Outta Fangton</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Lucifers-Star-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01MDM9MCT/ref=mt_kindle?_encoding=UTF8&amp;me=&amp;qid=\" target=\"_blank\">Lucifer's Star</a>, </i>and the <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Rules-Supervillainy-Saga-Book-ebook/dp/B07MB89S33/\" target=\"_blank\">Supervillainy Saga</a>.</i><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","name":"CTPhipps","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12002_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13933"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-06-21T20:51:17-07:00","id":1453110,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CTPhipps</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1443592-the-official-v5-vs-v20-thread?p=1453109#post1453109\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Except a lot of this is actually in CHICAGO BY NIGHT. They have a section about why they have accepted this and joined the Camarilla specifically. It's not me speculating. It's part of canon.<br /> <br /> The Lasombra joining the Camarilla was a suggestion made by the Gentleman Gamer and it was his proposal they adopted.<br /> <br /> I.e. heavily canon driven.</div> </div> </div> </div>You're not listening. I'm not debating whether it is plausible or canon or anything like that. I'm saying I don't care. You could come up with an explanation so elegant and plausible that God himself comes down from the Heavens and bows before you in sheer awe of how elegant and plausible your explanation was and I still won't care. I love the Sabbat. I want the Sabbat to remain as it was. Anything you do that destroys that I will oppose.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3598-cajunkhan","name":"CajunKhan","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3598_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1700"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-06-21T23:32:21-07:00","id":1453111,"title":"","content":"If we're talking personal tastes, here's my personal take--my &quot;headcanon&quot; if you will, which is canon at my table. I run a V20 game set in 2020 (began in 2019), mixing a couple ideas from various novels, BJD and V5.<br /> <br /> <div style=\"margin: 5px 20px 5px 20px;\"> <div style=\"margin-bottom:2px; font-size: 80%;\"> <input type=\"button\" value=\"Spoiler\" style=\"width:45px;font-size:10px;margin:0px;padding:0px;\" onClick=\"if (this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display != '') { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = ''; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Hide'; } else { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = 'none'; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Show'; }\" /> </div> <div style=\" margin: 0px; padding: 6px; border: 3px groove blue; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px; -webkit-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); -moz-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75);\"> <div style=\"display: none;\"><div style=\"background: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.8); padding: 6px; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px;\"><br /> -The years between 1997 and 2007 are remembered as &quot;The Gehenna Scare.&quot; Rise in Thinblood Population and the appearance of the <a href=\"https://whitewolf.fandom.com/wiki/Blood_Curse_(VTM)\" target=\"_blank\">Blood Curse</a> in cities all over the world, combined with the Week of Nightmares/appearance of the Red Star in 1999, sent vampires all over the world into a panic. My take on the Blood Curse is closer to <a href=\"https://whitewolf.fandom.com/wiki/Withering\" target=\"_blank\">the Withering</a> from the Gehenna novels, elders experiencing a loss of potency and feeding ability only ameliorated by feeding on Thinbloods or younger kindred. While many kindred died directly or indirectly because of this supernatural plague, it eventually petered out, perhaps due to magical intervention or the pandemic simply taking its course.<br /> <br /> -Following incursions by the <i>Wan Kuei</i> in L.A (1997) and San Francisco (1999), defection of the Baron of San Diego and solidification of Praxis by Sebastien LaCroix, the Anarch Free State of Southern California seemed finished. A whirlwind of spectacular events remembered as &quot;the Antediluvian Hoax&quot; or &quot;Jack's Prank,&quot; resulted in the death of LaCroix, ouster of the <i>Wan Kuei</i> from Los Angeles (their Mandrinate remains in San Francisco and its &quot;puppet princedom&quot; of San Jose, <i>contra</i> the Free State of Oakland), the establishment of Jenna Cross' &quot;Thin-Blood Empire,&quot; (a support/mutual defense network for the renamed Duskborn) and the Free State's miraculous resurrection in 2004.<br /> <br /> -Convinced that the return of Caine and final judgement of all Kindred was nigh, the Council of Seven called together almost all the senior members of Clan Tremere, gathering in the Great Chantry beneath Vienna in 2006. In that year they attempted the Ritual of the Red Sign, a rite researched and prepared to transform the seniormost warlocks back into living mortals. However, in their terror the Council enacted the ritual without full preparation, resulting in a backlash of energy which destroyed the Great Chantry (and collapsed much of the underground environs beneath the city of Vienna). The true story of this disaster and the Council's disappearance remains mysterious to most. Around the same time as this disaster Carna, the Regent of Milwaukee, finishes translating the legendary <i>Book of the Grave-War</i>, breaking her Blood Bond to the Pyramid. Unaware of the shakeup and expecting reprisal, Carna leads her followers to the West Coast and the establishment of an independent House. <br /> <br /> -In 2012 a great conclave was held in Prague, with some of the Camarilla's greatest heavyweights present. Fed up with the hypocrisy of his erstwhile employers and aware of the measures taken by Hardstadt to survive the winnowing, Archon Theo Bell and his coterie raid the conclave and publicly assassinate Hardestadt---the blow is commemorated as &quot;the Decapitation of Prague.&quot; Following Bell's example, Brujah all over the world renounce the Camarilla, reigniting the War of Ages into an open conflict not seen since the Chicago Anarch Massacre of 1968. While the Anarchs virtually as a whole now reject the Camarilla's authority, the sects find a truce in a few cities. In following years The Movement is bolstered by the emergence of a splinter group of &quot;ecumenical&quot; young Setites calling themselves the Ministry, and a group of Tremere branding themselves House Ipsissimus. <br /> <br /> -Also in 2012, London falls to a well-organized purge conducted by a body of cooperating government entities. Ann Bowesley and apparently Mithras himself (in the inconveniently weak body of Monte Coven) apparently fall victim to the Vampire Hunters, though the Living God's cult refuses to believe he is gone. A few years prior Las Vegas was similarly scoured, but curiously it remains the only city in the New World to be so purged. Such operations are more frequent in Europe and it is now thought Vienna was such a case; an assumption the surviving Tremere leadership sees no need to correct. This dangerously well-informed alliance of agencies and intelligence services is called a New or Second Inquisition by some elders, and the Camarilla enacts a policy of crackdown on the errant use of trackable social media within its ranks.<br /> <br /> -In 2016, Al Ashrad and Tegyrius lead a deposition of the so-called Schismatics before the Camarilla and seek admittance on behalf of their Clan. Reeling from the loss of first the Gangrel and now the rebellious Brujah, the Camarilla overrides the protests of Clan Tremere--now virtually led by Karl Schrekt---and grants the Schismatics permission to settle in cities under their aegis.<br /> <br /> -Ideas not used: The Beckoning/Gehenna Crusade, the Church of Caine. Despite the Gehenna Scare, the Camarilla remains a &quot;secular&quot; organization which officially categorizes Noddism as no more than a collection of dangerous myths. The Sabbat remains a potent force, with heavy fighting flaring up on the East Coast in the past couple of years---Atlanta, Baltimore and New York City (recently hard won by the Ivory Tower in the siege of 1999-2000) are epicenters of the Sect War. This has given the Anarchs' perhaps optimistic rebellion on the West Coast some breathing room. Washington D.C. maintains an enforced neutrality under an apparently-revived Marcus Vitel, thought killed by Theo Bell and <i>Dux Bellorum</i> Jan Pieterzoon (currently coordinating the sect war from his New York headquarters). The story goes that Vitel had somehow got his tentacles on the fabled nuclear football and intended to circumvent the Judgement of Caine by triggering WWIII, only stopped by Bell and Pieterzoon's unlikely Buddy Cop heroics. Bell and Pieterzoon maintain they killed the ancient but refuse to confirm or deny this silly story. Other independent domains of North America are: Vancouver, B.C., isolated by distance and its massive Lupine population; New Orleans, supposedly controlled by a coalition of &quot;Clans of Death&quot;; and perhaps Vegas, ostensibly reborn as a Free State but under the sway of a great many Followers of Set.</div></div> </div> </div><br /> <br /> Not much of this is really relevant to the substance of my Chronicle, which takes place in the Pacific Northwest and far from the great politics of moment. But having absorbed so much Vampire lore over the past few years it was inevitable my preferences would coalesce into a rough big picture.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":26710,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26710-ventrue-busboy","user":"Ventrue Busboy","date":". 06-22-2021, 03:38 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26710-ventrue-busboy","name":"Ventrue Busboy","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar26710_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"41"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-06-22T04:48:00-07:00","id":1453136,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CajunKhan</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1443592-the-official-v5-vs-v20-thread?p=1453110#post1453110\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> You're not listening. I'm not debating whether it is plausible or canon or anything like that. I'm saying I don't care. You could come up with an explanation so elegant and plausible that God himself comes down from the Heavens and bows before you in sheer awe of how elegant and plausible your explanation was and I still won't care. I love the Sabbat. I want the Sabbat to remain as it was. Anything you do that destroys that I will oppose.</div> </div> </div> </div>And that's your prerogative. No one is going to come to your house and force you to update the Sabbat to V5.<br /> <br /> It's just something that will come up in a thread devoted to discussing the benefits and downfalls of V5 vs. V20.<br /> <br /> If you don't want to hear and discuss people discussing the subject, this is not the thread for you.<br /> <br /> And I'm not sure I get the objection because I LOVE hearing different viewpoints and discussing the ups and downs of it. It makes me improve my world of darkness by addressing issues and incorporating problems people have in and out of universe.<br /> <br /> My Tremere are often benefited by <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25794-mywifeisscary\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar25794_2.png');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"25794\" data-vbnamecard=\"25794\">MyWifeIsScary</a> and <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25011-taggie\" style=\"background-image:url('data:image/svg+xml;base64,');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"25011\" data-vbnamecard=\"25011\">Taggie</a>'s view have influenced some of my Sabbat internal conflicts. <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar617_2.jpeg');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"617\" data-vbnamecard=\"617\">Heavy Arms</a> also has helped me improve my rules.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Author of <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Cthulhu-Armageddon-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01KUOM7SI/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982844&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Cthulhu+Armageddon\" target=\"_blank\">Cthulhu Armageddon</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Teenage-Weredeer-Bright-Falls-Mysteries-ebook/dp/B075TTN2FN/ref=sr_1_2?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982717&amp;sr=1-2&amp;keywords=Weredeer#customerReviews\" target=\"_blank\">I was a Teenage Weredeer</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Straight-Outta-Fangton-Comedic-Vampire-ebook/dp/B01KNHICCC/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982774&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Straight+Outta+Fangton\" target=\"_blank\">Straight Outta Fangton</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Lucifers-Star-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01MDM9MCT/ref=mt_kindle?_encoding=UTF8&amp;me=&amp;qid=\" target=\"_blank\">Lucifer's Star</a>, </i>and the <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Rules-Supervillainy-Saga-Book-ebook/dp/B07MB89S33/\" target=\"_blank\">Supervillainy Saga</a>.</i><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":12002,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","user":"CTPhipps","date":". 06-22-2021, 07:56 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","name":"CTPhipps","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12002_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13933"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-06-22T05:00:51-07:00","id":1453137,"title":"","content":"<b>OPINION: The Sabbat Lasombra will emerge stronger from this</b><br /> <br /> Mind you, I don't think the Sabbat are actually going to change from what has been released by Justin Achilli. The big thing about the Lasombra defection is that it changes the Camarilla but it DOESN'T CHANGE THE SABBAT. The Betrayal of the Lasombra is something that they assumed would be a death blow to the Sabbat but the Sword of Caine has long since slipped out of the<br /> Keeper's fingers.<br /> <br /> <b>How the Lasombra viewed the Sabbat</b>: Useful fools who exist to serve our whims.<br /> <b>How the Sabbat viewed the Lasombra</b>: A bunch of self-absorbed pricks who didn't realize we knew they were cowards and assholes.<br /> <br /> Part of the driving force of the Sabbat's Civil Wars was the repeated attempt to break the hold of the Lasombra (and to a lesser extent the Tzimisce) so that the antitribu could have equal power in the sect. The Anitribu who reject what was the Old Ways of Clans and their traditions. This is why the Sabbat SURVIVE the Lasombra leaving and also why the Lasombra possibly gravely miscalculated.<br /> <br /> First of all, I really do like what CBN said about the fact that only about half the Lasombra defected. Those Lasombra who already have a good thing going like Archbishops, Priscuses, and people who don't put Clan first are going to find that the defection is ludicrous. But more so than that, NOT ALL LASOMBRA BUY INTO THE PATH OF NIGHT.<br /> <br /> There's going to be ones who ARE true believers, who value their Pack over their Clan, and who may even be self-sacrificing or not worship the narcissitic pursuit of power over all. People who aren't on the Path of Night, Path of Power and the Inner Voice, or Low Humanity but maybe the Path of Honorable Accord or Path of Caine.<br /> <br /> These Lasombra have been betrayed by all their fellows just as much as anyone else and are now, themselves, the Antitribu. To know what it is like to be opposed to everything their Elders stand for.<br /> <br /> Just like the Tremere, adversity is going to make the Sabbat stronger because one of their leading sources of inner turmoil is now gone.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Author of <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Cthulhu-Armageddon-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01KUOM7SI/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982844&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Cthulhu+Armageddon\" target=\"_blank\">Cthulhu Armageddon</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Teenage-Weredeer-Bright-Falls-Mysteries-ebook/dp/B075TTN2FN/ref=sr_1_2?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982717&amp;sr=1-2&amp;keywords=Weredeer#customerReviews\" target=\"_blank\">I was a Teenage Weredeer</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Straight-Outta-Fangton-Comedic-Vampire-ebook/dp/B01KNHICCC/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982774&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Straight+Outta+Fangton\" target=\"_blank\">Straight Outta Fangton</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Lucifers-Star-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01MDM9MCT/ref=mt_kindle?_encoding=UTF8&amp;me=&amp;qid=\" target=\"_blank\">Lucifer's Star</a>, </i>and the <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Rules-Supervillainy-Saga-Book-ebook/dp/B07MB89S33/\" target=\"_blank\">Supervillainy Saga</a>.</i><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","name":"CTPhipps","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12002_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13933"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-06-22T05:21:01-07:00","id":1453139,"title":"","content":"All of the changes to the Camarilla range between 'ok' and 'mate what the fuck are you doing'; there's nothing that makes me go &quot;oh great I'm glad they made that change, these people really understand the Camarilla and what makes it tick.&quot; Like, even if they successfully tie everything together with exquisite storytelling, the Camarilla is left in a stage where I think your average person will find them less compelling, Perhaps they benefit from the Sabbat being something the players don't understand at all again, perhaps you personally like the idea of House Carna or enjoy the absolute nonsense of the &quot;Banu Haquim&quot; (Yes, the schismatics are totally going to call themselves that) but these all contribute into undermining the Camarilla identity, while open vampire-religion takes away the nuance and makes them more of a charicature than they really deserve to be. <br /> <br /> Part of the fun of being a Cam Lasombra was being a vainglorious elite forced to lay low, looking after your coterie like you were their mother; self assured but tempered enough to back it up. The V5 changes lasombra into a bunch of little-penis people trying to act like they've got a big one. The weakness is emasculating, your terms and conditions into joining the cam means you've got to suck up like no tomorrow. Consider it from an actual-fucking-lasombra perspective for a moment; You're the bitchboy of the sect whilst you need to &quot;prove&quot; yourself to the sect. A true Lasombra doesn't need to prove shit.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25794-mywifeisscary","name":"MyWifeIsScary","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25794_2.png","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3711"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-06-22T05:55:13-07:00","id":1453142,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MyWifeIsScary</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1443592-the-official-v5-vs-v20-thread?p=1453139#post1453139\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">the absolute nonsense of the &quot;Banu Haquim&quot; (Yes, the schismatics are totally going to call themselves that)</div> </div> </div> </div>Why wouldn't the progeny of Haquim call themselves a name that means children of Haquim? If anything, I've often found it a bit odd that so many of the clans go by names that should be insulting. Nosferatu is a generic word for the undead. Gangrel practically means hobo. Tzimisce is, irrc, the name of some minor, relatively recent by vampire standards, human nobles. Toreador is a bullfighter. Brujah means witch. Wouldn't the Torries call themselves something like the &quot;Children of Arikel&quot;? And wouldn't the Gangrel call themselves the Get of Ennoia or something like that?<br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3598-cajunkhan","name":"CajunKhan","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3598_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1700"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-06-22T06:07:49-07:00","id":1453146,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CajunKhan</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1443592-the-official-v5-vs-v20-thread?p=1453142#post1453142\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Why wouldn't the progeny of Haquim call themselves a name that means children of Haquim? If anything, I've often found it a bit odd that so many of the clans go by names that should be insulting. Nosferatu is a generic word for the undead. Gangrel practically means hobo. Tzimisce is, irrc, the name of some minor, relatively recent by vampire standards, human nobles. Toreador is a bullfighter. Brujah means witch. Wouldn't the Torries call themselves something like the &quot;Children of Arikel&quot;? And wouldn't the Gangrel call themselves the Get of Ennoia or something like that?<br /></div> </div> </div> </div>I dunno, a lot of vampires don't believe in the Antediluvians. They wouldn't call themselves the Children of Ennoia because a good chunk of them believe they're the Children of Odin or just vampires evolved as a predator.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Author of <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Cthulhu-Armageddon-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01KUOM7SI/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982844&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Cthulhu+Armageddon\" target=\"_blank\">Cthulhu Armageddon</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Teenage-Weredeer-Bright-Falls-Mysteries-ebook/dp/B075TTN2FN/ref=sr_1_2?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982717&amp;sr=1-2&amp;keywords=Weredeer#customerReviews\" target=\"_blank\">I was a Teenage Weredeer</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Straight-Outta-Fangton-Comedic-Vampire-ebook/dp/B01KNHICCC/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982774&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Straight+Outta+Fangton\" target=\"_blank\">Straight Outta Fangton</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Lucifers-Star-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01MDM9MCT/ref=mt_kindle?_encoding=UTF8&amp;me=&amp;qid=\" target=\"_blank\">Lucifer's Star</a>, </i>and the <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Rules-Supervillainy-Saga-Book-ebook/dp/B07MB89S33/\" target=\"_blank\">Supervillainy Saga</a>.</i><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","name":"CTPhipps","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12002_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13933"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-06-22T06:48:18-07:00","id":1453150,"title":"","content":"Somehow I suspect making the Catholic-themed Lasombra into the emasculated \u201cbitchboys\u201d of the \u201cevil religious conservatives\u201d was a considered a feature by the developers rather than a bug. V5 isn\u2019t exactly subtle in its politics.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1328-chris24601","name":"Chris24601","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"520"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-06-22T07:00:34-07:00","id":1453152,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CajunKhan</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1443592-the-official-v5-vs-v20-thread?p=1453142#post1453142\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Why wouldn't the progeny of Haquim call themselves a name that means children of Haquim?</div> </div> </div> </div>Mainly because the ones joining the Cam and Anarchs are schismatics who rejected Ur-Shugli\u2019s demands the reject all faiths except the worship of Haqim. The Cam/Anarch members are the Muslims, Copts and other believers who chose to flee rather than give up their faith for worship of Haqim.<br /> <br /> Calling themselves the Banu-Haqim is roughly equivalent to a Christian denomination deciding to name itself \u201cChildren of Satan.\u201d","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1328-chris24601","name":"Chris24601","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"520"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-06-22T07:05:22-07:00","id":1453154,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Chris24601</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1443592-the-official-v5-vs-v20-thread?p=1453150#post1453150\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Somehow I suspect making the Catholic-themed Lasombra into the emasculated \u201cbitchboys\u201d of the \u201cevil religious conservatives\u201d was a considered a feature by the developers rather than a bug. V5 isn\u2019t exactly subtle in its politics.</div> </div> </div> </div>I'm going to react with confusion because the Lasombra haven't been involved with the Catholic Church since the Dark Ages and run a literally Satanist death cult that mocks the Catholic Church.<br /> <br /> They revere Caine because Caine hates God and all of his works.<br /> <br /> I mean, people realize the whole Cardinal and Bishop stuff is meant to be IRONIC, right?<br /> <br /> They're about as Catholic as these guys.<br /> <br /> <img src=\"https://media2.fdncms.com/rochester/imager/u/zoom/2882573/music_feature1-1-416d36582a17a494.jpg\" class=\"bbcode-attachment bbcode-attachment--lightbox js-lightbox\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" itemprop=\"image\" loading=\"lazy\"/>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Author of <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Cthulhu-Armageddon-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01KUOM7SI/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982844&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Cthulhu+Armageddon\" target=\"_blank\">Cthulhu Armageddon</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Teenage-Weredeer-Bright-Falls-Mysteries-ebook/dp/B075TTN2FN/ref=sr_1_2?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982717&amp;sr=1-2&amp;keywords=Weredeer#customerReviews\" target=\"_blank\">I was a Teenage Weredeer</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Straight-Outta-Fangton-Comedic-Vampire-ebook/dp/B01KNHICCC/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982774&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Straight+Outta+Fangton\" target=\"_blank\">Straight Outta Fangton</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Lucifers-Star-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01MDM9MCT/ref=mt_kindle?_encoding=UTF8&amp;me=&amp;qid=\" target=\"_blank\">Lucifer's Star</a>, </i>and the <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Rules-Supervillainy-Saga-Book-ebook/dp/B07MB89S33/\" target=\"_blank\">Supervillainy Saga</a>.</i><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","name":"CTPhipps","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12002_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13933"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-06-22T07:07:56-07:00","id":1453155,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Chris24601</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1443592-the-official-v5-vs-v20-thread?p=1453152#post1453152\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Mainly because the ones joining the Cam and Anarchs are schismatics who rejected Ur-Shugli\u2019s demands the reject all faiths except the worship of Haqim. The Cam/Anarch members are the Muslims, Copts and other believers who chose to flee rather than give up their faith for worship of Haqim.<br /> <br /> Calling themselves the Banu-Haqim is roughly equivalent to a Christian denomination deciding to name itself \u201cChildren of Satan.\u201d</div> </div> </div> </div>Weren't most of them prior to Ur-Shulgi Haqim reverers?<br /> <br /> They just believed Haqim was a servant of Allah because he was teaching them to clean up the whole Caine mess?<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Author of <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Cthulhu-Armageddon-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01KUOM7SI/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982844&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Cthulhu+Armageddon\" target=\"_blank\">Cthulhu Armageddon</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Teenage-Weredeer-Bright-Falls-Mysteries-ebook/dp/B075TTN2FN/ref=sr_1_2?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982717&amp;sr=1-2&amp;keywords=Weredeer#customerReviews\" target=\"_blank\">I was a Teenage Weredeer</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Straight-Outta-Fangton-Comedic-Vampire-ebook/dp/B01KNHICCC/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982774&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Straight+Outta+Fangton\" target=\"_blank\">Straight Outta Fangton</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Lucifers-Star-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01MDM9MCT/ref=mt_kindle?_encoding=UTF8&amp;me=&amp;qid=\" target=\"_blank\">Lucifer's Star</a>, </i>and the <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Rules-Supervillainy-Saga-Book-ebook/dp/B07MB89S33/\" target=\"_blank\">Supervillainy Saga</a>.</i><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","name":"CTPhipps","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12002_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13933"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-06-22T09:50:15-07:00","id":1453176,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CTPhipps</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1443592-the-official-v5-vs-v20-thread?p=1453154#post1453154\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I'm going to react with confusion because the Lasombra haven't been involved with the Catholic Church since the Dark Ages and run a literally Satanist death cult that mocks the Catholic Church.<br /> <br /> They revere Caine because Caine hates God and all of his works.<br /> <br /> I mean, people realize the whole Cardinal and Bishop stuff is meant to be IRONIC, right?<br /> [Ghost]<br /> ]</div> </div> </div> </div>Ironic catholics still don't deserve to be emasculated and turned into bitchboys. <br /> <br /> yet, the Lasombra are still seriously religious. <br /> First, they draw heavily from the mediteranian and latin america, where most of their childer are going to be either catholic or 'culturally catholic' <br /> Second, they've got the profundities of the Abyss to concern themselves with, nuetered as that might be in V5. Drawing upon a realm that's apparently hostile to all creation is going to put the fear of god, or not-god, right into you, as if being a vampire wasn't enough. <br /> Third, when you're surrounded by people doing shit ironically, you're eventually going to find some people who take it seriously. <br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> RE: Assamites. <br /> First, it's somewhat paradoxical to both try move away from 'The arab clan' and be international and then choose to give your group a decisively arabic name. <br /> Second, the schismatics aren't all muslim asylum seekers; there are jews, christians, minority faiths, and also secular vampires who object to the Path of Blood and Ur-shulgi. None of these people are going to be happy Arabianizing the name. <br /> Third, being super explicit about your founder isn't endearing, especially since the guy put himself above the other antideluvians, and you're in a sect that at least thinks vampire religion is uncool, and has only recently lifted the ban. <br /> Lastly, Deciding on a new name for yourselves doesn't mean people are going to roll with it. See how, in english, &quot;Deutschland&quot; is still called Germany thanks to the romans, Hell this even persists when it's brazenly incorrect, like soldiers from WW2 using the names of WW1 weapons for WW2 equipment made by entirely different companies and designers. Now imagine you're dealing with vampires who're even slower to change than humans. <br /> <br /> But also Assamites seem to have lost their caste system and that upsets me.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25794-mywifeisscary","name":"MyWifeIsScary","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25794_2.png","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3711"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-06-22T10:26:50-07:00","id":1453179,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MyWifeIsScary</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1443592-the-official-v5-vs-v20-thread?p=1453176#post1453176\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Ironic catholics still don't deserve to be emasculated and turned into bitchboys.</div> </div> </div> </div>Which come back to the fact that I think the Lasombra gain a lot of power vacated by the Brujah, Gangrel, and, yes, Tremere.<br /> <br /> But yes, I suppose that's another reason also why some Lasombra would defect as the Catholic obsessed ones would probably want to leave the group that declares its loyalty to the First (Second? Third?) Rebel against God.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Author of <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Cthulhu-Armageddon-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01KUOM7SI/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982844&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Cthulhu+Armageddon\" target=\"_blank\">Cthulhu Armageddon</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Teenage-Weredeer-Bright-Falls-Mysteries-ebook/dp/B075TTN2FN/ref=sr_1_2?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982717&amp;sr=1-2&amp;keywords=Weredeer#customerReviews\" target=\"_blank\">I was a Teenage Weredeer</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Straight-Outta-Fangton-Comedic-Vampire-ebook/dp/B01KNHICCC/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982774&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Straight+Outta+Fangton\" target=\"_blank\">Straight Outta Fangton</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Lucifers-Star-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01MDM9MCT/ref=mt_kindle?_encoding=UTF8&amp;me=&amp;qid=\" target=\"_blank\">Lucifer's Star</a>, </i>and the <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Rules-Supervillainy-Saga-Book-ebook/dp/B07MB89S33/\" target=\"_blank\">Supervillainy Saga</a>.</i><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","name":"CTPhipps","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12002_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13933"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-06-22T12:50:14-07:00","id":1453199,"title":"","content":"The people who are Good Catholics enough to leave the Sabbat probably weren't Good Catholics enough to join or survive for any meaningful length of time in the Sabbat. Yet the Lasombra recruit often from those &quot;culturally catholic&quot; and the ritae provide warped familiarity for them. They're not praising the Trinity but they're still taking a lot of notes from the old testament, even if their edition is a little whack. Mexican gangs, at least in pop-culture, draw heavily from Catholic culture, even if they're terrible Catholics. Lasombra, similarly, are awful at being good catholics, but when you attack them for being catholic or religious, it seems like you're attacking catholics. Making them bitchboys and transforming the Camarilla into a faction of religious conservatives that twirl evil mustaches is a dick move. <br /> <br /> The Ventrue,Malkavians, Toreador and Nosferatu are going to gain power from what was vacated by the Brujah, Gangrel and Tremere (The first two generally having less power, and the latter probably still able to preserve the majority of their strength. ) The Lasombra would be like Cheetahs; they can manage a metaphorical kill after a few failures, but the lions and hyenas will drive them off any meal before they get a chance to eat; a cheetah has no hope in competing against lions, hyenas, even wild dogs will easily deprive a cheetah of an easy meal. <br /> <br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25794-mywifeisscary","name":"MyWifeIsScary","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25794_2.png","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3711"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-06-22T13:17:02-07:00","id":1453203,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MyWifeIsScary</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1443592-the-official-v5-vs-v20-thread?p=1453199#post1453199\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The people who are Good Catholics enough to leave the Sabbat probably weren't Good Catholics enough to join or survive for any meaningful length of time in the Sabbat. Yet the Lasombra recruit often from those &quot;culturally catholic&quot; and the ritae provide warped familiarity for them. They're not praising the Trinity but they're still taking a lot of notes from the old testament, even if their edition is a little whack. Mexican gangs, at least in pop-culture, draw heavily from Catholic culture, even if they're terrible Catholics. Lasombra, similarly, are awful at being good catholics, but when you attack them for being catholic or religious, it seems like you're attacking catholics. Making them bitchboys and transforming the Camarilla into a faction of religious conservatives that twirl evil mustaches is a dick move.<br /> <br /> The Ventrue,Malkavians, Toreador and Nosferatu are going to gain power from what was vacated by the Brujah, Gangrel and Tremere (The first two generally having less power, and the latter probably still able to preserve the majority of their strength. ) The Lasombra would be like Cheetahs; they can manage a metaphorical kill after a few failures, but the lions and hyenas will drive them off any meal before they get a chance to eat; a cheetah has no hope in competing against lions, hyenas, even wild dogs will easily deprive a cheetah of an easy meal.</div> </div> </div> </div>I suppose it's what you view the Camarilla as meant to be and what it represents. To me, the Lasombra being accepted into the Camarilla is due to the fact the Camarilla is simultaneously too weak to enforce its will the way it used to (due to the Anarchs becoming more Sabbat like) and yet simultaneously too strong to be defeated. Too big to fail so to speak. The Camarilla NEEDS new blood to replace their losses and the Assamites are certainly going to help with that but so are the Lasombra defectors. In the end, the Lasombra will do immense damage to the Sabbat on their exit because that is the price the Camarilla demands they pay.<br /> <br /> However, it is a price the Lasombra were willing to pay because they would have to do that anyway.<br /> <br /> I suppose I assumed the Lasombra were more cunning than the Ventrue Kevin Jackson because Kevin Jackson thinks the Lasombra are weakening themselves when the Lasombra think they're just making sure there's no one left to stab them in the back on their way out. There will be other prices and other humiliations, we see that in LA BY NIGHT (canonical) and SHADOWS OF NEW YORK but the Lasombra are playing the long game. They will replenish their ranks within the Camarilla eventually and the defectors will settle outside the traditional power structures until they're invited back in.<br /> <br /> Yes, you could certainly play that as the Lasombra being fools and beggars that will get shoved under the rug. However, I think they tend to be better at that. They will survive and thrive better in the Camarilla than the Sabbat where subtlety is rewarded over viciousness.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Author of <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Cthulhu-Armageddon-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01KUOM7SI/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982844&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Cthulhu+Armageddon\" target=\"_blank\">Cthulhu Armageddon</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Teenage-Weredeer-Bright-Falls-Mysteries-ebook/dp/B075TTN2FN/ref=sr_1_2?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982717&amp;sr=1-2&amp;keywords=Weredeer#customerReviews\" target=\"_blank\">I was a Teenage Weredeer</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Straight-Outta-Fangton-Comedic-Vampire-ebook/dp/B01KNHICCC/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982774&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Straight+Outta+Fangton\" target=\"_blank\">Straight Outta Fangton</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Lucifers-Star-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01MDM9MCT/ref=mt_kindle?_encoding=UTF8&amp;me=&amp;qid=\" target=\"_blank\">Lucifer's Star</a>, </i>and the <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Rules-Supervillainy-Saga-Book-ebook/dp/B07MB89S33/\" target=\"_blank\">Supervillainy Saga</a>.</i><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","name":"CTPhipps","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12002_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13933"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-06-23T08:00:18-07:00","id":1453275,"title":"","content":"Wut? Too weak but also too strong to be defeated but also too big to fail... <br /> Uh-huh. <br /> <br /> The Camarilla has chosen to cripple itself. It has chosen to oust the Brujah (because there's no way the brujah would agree with themselves on giving up a nice seat) so that it can strengthen it's political rivals but also invite the Lasombra... <br /> <br /> So, is this just high-clan/low clan again but we have to hand everyone an idiot ball to achieve that.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25794-mywifeisscary","name":"MyWifeIsScary","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25794_2.png","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3711"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-06-23T08:10:41-07:00","id":1453279,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MyWifeIsScary</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1443592-the-official-v5-vs-v20-thread?p=1453275#post1453275\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Wut? Too weak but also too strong to be defeated but also too big to fail...</div> </div> </div> </div>Yes, that would be literally what I wrote.<br /> <br /> The Camarilla is wounded but not so much that they could destroy it. They could, however, take advantage of its injury.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MyWifeIsScary</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1443592-the-official-v5-vs-v20-thread?p=1453275#post1453275\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The Camarilla has chosen to cripple itself. It has chosen to oust the Brujah (because there's no way the brujah would agree with themselves on giving up a nice seat) so that it can strengthen it's political rivals but also invite the Lasombra...<br /> <br /> So, is this just high-clan/low clan again but we have to hand everyone an idiot ball to achieve that.</div> </div> </div> </div>The Brujah fucked up because 90% of their people didn't care and the Hellenes are the 10% who had their own position at the party but couldn't control the rest.<br /> <br /> It makes sense the Rabble would look at their leaders and go, &quot;Nah, we don't need you. You're doing shit for us.&quot;","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Author of <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Cthulhu-Armageddon-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01KUOM7SI/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982844&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Cthulhu+Armageddon\" target=\"_blank\">Cthulhu Armageddon</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Teenage-Weredeer-Bright-Falls-Mysteries-ebook/dp/B075TTN2FN/ref=sr_1_2?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982717&amp;sr=1-2&amp;keywords=Weredeer#customerReviews\" target=\"_blank\">I was a Teenage Weredeer</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Straight-Outta-Fangton-Comedic-Vampire-ebook/dp/B01KNHICCC/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982774&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Straight+Outta+Fangton\" target=\"_blank\">Straight Outta Fangton</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Lucifers-Star-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01MDM9MCT/ref=mt_kindle?_encoding=UTF8&amp;me=&amp;qid=\" target=\"_blank\">Lucifer's Star</a>, </i>and the <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Rules-Supervillainy-Saga-Book-ebook/dp/B07MB89S33/\" target=\"_blank\">Supervillainy Saga</a>.</i><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","name":"CTPhipps","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12002_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13933"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-06-23T09:59:16-07:00","id":1453292,"title":"","content":"Bruh, it's a self inflicted injury. And your brujah explanation is whack; 90%? I know you're an anarch sympathiser but 90% of Brujah aren't anarchs and of the Brujah who are labeled 'anarchs' half are more 'The prince's loyal opposition' than revolutionaries. It's probable that most Brujah leaders <i>are</i> doing shit for their community to boot. For the Brujah who frenzy at the drop of a hat, a well regulated masquerade enforcement keeps them alive, because if the Inquisition was real, they'd be the first to go.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25794-mywifeisscary","name":"MyWifeIsScary","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25794_2.png","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3711"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-06-23T10:09:53-07:00","id":1453294,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MyWifeIsScary</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1443592-the-official-v5-vs-v20-thread?p=1453292#post1453292\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Bruh, it's a self inflicted injury. And your brujah explanation is whack; 90%? I know you're an anarch sympathiser but 90% of Brujah aren't anarchs and of the Brujah who are labeled 'anarchs' half are more 'The prince's loyal opposition' than revolutionaries. It's probable that most Brujah leaders <i>are</i> doing shit for their community to boot. For the Brujah who frenzy at the drop of a hat, a well regulated masquerade enforcement keeps them alive, because if the Inquisition was real, they'd be the first to go.</div> </div> </div> </div>They don't have to be Anarchs. They can also be Blood Cultists, Independents, and just plain people who don't want anything to do with the Camarilla.<br /> <br /> As for the Second Inquisition, the Camarilla used them as puppets to try to purge the people they viewed as enemies. The poor vampires, so to speak, and that's what caused the problem.<br /> <br /> You can't unleash the hounds and then steal their bone.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Author of <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Cthulhu-Armageddon-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01KUOM7SI/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982844&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Cthulhu+Armageddon\" target=\"_blank\">Cthulhu Armageddon</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Teenage-Weredeer-Bright-Falls-Mysteries-ebook/dp/B075TTN2FN/ref=sr_1_2?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982717&amp;sr=1-2&amp;keywords=Weredeer#customerReviews\" target=\"_blank\">I was a Teenage Weredeer</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Straight-Outta-Fangton-Comedic-Vampire-ebook/dp/B01KNHICCC/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982774&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Straight+Outta+Fangton\" target=\"_blank\">Straight Outta Fangton</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Lucifers-Star-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01MDM9MCT/ref=mt_kindle?_encoding=UTF8&amp;me=&amp;qid=\" target=\"_blank\">Lucifer's Star</a>, </i>and the <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Rules-Supervillainy-Saga-Book-ebook/dp/B07MB89S33/\" target=\"_blank\">Supervillainy Saga</a>.</i><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","name":"CTPhipps","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12002_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13933"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-06-23T23:32:48-07:00","id":1453332,"title":"","content":"Personally, I'm pretty mixed on the Anarchs fully diverging into their own sect (it was one of the V5 updates I chose to take on, but ended up diffusing it in my chronicle's city, where the local Anarchs and Cam are keeping a truce). On the one hand, I tend to go with the characterization of the Camarilla as basically a MLM scheme--to see any benefit, you need at least one rung of membership below you. For the &quot;rank and file&quot; Neonates, pretty much the only thing keeping them in the Ivory Tower is their Elders' insistence. All Kindred are considered <i>de jure</i> to be part of the Camarilla, whether they personally agree or not. To me however, replacing the tension of Anarchs being a restive element inside the Tower with pure emnity makes things a bit too simple. I like Anarchs being able to enter Elysium and trade barbs with the Harpies, developing tangled relationships across party lines. Having them be their own sect with their own territory does lose that.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26710-ventrue-busboy","name":"Ventrue Busboy","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar26710_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"41"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-06-24T03:58:41-07:00","id":1453341,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ventrue Busboy</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1443592-the-official-v5-vs-v20-thread?p=1453332#post1453332\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Personally, I'm pretty mixed on the Anarchs fully diverging into their own sect (it was one of the V5 updates I chose to take on, but ended up diffusing it in my chronicle's city, where the local Anarchs and Cam are keeping a truce). On the one hand, I tend to go with the characterization of the Camarilla as basically a MLM scheme--to see any benefit, you need at least one rung of membership below you. For the &quot;rank and file&quot; Neonates, pretty much the only thing keeping them in the Ivory Tower is their Elders' insistence. All Kindred are considered <i>de jure</i> to be part of the Camarilla, whether they personally agree or not. To me however, replacing the tension of Anarchs being a restive element inside the Tower with pure emnity makes things a bit too simple. I like Anarchs being able to enter Elysium and trade barbs with the Harpies, developing tangled relationships across party lines. Having them be their own sect with their own territory does lose that.</div> </div> </div> </div>It's an unfortunate fact that both the opposition and the reformers were essentially the same group because it means that if you do have the Anarchs tolerated by the Elders then they are almost certainly going to come across as toothless if you want to portray the system as corrupt and worthy of enmity. If you have the Anarchs not tolerated and treated as a genuine threat, then you run the risk of losing interactions you might normally have. Which is to say that the Anarchs looked like a bunch of poseurs in the games where they were defending their cities against the Sabbat while the Camarilla was eliminating them quietly.<br /> <br /> No one wants to join an RPG where the resistance is a bunch of guys just slashing paintings versus actually fighting to protect themselves in the street.<br /> <br /> I feel like we needed a sharper divide between radicals and idealists--but can you be the latter in a feudal state where all power belongs to the oligarchy?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Author of <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Cthulhu-Armageddon-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01KUOM7SI/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982844&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Cthulhu+Armageddon\" target=\"_blank\">Cthulhu Armageddon</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Teenage-Weredeer-Bright-Falls-Mysteries-ebook/dp/B075TTN2FN/ref=sr_1_2?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982717&amp;sr=1-2&amp;keywords=Weredeer#customerReviews\" target=\"_blank\">I was a Teenage Weredeer</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Straight-Outta-Fangton-Comedic-Vampire-ebook/dp/B01KNHICCC/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982774&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Straight+Outta+Fangton\" target=\"_blank\">Straight Outta Fangton</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Lucifers-Star-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01MDM9MCT/ref=mt_kindle?_encoding=UTF8&amp;me=&amp;qid=\" target=\"_blank\">Lucifer's Star</a>, </i>and the <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Rules-Supervillainy-Saga-Book-ebook/dp/B07MB89S33/\" target=\"_blank\">Supervillainy Saga</a>.</i><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","name":"CTPhipps","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12002_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13933"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-06-24T07:11:58-07:00","id":1453358,"title":"","content":"This is why it's nice to have a spectrum of &quot;Anarch&quot; <br /> <br /> Let's say you have Alice, who's rather close to the prince and benefits immensely from her loyalty. <br /> Then you have Ben, who would like changes to the status quo, but is Camarilla enough to get along with Alice.<br /> Then you have Chad, who sits the fence. Alice would describe Chad as an Anarch, but Ben would describe him as Camarilla, chad might describe himself as either or neither, it doesn't matter. <br /> Then you have Danny, who's a self-admited Anarch. Alice won't sit in the same room as her, Ben will keep the relationship quiet, and Chad is happy to deal with her. <br /> Then there's Ernest. Ernest is hardcore. Alice wants him dead. Ben won't touch him. Chad will keep the dealings secret. Danny is both in awe and repulsed by him. <br /> Lastly there's Frank. Everyone hates Frank, and Frank hates everyone, at least on the surface. Somebody probably has uses for Frank.<br /> <br /> And of course, in each category, there are people who are equally for or against the prince but also against people within their category. This gets more extreme as you move out; Alan merely wants to supplant alice as the prince's favourite, but Ernest, Ed, Erin and Eric absolutely fucking despise eachother, all being radical and yet having very different ideas of what to do when they get power. Fortunately there's more Alices, Bens and Chads than Ernests and Franks. <br /> <br /> <br /> V5 is like.. You're either red or blue, there is no purple, there is no yellow. The Anarchs fight the Cam. That's not realistic. That doesn't reflect reality in any way, That's just pulpy bullshit","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25794-mywifeisscary","name":"MyWifeIsScary","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25794_2.png","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3711"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-06-24T12:18:54-07:00","id":1453391,"title":"","content":"In earlier discussions, I have argued strongly in favor of anarchs as a tolerated faction within the Camarilla rather than a separate sect that has been kicked out of the Camarilla. It's no surprise that my tastes have a lot in common with the views expressed by <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26710-ventrue-busboy\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar26710_2.png');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"26710\" data-vbnamecard=\"26710\">Ventrue Busboy</a> and <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25794-mywifeisscary\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar25794_2.png');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"25794\" data-vbnamecard=\"25794\">MyWifeIsScary</a> above.<br /> <br /> In fact, although I don't always agree with the manner in which he presents his arguments, it was MyWifeIsScary who wrote something in the recent Sabbat thread that I have never been able to articulate as clearly. The conflict between anarchs and the Camarilla isn't disenfranchised punks versus The Man, it's low grade millionaires versus high grade millionaires. Even the lowliest anarchs are members of an elite class of superhuman people, literally 1 in 100,000 compared to us poor mortals. The real downtrodden masses of <i>Vampire: The Masquerade</i> are the humans. Even if the Camarilla were destroyed tomorrow, the anarchs would be perfectly happy to continue to exploit, abuse, violate and cultivate human beings like the resource they are. All vampires, regardless of whether they are Camarilla, anarch, independent or Sabbat, belong to a bloodsucking aristocracy. I would go so far as to argue that this concept is built into the very premise of the vampire as a fictional creature.<br /> <br /> What this means in practice is that, for me, the anarchs <i>have</i> to have a certain degree of &quot;just slashing paintings&quot; about them. The alternative, that I'm supposed to sympathize with and be invested in their revolutionary struggle -- even though anarch rule is likely to be just as abusive toward human beings as the great Camarilla conspiracy -- is too preposterous to consider.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1190,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1190-elphilm","user":"Elphilm","date":". 06-24-2021, 06:09 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":6}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1190-elphilm","name":"Elphilm","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1190_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"763"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-06-24T14:17:01-07:00","id":1453406,"title":"","content":"Yeah, the Anarchs are just John Wilkes Booth unironically shouting &quot;<i><b>Sic semper tyrannis</b></i>&quot; which is to say, &quot;thus always to tyrants!&quot; while assassinating Lincoln, because he genuinely believed that destroying his right to own slaves was destroying freedom.<br /> <br /> The Anarchs vs the Camarilla is just the low nobles vs the high nobles, and that conflict has been around forever without it helping the slaves one bit. The ancient Greeks, the Roman Republic, and the Confederacy were all places where the low nobles had the collective power. The various empires and absolute monarchies were all places where the high nobles had all the power. They were all awful places for the peasants and slaves.<br /> <br /> The Confederacy is remembered as especially heinous because there the low nobles thought they were rebelling against the high nobles, but they were actually rebelling against a government that, while it had elements of high noble government in that people who could trace their ancestry to the Mayflower had disproportionate power, and were seeking a more centralized government, was also well on its way to transitioning into a genuine democracy.<br /> <br /> But even if that were not true and Lincoln and company really had just been the latest iteration of the High Nobles seeking to centralize power and stick it to the Low Nobles, that would not have made the Confederacy the good guys. It would just have made it the latest iteration of Evil Low Noble vs Evil High Noble.<br /> <br /> The latest edition seems to be trying to brush that aside and push people into playing failed superheroes. You're always supposed to be an Anarch who is trying very hard to be a conventionally heroic, but who gets dragged down by the hunger and frenzy and the wearying complexity of vampire politics. You're supposed to try to be a superhero with fangs, every time, and fail, every time. That's it. That's all. Every game is supposed to be that one story with trivial changes like different powers and different backstories, but it's always supposed to be the story of a failed superhero, every single time.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":3598,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3598-cajunkhan","user":"CajunKhan","date":". 06-24-2021, 05:19 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3598-cajunkhan","name":"CajunKhan","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3598_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1700"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-06-24T15:15:38-07:00","id":1453408,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Elphilm</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1443592-the-official-v5-vs-v20-thread?p=1453391#post1453391\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">In earlier discussions, I have argued strongly in favor of anarchs as a tolerated faction within the Camarilla rather than a separate sect that has been kicked out of the Camarilla. It's no surprise that my tastes have a lot in common with the views expressed by <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26710-ventrue-busboy\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar26710_2.png');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"26710\" data-vbnamecard=\"26710\">Ventrue Busboy</a> and <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25794-mywifeisscary\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar25794_2.png');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"25794\" data-vbnamecard=\"25794\">MyWifeIsScary</a> above.<br /> <br /> In fact, although I don't always agree with the manner in which he presents his arguments, it was MyWifeIsScary who wrote something in the recent Sabbat thread that I have never been able to articulate as clearly. <b>The conflict between anarchs and the Camarilla isn't disenfranchised punks versus The Man, it's low grade millionaires versus high grade millionaires. Even the lowliest anarchs are members of an elite class of superhuman people, literally 1 in 100,000 compared to us poor mortals. </b>The real downtrodden masses of <i>Vampire: The Masquerade</i> are the humans. Even if the Camarilla were destroyed tomorrow, the anarchs would be perfectly happy to continue to exploit, abuse, violate and cultivate human beings like the resource they are. Every vampire, regardless of whether they are Camarilla, anarch, independent or Sabbat, belong to a bloodsucking aristocracy. I would go so far as to argue that this concept is built into the very premise of the vampire as a fictional creature.<br /> <br /> What this means in practice is that for me, the anarchs <i>have</i> to have a certain degree of &quot;just slashing paintings&quot; about them. The alternative, that I'm supposed to sympathize with and be invested in their revolutionary struggle -- even though anarch rule is likely to be just as abusive toward human beings as the great Camarilla conspiracy -- is too preposterous to consider.</div> </div> </div> </div>Thank you, you've maanged to actually provide the perfect example of what I've been searching for in discussing just how fundamentally DIFFERENT that Storytellers can have of their gameworlds even if you all have the same information, same books, and same basic adherence to canon. <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25794-mywifeisscary\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar25794_2.png');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"25794\" data-vbnamecard=\"25794\">MyWifeIsScary</a> and I particularly come at the issue of Anarchs from a very different perspective, probably because my biggest influence is <i>Chicago by Night</i> 1st Edition and <i>Los Angeles by Night</i>.<br /> <br /> Ask me how to describe what is the life of an Anarch in three words?<br /> <br /> Fear.<br /> Poverty.<br /> Survival.<br /> <br /> I'm imagining Anarchs primarily living on the outskirts of cities in abandoned houses, factories, and warehouses. They squat and don't hold jobs. Any money they have is primarily from people they've robbed or what they've managed to scavenge. They rarely have any regular sources of meals. They are almost all 11th-13th generation or Thin Bloods. Brujah, Caitiff, and the cast offs of other clans.<br /> <br /> They are also <i>hunted</i>.<br /> <br /> The police are very often able to gun them down and leave them to be burned alive by the sun the next day or staked and decapitated by the Sheriff once their bodies are identified in the coroner's office. Humans and police brutality are a threat, let alone the Sheriff who will act like a Southern hick and burn down your haven to try to get you to move along. Any crimes that Elders commit WILL be blamed on you to provide a scapegoat and the only safe places to feed are the Rack.<br /> <br /> Why are you an Anarch? Because you DIE alone.<br /> <br /> <b>Steel Drum Encounter</b>: Whenever I do a new group for the Anarchs, I like to do a scene where they meet a fellow vampire, who is nice, and then they find them in an oil drum the next night, having been burned inside out, as a lesson that you shouldn't walk the streets unarmed and out of a group with the Sheriff and his Hounds loose. After all, you might be caught &quot;resisting arrest.&quot;<br /> <br /> <b>Musical Theme</b>: &quot;Fight to Survive&quot; by Stan Bush<br /> <br /> <div class=\"videocontainer with-aspect-ratio videocontainer-horizontal\" style=\"aspect-ratio: 16/9;\"> <a class=\"video-frame\" href=\"https://youtu.be/dQ4XHW5Q4gU\" data-code=\"dQ4XHW5Q4gU\" data-provider=\"youtube_share\" data-height=\"0\" data-width=\"0\" itemprop=\"video\"> <div class=\"videothumbnail\" style=\"\"> <img src=\"https://img.youtube.com/vi/dQ4XHW5Q4gU/hqdefault.jpg\" alt=\"\" /> <div class=\"videothumbnailoverlay\"></div> </div> </a> </div><br /> <br /> It's why Anarchs work as mercs for the Elders they survive. It's a matter of life or death. You are PUNKS because the system was rigged from the beginning against you. If you're USEFUL to an Elder then you can fuck up other Elders for money and favors. At least until you stop being useful. Which is again, heavily influenced by Cyberpunk 2020.<br /> <br /> Edgerunners with Fangs vs. Corpos with Fangs","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Author of <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Cthulhu-Armageddon-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01KUOM7SI/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982844&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Cthulhu+Armageddon\" target=\"_blank\">Cthulhu Armageddon</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Teenage-Weredeer-Bright-Falls-Mysteries-ebook/dp/B075TTN2FN/ref=sr_1_2?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982717&amp;sr=1-2&amp;keywords=Weredeer#customerReviews\" target=\"_blank\">I was a Teenage Weredeer</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Straight-Outta-Fangton-Comedic-Vampire-ebook/dp/B01KNHICCC/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982774&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Straight+Outta+Fangton\" target=\"_blank\">Straight Outta Fangton</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Lucifers-Star-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01MDM9MCT/ref=mt_kindle?_encoding=UTF8&amp;me=&amp;qid=\" target=\"_blank\">Lucifer's Star</a>, </i>and the <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Rules-Supervillainy-Saga-Book-ebook/dp/B07MB89S33/\" target=\"_blank\">Supervillainy Saga</a>.</i><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":12002,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","user":"CTPhipps","date":". 06-24-2021, 06:19 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","name":"CTPhipps","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12002_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13933"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-06-24T15:29:52-07:00","id":1453410,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CajunKhan</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1443592-the-official-v5-vs-v20-thread?p=1453406#post1453406\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Yeah, the Anarchs are just John Wilkes Booth unironically shouting &quot;<i><b>Sic semper tyrannis</b></i>&quot; which is to say, &quot;thus always to tyrants!&quot; while assassinating Lincoln, because he genuinely believed that destroying his right to own slaves was destroying freedom.<br /> <br /> The Anarchs vs the Camarilla is just the low nobles vs the high nobles, and that conflict has been around forever without it helping the slaves one bit. The ancient Greeks, the Roman Republic, and the Confederacy were all places where the low nobles had the collective power. The various empires and absolute monarchies were all places where the high nobles had all the power. They were all awful places for the peasants and slaves.<br /> <br /> The Confederacy is remembered as especially heinous because there the low nobles thought they were rebelling against the high nobles, but they were actually rebelling against a government that, while it had elements of high noble government in that people who could trace their ancestry to the Mayflower had disproportionate power, and were seeking a more centralized government, was also well on its way to transitioning into a genuine democracy.<br /> <br /> But even if that were not true and Lincoln and company really had just been the latest iteration of the High Nobles seeking to centralize power and stick it to the Low Nobles, that would not have made the Confederacy the good guys. It would just have made it the latest iteration of Evil Low Noble vs Evil High Noble.<br /> <br /> The latest edition seems to be trying to brush that aside and push people into playing failed superheroes. You're always supposed to be an Anarch who is trying very hard to be a conventionally heroic, but who gets dragged down by the hunger and frenzy and the wearying complexity of vampire politics. You're supposed to try to be a superhero with fangs, every time, and fail, every time. That's it. That's all. Every game is supposed to be that one story with trivial changes like different powers and different backstories, but it's always supposed to be the story of a failed superhero, every single time.</div> </div> </div> </div>That's pretty much another area from which I draw heavily from Cyberpunk 2020.<br /> <br /> &quot;At what point does fighting the man mean becoming the Man?&quot;<br /> <br /> There are Anarchs who manage to &quot;make it.&quot; They are able to carve their own territory from the Camarilla in one of the larger cities, get concessions from the Prince and Primogen, or even take over one of the surrounding smaller cities. They are people who are like Juggler, guys who talk a good game but have sold out and now are every bit as exploitative as the people they once used to fight like Modius or Lodin.<br /> <br /> These Anarchs, called Barons or Bosses or just their names, are nothing more than crime bosses. Often figuratively and literally.<br /> <br /> However, each of them has had to answer, &quot;Isn't this BETTER than the life we lived before?&quot;<br /> <br /> Because V:TM is as much crime fiction as vampire fiction and this is a story that has been done many times before. The young gangster who wants revenge and then becomes the very thing they fight.<br /> <br /> In the end, most Anarchs sold out.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Author of <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Cthulhu-Armageddon-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01KUOM7SI/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982844&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Cthulhu+Armageddon\" target=\"_blank\">Cthulhu Armageddon</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Teenage-Weredeer-Bright-Falls-Mysteries-ebook/dp/B075TTN2FN/ref=sr_1_2?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982717&amp;sr=1-2&amp;keywords=Weredeer#customerReviews\" target=\"_blank\">I was a Teenage Weredeer</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Straight-Outta-Fangton-Comedic-Vampire-ebook/dp/B01KNHICCC/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982774&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Straight+Outta+Fangton\" target=\"_blank\">Straight Outta Fangton</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Lucifers-Star-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01MDM9MCT/ref=mt_kindle?_encoding=UTF8&amp;me=&amp;qid=\" target=\"_blank\">Lucifer's Star</a>, </i>and the <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Rules-Supervillainy-Saga-Book-ebook/dp/B07MB89S33/\" target=\"_blank\">Supervillainy Saga</a>.</i><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","name":"CTPhipps","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12002_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13933"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-06-25T01:10:35-07:00","id":1453437,"title":"","content":"I'm of multiple minds about this and my somewhat mealy-mouthed judgement is the WoD is big enough for both the &quot;Fangrunner&quot; interpretation and the more level political landscape--dependent on many factors: the number and strength of resident Elders, of local Anarch gangs, and the leadership style of the resident Prince. I try to avoid dropping Elders who can't be outfought or outmaneuvered into my games, as I don't like boxing my players into or out of a given path (&quot;you better do this guy's quest cuz he's REALLY STRONG&quot; is.... not good STing, to me). On the other hand, I don't want a WoD devoid of entities greater than the coterie of PCs (the Beckoning was one idea from V5 I didn't take onboard). Neonates who are simply at the mercy of their Elders isn't interesting, but &quot;stand together or fall divided&quot; is a useful impetus to bring dispirate PCs together and make politics happen at all levels of the Jyhad. The Camarilla in my chronicle's city can't simply murder luckless Neonates at will or throw their weight around through sheer terror. I've also found, gothpunk noir notwithstanding, my players tend to feel rudderless without some Big Good they can take a cue from; a Nines Rodriguez or a Rebecca to say &quot;it's not all horrible; see, this guy made it.&quot; Not that my Barons are angels or my Elders not ruthless and manipulative, but the gameworld needs carrots as well as sticks. L.A. and Chicago's canon environs provide useful goalposts for opposite ends of this spectrum---a wild west of baronies and gangs versus a monolithic power structure that holds everything in its orbit. Somewhere between these polarities is the city of my chronicle (literally split down the middle between Anarchs and the Tower, with peace and safety always hanging by a veritable thread).","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26710-ventrue-busboy","name":"Ventrue Busboy","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar26710_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"41"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-06-25T03:56:31-07:00","id":1453438,"title":"","content":"the thing is that anarchs aren't a movement, they're the inevitability of 'childer rebelling against their elders' within the camarilla. it's a byproduct of the cam but because of how fractured the cam is it's only natural that the anarchs are going to be a byproduct of the local camarilla and not the camarilla at-large and as such the differing anarch movements are going to vary widely. (so for exampe the antwerp anarchs are a secret cabal of low nobels trying to gain more power, the Houston anarchs are just slashing paintings because fuck you dad and the chicago anarchs are downthroten fighting for survival because the sheriff is a homicidal maniac)<br /> <br /> the big issue with the anarchs in V5 is that they're presented as a counter movement against the camarilla at-large when the camarilla is and always has been too fractured/disjointed(?) for such a thing and local camarilla governance can differ so widely that the very thought that they would all produce the exact same counter movement is just asinine. that they'd all produce a counter movement is an inevitability of the Jyhad, but all the exact same one is just ludicrous. anarchs as a singular movement just doesn't work","signature":"","edited":{"userid":25992,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25992-archderd","user":"archderd","date":". 06-25-2021, 09:04 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25992-archderd","name":"archderd","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25992_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2020"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"205"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-06-25T06:08:56-07:00","id":1453446,"title":"","content":"V5 in general seems to be a case of stripping out nuance in the name of, for wont of a better term \u201cnewbie accessibility.\u201d<br /> <br /> Its a lot easier to convey \u201cAlliance vs. Horde\u201d in a few bullet points than all the nuances you\u2019d need for a proper treatise on Camarilla/Anarch/Autarkis relations just within one city, much less how each city is different.<br /> <br /> The same for the Second Inquisition. Instead of the nuances of the various, sometimes even competing groups of vampire hunters... now they\u2019re basically a characture of every monolithic One World Government conspiracy (all the intelligence agencies of the world are cooperating to eliminate vampires while keeping it secret from the public) mixed with every myth of The Burning Times laid at the feet of the Catholic Church (never mind that the Pope had banned subjecting suspected witches to the Inquisition in 1258 before the rampant persecutions even began by CIVIL authorities).<br /> <br /> V5 feels like what happens when a popular novel or series gets adapted into a summer blockbuster by Hollywood. The shapes are still there, but there\u2019s no time for nuance because they have to hit all the story beats of an 800 page doorstopper novel in under three hours.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1328-chris24601","name":"Chris24601","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"520"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-06-25T06:39:43-07:00","id":1453448,"title":"","content":"<br /> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar12002_2.jpeg');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"12002\" data-vbnamecard=\"12002\">CTPhipps</a> There's certainly room for your style of Anarch, but It'd be unrealistic to apply that for most cases. <br /> \u200bThere are two big reasons to go hard as an Anarch<br /> <br /> First, your embrace was illegal, and thus by law you should be killed<br /> Second, You've fucked up really bad politically and got supressed as a result, which spiralled into you having a hard anti-cam stance. Perhaps your sire was an idiot in embracing a lefty, or perhaps you meerly overplayed yourself. Perhaps you were frustrated after being embraced for ghoul work.<br /> <br /> Here are some problems with having everyone either Hard-Cam or Hard-Anarch, and assuming the Anarch will be impoverished. <br /> 1- Cities are huge. There's lots of places for you to hide in.<br /> 2 -It takes three nights for you to establish a full blood bond. This easily allows you good shelter and some cash on the side. Now the Cam could try to seize or kill your breadwinner, but cities are big. <br /> 3-Squatting in abandoned buildings on the regular is a strategically bad idea since there are only so many of those and a cammy could easily have a ghoul just search those regularly. <br /> <br /> The hard Anarchs either <br /> A: Lose<br /> B: &quot;kill the prince&quot; only to see her replacement and whatever retribution is in store. <br /> C: Become rich and set up a new government that isn't really that much different from the one they're rebelling against. <br /> D: Take the next invite into the Cam. <br /> <br /> <br /> Soft anarchs just add more dynamics, more naunce, more 'I can totally believe this revolt has been going on for a hundred years and it isn't just something that pops up every few months before being squashed'. <br /> <br /> The Cam forcing extremes is just fucking stupid in any case.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25794-mywifeisscary","name":"MyWifeIsScary","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25794_2.png","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3711"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-06-25T09:07:55-07:00","id":1453457,"title":"","content":"^that might''ve been a bit obtuse. <br /> <br /> Another way of looking at it<br /> V20 suggest both soft and hard anarchs are functional, you can have shades of grey or you can have teams black, white, red and green who all wear team colours for easy identification. <br /> V5's metaplot demands hard anarchs. The Cam no longer want the greys. You can have black, or you can have white. <br /> <br /> Conversely; lifting the sectwide ban on crazed cults means that really, V5 can have both open cults and cults that the prince has banned; so you can enjoy both open religions and the old way of religious suppression. However, that's a smaller issue with a lot of other detracting factors; allowing cults is realy a terrible idea if you're also the sect that champions the masquerade, but i'd say that's not a deal breaker; Personally, the main thing that makes open faith off-putting is that's a blatant Segway into 'This faction are conservatives, this faction are liberals, just like mortal politics!<br /> <br /> Stop trying to make modern nights into Dark ages. Those sects were set up specifically to accommodate the social changes brought about by modernity. The Camarilla should still be doing a mostly-good job, or perhaps even becoming more necessary.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25794-mywifeisscary","name":"MyWifeIsScary","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25794_2.png","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3711"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-06-25T09:46:20-07:00","id":1453461,"title":"","content":"I suspect it\u2019s not so much trying to insert Dark Ages as it is inserting yet another Requiem element.<br /> <br /> I know some of those involved in V5 were also involved in the launch of Requiem and I\u2019ll admit that sometimes V5 with its Blood Potency, changed attributes, fixed difficulty, etc. feels more than a bit like because Requiem failed to supplant Masquerade, they decided to try and shoehorn many of those same ideas into Masquerade instead as if it\u2019s the wrapper that\u2019s the problem and not that the ideas just don\u2019t make a very good multiplayer tabletop RPG experience.<br /> <br /> V5 to me feels like it\u2019d be ideal for one-on-one games dealing with the deeply personal issues of a single protagonist. That sorta thing is great in that one-on-one experience... but is far less so when you\u2019ve got four other players sitting at the table waiting for their turns... which is why multi-player Vampire always slides back to the politics, trenchcoats and katanas that is much easier to have everyone at the table feel like they\u2019re involved in.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1328-chris24601","name":"Chris24601","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"520"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-06-25T10:11:21-07:00","id":1453463,"title":"","content":"To expand the thought; this is nothing against the developers of V5. I doubt anyone could make a better attempt.<br /> <br /> Rather its just the limitations of the medium. Some books are extremely difficult to adapt into movies due to them being mostly internal journeys with little overt action. Similarly, large spectacles like massive battles or dog fights can be clearly depicted in the span of minutes on screen that would take pages upon pages of a book to convey.<br /> <br /> I'm reminded of a discussion I had on another forum about the limits of genre emulation for superhero RPGs and how many classic comic plots; heroes being captured, heroes being mind controlled, splitting the party, etc. just aren't very fun when used in the context of a multi-player tabletop RPG. I think the same applies to the personal horror genre... multi-player tabletop rpgs just aren't that effective at conveying that genre in the way a television series, film, book or a single player computer (or tabletop) rpg experience could.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1328-chris24601","name":"Chris24601","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"520"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-06-25T10:14:01-07:00","id":1453464,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Chris24601</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1443592-the-official-v5-vs-v20-thread?p=1453461#post1453461\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I know some of those involved in V5 were also involved in the launch of Requiem and I\u2019ll admit that sometimes V5 with its Blood Potency, changed attributes, fixed difficulty, etc. feels more than a bit like because Requiem failed to supplant Masquerade, they decided to try and shoehorn many of those same ideas into Masquerade instead as if it\u2019s the wrapper that\u2019s the problem and not that the ideas just don\u2019t make a very good multiplayer tabletop RPG experience.</div> </div> </div> </div>Who do you think was involved in Requiem (either 1st or 2nd Edition) as well as V5? I really can't think of anyone that worked on VtR1 - which was the old WW team, VtR2 - which was Onyx Path freelancers, and then V5 - which was the WW over at Paradox. Thanks!","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5-richt","name":"RichT","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5_2.jpeg","title":"Onyx Path Creative Director","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"505"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-06-25T13:59:22-07:00","id":1453480,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Chris24601</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1443592-the-official-v5-vs-v20-thread?p=1453463#post1453463\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">To expand the thought; this is nothing against the developers of V5. I doubt anyone could make a better attempt.</div> </div> </div> </div> Look at V20, that's a better attempt, if polls are anything to go by.<br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Rather its just the limitations of the medium. Some books are extremely difficult to adapt into movies due to them being mostly internal journeys with little overt action. Similarly, large spectacles like massive battles or dog fights can be clearly depicted in the span of minutes on screen that would take pages upon pages of a book to convey.. </div> </div> </div>Huh? Aren't we talking about turning an RPG into another RPG.<br /> <br /> <br /> I don't know enough about requiem, but to me, it just seems like V5 wants to... how do I articulate this in compliance with forum rules...<br /> I feel the writers didn't like a lot of the setting and wanted to &quot;Fix&quot; it.<br /> I feel the setting no longer reflects reality as well as prior editions.<br /> I feel the writers have fulfilled too many of their own wishes. The Anarchs aren't meant to be big, the cam isn't meant to be small, the humans aren't meant to have their &quot;humanity fuck yeah&quot; moment, and thinbloods aren't meant to get their own super special power that only they can use. The setting is meant to be bleak. We're supposed to be horrified by politics<br /> I feel a lot of narratively powerful institutions have been watered down, whilst others have been made caricatures of themselves.<br /> <br /> I feel like a lot of &quot;fixes&quot; are born from misconceptions, or the writers understanding part of the setting but not why things are like that. For example the way Blood potency works is utterly contrary to why Generation was a thing. I can't help but think of Zack Snyder's <i>Man of Steel</i>. When I first watched it I didn't know much about Superman. It was a decent film. It had some very big flaws, but I thought Snyder and co did a lot of things very well. Then later I binged <i>Superman: The Animated series</i>, and with this newfound understanding of Superman,<i> Man of Steel</i> becomes a terrible Superman film. It's still a good, though by no means excellent film, but it's bad as a <i>S</i><i>uperman </i>film. To someone who knows superman a little better, Clark Kent is not obviously Superman and his disguise isn't just a pair of Glasses. Lois Lane, Award winning journalist, and Lex Luthor, world's most accomplished man, are both totally fooled by his disguise: This is something that bothers the layman, because to them the disguise is just a pair of Glasses, and no effort is made to give an all-too-handsome Henry Cavil a not-superman look for Clark Kent. but to someone that has greater knowledge of superman, having Lois Lane easily discover that CK is Superman is like... Telling an Egyptologist the pyramids were made by aliens. IDFK. A lot of the changes in V5 feel like Lois Lane easily discovering that CK is Superman, which seems internally reasonable to some people because &quot;CK&quot; isn't CK in V5. &quot;Clark Kent&quot; Is Wrong in V5, thus Lois Lane is rather reasonable in her discovery.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":25794,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25794-mywifeisscary","user":"MyWifeIsScary","date":". 06-25-2021, 05:03 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25794-mywifeisscary","name":"MyWifeIsScary","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25794_2.png","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3711"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-06-25T21:24:07-07:00","id":1453515,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MyWifeIsScary</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1443592-the-official-v5-vs-v20-thread?p=1453480#post1453480\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I feel like a lot of &quot;fixes&quot; are born from misconceptions, or the writers understanding part of the setting but not why things are like that. For example the way Blood potency works is utterly contrary to why Generation was a thing.</div> </div> </div> </div>I think generation works well when it serves as a cap on Blood Potency. Players needing to spend five Background dots to be 8th gen if they want to be an elder's childe (who they're also buying as a Mentor) isn't fun. It eats up pretty much all of your starting Background dots. <br /> <br /> There are mechanical benefits (in V20) to generation, but in my experience, players of 8th gen and 13th gen characters are happy to have the same initial benefits and leave &quot;my blood is purer than yours&quot; as an in-character bragging point. <br /> <br /> Mind, I think V5 could've imposed a much more strict cap on Blood Potency. IIRC, 13th generation neonates can reach as high as Blood Potency 3 under V5 rules? If they're capped at Blood Potency 1, the glass ceiling is suddenly a lot lower. <br /> <br /> That's what I've done in my games, anyway. 8th caps at BP 5, 9th at BP 4, 10th at BP 3, etc.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://blood-and-bourbon.obsidianportal.com/\" target=\"_blank\">Blood and Bourbon</a>, my New Orleans-based Vampire chronicle.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3110-false-epiphany","name":"False Epiphany","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3110_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"748"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-06-26T02:27:10-07:00","id":1453528,"title":"","content":"We can pretend the two systems are equally good if you want, but it doesn't change that V5's approach to Generations leads to a fundamentally different attitude towards it. <br /> <br /> In V1, Generation functions as a &quot;glass ceiling&quot;. It's unfair, it determines who can Dominate who, it determines how much blood you can hold and how much you can expend in a short period, and it determines the maximum level of your attributes. It's something everyone covets. you literally plan murders for it, and this instils a deep sense of distrust and paranoia in kindred society. If you just murder some elders, you gain their better blood capacity, you become the person who Dominates, not the person Dominated, and your limitations are pushed aside, allowing you to become more than you could've became before. It's a natural part of the order of things. The downsides of Diablerie are purely related to the social fallout of murdering another vampire. <br /> <br /> In V5, Generation is a a slide towards damnation. The closer you are to Caine, the hungrier you are, the less satisfying your meals are, your beast is resultingly more unstable, your clan curse becomes worse, the ancients have more sway over you. These are hugely undesirable traits, punishments for the transgression of Diablerie. What are the benefits of Diablerie? you can heal faster, blood buff more, and you can get some XP quick if you're diablerizing someone of higher gen and you have high humanity; these are helpful in moments of desperation, but not worth the consequences in the long run. Because of this, there are societal changes; It's not beneficial for a neonate to diablerize elders, and resultingly the Elders aught to be less worried about the younger gen trying to gobble them up.<br /> <br /> (also, due to how bad the mechanics are, Less humane vampires are paradoxically going to suffer more and benefit less from the inhumane act of Diablerie, which is really not what you want. ) <br /> <br /> In V1, Generation underlines much of the Jyhad, because vampires want power and they need to take it from others. In V5, Generation undermines the Jyhad, because it's a mess. <b>V1 Generation encourages you to eat the rich. V5's Generation would encourage you to only eat the &quot;poor&quot;,</b> were it not for the humanity paradox (I need high humanity to for maximum diablerie benefits, but if I'm looking for maximum diablerie benefits then obviously I'm not that humane...) <br /> <br /> Thematically, they're just massively different things.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25794-mywifeisscary","name":"MyWifeIsScary","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25794_2.png","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3711"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-06-26T03:29:50-07:00","id":1453531,"title":"","content":"I don't use V5's mechanics, so those problems are all non-problems for me. V5 doesn't model the kind of the setting I want. <br /> <br /> What I do like is the idea of blood pools, blood per turn, and &quot;who can Dominate who&quot; (or their equivalents in any system) being determined by a trait that increases with a vampire's age, but is capped by their generation. Ie, Blood Potency. It frees players from needing to spend Background dots during character creation if they don't want to be 13th generation while making diablerie even more tempting. A 7th generation fledgling has no incentive to diablerize a 7th generation elder if they both have the same generation-derived benefits; but if they have different Blood Potency scores, then diablerie becomes more tempting. A 13th generation fledgling will never reach high Blood Potency without diablerie, but a 7th generation fledgling will still have to wait hundreds of years for their blood to thicken without diablerie. It's a tempting shortcut to all neonates no matter who their sire is. <br /> <br /> V5 had a good idea in marrying Masquerade's generation with Requiem's Blood Potency. But like a lot of things with the edition, the execution was problematic and had implications for the setting in ways the writers didn't appear to fully think through.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://blood-and-bourbon.obsidianportal.com/\" target=\"_blank\">Blood and Bourbon</a>, my New Orleans-based Vampire chronicle.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3110-false-epiphany","name":"False Epiphany","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3110_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"748"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-06-26T04:18:46-07:00","id":1453533,"title":"","content":"But you see, in that instance, the 7th gen Neonate could just &quot;wait it out&quot;. When he's also 300 years old, he'll have just as much power, so without other factors involved, there's little need to risk the consequences of murder. Depending on how you do this getting stronger with age thing, then an 8th gen just has to wait longer, and so long as there's no massive pressure, the vampires will be happy to take the safe route. But if go with V1, and have an 8th gen and a 7th gen, there is no blood potency, so it doesn't matter who's the older vampire, the 8th gen absolutely needs to eat the 7th gen if she wants to raise her 5 obfuscate to 6 obfuscate. It doesn't matter if she waits twenty years, two hundred years or two thousand years, she'll never get that 6th dot without eating someone (profane rituals she doesn't have access to nonwithstanding)<br /> <br /> As foe vampires getting stronger with age... can't normal discipline accumulation satisfy you there? There is a big difference in V20 between a 13th gen who's 5 and a 13th gen who's 100, and an even bigger difference between a 5th gen who's 5 and a 5th gen who's 1000. &quot;vampires should get stronger with age&quot; is absolutely satisfied with Disciplines. Blood potency is redundant.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25794-mywifeisscary","name":"MyWifeIsScary","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25794_2.png","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3711"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-06-26T06:38:40-07:00","id":1453544,"title":"","content":"<b>Generation, Requiem, Masquerade, Power</b><br /> <br /> My opinion is that they HAVE done a lot of attempting to mix V5 and VTR for creating a kind of &quot;merged&quot; Vampire: The Masquerade and I'm kind of back and forth on it. As stated, I'm very positive about V5 in general but that doesn't mean that I am 100% pro-V5 because there's some fundamentally different design philosophies about V5 and Requiem. Requiem does what it does VERY well and it is a fantastic game but it is incompatible in its depiction of vampires with V:TM.<br /> <br /> In V:TR there's a &quot;glass ceiling&quot; (yes, <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25794-mywifeisscary\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar25794_2.png');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"25794\" data-vbnamecard=\"25794\">MyWifeIsScary</a> I'm using your metaphor) for vampires in terms of power level and it is MUCH-MUCH lower than generation. There are no Antediluvians and there's arguably no Methuselahs in terms of godlike and demigod power. While not quite 100% accurate, basically you can reach 8th generation and some level 5 Disciplines and that is IT. You are done whether you are as old as Caine or as old as Disco.<br /> <br /> Vampires do not even have the kind of power they did to hold cities. They are not the Illuminati but chiefly concerned with their hunting grounds. It's less about controlling the cops, newspapers, and billion dollar corporations and more about controlling the local gas station and a single city block where you feed. Being a vampire is not NEARLY as cool or sexy and there's not even that much power being the Prince if you can somehow herd the cats of five or six different factions in your hometown to say you're one.<br /> <br /> There's a lot to be said for Requiem's books on storytelling, low level personal horror, and more. However, I feel like you can fit Requiem's style into vampire WITHOUT restricting Elder Play and the big epic conspiracy theories that previous editions had. I feel the rules are too restrictive in terms of how much power you can accumulate and also some just flat out don't make sense with what we know of the lore. The Antediluvians and Methuselahs will DESTROY THE WORLD when Gehenna arises and dominate humanity. Ur-Shulgi is so old he terrifies an entire Clan. That isn't really possible with the current rules set.<br /> <br /> Right now, Helena's biggest advantage is the fact that she can use her Disciplines 1-4 without Rouse Checks and while spamming Presence is impressive--it's not exactly godlike.<br /> <br /> I will say that I DO like the changes to feeding and how its impacted by Generation. Generation was previously a purely good thing that everyone should want to have as low as possible. It was the motivation behind large amounts of diablerie and part of the War on Ages. The changes to feeding means that the lower your generation, the more inhuman you are and the less capable of &quot;sustainable feeding&quot; you are. Animals, Blood Bags, the blood of the dead, and so on are all things that higher generation vampires can survive on. It helps add a new dimension to the War of Ages that high generation vampires are likely to keep their Humanity longer.<br /> <br /> It makes the quest for POWER more POWER also even more explicitly one that will turn you into a monster.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Author of <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Cthulhu-Armageddon-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01KUOM7SI/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982844&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Cthulhu+Armageddon\" target=\"_blank\">Cthulhu Armageddon</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Teenage-Weredeer-Bright-Falls-Mysteries-ebook/dp/B075TTN2FN/ref=sr_1_2?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982717&amp;sr=1-2&amp;keywords=Weredeer#customerReviews\" target=\"_blank\">I was a Teenage Weredeer</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Straight-Outta-Fangton-Comedic-Vampire-ebook/dp/B01KNHICCC/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982774&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Straight+Outta+Fangton\" target=\"_blank\">Straight Outta Fangton</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Lucifers-Star-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01MDM9MCT/ref=mt_kindle?_encoding=UTF8&amp;me=&amp;qid=\" target=\"_blank\">Lucifer's Star</a>, </i>and the <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Rules-Supervillainy-Saga-Book-ebook/dp/B07MB89S33/\" target=\"_blank\">Supervillainy Saga</a>.</i><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","name":"CTPhipps","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12002_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13933"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-06-26T10:25:18-07:00","id":1453562,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MyWifeIsScary</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1443592-the-official-v5-vs-v20-thread?p=1453533#post1453533\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">But you see, in that instance, the 7th gen Neonate could just &quot;wait it out&quot;. When he's also 300 years old, he'll have just as much power, so without other factors involved, there's little need to risk the consequences of murder.</div> </div> </div> </div>It depends what benefits you attach to high Blood Potency. In V5, it's a double-edged sword and neonates may decide it's too much risk for too little reward. Under Requiem's Blood Potency, it makes you harder to affect with Disciplines, lets you store and spend more vitae, and has a variety of other lesser benefits (though also increases susceptibility to banes). For many Kindred, that's pretty tempting to obtain right now. 300 years is a lot of time for other factors can get involved. You might not survive that long without an extra edge. <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> As foe vampires getting stronger with age... can't normal discipline accumulation satisfy you there? There is a big difference in V20 between a 13th gen who's 5 and a 13th gen who's 100, and an even bigger difference between a 5th gen who's 5 and a 5th gen who's 1000. &quot;vampires should get stronger with age&quot; is absolutely satisfied with Disciplines. Blood potency is redundant. </div> </div> </div>There is a need for a game trait that establishes how much blood a vampire can store/spend and adds an additional layer of resistance to Disciplines (exact implementation of which varies by system). You can make that generation, but doing so removes incentive for lower-generation neonates to commit diablerie, and imposes a &quot;feat tax&quot; on character concepts by requiring players to spend starting Background dots on it.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://blood-and-bourbon.obsidianportal.com/\" target=\"_blank\">Blood and Bourbon</a>, my New Orleans-based Vampire chronicle.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3110-false-epiphany","name":"False Epiphany","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3110_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"748"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-06-26T10:36:26-07:00","id":1453564,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MyWifeIsScary</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1443592-the-official-v5-vs-v20-thread?p=1453533#post1453533\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">But you see, in that instance, the 7th gen Neonate could just &quot;wait it out&quot;.</div> </div> </div> </div>Both you and Bob from 25 years have brought this up and I'm genuinely confused by this argument. How do you &quot;wait out&quot; vampiredom? One of the most Darwinist, vicious, dog eat dog worlds ever? You diablerize so you can SURVIVE long enough to be 300. Not because you're impatient. I guess I just view undeath as a very dangerous world. Blame all those violent 2nd Edition shoot ups and katana fights.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Author of <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Cthulhu-Armageddon-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01KUOM7SI/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982844&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Cthulhu+Armageddon\" target=\"_blank\">Cthulhu Armageddon</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Teenage-Weredeer-Bright-Falls-Mysteries-ebook/dp/B075TTN2FN/ref=sr_1_2?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982717&amp;sr=1-2&amp;keywords=Weredeer#customerReviews\" target=\"_blank\">I was a Teenage Weredeer</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Straight-Outta-Fangton-Comedic-Vampire-ebook/dp/B01KNHICCC/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982774&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Straight+Outta+Fangton\" target=\"_blank\">Straight Outta Fangton</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Lucifers-Star-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01MDM9MCT/ref=mt_kindle?_encoding=UTF8&amp;me=&amp;qid=\" target=\"_blank\">Lucifer's Star</a>, </i>and the <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Rules-Supervillainy-Saga-Book-ebook/dp/B07MB89S33/\" target=\"_blank\">Supervillainy Saga</a>.</i><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":12002,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","user":"CTPhipps","date":". 06-26-2021, 02:21 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","name":"CTPhipps","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12002_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13933"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-06-26T11:29:28-07:00","id":1453573,"title":"","content":"Kindred Society is Darwinist because generation is coveted. If it isn't coveted, then all you're really fighting over is territory or some personal grudges, and the simplicity of these conflict creates a tendancy to stable out. If everyone has land and there isn't much to gain by persecuting others, vampires won't do it. Sit back, relax, maintain your territory, age up to gain power, and attend the occasional vampire social. If anyone wants to have a power fantasy, there are mortals for that, you don't need to rile up the vampires. Blood potency being more important than generation creates this kind of environment. <br /> <br /> Getting rid of blood potency and putting it all-in on generation creates a fundamental, inescapable conflict for vampire existence. Vampire A embraces Vampire B to fulfil a role that needs doing. Vampire B improves over the years and hits a bottleneck; the only way past this bottleneck is to devour Vampire A. Vampire A, fearing this, Embraces Vampire C to fulfil the role vampire B is performing, and then tries to remove vampire B from the equation. Vampire B, Fearing that, creates vampire D to help him, and tries to usurp vampire A. Vampire B essentially becomes the new vampire A, tries to play vampire D off against vampire C, and things get progressively messier. That's the core of the Jyhad. Without the need, there isn't fear, and without fear, elders aren't screwing over their childer, and without elders screwing over their childer, there is no need.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25794-mywifeisscary","name":"MyWifeIsScary","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25794_2.png","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3711"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-06-26T12:37:41-07:00","id":1453586,"title":"","content":"Kindred society is also Darwinist because every Kindred has a violent psychopathic rage-monster screaming RIP!TEAR!KILL! inside of their soul 24/7. Dipping back into VtR for a second, I actually liked the mechanic where vampires that had never met for the first time had to deal with a feral fight-or-flight moment because it emphasized the animalistic violence inherent in the Kindred that would inevitably have impacts on their social interactions. Not to mention that plenty of people find reasons to fight and kill each other over plenty of things without being vampires that need to maintain control over the source of their power/immortality/addiction. I can't speak to how good or bad V5's Diablerie and Generation mechanics are, but the argument that fighting over Generation via Diablerie is the only realistic motivation for violence and danger in Kindred unlife does not seem reasonable to me.<br /> <br /> P.S. regarding the idea that there's plenty of &quot;land&quot; (aka: herd) to go around, remember that the cities presented in games constantly have vampire populations that significantly exceed the hypothetical &quot;one vampire per fifty thousand humans&quot; ratio that has commonly been stated as ideal or typical. For whatever reason, the cities that we see tend to feature vampire populations that have scarce resources that they will need to struggle to control. I suspect it's because the cities chosen tend to be big cities, therefore seats of influence and power, and therefore vampires interested in gaining power (a lot of them) flock to those areas to fight over it. There is a LOT of potential for conflict between Kindred without even considering the struggle over Generation/Blood Potency. That comes up after, when most vampires find they need that more esoteric power to support their struggle for the more mundane power that gives them a Haven from the sun and Vitae in their veins. Vampires that prioritize mystical or esoteric goals are the exception, not the rule; I say that as someone whose favourite character-types are almost always said exception, but they are the exception.<br /> <br /> Funny enough, Generation was one of the things that led me to VtR before really getting into VtM, because I actually prefer the idea that power comes from age; the First Monster is the baddest mofo because they have been around longer than literally any other member of their species, not because power flows from a &quot;source&quot; only to inevitably degenerate. It's a supernatural version of a theory of history-as-decline that I've grown very tired of hearing. It was something that I accepted as I became attached to other parts of the lore, and more recently I've really leaned into the idea of Generation being part of Caine's Curse (or alternatively, from the Antediluvians), and that some Vampires may not even experience it, such as the Laibon.<br /> <br /> Vampire-as-Gnostic-Empowerment-via-Generation is a neat idea, and fine to put centre at your own table, but a lot of your arguments really seem to lean on it being an obvious thing that everyone should accept, when just as many people don't buy that particular interpretation. And I say that as someone who does actually like that take to some extent, though I tend to prefer the Vampiric Becoming as one of several valid options rather than the only obvious choice.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":25886,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25886-kharnov","user":"Kharnov","date":". 06-26-2021, 03:42 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25886-kharnov","name":"Kharnov","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2020"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"683"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-06-26T12:52:20-07:00","id":1453588,"title":"","content":"I prefer Blood Potency to Generation as well. I never liked the Generation mechanic, which seemed like an extension of Tolkien thinking, where the world becomes less magical every day. Just making Blood Potency very expensive is a plenty enough limiting mechanic without porting in Tolkien style notions of everything being an ever thinner shadow of a Platonic Ideal.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3598-cajunkhan","name":"CajunKhan","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3598_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1700"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-06-26T14:09:00-07:00","id":1453592,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CajunKhan</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1443592-the-official-v5-vs-v20-thread?p=1453588#post1453588\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I prefer Blood Potency to Generation as well. I never liked the Generation mechanic, which seemed like an extension of Tolkien thinking, where the world becomes less magical every day. Just making Blood Potency very expensive is a plenty enough limiting mechanic without porting in Tolkien style notions of everything being an ever thinner shadow of a Platonic Ideal.</div> </div> </div> </div>I think it's actually less Tolkien and more straight up Anne Rice.<br /> <br /> Akasha is the all-powerful godlike 1st Vampire and every vampire after her gets weaker and weaker until they're like Lestat before Lestat drinks his way up to her level.<br /> <br /> And Blood Potency may or may not be a good idea but so much of the game is based around the Ancients being godlike and eventually conquering the world.<br /> <br /> Much of the War of Ages also depends on the fact the Elders can kick Neonates' asses, so Neonates must team up against them.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Author of <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Cthulhu-Armageddon-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01KUOM7SI/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982844&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Cthulhu+Armageddon\" target=\"_blank\">Cthulhu Armageddon</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Teenage-Weredeer-Bright-Falls-Mysteries-ebook/dp/B075TTN2FN/ref=sr_1_2?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982717&amp;sr=1-2&amp;keywords=Weredeer#customerReviews\" target=\"_blank\">I was a Teenage Weredeer</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Straight-Outta-Fangton-Comedic-Vampire-ebook/dp/B01KNHICCC/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982774&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Straight+Outta+Fangton\" target=\"_blank\">Straight Outta Fangton</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Lucifers-Star-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01MDM9MCT/ref=mt_kindle?_encoding=UTF8&amp;me=&amp;qid=\" target=\"_blank\">Lucifer's Star</a>, </i>and the <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Rules-Supervillainy-Saga-Book-ebook/dp/B07MB89S33/\" target=\"_blank\">Supervillainy Saga</a>.</i><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","name":"CTPhipps","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12002_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13933"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-06-26T14:48:19-07:00","id":1453594,"title":"","content":"It's more than an Anne Rice thing, because it runs through all the gamelines. Getting into the umbra is harder and harder and the garou are dying out. Magick becoming ever more static. Banality is ever more of a problem. It's a very Tolkienesque thing where each age is a pale reflection of the age before it..","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3598-cajunkhan","name":"CajunKhan","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3598_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1700"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-06-26T14:52:27-07:00","id":1453595,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CajunKhan</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1443592-the-official-v5-vs-v20-thread?p=1453594#post1453594\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">It's more than an Anne Rice thing, because it runs through all the gamelines. Getting into the umbra is harder and harder and the garou are dying out. Magick becoming ever more static. Banality is ever more of a problem. It's a very Tolkienesque thing where each age is a pale reflection of the age before it..</div> </div> </div> </div>Well it's not the world becoming more static and weak, it's the world is ending and did in 2004. There was a lot of End of the World fever of the 90s that, well, obviously didn't happen.<br /> <br /> (No, we have at least 50 years until we all die out from global warming)<br /> <br /> It's actually a good point, though, that Werewolf is in a bit of a bind as a line because the whole thing is predicated on an Apocalypse that can never come.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Author of <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Cthulhu-Armageddon-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01KUOM7SI/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982844&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Cthulhu+Armageddon\" target=\"_blank\">Cthulhu Armageddon</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Teenage-Weredeer-Bright-Falls-Mysteries-ebook/dp/B075TTN2FN/ref=sr_1_2?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982717&amp;sr=1-2&amp;keywords=Weredeer#customerReviews\" target=\"_blank\">I was a Teenage Weredeer</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Straight-Outta-Fangton-Comedic-Vampire-ebook/dp/B01KNHICCC/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982774&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Straight+Outta+Fangton\" target=\"_blank\">Straight Outta Fangton</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Lucifers-Star-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01MDM9MCT/ref=mt_kindle?_encoding=UTF8&amp;me=&amp;qid=\" target=\"_blank\">Lucifer's Star</a>, </i>and the <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Rules-Supervillainy-Saga-Book-ebook/dp/B07MB89S33/\" target=\"_blank\">Supervillainy Saga</a>.</i><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","name":"CTPhipps","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12002_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13933"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-06-26T23:25:17-07:00","id":1453625,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CTPhipps</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1443592-the-official-v5-vs-v20-thread?p=1453592#post1453592\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I think it's actually less Tolkien and more straight up Anne Rice.<br /> <br /> Akasha is the all-powerful godlike 1st Vampire and every vampire after her gets weaker and weaker until they're like Lestat before Lestat drinks his way up to her level.</div> </div> </div> </div>I would argue that Anne Rice's vampires use Blood Potency instead of generation, but childer start with Blood Potency equal to (sire's -1 -number of recent-ish prior Embraces). Gabrielle is very strong-blooded when Lestat Embraces her, but his best friend is weaker than her, and Louis is weaker still. <br /> <br /> It's an interesting concept that Masquerade didn't carry over. Being the vampire big brother, not just the vampire dad, is better than being the vampire youngest son. Mass Embraces become truly relegated to the lowest of the low. <br /> <br /> Anne Rice also had the concept that drinking a sufficiently ancient elder's blood without diablerizing them (like Mekare does to Akasha) could make vampires more powerful. This actually got carried over to 1e Chicago, where Maldavis was supposed to enjoy incredible powers as a result of drinking multiple elders' super-blood, but lost those powers after the elders stopped feeding her. There weren't any firm mechanics to back it up and the concept was never referenced in future supplements. (Possibly because, why wouldn't elders do that sort of thing regularly with favored pawns?)","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://blood-and-bourbon.obsidianportal.com/\" target=\"_blank\">Blood and Bourbon</a>, my New Orleans-based Vampire chronicle.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3110-false-epiphany","name":"False Epiphany","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3110_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"748"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-06-27T00:58:23-07:00","id":1453632,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CajunKhan</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1443592-the-official-v5-vs-v20-thread?p=1453588#post1453588\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I prefer Blood Potency to Generation as well. I never liked the Generation mechanic, which seemed like an extension of Tolkien thinking, where the world becomes less magical every day. Just making Blood Potency very expensive is a plenty enough limiting mechanic without porting in Tolkien style notions of everything being an ever thinner shadow of a Platonic Ideal.</div> </div> </div> </div>I too don't like Tolkien's &quot;The past was great and it's just gonna get worse unless we return to how things were somehow&quot; but I don't really feel the WoD was entirely going that way. If anything, I think the WoD has a more grounded way of looking at this kind of thing. Think of historical Dynasties. Usually, they start strong, they decline over generations (or a single ruler, since a long reign gives plenty of time for faculties to decline, especially with the medical knowledge of the time) and after enough declining, either someone makes a glorious revival, or the next dynasty rises up and kicks them out. In some cases I'm in with the Gnostic idea (at some point the thinbloods will rise up, devour their way to thickness, become the new 5th gens, embrace prodigiously, &quot;revive&quot; the kindred race and make an attempt to slay god.) but in most cases the more mundane solutions are king<br /> <br /> The other splats are easier to discuss. <br /> The Garou are looking forward to the apocalypse because it'll come with a big societal change (edit: Also note that when the Garou pine for their glorious past, it's usually implied that they're full of shit)<br /> The Garou nation will be revitalized when the silver fangs exit leadership and the shadowlords take the helm. The shadow lords will lead extroadinarily well at first but will eventually plague themselves with infighting and hobbling the strong to maintain their rule. The Shadow lords will be replaced by... erhm... some tribe that only forms in the future.<br /> Alternatively, a different breed will oust the dominance of the Garou. Perhaps the Ratkin, perhaps Pentex will charge forth and make some better mockery breeds. Perhaps with bats redemption the Bat changers will return, or the Grondr will come back, or perhaps Gaia will make something new like she did with the Foxes.<br /> <br /> As for mage, the Technocrats are really just hinging on the next big thing. There are so many technologies that currently elude us mortals, so many bottlenecks, but once a breakthrough is made, massive opertunities are opened among Technocrats. Just think; if humans just found -the next battery- then Hit Marks, Exoskelletons, Cybernetics... they all lose their vulgarity (so long as you aren't giving them plasma guns) which opens up the options of making.. MORE heinous mechanical monstrosities. Once the mortals can work out how to make Gunther Hermann, the Mages can more easily create JC Denton. As for Traditions, as we all get wrapped up in ever more wonderful fantasy media, does that not decrease the vulgarity of Tradition based magic?<br /> <br /> Gnostic thought, but there's a nice little pattern to some of this stuff too<br /> -Reality's a prison.<br /> -Divine figures come into this prison to help us get out.<br /> -Divine figures progressively become more mundane as they too become trapped in the prison<br /> -At the lowest point, the figure makes a U turn and soars up back to divinity<br /> - The figure tries to break the prison.<br /> <br /> We're at stage 3, and it seems the splats are waiting for the next step. The Garou eagerly await their apocalypse, the mages await their ascension...<br /> <br /> Lastly<br /> Devouring your way to God is a lot cooler than waiting.<br /> Maybe someone'll uncover a super-unethical ritual to rise in generation. There was this wonderful new age ritual in rites of the blood...","signature":"","edited":{"userid":25794,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25794-mywifeisscary","user":"MyWifeIsScary","date":". 06-28-2021, 04:53 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25794-mywifeisscary","name":"MyWifeIsScary","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25794_2.png","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3711"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-06-28T02:15:05-07:00","id":1453687,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Kharnov</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1443592-the-official-v5-vs-v20-thread?p=1453586#post1453586\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> P.S. regarding the idea that there's plenty of &quot;land&quot; (aka: herd) to go around, remember that the cities presented in games constantly have vampire populations that significantly exceed the hypothetical &quot;one vampire per fifty thousand humans&quot; ratio that has commonly been stated as ideal or typical. For whatever reason, the cities that we see tend to feature vampire populations that have scarce resources that they will need to struggle to control. I suspect it's because the cities chosen tend to be big cities, therefore seats of influence and power, and therefore vampires interested in gaining power (a lot of them) flock to those areas to fight over it. There is a LOT of potential for conflict between Kindred without even considering the struggle over Generation/Blood Potency. That comes up after, when most vampires find they need that more esoteric power to support their struggle for the more mundane power that gives them a Haven from the sun and Vitae in their veins. Vampires that prioritize mystical or esoteric goals are the exception, not the rule; I say that as someone whose favourite character-types are almost always said exception, but they are the exception.<br /> .</div> </div> </div> </div>Kindred cities are overpopulated precisely because of the Generational struggle I outlined earlier: Vampires embrace, primarily, to achieve their goals. Without the generational conflict, vampires will embrace a little more than just-enough, but nowhere near overpopulation levels. Because of the Generation conflict, vampires embrace surplus kindred; To replace vampires with important functions who are growing too powerful, to keep the neonates fighting one another, to help them take down a rival, or because their rival is embracing and if they end up outnumbered things will go badly for them. <br /> <br /> Diablerie/The threat of Diablerie is, like wealth divides for mortals, is the catalyst for most vampire ills. Overpopulation? Generation. Not enough territory? Generation. Corrupt leadership? Generation. Gang violence? Generation. Asssamites flooding into the city? Generation. You live in an undead society where the method to advance is to canibalize eachother; that's going to dictate all policies going forward. That's the real curse of Caine. Marx would have a field day with VTM vampires.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":6}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25794-mywifeisscary","name":"MyWifeIsScary","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25794_2.png","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3711"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-06-28T10:19:42-07:00","id":1453702,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MyWifeIsScary</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1443592-the-official-v5-vs-v20-thread?p=1453687#post1453687\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Kindred cities are overpopulated precisely because of the Generational struggle I outlined earlier: Vampires embrace, primarily, to achieve their goals. Without the generational conflict, vampires will embrace a little more than just-enough, but nowhere near overpopulation levels. Because of the Generation conflict, vampires embrace surplus kindred; To replace vampires with important functions who are growing too powerful, to keep the neonates fighting one another, to help them take down a rival, or because their rival is embracing and if they end up outnumbered things will go badly for them.<br /> <br /> Diablerie/The threat of Diablerie is, like wealth divides for mortals, is the catalyst for most vampire ills. Overpopulation? Generation. Not enough territory? Generation. Corrupt leadership? Generation. Gang violence? Generation. Asssamites flooding into the city? Generation. You live in an undead society where the method to advance is to canibalize eachother; that's going to dictate all policies going forward. That's the real curse of Caine. Marx would have a field day with VTM vampires.</div> </div> </div> </div>Caine literally Embraced Zillah because he was horny. (P.S. 2/3 of Caine's 'canon' Embraces were definitely emotional, not pragmatic, matter of fact) &quot;I did it for silly human emotional reasons&quot; is one of the major categories of Embraces, especially among Clans like the Toreador. Not to mention the whole Cleopatra thing among the Nosferatu.<br /> <br /> One of our biggest viewpoint characters in the entire series is a bookworm, whose only interest in Generation is purely academic: Beckett.<br /> <br /> This is precisely what I mean. I don't deny that Generation and conflicts over it via Diablerie are important in the movements of Kindred politics and society. But acting like everything is a consequence of it is incredibly reductive and ignores a significant amount of the existing lore.<br /> <br /> P.S. I also wonder if this is precisely why the &quot;let one friend diablerize someone for low Generation, then have them Embrace a bunch of schmucks for us to diablerize for lower Generation&quot; is something that doesn't generally seem to come up in the lore, and is instead relegated to player theory-crafting. Players just looking to game the system for power are OOC, whereas the idea that diablerie is supposed to be monstrous crime is predominantly expressed IC (And yes MWiS, I am aware of your position that Diablerie-as-Super-Evil came from later editions, but I'm inclined to agree with that later interpretation). If you choose to target an elder vampire for diablerie, you are almost certainly going to be able to find *some* kind of excuse or mitigating factor to justify what you are doing to yourself, to some extent. But taking a bunch of innocent randos and turning them into diablerie-juice-boxes is just exponentially more soulless, the sort of thing reserved for the vilest of the vile, even among the Kindred.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":25886,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25886-kharnov","user":"Kharnov","date":". 06-28-2021, 01:42 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25886-kharnov","name":"Kharnov","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2020"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"683"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-06-28T11:26:21-07:00","id":1453707,"title":"","content":"Caine's embraces occured when he was completely alone, and as a god-like figure it's unlikely he would've needed to embrace for some pragmatic reason (We can also dispute how real the caine myth is, but the point being his circumstances are completely different from those that came later)<br /> <br /> And yes, obviously I don't believe that all embraces are purely rational choices. I wrote &quot;vampires will embrace a little more than just-enough, but nowhere near overpopulation levels&quot; not &quot;Vampires will perfectly control their population and be perfectly rational about it&quot;. The Attrition rate for non-strategic embraces are going to be naturally higher; suicide/childer-cide occurs frequently with those that aren't cut out for the embrace, and there's still going to be a prince trying to police numbers even without Generation creating a fundamental conflict. You're still going to have population increases and the occasional population pressure, but it's not to the extent you'd have with Generation.<br /> <br /> I believe the -let's mass embrace for my palls to diablerize their way to one-below-me- Is rare, because naturally, the person at the top then becomes the next obvious target, especially as the beneficiaries of such a ritual are going to take some hits to their humanity and may have their mindset shift resulting (in later editions, Diablerie is terribly addicting, something I use to a lesser extent in order to take a middle ground) You don't necessarily have to use &quot;Innocent&quot; people. Criminals, perceived criminals, or the victim's ghouls, who will need to be dealt with anyway, are likely options.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25794-mywifeisscary","name":"MyWifeIsScary","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25794_2.png","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3711"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-06-28T11:52:05-07:00","id":1453709,"title":"","content":"The point that Caine is somewhat unique in terms of not needing to Embrace for pragmatic reasons is fair, but the point was also to demonstrate just how core the idea of emotional Embraces are to the story.<br /> <br /> My point is that your statement is an assumption. We don't have hard numbers for the ratio of pragmatic Embraces to emotional ones, AFAIK. You are assuming that the vast majority are pragmatic because it fits your conception of the game. Unless there is a source that gives those hard numbers, this is simply a matter of Storyteller discretion, which is precisely what I am getting at every time I point out that a lot of your arguments about how V5 OBVIOUSLY doesn't make sense actually seem to be more based on how you have chosen to settle ambiguous facets of the setting in your personal canon.<br /> <br /> I wasn't clear, sorry, but I'm trying to get at more than just a simple dichotomy of &quot;innocent vs. guilty, good vs. bad, deserves it vs. not.&quot; My point is that the justification you will have for going after an elder is far more likely to be personal. They are likely an impediment or a threat in some fashion to you or your goals, even if it simply by virtue of existing as a powerful potential rival. It's not an emotionless calculation that someone else's life and soul can be thrown into a meatgrinder for your personal advancement. Morality is a complicated issue, and Diablerie-as-Ultimate-Evil is obviously not universally accepted among Kindred, the Banu Haqim and Lasombra Courts of Blood being the chief examples of pro-Diablerie authorities. I can also agree that the bodies regulating Diablerie are likely concerned more with the pragmatic consequences of out-of-control Diablerie than they are with the ethical problems. But I still think there's a significant difference between choosing an extreme course of action under circumstances not of your making versus the decision to actively create the circumstances in cold blood.<br /> <br /> P.S. I'm also willing to concede that pragmatic Embraces are a much better model for the behaviour of some Clans than others. Ventrue, Tremere, Tzimisce, those are clans where pragmatic Embraces and considerable concern over Generation make sense. But the Brujah, Malkavians, Toreador? Their Embraces are far less likely to involve Machiavellian calculations regarding pawns for the Jyhad. And plenty of other Clans probably fall in the middle.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":25886,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25886-kharnov","user":"Kharnov","date":". 06-28-2021, 02:57 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25886-kharnov","name":"Kharnov","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2020"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"683"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-06-28T12:24:42-07:00","id":1453710,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Kharnov</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1443592-the-official-v5-vs-v20-thread?p=1453709#post1453709\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The point that Caine is somewhat unique in terms of not needing to Embrace for pragmatic reasons is fair, but the point was also to demonstrate just how core the idea of emotional Embraces are to the story.</div> </div> </div> </div>Honestly, it's part of the setting that pragmatism actually has very little to do with the Embrace and that those that DO Embrace for pragmatic reasons aren't necessarily making the smart decision. One of the themes of Chicago by Night 1st Edition was that Lodin wanted to control the entire city with his massive brood of Ventrue and while he did Embrace solely on what he perceived as power and ability, that didn't always work. Jacob Schumpeter was a complete fool that was just good at keeping up appearances, Drummond was mono-focused on trains and useless at anything else, and Kevin Jackson was someone that Lodin underestimated terribly because he assumed gangs were just what Kevin was good at versus something he used as a substitute in lieu of achieving something in another field were he afforded opportunities.<br /> <br /> (Which is to say Kevin Jackson was only a gang leader because of institutional racism)<br /> <br /> You can't really predict what the Embrace will do to people. One thing VTM is better at than Requiem is that Requiem says you can't change and are frozen as who you were. VTM suggests that you may become a WHOLLY DIFFERENT PERSON because of the Embrace and your past self becomes meaningless.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Author of <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Cthulhu-Armageddon-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01KUOM7SI/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982844&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Cthulhu+Armageddon\" target=\"_blank\">Cthulhu Armageddon</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Teenage-Weredeer-Bright-Falls-Mysteries-ebook/dp/B075TTN2FN/ref=sr_1_2?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982717&amp;sr=1-2&amp;keywords=Weredeer#customerReviews\" target=\"_blank\">I was a Teenage Weredeer</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Straight-Outta-Fangton-Comedic-Vampire-ebook/dp/B01KNHICCC/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982774&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Straight+Outta+Fangton\" target=\"_blank\">Straight Outta Fangton</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Lucifers-Star-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01MDM9MCT/ref=mt_kindle?_encoding=UTF8&amp;me=&amp;qid=\" target=\"_blank\">Lucifer's Star</a>, </i>and the <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Rules-Supervillainy-Saga-Book-ebook/dp/B07MB89S33/\" target=\"_blank\">Supervillainy Saga</a>.</i><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","name":"CTPhipps","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12002_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13933"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-06-28T13:50:14-07:00","id":1453715,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MyWifeIsScary</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1443592-the-official-v5-vs-v20-thread?p=1453480#post1453480\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"> I can't help but think of Zack Snyder's <i>Man of Steel</i>. When I first watched it I didn't know much about Superman. It was a decent film. It had some very big flaws, but I thought Snyder and co did a lot of things very well. Then later I binged <i>Superman: The Animated series</i>, and with this newfound understanding of Superman,<i> Man of Steel</i> becomes a terrible Superman film. It's still a good, though by no means excellent film, but it's bad as a <i>S</i><i>uperman </i>film. To someone who knows superman a little better, Clark Kent is not obviously Superman and his disguise isn't just a pair of Glasses. Lois Lane, Award winning journalist, and Lex Luthor, world's most accomplished man, are both totally fooled by his disguise: This is something that bothers the layman, because to them the disguise is just a pair of Glasses, and no effort is made to give an all-too-handsome Henry Cavil a not-superman look for Clark Kent. but to someone that has greater knowledge of superman, having Lois Lane easily discover that CK is Superman is like... Telling an Egyptologist the pyramids were made by aliens. IDFK. A lot of the changes in V5 feel like Lois Lane easily discovering that CK is Superman, which seems internally reasonable to some people because &quot;CK&quot; isn't CK in V5. &quot;Clark Kent&quot; Is Wrong in V5, thus Lois Lane is rather reasonable in her discovery.</div> </div> </div> </div>I think this is a great analogy, but I want to throw two coin on top to illustrate how it can be taken a completely different way.<br /> <br /> You didn't know much about Superman, you liked Man of Steel, and then engaged with one of the multiple takes on Superman and came away with what you felt was an understanding of the character that invalidated the Snyder film. You expanded on some of the concepts of the character and it made you recoil from the way the character was presented in that film. <br /> <br /> You don't however seem to have delved deeply into Superman lore across the entirety of his 80 years to see that there are distinct difference between the Silver Age styled depiction that was in Bruce Timm's Animated series, the Bronze age depiction of the pre-Donner film Superman, the Bronze age reboot of the post Donner film Superman, the Modern age version of the character where he is very much the same figure whether he's in the suit or not and the the various tweaks to that character that have spawned since.<br /> <br /> Taken in the complete totality of Superman's arc from street level smasher of slum-lords to earth juggling demigod Man of Steel's presentation works just as well as S:TAS because they're both trying to construct different narratives with different types of viewer applicability.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> I don't know enough about requiem, but to me, it just seems like V5 wants to... how do I articulate this in compliance with forum rules...<br /> I feel the writers didn't like a lot of the setting and wanted to &quot;Fix&quot; it.<br /> I feel the setting no longer reflects reality as well as prior editions. </div> </div> </div>In absence of knowledge about how BP works in V:tR you are weighing it against past interpretations of the setting and seeing it as invalid in the context you're looking at it. This however is a lot like the Superman analogy in that your context is not necessarily the broadest or most applicable. The way that BP is utilized in Requiem, the way it utilized in V5 and the way Generation is utilized elsewhere are all equally valid because the narratives they are attempting to construct are slightly different. One doesn't necessarily invalidate the other or show that the creator of one had low regard for the other.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> If everyone has land and there isn't much to gain by persecuting others, vampires won't do it. Sit back, relax, maintain your territory, age up to gain power, and attend the occasional vampire social. If anyone wants to have a power fantasy, there are mortals for that, you don't need to rile up the vampires. Blood potency being more important than generation creates this kind of environment. </div> </div> </div>BP doesn't create that kind of environment in Requiem, so I'm not sure why it would in Masquerade.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23889-dirtypoolfilms","name":"dirtypoolfilms","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"36"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-06-28T14:08:47-07:00","id":1453716,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CTPhipps</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1443592-the-official-v5-vs-v20-thread?p=1453710#post1453710\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">You can't really predict what the Embrace will do to people. One thing VTM is better at than Requiem is that Requiem says you can't change and are frozen as who you were. VTM suggests that you may become a WHOLLY DIFFERENT PERSON because of the Embrace and your past self becomes meaningless.</div> </div> </div> </div>Where is that stated in Requiem?<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Requiem 2e CRB Chapter 3 Laws of the Dead</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\"><span style=\"font-family:GoudyOldStyleT\">Kindred are not human. They were, once, but now they\u2019re something entirely different. However, to blend in with mortals, to walk among the flock, Kindred must maintain perspective and understanding of their former lives.</span></div> </div> </div> </div><span style=\"font-family:GoudyOldStyleT\"><br /> <br /> In Requiem you already became a different entity, something completely removed from what you were. If you don't want to fall to the depravity that you immediately feel pulled toward becoming, you have to wear some semblance of what you once were like a suit that grows more and more threadbare the more you put it on. That game is entirely about a struggle between what you were, what you are, and what you inevitably will become. There is no sense of being frozen in place. </span> <br /> <br /> <br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23889-dirtypoolfilms","name":"dirtypoolfilms","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"36"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-06-28T14:45:46-07:00","id":1453722,"title":"","content":"I believe &quot;you are no longer you, just a memory of you warped by the Beast which struggles to change and grow&quot; was a feature of VtR 1E that was removed for 2E.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25886-kharnov","name":"Kharnov","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2020"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"683"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-06-28T14:55:05-07:00","id":1453724,"title":"","content":"In 2e when you are embraced you completely cease to be the human that you once were, and you begin to need to use touchstones to force yourself to remember what the experience of humanity and your own life was like so that you don't devolve into more and more of a monster. That description is supported by the quote I included from the 2nd edition Core Rulebook and bares no resemblance to being unable to change because you are &quot;frozen as you were&quot;","signature":"","edited":{"userid":23889,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23889-dirtypoolfilms","user":"dirtypoolfilms","date":".  edited to point out initial reference to 2e core. 06-28-2021, 05:57 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23889-dirtypoolfilms","name":"dirtypoolfilms","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"36"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-06-28T16:15:54-07:00","id":1453727,"title":"","content":"A lot of weird changes for VTR 2.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Author of <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Cthulhu-Armageddon-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01KUOM7SI/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982844&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Cthulhu+Armageddon\" target=\"_blank\">Cthulhu Armageddon</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Teenage-Weredeer-Bright-Falls-Mysteries-ebook/dp/B075TTN2FN/ref=sr_1_2?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982717&amp;sr=1-2&amp;keywords=Weredeer#customerReviews\" target=\"_blank\">I was a Teenage Weredeer</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Straight-Outta-Fangton-Comedic-Vampire-ebook/dp/B01KNHICCC/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982774&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Straight+Outta+Fangton\" target=\"_blank\">Straight Outta Fangton</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Lucifers-Star-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01MDM9MCT/ref=mt_kindle?_encoding=UTF8&amp;me=&amp;qid=\" target=\"_blank\">Lucifer's Star</a>, </i>and the <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Rules-Supervillainy-Saga-Book-ebook/dp/B07MB89S33/\" target=\"_blank\">Supervillainy Saga</a>.</i><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","name":"CTPhipps","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12002_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13933"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-06-28T16:30:01-07:00","id":1453728,"title":"","content":"I'm not sure how it's weird. VtR 2e just dumped a bunch of VtM holdovers to make VtR more sensible holistically. VtR is a setting with 2/5 of its main political factions as ones dedicated to change (externally with the Carthians, internally with the Ordo), and another that isn't focused on change, but considers vampires part of nature and nature is something that does change over time (the Circle). Dumping the holdover stuff around being unchanging static creatures helps make the default setting make more sense.<br /> <br /> <br /> But something, something, something.... VtM focused thread? VtM has always focused on how unchanging vampires are if left to their own devices. Elders lose touch with modern reality. Power stagnates at the top. Etc. I don't really see any edition really bucking these things in VtM. Some stress it differently than others, but VtM has always used the concept of vampires-as-static as part of setting up the conflicts of the game (and esp. how big changes are so disruptive to vampire society).","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-06-28T16:38:47-07:00","id":1453729,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CTPhipps</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1443592-the-official-v5-vs-v20-thread?p=1453727#post1453727\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">A lot of weird changes for VTR 2.</div> </div> </div> </div>However so?<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/9015-zee-patrick","name":"zee PaTrick","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"56"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-06-28T20:04:11-07:00","id":1453739,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CTPhipps</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1443592-the-official-v5-vs-v20-thread?p=1453727#post1453727\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">A lot of weird changes for VTR 2.</div> </div> </div> </div>For it to be a \u201cweird change\u201d Requiem would have to have presented Vampires as these unchanging things frozen at the moment of death as you claimed.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Requiem First Edition Corebook</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\"> While a vampire might believe that he feels an emotion, what he actually feels is the echo of mortal emotions that the remnants of his soul apply to his current experience.</div> </div> </div> </div><div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Requiem First Edition Corebook</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\"> The change from life to undeath affects more than a person\u2019s body. It changes the soul. A Kindred shares his human con- sciousness with a force completely opposite to humanity \u2014 a thing devoid of reason, conscience or any emotions except hunger and rage. Kindred call it the Beast.<br /> The presence of the Beast changes the very nature of mo- rality for vampires. The Kindred can pretend to be human, but they are not. Even the most evil and monstrous mortal does not have a Beast. A vampire\u2019s existence is a constant struggle between the Man, the aspect of a Kindred that can make moral choices, and the Beast, which cannot.<br /> The Beast follows a simple plan: Hunt. Kill. Feed. Sleep. Re- peat. It feels no pity, only thirst for blood. It cannot even speak.<br /> The Man consists of everything that resists the Beast: ratio- nal thought, a conscience, and most of all the ability to relate to other people. The Beast does not understand what other people think or feel, and it doesn\u2019t care.</div> </div> </div> </div>The Humanity system in that edition is likewise predicated on the idea that the vampire is fundamentally changed into something other than what the were at the moment of embrace, something they struggle to not succumb to.<br /> <br /> Both editions present a series of questions to consider during character creation - one of the first questions in both is \u201cHow did the Embrace change your character?\u201d<br /> <br /> Requiem in both iterations is a game about trying nightly to affect change on the world in an attempt to offset the impending change to yourself.<br /> <br /> Never really saw it as a game about a static figure unable to grow or change, but I\u2019d be happy to consider any passages you\u2019d like to quote.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23889-dirtypoolfilms","name":"dirtypoolfilms","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"36"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-06-29T00:20:45-07:00","id":1453745,"title":"","content":"<a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25886-kharnov\" style=\"background-image:url('data:image/svg+xml;base64,');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"25886\" data-vbnamecard=\"25886\">Kharnov</a> You're rather refreshing to argue with. I had a longer post but I lost it and I'm upset so I'll try send the gist. <br /> <br /> First, the issue of who's embraced for practical reasons and who's embraced on a whim is difficult because really, there's a scale. A vampire may need a childer for something and yet pick a &quot;romantic&quot; option because, well, why not go with instinct? A lot of &quot;romantic&quot; type embraces would really be from people that the vampire feels is well inclined to be -insert clan here-, especially as vampires tend to stay in their own subcultures and meet a lot of likeminded people that they'll often favour. Even with Cleopatras, the childer isn't just chosen because she's beautiful, few get torn down just for that, but because the childer-to-be is a scheming vindictive bitch that'll fit right in. If the childer is even half a good choice, the sire will have the opportunity to mold the childer into a good choice during their tutalage period. To complicate issues, A lot of sires will lie to their childer; A vampire may insist he has deeply practical reasons to embrace someone he took in on a whim to save himself embarrassment while another vampire might tell a strategic embrace that they chose them for romantic reasons to hide their intentions and garner loyalty. <br /> <br /> The ones that really, really don't fit in are going to have higher attrition rates. So most 'Romantic' embraces will turn to &quot;practical&quot; embraces.<br /> <br /> Now, how does this relate to Generational conflict? <br /> Because the crippling alienation brought about by the Generational conflict drives kindred to create emotional embraces. Its comparative to income disparity in the real world. <br /> A lot of crime and deviance isn't immediately practical. A lot of low-income kids at school behave poorly, not because they're stupid (though a good chunk of them are), but because they believe the system has failed them, the teachers are against them, the values of the system are thus wrong, and that to 'succeed' they need to work by their own values; toughness, comedic skills, promiscuity, an inordinate amount of attention on expensive branded clothing; these signify success. As the rest of society further alienates them, they lash out more. To the establishment, these people are failures, but to them and their peers, they are successful, because they've built up groups that celebrate what they see as success. A Vandal doesn't break stuff for money (usually) but to feel better. Similarly, as vampires find themselves marginalized by their elders or hated by their childer, they feel alienated, and as they feel alienated, they need to create support networks around them. The more horrific kindred society is, the more vampires are going to do seemingly irrational moves like sire childer for love. The more accepting vampire society becomes, the less vampires will lash out or need to build their own support networks. Desire for Generation really does an amazing job at keeping things messy, just like divides between rich and poor keep things messy in the real world. From a sociological point of view, Generation makes things wonderfully interesting, while blood potency really mitigates the Jyhad. <br /> <br /> <i>This goes really well with explaining Ravnos/Sabbat actually.... </i>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":25794,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25794-mywifeisscary","user":"MyWifeIsScary","date":". 06-29-2021, 08:57 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25794-mywifeisscary","name":"MyWifeIsScary","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25794_2.png","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3711"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-06-29T07:59:22-07:00","id":1453755,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>dirtypoolfilms</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1443592-the-official-v5-vs-v20-thread?p=1453739#post1453739\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> For it to be a \u201cweird change\u201d Requiem would have to have presented Vampires as these unchanging things frozen at the moment of death as you claimed.</div> </div> </div> </div>I'm confused because the first line you quote is literally what I was referring to.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Author of <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Cthulhu-Armageddon-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01KUOM7SI/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982844&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Cthulhu+Armageddon\" target=\"_blank\">Cthulhu Armageddon</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Teenage-Weredeer-Bright-Falls-Mysteries-ebook/dp/B075TTN2FN/ref=sr_1_2?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982717&amp;sr=1-2&amp;keywords=Weredeer#customerReviews\" target=\"_blank\">I was a Teenage Weredeer</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Straight-Outta-Fangton-Comedic-Vampire-ebook/dp/B01KNHICCC/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982774&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Straight+Outta+Fangton\" target=\"_blank\">Straight Outta Fangton</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Lucifers-Star-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01MDM9MCT/ref=mt_kindle?_encoding=UTF8&amp;me=&amp;qid=\" target=\"_blank\">Lucifer's Star</a>, </i>and the <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Rules-Supervillainy-Saga-Book-ebook/dp/B07MB89S33/\" target=\"_blank\">Supervillainy Saga</a>.</i><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","name":"CTPhipps","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12002_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13933"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-06-29T08:52:15-07:00","id":1453756,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CTPhipps</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1443592-the-official-v5-vs-v20-thread?p=1453755#post1453755\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I'm confused because the first line you quote is literally what I was referring to.</div> </div> </div> </div>That's even more confusing because &quot;<i>While a vampire might believe that he feels an emotion, what he actually feels is the echo of mortal emotions that the remnants of his soul apply to his current experience.&quot;</i> =/= &quot;you can't change and are frozen as who you were.&quot; <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23889-dirtypoolfilms","name":"dirtypoolfilms","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"36"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-06-29T10:32:33-07:00","id":1453763,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MyWifeIsScary</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1443592-the-official-v5-vs-v20-thread?p=1453745#post1453745\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25886-kharnov\" style=\"background-image:url('data:image/svg+xml;base64,');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"25886\" data-vbnamecard=\"25886\">Kharnov</a> You're rather refreshing to argue with. I had a longer post but I lost it and I'm upset so I'll try send the gist.<br /> First, the issue of who's embraced for practical reasons and who's embraced on a whim is difficult because really, there's a scale. A vampire may need a childer for something and yet pick a &quot;romantic&quot; option because, well, why not go with instinct? A lot of &quot;romantic&quot; type embraces would really be from people that the vampire feels is well inclined to be -insert clan here-, especially as vampires tend to stay in their own subcultures and meet a lot of likeminded people that they'll often favour. Even with Cleopatras, the childer isn't just chosen because she's beautiful, few get torn down just for that, but because the childer-to-be is a scheming vindictive bitch that'll fit right in. If the childer is even half a good choice, the sire will have the opportunity to mold the childer into a good choice during their tutalage period. To complicate issues, A lot of sires will lie to their childer; A vampire may insist he has deeply practical reasons to embrace someone he took in on a whim to save himself embarrassment while another vampire might tell a strategic embrace that they chose them for romantic reasons to hide their intentions and garner loyalty.<br /> <br /> The ones that really, really don't fit in are going to have higher attrition rates. So most 'Romantic' embraces will turn to &quot;practical&quot; embraces.</div> </div> </div> </div>I can absolutely agree that &quot;practical Embrace&quot; versus &quot;emotional Embrace&quot; is a bit of a false dichotomy, and that many Embraces contain elements of both. I don't necessarily agree with your claim about Cleopatras being chosen because they're &quot;scheming vindictive bitches who'll fit right in&quot;; the closest I have ever seen to a statement supporting that is the idea that some Cleopatras are chosen because their Sire thinks they are leaning too much on their beauty and wasting their other talents. But even that seems more like a personal judgment than a pragmatic calculation that the fledgling will be an asset, IMO.<br /> <br /> I also don't think that discussing later developments is relevant to the question of why there were chosen for the Embrace; circumstances ending the emotional value and leaving only the pragmatic value do not change the decision-making process of an Embrace that happened in the past. Similarly, the ability of someone subjected to an emotional Embrace to survive does not nullify the fact that their Embrace was primarily emotional, it's just good fortune for the recipient.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MyWifeIsScary</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1443592-the-official-v5-vs-v20-thread?p=1453745#post1453745\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Now, how does this relate to Generational conflict?<br /> Because the crippling alienation brought about by the Generational conflict drives kindred to create emotional embraces. Its comparative to income disparity in the real world.<br /> A lot of crime and deviance isn't immediately practical. A lot of low-income kids at school behave poorly, not because they're stupid (though a good chunk of them are), but because they believe the system has failed them, the teachers are against them, the values of the system are thus wrong, and that to 'succeed' they need to work by their own values; toughness, comedic skills, promiscuity, an inordinate amount of attention on expensive branded clothing; these signify success. As the rest of society further alienates them, they lash out more. To the establishment, these people are failures, but to them and their peers, they are successful, because they've built up groups that celebrate what they see as success. A Vandal doesn't break stuff for money (usually) but to feel better. Similarly, as vampires find themselves marginalized by their elders or hated by their childer, they feel alienated, and as they feel alienated, they need to create support networks around them. The more horrific kindred society is, the more vampires are going to do seemingly irrational moves like sire childer for love. The more accepting vampire society becomes, the less vampires will lash out or need to build their own support networks. Desire for Generation really does an amazing job at keeping things messy, just like divides between rich and poor keep things messy in the real world. From a sociological point of view, Generation makes things wonderfully interesting, while blood potency really mitigates the Jyhad.<br /> <br /> <i>This goes really well with explaining Ravnos/Sabbat actually.... </i></div> </div> </div> </div>To go back to one of my favourite examples, Beckett sired a childer purely out of spite. He literally took someone with the skills to hunt him down and kill him, and then turned them into a super-powered immortal with a personal grudge against him, because she pissed him off. Once again, it has nothing to do with Generational conflict.<br /> <br /> And again, I think you are assuming that Generation is the primary cause of Kindred conflict when Havens and Vitae are equally good explanation, arguably better given your focus on economic metaphors. Generation is capital, but Haven and Vitae are food and shelter. People fighting purely over capital, with little to no interest in the basic necessities that can be secured by capital, are extremely rare. People who only care about food or shelter are often co-opted into the struggles of people fighting over capital because the people holding the capital hold a significant amount of power and influence, but that doesn't mean that capital is their primary concern. I would argue that Generation is similar.<br /> <br /> I'm not arguing against the idea that Generation has a significant impact on Kindred conflict. I am denying the position that it is the primary or defining motive/influence. And I think we have too many examples of Kindred who don't give a damn about climbing the Generation ladder through Diablerie for that argument to be dismissed without strong evidence to the contrary.<br /> <br /> P.S. <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23889-dirtypoolfilms\" style=\"background-image:url('data:image/svg+xml;base64,');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"23889\" data-vbnamecard=\"23889\">dirtypoolfilms</a> I'm currently looking through the core book, and so far I haven't found it come right out and say it, it's more tidbits here and there:<br /> <br /> &quot;Some Kindred Embrace to preserve a mortal\u2019s talents, only to find that the Embrace renders that childe unable to reach the apex of her living abilities.&quot; (VtR Core 1E, 21)<br /> <br /> &quot;If part of the curse of undeath is stagnation and stasis, then the Kindred must be willing to change and adapt to the times if they are to endure.&quot; (VtR Core 1E, 47)<br /> <br /> I think Vampires generally had to pay more XP for things than mortals did as well, IIRC. If you really want some evidence, I would recommend checking out the 1E Ordo Dracul book; maybe they focus more on overcoming weaknesses in 2E, but change in opposition to the stagnation of the Kindred condition was explicitly part of their mission originally; hair dye and tattoos were considered good example of beginner-level experimentation for a Dragon. Maybe the book on Elders had something as well? Been a while since I was following Requiem.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":25886,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25886-kharnov","user":"Kharnov","date":". 06-29-2021, 01:42 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25886-kharnov","name":"Kharnov","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2020"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"683"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-06-29T11:00:08-07:00","id":1453767,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Kharnov</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1443592-the-official-v5-vs-v20-thread?p=1453763#post1453763\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> &quot;Some Kindred Embrace to preserve a mortal\u2019s talents, only to find that the Embrace renders that childe unable to reach the apex of her living abilities.&quot; (VtR Core 1E, 21)<br /> <br /> &quot;If part of the curse of undeath is stagnation and stasis, then the Kindred must be willing to change and adapt to the times if they are to endure.&quot; (VtR Core 1E, 47)</div> </div> </div> </div>Neither of these really says what what claimed. Embracing someone to preserve their talents means preserving access to their knowledge and experience not freezing them in amber so they do not change. Discovering that the childe is unable to reach the apex of their living abilities can mean many things, not the least of which is they stop pursuing it because their priorities change post embrace.<br /> <br /> The stasis and stagnation bit is talking about the stagnation of the nightly routine of the damned and the stasis of the body. Not of the personality.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> I think Vampires generally had to pay more XP for things than mortals did as well, IIRC. If you really want some evidence, I would recommend checking out the 1E Ordo Dracul book; maybe they focus more on overcoming weaknesses in 2E, but change in opposition to the stagnation of the Kindred condition was explicitly part of their mission originally; hair dye and tattoos were considered good example of beginner-level experimentation for a Dragon. Maybe the book on Elders had something as well? Been a while since I was following Requiem. </div> </div> </div>Yeah XP costs were variable on some things, but how does that support the idea that Requiem Vampires don't change but Masquerade Vampires do? Ordo attempting to permanently tattoo their bodies is an example of preserving bodily changes. <br /> <br /> The claim made was that a Requiem vampire stayed the same as they were in life while Masquerade vampires could become a completely different &quot;person.&quot; There is nothing to support that.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23889-dirtypoolfilms","name":"dirtypoolfilms","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"36"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-06-29T11:27:03-07:00","id":1453770,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>dirtypoolfilms</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1443592-the-official-v5-vs-v20-thread?p=1453767#post1453767\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Neither of these really says what what claimed. Embracing someone to preserve their talents means preserving access to their knowledge and experience not freezing them in amber so they do not change. Discovering that the childe is unable to reach the apex of their living abilities can mean many things, not the least of which is they stop pursuing it because their priorities change post embrace.<br /> <br /> The stasis and stagnation bit is talking about the stagnation of the nightly routine of the damned and the stasis of the body. Not of the personality.<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> Yeah XP costs were variable on some things, but how does that support the idea that Requiem Vampires don't change but Masquerade Vampires do? Ordo attempting to permanently tattoo their bodies is an example of preserving bodily changes.<br /> <br /> The claim made was that a Requiem vampire stayed the same as they were in life while Masquerade vampires could become a completely different &quot;person.&quot; There is nothing to support that.</div> </div> </div> </div>Two things:<br /> <br /> 1) It was a vague hand-wave at something from an entirely different game. Maybe you're getting a bit too hung up on the particulars of something that no one here was really trying to make a statement about? No one here is trying to say that VtR Kindred are unchanging statues, just that the idea of stagnation was significantly played up in VtR compared to VtM.<br /> <br /> 2) This is a Vampire: the Masquerade discussion, in a Vampire: the Masquerade forum. If people disagreeing with you about the text of the VtR corebook MUST be responded to, please make a thread in the VtR forum, tag anyone you want involved in the discussion, and I'll decide whether or not I actually want to bother spending 2 or 3 days mining texts to try and confirm if I remember things correctly, because I am pretty confident that VtR leaned into that position a fair bit. But you are derailing a thread at this point over something that is pretty much irrelevant to the larger discussion.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":25886,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25886-kharnov","user":"Kharnov","date":". 06-29-2021, 02:31 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25886-kharnov","name":"Kharnov","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2020"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"683"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-06-29T11:46:37-07:00","id":1453773,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>dirtypoolfilms</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1443592-the-official-v5-vs-v20-thread?p=1453756#post1453756\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> That's even more confusing because &quot;<i>While a vampire might believe that he feels an emotion, what he actually feels is the echo of mortal emotions that the remnants of his soul apply to his current experience.&quot;</i> =/= &quot;you can't change and are frozen as who you were.&quot;</div> </div> </div> </div>I mean if you're restricted to what is a pale echo of who you are, you can't exactly change can you? Requiem emphasizes you are a half-shell of what you are.<br /> <br /> A remnant.<br /> <br /> Vampire: The Masquerade emphasizes you are a exploding tower of emotion and fury.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Author of <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Cthulhu-Armageddon-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01KUOM7SI/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982844&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Cthulhu+Armageddon\" target=\"_blank\">Cthulhu Armageddon</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Teenage-Weredeer-Bright-Falls-Mysteries-ebook/dp/B075TTN2FN/ref=sr_1_2?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982717&amp;sr=1-2&amp;keywords=Weredeer#customerReviews\" target=\"_blank\">I was a Teenage Weredeer</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Straight-Outta-Fangton-Comedic-Vampire-ebook/dp/B01KNHICCC/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982774&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Straight+Outta+Fangton\" target=\"_blank\">Straight Outta Fangton</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Lucifers-Star-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01MDM9MCT/ref=mt_kindle?_encoding=UTF8&amp;me=&amp;qid=\" target=\"_blank\">Lucifer's Star</a>, </i>and the <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Rules-Supervillainy-Saga-Book-ebook/dp/B07MB89S33/\" target=\"_blank\">Supervillainy Saga</a>.</i><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","name":"CTPhipps","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12002_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13933"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-06-29T11:55:07-07:00","id":1453775,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CTPhipps</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1443592-the-official-v5-vs-v20-thread?p=1453773#post1453773\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I mean if you're restricted to what is a pale echo of who you are, you can't exactly change can you? Requiem emphasizes you are a half-shell of what you are.<br /> <br /> A remnant.<br /> <br /> Vampire: The Masquerade emphasizes you are a exploding tower of emotion and fury.</div> </div> </div> </div>But is that true of the current editions of either game?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/9015-zee-patrick","name":"zee PaTrick","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"56"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-06-29T12:22:05-07:00","id":1453778,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CTPhipps</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1443592-the-official-v5-vs-v20-thread?p=1453773#post1453773\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I mean if you're restricted to what is a pale echo of who you are, you can't exactly change can you? Requiem emphasizes you are a half-shell of what you are.<br /> <br /> A remnant.<br /> <br /> Vampire: The Masquerade emphasizes you are a exploding tower of emotion and fury.</div> </div> </div> </div>I feel like the issue is that it's very much a debate of semantics and interpretation. I agree with your read that the &quot;echo&quot; comment strongly implies something stuck to simply repeat the pattern that it's original living source gave to it, but others may not read it that way or may place less emphasis on it. I also suspect that the problem is one of overly literal interpretation. People have used the word &quot;unchanging,&quot; and the poster is reading that as us saying they literally never change.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>zee PaTrick</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1443592-the-official-v5-vs-v20-thread?p=1453775#post1453775\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> But is that true of the current editions of either game?</div> </div> </div> </div>I don't know much about Requiem 2E, but IIRC it has moved away from that significantly.<br /> <br /> There are some small degrees to which Masquerade Vampires are associated with stagnation or stasis, such as their association with Banality in Changeling. But for the most part it is much more open to Kindred changing and evolving over time.<br /> <br /> P.S. IMO, the whole &quot;Kindred are stagnant and struggle to change or grow&quot; thing in VtR 1E was about emphasizing the fact that Vampirism is supposed to be a Curse, not a Blessing for Sociopaths, without having to build the notion of religious damnation into the centre of the narrative like the Caine narrative did in VtM. I think they moved away from it in 2E because it was a messy and not especially popular concept, and I think they maybe emphasized the Beast as more of a problem in 2E to compensate, but I don't know that for sure.<br /> <br /> Moreover, it was not something that was universally accepted even in VtR 1E. Aside from the Ordo Dracul's whole thing being that changing the Kindred condition was possible, the Circle of the Crone also didn't buy into the idea. They considered the Kindred condition as different from most, but not unnatural or unchanging. The ability to change and grow through tribulation was one of their big tenets in 1E, IIRC. Again, Kindred-as-unchanging was a bit like the Caine myth in 1E; it was a core narrative, but not the only one.<br /> <br /> {This is why I suggested a new thread if people really want this discussion, there is a fair amount to say on the subject}","signature":"","edited":{"userid":25886,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25886-kharnov","user":"Kharnov","date":". 06-29-2021, 03:31 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25886-kharnov","name":"Kharnov","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2020"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"683"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-06-29T12:27:38-07:00","id":1453779,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Kharnov</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1443592-the-official-v5-vs-v20-thread?p=1453778#post1453778\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I don't know much about Requiem 2E, but IIRC it has moved away from that significantly.<br /> <br /> There are some small degrees to which Masquerade Vampires are associated with stagnation or stasis, such as their association with Banality in Changeling. But for the most part it is much more open to Kindred changing and evolving over time.</div> </div> </div> </div>But does &quot;Vampire: The Masquerade emphasizes you are a exploding tower of emotion and fury&quot; which is what my question was directly asking for V5 not about them changing and evolving over time.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/9015-zee-patrick","name":"zee PaTrick","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"56"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-06-29T12:48:48-07:00","id":1453782,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>zee PaTrick</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1443592-the-official-v5-vs-v20-thread?p=1453779#post1453779\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> But does &quot;Vampire: The Masquerade emphasizes you are a exploding tower of emotion and fury&quot; which is what my question was directly asking for V5 not about them changing and evolving over time.</div> </div> </div> </div>Kind of, definitely some more than others. I think that VtM and VtR both place a lot of emphasis on the Beast, which is an exploding tower of fury and Id at least. The Toreador in VtM emphasize the Anne Rice &quot;vampires as having feelings even more intense than normal humans&quot; thing in a core Clan, while they're relegated to a small Bloodline in VtR with more of an emphasis on art than emotion IIRC; instead you get the Daeva as a core clan, which is more vampire-as-sexual-predator. I don't know a ton about V5, but my understanding is that &quot;you succeed, but the Beast does something nasty in the process&quot; is a core mechanic in V5 (I think VtR2E as well).<br /> <br /> P.S. I am now laughing at the realization that the only thing a Vampire ever truly feels is murderously hangry. My brain is now awash with Snickers jokes.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":25886,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25886-kharnov","user":"Kharnov","date":". 06-29-2021, 03:55 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25886-kharnov","name":"Kharnov","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2020"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"683"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-06-29T12:58:48-07:00","id":1453783,"title":"","content":"Isn't it really in V5 less an exploding tower of emotion and fury and more a suddenly you can only be satiated by murder?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/9015-zee-patrick","name":"zee PaTrick","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"56"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-06-29T13:34:18-07:00","id":1453786,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Kharnov</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1443592-the-official-v5-vs-v20-thread?p=1453770#post1453770\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Two things:<br /> <br /> 1) It was a vague hand-wave at something from an entirely different game. Maybe you're getting a bit too hung up on the particulars of something that no one here was really trying to make a statement about? No one here is trying to say that VtR Kindred are unchanging statues, just that the idea of stagnation was significantly played up in VtR compared to VtM.<br /> <br /> 2) This is a Vampire: the Masquerade discussion, in a Vampire: the Masquerade forum. If people disagreeing with you about the text of the VtR corebook MUST be responded to, please make a thread in the VtR forum, tag anyone you want involved in the discussion, and I'll decide whether or not I actually want to bother spending 2 or 3 days mining texts to try and confirm if I remember things correctly, because I am pretty confident that VtR leaned into that position a fair bit. But you are derailing a thread at this point over something that is pretty much irrelevant to the larger discussion.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Two replies:<br /> <br /> 1. It was a vague hand-wave at something from an entirely different game... that neither you nor the person who brought it up have been able to prove even existed as a core conceit of said game.<br /> <br /> 2. It was brought up in the context of a direct comparison with Masquerade. The statement was literally about one system being better than the other because of the differences in how it handles the growth and change of Vampires. If the only way to engage with a comparison between the two games is to accept a premise I don't agree with and then be lectured about how I'm wrong by people who flatly admit to not knowing the new edition of that game very well, not remembering the older edition of that game very well and accept that their <b>belief</b> of how the game I've played fairly consistently for 17 years supersedes the quotes I've provided directly from its text - then you don't want a conversation. You want a Masquerade echo chamber where a statement doesn't have to be correct so long as it sounds complimentary.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> I mean if you're restricted to what is a pale echo of who you are, you can't exactly change can you? Requiem emphasizes you are a half-shell of what you are. </div> </div> </div>Your emotions are a pale echo of real human emotions is what that sentence expressly said. Applying that to the full &quot;personhood&quot; of the character is an extrapolation you are adding to the mix. One that doesn't jibe with the way the Humanity system of either edition describes the way Vampires devolve through play.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":23889,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23889-dirtypoolfilms","user":"dirtypoolfilms","date":". 06-29-2021, 04:37 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23889-dirtypoolfilms","name":"dirtypoolfilms","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"36"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-06-29T14:01:05-07:00","id":1453787,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>zee PaTrick</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1443592-the-official-v5-vs-v20-thread?p=1453783#post1453783\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Isn't it really in V5 less an exploding tower of emotion and fury and more a suddenly you can only be satiated by murder?</div> </div> </div> </div>This is another one of those things that I think was different at tables. V5 really is an improvement on V20.<br /> <br /> You were always described in Fluff as NEVER being full.<br /> <br /> With V5 you can now actually feel a release from the Beast for a night.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>dirtypoolfilms</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1443592-the-official-v5-vs-v20-thread?p=1453786#post1453786\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Your emotions are a pale echo of real human emotions is what that sentence expressly said. Applying that to the full &quot;personhood&quot; of the character is an extrapolation you are adding to the mix. One that doesn't jibe with the way the Humanity system of either edition describes the way Vampires devolve through play.</div> </div> </div> </div>I was actually arguing in the emotional context. So, I don't have any disagreement with you.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Author of <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Cthulhu-Armageddon-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01KUOM7SI/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982844&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Cthulhu+Armageddon\" target=\"_blank\">Cthulhu Armageddon</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Teenage-Weredeer-Bright-Falls-Mysteries-ebook/dp/B075TTN2FN/ref=sr_1_2?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982717&amp;sr=1-2&amp;keywords=Weredeer#customerReviews\" target=\"_blank\">I was a Teenage Weredeer</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Straight-Outta-Fangton-Comedic-Vampire-ebook/dp/B01KNHICCC/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982774&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Straight+Outta+Fangton\" target=\"_blank\">Straight Outta Fangton</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Lucifers-Star-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01MDM9MCT/ref=mt_kindle?_encoding=UTF8&amp;me=&amp;qid=\" target=\"_blank\">Lucifer's Star</a>, </i>and the <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Rules-Supervillainy-Saga-Book-ebook/dp/B07MB89S33/\" target=\"_blank\">Supervillainy Saga</a>.</i><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","name":"CTPhipps","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12002_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13933"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-06-29T14:27:17-07:00","id":1453788,"title":"","content":"I've never liked or used this idea of vampire emotions being a &quot;pale echo of human emotions&quot;. It doesn't fit vampires, who are generally presented as operatic creatures in fiction. It sounds like it's rooted in a throwaway line in &quot;Interview&quot; about Louis feeling like he's gotten dead inside.<br /> <br /> The thing is, Louis is an unreliable narrator, and the actual story heavily, heavily implies that he feels intense emotions, and that he is just misinterpreting his depression and apathy as a lack of emotion. Anne Ricepires are operatically emotional. And they are far from the only one. Wamphyri are specifically stated to have amplified emotions in the Necroscope book, and this is the root of why they are so dangerous: they overreact to everything. They exist in a state of perpetual melodrama acting like exponentially worse versions of angsty teens, on top of having an appetite for humans and horrific superpowers with witch to act out their urges and emotions.<br /> <br /> It's a very common thing in fiction that vampires are melodramatically emotional, so the game having their emotions being pale shadows of human's is something I throw right in the garbage, and I don't think I've ever even played in a game where it is enforced or even suggested by the ST that you play unemotionally. The closest would be some of my Death and the Soul players, and even they tend to roleplay struggling with repressing their emotions in service to their path, rather than it being some default thing.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3598-cajunkhan","name":"CajunKhan","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3598_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1700"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-06-29T14:37:26-07:00","id":1453791,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>dirtypoolfilms</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1443592-the-official-v5-vs-v20-thread?p=1453786#post1453786\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Two replies:<br /> <br /> 1. It was a vague hand-wave at something from an entirely different game... that neither you nor the person who brought it up have been able to prove even existed as a core conceit of said game.<br /> <br /> 2. It was brought up in the context of a direct comparison with Masquerade. The statement was literally about one system being better than the other because of the differences in how it handles the growth and change of Vampires. If the only way to engage with a comparison between the two games is to accept a premise I don't agree with and then be lectured about how I'm wrong by people who flatly admit to not knowing the new edition of that game very well, not remembering the older edition of that game very well and accept that their <b>belief</b> of how the game I've played fairly consistently for 17 years supersedes the quotes I've provided directly from its text - then you don't want a conversation. You want a Masquerade echo chamber where a statement doesn't have to be correct so long as it sounds complimentary.</div> </div> </div> </div>Ok then.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CTPhipps</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1443592-the-official-v5-vs-v20-thread?p=1453710#post1453710\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Honestly, it's part of the setting that pragmatism actually has very little to do with the Embrace and that those that DO Embrace for pragmatic reasons aren't necessarily making the smart decision. One of the themes of Chicago by Night 1st Edition was that Lodin wanted to control the entire city with his massive brood of Ventrue and while he did Embrace solely on what he perceived as power and ability, that didn't always work. Jacob Schumpeter was a complete fool that was just good at keeping up appearances, Drummond was mono-focused on trains and useless at anything else, and Kevin Jackson was someone that Lodin underestimated terribly because he assumed gangs were just what Kevin was good at versus something he used as a substitute in lieu of achieving something in another field were he afforded opportunities.<br /> <br /> (Which is to say Kevin Jackson was only a gang leader because of institutional racism)<br /> <br /> You can't really predict what the Embrace will do to people. One thing VTM is better at than Requiem is that Requiem says you can't change and are frozen as who you were. VTM suggests that you may become a WHOLLY DIFFERENT PERSON because of the Embrace and your past self becomes meaningless.</div> </div> </div> </div>To be clear, the thing that you are throwing down a gauntlet over was one brief off-topic comment. CTPhipps' opinion on VtM vs. VtR is utterly irrelevant to the rest of the conversation comparing two editions of VtM.<br /> <br /> Explain to me how this discussion of VtM versus VtR actually ties in to the discussion about V20 versus V5? CTPhipps provided a long list of VtM-only sources for his statement about VtM Vampires being changeable beings, so his later comparison to VtR isn't actually necessary to prove their point. It was just an off-the-cuff opinion. Can you explain to me how disproving this one opinion will actually contribute to the conversation about Vampire: the Masquerade? How does proving something about VtR Vampires actually prove anything about VtM Vampires?<br /> <br /> I'm not telling you to take the conversation somewhere else because I want an echo chamber. I'm asking you to take it somewhere else because it does not actually contribute to the topic people are here to discuss. And the argument that this is a happy little echo chamber is hilarious. Like, have you read 50 pages of &quot;VtM &gt; VtR, ra ra ra!&quot; that I just haven't seen? I think if you read everything that I've said on the subject, the only comparison I've ever made between VtM and VtR in this entire discussion was positive towards VtR, referring to the Predator's Taint. One person made one negative comparison, and you're now complaining that everyone wants a VtM echo chamber.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25886-kharnov","name":"Kharnov","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2020"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"683"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-06-29T15:08:57-07:00","id":1453793,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CTPhipps</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1443592-the-official-v5-vs-v20-thread?p=1453787#post1453787\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I was actually arguing in the emotional context. So, I don't have any disagreement with you.</div> </div> </div> </div>Could have been clearer because the implication of: &quot;<i>You can't really predict what the Embrace will do to people. One thing VTM is better at than Requiem is that Requiem says you can't change and are frozen as who you were. VTM suggests that you may become a WHOLLY DIFFERENT PERSON because of the Embrace and your past self becomes meaningless.</i>&quot; is that of a type of change beyond simply the emotional responses of the character. A Vampire now more in touch with his beast after the embrace who becomes more predatory in his interactions with people and pushes his strength and power to get what he wants in a way he never did in mortal life has become a &quot;wholly different person.&quot;<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Kharnov</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">Explain to me how this discussion of VtM versus VtR actually ties in to the discussion about V20 versus V5?</div> </div> </div> </div>I'm sorry, is there some rule I'm unaware of where if someone brings up a comparison between two games it's only fair game to respond to it if it furthers the titular conversation of the thread? Also, while we're requesting explanations: could you explain why it was a fair conversation for you to continue to reply to until two posts ago and then it became necessary for you to shut it down as being off topic? You were willing to engage and then suddenly it was now me threadjacking rather than a back and forth?<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Kharnov</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">I'm not telling you to take the conversation somewhere else because I want an echo chamber. I'm asking you to take it somewhere else because it does not actually contribute to the topic people are here to discuss. And the argument that this is a happy little echo chamber is hilarious. Like, have you read 50 pages of &quot;VtM &gt; VtR, ra ra ra!&quot; that I just haven't seen? I think if you read everything that I've said on the subject, the only comparison I've ever made between VtM and VtR in this entire discussion was positive towards VtR, referring to the Predator's Taint. One person made one negative comparison, and you're now complaining that everyone wants a VtM echo chamber.</div> </div> </div> </div>A lot to unpack here.<br /> <br /> 1. I didn't say anything about <b>everyone</b> wanting a VtM echo chamber. I said that if you're going to dictate to me how I'm allowed to respond to a direct comparison between VtR and VtM and should vacate this thread if I'm not responding to it in the way that you want solely on the basis of how it furthers this thread then <b>YOU </b>want a Masquerade echo chamber. The idea that I should leave because it doesn't contribute to the topic people are here to discuss is interesting because it was brought up by someone who posts here every day, and I'm a people, and I'm here and up until a few posts ago - you were discussing it with me... by choice.<br /> <br /> 2. Why are you so defensive about the echo chamber statement? It seems to have touched a nerve.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":23889,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23889-dirtypoolfilms","user":"dirtypoolfilms","date":". 06-29-2021, 06:13 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23889-dirtypoolfilms","name":"dirtypoolfilms","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"36"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-06-29T15:22:29-07:00","id":1453795,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>dirtypoolfilms</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1443592-the-official-v5-vs-v20-thread?p=1453793#post1453793\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I'm sorry, is there some rule I'm unaware of where if someone brings up a comparison between two games it's only fair game to respond to it if it furthers the titular conversation of the thread? Also, while we're requesting explanations: could you explain why it was a fair conversation for you to continue to reply to until two posts ago and then it became necessary for you to shut it down as being off topic? You were willing to engage and then suddenly it was now me threadjacking rather than a back and forth?<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> A lot to unpack here.<br /> <br /> 1. I didn't say anything about <b>everyone</b> wanting a VtM echo chamber. I said that if you're going to dictate to me how I'm allowed to respond to a direct comparison between VtR and VtM and should vacate this thread if I'm not responding to it in the way that you want solely on the basis of how it furthers this thread then <b>YOU </b>want a Masquerade echo chamber. The idea that I should leave because it doesn't contribute to the topic people are here to discuss is interesting because it was brought up by someone who posts here every day, and I'm a people, and I'm here and up until a few posts ago - you were discussing it with me... by choice.<br /> <br /> 2. Why are so defensive about the echo chamber statement? It seems to have touched a nerve.</div> </div> </div> </div>Inviting you to continue the conversation elsewhere doesn't sound like me trying to stop the conversation. It sounds like me asking you to have it elsewhere. I encouraged you to @ anyone you thought should be involved. And I've stated why: because I thought that actually resolving this argument to anything remotely resembling anyone's satisfaction would take a long time and a lot of posts. That is why I &quot;suddenly&quot; decided to start bringing up how off-topic it was, because a quick discussion about something else is fine, while an extensive semantic debate will make it legitimately difficult for people looking for posts on the relevant topic to find what they are looking for. Frankly, I'm glad it seems to have been worked out sooner than I expected.<br /> <br /> And asking that a topic which is supposed to be discussing Vampire: the Masquerade to discuss Vampire: the Masquerade isn't asking for an echo chamber. It's asking the topic to stay on topic, and inviting another conversation to continue somewhere else, allowing both topics to get the attention they deserve. If you want to have a discussion about something purely related to VtR, there is a forum for that.<br /> <br /> I'm not defensive. I'm irritated. As I noted, this whole matter was just misinterpretation and semantics, and it could have been resolved elsewhere. And I focused on the echo chamber comment because this thread has been nothing but fighting; it was ridiculously ironic.<br /> <br /> <br /> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3598-cajunkhan\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar3598_2.jpeg');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"3598\" data-vbnamecard=\"3598\">CajunKhan</a> I don't think emotionlessness was ever really depicted as a feature of Anne Rice vampires. I agree with you about Louis, but Louis was also the exception rather than the rule.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25886-kharnov","name":"Kharnov","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2020"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"683"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-06-29T15:28:53-07:00","id":1453796,"title":"","content":"<span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Speaking as the Moderator, maybe it's just best to move on. This is meant to be fun and I feel this is quibbling over details. If anyone has any complaints about other posters, remember to take it to the Moderators and not make them in the thread.</span><br /> <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Author of <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Cthulhu-Armageddon-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01KUOM7SI/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982844&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Cthulhu+Armageddon\" target=\"_blank\">Cthulhu Armageddon</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Teenage-Weredeer-Bright-Falls-Mysteries-ebook/dp/B075TTN2FN/ref=sr_1_2?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982717&amp;sr=1-2&amp;keywords=Weredeer#customerReviews\" target=\"_blank\">I was a Teenage Weredeer</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Straight-Outta-Fangton-Comedic-Vampire-ebook/dp/B01KNHICCC/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982774&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Straight+Outta+Fangton\" target=\"_blank\">Straight Outta Fangton</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Lucifers-Star-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01MDM9MCT/ref=mt_kindle?_encoding=UTF8&amp;me=&amp;qid=\" target=\"_blank\">Lucifer's Star</a>, </i>and the <i><a href=\"htt