iew Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Over 800 posts. Apparently this was a topic people were dying to discuss.</div> </div> </div> </div>there's alot to talk about when discussing the faults of V5 <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/tongue.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Stick Out Tongue\" smilieid=\"5\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":6}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25992-archderd","name":"archderd","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25992_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2020"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"205"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-06-29T16:23:54-07:00","id":1453800,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>archderd</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1443592-the-official-v5-vs-v20-thread?p=1453799#post1453799\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">there's alot to talk about when discussing the faults of V5 <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/tongue.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Stick Out Tongue\" smilieid=\"5\" class=\"inlineimg\" /></div> </div> </div> </div>*sad trombone*<br /> <br /> *hooks archderd off stage*","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Author of <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Cthulhu-Armageddon-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01KUOM7SI/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982844&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Cthulhu+Armageddon\" target=\"_blank\">Cthulhu Armageddon</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Teenage-Weredeer-Bright-Falls-Mysteries-ebook/dp/B075TTN2FN/ref=sr_1_2?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982717&amp;sr=1-2&amp;keywords=Weredeer#customerReviews\" target=\"_blank\">I was a Teenage Weredeer</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Straight-Outta-Fangton-Comedic-Vampire-ebook/dp/B01KNHICCC/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982774&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Straight+Outta+Fangton\" target=\"_blank\">Straight Outta Fangton</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Lucifers-Star-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01MDM9MCT/ref=mt_kindle?_encoding=UTF8&amp;me=&amp;qid=\" target=\"_blank\">Lucifer's Star</a>, </i>and the <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Rules-Supervillainy-Saga-Book-ebook/dp/B07MB89S33/\" target=\"_blank\">Supervillainy Saga</a>.</i><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","name":"CTPhipps","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12002_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13933"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-06-29T21:02:21-07:00","id":1453809,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CTPhipps</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1443592-the-official-v5-vs-v20-thread?p=1453798#post1453798\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Over 800 posts. Apparently this was a topic people were dying to discuss.</div> </div> </div> </div>&quot;What's with all the V5 sour grapes?&quot; was better.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24832-blailton","name":"blailton","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24832_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"389"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-06-30T03:32:51-07:00","id":1453829,"title":"","content":"No, it really wasn't.<br /> <br /> But anyway, to try to get back to VtM vs. VtM stuff:<br /> <br /> When it comes to how the different editions stress how vampires can change over time, I'm still feeling V20 offers more compelling game experiences. However much the Embrace might change you (and that's potentially quiet drastic in any of the editions), after that?<br /> <br /> The Nature/Demeanor setup offers some potential (if generally squandered as talking about changing those is a side-note in V20, and stuffed way back in ST oriented supplements previously). But the Paths of Enlightenment offer up a real place for characters to meaningfully change over time. Including Humanity itself, the Bearing rules help show a character changing as they pursue (or fail) an outlook on unlife. It's difficult and hard, but V20 right in the core book shows that vampires aren't stuck in one mode of thinking and reacting to their situation. The robust and/or overwrote Merit and Flaws also offer ways to represent changes in your character (assuming the optional rules are in play, and the optional rules about gaining/losing them are also in play).<br /> <br /> V5, even with all its optional rules as presented, still suffers a lot from no real way for vampires to change beyond the Beast vs. Man axis. The Beast can get strong or weaker. You can lose Convictions (or with house rules to back up the one unclear passage about possibly regaining them, regain them), but that's just losing a defense against the Beast. Even if V5 vampires aren't static, they're still on a single rail. If you look at a V5 character sheet at the start of play, and after a year of play, is there anything that would really show &quot;this character has had some major emotional developments?&quot; They lost a Conviction... but has the character really changed or just lost enough belief in an idea to use it as a bulwark against the Beast even if they're still struggling to hold on to that belief? They lost some Humanity, but since that can come from external sources and bad dice, that doesn't communicate nearly as much emotional change for the character.<br /> <br /> While a V20 character sheet isn't always going to show a story when you compare it over time, there's a lot of places where you can tell the character went through some major emotional changes just by seeing that those notations are different. V5 lacks that.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-06-30T04:27:00-07:00","id":1453831,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Heavy Arms</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1443592-the-official-v5-vs-v20-thread?p=1453829#post1453829\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The Nature/Demeanor setup offers some potential (if generally squandered as talking about changing those is a side-note in V20, and stuffed way back in ST oriented supplements previously).</div> </div> </div> </div>Nature and Demeanour were the two most important traits within <i>Vampire: the Masquerade</i>. They should probably be the last traits to be dumped when revising the system. <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/317-james_willoughby","name":"James_Willoughby","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar317_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"297"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-06-30T07:30:31-07:00","id":1453843,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>James_Willoughby</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1443592-the-official-v5-vs-v20-thread?p=1453831#post1453831\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Nature and Demeanour were the two most important traits within <i>Vampire: the Masquerade</i>. They should probably be the last traits to be dumped when revising the system.</div> </div> </div> </div>Nature and Demeanor are like Alignment. They're not actually a thing that should exist save as a gaming shorthand, IMHO for beginning players.<br /> <br /> If you have a three-dimensional personality, you don't need any of them.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Author of <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Cthulhu-Armageddon-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01KUOM7SI/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982844&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Cthulhu+Armageddon\" target=\"_blank\">Cthulhu Armageddon</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Teenage-Weredeer-Bright-Falls-Mysteries-ebook/dp/B075TTN2FN/ref=sr_1_2?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982717&amp;sr=1-2&amp;keywords=Weredeer#customerReviews\" target=\"_blank\">I was a Teenage Weredeer</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Straight-Outta-Fangton-Comedic-Vampire-ebook/dp/B01KNHICCC/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982774&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Straight+Outta+Fangton\" target=\"_blank\">Straight Outta Fangton</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Lucifers-Star-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01MDM9MCT/ref=mt_kindle?_encoding=UTF8&amp;me=&amp;qid=\" target=\"_blank\">Lucifer's Star</a>, </i>and the <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Rules-Supervillainy-Saga-Book-ebook/dp/B07MB89S33/\" target=\"_blank\">Supervillainy Saga</a>.</i><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","name":"CTPhipps","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12002_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13933"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-06-30T08:59:31-07:00","id":1453846,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CTPhipps</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1443592-the-official-v5-vs-v20-thread?p=1453843#post1453843\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Nature and Demeanor are like Alignment. They're not actually a thing that should exist save as a gaming shorthand, IMHO for beginning players.<br /> <br /> If you have a three-dimensional personality, you don't need any of them.</div> </div> </div> </div>A three-dimensional personality doesn't provide a mechanic for regaining willpower.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":6}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23889-dirtypoolfilms","name":"dirtypoolfilms","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"36"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-06-30T10:45:20-07:00","id":1453850,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>James_Willoughby</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1443592-the-official-v5-vs-v20-thread?p=1453831#post1453831\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Nature and Demeanour were the two most important traits within <i>Vampire: the Masquerade</i>. They should probably be the last traits to be dumped when revising the system.</div> </div> </div> </div>Eh....<br /> <br /> I actually think they were a vital part that needed reevaluation, and experimentation in other WW games even in the late 90s were showing there were other options that might be better.<br /> <br /> Or, more specifically, Nature is pretty important, but Demeanor was largely vestigial.<br /> <br /> Dumping them can be handled well, but you need something to take up the slack of helping to codify your character's emotional core. You can dump Demeanor and not even notice it because it has no actual game function. If anything dropping Demeanor helps because it allows characters to behave more naturally where they have more than two modes to pick from.<br /> <br /> My issue with V5 here is that they were just dumped without any evidence of thought towards what fills the gap left behind.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CTPhipps</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1443592-the-official-v5-vs-v20-thread?p=1453843#post1453843\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Nature and Demeanor are like Alignment. They're not actually a thing that should exist save as a gaming shorthand, IMHO for beginning players.<br /> <br /> If you have a three-dimensional personality, you don't need any of them.</div> </div> </div> </div>Yeesh there's a lot of problems with this take.<br /> <br /> First, if stuff is good for new players it absolutely needs to be in the game. People that know the games can take whatever shortcuts work for them and their group. New players need tools to understand the game the most and suffer the most when people get dismissive of rules like you've done here. If you want people to like a game you like, you want to make as new player accessible as possible, and you want to be happy about the existence of stuff that's new player friendly even if you skip it now.<br /> <br /> Second, it is very difficult to find a sufficient argument against the &quot;Systems Matter&quot; concept. While lots of people have tried, it more comes down to a critique of presentation of the concept, or ends up affirming the premise in objection. By which I mean, even for people that feel that being free to ignore the rules is a good thing, you can't feel good about ignore rules that aren't there. That whole smug expression of &quot;if you have a 'real' character you don't need these things,&quot; only exists because of an emotional validation in breaking the rules being fun (which is true for most people on some level). Disregarding any issues with the implementations of a given mechanic, concepts like Alignment, or Nature/Demeanor, have obvious value in shaping how people approach the game... even in how they house rule out those elements should they desire to.<br /> <br /> Finally, these are aspects of the system with actual mechanics to resolve. My D&amp;D character might have a spell that keys off Alignment, or even has differential effects based on Alignment; thus even with a &quot;three-dimensional personality&quot; I need Alignment or something to replace it if I don't want to completely rewrite the spell list. As noted, Nature is linked to the WP economy of the pre-V5 editions, as well as being meant to help guide how to interpret certain systems (including Dominate).<br /> <br /> You can't value emotional change in a game, and not have something in the system to represent major emotion based changes in the character. Alignment and Nature/Demeanor might not be great systems, but they allow a representation of change that V5 does not offer. If my D&amp;D PC goes from Lawful Good to Neutral Good, that is a major statement about my character's emotional journey. If my VtM vampire changes Nature from Cynic to Idealist, that's a huge sign of emotional change. Deriding those mechanics' flaws doesn't support any claim that V5 is better with nothing in this space.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-07-01T01:04:04-07:00","id":1453898,"title":"","content":"...I actually think the way V5 does willpower is pretty good. I'm not going to say its a grand improvement, because it needs work: social combat willpower loses are a clowns work, but the more dynamic nature of willpower and the part where it's tied to other stats more closely is pretty good. <br /> <br /> Messy criticals can die in a ditch <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar12002_2.jpeg');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"12002\" data-vbnamecard=\"12002\">CTPhipps</a> . They'd work as a derangement or a flaw, but they don't work as a universal constant among members of a secret international conspiracy concerned with 'The Masquerade'. It isn't a concept that lends itself well to the 9/10 game themes or character concepts that require characters to have their shit together to a greater degree. If i want to play a childish character that can't keep emotions in check, I'll make such a character. It is in no way a good idea to force this stupidity on everyone. <br /> <br /> Part of the greatness of VTM is that it gave you the freedom to play all sorts of vampires at once (unless you want to daywalk, in which case you're outa luck) One player can be Nosferatu, the next can be a sex symbol, the third player can be a high-flying corporate wizard, and the fourth can be an old-school can't-cross-running-water coffin-sleeping nutjob that thirsts for virgin girls while wielding impecable manners. V5 says you gotta be an angsty perpetual teen with control issues. That gets stupid quick.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25794-mywifeisscary","name":"MyWifeIsScary","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25794_2.png","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3711"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-07-01T01:20:31-07:00","id":1453902,"title":"","content":"I like the Bestial Failure/Messy Crit mechanics, but I'll admit it does seem intended for games that are more survival-horror than political-chess. It's the perfect mechanic for games that play almost like your typical werewolf movie, or those vampire movies where the protagonist is almost completely isolated from other vampires. That is, the protagonist is trying to survive despite being low-powered, isolated, and suffering from urges that make them routinely violent. &quot;Santa Clarita Diet&quot; comes to mind. &quot;Ginger Snaps&quot;, &quot;Let Me In&quot;. Really any move/novel where the monster is weak, suffers self-destructive urges, and more concerned with night-to-night survival than ruling the world.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3598-cajunkhan","name":"CajunKhan","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3598_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1700"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-07-01T01:37:45-07:00","id":1453904,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MyWifeIsScary</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1443592-the-official-v5-vs-v20-thread?p=1453898#post1453898\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">...I actually think the way V5 does willpower is pretty good. I'm not going to say its a grand improvement, because it needs work: social combat willpower loses are a clowns work, but the more dynamic nature of willpower and the part where it's tied to other stats more closely is pretty good.<br /> <br /> Messy criticals can die in a ditch <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar12002_2.jpeg');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"12002\" data-vbnamecard=\"12002\">CTPhipps</a> . They'd work as a derangement or a flaw, but they don't work as a universal constant among members of a secret international conspiracy concerned with 'The Masquerade'. It isn't a concept that lends itself well to the 9/10 game themes or character concepts that require characters to have their shit together to a greater degree. If i want to play a childish character that can't keep emotions in check, I'll make such a character. It is in no way a good idea to force this stupidity on everyone.<br /> <br /> Part of the greatness of VTM is that it gave you the freedom to play all sorts of vampires at once (unless you want to daywalk, in which case you're outa luck) One player can be Nosferatu, the next can be a sex symbol, the third player can be a high-flying corporate wizard, and the fourth can be an old-school can't-cross-running-water coffin-sleeping nutjob that thirsts for virgin girls while wielding impecable manners. V5 says you gotta be an angsty perpetual teen with control issues. That gets stupid quick.</div> </div> </div> </div>i think messy crits as a concept are fine but are lacking in execution because hunger dice are a default rather then say, a downside for certain behaviors such as poor feeding practices or an overreliance of disciplines.<br /> <br /> actually that's not completly true current hunger dice are a downside for not committing nightly murder","signature":"","edited":{"userid":25992,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25992-archderd","user":"archderd","date":". 07-01-2021, 10:11 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25992-archderd","name":"archderd","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25992_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2020"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"205"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-07-01T01:39:23-07:00","id":1453905,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CTPhipps</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1443592-the-official-v5-vs-v20-thread?p=1453843#post1453843\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Nature and Demeanor are like Alignment. They're not actually a thing that should exist save as a gaming shorthand, IMHO for beginning players.<br /> <br /> If you have a three-dimensional personality, you don't need any of them.</div> </div> </div> </div>Quite frankly, and all due respect, this is a shit take. I'll skip over how Nature ties to Willpower, how Nature interacts with disciplines and all that (others have said it better than I could), and focus on the perceived arrogance of the statement.<br /> <br /> Gaming shorthand is a poor wording, because it opens up the question of what <i>isn't</i> gaming shorthand? Literally any stat could be called that, and we could all go sheetless. It's possible, it's doable, someone's gonna respond in the next page or two how they have done it and still do it. But the majority don't play that way, because we need and enjoy our shorthand. Handwaving away an aspect of the game as &quot;shorthand&quot; that &quot;shouldn't exist&quot; seems rather short-sighted for an advocate of a game with Touchstones which are also just &quot;gaming shorthand&quot;. Throw Predator and stuff in added &quot;gaming shorthand&quot; fun.<br /> <br /> I'm sure you didn't <i>mean</i> to directly imply beginning players cannot make a three-dimensional character, but intent aside, you absolutely <i>did</i> imply that. Which is also a very poor phrasing, because a hobby known for a high barrier to entry compared to, say, sitting down with a brand new video game and just fiddling around, also has held a reputation for snobbery towards new players. And that post is a good example of why. It's so easy to brush things aside as &quot;this is for newbies, not grognads like me&quot; while staring down our noses with disgust. It's easy to do it without even trying. But there's a real need for more &quot;casual friendly&quot; components in a TTRPG, and casting our disgusted gaze upon them only furthers the belief of newer players that this type of community isn't for them.<br /> <br /> And then there's that last sentence, implying that players like me who build a three dimensional character around the foundation of a Nature I pick are somehow doing it wrong, because you &quot;don't even need any of that&quot;. I'm not the kind of person who can whip up a 30 page backstory, fully realized personality and a social connections map off the top of my head. I need a guide, a foundation, something to build from when making a character. And I'm hardly a new player, to VtM or TTRPGs in general. Yes, I do &quot;need any of that&quot;, and implying I'm somehow <i>doing it wrong </i>because I don't do it in your preferred manner is a bit irksome.<br /> <br /> Sorry if this comes across as rude or abrasive, but statements like this just rub me the worst kind of way.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Writing up Clanbook: Aabbt","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":9}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/700-vysha","name":"Vysha","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar700_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"602"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-07-01T04:34:33-07:00","id":1453913,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Kharnov</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1443592-the-official-v5-vs-v20-thread?p=1453763#post1453763\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">stuff</div> </div> </div> </div>I'm not saying societies ills are responsible for all personal ills: vampires are, after all, humans granted phenomenal power, and power tends to reveal what a shit people can be (Insert anti-Garou diatribe here). though I do believe it still has an indirect influence. without Generation adding so much fuel to the Jyhad and making kindred unlife a clusterfuck, vampires will look more to 'embracing stability': Conservative Ventrue types are adored while agressive Lasombra types abhored. Outliers like Beckett would be more heavily scrutinized You still get the odd asshole or the occasional political struggle but the general trend without the fuel of Generation veers towards stability. Eventually vampires will settle with territory and wont risk shaking things up if they want to live long. The nails that stand out get hammered down. With Gen, that fire is always being fueled creates a mess where Becket's act goes unnoticed. It's like... you commit a crime in a shitty part of town? nobody notices. you commit a crime in the rich gated community? The Army will come for you. The omnipresent mess of the Jyhad hides Beckett's dickery. The Quiet of a society where vampires arent fearing that someone will kick down the door and munch them? Any noise is too much noise. Almost Nobody locks their doors in the countryside. Everybody locks their doors on mean streets.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25794-mywifeisscary","name":"MyWifeIsScary","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25794_2.png","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3711"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-07-01T08:19:53-07:00","id":1453939,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Vysha</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1443592-the-official-v5-vs-v20-thread?p=1453905#post1453905\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Quite frankly, and all due respect, this is a shit take. I'll skip over how Nature ties to Willpower, how Nature interacts with disciplines and all that (others have said it better than I could), and focus on the perceived arrogance of the statement.</div> </div> </div> </div>Not to snip your conversational point but I think that maybe you may be taking a bit personally my dislike of using archetypes over full descriptions. But no, I prefer not to use Nature and Demeanor versus having the player characters describe their personalities and let them free form act as to how they present themselves to the world.<br /> <br /> Your idea this is an attack on gaming behavior is not my view or my players. But it's not my preference in the slightest.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Author of <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Cthulhu-Armageddon-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01KUOM7SI/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982844&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Cthulhu+Armageddon\" target=\"_blank\">Cthulhu Armageddon</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Teenage-Weredeer-Brig