egaining willpower once you've culled the existing mechanic for it?</div> </div> </div> </div>The players still put it down but generally I just reward them on good roleplaying and dramatic moments. A good ST knows their player characters after all.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Author of <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Cthulhu-Armageddon-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01KUOM7SI/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982844&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Cthulhu+Armageddon\" target=\"_blank\">Cthulhu Armageddon</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Teenage-Weredeer-Bright-Falls-Mysteries-ebook/dp/B075TTN2FN/ref=sr_1_2?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982717&amp;sr=1-2&amp;keywords=Weredeer#customerReviews\" target=\"_blank\">I was a Teenage Weredeer</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Straight-Outta-Fangton-Comedic-Vampire-ebook/dp/B01KNHICCC/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982774&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Straight+Outta+Fangton\" target=\"_blank\">Straight Outta Fangton</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Lucifers-Star-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01MDM9MCT/ref=mt_kindle?_encoding=UTF8&amp;me=&amp;qid=\" target=\"_blank\">Lucifer's Star</a>, </i>and the <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Rules-Supervillainy-Saga-Book-ebook/dp/B07MB89S33/\" target=\"_blank\">Supervillainy Saga</a>.</i><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","name":"CTPhipps","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12002_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13933"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-07-01T08:53:30-07:00","id":1453943,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CTPhipps</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1443592-the-official-v5-vs-v20-thread?p=1453941#post1453941\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> The players still put it down but generally I just reward them on good roleplaying and dramatic moments. A good ST knows their player characters after all.</div> </div> </div> </div>So, uh, well, um how would the not good STs reward them since they don't know their player characters?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":6}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/9015-zee-patrick","name":"zee PaTrick","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"56"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-07-01T09:02:24-07:00","id":1453944,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CTPhipps</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1443592-the-official-v5-vs-v20-thread?p=1453941#post1453941\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> The players still put it down but generally I just reward them on good roleplaying and dramatic moments. A good ST knows their player characters after all.</div> </div> </div> </div>So you treat Willpower like a Bennie or a Hero Point and use it to reward good roleplay rather than using the system as intended. <br /> <br /> To the other posters point about tone and implication maybe the value judgements you make about the game shouldn't include statements that seem to imply good players or good ST's do it a certain way - because that almost always implies that those who do it differently are bad players or bad ST's","signature":"","edited":{"userid":23889,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23889-dirtypoolfilms","user":"dirtypoolfilms","date":". 07-01-2021, 12:23 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":7}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23889-dirtypoolfilms","name":"dirtypoolfilms","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"36"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-07-01T09:29:55-07:00","id":1453946,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CTPhipps</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1443592-the-official-v5-vs-v20-thread?p=1453939#post1453939\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Not to snip your conversational point but I think that maybe you may be taking a bit personally my dislike of using archetypes over full descriptions.</div> </div> </div> </div>Y'know, I did outright give you the benefit of the doubt a few times in that snipped conversation. &quot;Poor wording&quot;, &quot;I'm sure you didn't mean to imply&quot;, etc.<br /> <br /> So no, I did understand you didn't intend for your post to read that way, but the post still read that way; an experienced player/ST/GM looking down on a system as &quot;too noob&quot;. I don't think I'm the only one who read it that way, given at least one other response to it had a similar read.<br /> <br /> But I'd like to move on to how this post reads; either nature/demeanor, OR a full description. Again, and I'm'a make sure this time it's plainly visible, <i><b>I KNOW YOU LIKELY DIDN'T INTEND FOR IT TO READ THIS WAY, BUT IT READS THIS WAY</b></i>. Because it's right there in the statement, and this type of thing is pretty disheartening to newer players. That if they're using N/D, then they are clearly unable to create a fully realized character, so says the Experienced Player. That nature and demeanor are just a cheap, easy, disposable replacement for making a fleshed out, three dimensional character.<br /> <br /> One last time and then I'm done with this tangent; I'm sure you don't <i><b>INTEND</b></i> to say this, but it clearly <i><b>READS</b></i> this way, and that read is very &quot;new player unfriendly&quot;.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Writing up Clanbook: Aabbt","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":9}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/700-vysha","name":"Vysha","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar700_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"602"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-07-01T10:37:20-07:00","id":1453950,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quot